-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Adam.Backend.Lowering.adam - The analyzed AST -> the SSA IR (PLAN-ADAM M2.2)

  LowerUnit turns every routine of one unit (a module of the program) into
  an IrFunction of its own IrModule (Adam.Backend.Ssa) at the debug level
  (DESIGN sec 5), SU2.4: each unit is its own object, so a unit compiled
  once is linked again unchanged. Another module's routine or variable is a
  declared function or blob (its symbol alone: that unit's object defines
  it), declared only for the modules the unit can name (its imports, theirs
  and the runtime's); what Lowering makes for its own use (texts, maps,
  vtables, descriptors, end and task functions) is internal, each unit's
  own. LowerProgramParts makes what only the whole program knows, every
  build: the entry, the program's thread release, the site list, every
  module's @linklibrary names. Every parameter and local lives in its stack slot (a value
  parameter is stored there at entry; a reference parameter's slot holds the
  address it was given), a local starts zero unless it has an initializer,
  and a value lives within one statement.

  Everything comes from the AST, never re-derived: a call's routine is its
  callee name's ResolvedDecl (a ForwardRoutine's own ResolvedDecl is its full
  declaration), a routine's or an external's symbol its ResolvedSymbol, an
  external's library its clause's ResolvedConst (String; "" when it names
  none, which the linker reports), a constant its ResolvedConst, a value's
  type its canonical type (ResolvedConvert where it converts, else
  ResolvedType), reference or value Types.PassedByReference under the
  routine's linkage, a slot's size and alignment Layout's. An aggregate by
  value crosses a call as the Target says (AggregateInRegister): in one
  integer register, else as a pointer to the caller's copy (an argument) or
  through a hidden first parameter, the caller's slot (a result).

  A clink variadic routine with a body (M3.7c) keeps a cursor in a ptr
  slot, set at entry to its first variadic argument (IrOp.VarargsStart, the
  arch part homing the register ones beside the stacked ones); each
  varargs.next(T) reads the cursor's place at T's promoted type (an
  aggregate as the caller passed it: its bytes there, or the address of its
  copy) and moves the cursor one Target.VariadicSlotBytes on.

  A cpplink variadic (M3.7d, BNF sec 6) takes a typed pack: its IR signature
  is its fixed parameters and one more ptr, the pack's header, built by the
  caller in its own frame (DoPackArguments). The layout, P the target's
  pointer size:
    header  items: ptr at 0, count: int32 at P, cursor: int32 at P + 4
            (P + 8 bytes, pointer aligned; a varargs local is one header)
    item    tag: uint64 at 0 (the argument's static type: DoPackTag, what
            next / get's run-time check compares), place: ptr at 8 (the
            address of the caller's copy of the value, at its own type),
            name: ptr at 8 + P (its type's text, a C string: a raise's
            message), kind: int64 at 8 + 2P (its VarKind's number:
            DoPackKindNumber), facts: ptr at 16 + 2P (what the kind alone
            does not tell, a read-only block by kind: DoPackFacts; nil for
            most); DoPackItemBytes rounds the item to 8
  count / next / get / reset / copy / kind read the header the routine was
  given (FPackSlot) or a varargs local's own; copy() copies the header (the
  items are the caller's and outlive the callee and its locals). next / get /
  kind find their item through the runtime's PackItem (the index against
  the count, next / get's type against the item's tag; raising as pcpp
  does); next moves the cursor only once its read succeeded (M3.8h).

  The slice (M2): routines with value and reference parameters, locals and
  their initializers, expression statements, calls to Adam routines and to
  external routines, integer / bool / pointer constants, assignment to a
  local or a parameter, return with and without a value. Anything else that
  reaches Lowering is reported at its node (LW0001, naming the construct),
  never dropped; M3 widens it.

  M2.3: print / println with a constant format (no arguments, no
  placeholders; {{ and }} are a brace) become a data blob of their text (a
  newline after it for println) and a call of the runtime's text writer, the
  call's ResolvedCallee. An exe's block becomes the entry function (the IR's
  Entry, made after every routine's): its statements, then the runtime's
  exit (the module's ResolvedCallee) with 0; a return in it exits the same
  way. Both routines come from the runtime unit (ATree.Runtime) Semantics
  found; without it, the call or the block is LW0001.

  M3.2: the integer and bool operators of BNF sec 6 (DoBinaryExpression,
  DoUnary, DoConvertTo). `and` / `or` short-circuit and `? :` picks one
  branch: the operands that may not run go in blocks of their own and meet
  in a join block's phi, so an expression may end in another block than it
  began in (DoShortCircuit, DoConditional). `<=>` is two compares
  (DoThreeWay); `++` / `--` and the compound assignments load, combine at
  the promoted type and store (DoStep, DoCompound over DoComputeIn).

  M3.3: the statements of BNF sec 5 as blocks and branches. An if branches
  to its then and else statements (DoIf over DoArm); the join is made only
  when a side falls through to it. A loop's exit and next blocks are made
  before its body (FExitOf / FNextOf by its node), so a leave / skip jumps
  to the block its ResolvedJump's statement owns (DoWhile, DoRepeat,
  DoLeaveSkip). A for keeps PaskalCPP's contract: its end evaluated once
  into the for's own slot, a stop-or-step test after each pass, so the
  iterator ends AT the end and never steps past its type's last value
  (DoFor). A match evaluates its subject once into the match's own slot,
  then tests each arm's labels in source order (a value =, a range by its
  two bounds, signed or unsigned as the subject's IR type is), the first
  that holds entering its arm; none holding runs the else statements; an
  arm that falls through and a leave go to the match's exit (DoMatch).

  M3.4: a scalar module variable lives in a data blob named by its
  ResolvedSymbol (internal when it is its module's private one): its
  initializer's folded bits when they are not all zero (a Variable blob),
  else a Zeroed one of its size (DoGlobal); a use of it is the blob's
  address (DoAddress), as `addr of` any name is (DoUnary). An initializer
  that did not fold leaves its blob Zeroed and runs in its unit's variable
  inits (DoUnitVarInit), in declaration order; with no entry to run them
  they are LW0001. A module's initialize and finalize sections are functions
  of their own (internal, __adam_initialize_ / __adam_finalize_ and the
  module's name; a `return;` leaves the section), called by its start and
  its teardown (DoUnitStart, DoTeardown). The parts' entry (DoEntryBody)
  calls every unit's variable inits, the runtime unit's first, then every
  module after the modules it imports (FOrder: the tree lists the main
  module first, so the order is computed), then every unit's start in that
  same order, then the exe unit's block function (DoBlockBody: the block's
  end and a return in it go to its end block), then the runtime's exit
  with 0, which runs the teardowns in reverse. With no entry the sections
  are LW0001.

  M3.5: every address step is one IrOp.Offset (a ptr and an int64 byte
  count): `P + n`, `P[i]` and the ptr compound forms scale by the target's
  size (DoMovePointer). A record is never an SSA value: a local lives in a
  slot of its size and alignment zeroed by Fill, a module variable in a
  Zeroed blob; each then takes its initializer's bytes (Copy); `:=`
  of a record copies its bytes (DoAggregateAssign). A field's address is the
  record's (or, through `->`, the ptr's) moved by the field's offset in the
  record, a parent part's offset added for a field the parent declares
  (DoMemberAddress); a field of a scalar type loads and stores like any
  place. An overlay is lowered exactly as a record (DoIsFieldAggregate):
  its fields share its storage, so zeroing the whole slot or blob zeroes it
  in every byte (BNF's overlay rule), wherever it sits, an anonymous
  overlay in a record included; a field of an anonymous record or overlay
  is reached by its offset from the named type's start (Layout). A
  bitfield has no address: it lives in a lane of its type's size at the
  offset Layout gives it, read as the lane widened to int64, shifted up
  then down (sar when signed), and written by read-modify-write of the lane
  with a constant mask (DoBitRead / DoBitWrite); every place access goes
  through DoPlaceAddress / DoReadAt / DoWriteAt, so `:=`, compound forms
  and steps work on one as on any place. A local aligned above the stack's
  alignment is a slot like any other: the arch realigns its frame
  (FrameLayout.Realign). A static array is an aggregate as a record is
  (DoIsAggregate: a zeroed slot or blob, `:=` and initializers copy its
  bytes); `A[i]` is the array's address moved by i less the low bound
  elements (DoArrayElement), a char or a wchar index widened by the
  target's char signedness as its bounds are read, so an array of records
  or of arrays reaches its fields and elements from that address.

  M3.6: float32 / float64 travel as the IR's Float32 / Float64 (the arch
  keeps them in vector registers). A float constant is its IEEE bits
  (System.SysUtils' Float64ToBits / Float32ToBits), and a folded integer
  used as a float is converted once at compile time, as C converts it
  (DoFloatConstant). A float's + - * and / are add / sub / mul / fdiv, its
  unary minus a neg, its compounds += -= *= /= the same ops (DoOpFits,
  DoUnaryFits name which types each operator takes). Its compares use the
  IR's float predicates (C's NaN rules: = and the orders false, <> true),
  `<=>` the ordered two (a NaN gives 0), and its truth is `x <> 0.0`. A
  conversion to or from an integer, or between the floats, is the IR's
  convert (C's rules: to nearest one way, toward zero the other); a cast of
  a folded float to an integer or bool is Folding's.

  M3.9: a dynamic array is managed as a text is (DoIsManaged): its value is
  nil or its counted block (System.Runtime's layout: ref count, length in
  elements, the elements), held, borrowed, passed, returned and kept in a
  temporary alike; released, stored, sized and made its own by the Arr*
  routines, each given the array type's element map (DoElementMap: the
  element's size, then the element type's managed map). A managed map
  (DoMapWords) places a type's texts and dynamic arrays at fixed offsets,
  each run's element word 0 for texts, else the offset of the arrays'
  element map, written after the runs in the same blob. A place is reached
  in a read or a write form (DoAddressFor): writing through an element of a
  dynamic array (an assignment, a var argument, `addr of`, a nested element
  or field) first makes every array on the way its holder's alone
  (ArrUnique: copy on write); reading never copies.

  PLAN-SELFHOST S2: a guard with a finally part (BNF sec 5) runs its body in
  blocks of its own, then its finally statements where the body falls
  through; the finally statements are lowered a second time as a funclet
  (an internal function the IR marks with its Parent: it runs in the
  parent's frame, its locals and parameters the parent's slots, reached
  through its frame parameter), and the body's blocks are a scope of the
  function naming it, so an unwind leaving the body runs the funclet (the
  platform unit's frame handler is the frame's handler: the module's
  FrameHandler). An except part's statements are blocks after the body's,
  the target of a catching scope over the body (the platform unit's
  PlatformCatch its filter), added before the finally's scope, which covers
  both (PLAN-ADAM H4t2b0); the except part starts with a call of the
  runtime's FaultTaken (a hardware fault the filter took becomes the raise in
  flight). A jump leaving a guard's body, or an except part
  of a guard with a finally (a return, a leave or skip of a loop around the
  guard), and a guard inside a finally are LW0001.

  PLAN-SELFHOST S3: raise is a call of the runtime's Raise, which keeps the
  text and raises the runtime's exception (the platform unit's
  PlatformRaise). A function holding managed slots (FManaged) gets a
  cleanup funclet releasing them all (DoCleanupFunclet), the handler of a
  scope over every block of it but its exit blocks (DoExitBlock: where an
  exit releases them, so nothing is released twice), added after its
  guards' scopes (DoCleanupScopes); every managed local's slot is empty
  before anything can raise (DoLocalSlots, then an init's parts, then
  DoLocalInits). The entry adds one catching scope around all its blocks,
  the platform unit's PlatformCatchRaise its filter, its target a catch
  block calling the runtime's Unhandled (the report, exit code 1): every
  raise ends there once the frames between are unwound (DoEntryCatch); a
  module teardown and the runtime's ThreadRun get the same (DoCatchAll). A
  hardware fault no guard takes passes it, on to the platform's last filter.
  The runtime's GeneratorRun (a generator's coroutine run, G1) gets one too,
  its filter PlatformCatchAbort (a generator's abort, which no guard takes),
  its catch the runtime's GeneratorEnd.

  Every routine with a body gets its function in AST order before any body
  is lowered (a call may name a routine declared later), so the IR's order
  is the source's; an external gets its entry the first time it is called.
  A type's declared operator is such a function too (no self); a binary or
  unary expression SEM gave it (OperatorCallOf) is a call of it, its
  operands the arguments (DoOperatorCall), its result a call's in every
  rule a call's result follows (DoIsCallSite: moves, temporaries, holds,
  write summaries).
  Statements after a return land in a new block nothing jumps to: still
  lowered, so whatever they hold is still reported.
*******************************************************************************/

module unit Adam.Backend.Lowering;

import System.SysUtils, Adam.Core.Common, Adam.Core.Messages, Adam.Core.Containers, Adam.Target,
  Adam.Compiler.Diagnostics, Adam.Compiler.AST, Adam.Compiler.Types, Adam.Compiler.Layout,
  Adam.Compiler.Symbols, Adam.Compiler.Scopes, Adam.Backend.Ssa;

public const
  ADAM_ERR_LOWERING_001: string = "LW0001";   // a construct code generation does not handle yet

  // The entry function's symbol (the program block, then the runtime's exit with 0; the
  // linker makes it the entry point) and the prefix of a print text's data symbol (its
  // data id follows)
  ADAM_LOWERING_ENTRY_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_entry";
  ADAM_LOWERING_TEXT_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_text";
  // The symbol of the function that releases the calling thread's managed threadstatics
  // (DoProgramRelease: the runtime runs it as each thread but the main one ends)
  ADAM_LOWERING_THREAD_RELEASE_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_threadrelease";
  // The prefix of a string literal's constant block's data symbol (its data id follows)
  ADAM_LOWERING_STRING_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_string";
  // The exe's allocation site table (M3.12b, DoSiteTable): its read-only data symbol, its
  // first 8 bytes and its layout's version (the table's header, see DoSiteTable)
  ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_allocsites";
  ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_MAGIC: string = "AdamSite";
  ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_VERSION: int64 = 3;
  // The exe's code-address line table (M4.L2): its read-only data symbol (the site table's
  // header holds its address); its bytes are the backend's (Adam.Backend.Generate's
  // LineTableMaker), once the code is laid out
  ADAM_LOWERING_LINES_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_lines";
  // A string literal's constant block (System.Runtime's string layout): the ref count of a
  // block never counted or freed, then the length, both int64, the bytes after them
  ADAM_LOWERING_STRING_CONSTANT_COUNT: int64 = -1;
  ADAM_LOWERING_STRING_HEADER: int64 = 16;
  // Where a string's, a wstring's or a dynamic array's block holds its length (units or
  // elements, int64), after its ref count (System.Runtime's StrLength reads it there)
  ADAM_LOWERING_BLOCK_LENGTH: int64 = 8;
  // The bytes of one wstring unit (UTF-16, DESIGN sec 8)
  ADAM_LOWERING_WIDE_UNIT: int64 = 2;
  // The prefix of a type's managed map's read-only data symbol (its data id follows): where
  // a record's or a static array's texts and dynamic arrays sit, as System.Runtime's
  // ManagedRelease / ManagedAssign read it (an int64 count of runs, then per run its first
  // offset, count, stride and element word: 0 texts, else the byte offset from the map's
  // start to the element map of the dynamic arrays it holds, after the runs)
  ADAM_LOWERING_MANAGED_MAP_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_managedmap";
  // The prefix of a choices type's names table's read-only data symbol (its data id
  // follows): System.Runtime's WriteChoice reads it (print of a choices value)
  ADAM_LOWERING_CHOICE_NAMES_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_choicenames";
  // The prefix of a pack item's facts' read-only data symbol (DoPackFacts; the data id
  // follows): System.Runtime's PackEntry.Facts
  ADAM_LOWERING_PACK_FACTS_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_packfacts";
  // The prefix of a placeholder spec's read-only data symbol (its data id follows) and the
  // values of its words, System.Runtime's ADAM_SPEC_* (its SinkSpec* routines read them,
  // M3.8f3); SpecWidth's argument kinds
  ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_spec";
  ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_ALIGN_DEFAULT: int64 = 0;
  ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_ALIGN_LEFT: int64 = 1;
  ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_ALIGN_CENTER: int64 = 2;
  ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_ALIGN_RIGHT: int64 = 3;
  ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_ALIGN_ZERO: int64 = 4;
  ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_SIGN_MINUS: int64 = 0;
  ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_SIGN_PLUS: int64 = 1;
  ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_SIGN_SPACE: int64 = 2;
  ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_WIDTH_SIGNED: int64 = 0;
  ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_WIDTH_UNSIGNED: int64 = 1;
  ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_WIDTH_NO_INTEGER: int64 = 2;
  // The prefix of a dynamic array type's element map's read-only data symbol (its data id
  // follows): the element's size, its build, copy and end routines (an address each, 0 for
  // none: DoElementRoutines), then the element type's managed map (System.Runtime's Arr*
  // routines read it)
  ADAM_LOWERING_ELEMENT_MAP_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_elementmap";
  // The words of an element map before its element type's managed map (the size, the
  // build, the copy, the end: System.Runtime's TArrElementMap)
  ADAM_LOWERING_ELEMENT_HEAD: int64 = 4;
  // The prefixes of the symbols of a dynamic array element type's routines (their index
  // follows; internal): the build (the element at its one parameter built), the copy (the
  // element at the second copied into the zeroed one at the first) and the end
  ADAM_LOWERING_ELEMENT_BUILD_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_elembuild";
  ADAM_LOWERING_ELEMENT_COPY_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_elemcopy";
  ADAM_LOWERING_ELEMENT_END_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_elemend";
  // The bytes of a dynamic array block's header before its elements (the ref count and the
  // length, both int64: System.Runtime's layout, a text's too)
  ADAM_LOWERING_ARRAY_HEADER: int64 = 16;
  // The words of one managed map run (offset, count, stride, element)
  ADAM_LOWERING_RUN_WORDS: int64 = 4;
  // A managed map run's element word for refs (System.Runtime's RefRelease ends each; an
  // element map's offset is never 1: the runs come before it)
  ADAM_LOWERING_REF_ELEMENT: int64 = 1;
  // A managed map run's element word for weaks (System.Runtime's WeakRelease gives each
  // back; never an element map's offset either)
  ADAM_LOWERING_WEAK_ELEMENT: int64 = 2;
  // A managed map run's element word for an own I / ref I (I3: its itable word's address;
  // System.Runtime's IntfRelease / IntfAddRef count it on its object's block); node 3 is
  // the tree's DerivedTypes, never an element map's array type
  ADAM_LOWERING_INTF_ELEMENT: int64 = 3;
  // The bytes of a ref block's header before its object (the ref count, the weak count,
  // the ref descriptor: System.Runtime's layout)
  ADAM_LOWERING_REF_HEADER: int64 = 24;
  // The prefix of an object type's ref descriptor's read-only data symbol (its data id
  // follows): the object's size, its done's address (0: none), then its managed map
  ADAM_LOWERING_REF_DESCRIPTOR_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_refdescriptor";
  // The prefix of the end function's symbol of an object type that declares no done
  // while its parts end by one (its function id follows; internal): the descriptor's done
  // word, it ends the parts (DoEndParts) of the object it is given
  ADAM_LOWERING_REF_END_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_refend";
  // A task's object (BNF sec 4 task type, System.Runtime's ADAM_RUNTIME_TASK_* words): the
  // runtime's seven words (the thread, the state, joined, the raise's code, its text at
  // ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_TEXT_OFFSET, the entry at ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_ENTRY_OFFSET, the cancel
  // word, T3), then the result (DoTaskResultOffset) and the call's copies (DoTaskLayout)
  ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_WORDS: int64 = 56;
  ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_TEXT_OFFSET: int64 = 32;
  ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_ENTRY_OFFSET: int64 = 40;
  // The prefix of an async call site's task descriptor's read-only data symbol (its data id
  // follows; a ref descriptor whose done is the runtime's TaskDone, or its task end:
  // DoTaskEndFunction)
  ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_DESCRIPTOR_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_taskdescriptor";
  // The prefix of an async call site's entry function's symbol (its index follows;
  // internal): TaskRun calls it with the task's object, it runs the call (DoTaskBody)
  ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_ENTRY_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_taskentry";
  // The prefix of an async call site's task end function's symbol (its index follows;
  // internal): the descriptor's done when the task's object holds value objects that end
  // by a done (DoTaskEndBody): TaskDone, then those values ended
  ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_END_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_taskend";
  // A generator's object (BNF sec 4 sequence type, G1; System.Runtime's
  // ADAM_RUNTIME_GENERATOR_* words): the runtime's nine words (its text and entry at the
  // task's offsets), then the value of its last yield (DoGeneratorValueOffset: placed by T
  // alone, so a for in over any sequence of T reads it), self's address for a method, then
  // the arguments' copies (DoGeneratorLayout)
  ADAM_LOWERING_GENERATOR_WORDS: int64 = 72;
  // The prefix of a generator's body function's symbol (its index follows; internal):
  // GeneratorRun calls it with the generator's object, it runs the routine's statements on
  // the generator's coroutine (DoGeneratorBody)
  ADAM_LOWERING_GENERATOR_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_generator";
  // The prefix of a for parallel's body function's symbol (its index follows; internal,
  // T2): System.Runtime's ParallelEntry, called per iteration with the loop's frame, the
  // iterator's value as 64 bits, the worker and the workers' count; true when the body
  // ran `leave` (DoParallelBody)
  ADAM_LOWERING_PARALLEL_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_parallel";
  // System.Runtime's ParallelRun flags (ADAM_RUNTIME_PARALLEL_*): a downto loop, unsigned
  // bounds, a workers' count written
  ADAM_LOWERING_PARALLEL_DOWNTO: int64 = 1;
  ADAM_LOWERING_PARALLEL_UNSIGNED: int64 = 2;
  ADAM_LOWERING_PARALLEL_GIVEN: int64 = 4;
  // The offset of a task's state word (System.Runtime's ADAM_RUNTIME_TASK_STATE) and the
  // state its call ended with when it returned (ADAM_RUNTIME_TASK_ENDED)
  ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_STATE_OFFSET: int64 = 8;
  ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_ENDED: int64 = 1;
  // The prefix of a polymorphic object type's vtable's read-only data symbol (its data id
  // follows; internal): one function address per slot (Layout's VtableSlots), the slot of
  // an abstract method the runtime's AbstractCall
  ADAM_LOWERING_VTABLE_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_vtable";
  // The prefix of an itable's read-only data symbol (I2; its data id follows; internal):
  // one per concrete object type and itable word (DoItableData)
  ADAM_LOWERING_ITABLE_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_itable";
  // The prefix of a forward's symbol (I4; its index follows; internal): an itable slot of
  // an interface method an embed's method fulfils, self moved to the embed
  // (DoForwardFunction)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FORWARD_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_forward";
  // The words of an itable before its slot 0 (DoItableData): the offset back from its
  // word to the object's start, then the interface's TypeInfo
  ADAM_LOWERING_ITABLE_HEADER: int64 = 2;

  // The prefixes of a module's initialize and finalize section functions' symbols (the
  // module's name follows; both internal)
  ADAM_LOWERING_INITIALIZE_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_initialize_";
  ADAM_LOWERING_FINALIZE_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_finalize_";
  // The prefix of a module's teardown function's symbol (the module's name follows;
  // internal): its finalize, then its module variables released, run at process exit
  ADAM_LOWERING_TEARDOWN_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_teardown_";
  // The prefixes of the three functions every unit's object defines for the program's
  // entry (SU2.4; the module's name follows; public): its variables' run-time inits (its
  // initializers that did not fold and its objects' builds, in declaration order), its
  // start (its initialize called, then its teardown registered as an exit handler) and
  // its thread release (the calling thread's copies of its managed threadstatics
  // released); each may be empty, so the entry calls every unit's without asking
  ADAM_LOWERING_VARINIT_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_varinit_";
  ADAM_LOWERING_START_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_start_";
  ADAM_LOWERING_UNIT_RELEASE_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_threadrelease_";
  // The prefix of the exe module's block function's symbol (its name follows; public: the
  // entry calls it, SU2.4)
  ADAM_LOWERING_BLOCK_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_block_";
  // The prefix of a test block's function's symbol (BNF sec 8; its module's name, "_" and
  // its index among the module's tests follow; public: the entry's test runner calls it)
  ADAM_LOWERING_TEST_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_test_";
  // The intrinsics an assert's name starts with (BNF sec 8: testAssert .. testFail)
  ADAM_LOWERING_ASSERT_PREFIX: string = "test";
  // The program parts' site list (SU2.4, DoSiteList): a uint64 count, then the address of
  // each unit's site table, which the entry hands to the runtime's HeapSiteList
  ADAM_LOWERING_SITELIST_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_sitelist";
  // The program parts' @addresdata table (DoResDataTable), which the entry hands to the
  // runtime's ResDataTable: a uint64 count, then per key in byte-wise key order its text's
  // address, its bytes' address and their count (uint64); the key texts NUL-ended in the
  // blob ADAM_LOWERING_RESDATA_KEYS_SYMBOL, each file's bytes and one zero byte after them
  // in the blob ADAM_LOWERING_RESDATA_SYMBOL, '_' and its place in the table
  ADAM_LOWERING_RESDATA_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_resdata";
  ADAM_LOWERING_RESDATA_KEYS_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_resdata_keys";
  // A data file's blob alignment (any reader may view it as wider words)
  ADAM_LOWERING_RESDATA_ALIGN: int64 = 16;
  // A unit's site table header bytes and where in it the runtime writes its base word
  // (DoSiteTable; System.Runtime's ADAM_RUNTIME_SITES_*)
  ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_HEADER: int64 = 32;
  ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_BASE: int64 = 24;
  // LowerUnit's AUnit for the program's parts (LowerProgramParts): no module is lowered,
  // every module is declared
  ADAM_LOWERING_PARTS: int64 = -1;

  // The prefix of a module constant's data blob symbol, when the constant is an aggregate
  // (its module's name, '_' and its own name follow; public: another unit's use of it is
  // a reference by this symbol, SU2.4)
  ADAM_LOWERING_CONST_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_const_";

  // The prefix of a constant set literal's read-only data symbol (its data id follows;
  // internal)
  ADAM_LOWERING_SET_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_set";

  // What a guard's finally funclet's symbol adds to its parent's (its function id follows;
  // internal)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FINALLY_SYMBOL: string = "$finally";
  // A function's cleanup funclet's symbol: the function's and this (DoCleanupFunclet)
  ADAM_LOWERING_CLEANUP_SYMBOL: string = "$cleanup";
  // A body copy's symbol: its declared function's and this (DoInlineCopy; internal), and
  // the most nodes a routine's subtree may have to be copied (DoCopyable)
  ADAM_LOWERING_INLINE_SYMBOL: string = "$inline";
  ADAM_LOWERING_COPY_NODES: int64 = 160;
  // A waiting jump's target when it is a return (DoPadJump): no block, the return's tail
  // after its last pad (DoPadReturn)
  ADAM_LOWERING_RETURN_PAD: int64 = -1;
  // The bytes (and alignment) of the slot a return's value waits in while the cleanups run
  // (DoEnterRegion): the largest IR value, an Int64, a Float64 or a pointer on Adam's
  // 64-bit targets
  ADAM_LOWERING_PAD_VALUE_BYTES: int64 = 8;
  // The directive that adds a library to the build (BNF sec 2), recorded on the IR module
  ADAM_LOWERING_DIRECTIVE_LINK: string = "@linklibrary";
  // The directive that builds a file into the binary under a key (BNF sec 2, DoResDataTable)
  ADAM_LOWERING_DIRECTIVE_RESDATA: string = "@addresdata";
  ADAM_LOWERING_DIRECTIVE_MESSAGE: string = "@message";
  ADAM_LOWERING_DIRECTIVE_BREAKPOINT: string = "@breakpoint";

  // Raised when a typed ptr's target or a static array's element has no size (Layout gave
  // none: a broken invariant, never a program's fault)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_ELEMENT_SIZE: string = "Lowering: no element size for the type ";
  // Raised when a static array's low bound has no value (Layout gave the type a size, so it
  // folded: a broken invariant)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_LOW_BOUND: string = "Lowering: no low bound for the static array ";
  // Raised when a static array's high bound has no folded value (an indexed element's
  // check, DoArrayElement; a range printed, DoRangeElements)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_HIGH_BOUND: string = "Lowering: no high bound for the static array ";
  // Raised when a record or a field has no layout (Layout gave none: a broken invariant)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_FIELD_OFFSET: string = "Lowering: no layout for the record or field ";
  // Raised when an object part whose every init takes arguments is built with no lead call
  // (SEM's SM0347 gives every init and copy of its holder one: a broken invariant)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_LEAD_INIT: string = "Lowering: no lead init call builds the part of type ";
  // Raised when a set literal reaches a set's value with no set type (SEM gives every set
  // literal one where a set is expected: a broken invariant)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_SET_TYPE: string = "Lowering: no set type for the set literal ";
  // Raised when a call whose value is an aggregate left no result slot (its routine's
  // result is an aggregate whenever SEM types the call so: a broken invariant)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_CALL_RESULT: string = "Lowering: no result slot for the call ";
  ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_HIDDEN_RESULT: string = "Lowering: no hidden result to return ";
  // A string temporary with no hidden slot (DoTemporaries and the lowering disagree)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_TEMP: string = "Lowering: no hidden slot for the string temporary ";
  // An argument a borrowed parameter needs held with no hold slot (DoArgHolds and
  // DoArgument disagree: a call shape DoCallSig does not map)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_HOLD: string = "Lowering: no hold slot for the borrowed argument ";
  // A write's anchor whose copy on write never ran (DoAnchorBegin waited for it: the
  // address reached the block another way)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_HOLD_WRITE: string = "Lowering: no copy on write held the anchor ";
  // A routine's write summary (SU2.8 e4, SummarizeWrites): its WriteEffects node's IntValue
  // bits. ALL: it may write anything (an unknown, external, dispatched or routine value
  // call somewhere below it, a write through a pointer, a release that may run a
  // polymorphic object's done); SELF: it writes through its own object (self or parent)
  ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_ALL: uint64 = 1;
  ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_SELF: uint64 = 2;
  // The most parameters a summary tracks by bit (one more is written as ALL)
  ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_PARAMS: int64 = 64;
  // A static array holding texts whose element count Layout did not give (it sized the
  // type, so the bounds folded: a broken invariant)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_ARRAY_COUNT: string = "Lowering: no element count for the static array ";
  // A dispatched method with no vtable slot (Layout numbers every virtual member: a
  // broken invariant)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_SLOT: string = "Lowering: no vtable slot for the method ";
  // An object converted to an interface it holds no itable word for (Semantics converts
  // only to one it or a level above implements, Layout gives each a word: a broken
  // invariant)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_ITABLE_WORD: string = "Lowering: no itable word for the interface ";
  // An indexed property read or written with no index (SEM reaches one only through an
  // index expression: a broken invariant)
  ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_PROPERTY_INDEX: string = "Lowering: no index for the indexed property ";

// True for the atomic intrinsics (BNF sec 7, H4t2): each one atomic op (DoAtomicOpOf)
routine DoIsAtomicIntrinsic(const AName: string): bool;
begin
  return (AName = "atomicadd") or (AName = "atomicswap") or (AName = "atomiccas") or
    (AName = "atomicload") or (AName = "atomicstore");
end;

// The atomic op the atomic intrinsic AName (DoIsAtomicIntrinsic) lowers to
routine DoAtomicOpOf(const AName: string): IrOp;
begin
  if AName = "atomicadd" then
    return IrOp.AtomicAdd;
  end;
  if AName = "atomicswap" then
    return IrOp.AtomicSwap;
  end;
  if AName = "atomiccas" then
    return IrOp.AtomicCas;
  end;
  if AName = "atomicload" then
    return IrOp.AtomicLoad;
  end;
  return IrOp.AtomicStore;
end;

// The VarKind value name (System.Runtime's VarKind) of the builtin type named AName; ""
// for a builtin no pack carries (varargs, mutex)
routine DoBuiltinKindName(const AName: string): string;
begin
  if AName = "int8" then
    return "Int8";
  end;
  if AName = "int16" then
    return "Int16";
  end;
  if AName = "int32" then
    return "Int32";
  end;
  if AName = "int64" then
    return "Int64";
  end;
  if AName = "uint8" then
    return "UInt8";
  end;
  if AName = "uint16" then
    return "UInt16";
  end;
  if AName = "uint32" then
    return "UInt32";
  end;
  if AName = "uint64" then
    return "UInt64";
  end;
  if AName = "clong" then
    return "CLong";
  end;
  if AName = "culong" then
    return "CULong";
  end;
  if AName = "float32" then
    return "Float32";
  end;
  if AName = "float64" then
    return "Float64";
  end;
  if AName = "bool" then
    return "Bool";
  end;
  if AName = "char" then
    return "Char";
  end;
  if AName = "wchar" then
    return "WChar";
  end;
  if AName = "string" then
    return "String";
  end;
  if AName = "wstring" then
    return "WString";
  end;
  if AName = "ptr" then
    return "Ptr";
  end;
  return "";
end;

// The module AModule (0: none) and every module it imports, theirs too, marked in AReached
// (by node id), each once
routine DoReach(const ATree: ref SyntaxTree; const AModule: int64; var AReached: BoolArray);
var
  LI: int64;
begin
  if (AModule = 0) or AReached[AModule] then
    return;
  end;
  AReached[AModule] := true;
  for LI := 0 to ATree.CountOf(AModule, NodeRole.Import) - 1 do
    DoReach(ATree, ATree[ATree.NthOf(AModule, NodeRole.Import, LI)].ResolvedUnit, AReached);
  end;
end;

public type
  // What a place's storage is rooted at (SU2.8 e4, PlacePath): None a value of the code's
  // own (a call's result, a literal, a constant); Own a local or a parameter by value;
  // Module a module variable; ByRef a var or by-reference parameter (the caller's place);
  // Receiver the object of a method (self, parent); Unknown any storage at all (a deref,
  // a ptr's element or member, a property's accessor, a cast)
  PathRoot = choices(None, Own, Module, ByRef, Receiver, Unknown);

  // What a walk over a static array's elements does to each (DoEachElement): Built by its
  // type's build, Ended by its end (the last first), Copied from the source array's
  // element at the same index (DoCopyValue)
  ElementWalk = choices(Built, Ended, Copied);

  // The form an assignment used as a value is read back in (DoAssignedValue): a scalar, a
  // managed value's block, an aggregate's address
  AssignedForm = choices(Scalar, Managed, Aggregate);

  // A place as SU2.8 e4 compares it (DoPlacePath): the fields, embeds and module variables
  // its storage lies in (Decls, Count of them), its root and the root's declaration
  // (Root: 0 for None, Receiver and Unknown)
  PlacePath = record
    Decls: array of int64;
    Count: int64;
    RootKind: PathRoot;
    Root: int64;
  end;

  // One lowering pass over a tree (see LowerUnit and the header)
  Lowerer = object
    hidden FTree: ref SyntaxTree;
    hidden FTarget: ref Target;
    hidden FDiagnostics: ref Diagnostics;
    hidden FModule: ref IrModule;
    // By node id (0: none): the function a routine or an initialize / finalize section
    // became, the external an external routine became (-1: refused once, not again), the
    // slot a parameter or a local lives in, whether a parameter is passed by reference (its
    // slot holds an address), and the data blob a module variable lives in
    hidden FFunctionOf: array of int64;
    hidden FExternalOf: array of int64;
    hidden FSlotOf: array of int64;
    hidden FByRef: array of bool;
    hidden FDataOf: array of int64;
    // By a local variable's node id: its slot was refused at its declaration (LW0001
    // reported there, DoLocalSlot), so a use of it reports nothing more
    hidden FSlotRefused: array of bool;
    // By a parameter's node id: an aggregate passed by value that the target sends as a
    // pointer to a copy the caller makes (FByRef is set too: the callee reaches it through
    // that address). By a routine's or an external's node id: its aggregate result comes
    // back through a hidden first parameter, the caller's slot (Target.AggregateInRegister)
    hidden FByCopy: array of bool;
    hidden FHiddenResult: array of bool;
    // By a canonical routine type's node id: the IR signature calls through its values
    // carry; by a dispatched method's node id: the IR signature its calls through a vtable
    // carry (0: none made yet, -1: refused once, not again)
    hidden FSignatureOf: array of int64;
    // The slot the current routine keeps its hidden result pointer in (0: it has none)
    hidden FResultSlot: int64;
    // The slot the current method keeps self in: the address of its object (0: the
    // current function is no method)
    hidden FSelfSlot: int64;
    // The slot a generator method's ramp keeps its hidden holder in (G1c2: the block of the
    // ref its call reached self through, nil for a self the ramp copies; 0: no such method)
    hidden FHolderSlot: int64;
    // The routine, method, init or done whose body is being lowered (0: the entry or a
    // section): a done ends its object's parts at each of its exits (DoExitParts)
    hidden FRoutine: int64;
    // The slot the current clink variadic routine keeps its varargs cursor in: the address
    // of the variadic argument its next varargs.next reads (0: it is not variadic)
    hidden FVarargsSlot: int64;
    // The slot the current cpplink variadic routine keeps the address of its typed pack's
    // header in (its hidden last parameter; 0: it has none)
    hidden FPackSlot: int64;
    // By a module variable's or constant's node id: its initializer's bytes were written
    // into its blob (DoConstBytes), so nothing runs for it at the entry
    hidden FDataWritten: array of bool;
    // The modules in run order, each after the modules it imports (DoOrderModule), and by
    // a module's node id whether it is placed in that order already
    hidden FOrder: ref Int64List;
    hidden FOrdered: BoolArray;
    // By a loop or match statement's node id (0: none yet): the block its leave jumps to
    // and the block a loop's skip jumps to (both made before its body is lowered; a leave /
    // skip's ResolvedJump names the statement)
    hidden FExitOf: array of int64;
    hidden FNextOf: array of int64;
    // The routines given a function, in AST order (their bodies are lowered after)
    hidden FRoutines: ref Int64List;
    // While an assignment used as a value is lowered (DoAssignedValue): by node id under its
    // target (FPinRoot), the address each place there got (the target's own included) and
    // the value each expression strictly below the target got, so reading the target back
    // makes none of them again (nil: no such assignment)
    hidden FPinned: ref Int64Map;
    hidden FPinRoot: int64;
    // Where code goes now: the function, its current block
    hidden FFunction: int64;
    hidden FBlock: int64;
    // The unit lowered alone (SU2.4, LowerUnit): its module node; ADAM_LOWERING_PARTS for
    // the program's parts (LowerProgramParts: the entry and what it hands the runtime)
    hidden FUnit: int64;
    // True while another unit's declarations are given their declared functions and
    // blobs (Run): nothing of them is lowered or reported here
    hidden FDeclaring: bool;
    // Each declared function another unit's routine became, its routine (DoRegister): the
    // ones a release build may copy the body of (DoInlineCopies)
    hidden FDeclaredRoutines: ref Int64Map;
    // True when the program has an entry to run a unit's initializers and sections (its
    // exe module's block, with the runtime's exit: DoFindEntry)
    hidden FHasEntry: bool;
    // By module node id: the runtime unit or a unit it imports (the platform unit, ...),
    // whose private routines and variables every unit's code may call (DoInternal)
    hidden FRuntimeUnits: BoolArray;
    // The exe module whose block is the entry's program block, and the function lowering
    // it (0: none): the parts' entry, or the main unit's block function, whose end block
    // (FEntryEnd) a return in the block goes to
    hidden FEntryModule: int64;
    hidden FEntry: int64;
    // The entry's last block (the finalize chain, then the runtime's exit), where the
    // program block's end and its returns go (0: none)
    hidden FEntryEnd: int64;
    // The current function's slots that hold texts it owns (its value text parameters and
    // the own copies of its managed aggregate ones, the hidden slots of its temporaries, its
    // managed locals), each released at every exit of the function (DoReleaseManaged), and
    // beside each the canonical type of what it holds (0: a text, any width); by an
    // expression's node id, the hidden slot its temporary lives in (DoTemporaries)
    hidden FManaged: ref Int64List;
    hidden FManagedType: ref Int64List;
    // Beside each of FManaged: its live flag's bool slot (DoAddManaged: one for a value
    // object that ends by a done, else 0), true while the slot holds a built object, so
    // the exits, an unwind and a full expression's end end it only then and a move (the
    // object's bytes taken by another slot) clears it (pcpp's truth: C++'s moved value is
    // never ended twice)
    hidden FManagedLive: ref Int64List;
    // By the node id of a local or a temporary (DoAddManaged's ANode): its live flag's slot
    // (0: none)
    hidden FLiveOf: array of int64;
    // The positions (in its Blocks) of the current function's exit blocks, where it
    // releases its FManaged at an exit (DoExitBlock): outside its cleanup scopes
    hidden FExitBlocks: ref Int64List;
    // The current function's protected regions being lowered, the innermost last (a guard
    // with a finally: its body and its except part; a lock's or a taken trylock's
    // statements: DoLock), whose cleanup (DoRegionCleanup) a jump out of one runs
    // on its way (DoJumpOut); and the jumps out of them waiting for their pads
    // (DoClosePads): by index, the jump, its target (a block, or ADAM_LOWERING_RETURN_PAD),
    // the loop or match it leaves (0: a return) and the depth in FRegions of the region it
    // waits on (-1 once its pad is made)
    hidden FRegions: ref Int64List;
    hidden FPadJumps: ref Int64List;
    hidden FPadTargets: ref Int64List;
    hidden FPadLoops: ref Int64List;
    hidden FPadDepths: ref Int64List;
    // The slot a return's value waits in while the cleanups run, made as the outermost
    // region is entered (DoEnterRegion; 0: none, the function gives no value), and the
    // value's IR type (the function's result type)
    hidden FPadValueSlot: int64;
    hidden FPadValueType: IrType;
    hidden FTempOf: array of int64;
    // By a temporary's node id (FTempOf): the canonical type its slot is released at when
    // its full expression ends (DoEndTemporary; 0: a text)
    hidden FTempTypeOf: array of int64;
    // By node id: true for a temporary that is an argument's hold (DoArgHolds: its value
    // with a holder of the call's own while a borrowed parameter has it, SU2.8 e3), not a
    // value the node makes; by a local's or a parameter's node id: true when its slot may
    // be reached from outside its routine's own code (DoPins: its address taken, passed to
    // a var parameter), so a callee could drop what it holds
    hidden FHeld: BoolArray;
    // By a hold's node id: the function it was made in (DoHoldSlot: one per node there)
    hidden FHeldIn: array of int64;
    hidden FUnpinned: BoolArray;
    // By an anchor's node id (DoAnchorOf: the ref, dynamic array or text whose block holds
    // the storage a callee is given the address of: self, a var or by-reference argument):
    // its value made and held for the call (DoAnchorBegin), handed to the address's own
    // reading of it (DoManagedValue) so it is read once; 0: none. FHoldAfter: a write's
    // anchor, held after its copy on write (ArrUnique / StrUnique) gives the block written
    hidden FPrimed: array of int64;
    hidden FHoldAfter: BoolArray;
    // By an anchor's node id: the function in which DoHoldAnchor left it unheld because no
    // callee of the access can drop its block (DoMayDrop, SU2.8 e4), so DoAnchorBegin takes
    // no hold there (0: none)
    hidden FDroppedIn: array of int64;
    // SummarizeWrites' state (SU2.8 e4; nothing else reads it). A slot per routine: by
    // routine node id its slot (FEffSlotOf, -1: none), by slot the routine (FEffRoutines),
    // its EFFECT bits (FEffFlags), its parameters written by bit (FEffParams), whether it
    // came from a summary already in the tree (FEffFixed: never rewritten), and its written
    // fields and module variables as bits over FEffDecls (FEffBits, FEffWords words a slot;
    // by declaration node id its bit, FEffDeclIndex). Before the words are known a write is
    // a pair (FEffLocalSlot, FEffLocalDecl). The calls and releases: by edge its routine's
    // slot, the routine run, the node that runs it (FEdgeFrom, FEdgeCallee, FEdgeSite; a
    // release's site 0). FReleaseMemo: by canonical type, what ending or copying a value of
    // it runs (DoReleaseRuns: 0 nothing, 1 known routines, 2 anything), FReleaseSeen the
    // types one DoReleaseRuns walk has met
    hidden FEffSlotOf: ref Int64Map;
    hidden FReleaseSeen: ref Int64Map;
    hidden FEffRoutines: ref Int64List;
    hidden FEffFlags: array of uint64;
    hidden FEffParams: array of uint64;
    hidden FEffFixed: BoolArray;
    hidden FEffDeclIndex: ref Int64Map;
    hidden FEffDecls: ref Int64List;
    hidden FEffWords: int64;
    hidden FEffBits: array of uint64;
    hidden FEffLocalSlot: ref Int64List;
    hidden FEffLocalDecl: ref Int64List;
    hidden FEdgeFrom: ref Int64List;
    hidden FEdgeCallee: ref Int64List;
    hidden FEdgeSite: ref Int64List;
    hidden FReleaseMemo: ref Int64Map;
    // SummarizeWrites' object family (SU2.8 e5): by object type its first direct
    // descendant's entry (FKidHead), by entry the descendant and the next entry (FKidType,
    // FKidNext; -1 ends); the object types a public alias names (FExposed), whose
    // descendants another module may declare
    hidden FKidHead: ref Int64Map;
    hidden FKidType: ref Int64List;
    hidden FKidNext: ref Int64List;
    hidden FExposed: ref Int64Map;
    // The allocation sites (M3.12b), by site number - 1 in the order Lowering met them: the
    // allocating construct's node and what it allocates ("string", "dynarray of int32" ...);
    // renumbered in source order at the end (DoNumberSites)
    hidden FSiteNodes: array of int64;
    hidden FSiteWhats: array of string;
    // By node id: the last site number made at that node (0: none), so the same construct
    // lowered again (a finally's copy, a pass of its own) keeps its one site (DoSiteOf)
    hidden FSiteOfNode: array of int64;
    // Every site id stored into GAllocSite (DoStoreSite): its Constant instruction and the
    // site number it holds before the renumbering (DoNumberSites patches its Imm)
    hidden FSiteStores: array of int64;
    hidden FSiteStoreOf: array of int64;
    // The site table's data blob (DoSiteData: made when first needed, the entry's address
    // of it before DoSiteTable writes its bytes); 0 until then
    hidden FSiteData: int64;
    // The site number of the construct being lowered around the current one (0: none): a
    // runtime call inside it (an argument's concatenation in a FormatStr) clears
    // GAllocSite back to it, not to 0, so the outer construct's later writes keep its site
    hidden FSiteOuter: int64;
    // By a print / println / FormatStr call's node id: one more than the index in
    // FRangeSlots of its first range scratch string (DoRangeTemporaries; 0: none), then one
    // per range level of its placeholders that is written into a scratch (a width or `?s`:
    // DoRangeNeedsScratch), the level's index added. Hidden string slots, emptied at the
    // function's start, released at its exits
    hidden FRangeScratchOf: array of int64;
    hidden FRangeSlots: ref Int64List;
    // By a canonical type's node id: the data blob of its managed map (DoManagedMap), and of
    // a dynamic array type's element map (DoElementMap); 0: none made yet, -1: refused
    // once, not again
    hidden FManagedMapOf: array of int64;
    hidden FElementMapOf: array of int64;
    // By a canonical choices type's node id: the data blob of its names table, print's
    // (DoChoiceNamesData); 0: none made yet
    hidden FChoiceNamesOf: array of int64;
    // By a canonical type's node id: the data blob of a pack item's facts (DoPackFacts),
    // its data id + 1; 0: none made yet
    hidden FPackFactsOf: array of int64;
    // By its text: the read-only C string blob a typed pack names a type or a member with
    // (DoPackText), its data id + 1
    hidden FPackTexts: ref StringIdMap;
    // By an object type's node id: the data blob of its ref descriptor (DoRefDescriptorData);
    // 0: none made yet, -1: refused once, not again
    hidden FDescriptorOf: array of int64;
    // By a polymorphic object type's node id: the data blob of its vtable (DoVtableData);
    // 0: none made yet, -1: refused once, not again
    hidden FVtableOf: array of int64;
    // By a concrete object type's node id times the tree's count plus the implements name
    // that made the word: the data blob of that word's itable (DoItableData, I2); -1:
    // refused once, not again
    hidden FItableOf: ref Int64Map;
    // By an object type's or an interface's node id: the data blob of its TypeInfo
    // (DoTypeInfo, I1); 0: none made yet
    hidden FTypeInfoOf: array of int64;
    // The end functions DoRefDescriptorData made (DoEndFunction), their bodies lowered
    // last (DoEndBodies): by index, the function, its object type, its node
    hidden FEndFunctions: ref Int64List;
    hidden FEndTypes: ref Int64List;
    hidden FEndNodes: ref Int64List;
    // The forwards DoItableData made (DoForwardFunction, I4), their bodies lowered last
    // (DoEndBodies: DoForwardBody): by index, the function, its concrete object type, its
    // Forward node, the interface method it runs for; FForwardOf by the type's node id
    // times the tree's count plus the Forward node: the function
    hidden FForwardFunctions: ref Int64List;
    hidden FForwardTypes: ref Int64List;
    hidden FForwardNodes: ref Int64List;
    hidden FForwardWants: ref Int64List;
    hidden FForwardOf: ref Int64Map;
    // How many forwards have their body (DoForwardBody): a release build's body copies may
    // ask for more after DoEndBodies (DoInlineCopies, then DoForwardBodies again)
    hidden FForwardsDone: int64;
    // The task entries DoAsync made (DoTaskEntry), their bodies lowered last
    // (DoDeferredBodies): by index, the function and its async expression
    hidden FTaskEntries: ref Int64List;
    hidden FTaskNodes: ref Int64List;
    // The slot a generator's body function keeps its object's address in (DoGeneratorBody;
    // a yield stores its value there, DoYield); 0 outside one
    hidden FGeneratorSlot: int64;
    // The for parallel bodies DoParallelFor made (DoParallelEntry, T2), lowered last
    // (DoParallelBodies): by index, the function, its for statement and whether its frame
    // starts with self (1: the routine holding it is a method's). FBodyRoot: the for
    // parallel or async block (T4) whose body is being lowered (0: none); FWorkerIndex /
    // FWorkerCount: a for parallel's
    // body's worker parameters, workerindex() / workercount() (0 outside one)
    hidden FParallelEntries: ref Int64List;
    hidden FParallelNodes: ref Int64List;
    hidden FParallelSelves: ref Int64List;
    hidden FBodyRoot: int64;
    hidden FWorkerIndex: int64;
    hidden FWorkerCount: int64;
    // The element routines DoElementRoutines made (DoElementFunction), their bodies lowered
    // last (DoEndBodies, DoElementBody): by index, the function, its element type, its
    // node and its walk (Built: the build, Copied: the copy, Ended: the end)
    hidden FElementFunctions: ref Int64List;
    hidden FElementTypes: ref Int64List;
    hidden FElementNodes: ref Int64List;
    hidden FElementWalks: array of ElementWalk;
    // By a canonical type's node id: its element routines (DoElementRoutines): 0 none made
    // yet, -1 its values run no code, -2 refused once, else the index + 1 of its three
    // words in FElementTriples (the build, the copy, the end: each a function id + 1, 0 for
    // none)
    hidden FElementRoutinesOf: array of int64;
    hidden FElementTriples: ref Int64List;
    // The task end functions DoTaskEndFunction made, their bodies lowered last
    // (DoEndBodies, DoTaskEndBody): by index, the function and its async expression
    hidden FTaskEndFunctions: ref Int64List;
    hidden FTaskEndNodes: ref Int64List;

    init(const ATree: ref SyntaxTree; const ATarget: ref Target; const ADiagnostics: ref Diagnostics;
      const AUnit: int64);
    begin
      self.FTree := ATree;
      self.FTarget := ATarget;
      self.FDiagnostics := ADiagnostics;
      self.FUnit := AUnit;
      self.FDeclaring := false;
      self.FHasEntry := false;
      setlength(self.FRuntimeUnits, ATree.Count);
      DoReach(ATree, ATree.Runtime, self.FRuntimeUnits);
      self.FModule := ref IrModule();
      self.FModule.Level := ATree.Level;
      setlength(self.FFunctionOf, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FExternalOf, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FSlotOf, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FByRef, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FDataOf, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FSlotRefused, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FByCopy, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FHiddenResult, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FSignatureOf, ATree.Count);
      self.FResultSlot := 0;
      self.FSelfSlot := 0;
      self.FHolderSlot := 0;
      self.FRoutine := 0;
      self.FVarargsSlot := 0;
      self.FPackSlot := 0;
      setlength(self.FDataWritten, ATree.Count);
      self.FOrder := ref Int64List();
      setlength(self.FOrdered, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FExitOf, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FNextOf, ATree.Count);
      self.FRoutines := ref Int64List();
      self.FPinned := nil;
      self.FPinRoot := 0;
      self.FDeclaredRoutines := ref Int64Map(0);
      self.FFunction := 0;
      self.FBlock := 0;
      self.FEntryModule := 0;
      self.FEntry := 0;
      self.FEntryEnd := 0;
      self.FSiteOuter := 0;
      self.FSiteData := 0;
      self.FManaged := ref Int64List();
      self.FManagedType := ref Int64List();
      self.FManagedLive := ref Int64List();
      self.FExitBlocks := ref Int64List();
      self.DoStartRegions();
      setlength(self.FTempOf, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FSiteOfNode, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FTempTypeOf, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FHeld, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FHeldIn, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FUnpinned, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FPrimed, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FHoldAfter, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FDroppedIn, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FLiveOf, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FRangeScratchOf, ATree.Count);
      self.FRangeSlots := ref Int64List();
      setlength(self.FManagedMapOf, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FElementMapOf, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FChoiceNamesOf, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FPackFactsOf, ATree.Count);
      self.FPackTexts := ref StringIdMap();
      setlength(self.FDescriptorOf, ATree.Count);
      setlength(self.FVtableOf, ATree.Count);
      self.FItableOf := ref Int64Map(0);
      setlength(self.FTypeInfoOf, ATree.Count);
      self.FEndFunctions := ref Int64List();
      self.FEndTypes := ref Int64List();
      self.FEndNodes := ref Int64List();
      self.FForwardFunctions := ref Int64List();
      self.FForwardTypes := ref Int64List();
      self.FForwardNodes := ref Int64List();
      self.FForwardWants := ref Int64List();
      self.FForwardOf := ref Int64Map(0);
      self.FForwardsDone := 0;
      self.FTaskEntries := ref Int64List();
      self.FTaskNodes := ref Int64List();
      self.FParallelEntries := ref Int64List();
      self.FParallelNodes := ref Int64List();
      self.FParallelSelves := ref Int64List();
      self.FBodyRoot := 0;
      self.FWorkerIndex := 0;
      self.FWorkerCount := 0;
      self.FElementFunctions := ref Int64List();
      self.FElementTypes := ref Int64List();
      self.FElementNodes := ref Int64List();
      setlength(self.FElementRoutinesOf, ATree.Count);
      self.FElementTriples := ref Int64List();
      self.FTaskEndFunctions := ref Int64List();
      self.FTaskEndNodes := ref Int64List();
    end;

    // The IR made so far
    property Lowered: ref IrModule read FModule;

    // LW0001 at AId: code generation does not handle AWhat yet; nothing while another
    // unit's declarations are declared (its own lowering reports them: Run)
    hidden method DoRefuse(const AId: int64; const AWhat: string);
    begin
      if self.FDeclaring then
        return;
      end;
      self.FDiagnostics.Add(Severity.Error, ADAM_ERR_LOWERING_001, self.FTree[AId].Place,
        ADAM_MSG_LOWERING_NOT_YET, NoArgs().Str(AWhat));
    end;

    // The IR type of an integer of ABits bits (signed with ASigned); Void for any other width
    hidden const method DoIntIr(const ABits: int64; const ASigned: bool): IrType;
    begin
      if ABits = 8 then
        if ASigned then
          return IrType.Int8;
        end;
        return IrType.UInt8;
      end;
      if ABits = 16 then
        if ASigned then
          return IrType.Int16;
        end;
        return IrType.UInt16;
      end;
      if ABits = 32 then
        if ASigned then
          return IrType.Int32;
        end;
        return IrType.UInt32;
      end;
      if ABits = 64 then
        if ASigned then
          return IrType.Int64;
        end;
        return IrType.UInt64;
      end;
      return IrType.Void;
    end;

    // The IR type a value of the canonical type AType travels as (a float32 / float64 as
    // the IR's floats); Void when the slice has none for it (a string, an aggregate, ...)
    hidden const method DoIrType(const AType: int64): IrType;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      if AType = 0 then
        return IrType.Void;
      end;
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if LClass = TypeClass.Boolean then
        return IrType.Bool;
      end;
      // A routine value is the routine's code address
      if IsPointerClass(LClass) or (LClass = TypeClass.RoutineType) then
        return IrType.Pointer;
      end;
      if LClass = TypeClass.SignedInt then
        return self.DoIntIr(IntBits(self.FTree, AType), true);
      end;
      if LClass = TypeClass.UnsignedInt then
        return self.DoIntIr(IntBits(self.FTree, AType), false);
      end;
      // char is C's char, wchar its wchar_t (DESIGN sec 6): the width and sign the target gives
      // them
      if (LClass = TypeClass.Char) or (LClass = TypeClass.WideChar) then
        return self.DoIntIr(CharTypeBits(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType),
          IsCharTypeSigned(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType));
      end;
      // A choices value is a signed integer of the size Layout gives the type
      if LClass = TypeClass.ChoicesType then
        return self.DoIntIr(TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType) * 8, true);
      end;
      if LClass = TypeClass.Float then
        if FloatBits(self.FTree, AType) = 32 then
          return IrType.Float32;
        end;
        return IrType.Float64;
      end;
      return IrType.Void;
    end;

    // The IR type of the canonical type AType, written at ANode; Void after LW0001 at
    // ANode naming the type when the slice has none for it
    hidden method DoTypeAt(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): IrType;
    var
      LIr: IrType;
    begin
      LIr := self.DoIrType(AType);
      if LIr = IrType.Void then
        self.DoRefuse(ANode, "type '" + TypeText(self.FTree, AType) + "'");
      end;
      return LIr;
    end;

    // The canonical type a parameter or a variable ADecl declares
    hidden const method DoDeclType(const ADecl: int64): int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[ADecl].ResolvedType <> 0 then
        return self.FTree[ADecl].ResolvedType;
      end;
      return CanonicalOf(self.FTree, self.FTree.FirstOf(ADecl, NodeRole.TypeOf));
    end;

    // The canonical type expression AId's value has where it is used: the type it converts
    // to, else its own
    hidden const method DoUsedType(const AId: int64): int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConvert <> 0 then
        return self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConvert;
      end;
      return self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType;
    end;

    // The integer IR type an aggregate of the canonical type AType (DoIsAggregate) crosses
    // a call as when the target passes its size in one register (Target.AggregateInRegister:
    // its bytes, unsigned, at its size); Void for any other aggregate (a pointer to a copy,
    // a hidden result pointer), for one that holds texts (it is copied by its text map, so
    // it always crosses by address: DoArgument, DoAggregateReturn) and for a type that is no
    // aggregate
    hidden method DoAggregateIr(const AType: int64): IrType;
    var
      LSize: int64;
    begin
      if (not self.DoIsAggregate(AType)) or self.DoHoldsManaged(AType) then
        return IrType.Void;
      end;
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType);
      if not self.FTarget.AggregateInRegister(LSize) then
        return IrType.Void;
      end;
      return self.DoIntIr(LSize * 8, false);
    end;

    // The canonical result type of the routine or external ARoutine (a read accessor: its
    // property's type); 0 for none
    hidden const method DoResultType(const ARoutine: int64): int64;
    var
      LTypeExpr: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[ARoutine].Kind = NodeKind.PropertyRead then
        return self.DoDeclType(self.FTree.ParentOf(ARoutine));
      end;
      LTypeExpr := self.FTree.FirstOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.ReturnType);
      if LTypeExpr = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return CanonicalOf(self.FTree, LTypeExpr);
    end;

    // The linkage of the signature ASig: a routine's or an external's (Symbols named it), a
    // method's C++ (DoHasSelf), a routine type expression's by Types.IsCppSignature
    // (`routine cpplink(...)`, else C: BNF sec 4, as its type's key reads it)
    hidden const method DoLinkageOf(const ASig: int64): Linkage;
    begin
      if self.FTree[ASig].ResolvedLinkage <> Linkage.Unset then
        return self.FTree[ASig].ResolvedLinkage;
      end;
      // a method is a C++ member function: its symbol mangles its parameters by C++
      // linkage (Symbols.DoEncoding), so they pass by C++'s rule too
      if self.DoHasSelf(ASig) then
        return Linkage.Cpp;
      end;
      if IsCppSignature(self.FTree, ASig) then
        return Linkage.Cpp;
      end;
      return Linkage.C;
    end;

    // The IR type parameter AParam of ARoutine travels as: its address when it is passed by
    // reference (FByRef); an aggregate by value in a register as that register's integer
    // (DoAggregateIr), any other aggregate as a pointer to the caller's copy (FByRef and
    // FByCopy; one that holds texts as the address of the caller's value, the callee
    // copying it: DoParams); a text or a dynamic array by value as its value (the callee
    // adds its own holder); Void after LW0001 at AParam
    hidden method DoParamIr(const ARoutine: int64; const AParam: int64): IrType;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
    begin
      if PassedByReference(self.FTree, AParam, self.DoLinkageOf(ARoutine)) then
        self.FByRef[AParam] := true;
        return IrType.Pointer;
      end;
      LType := self.DoDeclType(AParam);
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        LIr := self.DoAggregateIr(LType);
        if LIr <> IrType.Void then
          return LIr;
        end;
        self.FByRef[AParam] := true;
        self.FByCopy[AParam] := true;
        return IrType.Pointer;
      end;
      if self.DoIsManaged(LType) then
        return IrType.Pointer;
      end;
      return self.DoTypeAt(LType, AParam);
    end;

    // ARoutine's result IR type (Void for none): an aggregate in a register as that
    // register's integer (DoAggregateIr), any other aggregate as the hidden result pointer
    // it hands back (FHiddenResult); a text or a dynamic array as its value, a reference the
    // caller holds (DoReturn adds it, DoEmitCall keeps it in the call's hidden slot); true
    // unless its type was refused
    hidden method DoResultIr(const ARoutine: int64; var AResult: IrType): bool;
    var
      LType: int64;
    begin
      AResult := IrType.Void;
      LType := self.DoResultType(ARoutine);
      if LType = 0 then
        return true;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        AResult := self.DoAggregateIr(LType);
        // a value object that ends by a done or copies by a copy decl (DoHasLifetime)
        // always goes back through the hidden pointer (C++'s rule for a type that is not
        // trivial): the caller's slot is the result the callee moves or copies into, ended
        // once by the caller (its live flag)
        if self.DoHasLifetime(LType) then
          AResult := IrType.Void;
        end;
        if AResult = IrType.Void then
          self.FHiddenResult[ARoutine] := true;
          AResult := IrType.Pointer;
        end;
        return true;
      end;
      if self.DoIsManaged(LType) then
        AResult := IrType.Pointer;
        return true;
      end;
      // a read accessor has no ReturnType node: its type is refused at the accessor
      if self.FTree.FirstOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.ReturnType) = 0 then
        AResult := self.DoTypeAt(LType, ARoutine);
      else
        AResult := self.DoTypeAt(LType, self.FTree.FirstOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.ReturnType));
      end;
      return AResult <> IrType.Void;
    end;

    // True when every parameter of ARoutine has an IR type (each one refused is reported)
    hidden method DoParamsFit(const ARoutine: int64): bool;
    var
      LFit: bool;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LFit := true;
      for LI := 0 to self.DoParamCount(ARoutine) - 1 do
        if self.DoParamIr(ARoutine, self.DoParamAt(ARoutine, LI)) = IrType.Void then
          LFit := false;
        end;
      end;
      return LFit;
    end;

    // True when ARoutine is a method, an init, a copy, a done or a property accessor: its
    // function takes self (its object's address) as a hidden ptr parameter, after the
    // hidden result pointer and before the parameters (the Itanium C++ ABI's order, which
    // its symbol already follows); a routine type made from one too (Types.TakesSelf, the
    // one rule)
    hidden const method DoHasSelf(const ARoutine: int64): bool;
    begin
      return TakesSelf(self.FTree, ARoutine);
    end;

    // True when ARoutine is a generator method (G1c2): its function takes a hidden holder
    // after self, the block of the ref its call reached the object through (the generator
    // holds it), nil when the receiver is a value the ramp copies (only the call site knows
    // which). Known by its result alone (a sequence), so an abstract or an interface's
    // method is one too and every call path through a vtable or an itable passes it
    hidden const method DoGeneratorMethod(const ARoutine: int64): bool;
    var
      LResult: int64;
    begin
      if (ARoutine = 0) or (self.FTree[ARoutine].Kind <> NodeKind.MethodDecl) then
        return false;
      end;
      LResult := self.DoResultType(ARoutine);
      return (LResult <> 0) and (ClassOf(self.FTree, LResult) = TypeClass.SequenceType);
    end;

    // True when ARoutine is a property's read or write accessor
    hidden const method DoIsAccessor(const ARoutine: int64): bool;
    begin
      return (self.FTree[ARoutine].Kind = NodeKind.PropertyRead) or
        (self.FTree[ARoutine].Kind = NodeKind.PropertyWrite);
    end;

    // True when the accessor AAccessor is bound to a field (`read F` / `write F`: SEM wrote
    // the field to its ResolvedDecl) rather than given a body or left abstract
    hidden const method DoIsBound(const AAccessor: int64): bool;
    begin
      return (AAccessor <> 0) and (self.FTree[AAccessor].Text <> "");
    end;

    // How many parameters ARoutine's function takes after its hidden result and self
    // (DoParamAt names each): a routine's or a method's own; an accessor's are its
    // property's index first, then a write's value (Symbols' DoAccessorParams order)
    hidden const method DoParamCount(const ARoutine: int64): int64;
    var
      LCount: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoIsAccessor(ARoutine) then
        return self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param);
      end;
      LCount := self.FTree.CountOf(self.FTree.ParentOf(ARoutine), NodeRole.Param);
      if self.FTree[ARoutine].Kind = NodeKind.PropertyWrite then
        LCount := LCount + 1;
      end;
      return LCount;
    end;

    // The declaration of ARoutine's parameter AIndex (0-based, DoParamCount's order). A
    // write accessor's value is its Param node `write (AValue)`; a bound write has none,
    // so its property stands for it (the value has the property's type and no mode, and
    // no name refers to it: its slot is the bound body's alone, DoBoundAccessor), and so does
    // an interface's write (`write;`, I3: its calls run through the itable)
    hidden const method DoParamAt(const ARoutine: int64; const AIndex: int64): int64;
    var
      LProperty: int64;
      LIndexCount: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoIsAccessor(ARoutine) then
        return self.FTree.NthOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param, AIndex);
      end;
      LProperty := self.FTree.ParentOf(ARoutine);
      LIndexCount := self.FTree.CountOf(LProperty, NodeRole.Param);
      if AIndex < LIndexCount then
        return self.FTree.NthOf(LProperty, NodeRole.Param, AIndex);
      end;
      if self.DoIsBound(ARoutine) or self.DoIsInterfaceMember(ARoutine) then
        return LProperty;
      end;
      return self.FTree.FirstOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param);
    end;

    // ARoutine's parameters' IR types added to ASignature, in order, after the hidden
    // result pointer when it has one (DoResultIr and DoParamsFit first), a method's self
    // (DoHasSelf) and a generator method's holder (DoGeneratorMethod); a cpplink variadic (DoIsPackVariadic) then takes its pack's header as
    // one more ptr, a clink one is variadic (its calls pass the extra arguments after these)
    hidden method DoFillSignature(const ARoutine: int64; const ASignature: ref IrSignature);
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if self.FHiddenResult[ARoutine] then
        ASignature.AddParam(IrType.Pointer);
      end;
      if self.DoHasSelf(ARoutine) then
        ASignature.AddParam(IrType.Pointer);
      end;
      if self.DoGeneratorMethod(ARoutine) then
        ASignature.AddParam(IrType.Pointer);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.DoParamCount(ARoutine) - 1 do
        ASignature.AddParam(self.DoParamIr(ARoutine, self.DoParamAt(ARoutine, LI)));
      end;
      if self.DoIsPackVariadic(ARoutine) then
        ASignature.AddParam(IrType.Pointer);
        ASignature.Variadic := false;
        return;
      end;
      ASignature.Variadic := self.FTree[ARoutine].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Variadic);
    end;

    // True when the signature ASig (a routine, an external, a routine type's) is variadic
    // with C++ linkage: its extra arguments travel in a typed pack (BNF sec 6)
    hidden const method DoIsPackVariadic(const ASig: int64): bool;
    begin
      return self.FTree[ASig].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Variadic) and (self.DoLinkageOf(ASig) = Linkage.Cpp);
    end;

    // True when the signature ASig (a routine, an external, a routine type's) is one the
    // slice lowers or calls; LW0001 at ANode naming why not: generic
    hidden method DoPlainSignature(const ASig: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    begin
      if self.FTree.CountOf(ASig, NodeRole.GenericParam) > 0 then
        self.DoRefuse(ANode, "a generic " + self.FTree.ConstructText(ASig));
        return false;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // True when ARoutine (a routine or an external) is one the slice lowers or calls
    // (DoPlainSignature, reported at ARoutine)
    hidden method DoPlainRoutine(const ARoutine: int64): bool;
    begin
      return self.DoPlainSignature(ARoutine, ARoutine);
    end;

    // The routine ARoutine (with a body) given its function, its body lowered later
    hidden method DoRegister(const ARoutine: int64);
    var
      LResult: IrType;
      LFunction: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoPlainRoutine(ARoutine) then
        return;
      end;
      if not self.DoResultIr(ARoutine, LResult) then
        return;
      end;
      if not self.DoParamsFit(ARoutine) then
        return;
      end;
      LFunction := self.FModule.AddFunction(self.FTree[ARoutine].ResolvedSymbol, LResult, ARoutine);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Internal := self.DoInternal(ARoutine);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).NoReturn := self.FTree[ARoutine].HasFlag(NodeFlag.NoReturn);
      self.DoFillSignature(ARoutine, self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature);
      self.FFunctionOf[ARoutine] := LFunction;
      // another unit's routine: its code is that unit's object's, a call refers to it
      if self.FDeclaring then
        self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Declared := true;
        self.FDeclaredRoutines.Put(LFunction, ARoutine);
        return;
      end;
      self.FRoutines.Add(ARoutine);
    end;

    // The external the external routine ADecl became, made the first time; 0 when it was
    // refused (reported once, at ADecl)
    hidden method DoExternal(const ADecl: int64): int64;
    var
      LResult: IrType;
      LClause: int64;
      LLibrary: string;
      LExternal: int64;
    begin
      if self.FExternalOf[ADecl] > 0 then
        return self.FExternalOf[ADecl];
      end;
      if self.FExternalOf[ADecl] < 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.FExternalOf[ADecl] := -1;
      if not self.DoPlainRoutine(ADecl) then
        return 0;
      end;
      if not self.DoResultIr(ADecl, LResult) then
        return 0;
      end;
      if not self.DoParamsFit(ADecl) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LClause := self.FTree.FirstOf(ADecl, NodeRole.External);
      LLibrary := "";
      if self.FTree[LClause].ResolvedConst.Kind = ConstKind.String then
        LLibrary := self.FTree[LClause].ResolvedConst.Text;
      end;
      LExternal := self.FModule.AddExternal(self.FTree[ADecl].ResolvedSymbol, LLibrary, LResult, ADecl);
      self.DoFillSignature(ADecl, self.FModule.ExternalAt(LExternal).Signature);
      self.FModule.ExternalAt(LExternal).NoReturn := self.FTree[ADecl].HasFlag(NodeFlag.NoReturn);
      self.FExternalOf[ADecl] := LExternal;
      return LExternal;
    end;

    // True when the routine or module variable ADecl's symbol is its object's alone: it
    // binds an internal symbol (Symbols.HasInternalSymbol: a module's private one) and its
    // module is no runtime unit (FRuntimeUnits: code Lowering makes in every unit calls
    // the runtime's private routines and stores into its variables, SU2.4, so their
    // objects keep them public under the same names)
    hidden const method DoInternal(const ADecl: int64): bool;
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      if not HasInternalSymbol(self.FTree, ADecl) then
        return false;
      end;
      LAt := ADecl;
      while (LAt <> 0) and (self.FTree.ParentOf(LAt) <> ADAM_AST_PROGRAM) do
        LAt := self.FTree.ParentOf(LAt);
      end;
      return (LAt = 0) or not self.FRuntimeUnits[LAt];
    end;

    // A new read-only blob Lowering makes for its own use (a text, a map, a vtable ...),
    // named by APrefix and its data id, internal: each unit's object has its own (SU2.4),
    // so two units' blobs never meet at the link; returns its id
    hidden method DoHelperData(const APrefix: string; const AAlign: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LData: int64;
    begin
      LData := self.FModule.AddData(APrefix + IntToStr(self.FModule.DataCount), AAlign, ANode);
      self.FModule.DataAt(LData).Internal := true;
      return LData;
    end;

    // True when the current block ends in a call of a noreturn function or external (its
    // routine written noreturn: BNF sec 3), which no terminator follows yet
    hidden const method DoEndsNoReturn(): bool;
    var
      LInstrs: ref Int64List;
      LLast: ref IrInstr;
    begin
      LInstrs := self.FModule.BlockAt(self.FBlock).Instrs;
      if LInstrs.Count = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LLast := self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstrs[LInstrs.Count - 1]);
      if LLast.Kind = IrOp.Call then
        return self.FModule.FunctionAt(LLast.Link).NoReturn;
      end;
      if LLast.Kind = IrOp.CallExternal then
        return self.FModule.ExternalAt(LLast.Link).NoReturn;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // The current block, when it ends in a noreturn call, ended there by an Unreachable at
    // that call's node (control never comes back to it); true when it was
    hidden method DoCloseNoReturn(): bool;
    var
      LInstrs: ref Int64List;
    begin
      if not self.DoEndsNoReturn() then
        return false;
      end;
      LInstrs := self.FModule.BlockAt(self.FBlock).Instrs;
      self.FModule.Emit(self.FBlock, IrOp.Unreachable, IrType.Void,
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstrs[LInstrs.Count - 1]).Node);
      return true;
    end;

    // A new instruction of AKind and AType at the end of the current block, for ANode;
    // after a noreturn call the block is ended (DoCloseNoReturn) and the instruction goes
    // to a new block nothing jumps to, as code after a return does (DoStatement)
    hidden method DoEmit(const AKind: IrOp; const AType: IrType; const ANode: int64): int64;
    begin
      if self.DoCloseNoReturn() then
        self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      end;
      return self.FModule.Emit(self.FBlock, AKind, AType, ANode);
    end;

    // A constant AValue of AType
    hidden method DoConstant(const AType: IrType; const AValue: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Constant, AType, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Imm := AValue;
      return LId;
    end;

    // The value of AType at the address AAddress
    hidden method DoLoad(const AAddress: int64; const AType: IrType; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Load, AType, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(AAddress);
      return LId;
    end;

    // AValue stored at the address AAddress
    hidden method DoStore(const AAddress: int64; const AValue: int64; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Store, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(AAddress);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(AValue);
    end;

    // The stack slot ADecl lives in: an address's size when it holds one (AByRef), else
    // its canonical type AType's; 0 after LW0001 when that type has no size
    hidden method DoSlot(const ADecl: int64; const AType: int64; const AByRef: bool): int64;
    var
      LSize: int64;
      LAlign: int64;
    begin
      if AByRef then
        LSize := self.FTarget.PointerSize();
        LAlign := self.FTarget.PointerAlign();
      else
        LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType);
        LAlign := TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType);
      end;
      if (LSize <= 0) or (LAlign <= 0) then
        self.DoRefuse(ADecl, "type '" + TypeText(self.FTree, AType) + "'");
        return 0;
      end;
      self.FSlotOf[ADecl] := self.DoSizedSlot(ADecl, LSize, LAlign);
      return self.FSlotOf[ADecl];
    end;

    // A stack slot of ASize bytes aligned to AAlign, made at ANode (FSlotOf is the caller's
    // to set: a pack's slots are no node's)
    hidden method DoSizedSlot(const ANode: int64; const ASize: int64; const AAlign: int64): int64;
    var
      LId: int64;
    begin
      // A slot aligned above the target's stack alignment is the arch's to honour (a
      // realigned frame: Adam.Backend.Parts' FrameLayout.Realign)
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Slot, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Imm := ASize;
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Align := AAlign;
      return LId;
    end;

    // True when the current block ends in a terminator
    hidden const method DoEnded(): bool;
    var
      LInstrs: ref Int64List;
    begin
      LInstrs := self.FModule.BlockAt(self.FBlock).Instrs;
      if LInstrs.Count = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      return IsTerminator(self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstrs[LInstrs.Count - 1]).Kind);
    end;

    // The address of module variable ADecl's data blob (DoGlobal), emitted for ANode: the
    // calling thread's copy (a ThreadAddress) of a thread-local one (DoThreadStatic)
    hidden method DoDataAddress(const ADecl: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LId: int64;
    begin
      if self.FModule.DataAt(self.FDataOf[ADecl]).ThreadLocal then
        LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.ThreadAddress, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      else
        LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      end;
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Link := self.FDataOf[ADecl];
      return LId;
    end;

    // True when AId is a deref, prefix `*P` or postfix `P^` (its operand's value is the
    // address it names)
    hidden const method DoIsDeref(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LKind: NodeKind;
    begin
      LKind := self.FTree[AId].Kind;
      return ((LKind = NodeKind.UnaryExpression) or (LKind = NodeKind.PostfixExpression)) and
        (self.FTree[AId].Op = OperatorKind.Deref);
    end;

    // True when expression AId names storage DoAddress reaches (a name, a deref, an index, a
    // member), so its value is a load from there. A property is storage only as its bound
    // field (DoBoundField, through a member access); any other property access is a call
    // of its accessors (DoIsPropertyAccess)
    hidden const method DoIsPlace(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LKind: NodeKind;
    begin
      LKind := NameKindOf(self.FTree, AId);
      if ((LKind = NodeKind.MemberExpression) or (LKind = NodeKind.IndexExpression)) and self.DoNamesProperty(AId) then
        return (LKind = NodeKind.MemberExpression) and (self.DoBoundField(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedDecl) <> 0);
      end;
      return (LKind = NodeKind.NameExpression) or (LKind = NodeKind.IndexExpression) or
        (LKind = NodeKind.MemberExpression) or self.DoIsDeref(AId) or
        (LKind = NodeKind.SelfExpression) or (LKind = NodeKind.ParentExpression) or
        self.DoIsAsObject(AId);
    end;

    // True when the member or index expression AId reads or writes a property (SEM's
    // ResolvedDecl: X.P, X.P[i], a default X[i])
    hidden const method DoNamesProperty(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      LDecl := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedDecl;
      return (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.PropertyDecl);
    end;

    // The field the property AProperty is as a whole, when it is no more than that field:
    // not dispatched, no index, its read bound to the field and its write (if any) bound
    // to the same one, the field no bitfield; 0 otherwise (its accessors are called,
    // DoPropertyGet / DoPropertySet)
    hidden const method DoBoundField(const AProperty: int64): int64;
    var
      LRead: int64;
      LWrite: int64;
      LField: int64;
    begin
      if self.DoIsDispatched(AProperty) or (self.FTree.FirstOf(AProperty, NodeRole.Param) <> 0) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LRead := self.FTree.FirstOf(AProperty, NodeRole.Read);
      if not self.DoIsBound(LRead) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LField := self.FTree[LRead].ResolvedDecl;
      if (LField = 0) or (self.FTree[LField].ResolvedBitWidth >= 0) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LWrite := PropertyWriteOf(self.FTree, AProperty);
      if (LWrite <> 0) and ((not self.DoIsBound(LWrite)) or (self.FTree[LWrite].ResolvedDecl <> LField)) then
        return 0;
      end;
      return LField;
    end;

    // The field the member access AMember names as storage: its field, its embed (BNF sec 4:
    // an embed is a field, `self.Place` its storage), or the field its property is as a
    // whole (DoBoundField); 0 for anything else
    hidden const method DoMemberField(const AMember: int64): int64;
    var
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      LDecl := self.FTree[AMember].ResolvedDecl;
      if LDecl = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.FieldDecl) or (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.EmbedDecl) then
        return LDecl;
      end;
      if self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.PropertyDecl then
        return self.DoBoundField(LDecl);
      end;
      return 0;
    end;

    // True when AId (through no parentheses) is a property access through its accessors
    // (a member or an index expression naming a property that is no place: DoIsPlace)
    hidden const method DoIsPropertyAccess(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LKind: NodeKind;
    begin
      LKind := self.FTree[AId].Kind;
      return ((LKind = NodeKind.MemberExpression) or (LKind = NodeKind.IndexExpression)) and
        self.DoNamesProperty(AId) and (not self.DoIsPlace(AId));
    end;

    // The byte size of one element of the canonical type AType: what a typed ptr points to,
    // or a static array's element (its target: a canonical derived type holds it,
    // Types.TargetOf); a target with no size faults (Layout sizes every declared type, a
    // forward type through its full declaration, so a missing size is a broken invariant)
    hidden const method DoElementSize(const AType: int64): int64;
    var
      LSize: int64;
    begin
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, TargetOf(self.FTree, AType));
      if LSize < 0 then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_ELEMENT_SIZE + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
      end;
      return LSize;
    end;

    // The ptr APointer moved by ACount (an integer value of any width) elements of AType (a
    // typed ptr type, or a static array type whose start APointer is), backwards when ABack,
    // at ANode: the count widened to int64 by its own signedness, times the element's size
    // (DoElementSize), as one offset (BNF sec 4: `P + n` moves P)
    hidden method DoMovePointer(const APointer: int64; const ACount: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ABack: bool; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LBytes: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LScale: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      // every operand is emitted before the instruction that uses it
      LBytes := self.DoConvertIr(ACount, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LSize := self.DoElementSize(AType);
      if LSize <> 1 then
        LScale := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LSize, ANode);
        LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Mul, IrType.Int64, ANode);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LBytes);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LScale);
        LBytes := LId;
      end;
      if ABack then
        LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Neg, IrType.Int64, ANode);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LBytes);
        LBytes := LId;
      end;
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Offset, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(APointer);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LBytes);
      return LId;
    end;

    // The index check (M3.11a; DESIGN sec 5: kept at debug and safe, none at fast and small:
    // OptLevelKeepsIndexChecks) of a static array's index AIndex (widened to int64) whose
    // position APosition is AIndex less the low bound ALow: one unsigned compare of the
    // position with AHigh - ALow; outside, a block of its own calls the runtime's IndexFail
    // (code 14, `index N is out of bounds L..H`), which never returns (the block still ends
    // in a jump, as every block does). False after LW0001
    hidden method DoCheckBounds(const AIndex: int64; const APosition: int64; const ALow: int64;
      const AHigh: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LInRange: int64;
      LBad: int64;
      LGood: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
    begin
      if not OptLevelKeepsIndexChecks(self.FTree.Level) then
        return true;
      end;
      LInRange := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.ULessEqual, self.DoConvertIr(APosition, IrType.UInt64, ANode),
        self.DoConstant(IrType.UInt64, AHigh - ALow, ANode), ANode);
      LBad := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LGood := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(LInRange, LGood, LBad, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LBad;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(AIndex);
      LArgs.Add(self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, ALow, ANode));
      LArgs.Add(self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, AHigh, ANode));
      if self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.IndexFail, LArgs, ANode) = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoJumpTo(LGood, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LGood;
      return true;
    end;

    // The index check (M3.11a; DESIGN sec 5: kept at debug and safe, none at fast and small:
    // OptLevelKeepsIndexChecks) of the index AIndex (an int64, counted from 0) into the
    // block ABlock of a string, a wstring or a dynamic array (nil when empty): a nil block
    // holds nothing; a held one's length (ADAM_LOWERING_BLOCK_LENGTH) above the index, one
    // unsigned compare (a negative index is past every length). Outside, a block of its own
    // calls the runtime's IndexFailIn (code 14, the block's bounds or `it is empty`), which
    // never returns. False after LW0001
    hidden method DoCheckLength(const ABlock: int64; const AIndex: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LHeld: int64;
      LBad: int64;
      LInBlock: int64;
      LGood: int64;
      LLength: int64;
      LInRange: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
    begin
      if not OptLevelKeepsIndexChecks(self.FTree.Level) then
        return true;
      end;
      LHeld := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.NotEqual, ABlock, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ANode), ANode);
      LBad := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LInBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LGood := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(LHeld, LInBlock, LBad, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LInBlock;
      LLength := self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(ABlock, ADAM_LOWERING_BLOCK_LENGTH, ANode), IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LInRange := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.ULess, self.DoConvertIr(AIndex, IrType.UInt64, ANode),
        self.DoConvertIr(LLength, IrType.UInt64, ANode), ANode);
      self.DoBranchOn(LInRange, LGood, LBad, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LBad;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(AIndex);
      LArgs.Add(ABlock);
      if self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.IndexFailIn, LArgs, ANode) = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoJumpTo(LGood, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LGood;
      return true;
    end;

    // The address of the element of the static array AArray (of the canonical type AType)
    // the index expression AId names: the array's address first, then the index widened to
    // int64 by its own signedness (a char or a wchar by the target's, as its bounds are
    // read) less the low bound, moved over by that many elements (DoMovePointer). A record's
    // or an array's element is reached the same way, its own fields or elements from there.
    // AWrite: DoAddressFor's write form, passed to the array's own address. 0 after LW0001;
    // a low bound with no value faults
    hidden method DoArrayElement(const AId: int64; const AArray: int64; const AType: int64;
      const AWrite: bool): int64;
    var
      LBase: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LWide: int64;
      LPosition: int64;
      LLow: int64;
      LHigh: int64;
      LLowValue: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LBase := self.DoAddressFor(AArray, AWrite);
      if LBase = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LIndex := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Index));
      if LIndex = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LWide := self.DoConvertIr(LIndex, IrType.Int64, AId);
      LPosition := LWide;
      if not BoundValue(self.FTree, self.FTarget, self.FTree.FirstOf(self.FTree[AType].ResolvedDecl,
        NodeRole.LowBound), LLow) then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_LOW_BOUND + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
      end;
      if not BoundValue(self.FTree, self.FTarget, self.FTree.FirstOf(self.FTree[AType].ResolvedDecl,
        NodeRole.HighBound), LHigh) then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_HIGH_BOUND + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
      end;
      if LLow <> 0 then
        // every operand is emitted before the instruction that uses it
        LLowValue := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LLow, AId);
        LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Sub, IrType.Int64, AId);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LPosition);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LLowValue);
        LPosition := LId;
      end;
      if not self.DoCheckBounds(LWide, LPosition, LLow, LHigh, AId) then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoMovePointer(LBase, LPosition, AType, false, AId);
    end;

    // The address of the element the index expression AId names: on a typed ptr, the ptr
    // moved by the index (`P[i]` is `(P + i)^`, P first, then i); on a static array, its
    // element (DoArrayElement); on a dynamic array, its element (DoDynamicElement); on a
    // string, its byte (DoStringElement); AWrite: DoAddressFor's write form; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoElementAddress(const AId: int64; const AWrite: bool): int64;
    var
      LOperand: int64;
      LPtrType: int64;
      LBase: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
    begin
      LOperand := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand);
      LPtrType := self.DoUsedType(LOperand);
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, LPtrType) = TypeClass.StaticArray then
        return self.DoArrayElement(AId, LOperand, LPtrType, AWrite);
      end;
      if self.DoIsArrayValue(LPtrType) then
        return self.DoDynamicElement(AId, AWrite);
      end;
      if self.DoIsText(LPtrType) then
        return self.DoStringElement(AId, AWrite);
      end;
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, LPtrType) <> TypeClass.Pointer then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LBase := self.DoValue(LOperand);
      if LBase = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LIndex := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Index));
      if LIndex = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoMovePointer(LBase, LIndex, LPtrType, false, AId);
    end;

    // The address of the element of a dynamic array the index expression AId names (the
    // array's index starts at 0): the array first, then the index, moved over by that many
    // elements from the block's first (DoMovePointer). To read it, the array's value (a
    // borrowed one); to write it (AWrite: DoAddressFor's write form), the array's own place
    // in its write form, its block made the place's alone first (ArrUnique with the type's
    // element map: copy on write). The index is checked against the block's length
    // (DoCheckLength, M3.11a); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoDynamicElement(const AId: int64; const AWrite: bool): int64;
    var
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LOperand: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LMap: int64;
      LBase: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
    begin
      LOperand := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand);
      LType := self.DoUsedType(LOperand);
      if AWrite then
        LSlot := self.DoAddressFor(LOperand, true);
        if LSlot = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LMap := self.DoElementMap(LType, AId);
        if LMap = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LArgs := ref Int64List();
        LArgs.Add(LSlot);
        LArgs.Add(LMap);
        LBase := self.DoCallRuntimeSite(RuntimeRoutine.ArrUnique, LArgs, AId,
          self.DoArrayWhat(LType));
        if not self.DoHoldWritten(LOperand, LBase, LType, AId) then
          return 0;
        end;
      else
        LBase := self.DoValue(LOperand);
      end;
      if LBase = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LIndex := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Index));
      if LIndex = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LIndex := self.DoConvertIr(LIndex, IrType.Int64, AId);
      if not self.DoCheckLength(LBase, LIndex, AId) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LBase := self.DoByteOffset(LBase, ADAM_LOWERING_ARRAY_HEADER, AId);
      return self.DoMovePointer(LBase, LIndex, LType, false, AId);
    end;

    // True when the canonical type AType is a record or an overlay: an aggregate of fields
    // that lives in a slot or a blob and is reached by its address, never an SSA value. An
    // overlay is its fields' shared storage (Layout gives each field its offset, 0 at the
    // overlay's own level), so it zeroes, copies and reaches its fields exactly as a record
    // does; its fields inside anonymous parts are found and placed by MemberOf and Layout.
    // An object by value is one too (M3.10a): its fields where Layout puts them (after the
    // vptr of a polymorphic one), its parent part first, its methods functions taking its
    // address (DoHasSelf)
    hidden const method DoIsFieldAggregate(const AType: int64): bool;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      if AType = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      return (LClass = TypeClass.RecordType) or (LClass = TypeClass.OverlayType) or
        (LClass = TypeClass.ObjectType);
    end;

    // The canonical type the field or embed AMember of an object holds
    hidden const method DoPartType(const AMember: int64): int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AMember].Kind = NodeKind.EmbedDecl then
        return CanonicalOf(self.FTree, self.FTree.FirstOf(AMember, NodeRole.TypeOf));
      end;
      return self.DoDeclType(AMember);
    end;

    // The member of kind AKind (an init, a done, a copy) that the object type AType's own
    // body declares first, 0 for none (an inherited one is the parent part's)
    hidden const method DoOwnMember(const AType: int64; const AKind: NodeKind): int64;
    var
      LBody: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, AType);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
        LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
        if self.FTree[LMember].Kind = AKind then
          return LMember;
        end;
      end;
      return 0;
    end;

    // True when a value of the canonical type AType holds, at any depth, an object whose
    // type declares a member of kind AKind: an init (it must be built), a done (it must be
    // ended), a copy (it copies by it). Through a static array's element, an object's
    // parent chain, its fields and embeds; a record holds no object (BNF sec 4)
    hidden const method DoHoldsMember(const AType: int64; const AKind: NodeKind): bool;
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LDepth: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.StaticArray then
        return self.DoHoldsMember(TargetOf(self.FTree, AType), AKind);
      end;
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) <> TypeClass.ObjectType then
        return false;
      end;
      LAt := AType;
      LDepth := 0;
      while (LAt <> 0) and (LDepth <= ADAM_TYPES_MAX_DEPTH) do
        if self.DoOwnMember(LAt, AKind) <> 0 then
          return true;
        end;
        LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, LAt);
        for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
          LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
          LKind := self.FTree[LMember].Kind;
          if (LKind = NodeKind.FieldDecl) or (LKind = NodeKind.EmbedDecl) then
            if self.DoHoldsMember(self.DoPartType(LMember), AKind) then
              return true;
            end;
          end;
        end;
        LAt := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, LAt);
        LDepth := LDepth + 1;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // True when a value of the canonical type AType holds, at any depth, a polymorphic
    // object (its vptr is set as it is built, DoSetVptr): itself, a static array's
    // element, a field or an embed of any level of its parent chain
    hidden const method DoHoldsVtable(const AType: int64): bool;
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LDepth: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.StaticArray then
        return self.DoHoldsVtable(TargetOf(self.FTree, AType));
      end;
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) <> TypeClass.ObjectType then
        return false;
      end;
      // IsPolymorphic looks through the parent chain
      if IsPolymorphic(self.FTree, AType) then
        return true;
      end;
      LAt := AType;
      LDepth := 0;
      while (LAt <> 0) and (LDepth <= ADAM_TYPES_MAX_DEPTH) do
        LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, LAt);
        for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
          LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
          LKind := self.FTree[LMember].Kind;
          if ((LKind = NodeKind.FieldDecl) or (LKind = NodeKind.EmbedDecl)) and
            self.DoHoldsVtable(self.DoPartType(LMember)) then
            return true;
          end;
        end;
        LAt := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, LAt);
        LDepth := LDepth + 1;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // True when building a value of the canonical type AType runs code: an init somewhere
    // in it (DoHoldsMember), or a polymorphic object's vptr to set (DoHoldsVtable)
    hidden const method DoNeedsBuild(const AType: int64): bool;
    begin
      return self.DoHoldsMember(AType, NodeKind.InitDecl) or self.DoHoldsVtable(AType);
    end;

    // True when ending a value of the canonical type AType runs code: a done somewhere in
    // it (DoHoldsMember)
    hidden const method DoNeedsEnd(const AType: int64): bool;
    begin
      return self.DoHoldsMember(AType, NodeKind.DoneDecl);
    end;

    // True when a value of the canonical type AType runs code of its type where it is
    // copied or ended (BNF sec 4 O5): a done or a copy decl somewhere in it. Such a value
    // is moved (a call's result, `return` of a local, an argument that is a call's
    // result: its bytes taken, its source's live flag cleared) or copied by its type's
    // copy (DoCopyValue), never byte by byte; its slots carry a live flag (DoLiveFlag),
    // a result goes back through the hidden pointer (C++'s rule for a type that is not
    // trivial), a value argument is the callee's to end (DoOwnParam)
    hidden const method DoHasLifetime(const AType: int64): bool;
    begin
      return self.DoNeedsEnd(AType) or self.DoHoldsMember(AType, NodeKind.CopyDecl);
    end;

    // The node whose live flag (FLiveOf) owns the value object AExpr names, when AExpr
    // (through parentheses) can be MOVED from: a call's result in its temporary, or a
    // local variable or a value parameter the routine owns (DoOwnParam) of the current
    // routine (only `return` moves one); 0 for anything else (a field, a const or var
    // parameter, self: copied, DoCopyValue). AExpr is not lowered here
    hidden const method DoMoveSource(const AExpr: int64): int64;
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      LAt := AExpr;
      while self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LAt := self.FTree.FirstOf(LAt, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      if self.DoIsCallSite(LAt) then
        if self.FLiveOf[LAt] <> 0 then
          return LAt;
        end;
        return 0;
      end;
      if NameKindOf(self.FTree, LAt) = NodeKind.NameExpression then
        LDecl := self.FTree[LAt].ResolvedDecl;
        if (LDecl <> 0) and ((self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.VarDecl) or
          (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.Param)) and (self.FLiveOf[LDecl] <> 0) then
          return LDecl;
        end;
      end;
      return 0;
    end;

    // True when AId is a call that runs a routine of its own: a call expression, or a
    // binary or unary expression running a type's declared operator (OperatorCallOf: its
    // operands its arguments, DoOperatorCall)
    hidden const method DoIsCallSite(const AId: int64): bool;
    begin
      return (self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.CallExpression) or (OperatorCallOf(self.FTree, AId) <> 0);
    end;

    // The value object of the canonical type AType (DoHasLifetime) at ASource moved to
    // ADest at ANode: its bytes copied, its source's live flag (AFrom, DoMoveSource)
    // cleared, so only the slot it lands in ends it
    hidden method DoMoveObject(const ADest: int64; const ASource: int64; const AFrom: int64;
      const AType: int64; const ANode: int64);
    begin
      self.DoCopyBytes(ADest, ASource, TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType), ANode);
      self.DoSetLive(AFrom, false, ANode);
    end;

    // The init of the object type AType that takes no argument (what builds it as a parent
    // part or a field no lead call builds, DoLeadCall); 0 when it declares none
    hidden const method DoDefaultInit(const AType: int64): int64;
    var
      LBody: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, AType);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
        LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
        if (self.FTree[LMember].Kind = NodeKind.InitDecl) and (self.FTree.CountOf(LMember, NodeRole.Param) = 0) then
          return LMember;
        end;
      end;
      return 0;
    end;

    // The object at AAddress, of the canonical type AType, built at ANode (BNF sec 4, D3:
    // its parent part first, then its fields in declaration order, then its init's body):
    // by the init AInit when it has one (SEM's pick: the holder AHolder's ResolvedCallee,
    // its arguments AHolder's children of ARole; the init function builds the parts
    // first, DoBody), else its parts here (DoBuildParts: the type declares no init); a
    // polymorphic object's vptr then names its own type's vtable (DoSetVptr: a part's
    // init left its own level's there, as C++ constructors do). A type whose every init
    // takes arguments always comes with AInit (SEM: SM0349, a part's lead call SM0347); a
    // static array of objects is built element by element, the first first (DoEachElement:
    // SEM gives an array no init); false after LW0001
    hidden method DoBuildObject(const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64; const AInit: int64;
      const AHolder: int64; const ARole: NodeRole; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LInit: int64;
    begin
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.StaticArray then
        return self.DoEachElement(AAddress, 0, AType, ElementWalk.Built, ANode);
      end;
      LInit := AInit;
      if (LInit = 0) and (self.DoOwnMember(AType, NodeKind.InitDecl) <> 0) then
        LInit := self.DoDefaultInit(AType);
        if LInit = 0 then
          raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_LEAD_INIT + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
        end;
      end;
      if LInit = 0 then
        if not self.DoBuildParts(AAddress, AType, 0, ANode) then
          return false;
        end;
      else
        if not self.DoCallMember(LInit, AAddress, AHolder, ARole, ANode) then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      return self.DoSetVptr(AAddress, AType, ANode);
    end;

    // The vptr of the object at AAddress (of the canonical type AType) set to AType's
    // vtable at ANode (DoVtable: the vptr is at 0 of every polymorphic object, a
    // polymorphic parent sharing it), then its itable words to AType's itables
    // (DoSetItables, I2); nothing for a type that is not polymorphic; false after LW0001
    hidden method DoSetVptr(const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LVtable: int64;
    begin
      if not IsPolymorphic(self.FTree, AType) then
        return true;
      end;
      LVtable := self.DoVtable(AType, ANode);
      if LVtable = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoStore(AAddress, LVtable, ANode);
      return self.DoSetItables(AAddress, AType, ANode);
    end;

    // The itable words (Layout's, I2) of the object at AAddress of the canonical type AType
    // set at ANode, each to the itable AType gives it (DoItableData): the levels from the
    // root down, each implements name's word (its level's offset in AType plus the name's
    // ResolvedOffset) once, by the name that made it (the root-most: a word a level below
    // shares keeps the itable of the interface it was made for, whose slots start with the
    // shared one's); false after LW0001
    hidden method DoSetItables(const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LLevels: ref Int64List;
      LDone: ref Int64List;
      LAt: int64;
      LDepth: int64;
      LLevel: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LNode: int64;
      LInterface: int64;
      LOffset: int64;
      LSeen: bool;
      LTable: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LJ: int64;
      LK: int64;
    begin
      LLevels := ref Int64List();
      LAt := AType;
      LDepth := 0;
      while (LAt <> 0) and (LDepth <= ADAM_TYPES_MAX_DEPTH) do
        LLevels.Add(LAt);
        LAt := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, LAt);
        LDepth := LDepth + 1;
      end;
      LDone := ref Int64List();
      LI := LLevels.Count - 1;
      while LI >= 0 do
        LLevel := LLevels[LI];
        LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, LLevel);
        for LJ := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Implements) - 1 do
          LNode := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Implements, LJ);
          LInterface := CanonicalOf(self.FTree, LNode);
          if (ClassOf(self.FTree, LInterface) = TypeClass.InterfaceType) and (self.FTree[LNode].ResolvedOffset >= 0) then
            LOffset := self.DoPartOffset(AType, LLevel) + self.FTree[LNode].ResolvedOffset;
            LSeen := false;
            for LK := 0 to LDone.Count - 1 do
              if LDone[LK] = LOffset then
                LSeen := true;
              end;
            end;
            if not LSeen then
              LDone.Add(LOffset);
              LTable := self.DoItableData(AType, LNode, LInterface, LOffset, ANode);
              if LTable = 0 then
                return false;
              end;
              self.DoStore(self.DoByteOffset(AAddress, LOffset, ANode), self.DoBlobAddress(LTable, ANode), ANode);
            end;
          end;
        end;
        LI := LI - 1;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The address of the data blob AData, at ANode
    hidden method DoBlobAddress(const AData: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := AData;
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // The read-only data of the itable the concrete object type AType gives the word at
    // AOffset of its objects, made for the interface AInterface by the implements name
    // ANameNode (I2, made the first time: FItableOf): the offset back from the word to the
    // object's start (-AOffset, an int64), the interface's TypeInfo's address (DoTypeInfo;
    // 0 when it has none), then one address word per slot of the interface (Layout's
    // VtableSlots: its parents' slots first, a property's read then its write), each the
    // function AType's vtable runs for the member implementing it (MemberOf from AType up,
    // the nearest level: its vtable slot's function, DoVtableSlots / DoSlotFunction), or for
    // a method an embed's fulfils the forward ANameNode's Forward child names
    // (DoForwardFunction, I4). 0 after LW0001 at ANode (reported once)
    hidden method DoItableData(const AType: int64; const ANameNode: int64; const AInterface: int64;
      const AOffset: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LKey: int64;
      LImpl: Int64Array;
      LEntries: Int64Array;
      LCount: int64;
      LLevel: int64;
      LDepth: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LHave: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LHaveSlot: int64;
      LAbstract: int64;
      LFunction: int64;
      LFunctions: ref Int64List;
      LInfo: int64;
      LData: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LForwards: Int64Array;
      LWants: Int64Array;
      LForward: int64;
    begin
      LKey := AType * self.FTree.Count + ANameNode;
      LData := self.FItableOf.Find(LKey);
      if LData <> 0 then
        if LData < 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return LData;
      end;
      self.FItableOf.Put(LKey, -1);
      if not self.DoVtableSlots(AType, ANode, LImpl) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LCount := VtableSlots(self.FTree, AInterface);
      // setlength zeroes the new elements: no slot filled yet
      setlength(LEntries, LCount);
      setlength(LForwards, LCount);
      setlength(LWants, LCount);
      LLevel := AInterface;
      LDepth := 0;
      while (LLevel <> 0) and (LDepth <= ADAM_TYPES_MAX_DEPTH) do
        LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, LLevel);
        for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
          LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
          LSlot := int64(self.FTree[LMember].ResolvedSlot);
          LHave := MemberOf(self.FTree, AType, self.FTree[LMember].Text);
          // an embed's method fulfils it (I4): the forward Semantics wrote
          LForward := self.DoForwardNode(ANameNode, self.FTree[LMember].Text);
          if (LHave = 0) and (LForward <> 0) and (LSlot >= 0) and (LSlot < LCount) then
            LForwards[LSlot] := LForward;
            LWants[LSlot] := LMember;
          end;
          if (LSlot >= 0) and (LHave <> 0) and (self.FTree[LHave].ResolvedSlot >= 0) then
            LHaveSlot := int64(self.FTree[LHave].ResolvedSlot);
            if (LSlot < LCount) and (LHaveSlot < len(LImpl)) then
              LEntries[LSlot] := LImpl[LHaveSlot];
            end;
            // an interface property's write slot follows its read's (Layout.VtableSlots)
            if (self.FTree[LMember].Kind = NodeKind.PropertyDecl) and
              (self.FTree.CountOf(LMember, NodeRole.Write) > 0) and (LSlot + 1 < LCount) and
              (LHaveSlot + 1 < len(LImpl)) then
              LEntries[LSlot + 1] := LImpl[LHaveSlot + 1];
            end;
          end;
        end;
        LLevel := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, LLevel);
        LDepth := LDepth + 1;
      end;
      // Every slot's function found before the data is made: a refusal leaves no
      // half-written itable behind
      LFunctions := ref Int64List();
      LAbstract := 0;
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        if LForwards[LI] <> 0 then
          LFunction := self.DoForwardFunction(AType, LForwards[LI], LWants[LI], ANode);
        else
          LFunction := self.DoSlotFunction(LEntries[LI], LAbstract, ANode);
        end;
        if LFunction = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LFunctions.Add(LFunction);
      end;
      LInfo := self.DoTypeInfo(AInterface, ANode);
      LData := self.DoHelperData(ADAM_LOWERING_ITABLE_SYMBOL, self.FTarget.PointerAlign(), ANode);
      self.DoAddIntWord(LData, -AOffset);
      if LInfo <> 0 then
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddAddress(self.FModule.DataAt(LInfo).Symbol, 0);
      else
        self.DoAddZeroWord(LData);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LFunctions.Count - 1 do
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddAddress(self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunctions[LI]).Symbol, 0);
      end;
      self.FItableOf.Put(LKey, LData);
      return LData;
    end;

    // The Forward child of the implements name ANameNode for the interface method named
    // AName (I4, Semantics' DoImplementsByEmbed); 0 when an embed fulfils none of that name
    hidden const method DoForwardNode(const ANameNode: int64; const AName: string): int64;
    var
      LForward: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ANameNode, NodeRole.Forward) - 1 do
        LForward := self.FTree.NthOf(ANameNode, NodeRole.Forward, LI);
        if self.FTree[LForward].Text = AName then
          return LForward;
        end;
      end;
      return 0;
    end;

    // The forward function of the concrete object type AType for its Forward node AForward
    // (I4), the itable slot of the interface method AWant: AWant's IR signature
    // (DoMethodSignature: hidden result, self, then the parameters), made the first time
    // (FForwardOf), its body lowered last (DoForwardBody); 0 after LW0001 at ANode
    hidden method DoForwardFunction(const AType: int64; const AForward: int64; const AWant: int64;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LKey: int64;
      LSignature: int64;
      LFunction: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LKey := AType * self.FTree.Count + AForward;
      LFunction := self.FForwardOf.Find(LKey);
      if LFunction <> 0 then
        return LFunction;
      end;
      if self.FFunctionOf[self.FTree[AForward].ResolvedDecl] = 0 then
        // the embed's method was refused at its declaration (reported there)
        return 0;
      end;
      LSignature := self.DoMethodSignature(AWant, ANode);
      if LSignature = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LFunction := self.FModule.AddFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_FORWARD_SYMBOL + IntToStr(self.FForwardFunctions.Count),
        self.FModule.SignatureAt(LSignature).ResultType, ANode);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Internal := true;
      for LI := 0 to self.FModule.SignatureAt(LSignature).ParamCount - 1 do
        self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.AddParam(self.FModule.SignatureAt(LSignature).ParamTypes[LI]);
      end;
      self.FForwardFunctions.Add(LFunction);
      self.FForwardTypes.Add(AType);
      self.FForwardNodes.Add(AForward);
      self.FForwardWants.Add(AWant);
      self.FForwardOf.Put(LKey, LFunction);
      return LFunction;
    end;

    // The bytes from the start of an object of the concrete type AType to the embed its
    // Forward node AForward reaches (I4): the outermost embed's offset in AType (its level's
    // part included, DoMemberOffset), then each EmbedStep's in the embed before it
    hidden method DoForwardOffset(const AType: int64; const AForward: int64): int64;
    var
      LEmbed: int64;
      LStep: int64;
      LOffset: int64;
      LHolder: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LEmbed := self.FTree[AForward].ResolvedEmbed;
      LOffset := self.DoMemberOffset(AType, LEmbed);
      LHolder := self.DoPartType(LEmbed);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AForward, NodeRole.EmbedStep) - 1 do
        LStep := self.FTree[self.FTree.NthOf(AForward, NodeRole.EmbedStep, LI)].ResolvedDecl;
        LOffset := LOffset + self.DoMemberOffset(LHolder, LStep);
        LHolder := self.DoPartType(LStep);
      end;
      return LOffset;
    end;

    // Every forward's body not lowered yet (DoForwardBody, FForwardsDone): a forward's body
    // asks for nothing more
    hidden method DoForwardBodies();
    begin
      while self.FForwardsDone < self.FForwardFunctions.Count do
        self.DoForwardBody(self.FForwardsDone);
        self.FForwardsDone := self.FForwardsDone + 1;
      end;
    end;

    // The body of the forward AIndex (DoForwardFunction, I4) in a fresh function state: its
    // parameters as they came (the interface method's: hidden result, self, then the
    // arguments), self (the object's start, as an itable call gives it) moved to the embed
    // (DoForwardOffset), then the embed's method called directly with them (the embed holds
    // exactly its type) and its result returned as it is: the forward adds and drops no
    // holder of anything
    hidden method DoForwardBody(const AIndex: int64);
    var
      LFunction: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LForward: int64;
      LWant: int64;
      LTarget: int64;
      LNode: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LSelfAt: int64;
      LParams: ref Int64List;
      LParam: int64;
      LCall: int64;
      LResult: IrType;
      LRet: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LFunction := self.FForwardFunctions[AIndex];
      LType := self.FForwardTypes[AIndex];
      LForward := self.FForwardNodes[AIndex];
      LWant := self.FForwardWants[AIndex];
      LTarget := self.FFunctionOf[self.FTree[LForward].ResolvedDecl];
      LNode := LForward;
      self.FFunction := LFunction;
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoStartManaged();
      LCount := self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.ParamCount;
      // self comes after the hidden result (when there is one), before the arguments
      LSelfAt := LCount - self.DoParamCount(LWant) - 1;
      LParams := ref Int64List();
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LParam := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.ParamTypes[LI], LNode);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LParam).Imm := LI;
        if LI = LSelfAt then
          LParam := self.DoByteOffset(LParam, self.DoForwardOffset(LType, LForward), LNode);
        end;
        LParams.Add(LParam);
      end;
      LResult := self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.ResultType;
      LCall := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Call, LResult, LNode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LCall).Link := LTarget;
      for LI := 0 to LParams.Count - 1 do
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LCall).Operands.Add(LParams[LI]);
      end;
      LRet := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, LNode);
      if LResult <> IrType.Void then
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LRet).Operands.Add(LCall);
      end;
    end;

    // The function a vtable or itable slot runs for AImpl, the member DoVtableSlots gave it
    // (its function), -1 abstract (the runtime's AbstractCall, made once into AAbstract) or
    // 0 none (a slot no level decided: AbstractCall too); 0 after LW0001 at ANode (a member
    // refused at its declaration was reported there)
    hidden method DoSlotFunction(const AImpl: int64; var AAbstract: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    begin
      if AImpl > 0 then
        return self.FFunctionOf[AImpl];
      end;
      if AAbstract = 0 then
        AAbstract := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.AbstractCall, ANode);
      end;
      return AAbstract;
    end;

    // The integer AValue as one little-endian word (the target's pointer size) at the end
    // of the blob AData
    hidden method DoAddIntWord(const AData: int64; const AValue: int64);
    var
      LBits: uint64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LBits := uint64(AValue);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTarget.PointerSize() - 1 do
        self.FModule.DataAt(AData).AddByte(uint8(LBits & uint64(0xFF)));
        LBits := LBits shr uint64(8);
      end;
    end;

    // The TypeInfo blob of the object type or interface AType (I1, RTTI: System.Runtime's
    // ADAM_RUNTIME_TYPEINFO_* words): the address of its parent's TypeInfo (0 at a root),
    // then the address of its name (a NUL-ended text, as TypeText writes the type), then its
    // interface entries (DoTypeInfoEntries, I3: their count, then per entry an interface's
    // TypeInfo and the offset of the object's itable word for it), named by the type's
    // ResolvedSymbol (Symbols: Itanium's _ZTI and its class). Its own unit's blob
    // is public (DoDeclaration makes it whether or not the unit uses it, so another unit's
    // reference always links); another unit's is declared (its bytes are that unit's, as
    // DoDeclareData's). Made the first time (FTypeInfoOf); 0 for a type with no symbol (no
    // object or interface, a generic's: M10)
    hidden method DoTypeInfo(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LSymbol: string;
      LText: string;
      LData: int64;
      LName: int64;
      LParent: int64;
      LParentData: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTypeInfoOf[AType] <> 0 then
        return self.FTypeInfoOf[AType];
      end;
      LSymbol := self.FTree[AType].ResolvedSymbol;
      if (self.FTree[AType].Kind <> NodeKind.TypeDecl) or (LSymbol = "") then
        return 0;
      end;
      if ModuleOf(self.FTree, AType) <> self.FUnit then
        LData := self.FModule.AddDataOfKind(LSymbol, IrDataKind.Zeroed, 1, AType);
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).Declared := true;
        self.FTypeInfoOf[AType] := LData;
        return LData;
      end;
      // The parent's first: its symbol is the word's (it may be this unit's or declared)
      LParentData := 0;
      LParent := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if LParent <> 0 then
        LParentData := self.DoTypeInfo(LParent, ANode);
      end;
      LText := TypeText(self.FTree, AType);
      LName := self.DoHelperData(ADAM_LOWERING_TEXT_SYMBOL, 1, ANode);
      for LI := 0 to len(LText) - 1 do
        self.FModule.DataAt(LName).AddByte(uint8(LText[LI]));
      end;
      self.FModule.DataAt(LName).AddByte(uint8(0));
      LData := self.FModule.AddData(LSymbol, self.FTarget.PointerAlign(), AType);
      self.FTypeInfoOf[AType] := LData;
      if LParentData <> 0 then
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddAddress(self.FModule.DataAt(LParentData).Symbol, 0);
      else
        self.DoAddZeroWord(LData);
      end;
      self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddAddress(self.FModule.DataAt(LName).Symbol, 0);
      self.DoTypeInfoEntries(LData, AType, ANode);
      return LData;
    end;

    // The interface entries of the TypeInfo blob AData of the object type or interface AType
    // (I3, System.Runtime's InterfaceOffset reads them): their count, then for each
    // implements name of AType's levels from AType up its parents, the TypeInfo of the interface it
    // names (a child interface's entry serves its parents: the runtime walks the chain) and
    // the offset of AType's itable word for it from AType's start (its level's part offset
    // plus the name's ResolvedOffset, as DoSetItables places it); none for an interface
    hidden method DoTypeInfoEntries(const AData: int64; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LInfos: ref Int64List;
      LOffsets: ref Int64List;
      LLevel: int64;
      LDepth: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LNode: int64;
      LInterface: int64;
      LInfo: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LInfos := ref Int64List();
      LOffsets := ref Int64List();
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.ObjectType then
        LLevel := AType;
        LDepth := 0;
        while (LLevel <> 0) and (LDepth <= ADAM_TYPES_MAX_DEPTH) do
          LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, LLevel);
          for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Implements) - 1 do
            LNode := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Implements, LI);
            LInterface := CanonicalOf(self.FTree, LNode);
            if (ClassOf(self.FTree, LInterface) = TypeClass.InterfaceType) and (self.FTree[LNode].ResolvedOffset >= 0) then
              LInfo := self.DoTypeInfo(LInterface, ANode);
              if LInfo <> 0 then
                LInfos.Add(LInfo);
                LOffsets.Add(self.DoPartOffset(AType, LLevel) + self.FTree[LNode].ResolvedOffset);
              end;
            end;
          end;
          LLevel := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, LLevel);
          LDepth := LDepth + 1;
        end;
      end;
      self.DoAddIntWord(AData, LInfos.Count);
      for LI := 0 to LInfos.Count - 1 do
        self.FModule.DataAt(AData).AddAddress(self.FModule.DataAt(LInfos[LI]).Symbol, 0);
        self.DoAddIntWord(AData, LOffsets[LI]);
      end;
    end;

    // A zero address word (the target's pointer size) at the end of the blob AData
    hidden method DoAddZeroWord(const AData: int64);
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTarget.PointerSize() - 1 do
        self.FModule.DataAt(AData).AddByte(uint8(0));
      end;
    end;

    // The address of the TypeInfo of the object type AType (DoTypeInfo) at ANode; 0 after
    // LW0001 (a type with none)
    hidden method DoTypeInfoAddress(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LData: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      LData := self.DoTypeInfo(AType, ANode);
      if LData = 0 then
        self.DoRefuse(ANode, "the type info of '" + TypeText(self.FTree, AType) + "'");
        return 0;
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := LData;
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // The TypeInfo of the dynamic type of the polymorphic object at AObject (I1): its
    // vtable's word before slot 0 (the vptr at 0 of the object, DoSetVptr)
    hidden method DoDynamicTypeInfo(const AObject: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LVtable: int64;
    begin
      LVtable := self.DoLoad(AObject, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      return self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(LVtable, -self.FTarget.PointerSize(), ANode),
        IrType.Pointer, ANode);
    end;

    // The bool `the object at AObject is a T` for the TypeInfo address ATarget of T (the
    // runtime's IsInstance over the object's dynamic TypeInfo); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoInstanceTest(const AObject: int64; const ATarget: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.IsInstance, self.DoDynamicTypeInfo(AObject, ANode),
        ATarget, ANode);
    end;

    // `as`'s check of the object at AObject against the type AType (I1, BNF sec 6): an
    // object that is no AType is a cold block of its own calling the runtime's InvalidCast
    // (code 13, `invalid cast: the object is not a T`), which never returns (the block
    // still ends in a jump, as DoCheckNilOwner's does). False after LW0001
    hidden method DoCastCheck(const AObject: int64; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LTarget: int64;
      LIs: int64;
      LBad: int64;
      LGood: int64;
    begin
      LTarget := self.DoTypeInfoAddress(AType, ANode);
      if LTarget = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LIs := self.DoInstanceTest(AObject, LTarget, ANode);
      if LIs = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LBad := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LGood := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(LIs, LGood, LBad, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LBad;
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.InvalidCast, LTarget, 0, ANode) = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoJumpTo(LGood, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LGood;
      return true;
    end;

    // True when the `is` / `as` AId's operand is nil-able, a ptr, a ref or an own (its
    // object reached past a nil test), not an object or an interface reached as a place
    // (BNF sec 6)
    hidden const method DoTestsHolder(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand)));
      return (LClass = TypeClass.Pointer) or (LClass = TypeClass.RefType) or (LClass = TypeClass.OwnType);
    end;

    // The object type or interface the `is` / `as` AId's operand is or holds: a place's own
    // type, a ptr's, a ref's or an own's target
    hidden const method DoTestedType(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoUsedType(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand));
      if self.DoTestsHolder(AId) then
        return TargetOf(self.FTree, LType);
      end;
      return LType;
    end;

    // The type an `is` / `as` AId tests for (BNF sec 6: an object type or an interface; I3:
    // either side may be an interface)
    hidden const method DoTestTarget(const AId: int64): int64;
    begin
      return CanonicalOf(self.FTree, self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.TypeOf));
    end;

    // True when the canonical type AType is an interface (I3: an interface's place is its
    // object's itable word for it)
    hidden const method DoIsInterface(const AType: int64): bool;
    begin
      return (AType <> 0) and (ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.InterfaceType);
    end;

    // True when the `is` / `as` AId has an interface on either side (I3)
    hidden const method DoTestsInterface(const AId: int64): bool;
    begin
      return self.DoIsInterface(self.DoTestTarget(AId)) or self.DoIsInterface(self.DoTestedType(AId));
    end;

    // The start of the object behind ASubject, the address the `is` / `as` AId's operand
    // is or holds (a place's, or a holder's object, DoHeldObjectOf): ASubject itself for an
    // object (a polymorphic type's part is at 0 of any descendant), an interface's itable
    // word moved back by the itable's offset (I3)
    hidden method DoTestedObject(const AId: int64; const ASubject: int64): int64;
    var
      LBack: int64;
      LObject: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoIsInterface(self.DoTestedType(AId)) then
        return ASubject;
      end;
      LBack := self.DoLoad(self.DoLoad(ASubject, IrType.Pointer, AId), IrType.Int64, AId);
      LObject := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Offset, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LObject).Operands.Add(ASubject);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LObject).Operands.Add(LBack);
      return LObject;
    end;

    // The block or address a nil-able `is` / `as` operand AOperand holds (a ptr's value, a
    // ref's or an own's block: borrowed, its holder keeps it; an own I / ref I's itable
    // word); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoHolderValue(const AOperand: int64): int64;
    begin
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(AOperand)) = TypeClass.Pointer then
        return self.DoValue(AOperand);
      end;
      return self.DoManagedValue(AOperand);
    end;

    // The object or interface place a nil-able operand's value AValue (DoHolderValue)
    // holds: a ptr's own address, an own I / ref I's itable word (I3), a ref's or an own's
    // block past its header
    hidden method DoHeldObjectOf(const AOperand: int64; const AValue: int64): int64;
    begin
      if (ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(AOperand)) = TypeClass.Pointer) or
        self.DoIsInterfaceOwner(self.DoUsedType(AOperand)) then
        return AValue;
      end;
      return self.DoByteOffset(AValue, ADAM_LOWERING_REF_HEADER, AOperand);
    end;

    // The bool `the object at AObject (its start) is a T` for the type AType (I1, I3): an
    // object type by the runtime's IsInstance over the object's dynamic TypeInfo, an
    // interface by its InterfaceOffset finding the object's itable word for it; 0 after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoTypeTest(const AObject: int64; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LTarget: int64;
      LOffset: int64;
    begin
      LTarget := self.DoTypeInfoAddress(AType, ANode);
      if LTarget = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if not self.DoIsInterface(AType) then
        return self.DoInstanceTest(AObject, LTarget, ANode);
      end;
      LOffset := self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.InterfaceOffset, self.DoDynamicTypeInfo(AObject, ANode), LTarget,
        ANode);
      if LOffset = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.SGreaterEqual, LOffset, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, ANode), ANode);
    end;

    // `as`'s checked conversion of the object at AObject (its start) to the type AType (I1,
    // I3, BNF sec 6): the object itself for an object type (DoCastCheck); for an interface
    // its itable word for it, found by the runtime's InterfaceOffset over its dynamic
    // TypeInfo (none: a cold block of its own calling InvalidCast, as DoCastCheck's); 0
    // after LW0001
    hidden method DoCastTo(const AObject: int64; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LTarget: int64;
      LOffset: int64;
      LFound: int64;
      LBad: int64;
      LGood: int64;
      LWord: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoIsInterface(AType) then
        if not self.DoCastCheck(AObject, AType, ANode) then
          return 0;
        end;
        return AObject;
      end;
      LTarget := self.DoTypeInfoAddress(AType, ANode);
      if LTarget = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LOffset := self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.InterfaceOffset, self.DoDynamicTypeInfo(AObject, ANode), LTarget,
        ANode);
      if LOffset = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LFound := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.SGreaterEqual, LOffset, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, ANode), ANode);
      LBad := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LGood := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(LFound, LGood, LBad, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LBad;
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.InvalidCast, LTarget, 0, ANode) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoJumpTo(LGood, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LGood;
      LWord := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Offset, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LWord).Operands.Add(AObject);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LWord).Operands.Add(LOffset);
      return LWord;
    end;

    // `X is T` (I1, I3, BNF sec 6): the bool the runtime gives over X's dynamic TypeInfo and
    // T's (DoTypeTest; an interface X reached back to its object first, DoTestedObject); a
    // nil ptr, ref or own is never a T (false, past the test: a join of the two edges); 0
    // after LW0001
    hidden method DoIsValue(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LOperand: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LFalse: int64;
      LHeld: int64;
      LTest: int64;
      LTestBlock: int64;
      LTestEnd: int64;
      LNilEnd: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
      LObject: int64;
    begin
      LOperand := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand);
      LType := self.DoTestTarget(AId);
      if not self.DoTestsHolder(AId) then
        LObject := self.DoAddressFor(LOperand, false);
        if LObject = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return self.DoTypeTest(self.DoTestedObject(AId, LObject), LType, AId);
      end;
      LValue := self.DoHolderValue(LOperand);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LFalse := self.DoConstant(IrType.Bool, 0, AId);
      LHeld := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.NotEqual, LValue, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, AId), AId);
      LTestBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LNilEnd := self.FBlock;
      self.DoBranchOn(LHeld, LTestBlock, LJoin, AId);
      self.FBlock := LTestBlock;
      LTest := self.DoTypeTest(self.DoTestedObject(AId, self.DoHeldObjectOf(LOperand, LValue)), LType, AId);
      if LTest = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LTestEnd := self.FBlock;
      self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, AId);
      self.FBlock := LJoin;
      return self.DoJoinOf(IrType.Bool, LTest, LTestEnd, LFalse, LNilEnd, AId);
    end;

    // `X as T` of a ptr, an own or a ref X (I1, I3, BNF sec 6): checked past a nil test (nil
    // stays nil), keeping X's kind: between object types X's own value (a ptr, a ref's
    // block, borrowed as X's is); with an interface on either side the place DoCastTo gives
    // (a ptr's address, an own I / ref I's itable word, or an own T / ref T's block before
    // its object), joined with nil; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAsHolder(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LOperand: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LHeld: int64;
      LCheck: int64;
      LDone: int64;
      LStart: int64;
      LPlace: int64;
      LResult: int64;
      LNil: int64;
    begin
      LOperand := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand);
      LType := self.DoTestTarget(AId);
      LValue := self.DoHolderValue(LOperand);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      // nil made before the branch: the join's operand from the nil edge
      LNil := self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, AId);
      LHeld := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.NotEqual, LValue, LNil, AId);
      LCheck := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LDone := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LStart := self.FBlock;
      self.DoBranchOn(LHeld, LCheck, LDone, AId);
      self.FBlock := LCheck;
      if not self.DoTestsInterface(AId) then
        if not self.DoCastCheck(self.DoHeldObjectOf(LOperand, LValue), LType, AId) then
          return 0;
        end;
        self.DoJumpTo(LDone, AId);
        self.FBlock := LDone;
        return LValue;
      end;
      LPlace := self.DoCastTo(self.DoTestedObject(AId, self.DoHeldObjectOf(LOperand, LValue)), LType, AId);
      if LPlace = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LResult := LPlace;
      if (ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(AId)) <> TypeClass.Pointer) and not self.DoIsInterface(LType) then
        // an own T / ref T: its block, before the object
        LResult := self.DoByteOffset(LPlace, -ADAM_LOWERING_REF_HEADER, AId);
      end;
      LCheck := self.FBlock;
      self.DoJumpTo(LDone, AId);
      self.FBlock := LDone;
      return self.DoJoinOf(IrType.Pointer, LResult, LCheck, LNil, LStart, AId);
    end;

    // The address of the object or interface place `X as T` is when its result is one (I1,
    // I3, BNF sec 6: an object or an interface X, a place, as T; an own X's object or
    // itable word, a nil own raising as any reach of it does, DoRefObject), checked
    // (DoCastTo: an interface X reached back to its object first, DoTestedObject); AWrite:
    // DoAddressFor's write form for a place X. 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAsObject(const AId: int64; const AWrite: bool): int64;
    var
      LOperand: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LObject: int64;
    begin
      LOperand := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand);
      LType := self.DoTestTarget(AId);
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(LOperand)) = TypeClass.OwnType then
        LObject := self.DoRefObject(LOperand);
      else
        LObject := self.DoAddressFor(LOperand, AWrite);
      end;
      if LObject = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoCastTo(self.DoTestedObject(AId, LObject), LType, AId);
    end;

    // True when the `as` AId is a place: its result an object or an interface (DoAsObject,
    // I3), not a ptr or a ref value (DoAsHolder)
    hidden const method DoIsAsObject(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind <> NodeKind.AsExpression then
        return false;
      end;
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(AId));
      return (LClass = TypeClass.ObjectType) or (LClass = TypeClass.InterfaceType);
    end;

    // The address of the vtable of the polymorphic object type AType (DoVtableData): its
    // slot 0, past the word holding its TypeInfo; at ANode; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoVtable(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LData: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      LData := self.DoVtableData(AType, ANode);
      if LData = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := LData;
      return self.DoByteOffset(LAddress, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), ANode);
    end;

    // The read-only data of the vtable of the polymorphic object type AType, made the first
    // time (FVtableOf): its type's TypeInfo's address (DoTypeInfo, I1: the word before slot
    // 0, `is` / `as` read it), then one address word per slot (Layout's VtableSlots: the parent's
    // slots first, an override in the slot of what it overrides), each the function of the
    // nearest level from AType up that gives the slot a body (DoVtableSlots), an abstract
    // one the runtime's AbstractCall (a virtual property's accessors fill its slots the
    // same way: DoSlotFunction). 0 after LW0001 at ANode (reported once)
    hidden method DoVtableData(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LImpl: Int64Array;
      LFunctions: ref Int64List;
      LAbstract: int64;
      LFunction: int64;
      LData: int64;
      LInfo: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if self.FVtableOf[AType] <> 0 then
        if self.FVtableOf[AType] < 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return self.FVtableOf[AType];
      end;
      self.FVtableOf[AType] := -1;
      if not self.DoVtableSlots(AType, ANode, LImpl) then
        return 0;
      end;
      // Every slot's function found before the data is made: a refusal leaves no
      // half-written vtable behind
      LFunctions := ref Int64List();
      LAbstract := 0;
      for LI := 0 to len(LImpl) - 1 do
        LFunction := self.DoSlotFunction(LImpl[LI], LAbstract, ANode);
        if LFunction = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LFunctions.Add(LFunction);
      end;
      LInfo := self.DoTypeInfo(AType, ANode);
      LData := self.DoHelperData(ADAM_LOWERING_VTABLE_SYMBOL,
        self.FTarget.PointerAlign(), ANode);
      if LInfo <> 0 then
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddAddress(self.FModule.DataAt(LInfo).Symbol, 0);
      else
        self.DoAddZeroWord(LData);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LFunctions.Count - 1 do
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddAddress(self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunctions[LI]).Symbol, 0);
      end;
      self.FVtableOf[AType] := LData;
      return LData;
    end;

    // The slot ASlot (of ACount) of a vtable decided by AMember, a method or a property's
    // accessor (0: none, the property has no write), unless a nearer level decided it
    // already: -1 when it is abstract, else AMember (its function: a body, or a bound
    // accessor's made from its field, DoBoundAccessor)
    hidden method DoSlotImpl(const AMember: int64; const ASlot: int64; const ACount: int64;
      var AImpl: Int64Array);
    begin
      if (AMember = 0) or (ASlot < 0) or (ASlot >= ACount) or (AImpl[ASlot] <> 0) then
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[AMember].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Abstract) then
        AImpl[ASlot] := -1;
      else
        AImpl[ASlot] := AMember;
      end;
    end;

    // The method or accessor each slot of the polymorphic object type AType's vtable runs,
    // into AImpl by slot (VtableSlots' count of them; -1: abstract): from AType up its
    // parent chain, the first level whose method or property has the slot decides it
    // (DoSlotImpl: a body or a bound accessor its function; abstract: -1, an abstract
    // override reopens what a parent gave). Always true today (a level's interfaces get
    // their own itables, DoItableData)
    hidden method DoVtableSlots(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64; var AImpl: Int64Array): bool;
    var
      LCount: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LDepth: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LCount := VtableSlots(self.FTree, AType);
      // setlength zeroes the new elements: no slot decided yet
      setlength(AImpl, LCount);
      LAt := AType;
      LDepth := 0;
      while (LAt <> 0) and (LDepth <= ADAM_TYPES_MAX_DEPTH) do
        LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, LAt);
        for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
          LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
          LSlot := int64(self.FTree[LMember].ResolvedSlot);
          if (self.FTree[LMember].Kind = NodeKind.PropertyDecl) and (LSlot >= 0) then
            // a property spans its read's slot, then its write's (Layout.VtableSlots)
            self.DoSlotImpl(self.FTree.FirstOf(LMember, NodeRole.Read), LSlot, LCount, AImpl);
            self.DoSlotImpl(self.FTree.FirstOf(LMember, NodeRole.Write), LSlot + 1, LCount, AImpl);
          end;
          if (self.FTree[LMember].Kind = NodeKind.MethodDecl) and (LSlot >= 0) then
            self.DoSlotImpl(LMember, LSlot, LCount, AImpl);
          end;
        end;
        LAt := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, LAt);
        LDepth := LDepth + 1;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // A call at ANode of the init or done AMember's function with self AAddress and the
    // arguments of AHolder's children of ARole (none when AHolder is 0), each taken as its
    // parameter takes it (DoArgument); false when it was refused (at its declaration, or an
    // argument here)
    hidden method DoCallMember(const AMember: int64; const AAddress: int64; const AHolder: int64;
      const ARole: NodeRole; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LFunction: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LValue: int64;
      LId: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LFunction := self.FFunctionOf[AMember];
      if LFunction = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      if AHolder <> 0 then
        for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AHolder, ARole) - 1 do
          LValue := self.DoArgument(self.FTree.NthOf(AHolder, ARole, LI), self.FTree.NthOf(AMember, NodeRole.Param, LI));
          if LValue = 0 then
            return false;
          end;
          LArgs.Add(LValue);
        end;
      end;
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Call, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Link := LFunction;
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(AAddress);
      for LI := 0 to LArgs.Count - 1 do
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LArgs[LI]);
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The lead call of the init or copy ARoutine (0: none) that builds APart (BNF sec 4 D3:
    // `parent.init(...)` / `self.F.init(...)` at the start of its body): the call whose
    // ResolvedDecl SEM made APart (the parent's canonical type for the parent part, the
    // field or embed for a field; its ResolvedCallee the init picked, 0 when the part's type
    // declares none); 0 when none builds it
    hidden const method DoLeadCall(const ARoutine: int64; const APart: int64): int64;
    var
      LBody: int64;
      LStatement: int64;
      LCall: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if ARoutine = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LBody := self.FTree.FirstOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Body);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Statement) - 1 do
        LStatement := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Statement, LI);
        if not self.DoIsLeadStatement(LStatement) then
          return 0;
        end;
        LCall := self.FTree.FirstOf(LStatement, NodeRole.Value);
        if self.FTree[LCall].ResolvedDecl = APart then
          return LCall;
        end;
      end;
      return 0;
    end;

    // True when the statement AStatement is a lead init call (SEM gives only a lead call a
    // ResolvedDecl of its own: the part it builds); it builds that part before the body
    // runs (DoBuildParts), so the body's own walk passes it by (DoStatement)
    hidden const method DoIsLeadStatement(const AStatement: int64): bool;
    var
      LCall: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AStatement].Kind <> NodeKind.ExpressionStatement then
        return false;
      end;
      LCall := self.FTree.FirstOf(AStatement, NodeRole.Value);
      return (self.FTree[LCall].Kind = NodeKind.CallExpression) and (self.FTree[LCall].ResolvedDecl <> 0);
    end;

    // The part APart (the parent's type or a field / embed) of type APartType at AAddress,
    // built at ANode by the lead call of ARoutine that builds it (DoLeadCall: its init, its
    // arguments) or else by its type's own build (DoBuildObject); false after LW0001
    hidden method DoBuildPart(const AAddress: int64; const APart: int64; const APartType: int64;
      const ARoutine: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LCall: int64;
    begin
      LCall := self.DoLeadCall(ARoutine, APart);
      if LCall <> 0 then
        return self.DoBuildObject(AAddress, APartType, self.FTree[LCall].ResolvedCallee, LCall,
          NodeRole.Argument, ANode);
      end;
      return self.DoBuildObject(AAddress, APartType, 0, 0, NodeRole.Argument, ANode);
    end;

    // The parts of the object at AAddress (of the canonical type AType) built at ANode: its
    // parent part (at its offset, DoUpcast), then its fields (DoBuildFields), each by the
    // lead call of the init ARoutine that builds it (0: none, DoBuildPart); false after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoBuildParts(const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64; const ARoutine: int64;
      const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LParent: int64;
    begin
      LParent := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if (LParent <> 0) and self.DoNeedsBuild(LParent) then
        if not self.DoBuildPart(self.DoUpcast(AAddress, AType, LParent, ANode), LParent, LParent, ARoutine,
          ANode) then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      return self.DoBuildFields(AAddress, AType, ARoutine, ANode);
    end;

    // The fields and embeds of AType's own level of the object at AAddress built at ANode:
    // each that needs one (DoNeedsBuild) in declaration order, by the lead call of the init
    // or copy ARoutine that builds it (0: none), else by its type's init that takes no
    // argument (DoBuildPart, DoBuildObject: which sets a polymorphic part's vptr; a static
    // array of objects element by element); false after LW0001
    hidden method DoBuildFields(const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64; const ARoutine: int64;
      const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LBody: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LPart: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, AType);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
        LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
        if (self.FTree[LMember].Kind = NodeKind.FieldDecl) or (self.FTree[LMember].Kind = NodeKind.EmbedDecl) then
          LPart := self.DoPartType(LMember);
          if self.DoNeedsBuild(LPart) then
            if (ClassOf(self.FTree, LPart) <> TypeClass.ObjectType) and
              (ClassOf(self.FTree, LPart) <> TypeClass.StaticArray) then
              self.DoRefuse(ANode, "the lifetime of type '" + TypeText(self.FTree, LPart) + "'");
              return false;
            end;
            if self.FTree[LMember].ResolvedOffset < 0 then
              raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_FIELD_OFFSET + self.FTree[LMember].Text);
            end;
            if not self.DoBuildPart(self.DoByteOffset(AAddress, self.FTree[LMember].ResolvedOffset, ANode),
              LMember, LPart, ARoutine, ANode) then
              return false;
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The object at AAddress, of the canonical type AType, ended at ANode (BNF sec 4, D3:
    // the reverse of its build): by its done when its type declares one (the done function
    // ends the parts after its body, DoBody), else its parts here (DoEndParts); a static
    // array of objects element by element, the last first (DoEachElement); false after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoEndObject(const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LDone: int64;
    begin
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.StaticArray then
        return self.DoEachElement(AAddress, 0, AType, ElementWalk.Ended, ANode);
      end;
      LDone := self.DoOwnMember(AType, NodeKind.DoneDecl);
      if LDone = 0 then
        return self.DoEndParts(AAddress, AType, ANode);
      end;
      return self.DoCallMember(LDone, AAddress, 0, NodeRole.Argument, ANode);
    end;

    // Every element of the static array at AAddress (of the canonical type AType, its
    // elements objects or arrays of them) walked at ANode as AWalk says: built
    // (DoBuildObject, the first element first), ended (DoEndObject, the last first: the
    // reverse of the build) or copied from the element at the same index of the array at
    // ASource (DoCopyValue, the first first; ASource is 0 for the other walks), by a loop:
    // a counter slot from the first index the walk takes; a head block testing it against
    // the walk's end, to the body or the exit; the body the element at AAddress (and
    // ASource) moved by the counter (DoMovePointer), the counter one step on, back to the
    // head; the exit the current block after it. An element whose type builds (ends,
    // copies) no code of its own makes no loop: a copy's bytes then go at once
    // (DoCopyValue). False after LW0001
    hidden method DoEachElement(const AAddress: int64; const ASource: int64; const AType: int64;
      const AWalk: ElementWalk; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LElement: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LCounter: int64;
      LHead: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LExit: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LTest: int64;
      LNext: int64;
      LOne: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LFrom: int64;
      LDone: bool;
      LForward: bool;
    begin
      LElement := TargetOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if (AWalk = ElementWalk.Built) and not self.DoNeedsBuild(LElement) then
        return true;
      end;
      if (AWalk = ElementWalk.Ended) and not self.DoNeedsEnd(LElement) then
        return true;
      end;
      if (AWalk = ElementWalk.Copied) and not self.DoHoldsMember(LElement, NodeKind.CopyDecl) then
        return self.DoCopyValue(AAddress, ASource, AType, ANode);
      end;
      // a build and a copy go from the first element, an end from the last
      LForward := AWalk <> ElementWalk.Ended;
      LCount := ArrayCount(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType);
      if LCount < 0 then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_ARRAY_COUNT + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
      end;
      if LCount = 0 then
        return true;
      end;
      LCounter := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, 8, 8);
      if LForward then
        self.DoStore(LCounter, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, ANode), ANode);
      else
        self.DoStore(LCounter, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LCount - 1, ANode), ANode);
      end;
      LHead := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LExit := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoJumpTo(LHead, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LHead;
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      if LForward then
        LTest := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.SLess, LIndex, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LCount, ANode),
          ANode);
      else
        LTest := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.SGreaterEqual, LIndex, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, ANode),
          ANode);
      end;
      self.DoBranchOn(LTest, LBody, LExit, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LBody;
      // the counter read again in the body: its value is the body's own, whatever blocks an
      // element's build or end adds after it
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LAt := self.DoMovePointer(AAddress, LIndex, AType, false, ANode);
      if AWalk = ElementWalk.Built then
        LDone := self.DoBuildObject(LAt, LElement, 0, 0, NodeRole.Argument, ANode);
      else
        if AWalk = ElementWalk.Ended then
          LDone := self.DoEndObject(LAt, LElement, ANode);
        else
          LFrom := self.DoMovePointer(ASource, LIndex, AType, false, ANode);
          LDone := self.DoCopyValue(LAt, LFrom, LElement, ANode);
        end;
      end;
      if not LDone then
        return false;
      end;
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      // every operand is emitted before the instruction that uses it
      LOne := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 1, ANode);
      if LForward then
        LNext := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Add, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      else
        LNext := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Sub, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      end;
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LNext).Operands.Add(LIndex);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LNext).Operands.Add(LOne);
      self.DoStore(LCounter, LNext, ANode);
      self.DoJumpTo(LHead, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LExit;
      return true;
    end;

    // The parts of the object at AAddress (of the canonical type AType) ended at ANode, in
    // reverse of their build: each field and embed that needs it (DoNeedsEnd) from the last
    // declared, then the parent part (DoEndObject); false after LW0001
    hidden method DoEndParts(const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LParent: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LPart: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, AType);
      for LI := self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 downto 0 do
        LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
        if (self.FTree[LMember].Kind = NodeKind.FieldDecl) or (self.FTree[LMember].Kind = NodeKind.EmbedDecl) then
          LPart := self.DoPartType(LMember);
          if self.DoNeedsEnd(LPart) then
            if (ClassOf(self.FTree, LPart) <> TypeClass.ObjectType) and
              (ClassOf(self.FTree, LPart) <> TypeClass.StaticArray) then
              self.DoRefuse(ANode, "the lifetime of type '" + TypeText(self.FTree, LPart) + "'");
              return false;
            end;
            if not self.DoEndObject(self.DoByteOffset(AAddress, self.FTree[LMember].ResolvedOffset, ANode),
              LPart, ANode) then
              return false;
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      LParent := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if (LParent <> 0) and self.DoNeedsEnd(LParent) then
        return self.DoEndObject(self.DoUpcast(AAddress, AType, LParent, ANode), LParent, ANode);
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The object type whose init, done or method ADecl is (as SEM's DoSelf types self in
    // it: MethodOwnerOf gives the object's body, its parent the type declaration)
    hidden const method DoOwnerType(const ADecl: int64): int64;
    begin
      return DeclaredTypeOf(self.FTree, self.FTree.ParentOf(MethodOwnerOf(self.FTree, ADecl)));
    end;

    // True when a value of the canonical type AType is or holds, at any depth, an owner (a
    // ref, an own, a task or a weak: each a managed value): through a static array's
    // element, a record's or an object's fields (its parent chain's too) and an object's
    // embeds (Layout.HoldsOwner also counts an object held by value, which is no
    // reference). A dynamic array's elements are its block's (its element map maps them)
    hidden const method DoHoldsOwner(const AType: int64): bool;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
      LAt: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LDepth: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if AType = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      // an own, a task and a sequence are ref blocks (DoIsRefValue), a weak watches one
      if (LClass = TypeClass.RefType) or (LClass = TypeClass.OwnType) or
        (LClass = TypeClass.TaskType) or (LClass = TypeClass.SequenceType) or
        (LClass = TypeClass.WeakType) then
        return true;
      end;
      if LClass = TypeClass.StaticArray then
        return self.DoHoldsOwner(TargetOf(self.FTree, AType));
      end;
      if (LClass <> TypeClass.RecordType) and (LClass <> TypeClass.ObjectType) then
        return false;
      end;
      LAt := AType;
      LDepth := 0;
      while (LAt <> 0) and (LDepth <= ADAM_TYPES_MAX_DEPTH) do
        LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, LAt);
        for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
          LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
          LKind := self.FTree[LMember].Kind;
          if LKind = NodeKind.FieldDecl then
            if self.DoHoldsOwner(self.DoDeclType(LMember)) then
              return true;
            end;
          end;
          if LKind = NodeKind.EmbedDecl then
            if self.DoHoldsOwner(CanonicalOf(self.FTree, self.FTree.FirstOf(LMember, NodeRole.TypeOf))) then
              return true;
            end;
          end;
        end;
        LAt := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, LAt);
        LDepth := LDepth + 1;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // True when the canonical type AType lives in a slot or a blob and is reached by its
    // address, never an SSA value: a record or an overlay (DoIsFieldAggregate), a static
    // array, whose elements sit one after another at its element's size (Layout), or a set
    // (one bit per member, bit i member low + i: Layout.SetRange; its operations work lane
    // by lane, DoSetLanes), or a mutex (System.Runtime's words, reached by the address
    // lock / trylock hand the runtime; never copied: SEM's SM0621). Such a variable starts
    // zeroed, as every variable without an initializer does here (a record or an overlay by
    // BNF sec 4; a set empty; a mutex free), and a copy of it copies its bytes (DoCopyBytes)
    hidden const method DoIsAggregate(const AType: int64): bool;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      if AType = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      if self.DoIsFieldAggregate(AType) then
        return true;
      end;
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      return (LClass = TypeClass.StaticArray) or (LClass = TypeClass.SetType) or
        (LClass = TypeClass.Mutex);
    end;

    // The byte offset of the field AField from the start of the record or overlay AType: a
    // field's ResolvedOffset counts from its declaring type (through any anonymous record or
    // overlay it sits in), so each parent part between AType and that type adds its Parent
    // node's ResolvedOffset (a field the parent also finds lives in the parent or above; an
    // overlay has no parent). Layout lays AType out first; an offset it never wrote faults
    hidden method DoMemberOffset(const AType: int64; const AField: int64): int64;
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LParent: int64;
      LOffset: int64;
      LPart: int64;
      LDepth: int64;
    begin
      if TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType) < 0 then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_FIELD_OFFSET + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
      end;
      LAt := AType;
      LOffset := 0;
      LDepth := 0;
      while LDepth <= ADAM_TYPES_MAX_DEPTH do
        LParent := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, LAt);
        if (LParent = 0) or (MemberOf(self.FTree, LParent, self.FTree[AField].Text) <> AField) then
          if self.FTree[AField].ResolvedOffset < 0 then
            raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_FIELD_OFFSET + self.FTree[AField].Text);
          end;
          return LOffset + self.FTree[AField].ResolvedOffset;
        end;
        LPart := self.FTree.FirstOf(BodyOf(self.FTree, LAt), NodeRole.Parent);
        if self.FTree[LPart].ResolvedOffset < 0 then
          raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_FIELD_OFFSET + TypeText(self.FTree, LAt));
        end;
        LOffset := LOffset + self.FTree[LPart].ResolvedOffset;
        LAt := LParent;
        LDepth := LDepth + 1;
      end;
      raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_FIELD_OFFSET + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
    end;

    // The address of the field the member access AId names: `R.F` the record's or overlay's
    // address, `P->F` (and `P^.F`, a member of a deref) the ptr's value, moved by the
    // field's offset in it (DoMemberOffset; no move at 0; a field of an anonymous part is
    // named directly); 0 after LW0001 for a bitfield, which has no address of its own (it
    // is read and written through its lane: DoBitRead / DoBitWrite; SEM reports `addr of`
    // one and one given to a var parameter as SM0262, so this is only a guard), and as
    // DoFieldAddress (AWrite: DoAddressFor's write form)
    hidden method DoMemberAddress(const AId: int64; const AWrite: bool): int64;
    var
      LField: int64;
    begin
      LField := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedDecl;
      if (LField <> 0) and (self.FTree[LField].Kind = NodeKind.FieldDecl) and
        (self.FTree[LField].ResolvedBitWidth >= 0) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, "the bitfield '" + self.FTree[LField].Text + "'");
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoFieldAddress(AId, AWrite);
    end;

    // The address of the storage of the field the member access AId names (DoMemberField:
    // a field, an embed, or the field a property is as a whole): DoMemberAddress's address,
    // and for a bitfield its lane's (Layout's ResolvedOffset of a bitfield is the start of
    // its lane); a member reached through an embed (ResolvedEmbed) is at its offset in the
    // embed's own type, from the embed's address (DoEmbedObject); 0 after LW0001 for a
    // member that is no field (a method) or a member of anything but a record, an overlay,
    // an object or a ref. AWrite: DoAddressFor's write form, passed to the record's own
    // address (a `->` operand is read)
    hidden method DoFieldAddress(const AId: int64; const AWrite: bool): int64;
    var
      LField: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LBase: int64;
    begin
      LField := self.DoMemberField(AId);
      if LField = 0 then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.FTree[AId].ResolvedEmbed <> 0 then
        LBase := self.DoEmbedObject(AId, AId, AWrite, LType);
        if LBase = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return self.DoByteOffset(LBase, self.DoMemberOffset(LType, LField), AId);
      end;
      return self.DoFieldAddressIn(AId, self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand),
        self.FTree[AId].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Arrow), LField, AWrite);
    end;

    // The member access whose member is reached through an embed (SEM's ResolvedEmbed) for
    // the access AId: AId itself, or X.P of an indexed property access X.P[i] naming the
    // same property; 0 when AId reaches its member directly
    hidden const method DoEmbedOf(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LOperand: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.MemberExpression then
        if self.FTree[AId].ResolvedEmbed <> 0 then
          return AId;
        end;
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind <> NodeKind.IndexExpression then
        return 0;
      end;
      LOperand := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand);
      if (self.FTree[LOperand].Kind = NodeKind.MemberExpression) and
        (self.FTree[LOperand].ResolvedDecl = self.FTree[AId].ResolvedDecl) and
        (self.FTree[LOperand].ResolvedEmbed <> 0) then
        return LOperand;
      end;
      return 0;
    end;

    // The address of the innermost embed the member access AMember reaches its member
    // through (its ResolvedEmbed, then each EmbedStep child: X.M of an embed E's M is
    // X.E.M, of E's embed F's M X.E.F.M, BNF sec 4), for the access at ANode, in
    // DoAddressFor's write form when AWrite; AType that embed's canonical type (the object
    // or record its member is laid out in). 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoEmbedObject(const AMember: int64; const ANode: int64; const AWrite: bool;
      var AType: int64): int64;
    var
      LEmbed: int64;
      LStep: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LEmbed := self.FTree[AMember].ResolvedEmbed;
      AType := self.DoPartType(LEmbed);
      LAddress := self.DoFieldAddressIn(ANode, self.FTree.FirstOf(AMember, NodeRole.Operand),
        self.FTree[AMember].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Arrow), LEmbed, AWrite);
      if LAddress = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      // Each embed past the first is a field of the embed before it, held by value
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AMember, NodeRole.EmbedStep) - 1 do
        LStep := self.FTree[self.FTree.NthOf(AMember, NodeRole.EmbedStep, LI)].ResolvedDecl;
        LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(LAddress, self.DoMemberOffset(AType, LStep), ANode);
        AType := self.DoPartType(LStep);
      end;
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // The address of the field AField of the value AOperand (through a ptr's value when
    // AArrow: `P->F`), for the access at AId: DoFieldAddress's address, for a bound
    // accessor's field too (DoPropertyGet / DoPropertySet); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoFieldAddressIn(const AId: int64; const AOperand: int64; const AArrow: bool;
      const AField: int64; const AWrite: bool): int64;
    var
      LField: int64;
      LOperand: int64;
      LRecord: int64;
      LBase: int64;
    begin
      LField := AField;
      LOperand := AOperand;
      LRecord := self.DoUsedType(LOperand);
      // `R.F` on a ref: a field of the object it holds (shared: no copy on write)
      if (not AArrow) and self.DoIsRefValue(LRecord) then
        LRecord := TargetOf(self.FTree, LRecord);
        LBase := self.DoRefObject(LOperand);
        if LBase = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return self.DoByteOffset(LBase, self.DoMemberOffset(LRecord, LField), AId);
      end;
      if AArrow then
        if ClassOf(self.FTree, LRecord) <> TypeClass.Pointer then
          self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
          return 0;
        end;
        LRecord := TargetOf(self.FTree, LRecord);
      end;
      if not self.DoIsFieldAggregate(LRecord) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      if AArrow then
        LBase := self.DoValue(LOperand);
      else
        if (not AWrite) and self.DoIsResultCall(LOperand) then
          // a field read of a call's result (`F().X`): the call's result slot
          LBase := self.DoAggregateSource(LOperand);
        else
          LBase := self.DoAddressFor(LOperand, AWrite);
        end;
      end;
      if LBase = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoByteOffset(LBase, self.DoMemberOffset(LRecord, LField), AId);
    end;

    // True when AId (through parentheses) is a call that is no cast: its aggregate result
    // lands in a slot DoAggregateSource reaches (DoCallResult), not a place
    hidden const method DoIsResultCall(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LAt := AId;
      while self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LAt := self.FTree.FirstOf(LAt, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      if OperatorCallOf(self.FTree, LAt) <> 0 then
        return true;
      end;
      return (self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.CallExpression) and (not self.DoIsCastCall(LAt));
    end;

    // The member access a place AId names when it names a bitfield (through parens), else 0
    hidden const method DoBitfieldPlace(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LField: int64;
    begin
      LAt := AId;
      while self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LAt := self.FTree.FirstOf(LAt, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      if self.FTree[LAt].Kind <> NodeKind.MemberExpression then
        return 0;
      end;
      LField := self.FTree[LAt].ResolvedDecl;
      if (LField = 0) or (self.FTree[LField].Kind <> NodeKind.FieldDecl) or
        (self.FTree[LField].ResolvedBitWidth < 0) then
        return 0;
      end;
      return LAt;
    end;

    // The IR type of the lane the bitfield AMember sits in (a member access or a record
    // literal's field init: either's ResolvedDecl is the field): the field's declared type
    // (the Microsoft rule's unit is the field type's size), a bool's lane its byte as uint8
    hidden const method DoLaneType(const AMember: int64): IrType;
    begin
      return self.DoFieldLane(self.FTree[AMember].ResolvedDecl);
    end;

    // The IR type of the lane the bitfield AField sits in (DoLaneType's rule, by the field)
    hidden const method DoFieldLane(const AField: int64): IrType;
    var
      LType: IrType;
    begin
      LType := self.DoIrType(self.DoDeclType(AField));
      if LType = IrType.Bool then
        return IrType.UInt8;
      end;
      return LType;
    end;

    // AValue (an int64) AOp ACount bits (shl, shr or sar), at ANode; AValue itself at 0
    hidden method DoShiftBy(const AOp: IrOp; const AValue: int64; const ACount: int64;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LCount: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      if ACount = 0 then
        return AValue;
      end;
      // every operand is emitted before the instruction that uses it
      LCount := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, ACount, ANode);
      LId := self.DoEmit(AOp, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(AValue);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LCount);
      return LId;
    end;

    // ALeft AOp AMask (and / or with the int64 constant AMask), at ANode
    hidden method DoMaskWith(const AOp: IrOp; const ALeft: int64; const AMask: int64;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LMask: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LMask := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, AMask, ANode);
      LId := self.DoEmit(AOp, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(ALeft);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LMask);
      return LId;
    end;

    // The value of the bitfield the member access AMember names, read from its lane at
    // AAddress: the lane widened to int64, the field moved to the top bits (shl by 64 - bit -
    // width), then down to bit 0 (sar for a signed field, which copies its sign bit down;
    // shr otherwise) and narrowed to the field's type; a bool field is that bit compared
    // with 0. Widening's own extension never matters: the shl drops every bit above the field
    hidden method DoBitRead(const AMember: int64; const AAddress: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoFieldBitRead(self.FTree[AMember].ResolvedDecl, AAddress, AMember);
    end;

    // The value of the bitfield AField read from its lane at AAddress, at ANode (DoBitRead's
    // way, by the field: a property bound to a bitfield reads it so)
    hidden method DoFieldBitRead(const AField: int64; const AAddress: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LBit: int64;
      LWidth: int64;
      LLane: IrType;
      LDown: IrOp;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      LBit := int64(self.FTree[AField].ResolvedBitOffset);
      LWidth := int64(self.FTree[AField].ResolvedBitWidth);
      LLane := self.DoFieldLane(AField);
      LValue := self.DoConvertIr(self.DoLoad(AAddress, LLane, ANode), IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LValue := self.DoShiftBy(IrOp.Shl, LValue, 64 - LBit - LWidth, ANode);
      LDown := IrOp.Shr;
      if IsSignedType(LLane) then
        LDown := IrOp.Sar;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoShiftBy(LDown, LValue, 64 - LWidth, ANode);
      if self.DoIrType(self.DoDeclType(AField)) = IrType.Bool then
        return self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.NotEqual, LValue,
          self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, ANode), ANode);
      end;
      return self.DoConvertIr(LValue, LLane, ANode);
    end;

    // AValue (of the field's type, already computed) stored into the bitfield the member
    // access AMember names, in its lane at AAddress: the lane read and widened to int64, the
    // field's bits cleared (and with the inverted mask), AValue widened, moved up to the
    // field's bit and masked to its width (the low bits a C++ store keeps), or-ed in, and
    // the lane narrowed and stored back; the neighbours' bits come back as they were
    hidden method DoBitWrite(const AMember: int64; const AAddress: int64; const AValue: int64);
    begin
      self.DoFieldBitWrite(self.FTree[AMember].ResolvedDecl, AAddress, AValue, AMember);
    end;

    // AValue stored into the bitfield AField in its lane at AAddress, at ANode (DoBitWrite's
    // way, by the field: a property bound to a bitfield writes it so)
    hidden method DoFieldBitWrite(const AField: int64; const AAddress: int64; const AValue: int64;
      const ANode: int64);
    var
      LBit: int64;
      LMask: int64;
      LLane: IrType;
      LOld: int64;
      LPart: int64;
      LNew: int64;
    begin
      LBit := int64(self.FTree[AField].ResolvedBitOffset);
      LMask := BitMask(int64(self.FTree[AField].ResolvedBitWidth), LBit);
      LLane := self.DoFieldLane(AField);
      LOld := self.DoConvertIr(self.DoLoad(AAddress, LLane, ANode), IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LOld := self.DoMaskWith(IrOp.BitAnd, LOld, ~LMask, ANode);
      LPart := self.DoConvertIr(AValue, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LPart := self.DoShiftBy(IrOp.Shl, LPart, LBit, ANode);
      LPart := self.DoMaskWith(IrOp.BitAnd, LPart, LMask, ANode);
      LNew := self.DoEmit(IrOp.BitOr, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LNew).Operands.Add(LOld);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LNew).Operands.Add(LPart);
      self.DoStore(AAddress, self.DoConvertIr(LNew, LLane, ANode), ANode);
    end;

    // ASize bytes at the address AAddress set to zero, at ANode (a record's start, BNF sec 4)
    hidden method DoFill(const AAddress: int64; const ASize: int64; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Fill, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Imm := ASize;
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(AAddress);
    end;

    // ASize bytes copied from the address ASource to the address ADest, at ANode (a value
    // copy of an aggregate is its bytes, BNF sec 6)
    hidden method DoCopyBytes(const ADest: int64; const ASource: int64; const ASize: int64;
      const ANode: int64);
    var
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Copy, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Imm := ASize;
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(ADest);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(ASource);
    end;

    // The address ABase moved by AOffset bytes, at ANode; ABase itself at 0
    hidden method DoByteOffset(const ABase: int64; const AOffset: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LOffset: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      if AOffset = 0 then
        return ABase;
      end;
      // every operand is emitted before the instruction that uses it
      LOffset := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, AOffset, ANode);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Offset, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(ABase);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LOffset);
      return LId;
    end;

    // The field init AInit of a record literal written into the record at ARecord (of the
    // record type AType): an aggregate field's bytes copied from its value's address
    // (DoAggregateSource), a bitfield written into its lane (DoBitWrite; its offset is the
    // lane's start), any other field's value stored at its offset
    hidden method DoFieldInit(const ARecord: int64; const AType: int64; const AInit: int64);
    var
      LField: int64;
      LFieldType: int64;
      LValueExpr: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      LField := self.FTree[AInit].ResolvedDecl;
      LFieldType := self.DoDeclType(LField);
      LValueExpr := self.FTree.FirstOf(AInit, NodeRole.Value);
      LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(ARecord, self.DoMemberOffset(AType, LField), AInit);
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LFieldType) then
        LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(LValueExpr);
        if LSource <> 0 then
          self.DoCopyBytes(LAddress, LSource, TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LFieldType), AInit);
        end;
        return;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(LValueExpr);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[LField].ResolvedBitWidth >= 0 then
        self.DoBitWrite(AInit, LAddress, LValue);
        return;
      end;
      self.DoStore(LAddress, LValue, AInit);
    end;

    // The record literal AId (BNF sec 6, `T(F: v, ...)`) built in its own slot: the slot
    // zeroed (a field the literal does not name is zero), then each field init written in
    // the order written (DoFieldInit); the slot's address. Building apart from where the
    // value goes keeps `R := T(A: R.B)` reading R before R is written
    hidden method DoRecordLiteral(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType;
      LSlot := self.DoSlot(AId, LType, false);
      if LSlot = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoFill(LSlot, TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType), AId);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AId, NodeRole.Argument) - 1 do
        self.DoFieldInit(LSlot, LType, self.FTree.NthOf(AId, NodeRole.Argument, LI));
      end;
      return LSlot;
    end;

    // The element AExpr of an array literal (BNF sec 6) written at AAddress as a value of
    // its element type AType, at ANode. AOwned (a dynamic array's block, which holds its
    // elements): a managed value stored as an assignment stores it (DoStoreManaged: one more
    // holder), an aggregate copied with its managed values (DoAggregateCopy); else (a static
    // array literal's own slot, as a record literal's: the copy to where the value goes adds
    // the holders) its bytes or its value as they are. False after LW0001
    hidden method DoElementInit(const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64; const AExpr: int64;
      const AOwned: bool; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LSource: int64;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      if self.DoIsAggregate(AType) then
        LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(AExpr);
        if LSource = 0 then
          return false;
        end;
        if AOwned then
          // the block's element is empty: the value is copied in
          if not self.DoCopyValue(AAddress, LSource, AType, ANode) then
            return false;
          end;
        else
          self.DoCopyBytes(AAddress, LSource, TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType), ANode);
        end;
        return true;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(AExpr);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      if AOwned and self.DoIsManaged(AType) then
        return self.DoStoreManaged(AAddress, LValue, AType, ANode) <> 0;
      end;
      self.DoStore(AAddress, LValue, ANode);
      return true;
    end;

    // The array literal AId of a static array type (BNF sec 6) built in its own slot, as a
    // record literal is (DoRecordLiteral): the slot zeroed, then each element written at its
    // index times the element's size in the order written (DoElementInit); the slot's
    // address, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoArrayLiteral(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LElement: int64;
      LStride: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType;
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, LType) <> TypeClass.StaticArray then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LElement := TargetOf(self.FTree, LType);
      LStride := self.DoElementSize(LType);
      LSlot := self.DoSlot(AId, LType, false);
      if LSlot = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoFill(LSlot, TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType), AId);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AId, NodeRole.Element) - 1 do
        LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(LSlot, LI * LStride, AId);
        if not self.DoElementInit(LAddress, LElement,
          self.FTree.FirstOf(self.FTree.NthOf(AId, NodeRole.Element, LI), NodeRole.LowBound), false, AId) then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      return LSlot;
    end;

    // The array literal AId of a dynamic array type (BNF sec 6) as a value: a new block in
    // AId's hidden slot (DoTemporaries made it, one of FManaged by its type). What an
    // earlier pass left there is released (ArrRelease: its elements too), the slot emptied,
    // then ArrSetLength makes the block of the literal's count (none for `[]`: nil) and each
    // element is stored into it as the block's own (DoElementInit owned), in the order
    // written; the slot's block handed back borrowed, as a concatenation's text is (where
    // it goes adds its holder). 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoDynamicLiteral(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LElement: int64;
      LStride: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LMap: int64;
      LOld: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LBlock: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType;
      if not self.DoIsArrayValue(LType) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LElement := TargetOf(self.FTree, LType);
      LStride := self.DoElementSize(LType);
      LCount := self.FTree.CountOf(AId, NodeRole.Element);
      LSlot := self.DoTempSlot(AId);
      LMap := self.DoElementMap(LType, AId);
      if LMap = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LOld := self.DoLoad(LSlot, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.ArrRelease, LOld, LMap, AId) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoStore(LSlot, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, AId), AId);
      if LCount > 0 then
        LArgs := ref Int64List();
        LArgs.Add(LSlot);
        LArgs.Add(self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LCount, AId));
        LArgs.Add(LMap);
        if self.DoCallRuntimeSite(RuntimeRoutine.ArrSetLength, LArgs, AId,
          self.DoArrayWhat(LType)) = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LBlock := self.DoLoad(LSlot, IrType.Pointer, AId);
        for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
          LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(LBlock, ADAM_LOWERING_ARRAY_HEADER + LI * LStride, AId);
          if not self.DoElementInit(LAddress, LElement,
            self.FTree.FirstOf(self.FTree.NthOf(AId, NodeRole.Element, LI), NodeRole.LowBound), true, AId) then
            return 0;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return self.DoLoad(LSlot, IrType.Pointer, AId);
    end;

    // The IR lanes a set of the type ASet is worked in, into ALane / ACount: its whole size
    // as one uint8 / uint16 / uint32 when it is 1, 2 or 4 bytes, else ACount uint64 words
    // (Layout sizes a set so); a lane's bit j is the set's bit (lane * its width + j),
    // little-endian, so a member's bit is the same in every view of the bytes
    hidden method DoSetLanes(const ASet: int64; var ALane: IrType; var ACount: int64);
    var
      LSize: int64;
    begin
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, ASet);
      ACount := 1;
      if LSize = 1 then
        ALane := IrType.UInt8;
        return;
      end;
      if LSize = 2 then
        ALane := IrType.UInt16;
        return;
      end;
      if LSize = 4 then
        ALane := IrType.UInt32;
        return;
      end;
      ALane := IrType.UInt64;
      ACount := LSize div 8;
    end;

    // The set operation of the operator or compound operator AOp into ASetOp (BNF sec 4):
    // BitOr for union (+ | += |=), Subtract for difference (- -=), BitAnd for intersection
    // (* & *= &=); false for any other
    hidden const method DoSetOpOf(const AOp: OperatorKind; var ASetOp: OperatorKind): bool;
    begin
      if (AOp = OperatorKind.Add) or (AOp = OperatorKind.BitOr) or (AOp = OperatorKind.AddAssign) or
        (AOp = OperatorKind.BitOrAssign) then
        ASetOp := OperatorKind.BitOr;
        return true;
      end;
      if (AOp = OperatorKind.Subtract) or (AOp = OperatorKind.SubtractAssign) then
        ASetOp := OperatorKind.Subtract;
        return true;
      end;
      if (AOp = OperatorKind.Multiply) or (AOp = OperatorKind.BitAnd) or
        (AOp = OperatorKind.MultiplyAssign) or (AOp = OperatorKind.BitAndAssign) then
        ASetOp := OperatorKind.BitAnd;
        return true;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // ALeft ASetOp ARight for two lanes of the IR type AType (DoSetOpOf's union, difference
    // or intersection), at ANode: a difference keeps the left's bits the right lacks
    hidden method DoSetCombine(const ASetOp: OperatorKind; const ALeft: int64; const ARight: int64;
      const AType: IrType; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LNot: int64;
    begin
      if ASetOp = OperatorKind.BitOr then
        return self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.BitOr, ALeft, ARight, AType, ANode);
      end;
      if ASetOp = OperatorKind.BitAnd then
        return self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.BitAnd, ALeft, ARight, AType, ANode);
      end;
      LNot := self.DoEmit(IrOp.BitNot, AType, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LNot).Operands.Add(ARight);
      return self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.BitAnd, ALeft, LNot, AType, ANode);
    end;

    // Every lane of the set of the type ASet at ADest set to the lanes at ALeft ASetOp those
    // at ARight (DoSetCombine), lane by lane, each lane's two loads before its store (so
    // ADest may be ALeft or ARight: S -= S empties S), at ANode
    hidden method DoSetLanesInto(const ADest: int64; const ALeft: int64; const ARight: int64;
      const ASet: int64; const ASetOp: OperatorKind; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LLane: IrType;
      LCount: int64;
      LBytes: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LLeft: int64;
      LRight: int64;
    begin
      LLane := IrType.UInt8;
      self.DoSetLanes(ASet, LLane, LCount);
      LBytes := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, ASet) div LCount;
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LLeft := self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(ALeft, LI * LBytes, ANode), LLane, ANode);
        LRight := self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(ARight, LI * LBytes, ANode), LLane, ANode);
        self.DoStore(self.DoByteOffset(ADest, LI * LBytes, ANode),
          self.DoSetCombine(ASetOp, LLeft, LRight, LLane, ANode), ANode);
      end;
    end;

    // The set operation AId (+ - * & | on two sets of its type, BNF sec 4) built in its own
    // slot from its operands' addresses (left first); the slot's address; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoSetOperation(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LSetOp: OperatorKind;
      LLeft: int64;
      LRight: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType;
      LSetOp := OperatorKind.None;
      if not self.DoSetOpOf(self.FTree[AId].Op, LSetOp) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LLeft := self.DoAggregateSource(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Left));
      if LLeft = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LRight := self.DoAggregateSource(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Right));
      if LRight = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LSlot := self.DoSlot(AId, LType, false);
      if LSlot = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoSetLanesInto(LSlot, LLeft, LRight, LType, LSetOp, AId);
      return LSlot;
    end;

    // The compound assignment AId on a set target (+= -= *= &= |=): the value's address
    // first (as the scalar path's order), then the target's once, combined into the target
    // lane by lane (DoSetLanesInto)
    hidden method DoSetCompound(const AId: int64);
    var
      LTarget: int64;
      LSetOp: OperatorKind;
      LSource: int64;
      LDest: int64;
    begin
      LTarget := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target);
      LSetOp := OperatorKind.None;
      if not self.DoSetOpOf(self.FTree[AId].Op, LSetOp) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsBoundProperty(LTarget) then
        // a property bound to its field: the object first, then the value (BNF sec 4)
        LDest := self.DoAddressFor(LTarget, true);
        if LDest = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
        if LSource = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      else
        LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
        if LSource = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LDest := self.DoAddressFor(LTarget, true);
        if LDest = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      self.DoSetLanesInto(LDest, LDest, LSource, self.FTree[LTarget].ResolvedType, LSetOp, AId);
    end;

    // The set comparison AId (= <> >= <=, two sets of one type, BNF sec 4): per lane the
    // bits that decide it (= <>: the two differ, a xor b; >= : the right's bits the left
    // lacks; <= : the left's bits the right lacks), or-ed together at uint64; = >= <= hold
    // when none is set, <> when any is
    hidden method DoSetCompare(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LLeftId: int64;
      LLeftAt: int64;
      LRightAt: int64;
    begin
      LLeftId := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Left);
      LLeftAt := self.DoAggregateSource(LLeftId);
      if LLeftAt = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LRightAt := self.DoAggregateSource(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Right));
      if LRightAt = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoSetCompareAt(LLeftAt, LRightAt, self.DoUsedType(LLeftId), self.FTree[AId].Op, AId);
    end;

    // DoSetCompare's bool for the two sets of the set type AType at ALeftAt and ARightAt,
    // by the operator AOp (= <> >= <=), at ANode (an array's elements too: DoEqualAt)
    hidden method DoSetCompareAt(const ALeftAt: int64; const ARightAt: int64; const AType: int64;
      const AOp: OperatorKind; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LLane: IrType;
      LCount: int64;
      LBytes: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LLeft: int64;
      LRight: int64;
      LBits: int64;
      LAcc: int64;
      LPredicate: IrPredicate;
    begin
      LLane := IrType.UInt8;
      self.DoSetLanes(AType, LLane, LCount);
      LBytes := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType) div LCount;
      LAcc := 0;
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LLeft := self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(ALeftAt, LI * LBytes, ANode), LLane, ANode);
        LRight := self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(ARightAt, LI * LBytes, ANode), LLane, ANode);
        if AOp = OperatorKind.GreaterEqual then
          LBits := self.DoSetCombine(OperatorKind.Subtract, LRight, LLeft, LLane, ANode);
        else
          if AOp = OperatorKind.LessEqual then
            LBits := self.DoSetCombine(OperatorKind.Subtract, LLeft, LRight, LLane, ANode);
          else
            LBits := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.BitXor, LLeft, LRight, LLane, ANode);
          end;
        end;
        LBits := self.DoConvertIr(LBits, IrType.UInt64, ANode);
        if LAcc = 0 then
          LAcc := LBits;
        else
          LAcc := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.BitOr, LAcc, LBits, IrType.UInt64, ANode);
        end;
      end;
      LPredicate := IrPredicate.Equal;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.NotEqual then
        LPredicate := IrPredicate.NotEqual;
      end;
      return self.DoCompareWith(LPredicate, LAcc, self.DoConstant(IrType.UInt64, 0, ANode), ANode);
    end;

    // `X in S` AId on a set S (BNF sec 4): X's value (SEM converted it to the element type)
    // less the set's low member is its bit; one unsigned compare decides it is inside the
    // set's members (any value outside, below too, is in no set), and only then is its
    // byte loaded and the bit tested, in a block of its own (never a load past the set); a
    // join's phi takes false from the range test's edge. `X in [a, b..c]` with no set type
    // tests the items (DoInItems)
    hidden method DoSetIn(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LLeftId: int64;
      LRightId: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LSet: int64;
      LLow: int64;
      LHigh: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LSetAt: int64;
      LInRange: int64;
      LStart: int64;
      LTest: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
      LByteAt: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LByte: int64;
      LBitAt: int64;
      LBit: int64;
      LHas: int64;
      LTestEnd: int64;
    begin
      LLeftId := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Left);
      LRightId := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Right);
      LSet := self.DoUsedType(LRightId);
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, LSet) <> TypeClass.SetType then
        LAt := LRightId;
        while self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
          LAt := self.FTree.FirstOf(LAt, NodeRole.Operand);
        end;
        if self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.SetLiteral then
          return self.DoInItems(AId, LAt);
        end;
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      if not SetRange(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LSet, LLow, LHigh) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(LLeftId);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LIndex := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.Sub, self.DoConvertIr(LValue, IrType.Int64, AId),
        self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LLow, AId), IrType.Int64, AId);
      LSetAt := self.DoAggregateSource(LRightId);
      if LSetAt = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LInRange := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.ULessEqual, self.DoConvertIr(LIndex, IrType.UInt64, AId),
        self.DoConstant(IrType.UInt64, LHigh - LLow, AId), AId);
      LStart := self.FBlock;
      LTest := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(LInRange, LTest, LJoin, AId);
      self.FBlock := LTest;
      // the member's byte (its bit div 8), then its bit in that byte (its bit mod 8); the
      // byte index is emitted before the offset that uses it
      LByteAt := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.Shr, LIndex, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 3, AId),
        IrType.Int64, AId);
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Offset, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Operands.Add(LSetAt);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Operands.Add(LByteAt);
      LByte := self.DoConvertIr(self.DoLoad(LAddress, IrType.UInt8, AId), IrType.Int64, AId);
      LBitAt := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.BitAnd, LIndex, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 7, AId),
        IrType.Int64, AId);
      LBit := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.BitAnd, self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.Shr, LByte, LBitAt, IrType.Int64, AId),
        self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 1, AId), IrType.Int64, AId);
      LHas := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.NotEqual, LBit, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, AId), AId);
      LTestEnd := self.FBlock;
      self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, AId);
      self.FBlock := LJoin;
      return self.DoJoinOf(IrType.Bool, LInRange, LStart, LHas, LTestEnd, AId);
    end;

    // `X in [a, b..c]` AId with no set type around the literal ALiteral (BNF F53): X equals
    // an item, or lies in a span lo..hi (lo <= X <= hi, as X's type orders; a span with lo
    // above hi holds nothing); every item is evaluated, the tests or-ed (an empty literal
    // holds nothing)
    hidden method DoInItems(const AId: int64; const ALiteral: int64): int64;
    var
      LLeftId: int64;
      LType: IrType;
      LValue: int64;
      LAcc: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LItem: int64;
      LHighExpr: int64;
      LLo: int64;
      LHi: int64;
      LTest: int64;
      LAbove: IrPredicate;
      LBelow: IrPredicate;
    begin
      LLeftId := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Left);
      LType := self.DoIrType(self.DoUsedType(LLeftId));
      LAbove := IrPredicate.Equal;
      LBelow := IrPredicate.Equal;
      if ((not IsIntegerType(LType)) and (LType <> IrType.Bool)) or
        (not self.DoPredicateOf(OperatorKind.GreaterEqual, LType, LAbove)) or
        (not self.DoPredicateOf(OperatorKind.LessEqual, LType, LBelow)) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(LLeftId);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LAcc := self.DoConstant(IrType.UInt8, 0, AId);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ALiteral, NodeRole.Element) - 1 do
        LItem := self.FTree.NthOf(ALiteral, NodeRole.Element, LI);
        LLo := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(LItem, NodeRole.LowBound));
        if LLo = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LHighExpr := self.FTree.FirstOf(LItem, NodeRole.HighBound);
        if LHighExpr = 0 then
          LTest := self.DoConvertIr(self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.Equal, LValue, LLo, AId), IrType.UInt8, AId);
        else
          LHi := self.DoValue(LHighExpr);
          if LHi = 0 then
            return 0;
          end;
          LTest := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.BitAnd,
            self.DoConvertIr(self.DoCompareWith(LAbove, LValue, LLo, AId), IrType.UInt8, AId),
            self.DoConvertIr(self.DoCompareWith(LBelow, LValue, LHi, AId), IrType.UInt8, AId),
            IrType.UInt8, AId);
        end;
        LAcc := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.BitOr, LAcc, LTest, IrType.UInt8, AId);
      end;
      return self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.NotEqual, LAcc, self.DoConstant(IrType.UInt8, 0, AId), AId);
    end;

    // The set literal ALiteral of the set type ASet written into ABytes at AOffset: each
    // member an item names (an element, or a span lo..hi; lo above hi names none) sets its
    // bit (member less the set's low member: Layout.SetRange), the values read in the
    // element type they converted to (DoConstBits); false when an item did not fold, or a
    // member lies outside the set (SEM's SM0200 reports a constant one). AOpen: a single item
    // that did not fold is skipped (its bit is set at run time, DoSetLiteralSlot); a span
    // with a bound that did not fold is still false
    hidden method DoSetBytes(const ALiteral: int64; const ASet: int64; var ABytes: ByteArray;
      const AOffset: int64; const AOpen: bool): bool;
    var
      LLow: int64;
      LHigh: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LItem: int64;
      LLowExpr: int64;
      LHighExpr: int64;
      LFrom: int64;
      LTo: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LBit: int64;
    begin
      if not SetRange(self.FTree, self.FTarget, ASet, LLow, LHigh) then
        return false;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ALiteral, NodeRole.Element) - 1 do
        LItem := self.FTree.NthOf(ALiteral, NodeRole.Element, LI);
        LLowExpr := self.FTree.FirstOf(LItem, NodeRole.LowBound);
        LHighExpr := self.FTree.FirstOf(LItem, NodeRole.HighBound);
        if AOpen and (LHighExpr = 0) and (not self.DoIsFolded(LLowExpr)) then
          skip;
        end;
        if not self.DoIsFolded(LLowExpr) then
          return false;
        end;
        LFrom := self.DoConstBits(LLowExpr, self.DoUsedType(LLowExpr));
        LTo := LFrom;
        if LHighExpr <> 0 then
          if not self.DoIsFolded(LHighExpr) then
            return false;
          end;
          LTo := self.DoConstBits(LHighExpr, self.DoUsedType(LHighExpr));
        end;
        if LFrom <= LTo then
          if (LFrom < LLow) or (LTo > LHigh) then
            return false;
          end;
          for LValue := LFrom to LTo do
            LBit := LValue - LLow;
            // uint8 | uint8 is computed at int32 (C++'s promotion): back to the byte
            ABytes[AOffset + LBit div 8] := uint8(ABytes[AOffset + LBit div 8] |
              uint8(uint64(1) shl uint64(LBit mod 8)));
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The set literal AId of a set type as a value: its bytes (DoSetBytes) in a read-only
    // blob of their own, internal, named by ADAM_LOWERING_SET_SYMBOL and its data id; its
    // address. One with a single item that is not constant is built at run time
    // (DoSetLiteralSlot: such an item outside the set raises, pcpp's EXC_SET_RANGE)
    hidden method DoSetLiteral(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LBytes: ByteArray;
      LK: int64;
      LData: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType;
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, LType) <> TypeClass.SetType then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_SET_TYPE + self.FTree.ConstructText(AId));
      end;
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType);
      setlength(LBytes, LSize);
      for LK := 0 to LSize - 1 do
        LBytes[LK] := 0;
      end;
      if not self.DoSetBytes(AId, LType, LBytes, 0, false) then
        return self.DoSetLiteralSlot(AId, LType);
      end;
      LData := self.DoHelperData(ADAM_LOWERING_SET_SYMBOL,
        TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType), AId);
      for LK := 0 to LSize - 1 do
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(LBytes[LK]);
      end;
      self.FModule.DataAt(LData).Internal := true;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := LData;
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // The set literal AId of the set type AType with a single item that is not constant
    // (DoSetLiteral): built in a slot of its own each time it runs, zeroed, its constant
    // items' bytes stored (DoSetBytes with AOpen), then each open item's bit set at run time
    // in the literal's order (DoSetMemberAt); the slot's address; 0 after LW0001 (a span
    // with a bound that is not constant)
    hidden method DoSetLiteralSlot(const AId: int64; const AType: int64): int64;
    var
      LSize: int64;
      LBytes: ByteArray;
      LK: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LItem: int64;
      LLowExpr: int64;
    begin
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType);
      setlength(LBytes, LSize);
      for LK := 0 to LSize - 1 do
        LBytes[LK] := 0;
      end;
      if not self.DoSetBytes(AId, AType, LBytes, 0, true) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, "a set literal's span that is not constant");
        return 0;
      end;
      LSlot := self.DoSlot(AId, AType, false);
      if LSlot = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoFill(LSlot, LSize, AId);
      for LK := 0 to LSize - 1 do
        if LBytes[LK] <> 0 then
          self.DoStore(self.DoByteOffset(LSlot, LK, AId),
            self.DoConstant(IrType.UInt8, int64(LBytes[LK]), AId), AId);
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AId, NodeRole.Element) - 1 do
        LItem := self.FTree.NthOf(AId, NodeRole.Element, LI);
        LLowExpr := self.FTree.FirstOf(LItem, NodeRole.LowBound);
        if (self.FTree.FirstOf(LItem, NodeRole.HighBound) = 0) and (not self.DoIsFolded(LLowExpr)) then
          if not self.DoSetMemberAt(LSlot, AType, LLowExpr, AId) then
            return 0;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return LSlot;
    end;

    // The bit of the open item AExpr (a set literal's single item that did not fold) set in
    // the set of the type ASet at ASlot, at ANode: its value (widened to int64) less the
    // set's low member is its bit. A value outside the set's members (one unsigned compare,
    // as DoSetIn's) goes to a block of its own that raises (the runtime's SetRange: pcpp's
    // EXC_SET_RANGE, its text naming the value) and never returns; false after LW0001
    hidden method DoSetMemberAt(const ASlot: int64; const ASet: int64; const AExpr: int64;
      const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LLow: int64;
      LHigh: int64;
      LType: IrType;
      LValue: int64;
      LWide: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LInRange: int64;
      LBad: int64;
      LGood: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LByteAt: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LByte: int64;
      LBit: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoIrType(self.DoUsedType(AExpr));
      if (not SetRange(self.FTree, self.FTarget, ASet, LLow, LHigh)) or
        ((not IsIntegerType(LType)) and (LType <> IrType.Bool)) then
        self.DoRefuse(AExpr, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AExpr));
        return false;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(AExpr);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LWide := self.DoConvertIr(LValue, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LIndex := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.Sub, LWide, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LLow, ANode),
        IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LInRange := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.ULessEqual, self.DoConvertIr(LIndex, IrType.UInt64, ANode),
        self.DoConstant(IrType.UInt64, LHigh - LLow, ANode), ANode);
      LBad := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LGood := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(LInRange, LGood, LBad, ANode);
      // outside the set: SetRange(value, low, high) raises; the block still ends in a jump,
      // as every block does
      self.FBlock := LBad;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(LWide);
      LArgs.Add(self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LLow, ANode));
      LArgs.Add(self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LHigh, ANode));
      if self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.SetRange, LArgs, ANode) = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoJumpTo(LGood, ANode);
      // inside: the member's byte (its bit div 8) or-ed with its bit (its bit mod 8)
      self.FBlock := LGood;
      LByteAt := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.Shr, LIndex, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 3, ANode),
        IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Offset, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Operands.Add(ASlot);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Operands.Add(LByteAt);
      LByte := self.DoLoad(LAddress, IrType.UInt8, ANode);
      LBit := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.Shl, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 1, ANode),
        self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.BitAnd, LIndex, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 7, ANode), IrType.Int64, ANode),
        IrType.Int64, ANode);
      self.DoStore(LAddress, self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.BitOr, LByte,
        self.DoConvertIr(LBit, IrType.UInt8, ANode), IrType.UInt8, ANode), ANode);
      return true;
    end;

    // The address an aggregate value AId (DoIsAggregate) is copied from: the place it names
    // (through parentheses), a record literal's slot (DoRecordLiteral), a set literal's
    // read-only bytes (DoSetLiteral), a set operation's slot (DoSetOperation), a call's
    // result slot (DoCallResult), an assignment's target (DoAssignedValue); 0 after LW0001
    // for any other aggregate value
    hidden method DoAggregateSource(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LAt := AId;
      while self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LAt := self.FTree.FirstOf(LAt, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      if self.DoIsPackAccess(LAt) then
        return self.DoPackSourceAddress(LAt);
      end;
      // an assignment's value: its target after the write
      if self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.AssignExpression then
        return self.DoAssignedValue(LAt, AssignedForm.Aggregate);
      end;
      if ((self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.CallExpression) and (not self.DoIsCastCall(LAt))) or
        (OperatorCallOf(self.FTree, LAt) <> 0) then
        return self.DoCallResult(LAt);
      end;
      // an await's result, in the task's object
      if self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.AwaitExpression then
        return self.DoAwaitResult(LAt);
      end;
      // a property read through its accessors: its call's result slot, or a bound field
      if self.DoIsPropertyAccess(LAt) then
        return self.DoPropertyGet(LAt);
      end;
      if self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.RecordLiteral then
        return self.DoRecordLiteral(LAt);
      end;
      if self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.ArrayLiteral then
        return self.DoArrayLiteral(LAt);
      end;
      if self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.VarargsExpression then
        return self.DoVarargsPlace(LAt);
      end;
      if self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.SetLiteral then
        return self.DoSetLiteral(LAt);
      end;
      if (self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.BinaryExpression) and
        (ClassOf(self.FTree, self.FTree[LAt].ResolvedType) = TypeClass.SetType) then
        return self.DoSetOperation(LAt);
      end;
      if not self.DoIsPlace(LAt) then
        self.DoRefuse(LAt, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(LAt));
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoAddress(LAt);
    end;

    // The address of the object `self` (AId a SelfExpression) or `parent` (a
    // ParentExpression: self's parent part, at its Parent node's offset in self's type)
    // stand for in the current method: self's value (FSelfSlot); 0 after LW0001 where the
    // current function has no self (an init, a done, an accessor: their atoms)
    hidden method DoSelfAddress(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LSelf: int64;
      LOwner: int64;
      LPart: int64;
    begin
      if self.FSelfSlot = 0 then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId) + " outside a method");
        return 0;
      end;
      LSelf := self.DoLoad(self.FSelfSlot, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.SelfExpression then
        return LSelf;
      end;
      LOwner := self.DoOwnerType(AId);
      LPart := self.FTree.FirstOf(BodyOf(self.FTree, LOwner), NodeRole.Parent);
      if (LPart = 0) or (self.FTree[LPart].ResolvedOffset < 0) then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_FIELD_OFFSET + TypeText(self.FTree, LOwner));
      end;
      return self.DoByteOffset(LSelf, self.FTree[LPart].ResolvedOffset, AId);
    end;

    // The address the place AId stands for, to read it (DoAddressFor's read form)
    hidden method DoAddress(const AId: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoAddressFor(AId, false);
    end;

    // The address the place AId stands for: a name's (its slot, the address a reference
    // parameter's slot holds, or a module variable's data), a deref's (its operand's value),
    // an element's (DoElementAddress), a field's (DoMemberAddress), through parentheses; 0
    // after LW0001 when it names nothing that has one. AWrite: the place is about to be
    // written (an assignment's target, a var argument, `addr of`, a text's slot): every
    // dynamic array on the way to it (an element of one, a field of such an element, an
    // element of an element) is made its holder's alone first (ArrUnique: copy on write).
    // The form passes through parentheses, an indexed array and a record whose field is
    // named; whatever is read on the way (an index, a deref's or a `->` operand) is read.
    // Under the target of an assignment used as a value each place's address is made once
    // (FPinned, DoAssignedValue)
    hidden method DoAddressFor(const AId: int64; const AWrite: bool): int64;
    var
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      if (self.FPinned = nil) or not self.DoIsPinned(AId, false) then
        return self.DoAddressMade(AId, AWrite);
      end;
      LAddress := self.FPinned.Find(AId);
      if LAddress >= 0 then
        return LAddress;
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoAddressMade(AId, AWrite);
      if LAddress <> 0 then
        self.FPinned.Put(AId, LAddress);
      end;
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // True when AId is the target of the assignment being lowered as a value (FPinRoot) or
    // under it; AStrict: strictly under it
    hidden const method DoIsPinned(const AId: int64; const AStrict: bool): bool;
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LAt := AId;
      if AStrict then
        if LAt = self.FPinRoot then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      while LAt <> 0 do
        if LAt = self.FPinRoot then
          return true;
        end;
        LAt := self.FTree.ParentOf(LAt);
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // DoAddressFor's address of the place AId, made
    hidden method DoAddressMade(const AId: int64; const AWrite: bool): int64;
    var
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      LKind := NameKindOf(self.FTree, AId);
      if LKind = NodeKind.ParenExpression then
        return self.DoAddressFor(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand), AWrite);
      end;
      if self.DoIsDeref(AId) then
        return self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand));
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.IndexExpression then
        return self.DoElementAddress(AId, AWrite);
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.MemberExpression then
        return self.DoMemberAddress(AId, AWrite);
      end;
      if (LKind = NodeKind.SelfExpression) or (LKind = NodeKind.ParentExpression) then
        return self.DoSelfAddress(AId);
      end;
      if self.DoIsAsObject(AId) then
        return self.DoAsObject(AId, AWrite);
      end;
      if LKind <> NodeKind.NameExpression then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LDecl := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedDecl;
      if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FDataOf[LDecl] <> 0) then
        return self.DoDataAddress(LDecl, AId);
      end;
      if (LDecl = 0) or (self.FSlotOf[LDecl] = 0) then
        if LDecl = 0 then
          self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        else
          // a local refused at its declaration was reported there
          if not self.FSlotRefused[LDecl] then
            self.DoRefuse(AId, "a use of " + self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(LDecl));
          end;
        end;
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.FByRef[LDecl] then
        return self.DoLoad(self.FSlotOf[LDecl], IrType.Pointer, AId);
      end;
      return self.FSlotOf[LDecl];
    end;

    // The slot the call AId of a routine with an aggregate result leaves that result in
    // (DoCall keys it by AId: the hidden result slot, or the register's bytes stored there);
    // 0 when the call was refused
    hidden method DoCallResult(const AId: int64): int64;
    begin
      if self.DoCall(AId) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.FSlotOf[AId] = 0 then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_CALL_RESULT + self.FTree.ConstructText(AId));
      end;
      return self.FSlotOf[AId];
    end;

    // The operand the argument AArg passes for the parameter AParam: its address for a var
    // parameter, for a const one by reference the address of its value (DoAggregateSource,
    // a text's DoManagedReference: a value that is no place gets one); for an aggregate by copy
    // (FByCopy) the address of a slot keyed by AArg its bytes are copied into (one that
    // holds texts: the source's own address, the callee makes its copy, DoParams); for an
    // aggregate in a register its bytes loaded as that register's integer (DoAggregateIr);
    // else its value (a managed one borrowed: a value parameter's callee adds its own
    // holder, a const one's borrows it too, so an argument the callee could drop is held
    // by the call: DoHeldValue); a value object whose type runs code where it is copied
    // or ended, by value, the callee's own (DoOwnArgument). 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoArgument(const AArg: int64; const AParam: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoDeclType(AParam);
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) and self.DoHasLifetime(LType) and
        (not self.FTree[AParam].HasFlag(NodeFlag.ConstParam)) and
        ((not self.FByRef[AParam]) or self.FByCopy[AParam]) then
        return self.DoOwnArgument(AArg, AParam, LType);
      end;
      if self.FByCopy[AParam] then
        LSource := self.DoArgumentSource(AArg, LType);
        if (LSource = 0) or self.DoHoldsManaged(LType) then
          return LSource;
        end;
        LSlot := self.DoSlot(AArg, LType, false);
        if LSlot = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        self.DoCopyBytes(LSlot, LSource, TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType), AArg);
        return LSlot;
      end;
      if self.FByRef[AParam] then
        if self.FTree[AParam].HasFlag(NodeFlag.VarParam) then
          return self.DoReachArgument(self.DoAnchoredAddress(AArg, true, false), AArg, LType);
        end;
        if self.DoIsManaged(LType) then
          return self.DoAnchoredReference(AArg);
        end;
        return self.DoReachArgument(self.DoAnchoredAddress(AArg, false, self.DoIsAggregate(LType)), AArg, LType);
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        LSource := self.DoArgumentSource(AArg, LType);
        if LSource = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return self.DoLoad(LSource, self.DoAggregateIr(LType), AArg);
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(AArg);
      if (LValue = 0) or not self.DoNeedsHold(AArg, AParam) then
        return LValue;
      end;
      return self.DoHeldValue(AArg, LValue, LType);
    end;

    // The address of the value of the argument AArg (DoAggregateSource) as the parameter's
    // canonical type AType reaches it (DoReachArgument: a descendant given where an
    // ancestor is wanted gives that ancestor's part, copied from there); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoArgumentSource(const AArg: int64; const AType: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoReachArgument(self.DoAggregateSource(AArg), AArg, AType);
    end;

    // The address AAddress of the argument AArg (or of its value) as the parameter's
    // canonical type AType reaches it (BNF sec 6: a var or const parameter of a record, object or
    // interface takes a descendant, Types.ReachesAs): moved to AType's part of it
    // (DoUpcast: a parent part's offset, an interface's itable word, I2); AAddress itself
    // for one type, any other type, or 0 (after LW0001)
    hidden method DoReachArgument(const AAddress: int64; const AArg: int64; const AType: int64): int64;
    var
      LFrom: int64;
    begin
      LFrom := self.FTree[AArg].ResolvedType;
      if (AAddress = 0) or (LFrom = AType) or not self.DoIsReachable(LFrom) or not self.DoIsReachable(AType) or
        not IsAncestorOf(self.FTree, AType, LFrom) then
        return AAddress;
      end;
      return self.DoUpcast(AAddress, LFrom, AType, AArg);
    end;

    // True when a reference to a value of the canonical type AType may stand for one of an
    // ancestor (DoReachOffset): a record, an object or an interface
    hidden const method DoIsReachable(const AType: int64): bool;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      if AType = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      return (LClass = TypeClass.RecordType) or (LClass = TypeClass.ObjectType) or
        (LClass = TypeClass.InterfaceType);
    end;

    // The argument AArg for the value parameter AParam of the canonical type AType, whose
    // values run code where they are copied or ended (DoHasLifetime): the callee's own
    // value (it ends it, DoOwnParam) in a zeroed slot of the call's: a call's result moved
    // in (DoMoveObject: its temporary no longer live), any other value copied by its
    // type's copy (DoCopyValue, BNF sec 4 O5); by copy that slot's address, in a register
    // its bytes as that register's integer (DoAggregateIr); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoOwnArgument(const AArg: int64; const AParam: int64; const AType: int64): int64;
    var
      LSource: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LFrom: int64;
    begin
      LSource := self.DoArgumentSource(AArg, AType);
      if LSource = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType);
      LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(AArg, LSize, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType));
      // zeroed each time it runs: a loop's next call starts from nothing too
      self.DoFill(LSlot, LSize, AArg);
      LFrom := self.DoMoveSource(AArg);
      if (LFrom <> 0) and self.DoIsCallSite(LFrom) then
        self.DoMoveObject(LSlot, LSource, LFrom, AType, AArg);
      else
        if not self.DoCopyValue(LSlot, LSource, AType, AArg) then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      if self.FByCopy[AParam] then
        return LSlot;
      end;
      return self.DoLoad(LSlot, self.DoAggregateIr(AType), AArg);
    end;

    // The value AValue of the argument AArg (of the parameter's canonical type AType) given
    // a holder of the call's own (SU2.8 e3): stored into the hold DoArgHolds made at its
    // root (an assignment's store: a holder added), released as its full expression ends
    // (DoEndTemporary) or by an exit or an unwind, so the borrowed parameter's block lives
    // through the call whatever the callee does; AValue, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoHeldValue(const AArg: int64; const AValue: int64; const AType: int64): int64;
    var
      LRoot: int64;
    begin
      LRoot := self.DoArgRoot(AArg);
      if (self.FTempOf[LRoot] = 0) or not self.FHeld[LRoot] then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_HOLD + self.FTree.ConstructText(AArg));
      end;
      if self.DoStoreManaged(self.FTempOf[LRoot], AValue, AType, AArg) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return AValue;
    end;

    // The argument AArg through its parentheses: the node a hold is kept at (DoArgHolds)
    hidden const method DoArgRoot(const AArg: int64): int64;
    var
      LRoot: int64;
    begin
      LRoot := AArg;
      while self.FTree[LRoot].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LRoot := self.FTree.FirstOf(LRoot, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      return LRoot;
    end;

    // True when the argument AArg for the parameter AParam must be held by the call (SU2.8
    // e3): the parameter is a const managed one passed by value (DoOwnParam borrows it) of
    // a routine with a body in Adam (an external's code never counts), and AArg is no
    // value the call already keeps alive (DoStableArg), nor one the callee's write summary
    // proves it cannot drop (DoMayDrop, SU2.8 e4). A const one by reference (C++
    // linkage) aliases the caller's place (BNF sec 3: the callee reads it as it changes),
    // so its place's anchor is held instead (DoAnchoredReference)
    hidden const method DoNeedsHold(const AArg: int64; const AParam: int64): bool;
    var
      LSig: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoIsManaged(self.DoDeclType(AParam)) then
        return false;
      end;
      if (not self.FTree[AParam].HasFlag(NodeFlag.ConstParam)) or self.FTree[AParam].HasFlag(NodeFlag.VarParam) then
        return false;
      end;
      LSig := self.FTree.ParentOf(AParam);
      if PassedByReference(self.FTree, AParam, self.DoLinkageOf(LSig)) then
        return false;
      end;
      if self.FTree.FirstOf(LSig, NodeRole.External) <> 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      if self.DoStableArg(AArg) then
        return false;
      end;
      return self.DoMayDrop(LSig, self.FTree.ParentOf(AArg), AArg);
    end;

    // True when the argument AArg's value lives through any call it is passed to, whatever
    // the callee does (SU2.8 e3): a constant (a literal's block, nil); a temporary's own
    // reference (a call's result, a concatenation's, a ref new's: DoTemporaries' hidden
    // slot, ended only after the call); the value of a local or a parameter of this routine
    // whose slot nothing outside its own code reaches (DoPins), a parameter by value (its
    // own holder, or its caller's guarantee). A field, an element, a deref, a module
    // variable, a var parameter, a converted value and any other expression may be dropped
    // by the callee: not stable
    hidden const method DoStableArg(const AArg: int64): bool;
    var
      LRoot: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      if (self.FTree[AArg].ResolvedConvert <> 0) and (not self.DoKeepsBlock(AArg)) then
        return false;
      end;
      LRoot := self.DoArgRoot(AArg);
      if (LRoot <> AArg) and (self.FTree[LRoot].ResolvedConvert <> 0) and (not self.DoKeepsBlock(LRoot)) then
        return false;
      end;
      if (self.FTree[LRoot].ResolvedConst.Kind <> ConstKind.Unknown) or
        (self.FTree[LRoot].Kind = NodeKind.NilLiteral) then
        return true;
      end;
      if (self.FTempOf[LRoot] <> 0) and not self.FHeld[LRoot] then
        return true;
      end;
      if self.FTree[LRoot].Kind <> NodeKind.NameExpression then
        return false;
      end;
      LDecl := self.FTree[LRoot].ResolvedDecl;
      if (LDecl = 0) or self.FUnpinned[LDecl] then
        return false;
      end;
      // a parameter by value: its own copy, or a const one borrowed under the caller's
      // guarantee (its argument held when its callee could drop it); one by reference (a
      // var one, a const one under C++ linkage) aliases the caller's place, whose value may
      // change under it (its storage is the caller's to keep: DoAnchoredReference)
      if self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.Param then
        return not self.FByRef[LDecl];
      end;
      return (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.VarDecl) and (self.FTree.RoleOf(LDecl) = NodeRole.Local);
    end;

    // The anchor of the place APlace (SU2.8 e3): the ref, dynamic array or text whose block
    // its storage lies in, so a callee given its address works in that block (a field of a
    // ref's object, through value fields and static elements; an element of a dynamic
    // array or a text); 0 when its storage is no block's (a local, a parameter, a module
    // variable, self, parent, a deref, a call's result: storage the routine or its caller
    // keeps for the call)
    hidden const method DoAnchorOf(const APlace: int64): int64;
    var
      LNode: int64;
      LOperand: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LDepth: int64;
    begin
      LNode := self.DoArgRoot(APlace);
      LDepth := 0;
      while LDepth <= ADAM_TYPES_MAX_DEPTH do
        if (self.FTree[LNode].Kind <> NodeKind.MemberExpression) and
          (self.FTree[LNode].Kind <> NodeKind.IndexExpression) then
          return 0;
        end;
        if self.FTree[LNode].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Arrow) then
          return 0;
        end;
        LOperand := self.DoArgRoot(self.FTree.FirstOf(LNode, NodeRole.Operand));
        LType := self.DoUsedType(LOperand);
        if self.FTree[LNode].Kind = NodeKind.MemberExpression then
          if self.DoIsRefValue(LType) then
            return LOperand;
          end;
          if not self.DoIsFieldAggregate(LType) then
            return 0;
          end;
        else
          if self.DoIsArrayValue(LType) or self.DoIsText(LType) then
            return LOperand;
          end;
          if ClassOf(self.FTree, LType) <> TypeClass.StaticArray then
            return 0;
          end;
        end;
        LNode := LOperand;
        LDepth := LDepth + 1;
      end;
      return 0;
    end;

    // The anchor of the object a method or an accessor runs on, given as the expression
    // AOperand (reached through a ptr's value when AArrow: no anchor): a ref's own block,
    // else its place's anchor (DoAnchorOf)
    hidden const method DoObjectAnchor(const AOperand: int64; const AArrow: bool): int64;
    var
      LRoot: int64;
    begin
      if AArrow then
        return 0;
      end;
      LRoot := self.DoArgRoot(AOperand);
      if self.DoIsRefValue(self.DoUsedType(LRoot)) then
        return LRoot;
      end;
      return self.DoAnchorOf(LRoot);
    end;

    // True when the anchor AAnchor (0: none) needs the call's hold: a callee could drop its
    // block (DoStableArg)
    hidden const method DoAnchorHeld(const AAnchor: int64): bool;
    begin
      return (AAnchor <> 0) and not self.DoStableArg(AAnchor);
    end;

    // The anchor AAnchor (DoAnchorOf / DoObjectAnchor; 0: none) held for the call whose
    // address is made next, at ANode (SU2.8 e3): its value made now and stored into its
    // hold (DoArgHolds made it: an assignment's store, a holder added), handed to the
    // address's own reading (FPrimed); a write's text or dynamic array held after its copy
    // on write instead (FHoldAfter: DoHoldWritten). Nothing when the block lives through
    // the call anyway (DoAnchorHeld); false after LW0001
    hidden method DoAnchorBegin(const AAnchor: int64; const AWrite: bool; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoAnchorHeld(AAnchor) then
        return true;
      end;
      // no callee of the access can drop the block (DoHoldAnchor left it unheld, SU2.8 e4)
      if (self.FDroppedIn[AAnchor] = self.FFunction + 1) and
        not (self.FHeld[AAnchor] and (self.FHeldIn[AAnchor] = self.FFunction)) then
        return true;
      end;
      if (self.FTempOf[AAnchor] = 0) or not self.FHeld[AAnchor] then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_HOLD + self.FTree.ConstructText(AAnchor));
      end;
      LType := self.DoUsedType(AAnchor);
      if AWrite and (self.DoIsArrayValue(LType) or self.DoIsText(LType)) then
        self.FHoldAfter[AAnchor] := true;
        return true;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoManagedValue(AAnchor);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      if self.DoStoreManaged(self.FTempOf[AAnchor], LValue, LType, ANode) = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      self.FPrimed[AAnchor] := LValue;
      return true;
    end;

    // The anchor AAnchor's call address made: its value no longer handed out
    // (DoAnchorBegin); a write's hold the copy on write never filled (DoHoldWritten) is a
    // broken invariant (the address reached its block another way), unless the address
    // was refused (AMade false: LW0001 reported)
    hidden method DoAnchorEnd(const AAnchor: int64; const AMade: bool);
    begin
      if AAnchor = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.FPrimed[AAnchor] := 0;
      if self.FHoldAfter[AAnchor] and AMade then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_HOLD_WRITE + self.FTree.ConstructText(AAnchor));
      end;
      self.FHoldAfter[AAnchor] := false;
    end;

    // The block ABlock a write's copy on write gave the text or dynamic array AOperand (of
    // the canonical type AType) held as its anchor's hold when the call being lowered waits
    // for it (FHoldAfter: DoAnchorBegin), at ANode; false after LW0001
    hidden method DoHoldWritten(const AOperand: int64; const ABlock: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LRoot: int64;
    begin
      LRoot := self.DoArgRoot(AOperand);
      if (ABlock = 0) or not self.FHoldAfter[LRoot] then
        return true;
      end;
      self.FHoldAfter[LRoot] := false;
      return self.DoStoreManaged(self.FTempOf[LRoot], ABlock, AType, ANode) <> 0;
    end;

    // The address of the argument AArg's place for a by-reference parameter: a var one's
    // write form when AWrite, else a const aggregate's source (AAggregate) or the place's
    // address; its anchor held for the call first (DoAnchorBegin, SU2.8 e3); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAnchoredAddress(const AArg: int64; const AWrite: bool; const AAggregate: bool): int64;
    var
      LAnchor: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      LAnchor := self.DoAnchorOf(AArg);
      if not self.DoAnchorBegin(LAnchor, AWrite, AArg) then
        return 0;
      end;
      if AWrite then
        LAddress := self.DoAddressFor(AArg, true);
      else
        if AAggregate then
          LAddress := self.DoAggregateSource(AArg);
        else
          LAddress := self.DoAddress(AArg);
        end;
      end;
      self.DoAnchorEnd(LAnchor, LAddress <> 0);
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // The address the managed argument AArg is passed at for a const parameter by reference
    // (DoManagedReference: the place itself, so the callee reads it as it changes), the
    // anchor of that place held for the call first (DoAnchorBegin, SU2.8 e3: the block the
    // place lies in lives through the call); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAnchoredReference(const AArg: int64): int64;
    var
      LAnchor: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      LAnchor := self.DoAnchorOf(AArg);
      if not self.DoAnchorBegin(LAnchor, false, AArg) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoManagedReference(AArg);
      self.DoAnchorEnd(LAnchor, LAddress <> 0);
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // The IR type C's default argument promotions give a variadic argument of AType: bool,
    // the 8- and 16-bit integers (a char, a wchar too) int32, float32 float64, the rest as it
    // is (Ssa.IsVariadicArgType holds after it)
    hidden const method DoVariadicIr(const AType: IrType): IrType;
    begin
      if (AType = IrType.Bool) or (AType = IrType.Int8) or (AType = IrType.Int16) or
        (AType = IrType.UInt8) or (AType = IrType.UInt16) then
        return IrType.Int32;
      end;
      if AType = IrType.Float32 then
        return IrType.Float64;
      end;
      return AType;
    end;

    // The operand the variadic argument AArg (one past a clink routine's fixed parameters)
    // passes, at its own type (SEM converts none, BNF sec 4): an aggregate as a by-value
    // parameter would be (its bytes in a register, widened to the 8-byte slot, or the
    // address of a copy keyed by AArg), any other value promoted (DoVariadicIr); 0 after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoVariadicArgument(const AArg: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
      LSource: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoUsedType(AArg);
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(AArg);
        if LSource = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LIr := self.DoAggregateIr(LType);
        if LIr <> IrType.Void then
          return self.DoConvertIr(self.DoLoad(LSource, LIr, AArg), IrType.UInt64, AArg);
        end;
        LSlot := self.DoSlot(AArg, LType, false);
        if LSlot = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        self.DoCopyBytes(LSlot, LSource, TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType), AArg);
        return LSlot;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(AArg);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LIr := self.FModule.InstrAt(LValue).ValueType;
      return self.DoConvertIr(LValue, self.DoVariadicIr(LIr), AArg);
    end;

    // The address varargs.next(T) AId reads its argument at, the cursor moved one
    // Target.VariadicSlotBytes on (a clink variadic, BNF sec 6: C's va_arg, unchecked): the
    // cursor's place, or for an aggregate T the caller passed as the address of its copy
    // (DoAggregateIr Void, as DoVariadicArgument passes it) the address that place holds;
    // 0 after LW0001 (another member, or no cursor: never from a valid tree, SEM's SM0417 /
    // SM0418, and a cpplink variadic is refused before its body)
    hidden method DoVarargsPlace(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LCursor: int64;
      LType: int64;
    begin
      if (self.FTree[AId].Text <> "next") or (self.FVarargsSlot = 0) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LCursor := self.DoLoad(self.FVarargsSlot, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      self.DoStore(self.FVarargsSlot, self.DoByteOffset(LCursor, self.FTarget.VariadicSlotBytes(), AId),
        AId);
      LType := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) and (self.DoAggregateIr(LType) = IrType.Void) then
        return self.DoLoad(LCursor, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      end;
      return LCursor;
    end;

    // The value of varargs.next(T) AId for a T that is no aggregate: its place read at the
    // type the caller promoted it to (DoVariadicIr: an int8 came as an int32, a float32 as a
    // float64), converted back to T (DoConvertTo: a bool as `<> 0`); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoVarargsValue(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
      LPlace: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType;
      LIr := self.DoTypeAt(LType, AId);
      if LIr = IrType.Void then
        return 0;
      end;
      LPlace := self.DoVarargsPlace(AId);
      if LPlace = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoConvertTo(self.DoLoad(LPlace, self.DoVariadicIr(LIr), AId), LType, LType, AId);
    end;

    // The bytes of a typed pack's header: items (a ptr), count and cursor (int32 each)
    hidden method DoPackHeaderBytes(): int64;
    begin
      return self.FTarget.PointerSize() + 8;
    end;

    // The offset of a pack header's count (its cursor 4 bytes on)
    hidden method DoPackCountAt(): int64;
    begin
      return self.FTarget.PointerSize();
    end;

    // The bytes of one pack item: its tag (uint64), its place (a ptr at 8), its type's name
    // (a ptr at DoPackNameAt), its kind (an int64 at DoPackKindAt) and its facts (a ptr at
    // DoPackFactsAt), rounded up to 8 so every item's tag stays aligned (System.Runtime's
    // PackEntry)
    hidden method DoPackItemBytes(): int64;
    var
      LBytes: int64;
    begin
      LBytes := self.DoPackFactsAt() + self.FTarget.PointerSize();
      return ((LBytes + 7) div 8) * 8;
    end;

    // The offset of a pack item's type name (its place's end)
    hidden method DoPackNameAt(): int64;
    begin
      return 8 + self.FTarget.PointerSize();
    end;

    // The offset of a pack item's kind (its type name's end)
    hidden method DoPackKindAt(): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoPackNameAt() + self.FTarget.PointerSize();
    end;

    // The offset of a pack item's facts (its kind's end)
    hidden method DoPackFactsAt(): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoPackKindAt() + 8;
    end;

    // The facts of a pack item of the canonical type AType (what its VarKind alone does not
    // tell a reader of the pack, System.Runtime's PackEntry.Facts): the address of a
    // read-only block of int64 words (DoPackFactWords), made once per type (FPackFactsOf),
    // at ANode; nil for a type that has none (DoHasPackFacts)
    hidden method DoPackFacts(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LWords: ref Int64List;
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoHasPackFacts(AType) then
        return self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ANode);
      end;
      if self.FPackFactsOf[AType] = 0 then
        LWords := ref Int64List();
        self.DoPackFactWords(AType, LWords, ANode);
        self.FPackFactsOf[AType] := self.DoWordsData(ADAM_LOWERING_PACK_FACTS_SYMBOL, LWords,
          ref Int64List(), ANode) + 1;
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := self.FPackFactsOf[AType] - 1;
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // True when a pack item of the canonical type AType has facts (DoPackFactWords): a typed
    // pointer, a choices value, a static array, a set
    hidden const method DoHasPackFacts(const AType: int64): bool;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      return (LClass = TypeClass.Pointer) or (LClass = TypeClass.ChoicesType) or
        (LClass = TypeClass.StaticArray) or (LClass = TypeClass.DynamicArray) or
        (LClass = TypeClass.SetType);
    end;

    // The facts words of a pack item of the canonical type AType added to AWords, at ANode
    // (System.Runtime's PackEntry.Facts). A typed pointer: [the VarKind number of what print
    // writes for it, by its target (PrintFormOf): Char its C string, WChar its C wide
    // string, Ptr its address]; a choices value: [its byte size, then its names table
    // (DoChoiceNameWords)]; a static array: [its element count, its element's size (the
    // stride), its element's VarKind number (DoVarKindFound: -1 for a type no pack names),
    // then its element's own facts]; a dynamic array the same with -1 for the count (the
    // runtime reads it from the block its place holds); a set: [its lowest member, its
    // highest, its member's
    // VarKind number, then its member's own facts] (its bytes are the place: bit i member
    // low + i, Layout.SetRange). So a range's facts hold every level below it, in one block
    // with no addresses; nothing for any other type. A bound or a set range with no value
    // faults, as print's own range writers fault
    hidden method DoPackFactWords(const AType: int64; const AWords: ref Int64List; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
      LForm: PrintForm;
      LNames: ref Int64List;
      LElement: int64;
      LLow: int64;
      LHigh: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if LClass = TypeClass.Pointer then
        LForm := PrintFormOf(self.FTree, AType);
        if LForm = PrintForm.CText then
          AWords.Add(self.DoVarKindNumber("Char", AType, ANode));
        else
          if LForm = PrintForm.WideCText then
            AWords.Add(self.DoVarKindNumber("WChar", AType, ANode));
          else
            AWords.Add(self.DoVarKindNumber("Ptr", AType, ANode));
          end;
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if LClass = TypeClass.ChoicesType then
        AWords.Add(TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType));
        LNames := self.DoChoiceNameWords(AType);
        for LI := 0 to LNames.Count - 1 do
          AWords.Add(LNames[LI]);
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if LClass = TypeClass.StaticArray then
        if not BoundValue(self.FTree, self.FTarget, self.FTree.FirstOf(self.FTree[AType].ResolvedDecl,
          NodeRole.LowBound), LLow) then
          raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_LOW_BOUND + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
        end;
        if not BoundValue(self.FTree, self.FTarget, self.FTree.FirstOf(self.FTree[AType].ResolvedDecl,
          NodeRole.HighBound), LHigh) then
          raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_HIGH_BOUND + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
        end;
        LElement := TargetOf(self.FTree, AType);
        AWords.Add(LHigh - LLow + 1);
        AWords.Add(self.DoElementSize(AType));
        AWords.Add(self.DoVarKindFound(self.DoPackKindName(LElement)));
        self.DoPackFactWords(LElement, AWords, ANode);
        return;
      end;
      if LClass = TypeClass.DynamicArray then
        LElement := TargetOf(self.FTree, AType);
        AWords.Add(-1);
        AWords.Add(self.DoElementSize(AType));
        AWords.Add(self.DoVarKindFound(self.DoPackKindName(LElement)));
        self.DoPackFactWords(LElement, AWords, ANode);
        return;
      end;
      if LClass = TypeClass.SetType then
        LElement := SetMemberOf(self.FTree, AType);
        if (LElement = 0) or (not SetRange(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType, LLow, LHigh)) then
          raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_LOW_BOUND + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
        end;
        AWords.Add(LLow);
        AWords.Add(LHigh);
        AWords.Add(self.DoVarKindFound(self.DoPackKindName(LElement)));
        self.DoPackFactWords(LElement, AWords, ANode);
      end;
    end;

    // The type a pack item of the argument's canonical type AType is stored and tagged as:
    // nil as an untyped ptr (BNF sec 6 literal typing), anything else as itself
    hidden const method DoPackType(const AType: int64): int64;
    begin
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.NilType then
        return BuiltinType(self.FTree, "ptr");
      end;
      return AType;
    end;

    // The tag of a pack item of the canonical type AType: FNV-1a 64 over the type's text
    // and the module that declares it, so one type has one tag in every module (what a
    // pack read's run-time type check compares, M3.11)
    hidden const method DoPackTag(const AType: int64): int64;
    var
      LText: string;
      LModule: int64;
    begin
      LText := TypeText(self.FTree, AType);
      LModule := ModuleOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if LModule <> 0 then
        LText := LText + "@" + self.FTree[LModule].Text;
      end;
      return int64(Fnv1a64(LText));
    end;

    // The address of the read-only C string AText (its bytes and a NUL) a typed pack names
    // a type or a member with: one blob per text (FPackTexts), an Address at ANode
    hidden method DoPackText(const AText: string; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LData: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LData := self.FPackTexts.Find(AText) - 1;
      if LData < 0 then
        LData := self.DoHelperData(ADAM_LOWERING_TEXT_SYMBOL,
          1, ANode);
        for LI := 0 to len(AText) - 1 do
          self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(uint8(AText[LI]));
        end;
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(uint8(0));
        self.FPackTexts.Put(AText, LData + 1);
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := LData;
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // The VarKind value name of a pack item of the canonical type AType (System.Runtime's
    // VarKind, BNF sec 6 kind): a builtin its own name (int32 Int32, clong CLong, ptr Ptr),
    // any other type what it is; "" for a type no pack carries
    hidden const method DoPackKindName(const AType: int64): string;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AType].Kind = NodeKind.BuiltinTypeDecl then
        return DoBuiltinKindName(self.FTree[AType].Text);
      end;
      match ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) of
        TypeClass.Pointer: return "Pointer";
        TypeClass.StaticArray: return "StaticArray";
        TypeClass.DynamicArray: return "DynamicArray";
        TypeClass.RecordType: return "Record";
        TypeClass.ObjectType: return "Object";
        TypeClass.InterfaceType: return "Interface";
        TypeClass.OverlayType: return "Overlay";
        TypeClass.ChoicesType: return "Choices";
        TypeClass.SetType: return "Set";
        TypeClass.RoutineType: return "Routine";
        TypeClass.OwnType: return "Own";
        TypeClass.RefType: return "Ref";
        TypeClass.WeakType: return "Weak";
        TypeClass.TaskType: return "Task";
      else
        return "";
      end;
    end;

    // The number of the VarKind value a pack item of the canonical type AType carries
    // (DoPackKindName), as SEM folded it in the runtime's VarKind (SyntaxTree.VarKind); 0
    // after LW0001 at ANode when the runtime has no VarKind or no such value
    hidden method DoPackKindNumber(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoVarKindNumber(self.DoPackKindName(AType), AType, ANode);
    end;

    // The number of the VarKind value named AName, as SEM folded it in the runtime's VarKind
    // (SyntaxTree.VarKind), for a pack item of the canonical type AType; 0 after LW0001 at
    // ANode naming AType when the runtime has no VarKind or no such value
    hidden method DoVarKindNumber(const AName: string; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LNumber: int64;
    begin
      LNumber := self.DoVarKindFound(AName);
      if LNumber >= 0 then
        return LNumber;
      end;
      self.DoRefuse(ANode, "a pack argument of type '" + TypeText(self.FTree, AType) +
        "' with no VarKind value");
      return 0;
    end;

    // The number of the VarKind value named AName, as SEM folded it in the runtime's VarKind
    // (SyntaxTree.VarKind); -1 when the runtime has no VarKind or no such value (AName "":
    // a type no pack carries)
    hidden const method DoVarKindFound(const AName: string): int64;
    var
      LBody: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if (self.FTree.VarKind = 0) or (AName = "") then
        return -1;
      end;
      LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, self.FTree.VarKind);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
        LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
        if (self.FTree[LMember].Kind = NodeKind.ChoiceValue) and (self.FTree[LMember].Text = AName) then
          return int64(self.FTree[LMember].ResolvedConst.Bits);
        end;
      end;
      return -1;
    end;

    // The address of the caller's copy of the pack argument AArg at its own type
    // (DoPackType), in a slot of that type: an aggregate's bytes copied in, a managed value
    // (a text, a dynamic array, a ref: DoIsManaged) as its block borrowed (DoManagedValue:
    // the caller's place, or the statement's temporary, keeps the reference for the whole
    // call, as for a const parameter), any other value stored; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPackPlace(const AArg: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoPackType(self.DoUsedType(AArg));
      if self.DoIsManaged(LType) then
        LValue := self.DoManagedValue(AArg);
        if LValue = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(AArg, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
        self.DoStore(LSlot, LValue, AArg);
        return LSlot;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(AArg);
        if LSource = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(AArg, TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType),
          TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType));
        self.DoCopyBytes(LSlot, LSource, TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType), AArg);
        return LSlot;
      end;
      if self.DoTypeAt(LType, AArg) = IrType.Void then
        return 0;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(AArg);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(AArg, TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType),
        TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType));
      self.DoStore(LSlot, LValue, AArg);
      return LSlot;
    end;

    // The typed pack of the call ACall's arguments from the AFirst-th on (one past a
    // cpplink variadic's fixed parameters), built in the caller's frame: each argument's
    // copy (DoPackPlace, in order), then the pack over them (DoPackFrom); the header's
    // address, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPackArguments(const ACall: int64; const AFirst: int64): int64;
    var
      LPlaces: ref Int64List;
      LPlace: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LPlaces := ref Int64List();
      for LI := AFirst to self.FTree.CountOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument) - 1 do
        LPlace := self.DoPackPlace(self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, LI));
        if LPlace = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LPlaces.Add(LPlace);
      end;
      return self.DoPackFrom(ACall, AFirst, LPlaces);
    end;

    // The typed pack of the call ACall's arguments from the AFirst-th on over their copies'
    // places APlaces (one per argument, in order: the caller's, DoPackPlace, or a task's
    // object's, DoTaskBody), built in the current frame: each item (tag, place, type name,
    // kind, facts), then the header (items, count, cursor 0); the header's address, 0 after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoPackFrom(const ACall: int64; const AFirst: int64; const APlaces: ref Int64List): int64;
    var
      LCount: int64;
      LItems: int64;
      LItem: int64;
      LArg: int64;
      LPlace: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LHeader: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LCount := self.FTree.CountOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument) - AFirst;
      LItems := 0;
      if LCount > 0 then
        LItems := self.DoSizedSlot(self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, AFirst),
          LCount * self.DoPackItemBytes(), 8);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LArg := self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, AFirst + LI);
        LPlace := APlaces[LI];
        LType := self.DoPackType(self.DoUsedType(LArg));
        LItem := self.DoByteOffset(LItems, LI * self.DoPackItemBytes(), LArg);
        self.DoStore(LItem, self.DoConstant(IrType.UInt64, self.DoPackTag(LType), LArg), LArg);
        self.DoStore(self.DoByteOffset(LItem, 8, LArg), LPlace, LArg);
        self.DoStore(self.DoByteOffset(LItem, self.DoPackNameAt(), LArg),
          self.DoPackText(TypeText(self.FTree, LType), LArg), LArg);
        self.DoStore(self.DoByteOffset(LItem, self.DoPackKindAt(), LArg),
          self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, self.DoPackKindNumber(LType, LArg), LArg), LArg);
        self.DoStore(self.DoByteOffset(LItem, self.DoPackFactsAt(), LArg),
          self.DoPackFacts(LType, LArg), LArg);
      end;
      LHeader := self.DoSizedSlot(ACall, self.DoPackHeaderBytes(), self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
      if LItems = 0 then
        LItems := self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ACall);
      end;
      self.DoStore(LHeader, LItems, ACall);
      self.DoStore(self.DoByteOffset(LHeader, self.DoPackCountAt(), ACall),
        self.DoConstant(IrType.Int32, LCount, ACall), ACall);
      self.DoStore(self.DoByteOffset(LHeader, self.DoPackCountAt() + 4, ACall),
        self.DoConstant(IrType.Int32, 0, ACall), ACall);
      return LHeader;
    end;

    // True when AId reads a typed pack: varargs.<member> in a cpplink variadic (FPackSlot),
    // a call of next / get / reset / copy / kind on a varargs local, a varargs local's count
    // (SEM typed the receiver varargs: DoPackCall / DoPackMember)
    hidden const method DoIsPackAccess(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LMember: int64;
    begin
      LKind := self.FTree[AId].Kind;
      if LKind = NodeKind.VarargsExpression then
        return self.FPackSlot <> 0;
      end;
      LMember := AId;
      if LKind = NodeKind.CallExpression then
        LMember := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Callee);
      end;
      if self.FTree[LMember].Kind <> NodeKind.MemberExpression then
        return false;
      end;
      return ClassOf(self.FTree, self.FTree[self.FTree.FirstOf(LMember, NodeRole.Operand)].ResolvedType) =
        TypeClass.Varargs;
    end;

    // The member word of the pack access AId (DoIsPackAccess): count, next, get, reset, copy
    hidden const method DoPackWord(const AId: int64): string;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.CallExpression then
        return self.FTree[self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Callee)].Text;
      end;
      return self.FTree[AId].Text;
    end;

    // The address of the header the pack access AId reads: the one the routine was given
    // (FPackSlot holds it) for varargs.<member>, a varargs local's own slot; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPackHeader(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LMember: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.VarargsExpression then
        return self.DoLoad(self.FPackSlot, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      end;
      LMember := AId;
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.CallExpression then
        LMember := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Callee);
      end;
      return self.DoAddress(self.FTree.FirstOf(LMember, NodeRole.Operand));
    end;

    // The index get(I, T) / kind(I) AId reads at: its I (a varargs expression's Argument, a
    // call's first)
    hidden const method DoPackIndexNode(const AId: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Argument);
    end;

    // The address of the item the pack read AId (next / get / kind) names in the header at
    // AHeader, found by the runtime's PackItem (BNF sec 6: the index against the count,
    // next / get's T against the item's type, each raising as pcpp does): next takes the
    // cursor's item and moves the cursor one on once the read succeeded (PackItem returned),
    // get and kind the I-th; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPackItem(const AId: int64; const AHeader: int64): int64;
    var
      LWord: string;
      LFunction: int64;
      LCursorAt: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LWanted: int64;
      LWantedName: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LOne: int64;
      LNext: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LWord := self.DoPackWord(AId);
      LFunction := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.PackItem, AId);
      if LFunction = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LCursorAt := 0;
      if LWord = "next" then
        LCursorAt := self.DoByteOffset(AHeader, self.DoPackCountAt() + 4, AId);
        LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCursorAt, IrType.Int32, AId);
      else
        LIndex := self.DoValue(self.DoPackIndexNode(AId));
        if LIndex = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LIndex := self.DoConvertIr(LIndex, IrType.Int32, AId);
      end;
      // kind wants no type (a tag of 0); next / get want T's (DoPackTag, as the caller tagged)
      if LWord = "kind" then
        LWanted := self.DoConstant(IrType.UInt64, 0, AId);
        LWantedName := self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, AId);
      else
        LType := self.DoPackType(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType);
        LWanted := self.DoConstant(IrType.UInt64, self.DoPackTag(LType), AId);
        LWantedName := self.DoPackText(TypeText(self.FTree, LType), AId);
      end;
      LMember := self.DoPackText(LWord, AId);
      // every operand is emitted before the instruction that uses it
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Call, self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.ResultType, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Link := LFunction;
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(AHeader);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LIndex);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LMember);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LWanted);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LWantedName);
      if LWord = "next" then
        LOne := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int32, 1, AId);
        LNext := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Add, IrType.Int32, AId);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LNext).Operands.Add(LIndex);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LNext).Operands.Add(LOne);
        self.DoStore(LCursorAt, LNext, AId);
      end;
      return LId;
    end;

    // The place of the item the pack read AId (next / get) names in the header at AHeader
    // (DoPackItem): the address the item's place holds, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPackItemPlace(const AId: int64; const AHeader: int64): int64;
    var
      LItem: int64;
    begin
      LItem := self.DoPackItem(AId, AHeader);
      if LItem = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(LItem, 8, AId), IrType.Pointer, AId);
    end;

    // The value of the pack access AId: count (an int32), next / get of a T that is no
    // aggregate (its place read at T), reset (the cursor set to 0: the store), kind (the
    // item's VarKind number at the VarKind's IR type); 0 after LW0001 (copy is no value:
    // only a varargs local's source, DoPackSourceAddress)
    hidden method DoPackValue(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LWord: string;
      LHeader: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
      LPlace: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LWord := self.DoPackWord(AId);
      if (LWord <> "count") and (LWord <> "next") and (LWord <> "get") and (LWord <> "reset") and
        (LWord <> "kind") then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LIr := IrType.Void;
      if (LWord = "next") or (LWord = "get") or (LWord = "kind") then
        LIr := self.DoTypeAt(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType, AId);
        if LIr = IrType.Void then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      LHeader := self.DoPackHeader(AId);
      if LHeader = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if LWord = "count" then
        return self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(LHeader, self.DoPackCountAt(), AId), IrType.Int32, AId);
      end;
      if LWord = "reset" then
        // every operand is emitted before the instruction that uses it
        LPlace := self.DoByteOffset(LHeader, self.DoPackCountAt() + 4, AId);
        LIr := IrType.Int32;
        LId := self.DoConstant(LIr, 0, AId);
        self.DoStore(LPlace, LId, AId);
        return LId;
      end;
      if LWord = "kind" then
        LPlace := self.DoPackItem(AId, LHeader);
        if LPlace = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LId := self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(LPlace, self.DoPackKindAt(), AId), IrType.Int64, AId);
        return self.DoConvertIr(LId, LIr, AId);
      end;
      LPlace := self.DoPackItemPlace(AId, LHeader);
      if LPlace = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoLoad(LPlace, LIr, AId);
    end;

    // The value of the pack read AId (next / get) of a managed T (DoIsManaged): the block
    // its item's place holds, borrowed (the caller's argument keeps the reference for the
    // whole call: DoPackPlace), so a store, a concatenation or a return of it adds its own
    // holder as for any place's value; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPackManaged(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LWord: string;
      LHeader: int64;
      LPlace: int64;
    begin
      LWord := self.DoPackWord(AId);
      if (LWord <> "next") and (LWord <> "get") then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LHeader := self.DoPackHeader(AId);
      if LHeader = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LPlace := self.DoPackItemPlace(AId, LHeader);
      if LPlace = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoLoad(LPlace, IrType.Pointer, AId);
    end;

    // The address the pack access AId is copied from: an aggregate next / get's item place,
    // copy()'s header (a varargs local is set from it: SEM's SM0422); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPackSourceAddress(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LWord: string;
      LHeader: int64;
    begin
      LWord := self.DoPackWord(AId);
      if (LWord <> "copy") and (LWord <> "next") and (LWord <> "get") then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LHeader := self.DoPackHeader(AId);
      if LHeader = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if LWord = "copy" then
        return LHeader;
      end;
      return self.DoPackItemPlace(AId, LHeader);
    end;

    // The varargs local ALocal: a header slot, zeroed (an empty pack), its initializer's
    // header copied in when it has one (a copy(): SEM's SM0422)
    hidden method DoPackLocal(const ALocal: int64);
    var
      LSlot: int64;
      LInit: int64;
      LSource: int64;
    begin
      LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(ALocal, self.DoPackHeaderBytes(), self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
      self.FSlotOf[ALocal] := LSlot;
      self.DoFill(LSlot, self.DoPackHeaderBytes(), ALocal);
      LInit := self.FTree.FirstOf(ALocal, NodeRole.Initializer);
      if LInit = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(LInit);
      if LSource <> 0 then
        self.DoCopyBytes(LSlot, LSource, self.DoPackHeaderBytes(), ALocal);
      end;
    end;

    // The assignment AId into a varargs local: the copy()'s header first, then the
    // target's, then the header's bytes copied (DoAggregateAssign's order)
    hidden method DoPackAssign(const AId: int64);
    var
      LSource: int64;
      LDest: int64;
    begin
      LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
      if LSource = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LDest := self.DoAddressFor(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target), true);
      if LDest = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoCopyBytes(LDest, LSource, self.DoPackHeaderBytes(), AId);
    end;

    // The operands of call ACall of the routine ADecl, each argument's (DoArgument; one
    // past a clink variadic routine's fixed parameters DoVariadicArgument), then for a
    // cpplink variadic the address of the pack its extra arguments go in
    // (DoPackArguments); nil when one was refused
    hidden method DoArguments(const ACall: int64; const ADecl: int64): ref Int64List;
    var
      LList: ref Int64List;
      LArg: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LParams: int64;
      LGiven: int64;
      LPack: bool;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LList := ref Int64List();
      LParams := self.FTree.CountOf(ADecl, NodeRole.Param);
      LPack := self.DoIsPackVariadic(ADecl);
      LGiven := self.FTree.CountOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument);
      if LPack and (LGiven > LParams) then
        LGiven := LParams;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LGiven - 1 do
        LArg := self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, LI);
        if LI < LParams then
          LValue := self.DoArgument(LArg, self.FTree.NthOf(ADecl, NodeRole.Param, LI));
        else
          LValue := self.DoVariadicArgument(LArg);
        end;
        if LValue = 0 then
          return nil;
        end;
        LList.Add(LValue);
      end;
      if LPack then
        LValue := self.DoPackArguments(ACall, LParams);
        if LValue = 0 then
          return nil;
        end;
        LList.Add(LValue);
      end;
      return LList;
    end;

    // The routine the callee name ACallee runs (a forward's full declaration); 0 for none
    hidden const method DoCalled(const ACallee: int64): int64;
    var
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      LDecl := self.FTree[ACallee].ResolvedDecl;
      if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.ForwardRoutine) then
        LDecl := self.FTree[LDecl].ResolvedDecl;
      end;
      if (LDecl = 0) or (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind <> NodeKind.RoutineDecl) then
        return 0;
      end;
      return LDecl;
    end;

    // True when the placeholder AItem writes no spec (`{}` / `{N}`, or a `:` with nothing
    // after it): its argument in its form's own text
    hidden const method DoIsPlainItem(const AItem: FormatItem): bool;
    begin
      return (len(AItem.Specs) = 1) and self.DoIsPlainSpec(AItem.Specs[0]);
    end;

    // True when the spec level ASpec writes nothing (DefaultFormatSpec's fields): its value
    // in its form's own text
    hidden const method DoIsPlainSpec(const ASpec: FormatSpec): bool;
    begin
      return (ASpec.Fill = "") and (ASpec.Align = FormatAlign.None) and
        (ASpec.Sign = FormatSign.None) and (not ASpec.Alternate) and (not ASpec.ZeroPad) and
        (ASpec.Width = 0) and (ASpec.WidthArgument = -1) and (ASpec.Precision = -1) and
        (ASpec.PrecisionArgument = -1) and (not ASpec.Localized) and
        (not ASpec.ClearBrackets) and (ASpec.Presentation = "");
    end;

    // The bytes of AText as a data blob, written to the print sink ASink (an IR value: nil
    // for stdout, else a string slot's address) by the runtime's text writer AWriter (a
    // function, SinkText) called with the sink, their address and count at ACall; the call
    hidden method DoWriteText(const AWriter: int64; const ASink: int64; const AText: string;
      const ACall: int64): int64;
    var
      LData: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LId: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LData := self.DoHelperData(ADAM_LOWERING_TEXT_SYMBOL,
        1, ACall);
      for LI := 0 to len(AText) - 1 do
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(uint8(AText[LI]));
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ACall);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := LData;
      LCount := self.DoConstant(self.FModule.FunctionAt(AWriter).Signature.ParamTypes[2],
        len(AText), ACall);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Call, self.FModule.FunctionAt(AWriter).Signature.ResultType, ACall);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Link := AWriter;
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(ASink);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LAddress);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LCount);
      return LId;
    end;

    // The call of print / println ACall (ANewLine: println): its pieces written to stdout
    // (DoPrintPieces, the print sink nil). When its text can raise as it is written
    // (DoPrintMayRaise; its hidden slot made by DoTemporaries) they go into that slot's
    // string first (emptied by StrTake), then that string to stdout at once (StrWrite) and
    // the slot emptied again: a raise leaves none of the print's text written, as
    // std::print formats its whole text before it writes any. The last call, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPrint(const ACall: int64; const AIntrinsic: int64; const ANewLine: bool): int64;
    var
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoPrintMayRaise(ACall) then
        // straight to stdout: only its range scratch strings (if any) allocate
        return self.DoSitedPieces(ACall, AIntrinsic, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ACall),
          ANewLine, self.FRangeScratchOf[ACall] <> 0);
      end;
      LSlot := self.DoTempSlot(ACall);
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrTake, LSlot, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ACall),
        ACall) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.DoSitedPieces(ACall, AIntrinsic, LSlot, ANewLine, true) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrWrite, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ACall),
        self.DoLoad(LSlot, IrType.Pointer, ACall), ACall) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrTake, LSlot, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ACall),
        ACall);
    end;

    // True when the text of the print / println call ACall can raise while it is written
    // (DoPrint then writes it into a scratch string first). The runtime raises libc++'s
    // format errors as it writes in exactly these cases: a width or a precision taken from
    // an argument (SpecWidth: negative, past the maximum, no integer) and an integer's `c`
    // out of a char's range (SinkSpecInt), at any level of a placeholder's spec (a range's
    // element's too), and every format read only when the call runs (FormatRun: any text
    // that does not fit). A print writer that gains a raise is added here
    hidden const method DoPrintMayRaise(const ACall: int64): bool;
    var
      LPlan: FormatPlan;
      LSpec: FormatSpec;
      LI: int64;
      LJ: int64;
    begin
      LPlan := self.FTree.FormatOf(ACall);
      if LPlan.AtRunTime then
        return true;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to len(LPlan.Items) - 1 do
        for LJ := 0 to len(LPlan.Items[LI].Specs) - 1 do
          LSpec := LPlan.Items[LI].Specs[LJ];
          if (LSpec.WidthArgument >= 0) or (LSpec.PrecisionArgument >= 0) or
            (LSpec.Presentation = "c") then
            return true;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // The call FormatStr(F, ..) ACall (M3.8f2b): print's pieces of it (DoPrintPieces)
    // written to the string in the call's hidden slot, its print sink (the slot emptied
    // first: StrTake releases what an earlier pass left there). That string, a reference the
    // slot keeps (released at the function's exits); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoFormatStr(const ACall: int64): int64;
    var
      LSlot: int64;
      LIntrinsic: int64;
    begin
      LSlot := self.DoTempSlot(ACall);
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrTake, LSlot, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ACall),
        ACall) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LIntrinsic := self.FTree[self.FTree.FirstOf(ACall, NodeRole.Callee)].ResolvedDecl;
      if self.DoSitedPieces(ACall, LIntrinsic, LSlot, false, true) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoLoad(LSlot, IrType.Pointer, ACall);
    end;

    // DoPrintPieces of the print / println / FormatStr call ACall into the sink ASink, its
    // text's blocks sited when ASited (M3.12b): the call's site ("string": the sink string
    // and the range scratch strings growing as the pieces are written) stored before the
    // pieces and made the enclosing one while they lower (an argument's own runtime call
    // gives GAllocSite back to it), the enclosing construct's stored after them
    hidden method DoSitedPieces(const ACall: int64; const AIntrinsic: int64; const ASink: int64;
      const ANewLine: bool; const ASited: bool): int64;
    var
      LOuter: int64;
      LSite: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LSite := 0;
      if ASited then
        LSite := self.DoEnterSite(ACall, "string");
      end;
      LOuter := self.FSiteOuter;
      if LSite <> 0 then
        self.FSiteOuter := LSite;
      end;
      LId := self.DoPrintPieces(ACall, AIntrinsic, ASink, ANewLine);
      self.FSiteOuter := LOuter;
      if LId <> 0 then
        self.DoLeaveSite(LSite, ACall);
      end;
      return LId;
    end;

    // The address a range print argument AArg (PrintForm.Range) is written from: a static
    // array's or a set's place or slot (DoAggregateSource, a call's result too); a dynamic
    // array's value (its block, nil when empty) in a slot of its own, so every range level
    // is reached by an address (DoPrintRangeOf); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoRangeSource(const AArg: int64): int64;
    var
      LBlock: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(AArg)) <> TypeClass.DynamicArray then
        return self.DoAggregateSource(AArg);
      end;
      LBlock := self.DoValue(AArg);
      if LBlock = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(AArg, 8, 8);
      self.DoStore(LSlot, LBlock, AArg);
      return LSlot;
    end;

    // The pieces of the print / println / FormatStr call ACall (of the intrinsic AIntrinsic;
    // ANewLine: println's newline after them) written to the print sink ASink (an IR value:
    // nil for stdout, else a string slot's address), by the format Semantics read (its
    // FormatPlan): every argument after the format evaluated first, each once, in order
    // (std::format's arguments, the ones no placeholder names too); then each placeholder's
    // text before it written by the runtime's text writer (ACall's ResolvedCallee), then its
    // argument's text by its print form (DoPrintValue; with a spec DoPrintSpecValue; a static
    // array or a set, evaluated to its address, as a range: DoPrintRangeOf), then the text
    // after the last (a newline after it for println). With no placeholder the text is
    // written as it is, even when empty. The last call, 0 after LW0001 (no runtime unit; a
    // dynamic array under a run-time format: DoPrintRunTime)
    hidden method DoPrintPieces(const ACall: int64; const AIntrinsic: int64; const ASink: int64;
      const ANewLine: bool): int64;
    var
      LWriter: int64;
      LPlan: FormatPlan;
      LValues: ref Int64List;
      LArg: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LForm: PrintForm;
      LTail: string;
      LId: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LWriter := self.FTree[ACall].ResolvedCallee;
      if (LWriter = 0) or (self.FFunctionOf[LWriter] = 0) then
        self.DoRefuse(ACall, "a call of " + self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AIntrinsic) + " with no runtime unit");
        return 0;
      end;
      LWriter := self.FFunctionOf[LWriter];
      LPlan := self.FTree.FormatOf(ACall);
      if LPlan.AtRunTime then
        return self.DoPrintRunTime(ACall, LWriter, ASink, ANewLine);
      end;
      LValues := ref Int64List();
      for LI := 1 to self.FTree.CountOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument) - 1 do
        LArg := self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, LI);
        // a static array is written element by element from its address, a set member by
        // member from its bytes' (DoPrintRangeOf; any such expression, a call's result too:
        // DoAggregateSource); a dynamic array from a slot holding its block (DoRangeSource);
        // SEM turned every unprintable form away
        LForm := PrintFormOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(LArg));
        if LForm = PrintForm.Range then
          LValue := self.DoRangeSource(LArg);
        else
          LValue := self.DoValue(LArg);
        end;
        if LValue = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LValues.Add(LValue);
      end;
      LTail := LPlan.Tail;
      if ANewLine then
        LTail := LTail + "\n";
      end;
      if len(LPlan.Items) = 0 then
        return self.DoWriteText(LWriter, ASink, LTail, ACall);
      end;
      LId := 0;
      for LI := 0 to len(LPlan.Items) - 1 do
        if len(LPlan.Items[LI].Text) > 0 then
          LId := self.DoWriteText(LWriter, ASink, LPlan.Items[LI].Text, ACall);
        end;
        LArg := self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, LPlan.Items[LI].Argument + 1);
        if PrintFormOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(LArg)) = PrintForm.Range then
          LId := self.DoPrintRangeOf(ASink, LValues[LPlan.Items[LI].Argument], self.DoUsedType(LArg),
            LPlan.Items[LI], 0, ACall, LValues, LArg);
        else
          if self.DoIsPlainItem(LPlan.Items[LI]) then
            LId := self.DoPrintValue(ASink, LValues[LPlan.Items[LI].Argument], LArg);
          else
            LId := self.DoPrintSpecValue(ASink, LValues, ACall, LPlan.Items[LI]);
          end;
        end;
        if LId = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      if len(LTail) > 0 then
        LId := self.DoWriteText(LWriter, ASink, LTail, ACall);
      end;
      return LId;
    end;

    // The pieces of the print / println / FormatStr call ACall whose format is known only
    // when it runs (its FormatPlan AtRunTime, BNF sec 7) written to the print sink ASink:
    // the format evaluated first (a string, its block borrowed as a const argument's:
    // DoManagedValue), then every argument after it into a typed pack (DoPackArguments: each
    // once, in order, the ones no placeholder names too), then the runtime's FormatRun walks
    // the text over that pack through print's own Sink* routines; println's newline after
    // it (the text writer AWriter). A static array, a dynamic array or a set travels with
    // its every level in its pack item's facts (DoPackFactWords), the runtime writing it as
    // print's own range writers do. The last call, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPrintRunTime(const ACall: int64; const AWriter: int64; const ASink: int64;
      const ANewLine: bool): int64;
    var
      LFormat: int64;
      LPack: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LFormat := self.DoManagedValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument));
      if LFormat = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LPack := self.DoPackArguments(ACall, 1);
      if LPack = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(ASink);
      LArgs.Add(LFormat);
      LArgs.Add(LPack);
      LId := self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.FormatRun, LArgs, ACall);
      if (LId = 0) or (not ANewLine) then
        return LId;
      end;
      return self.DoWriteText(AWriter, ASink, "\n", ACall);
    end;

    // The runtime routine that writes a print argument of the canonical type AType to a print
    // sink, by its print form (Types.PrintFormOf; the runtime's Sink* routines): a string
    // StrWrite, an integer WriteInt or (unsigned) WriteUInt, a bool WriteBool, a char
    // WriteChar, a wchar WriteWideChar, a wstring WriteWideText, a ptr to char / wchar
    // WriteCText / WriteWideCText, any other pointer, a routine value and nil WriteAddress, a
    // choices value WriteChoice, a float32 WriteFloat32, a float64 WriteFloat64 (by the IR
    // type the value travels as)
    hidden const method DoPrintWriter(const AType: int64): RuntimeRoutine;
    var
      LForm: PrintForm;
    begin
      LForm := PrintFormOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if LForm = PrintForm.Integer then
        if ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.UnsignedInt then
          return RuntimeRoutine.WriteUInt;
        end;
        return RuntimeRoutine.WriteInt;
      end;
      if LForm = PrintForm.Boolean then
        return RuntimeRoutine.WriteBool;
      end;
      if LForm = PrintForm.Char then
        return RuntimeRoutine.WriteChar;
      end;
      if LForm = PrintForm.WideChar then
        return RuntimeRoutine.WriteWideChar;
      end;
      if LForm = PrintForm.WideText then
        return RuntimeRoutine.WriteWideText;
      end;
      if LForm = PrintForm.CText then
        return RuntimeRoutine.WriteCText;
      end;
      if LForm = PrintForm.WideCText then
        return RuntimeRoutine.WriteWideCText;
      end;
      if LForm = PrintForm.Address then
        return RuntimeRoutine.WriteAddress;
      end;
      if LForm = PrintForm.Choice then
        return RuntimeRoutine.WriteChoice;
      end;
      if LForm = PrintForm.Float then
        if self.DoIrType(AType) = IrType.Float32 then
          return RuntimeRoutine.WriteFloat32;
        end;
        return RuntimeRoutine.WriteFloat64;
      end;
      return RuntimeRoutine.StrWrite;
    end;

    // The call at AArg writing AValue, the value of the print argument AArg, to the print
    // sink ASink in its form's own text (DoPrintValueOf by the argument's type); 0 after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoPrintValue(const ASink: int64; const AValue: int64; const AArg: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoPrintValueOf(ASink, AValue, self.DoUsedType(AArg), AArg);
    end;

    // The call at ANode writing AValue, a value of the canonical type AType (a print
    // argument's, a range's element's), to the print sink ASink by its writer
    // (DoPrintWriter): the sink first; a text passed as it is; any other value converted to
    // the writer's parameter type (an integer widened to 64 bits by its signedness); a
    // choices value with its type's names table (DoChoiceNamesData). 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPrintValueOf(const ASink: int64; const AValue: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LKind: RuntimeRoutine;
      LFunction: int64;
      LOperand: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LTable: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      LKind := self.DoPrintWriter(AType);
      if LKind = RuntimeRoutine.StrWrite then
        return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrWrite, ASink, AValue, ANode);
      end;
      LFunction := self.DoRuntimeFunction(LKind, ANode);
      if LFunction = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LOperand := AValue;
      if not self.DoIsText(AType) then
        LOperand := self.DoConvertIr(AValue, self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.ParamTypes[1],
          ANode);
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(ASink);
      LArgs.Add(LOperand);
      if LKind = RuntimeRoutine.WriteChoice then
        LTable := self.DoChoiceNamesData(AType, ANode);
        LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := LTable;
        LArgs.Add(LAddress);
      end;
      return self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(LKind, LArgs, ANode);
    end;

    // The runtime routine that writes a print argument of the print form AForm with a spec
    // (M3.8f3; the runtime's SinkSpec* routines): an integer WriteSpecInt, a bool
    // WriteSpecBool, a char WriteSpecChar, a pointer, a routine value and nil
    // WriteSpecAddress, a choices value WriteSpecChoice; (M3.8f4) a string WriteSpecStr, a
    // wstring WriteSpecWideText, a wchar WriteSpecWideChar, a ptr to char / wchar
    // WriteSpecCText / WriteSpecWideCText; (M3.8f5) a float32 / float64 WriteSpecFloat32 /
    // WriteSpecFloat64 (by the IR type of AType, the value's type); true with it in AKind,
    // false for a form with no SinkSpec* routine of its own (a range: DoPrintRangeOf)
    hidden const method DoSpecWriter(const AForm: PrintForm; const AType: int64;
      var AKind: RuntimeRoutine): bool;
    begin
      if AForm = PrintForm.Float then
        AKind := RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecFloat64;
        if self.DoIrType(AType) = IrType.Float32 then
          AKind := RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecFloat32;
        end;
        return true;
      end;
      if AForm = PrintForm.Text then
        AKind := RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecStr;
        return true;
      end;
      if AForm = PrintForm.WideText then
        AKind := RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecWideText;
        return true;
      end;
      if AForm = PrintForm.WideChar then
        AKind := RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecWideChar;
        return true;
      end;
      if AForm = PrintForm.CText then
        AKind := RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecCText;
        return true;
      end;
      if AForm = PrintForm.WideCText then
        AKind := RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecWideCText;
        return true;
      end;
      if AForm = PrintForm.Integer then
        AKind := RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecInt;
        return true;
      end;
      if AForm = PrintForm.Boolean then
        AKind := RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecBool;
        return true;
      end;
      if AForm = PrintForm.Char then
        AKind := RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecChar;
        return true;
      end;
      if AForm = PrintForm.Address then
        AKind := RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecAddress;
        return true;
      end;
      if AForm = PrintForm.Choice then
        AKind := RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecChoice;
        return true;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // The read-only words of the placeholder spec ASpec as System.Runtime's SinkSpec*
    // routines read them (its ADAM_SPEC_* layout): the fill's bytes packed little-endian and
    // their count, the alignment (`0` with none written: zero padding), the sign, `#`, the
    // written width, the type letter's byte, the written precision (-1: none); the data, at
    // ANode
    hidden method DoSpecData(const ASpec: FormatSpec; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LWords: ref Int64List;
      LFill: uint64;
      LAlign: int64;
      LSign: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LFill := 0;
      for LI := 0 to len(ASpec.Fill) - 1 do
        LFill := LFill | (uint64(uint8(ASpec.Fill[LI])) shl (8 * LI));
      end;
      LAlign := ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_ALIGN_DEFAULT;
      if ASpec.Align = FormatAlign.Left then
        LAlign := ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_ALIGN_LEFT;
      end;
      if ASpec.Align = FormatAlign.Center then
        LAlign := ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_ALIGN_CENTER;
      end;
      if ASpec.Align = FormatAlign.Right then
        LAlign := ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_ALIGN_RIGHT;
      end;
      // libc++'s `0` takes effect only where no alignment was written
      if ASpec.ZeroPad and (ASpec.Align = FormatAlign.None) then
        LAlign := ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_ALIGN_ZERO;
      end;
      LSign := ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_SIGN_MINUS;
      if ASpec.Sign = FormatSign.Plus then
        LSign := ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_SIGN_PLUS;
      end;
      if ASpec.Sign = FormatSign.Space then
        LSign := ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_SIGN_SPACE;
      end;
      LWords := ref Int64List();
      LWords.Add(int64(LFill));
      LWords.Add(len(ASpec.Fill));
      LWords.Add(LAlign);
      LWords.Add(LSign);
      if ASpec.Alternate then
        LWords.Add(1);
      else
        LWords.Add(0);
      end;
      LWords.Add(int64(ASpec.Width));
      if ASpec.Presentation = "" then
        LWords.Add(0);
      else
        LWords.Add(int64(uint8(ASpec.Presentation[0])));
      end;
      LWords.Add(int64(ASpec.Precision));
      return self.DoWordsData(ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_SYMBOL, LWords, ref Int64List(), ANode);
    end;

    // A width or precision operand of a placeholder spec of the print call ACall (AValues
    // its arguments' values after the format), AArgument the argument that gives it (the
    // spec's WidthArgument / PrecisionArgument): -1 (the written one) as the IR type AType
    // when it is -1, else the runtime's SpecWidth of that argument (checked as libc++'s
    // __substitute_arg_id checks either when the format runs: an argument of no integer type
    // raises there); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoSpecCountOperand(const ACall: int64; const AValues: ref Int64List;
      const AArgument: int32; const AType: IrType): int64;
    var
      LFunction: int64;
      LArg: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LKind: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
    begin
      if AArgument < 0 then
        return self.DoConstant(AType, -1, ACall);
      end;
      LFunction := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.SpecWidth, ACall);
      if LFunction = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LArg := self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, AArgument + 1);
      LKind := ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_WIDTH_SIGNED;
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(LArg)) = TypeClass.UnsignedInt then
        LKind := ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_WIDTH_UNSIGNED;
      end;
      if PrintFormOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(LArg)) = PrintForm.Integer then
        LValue := self.DoConvertIr(AValues[AArgument],
          self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.ParamTypes[0], LArg);
      else
        LKind := ADAM_LOWERING_SPEC_WIDTH_NO_INTEGER;
        LValue := self.DoConstant(self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.ParamTypes[0], 0, LArg);
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(LValue);
      LArgs.Add(self.DoConstant(self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.ParamTypes[1], LKind, LArg));
      return self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.SpecWidth, LArgs, LArg);
    end;

    // The IR type of parameter AIndex of the function AFunction
    hidden method DoParamTypeOf(const AFunction: int64; const AIndex: int64): IrType;
    begin
      return self.FModule.FunctionAt(AFunction).Signature.ParamTypes[AIndex];
    end;

    // The call writing the argument of the placeholder AItem (with a spec) of the print call
    // ACall to the print sink ASink (AValues its arguments' values after the format): its one
    // spec by DoPrintSpecOf (a range's levels are DoPrintRangeOf's). 0 after LW0001: a nested
    // spec on a form that is no range
    hidden method DoPrintSpecValue(const ASink: int64; const AValues: ref Int64List;
      const ACall: int64; const AItem: FormatItem): int64;
    var
      LArg: int64;
    begin
      LArg := self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, AItem.Argument + 1);
      if len(AItem.Specs) <> 1 then
        self.DoRefuse(self.FTree.FirstOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument), "a format placeholder with a spec");
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoPrintSpecOf(ASink, AValues[AItem.Argument], self.DoUsedType(LArg), AItem.Specs[0],
        ACall, AValues, LArg);
    end;

    // The call at ANode writing AValue, a value of the canonical type AType (a print
    // argument's, a range's element's), with the spec ASpec to the print sink ASink, by its
    // form's SinkSpec* routine (DoSpecWriter): the sink, the value as the routine's parameter
    // type (an integer's signedness after it; a choices value's names table after it), the
    // spec's words (DoSpecData), the width operand, a text form's precision operand
    // (DoSpecCountOperand both, from the print call ACall's argument values AValues;
    // DoSpecTakesPrecision). A text value goes as it is, as DoPrintValueOf passes one. 0
    // after LW0001: a form with no SinkSpec* routine
    hidden method DoPrintSpecOf(const ASink: int64; const AValue: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ASpec: FormatSpec; const ACall: int64; const AValues: ref Int64List;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LKind: RuntimeRoutine;
      LFunction: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LAddress: int64;
      LWidth: int64;
      LPrecision: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoSpecWriter(PrintFormOf(self.FTree, AType), AType, LKind) then
        self.DoRefuse(ANode, "a format placeholder with a spec");
        return 0;
      end;
      LFunction := self.DoRuntimeFunction(LKind, ANode);
      if LFunction = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(ASink);
      if self.DoIsText(AType) then
        LArgs.Add(AValue);
      else
        LArgs.Add(self.DoConvertIr(AValue, self.DoParamTypeOf(LFunction, 1), ANode));
      end;
      if LKind = RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecInt then
        if ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.UnsignedInt then
          LArgs.Add(self.DoConstant(self.DoParamTypeOf(LFunction, 2), 1, ANode));
        else
          LArgs.Add(self.DoConstant(self.DoParamTypeOf(LFunction, 2), 0, ANode));
        end;
      end;
      if LKind = RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecChoice then
        LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := self.DoChoiceNamesData(AType, ANode);
        LArgs.Add(LAddress);
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := self.DoSpecData(ASpec, ANode);
      LArgs.Add(LAddress);
      LWidth := self.DoSpecCountOperand(ACall, AValues, ASpec.WidthArgument,
        self.DoParamTypeOf(LFunction, LArgs.Count));
      if LWidth = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LArgs.Add(LWidth);
      if self.DoSpecTakesPrecision(LKind) then
        LPrecision := self.DoSpecCountOperand(ACall, AValues, ASpec.PrecisionArgument,
          self.DoParamTypeOf(LFunction, LArgs.Count));
        if LPrecision = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LArgs.Add(LPrecision);
      end;
      return self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(LKind, LArgs, ANode);
    end;

    // The spec of level ALevel of the placeholder AItem (Specs[0] its own, then a range's
    // element's, ...): the one written, else the unwritten one (DefaultFormatSpec: a range's
    // element with no spec of its own)
    hidden const method DoLevelSpec(const AItem: FormatItem; const ALevel: int64): FormatSpec;
    begin
      if ALevel < len(AItem.Specs) then
        return AItem.Specs[ALevel];
      end;
      return DefaultFormatSpec();
    end;

    // True when a range level with the spec ASpec is written into a scratch string first,
    // that string then written to the sink by the string formatter with the spec: a width
    // (libc++'s range_formatter pads its whole text: __write_string_no_precision) or `?s`
    // (its chars escaped as one string: __format_as_string)
    hidden const method DoRangeNeedsScratch(const ASpec: FormatSpec): bool;
    begin
      return (ASpec.Width > 0) or (ASpec.WidthArgument >= 0) or (ASpec.Presentation = "?s");
    end;

    // The range levels the placeholder AItem writes for a print argument of the canonical
    // type AType: one per range it goes through (an array whose element is an array: one
    // more), none past a range written as a string (`s` / `?s`) or a set; 0 when AType is
    // no range
    hidden const method DoRangeLevels(const AItem: FormatItem; const AType: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LSpec: FormatSpec;
      LLevels: int64;
    begin
      LType := AType;
      LLevels := 0;
      while PrintFormOf(self.FTree, LType) = PrintForm.Range do
        LSpec := self.DoLevelSpec(AItem, LLevels);
        LLevels := LLevels + 1;
        if (LSpec.Presentation <> "") or (ClassOf(self.FTree, LType) = TypeClass.SetType) then
          return LLevels;
        end;
        LType := TargetOf(self.FTree, LType);
      end;
      return LLevels;
    end;

    // How many range scratch strings the print / println / FormatStr call ACall needs: one
    // per level down to the deepest of its placeholders' range levels written into a
    // scratch (DoRangeNeedsScratch); 0 for a call that needs none
    hidden const method DoRangeScratchCount(const ACall: int64): int64;
    var
      LPlan: FormatPlan;
      LArg: int64;
      LLevels: int64;
      LLevel: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LPlan := self.FTree.FormatOf(ACall);
      LCount := 0;
      for LI := 0 to len(LPlan.Items) - 1 do
        LArg := self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, LPlan.Items[LI].Argument + 1);
        LLevels := self.DoRangeLevels(LPlan.Items[LI], self.DoUsedType(LArg));
        for LLevel := 0 to LLevels - 1 do
          if self.DoRangeNeedsScratch(self.DoLevelSpec(LPlan.Items[LI], LLevel)) and
            (LLevel + 1 > LCount) then
            LCount := LLevel + 1;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return LCount;
    end;

    // The range scratch strings of the print / println / FormatStr call ACall
    // (FRangeScratchOf, FRangeSlots): DoRangeScratchCount of them, each a hidden string
    // slot empty from the function's start, one of FManaged (a level's string is emptied
    // before each use by StrTake, as FormatStr's is, and released at the call's full
    // expression's end: DoEndRangeScratch); none for a call that needs none
    hidden method DoRangeTemporaries(const ACall: int64);
    var
      LCount: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LCount := self.DoRangeScratchCount(ACall);
      if LCount = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.FRangeScratchOf[ACall] := self.FRangeSlots.Count + 1;
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(ACall, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
        self.DoStore(LSlot, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ACall), ACall);
        self.DoAddManaged(LSlot, 0, ACall);
        self.FRangeSlots.Add(LSlot);
      end;
    end;

    // The scratch string slot of range level ALevel of the print call ACall
    // (DoRangeTemporaries); raises when there is none (a broken invariant: the scan and the
    // lowering disagree)
    hidden const method DoRangeScratch(const ACall: int64; const ALevel: int64): int64;
    begin
      if self.FRangeScratchOf[ACall] = 0 then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_TEMP + IntToStr(ACall));
      end;
      return self.FRangeSlots[self.FRangeScratchOf[ACall] - 1 + ALevel];
    end;

    // The runtime routine that writes an element of the print form AForm in the debug form a
    // range gives an element with no spec of its own where it differs from `?`'s
    // (PaskalCPP's formatters: a wchar in apostrophes as a char, WriteDebugWideChar; a ptr
    // to char / wchar's nil as `nil`, WriteDebugCText / WriteDebugWideCText); false for any
    // other form
    hidden const method DoDebugWriter(const AForm: PrintForm; var AKind: RuntimeRoutine): bool;
    begin
      if AForm = PrintForm.WideChar then
        AKind := RuntimeRoutine.WriteDebugWideChar;
        return true;
      end;
      if AForm = PrintForm.CText then
        AKind := RuntimeRoutine.WriteDebugCText;
        return true;
      end;
      if AForm = PrintForm.WideCText then
        AKind := RuntimeRoutine.WriteDebugWideCText;
        return true;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // The call at ANode writing AValue, an element of the canonical type AType of a range
    // that writes no type and no element spec, in the debug form libc++'s range_formatter
    // sets on its element's formatter (__set_debug_format) as PaskalCPP's formatters take
    // it: a char, a string and a wstring as `?` writes them (DoPrintSpecOf); a wchar, a ptr
    // to char / wchar by DoDebugWriter's routine (the C texts with the `?` spec's words);
    // every other form, a choices value too, its own text (DoPrintValueOf). The print call
    // ACall and its argument values AValues as DoPrintSpecOf takes them. 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPrintDebugOf(const ASink: int64; const AValue: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ACall: int64; const AValues: ref Int64List; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LForm: PrintForm;
      LSpec: FormatSpec;
      LKind: RuntimeRoutine;
      LFunction: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      LForm := PrintFormOf(self.FTree, AType);
      LSpec := DefaultFormatSpec();
      LSpec.Presentation := "?";
      if (LForm = PrintForm.Char) or (LForm = PrintForm.Text) or (LForm = PrintForm.WideText) then
        return self.DoPrintSpecOf(ASink, AValue, AType, LSpec, ACall, AValues, ANode);
      end;
      if not self.DoDebugWriter(LForm, LKind) then
        return self.DoPrintValueOf(ASink, AValue, AType, ANode);
      end;
      LFunction := self.DoRuntimeFunction(LKind, ANode);
      if LFunction = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(ASink);
      LArgs.Add(self.DoConvertIr(AValue, self.DoParamTypeOf(LFunction, 1), ANode));
      if LKind <> RuntimeRoutine.WriteDebugWideChar then
        LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := self.DoSpecData(LSpec, ANode);
        LArgs.Add(LAddress);
      end;
      return self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(LKind, LArgs, ANode);
    end;

    // The calls writing range level ALevel of the placeholder AItem of the print call ACall
    // (AValues its arguments' values after the format) to the print sink ASink: the static
    // array of the canonical type AType at AAddress as libc++'s range_formatter formats it
    // with the level's spec (DoLevelSpec). With a width or `?s` (DoRangeNeedsScratch) the
    // width operand first (std::format reads a range's spec before its elements), then the
    // elements into the level's scratch string (DoRangeScratch, emptied by StrTake), then
    // that string to ASink by the string formatter with the level's spec (WriteSpecStr: its
    // fill, align and width, `?s` the debug form, no precision); else the elements straight
    // to ASink (DoRangeElements). A set at AAddress (its bytes) the same way, its members
    // for elements; a dynamic array from the slot at AAddress holding its block, its
    // elements counted when it runs. The last call, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPrintRangeOf(const ASink: int64; const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64;
      const AItem: FormatItem; const ALevel: int64; const ACall: int64; const AValues: ref Int64List;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LSpec: FormatSpec;
      LSlot: int64;
      LFunction: int64;
      LWidth: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      if (ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) <> TypeClass.StaticArray) and
        (ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) <> TypeClass.DynamicArray) and
        (ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) <> TypeClass.SetType) then
        self.DoRefuse(ANode, "a print argument of type '" + TypeText(self.FTree, AType) + "'");
        return 0;
      end;
      LSpec := self.DoLevelSpec(AItem, ALevel);
      if not self.DoRangeNeedsScratch(LSpec) then
        return self.DoRangeElements(ASink, AAddress, AType, AItem, ALevel, ACall, AValues, ANode);
      end;
      LFunction := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecStr, ANode);
      if LFunction = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LWidth := self.DoSpecCountOperand(ACall, AValues, LSpec.WidthArgument,
        self.DoParamTypeOf(LFunction, 3));
      if LWidth = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LSlot := self.DoRangeScratch(ACall, ALevel);
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrTake, LSlot, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ANode),
        ANode) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.DoRangeElements(LSlot, AAddress, AType, AItem, ALevel, ACall, AValues, ANode) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(ASink);
      LArgs.Add(self.DoLoad(LSlot, IrType.Pointer, ANode));
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := self.DoSpecData(LSpec, ANode);
      LArgs.Add(LAddress);
      LArgs.Add(LWidth);
      LArgs.Add(self.DoConstant(self.DoParamTypeOf(LFunction, 4), -1, ANode));
      return self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecStr, LArgs, ANode);
    end;

    // The calls writing the elements of the static array of the canonical type AType at
    // AAddress, range level ALevel of the placeholder AItem (its spec DoLevelSpec), to the
    // print sink ASink as libc++'s range_formatter writes them: `s` / `?s` its chars one
    // after another (the string's bytes: __format_as_string); else `[` and `]` around them
    // unless `n`, ", " between them (__format_as_sequence); each by DoRangeElement. The first
    // element at AAddress, then a loop over a counter slot from 1 while below the count, each
    // element's address AAddress moved by the counter (DoMovePointer). A set's members by
    // DoSetMembers. A dynamic array's elements from its block (the slot at AAddress holds
    // it) by DoDynamicRange. The last call, 0 after LW0001; a bound with no value faults
    hidden method DoRangeElements(const ASink: int64; const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64;
      const AItem: FormatItem; const ALevel: int64; const ACall: int64; const AValues: ref Int64List;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LSpec: FormatSpec;
      LWriter: int64;
      LElement: int64;
      LLow: int64;
      LHigh: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LSequence: bool;
      LBrackets: bool;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.SetType then
        return self.DoSetMembers(ASink, AAddress, AType, AItem, ALevel, ACall, AValues, ANode);
      end;
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.DynamicArray then
        return self.DoDynamicRange(ASink, AAddress, AType, AItem, ALevel, ACall, AValues, ANode);
      end;
      LSpec := self.DoLevelSpec(AItem, ALevel);
      LWriter := self.FFunctionOf[self.FTree[ACall].ResolvedCallee];
      LElement := TargetOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if not BoundValue(self.FTree, self.FTarget, self.FTree.FirstOf(self.FTree[AType].ResolvedDecl,
        NodeRole.LowBound), LLow) then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_LOW_BOUND + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
      end;
      if not BoundValue(self.FTree, self.FTarget, self.FTree.FirstOf(self.FTree[AType].ResolvedDecl,
        NodeRole.HighBound), LHigh) then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_HIGH_BOUND + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
      end;
      LCount := LHigh - LLow + 1;
      LSequence := LSpec.Presentation = "";
      LBrackets := LSequence and (not LSpec.ClearBrackets);
      LId := -1;
      if LBrackets then
        LId := self.DoWriteText(LWriter, ASink, "[", ACall);
      end;
      if LCount > 0 then
        LId := self.DoRangeElement(ASink, AAddress, LElement, AItem, ALevel, ACall, AValues, ANode);
        if LId = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      if LCount > 1 then
        if not self.DoRangeLoop(ASink, AAddress, AType, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LCount, ANode),
          LSequence, AItem, ALevel, ACall, AValues, ANode) then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      if LBrackets then
        LId := self.DoWriteText(LWriter, ASink, "]", ACall);
      end;
      return LId;
    end;

    // The calls writing the elements of the dynamic array of the canonical type AType whose
    // block the slot at AAddress holds (nil: empty), range level ALevel of the placeholder
    // AItem, to the print sink ASink as DoRangeElements writes a static array's: `s` / `?s`
    // its chars one after another, else `[` and `]` unless `n` and ", " between; the count
    // read from the block when it runs (DoBlockCount), the first element and the loop over
    // the rest (DoRangeLoop) only when it holds any. The last call, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoDynamicRange(const ASink: int64; const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64;
      const AItem: FormatItem; const ALevel: int64; const ACall: int64; const AValues: ref Int64List;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LSpec: FormatSpec;
      LWriter: int64;
      LBlock: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LHeld: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
      LSequence: bool;
      LBrackets: bool;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LSpec := self.DoLevelSpec(AItem, ALevel);
      LWriter := self.FFunctionOf[self.FTree[ACall].ResolvedCallee];
      LSequence := LSpec.Presentation = "";
      LBrackets := LSequence and (not LSpec.ClearBrackets);
      LId := -1;
      if LBrackets then
        LId := self.DoWriteText(LWriter, ASink, "[", ACall);
      end;
      LBlock := self.DoLoad(AAddress, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      LCount := self.DoBlockCount(LBlock, ANode);
      LHeld := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.SGreater, LCount, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, ANode),
        ANode), LHeld, LJoin, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LHeld;
      LFirst := self.DoByteOffset(LBlock, ADAM_LOWERING_ARRAY_HEADER, ANode);
      if self.DoRangeElement(ASink, LFirst, TargetOf(self.FTree, AType), AItem, ALevel, ACall, AValues,
        ANode) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if not self.DoRangeLoop(ASink, LFirst, AType, LCount, LSequence, AItem, ALevel, ACall, AValues, ANode) then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LJoin;
      if LBrackets then
        LId := self.DoWriteText(LWriter, ASink, "]", ACall);
      end;
      return LId;
    end;

    // The loop writing elements 1 .. ACount - 1 (ACount an int64 value) of the array of the
    // canonical type AType whose first element is at AAddress (range level ALevel of the
    // placeholder AItem) to the print sink
    // ASink: a counter slot from 1; a head block testing it below ACount, to the body or
    // the exit; the body ", " first when ASequence (DoRangeElements), the element at
    // AAddress moved by the counter (DoMovePointer, DoRangeElement), the counter one more,
    // back to the head; the exit the current block after it. False after LW0001
    hidden method DoRangeLoop(const ASink: int64; const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ACount: int64; const ASequence: bool; const AItem: FormatItem; const ALevel: int64;
      const ACall: int64; const AValues: ref Int64List; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LWriter: int64;
      LCounter: int64;
      LHead: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LExit: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LOne: int64;
      LNext: int64;
    begin
      LWriter := self.FFunctionOf[self.FTree[ACall].ResolvedCallee];
      LCounter := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, 8, 8);
      self.DoStore(LCounter, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 1, ANode), ANode);
      LHead := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LExit := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoJumpTo(LHead, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LHead;
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      self.DoBranchOn(self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.SLess, LIndex, ACount, ANode), LBody, LExit, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LBody;
      // the counter read again in the body: its value is the body's own, whatever blocks an
      // element's writing adds after it
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      if ASequence then
        if self.DoWriteText(LWriter, ASink, ", ", ACall) = 0 then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      if self.DoRangeElement(ASink, self.DoMovePointer(AAddress, LIndex, AType, false, ANode),
        TargetOf(self.FTree, AType), AItem, ALevel, ACall, AValues, ANode) = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LOne := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 1, ANode);
      LNext := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Add, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LNext).Operands.Add(LIndex);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LNext).Operands.Add(LOne);
      self.DoStore(LCounter, LNext, ANode);
      self.DoJumpTo(LHead, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LExit;
      return true;
    end;

    // The call writing the element of the canonical type AElement at AAddress of range level
    // ALevel of the placeholder AItem (its spec DoLevelSpec) to the print sink ASink: an
    // array or a set the next level (DoPrintRangeOf); else its value (a text's pointer, any
    // other by its IR type) by DoRangeValue. 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoRangeElement(const ASink: int64; const AAddress: int64; const AElement: int64;
      const AItem: FormatItem; const ALevel: int64; const ACall: int64; const AValues: ref Int64List;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LSpec: FormatSpec;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      LSpec := self.DoLevelSpec(AItem, ALevel);
      if (LSpec.Presentation = "") and (PrintFormOf(self.FTree, AElement) = PrintForm.Range) then
        return self.DoPrintRangeOf(ASink, AAddress, AElement, AItem, ALevel + 1, ACall, AValues, ANode);
      end;
      if self.DoIsText(AElement) then
        LValue := self.DoLoad(AAddress, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      else
        LValue := self.DoLoad(AAddress, self.DoIrType(AElement), ANode);
      end;
      return self.DoRangeValue(ASink, LValue, AElement, AItem, ALevel, ACall, AValues, ANode);
    end;

    // The call writing AValue, an element of the canonical type AElement of range level
    // ALevel of the placeholder AItem (its spec DoLevelSpec; an array's element loaded by
    // DoRangeElement, a set's member by DoSetMember), to the print sink ASink: `s` / `?s` a
    // char in its own text; with the element spec written after the level's `:` by
    // DoPrintSpecOf (one that writes nothing: its own text); with none in the debug form
    // (DoPrintDebugOf: libc++ sets it when a range writes no type and no element spec). 0
    // after LW0001
    hidden method DoRangeValue(const ASink: int64; const AValue: int64; const AElement: int64;
      const AItem: FormatItem; const ALevel: int64; const ACall: int64; const AValues: ref Int64List;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LSpec: FormatSpec;
    begin
      LSpec := self.DoLevelSpec(AItem, ALevel);
      if LSpec.Presentation <> "" then
        return self.DoPrintValueOf(ASink, AValue, AElement, ANode);
      end;
      if ALevel + 1 < len(AItem.Specs) then
        if self.DoIsPlainSpec(AItem.Specs[ALevel + 1]) then
          return self.DoPrintValueOf(ASink, AValue, AElement, ANode);
        end;
        return self.DoPrintSpecOf(ASink, AValue, AElement, AItem.Specs[ALevel + 1], ACall, AValues,
          ANode);
      end;
      return self.DoPrintDebugOf(ASink, AValue, AElement, ACall, AValues, ANode);
    end;

    // The calls writing the members of the set of the canonical type AType at AAddress (its
    // bytes: bit i member low + i, Layout.SetRange), range level ALevel of the placeholder
    // AItem (its spec DoLevelSpec), to the print sink ASink as PaskalCPP prints a set: its
    // members in ascending order as a range's elements (`[` and `]` around them unless `n`,
    // ", " between them; `s` / `?s` a set of char's members one after another). A loop over
    // a counter slot from 0 while below the member count: a head block testing it, a body
    // testing the member's bit (DoSetIn's byte and bit), to a block writing it
    // (DoSetMember) or straight on; the counter one more, back to the head. Which member
    // comes first is known only at run time: a flag slot, 1 until a member is written. The
    // last call, 0 after LW0001; a set with no known range faults
    hidden method DoSetMembers(const ASink: int64; const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64;
      const AItem: FormatItem; const ALevel: int64; const ACall: int64; const AValues: ref Int64List;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LSpec: FormatSpec;
      LWriter: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LLow: int64;
      LHigh: int64;
      LSequence: bool;
      LBrackets: bool;
      LFirst: int64;
      LCounter: int64;
      LHead: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LWrite: int64;
      LNext: int64;
      LExit: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LByteAt: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LByte: int64;
      LBitAt: int64;
      LBit: int64;
      LHas: int64;
      LOne: int64;
      LMore: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LSpec := self.DoLevelSpec(AItem, ALevel);
      LWriter := self.FFunctionOf[self.FTree[ACall].ResolvedCallee];
      LMember := SetMemberOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if (LMember = 0) or (not SetRange(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType, LLow, LHigh)) then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_LOW_BOUND + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
      end;
      LSequence := LSpec.Presentation = "";
      LBrackets := LSequence and (not LSpec.ClearBrackets);
      LId := -1;
      if LBrackets then
        LId := self.DoWriteText(LWriter, ASink, "[", ACall);
        if LId = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      LFirst := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, 8, 8);
      self.DoStore(LFirst, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 1, ANode), ANode);
      LCounter := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, 8, 8);
      self.DoStore(LCounter, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, ANode), ANode);
      LHead := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LWrite := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LNext := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LExit := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoJumpTo(LHead, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LHead;
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      self.DoBranchOn(self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.SLess, LIndex,
        self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LHigh - LLow + 1, ANode), ANode), LBody, LExit, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LBody;
      // the member's byte (its bit div 8), then its bit in that byte (its bit mod 8)
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LByteAt := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.Shr, LIndex, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 3, ANode),
        IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Offset, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Operands.Add(AAddress);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Operands.Add(LByteAt);
      LByte := self.DoConvertIr(self.DoLoad(LAddress, IrType.UInt8, ANode), IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LBitAt := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.BitAnd, LIndex, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 7, ANode),
        IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LBit := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.BitAnd, self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.Shr, LByte, LBitAt, IrType.Int64,
        ANode), self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 1, ANode), IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LHas := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.NotEqual, LBit, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, ANode),
        ANode);
      self.DoBranchOn(LHas, LWrite, LNext, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LWrite;
      if not self.DoSetMember(ASink, LIndex, LLow, LMember, LFirst, LSequence, AItem, ALevel, ACall,
        AValues, ANode) then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoJumpTo(LNext, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LNext;
      // the operands emitted before the add that uses them
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LOne := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 1, ANode);
      LMore := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Add, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LMore).Operands.Add(LIndex);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LMore).Operands.Add(LOne);
      self.DoStore(LCounter, LMore, ANode);
      self.DoJumpTo(LHead, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LExit;
      if LBrackets then
        LId := self.DoWriteText(LWriter, ASink, "]", ACall);
      end;
      return LId;
    end;

    // The calls writing the member at bit AIndex (an Int64 IR value) of a set whose lowest
    // member is ALow and whose members have the canonical type AMember, range level ALevel
    // of the placeholder AItem, to the print sink ASink (DoSetMembers' write block): when
    // ASequence ", " first unless the flag slot AFirst still holds 1 (no member written
    // yet), the flag then 0; the member's value (ALow + AIndex as AMember's IR type, a bool
    // by a compare) by DoRangeValue. False after LW0001
    hidden method DoSetMember(const ASink: int64; const AIndex: int64; const ALow: int64;
      const AMember: int64; const AFirst: int64; const ASequence: bool; const AItem: FormatItem;
      const ALevel: int64; const ACall: int64; const AValues: ref Int64List; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LWriter: int64;
      LComma: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
    begin
      LWriter := self.FFunctionOf[self.FTree[ACall].ResolvedCallee];
      if ASequence then
        LComma := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
        LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
        self.DoBranchOn(self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.Equal, self.DoLoad(AFirst, IrType.Int64, ANode),
          self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, ANode), ANode), LComma, LJoin, ANode);
        self.FBlock := LComma;
        if self.DoWriteText(LWriter, ASink, ", ", ACall) = 0 then
          return false;
        end;
        self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, ANode);
        self.FBlock := LJoin;
        self.DoStore(AFirst, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, ANode), ANode);
      end;
      LValue := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.Add, AIndex, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, ALow, ANode),
        IrType.Int64, ANode);
      // a bool member is the compare (no integer converts to bool), any other the value as
      // its IR type
      if self.DoIrType(AMember) = IrType.Bool then
        LValue := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.NotEqual, LValue, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0,
          ANode), ANode);
      else
        LValue := self.DoConvertIr(LValue, self.DoIrType(AMember), ANode);
      end;
      return self.DoRangeValue(ASink, LValue, AMember, AItem, ALevel, ACall, AValues, ANode) <> 0;
    end;

    // True when the SinkSpec* routine AKind takes a precision operand after the width (the
    // string formatter's forms: the text forms and a choices value; the float formatter's)
    hidden const method DoSpecTakesPrecision(const AKind: RuntimeRoutine): bool;
    begin
      return (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecStr) or (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecWideText) or
        (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecWideChar) or (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecCText) or
        (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecWideCText) or (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecChoice) or
        (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecFloat32) or (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.WriteSpecFloat64);
    end;

    // The words of the text AText as WriteChoice reads a name, added to AWords: its length,
    // then its bytes packed 8 to an int64 word, little-endian (the last word's unused bytes
    // zero)
    hidden method DoNameWords(const AText: string; const AWords: ref Int64List);
    var
      LWord: uint64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      AWords.Add(len(AText));
      LWord := 0;
      for LI := 0 to len(AText) - 1 do
        LWord := LWord | (uint64(uint8(AText[LI])) shl (8 * (LI mod 8)));
        if ((LI mod 8) = 7) or (LI = len(AText) - 1) then
          AWords.Add(int64(LWord));
          LWord := 0;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The read-only names table of the canonical choices type AType, made the first time
    // (FChoiceNamesOf) of DoChoiceNameWords' words, as WriteChoice reads it
    hidden method DoChoiceNamesData(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    begin
      if self.FChoiceNamesOf[AType] <> 0 then
        return self.FChoiceNamesOf[AType];
      end;
      self.FChoiceNamesOf[AType] := self.DoWordsData(ADAM_LOWERING_CHOICE_NAMES_SYMBOL,
        self.DoChoiceNameWords(AType), ref Int64List(), ANode);
      return self.FChoiceNamesOf[AType];
    end;

    // The words of the names table of the canonical choices type AType (System.Runtime's
    // SinkChoice ATable): the count of its values, its name (TypeText, DoNameWords), then per
    // value in declaration order its number and its name. The values are the ChoiceValue
    // members of its body (the ChoicesType node itself for a type written in place, else its
    // declaration's), their numbers as SEM folded them
    hidden method DoChoiceNameWords(const AType: int64): ref Int64List;
    var
      LBody: int64;
      LWords: ref Int64List;
      LMember: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LBody := AType;
      if self.FTree[AType].Kind <> NodeKind.ChoicesType then
        LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, AType);
      end;
      LCount := 0;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
        if self.FTree[self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI)].Kind = NodeKind.ChoiceValue then
          LCount := LCount + 1;
        end;
      end;
      LWords := ref Int64List();
      LWords.Add(LCount);
      self.DoNameWords(TypeText(self.FTree, AType), LWords);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
        LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
        if self.FTree[LMember].Kind = NodeKind.ChoiceValue then
          LWords.Add(int64(self.FTree[LMember].ResolvedConst.Bits));
          self.DoNameWords(self.FTree[LMember].Text, LWords);
        end;
      end;
      return LWords;
    end;

    // True when the canonical type AType is of the string family: string (UTF-8 bytes) or
    // wstring (UTF-16 units, DESIGN sec 8). Its values travel as a pointer (nil or its
    // block, System.Runtime's layout, one for both), but DoIrType keeps it Void: only the
    // forms below lower a string, so a form not built yet is LW0001, never pointer code
    hidden const method DoIsText(const AType: int64): bool;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      if AType = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      return (LClass = TypeClass.Text) or (LClass = TypeClass.WideText);
    end;

    // True when the canonical type AType is a dynamic array: like a text, its value travels
    // as a pointer (nil or its block, System.Runtime's layout), DoIrType keeping it Void
    hidden const method DoIsArrayValue(const AType: int64): bool;
    begin
      return (AType <> 0) and (ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.DynamicArray);
    end;

    // True when the canonical type AType is a ref (`ref T`), an own (`own T`: the same
    // counted block, which Semantics keeps to one owner by moves (SM0427), so an own converts
    // to a ref as it is) or a task (`task T`, a ref block whose descriptor is its async call
    // site's): like a text, its value travels as a pointer (nil or its block,
    // System.Runtime's layout: the object after the header), DoIrType keeping it Void
    hidden const method DoIsRefValue(const AType: int64): bool;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      if AType = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      return (LClass = TypeClass.RefType) or (LClass = TypeClass.OwnType) or
        (LClass = TypeClass.TaskType) or (LClass = TypeClass.SequenceType);
    end;

    // True when the canonical type AType is an own I or a ref I (I3): its value is nil or
    // the address of its object's itable word for I, counted on the object's block through
    // the itable's offset back (System.Runtime's IntfAddRef / IntfRelease / IntfAssign)
    hidden const method DoIsInterfaceOwner(const AType: int64): bool;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      if AType = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      return ((LClass = TypeClass.RefType) or (LClass = TypeClass.OwnType)) and
        (ClassOf(self.FTree, TargetOf(self.FTree, AType)) = TypeClass.InterfaceType);
    end;

    // True when the canonical type AType is a weak (`weak T`, M3.10g): its value is nil or
    // the ref block it watches (System.Runtime's layout), counted in the block's weak count
    // (WeakAddRef, WeakRelease, WeakAssign), never its ref count; it travels as a pointer
    hidden const method DoIsWeakValue(const AType: int64): bool;
    begin
      return (AType <> 0) and (ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.WeakType);
    end;

    // True when a value of the canonical type AType is a block pointer a slot of its own
    // holds that is neither a text nor a dynamic array: a ref (DoIsRefValue) or a weak
    // (DoIsWeakValue); a temporary of one is a pointer slot (DoPointerTemporary)
    hidden const method DoIsOwnerValue(const AType: int64): bool;
    begin
      return self.DoIsRefValue(AType) or self.DoIsWeakValue(AType);
    end;

    // True when a value of the canonical type AType is a reference to a counted block: a
    // text (DoIsText), a dynamic array (DoIsArrayValue), a ref (DoIsRefValue) or a weak
    // (DoIsWeakValue). Held, borrowed, passed and returned alike (a holder added by
    // DoAddHolder); released and stored by each one's routines (DoReleaseAt,
    // DoStoreManaged)
    hidden const method DoIsManaged(const AType: int64): bool;
    begin
      return self.DoIsText(AType) or self.DoIsArrayValue(AType) or self.DoIsOwnerValue(AType);
    end;

    // One more holder of the managed value AValue of the canonical type AType (DoIsManaged)
    // at ANode: a weak's by WeakAddRef (its block's weak count), any other's by StrAddRef
    // (texts, dynamic arrays and refs count their holders alike); the call, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAddHolder(const AValue: int64; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    begin
      if self.DoIsWeakValue(AType) then
        return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.WeakAddRef, AValue, 0, ANode);
      end;
      // an own I / ref I counts its object's block (I3)
      if self.DoIsInterfaceOwner(AType) then
        return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.IntfAddRef, AValue, 0, ANode);
      end;
      return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrAddRef, AValue, 0, ANode);
    end;

    // True when a value of the canonical type AType is or holds, at any depth, a managed
    // value (DoIsManaged): Layout.HoldsManaged's texts and dynamic arrays, or a ref
    // (DoHoldsOwner's walk)
    hidden const method DoHoldsManaged(const AType: int64): bool;
    begin
      return HoldsManaged(self.FTree, AType) or self.DoHoldsOwner(AType);
    end;

    // True when the canonical type AType is wstring (its units 2 bytes: DoTextRoutine)
    hidden const method DoIsWideText(const AType: int64): bool;
    begin
      return (AType <> 0) and (ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.WideText);
    end;

    // The runtime routine AKind (a string one) for a text of the canonical type AType: its
    // WStr* twin when AType is wstring and AKind depends on the unit size, else AKind
    // itself (StrRelease / StrAssign / StrTake / StrLength serve both; StrWrite is a
    // string's)
    hidden const method DoTextRoutine(const AKind: RuntimeRoutine; const AType: int64): RuntimeRoutine;
    begin
      if not self.DoIsWideText(AType) then
        return AKind;
      end;
      if AKind = RuntimeRoutine.StrConcat then
        return RuntimeRoutine.WStrConcat;
      end;
      if AKind = RuntimeRoutine.StrFromChar then
        return RuntimeRoutine.WStrFromChar;
      end;
      if AKind = RuntimeRoutine.StrCompare then
        return RuntimeRoutine.WStrCompare;
      end;
      if AKind = RuntimeRoutine.StrUnique then
        return RuntimeRoutine.WStrUnique;
      end;
      if AKind = RuntimeRoutine.StrSetLength then
        return RuntimeRoutine.WStrSetLength;
      end;
      return AKind;
    end;

    // The function of the runtime unit's routine AKind (SEM found it once:
    // SyntaxTree.RuntimeRoutineOf); 0 after LW0001 at ANode when the program has none
    hidden method DoRuntimeFunction(const AKind: RuntimeRoutine; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      LDecl := self.FTree.RuntimeRoutineOf(AKind);
      if (LDecl = 0) or (self.FFunctionOf[LDecl] = 0) then
        self.DoRefuse(ANode, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(ANode) + " with no runtime unit");
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.FFunctionOf[LDecl];
    end;

    // A call at ANode of the runtime unit's routine AKind with the operand AFirst, then
    // ASecond (0: none), its allocation site stored around it when AKind makes a text
    // (DoKindWhat, DoCallRuntimeSite); the call (its result when the routine has one), 0
    // after LW0001
    hidden method DoCallRuntime(const AKind: RuntimeRoutine; const AFirst: int64;
      const ASecond: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
    begin
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(AFirst);
      if ASecond <> 0 then
        LArgs.Add(ASecond);
      end;
      return self.DoCallRuntimeSite(AKind, LArgs, ANode, self.DoKindWhat(AKind));
    end;

    // What the runtime routine AKind allocates on its own construct's behalf when the
    // routine's kind alone tells it (M3.12b): "string" for a string made or grown (and a
    // format known only at run time: FormatRun's text), "wstring" for a wstring; "" for
    // every other kind (allocating nothing, or a kind whose caller names what it allocates:
    // a dynamic array's element type, an object's type, DoCallRuntimeSite)
    hidden const method DoKindWhat(const AKind: RuntimeRoutine): string;
    begin
      if (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.StrConcat) or (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.StrFromChar) or
        (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.StrSetLength) or (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.StrUnique) or
        (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.WStrToUtf8) or (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.FormatRun) then
        return "string";
      end;
      if (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.WStrConcat) or (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.WStrFromChar) or
        (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.WStrSetLength) or (AKind = RuntimeRoutine.WStrUnique) then
        return "wstring";
      end;
      return "";
    end;

    // What a dynamic array of the canonical type AType allocates (M3.12b): "dynarray of"
    // and its element type's text
    hidden const method DoArrayWhat(const AType: int64): string;
    begin
      return "dynarray of " + TypeText(self.FTree, TargetOf(self.FTree, AType));
    end;

    // True when the program's allocation sites are stored (M3.12b): a debug build only
    // (SyntaxTree.IsDebugBuild; a release build gets no site store, no site table: every
    // runtime call compiles as it would without them), whose runtime declares GAllocSite
    // (Semantics: SyntaxTree.AllocSite) with its blob made (DoThreadStatic)
    hidden const method DoSitesOn(): bool;
    var
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      if not self.FTree.IsDebugBuild() then
        return false;
      end;
      LDecl := self.FTree.AllocSite;
      return (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FDataOf[LDecl] <> 0);
    end;

    // The site number of the allocating construct ANode that allocates AWhat (M3.12b): the
    // one made at ANode before for the same AWhat (the construct lowered again), else a new
    // one; numbered in the order met until DoNumberSites renumbers them in source order
    hidden method DoSiteOf(const ANode: int64; const AWhat: string): int64;
    var
      LSite: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LSite := self.FSiteOfNode[ANode];
      if (LSite <> 0) and (self.FSiteWhats[LSite - 1] = AWhat) then
        return LSite;
      end;
      // a node making two kinds of block (rare) is searched for its other one
      if LSite <> 0 then
        for LI := len(self.FSiteNodes) - 1 downto 0 do
          if (self.FSiteNodes[LI] = ANode) and (self.FSiteWhats[LI] = AWhat) then
            return LI + 1;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      LI := len(self.FSiteNodes);
      setlength(self.FSiteNodes, LI + 1);
      setlength(self.FSiteWhats, LI + 1);
      self.FSiteNodes[LI] := ANode;
      self.FSiteWhats[LI] := AWhat;
      self.FSiteOfNode[ANode] := LI + 1;
      return LI + 1;
    end;

    // GAllocSite set to the site number ASite (0: none) at ANode, in the calling thread's
    // copy; a site's constant is recorded for DoNumberSites to give it its id in the unit,
    // and the unit's base word added to it (SU2.4: the runtime numbers every unit's sites
    // on from the units before it as the entry hands the site list over, HeapSiteList)
    hidden method DoStoreSite(const ASite: int64; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LValue: int64;
      LTable: int64;
      LOffset: int64;
      LBaseAt: int64;
      LBase: int64;
      LSum: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LValue := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int32, ASite, ANode);
      if ASite <> 0 then
        LI := len(self.FSiteStores);
        setlength(self.FSiteStores, LI + 1);
        setlength(self.FSiteStoreOf, LI + 1);
        self.FSiteStores[LI] := LValue;
        self.FSiteStoreOf[LI] := ASite;
        LTable := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LTable).Link := self.DoSiteData();
        // the offset's operands are made before it (an operand comes before its use)
        LOffset := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_BASE, ANode);
        LBaseAt := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Offset, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LBaseAt).Operands.Add(LTable);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LBaseAt).Operands.Add(LOffset);
        LBase := self.DoLoad(LBaseAt, IrType.Int32, ANode);
        LSum := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Add, IrType.Int32, ANode);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LSum).Operands.Add(LBase);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LSum).Operands.Add(LValue);
        LValue := LSum;
      end;
      self.DoStore(self.DoDataAddress(self.FTree.AllocSite, ANode), LValue, ANode);
    end;

    // The site of the construct ANode that allocates AWhat stored into GAllocSite (M3.12b);
    // the site number, 0 when sites are off or AWhat is "" (nothing stored). The caller
    // emits its runtime call next, then DoLeaveSite
    hidden method DoEnterSite(const ANode: int64; const AWhat: string): int64;
    var
      LSite: int64;
    begin
      if (AWhat = "") or not self.DoSitesOn() then
        return 0;
      end;
      LSite := self.DoSiteOf(ANode, AWhat);
      self.DoStoreSite(LSite, ANode);
      return LSite;
    end;

    // GAllocSite given back to the enclosing construct's site (FSiteOuter; 0: none) at
    // ANode after the call DoEnterSite stored ASite for (nothing when ASite is 0, or the
    // block already ended)
    hidden method DoLeaveSite(const ASite: int64; const ANode: int64);
    begin
      if (ASite = 0) or self.DoEnded() then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoStoreSite(self.FSiteOuter, ANode);
    end;

    // A call at ANode of the runtime unit's routine AKind with the operands AArgs in order,
    // that allocates AWhat on its construct's behalf ("": nothing): the construct's site
    // stored into GAllocSite before the call, the enclosing one's after it (DoEnterSite,
    // DoLeaveSite; M3.12b); the call, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoCallRuntimeSite(const AKind: RuntimeRoutine; const AArgs: ref Int64List;
      const ANode: int64; const AWhat: string): int64;
    var
      LFunction: int64;
      LSite: int64;
      LId: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LFunction := self.DoRuntimeFunction(AKind, ANode);
      if LFunction = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LSite := self.DoEnterSite(ANode, AWhat);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Call, self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.ResultType, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Link := LFunction;
      for LI := 0 to AArgs.Count - 1 do
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(AArgs[LI]);
      end;
      self.DoLeaveSite(LSite, ANode);
      return LId;
    end;

    // DoCallRuntimeSite with the one operand AFirst
    hidden method DoCallRuntimeSiteOne(const AKind: RuntimeRoutine; const AFirst: int64;
      const ANode: int64; const AWhat: string): int64;
    var
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
    begin
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(AFirst);
      return self.DoCallRuntimeSite(AKind, LArgs, ANode, AWhat);
    end;

    // The 8 bytes of AValue, little-endian, added to the data blob AData
    hidden method DoAddLe64(const AData: int64; const AValue: int64);
    var
      LBits: uint64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LBits := uint64(AValue);
      for LI := 0 to 7 do
        self.FModule.DataAt(AData).AddByte(uint8(LBits & 255));
        LBits := LBits shr 8;
      end;
    end;

    // The read-only data blob of the string literal AId (folded to the bytes AText): a block
    // in System.Runtime's string layout whose ref count says constant (never counted or
    // freed); 0 for "" (the empty string is nil, no block)
    hidden method DoStringBlock(const AId: int64; const AText: string): int64;
    var
      LData: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if len(AText) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LData := self.DoHelperData(ADAM_LOWERING_STRING_SYMBOL,
        8, AId);
      self.DoAddLe64(LData, ADAM_LOWERING_STRING_CONSTANT_COUNT);
      self.DoAddLe64(LData, len(AText));
      for LI := 0 to len(AText) - 1 do
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(uint8(AText[LI]));
      end;
      self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(0);
      return LData;
    end;

    // The value of the string literal AId (folded to the bytes AText): the address of its
    // constant block (DoStringBlock); "" is the empty string, nil
    hidden method DoStringLiteral(const AId: int64; const AText: string): int64;
    var
      LData: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      LData := self.DoStringBlock(AId, AText);
      if LData = 0 then
        return self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, AId);
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := LData;
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // The read-only data blob of the string literal AId used as a wstring (its UTF-16 units
    // AUnits): a block in System.Runtime's layout as DoStringBlock's, its length in units,
    // each unit little-endian, a 0 unit after them; 0 for no unit (the empty wstring is nil)
    hidden method DoWideBlock(const AId: int64; const AUnits: wstring): int64;
    var
      LData: int64;
      LUnit: uint16;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if len(AUnits) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LData := self.DoHelperData(ADAM_LOWERING_STRING_SYMBOL,
        8, AId);
      self.DoAddLe64(LData, ADAM_LOWERING_STRING_CONSTANT_COUNT);
      self.DoAddLe64(LData, len(AUnits));
      for LI := 0 to len(AUnits) - 1 do
        LUnit := uint16(AUnits[LI]);
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(uint8(LUnit & 255));
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(uint8(LUnit shr 8));
      end;
      self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(0);
      self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(0);
      return LData;
    end;

    // The value of the string literal AId used as a wstring (its UTF-16 units AUnits): the
    // address of its constant block (DoWideBlock); no unit is the empty wstring, nil
    hidden method DoWideLiteral(const AId: int64; const AUnits: wstring): int64;
    var
      LData: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      LData := self.DoWideBlock(AId, AUnits);
      if LData = 0 then
        return self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, AId);
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := LData;
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // The UTF-16 units of the string constant AId used as a wstring: a literal's own wide
    // encoding (the parser decoded it: BNF sec 9, type-driven), a const's through its
    // initializer, else (a constant folded from several) its UTF-8 text decoded
    hidden const method DoWideUnits(const AId: int64): wstring;
    var
      LRoot: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
      LText: string;
      LUnits: wstring;
      LIndex: int64;
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LRoot := AId;
      while self.FTree[LRoot].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LRoot := self.FTree.FirstOf(LRoot, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      if self.FTree[LRoot].Kind = NodeKind.StringLiteral then
        return self.FTree[LRoot].DecodedWide;
      end;
      LDecl := self.FTree[LRoot].ResolvedDecl;
      if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.ConstDecl) and
        (self.FTree.FirstOf(LDecl, NodeRole.Initializer) <> 0) then
        return self.DoWideUnits(self.FTree.FirstOf(LDecl, NodeRole.Initializer));
      end;
      LText := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConst.Text;
      // a code point takes at most 2 units, and a UTF-8 byte at least 1
      setlength(LUnits, len(LText) + 1);
      LIndex := 0;
      LAt := 0;
      while LIndex < len(LText) do
        EncodeUtf16Char(LUnits, LAt, DecodeUtf8Char(LText, LIndex));
      end;
      setlength(LUnits, LAt);
      return LUnits;
    end;

    // The value of the expression AId whose type where used is managed (DoIsManaged: of the
    // string family, or a dynamic array): a literal's constant block (DoWideLiteral's when
    // it is used as a wstring), a concatenation's new text (DoConcatValue), utf8's new
    // string (DoUtf8Value), a call's result (kept in the call's hidden slot: DoEmitCall), a
    // conditional's chosen side (DoConditional), an array literal's new block
    // (DoDynamicLiteral), a typed pack's next / get (its item's block, borrowed:
    // DoPackManaged), else the block a place holds (a borrowed value: the place keeps its
    // reference); an own or a ref converted to an own I / ref I moved to the itable word
    // (DoReachOwner, I3); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoManagedValue(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      // an anchor held for the call being lowered: its value made once (DoAnchorBegin)
      if self.FPrimed[AId] <> 0 then
        return self.FPrimed[AId];
      end;
      LValue := self.DoManagedOwn(AId);
      if (LValue = 0) or (self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConvert = 0) then
        return LValue;
      end;
      return self.DoReachOwner(LValue, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConvert, AId);
    end;

    // The own or ref AValue of the canonical type AFrom as the own or ref ATo, at ANode (I3):
    // an object's block converted to an interface the object implements moved to its
    // itable word for it (past the block's header: DoReachOffset), nil staying nil
    // (DoMoveUnlessNil); AValue itself for any other pair (one block, or between
    // interfaces: an interface's itable starts with its parent's slots)
    hidden method DoReachOwner(const AValue: int64; const AFrom: int64; const ATo: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LFromTarget: int64;
      LToTarget: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoIsInterfaceOwner(ATo) or not self.DoIsRefValue(AFrom) or self.DoIsInterfaceOwner(AFrom) then
        return AValue;
      end;
      LFromTarget := TargetOf(self.FTree, AFrom);
      LToTarget := TargetOf(self.FTree, ATo);
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, LFromTarget) <> TypeClass.ObjectType then
        return AValue;
      end;
      return self.DoMoveUnlessNil(AValue, ADAM_LOWERING_REF_HEADER + self.DoReachOffset(LFromTarget, LToTarget), ANode);
    end;

    // True when the expression AId's own or ref value converts to an own I / ref I of an
    // interface its object implements (DoReachOwner moves it to the itable word, I3)
    hidden const method DoMovesOwner(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LFrom: int64;
    begin
      LFrom := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType;
      return (self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConvert <> 0) and self.DoIsInterfaceOwner(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConvert) and
        self.DoIsRefValue(LFrom) and not self.DoIsInterfaceOwner(LFrom);
    end;

    // DoManagedValue's value of AId before a conversion to an own I / ref I
    hidden method DoManagedOwn(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConst.Kind = ConstKind.String then
        if self.DoIsWideText(self.DoUsedType(AId)) then
          return self.DoWideLiteral(AId, self.DoWideUnits(AId));
        end;
        return self.DoStringLiteral(AId, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConst.Text);
      end;
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression then
        return self.DoManagedValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand));
      end;
      // an assignment's value: its target's block after the write (borrowed: the target
      // keeps its reference)
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.AssignExpression then
        return self.DoAssignedValue(AId, AssignedForm.Managed);
      end;
      // nil: no block (a ref's, an empty text's or array's)
      if (self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.NilLiteral) or (self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConst.Kind = ConstKind.Nil) then
        return self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, AId);
      end;
      if (self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.RefNew) or (self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.OwnNew) then
        return self.DoRefNew(AId);
      end;
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.AsyncExpression then
        return self.DoAsync(AId);
      end;
      // `ref S as T`: the ref's block, borrowed as the operand's is, checked (DoAsHolder)
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.AsExpression then
        return self.DoAsHolder(AId);
      end;
      // an await's managed result, borrowed: the task's object holds it
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.AwaitExpression then
        return self.DoAwaitManaged(AId);
      end;
      // a typed pack's next / get of a managed T: its item's block, borrowed (before the
      // call and place forms its member and call look like, as in DoOwnValue)
      if self.DoIsPackAccess(AId) then
        return self.DoPackManaged(AId);
      end;
      if self.DoIsConcat(AId) then
        return self.DoConcatValue(AId);
      end;
      if self.DoIsUtf8Call(AId) then
        return self.DoUtf8Value(AId);
      end;
      if self.DoIsIntrinsicCall(AId, "FormatStr") then
        return self.DoFormatStr(AId);
      end;
      if self.DoIsIntrinsicCall(AId, "lock") then
        return self.DoWeakLock(AId);
      end;
      if self.DoIsManagedCall(AId) or self.DoIsTextIntrinsicCall(AId) then
        return self.DoCall(AId);
      end;
      // a property read through its accessors: a call's result (kept in its hidden slot),
      // or a bound field's block borrowed
      if self.DoIsPropertyAccess(AId) then
        return self.DoPropertyGet(AId);
      end;
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.ConditionalExpression then
        return self.DoConditional(AId);
      end;
      // a dynamic array's array literal: its new block, kept in its hidden slot
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.ArrayLiteral then
        return self.DoDynamicLiteral(AId);
      end;
      if not self.DoIsPlace(AId) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoAddress(AId);
      if LAddress = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoLoad(LAddress, IrType.Pointer, AId);
    end;

    // True when AId is a concatenation SEM did not fold: `+` typed string (BNF sec 6)
    hidden const method DoIsConcat(const AId: int64): bool;
    begin
      return (self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.BinaryExpression) and
        (self.FTree[AId].Op = OperatorKind.Add) and self.DoIsText(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType) and
        (self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConst.Kind <> ConstKind.String) and (OperatorCallOf(self.FTree, AId) = 0);
    end;

    // True when ASide, one side of a concatenation, is a char or a wchar (its one-char text
    // is a temporary)
    hidden const method DoIsCharSide(const ASide: int64): bool;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(ASide));
      return (LClass = TypeClass.Char) or (LClass = TypeClass.WideChar);
    end;

    // True when AId is a call of the intrinsic named AName
    hidden const method DoIsIntrinsicCall(const AId: int64; const AName: string): bool;
    var
      LCallee: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind <> NodeKind.CallExpression then
        return false;
      end;
      LCallee := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Callee);
      if NameKindOf(self.FTree, LCallee) <> NodeKind.NameExpression then
        return false;
      end;
      LDecl := self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl;
      return (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) and
        (self.FTree[LDecl].Text = AName);
    end;

    // True when AId is a call of the intrinsic utf8 (its new string is a temporary,
    // DoUtf8Value; DoManagedValue reaches it through parentheses)
    hidden const method DoIsUtf8Call(const AId: int64): bool;
    begin
      return self.DoIsIntrinsicCall(AId, "utf8");
    end;

    // The call AId of utf8 (DoIsUtf8Call): its wstring argument's UTF-8 string
    // (WStrToUtf8), a new reference kept in the call's hidden slot (StrTake releases what an
    // earlier pass left there); that string, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoUtf8Value(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LWide: int64;
      LText: int64;
    begin
      LWide := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Argument));
      if LWide = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LText := self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.WStrToUtf8, LWide, 0, AId);
      if LText = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrTake, self.DoTempSlot(AId), LText, AId) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return LText;
    end;

    // The concatenation AId: each side's text (DoConcatSide), joined by StrConcat (a
    // wstring's by WStrConcat) into a new reference kept in AId's hidden slot (StrTake
    // releases what an earlier pass left there); that text, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoConcatValue(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LLeft: int64;
      LRight: int64;
      LJoined: int64;
    begin
      LLeft := self.DoConcatSide(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Left));
      if LLeft = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LRight := self.DoConcatSide(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Right));
      if LRight = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LJoined := self.DoCallRuntime(self.DoTextRoutine(RuntimeRoutine.StrConcat,
        self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType), LLeft, LRight, AId);
      if LJoined = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrTake, self.DoTempSlot(AId), LJoined, AId) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return LJoined;
    end;

    // The text of ASide, one side of a concatenation (or a `+=`'s source): a text's value,
    // or a char's one-char string (StrFromChar), a wchar's one-unit wstring (WStrFromChar),
    // kept in ASide's hidden slot; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoConcatSide(const ASide: int64): int64;
    var
      LChar: int64;
      LText: int64;
      LKind: RuntimeRoutine;
    begin
      if not self.DoIsCharSide(ASide) then
        return self.DoValue(ASide);
      end;
      LChar := self.DoValue(ASide);
      if LChar = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LKind := RuntimeRoutine.StrFromChar;
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(ASide)) = TypeClass.WideChar then
        LKind := RuntimeRoutine.WStrFromChar;
      end;
      LText := self.DoCallRuntime(LKind, LChar, 0, ASide);
      if LText = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrTake, self.DoTempSlot(ASide), LText, ASide) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return LText;
    end;

    // The hidden slot of the string temporary AId (DoTemporaries made it); raises when there
    // is none (a broken invariant: the scan and the lowering disagree)
    hidden const method DoTempSlot(const AId: int64): int64;
    begin
      if self.FTempOf[AId] = 0 then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_TEMP + IntToStr(AId));
      end;
      return self.FTempOf[AId];
    end;

    // A hidden string slot for the temporary AId, empty (made where the function's first
    // block is being written, before any of its code runs), one of FManaged
    hidden method DoTemporary(const AId: int64);
    var
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(AId, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
      self.DoStore(LSlot, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, AId), AId);
      self.FTempOf[AId] := LSlot;
      self.FTempTypeOf[AId] := 0;
      self.DoAddManaged(LSlot, 0, AId);
    end;

    // A hidden pointer slot for the temporary AId whose value is a dynamic array or a ref
    // of the canonical type AType, empty, one of FManaged by its type (released by its own
    // routine: DoReleaseAt)
    hidden method DoPointerTemporary(const AId: int64; const AType: int64);
    var
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(AId, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
      self.DoStore(LSlot, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, AId), AId);
      self.FTempOf[AId] := LSlot;
      self.FTempTypeOf[AId] := AType;
      self.DoAddManaged(LSlot, AType, AId);
    end;

    // The hidden slot of the call AId whose result is or holds managed values
    // (DoIsManagedCall): a text's as DoTemporary's; a dynamic array's the same, one of
    // FManaged by its type; an aggregate's of its type's size and alignment, zeroed, one of
    // FManaged by its type (the callee assigns its result into it, DoAggregateReturn, so a
    // second pass over the call releases the first one's values)
    hidden method DoResultTemporary(const AId: int64);
    var
      LType: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LSize: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType;
      if self.DoIsText(LType) then
        self.DoTemporary(AId);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsArrayValue(LType) or self.DoIsOwnerValue(LType) then
        self.DoPointerTemporary(AId, LType);
        return;
      end;
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType);
      LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(AId, LSize, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType));
      self.DoFill(LSlot, LSize, AId);
      self.FTempOf[AId] := LSlot;
      self.FTempTypeOf[AId] := LType;
      self.DoAddManaged(LSlot, LType, AId);
    end;

    // True when AId is a call of a routine, an external or a routine value whose result is
    // or holds managed values (a text, a dynamic array, or an aggregate holding one): its
    // result is a temporary in a hidden slot (DoResultTemporary, DoEmitCall). A cast, an
    // intrinsic (utf8 has its own temporary), a typed pack's read (a varargs local's
    // next / get: its item borrowed, DoPackManaged) and a call of no routine's type are not
    hidden const method DoIsManagedCall(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LCallee: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
      LType: int64;
    begin
      // a declared operator's result is a call's like any other
      if OperatorCallOf(self.FTree, AId) <> 0 then
        LType := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType;
        return self.DoIsManaged(LType) or
          (self.DoIsAggregate(LType) and (self.DoHoldsManaged(LType) or self.DoHasLifetime(LType)));
      end;
      if (self.FTree[AId].Kind <> NodeKind.CallExpression) or self.DoIsCastCall(AId) then
        return false;
      end;
      if self.DoIsPackAccess(AId) then
        return false;
      end;
      LCallee := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Callee);
      if NameKindOf(self.FTree, LCallee) = NodeKind.NameExpression then
        LDecl := self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl;
        if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      LType := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType;
      if self.DoIsManaged(LType) then
        return true;
      end;
      // a value object that ends by a done or copies by a copy decl is a temporary too
      // (ended at its full expression's end under its live flag: DoEndTemporary)
      return self.DoIsAggregate(LType) and (self.DoHoldsManaged(LType) or self.DoHasLifetime(LType));
    end;

    // A hidden slot for every temporary under ARoot: each concatenation's result, each char
    // side's text (a concatenation's, a `+=`'s), each utf8 / paramstr call's string, each
    // call's result that holds texts (DoResultTemporary), each dynamic array's array
    // literal's block (DoDynamicLiteral) and each print call's range scratch strings
    // (DoRangeTemporaries)
    hidden method DoTemporaries(const ARoot: int64);
    var
      LChild: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.ChildCount(ARoot) - 1 do
        LChild := self.FTree.ChildAt(ARoot, LI);
        if self.DoPassesTemporaries(ARoot, LChild) then
          skip;
        end;
        // a statement local's slot is made with them (DoStatementSlot)
        if self.DoIsStatementLocal(LChild) then
          self.DoStatementSlot(LChild);
        end;
        if self.DoIsUtf8Call(LChild) or self.DoIsTextIntrinsicCall(LChild) or
          self.DoIsIntrinsicCall(LChild, "FormatStr") then
          self.DoTemporary(LChild);
        end;
        if self.DoIsIntrinsicCall(LChild, "print") or self.DoIsIntrinsicCall(LChild, "println") then
          if self.DoPrintMayRaise(LChild) then
            self.DoTemporary(LChild);
          end;
          self.DoRangeTemporaries(LChild);
        end;
        if self.DoIsIntrinsicCall(LChild, "FormatStr") then
          self.DoRangeTemporaries(LChild);
        end;
        if self.DoIsManagedCall(LChild) or self.DoIsManagedPropertyCall(LChild) then
          self.DoResultTemporary(LChild);
        end;
        // lock(W)'s ref, a holder of its own (DoWeakLock)
        if self.DoIsIntrinsicCall(LChild, "lock") then
          self.DoPointerTemporary(LChild, self.FTree[LChild].ResolvedType);
        end;
        if ((self.FTree[LChild].Kind = NodeKind.RefNew) or (self.FTree[LChild].Kind = NodeKind.OwnNew) or
          (self.FTree[LChild].Kind = NodeKind.AsyncExpression)) and
          self.DoIsRefValue(self.FTree[LChild].ResolvedType) then
          self.DoPointerTemporary(LChild, self.FTree[LChild].ResolvedType);
        end;
        if (self.FTree[LChild].Kind = NodeKind.ArrayLiteral) and
          self.DoIsArrayValue(self.FTree[LChild].ResolvedType) then
          self.DoPointerTemporary(LChild, self.FTree[LChild].ResolvedType);
        end;
        if self.FTree[LChild].Kind = NodeKind.ForInStatement then
          self.DoForInTemporary(LChild);
        end;
        if self.DoIsCharCompound(LChild) then
          self.DoTemporary(self.FTree.FirstOf(LChild, NodeRole.Source));
        end;
        if self.DoIsPropertyTextCompound(LChild) then
          self.DoTemporary(LChild);
        end;
        if self.DoIsConcat(LChild) then
          self.DoTemporary(LChild);
          if self.DoIsCharSide(self.FTree.FirstOf(LChild, NodeRole.Left)) then
            self.DoTemporary(self.FTree.FirstOf(LChild, NodeRole.Left));
          end;
          if self.DoIsCharSide(self.FTree.FirstOf(LChild, NodeRole.Right)) then
            self.DoTemporary(self.FTree.FirstOf(LChild, NodeRole.Right));
          end;
        end;
        self.DoTemporaries(LChild);
        // after the arguments' own temporaries: an argument that is one needs no hold
        self.DoArgHolds(LChild);
      end;
    end;

    // The temporaries of the code under ARoot (DoTemporaries), its locals' and parameters'
    // pins settled first (DoPins: whether an argument needs a hold rests on every use in
    // the routine, a later one too), then ARoot's own holds (a module variable's
    // constructor arguments: DoArgHolds)
    hidden method DoCodeTemporaries(const ARoot: int64);
    begin
      self.DoPins(ARoot);
      self.DoTemporaries(ARoot);
      self.DoArgHolds(ARoot);
    end;

    // The holds the call or access ANode needs (SU2.8 e3; each a hidden slot, empty, one of
    // FManaged, marked FHeld, filled as the call is lowered, released as its full
    // expression ends: DoEndTemporary): a call's arguments (DoHoldArgs) and a method's
    // object (DoObjectAnchor); a property access running an accessor: its object, its
    // index and, as an assignment's target, its source; an object's init (a ref new, a
    // local's or a module variable's constructor arguments): its arguments. Nothing for a
    // call DoCallSig does not map
    hidden method DoArgHolds(const ANode: int64);
    var
      LSig: int64;
      LCallee: int64;
      LInit: int64;
      LParam: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      // an array comparison running its elements' declared operator: its operands live
      // through the operator's calls (DoArrayCompareHolds)
      if self.DoElementOperatorOf(ANode) <> 0 then
        self.DoArrayCompareHolds(ANode, self.DoElementOperatorOf(ANode));
        return;
      end;
      // a declared operator's operands are its arguments
      LSig := OperatorCallOf(self.FTree, ANode);
      if LSig <> 0 then
        for LI := 0 to OperandCount(self.FTree, ANode) - 1 do
          LParam := self.FTree.NthOf(LSig, NodeRole.Param, LI);
          self.DoHoldArg(OperandAt(self.FTree, ANode, LI), LParam,
            PassedByReference(self.FTree, LParam, self.DoLinkageOf(LSig)));
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[ANode].Kind = NodeKind.CallExpression then
        LSig := self.DoCallSig(ANode);
        if LSig = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        self.DoHoldArgs(ANode, NodeRole.Argument, LSig);
        LCallee := self.FTree.FirstOf(ANode, NodeRole.Callee);
        if (self.FTree[LCallee].Kind = NodeKind.MemberExpression) and
          (self.FTree[LSig].Kind = NodeKind.MethodDecl) then
          self.DoHoldAnchor(self.DoObjectAnchor(self.FTree.FirstOf(LCallee, NodeRole.Operand),
            self.FTree[LCallee].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Arrow)), LSig, 0, ANode);
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsPropertyAccess(ANode) then
        self.DoAccessorHolds(ANode);
        return;
      end;
      LInit := self.FTree[ANode].ResolvedCallee;
      if (LInit = 0) or (self.FTree[LInit].Kind <> NodeKind.InitDecl) then
        return;
      end;
      if (self.FTree[ANode].Kind = NodeKind.RefNew) or (self.FTree[ANode].Kind = NodeKind.OwnNew) then
        self.DoHoldArgs(ANode, NodeRole.Argument, LInit);
      end;
      if self.FTree[ANode].Kind = NodeKind.VarDecl then
        self.DoHoldArgs(ANode, NodeRole.ConstructorArgument, LInit);
      end;
    end;

    // The holds of AHolder's arguments (its children of ARole) for the parameters of ASig,
    // in order: an argument a borrowed parameter takes that the callee could drop
    // (DoNeedsHold: its value held, DoHeldValue), the anchor of one a
    // var or by-reference parameter takes (DoAnchoredAddress)
    hidden method DoHoldArgs(const AHolder: int64; const ARole: NodeRole; const ASig: int64);
    var
      LCount: int64;
      LArg: int64;
      LParam: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LCount := self.FTree.CountOf(AHolder, ARole);
      if LCount > self.FTree.CountOf(ASig, NodeRole.Param) then
        LCount := self.FTree.CountOf(ASig, NodeRole.Param);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LArg := self.FTree.NthOf(AHolder, ARole, LI);
        LParam := self.FTree.NthOf(ASig, NodeRole.Param, LI);
        self.DoHoldArg(LArg, LParam, PassedByReference(self.FTree, LParam, self.DoLinkageOf(ASig)));
      end;
    end;

    // The hold of the argument AArg for the parameter AParam (passed by reference when
    // AByRef): its value's for a borrowed one by value (DoNeedsHold), else a var or
    // by-reference place's anchor (DoAnchoredAddress, DoAnchoredReference)
    hidden method DoHoldArg(const AArg: int64; const AParam: int64; const AByRef: bool);
    var
      LRoot: int64;
      LType: int64;
    begin
      if self.DoNeedsHold(AArg, AParam) then
        LRoot := self.DoArgRoot(AArg);
        LType := self.DoDeclType(AParam);
        self.DoHoldSlot(LRoot, LType);
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[AParam].HasFlag(NodeFlag.VarParam) or AByRef then
        self.DoHoldAnchor(self.DoAnchorOf(AArg), self.FTree.ParentOf(AParam), 0,
          self.FTree.ParentOf(AArg));
      end;
    end;

    // The holds of the property access AId when an accessor's function runs for it (an
    // unbound or a dispatched read or write: DoAccessorCall): its object's anchor, its
    // index for the property's index parameter, and the source an assignment to it writes
    // for the write accessor's value parameter
    hidden method DoAccessorHolds(const AId: int64);
    var
      LProperty: int64;
      LRead: int64;
      LWrite: int64;
      LObject: int64;
      LArrow: bool;
      LParent: int64;
      LParam: int64;
      LByRef: bool;
      LFirst: int64;
      LSecond: int64;
    begin
      LProperty := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedDecl;
      LRead := self.FTree.FirstOf(LProperty, NodeRole.Read);
      LWrite := PropertyWriteOf(self.FTree, LProperty);
      if not (self.DoRunsAccessor(LProperty, LRead) or self.DoRunsAccessor(LProperty, LWrite)) then
        return;
      end;
      LObject := self.DoPropertyObject(AId, LArrow);
      // the accessors the access runs are its callees (a dispatched one's summary is its own
      // body's alone: 0, unknown)
      LFirst := 0;
      LSecond := 0;
      if not self.DoIsDispatched(LProperty) then
        if self.DoRunsAccessor(LProperty, LRead) then
          LFirst := LRead;
        end;
        if self.DoRunsAccessor(LProperty, LWrite) then
          if LFirst = 0 then
            LFirst := LWrite;
          else
            LSecond := LWrite;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      self.DoHoldAnchor(self.DoObjectAnchor(LObject, LArrow), LFirst, LSecond, AId);
      LParam := self.FTree.FirstOf(LProperty, NodeRole.Param);
      if (LParam <> 0) and (self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.IndexExpression) then
        LByRef := PassedByReference(self.FTree, LParam, Linkage.Cpp);
        self.DoHoldArg(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Index), LParam, LByRef);
      end;
      LParent := self.FTree.ParentOf(AId);
      if (self.FTree[LParent].Kind = NodeKind.AssignExpression) and (self.FTree.RoleOf(AId) = NodeRole.Target) and
        self.DoRunsAccessor(LProperty, LWrite) then
        LParam := self.DoParamAt(LWrite, self.DoParamCount(LWrite) - 1);
        LByRef := PassedByReference(self.FTree, LParam, Linkage.Cpp);
        self.DoHoldArg(self.FTree.FirstOf(LParent, NodeRole.Source), LParam, LByRef);
      end;
    end;

    // True when the accessor AAccessor (0: none) of the property AProperty runs as a
    // function (DoAccessorCall): it is unbound, or the property is dispatched
    hidden const method DoRunsAccessor(const AProperty: int64; const AAccessor: int64): bool;
    begin
      if AAccessor = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      return (not self.DoIsBound(AAccessor)) or self.DoIsDispatched(AProperty);
    end;

    // The hold of the anchor AAnchor (0: none) when a callee could drop its block
    // (DoAnchorHeld): a hidden slot of its own type (DoHoldSlot). None when the routine
    // ASig the site ASite runs, and ASecond (0: none; an access running both accessors),
    // provably cannot drop it (DoMayDrop, SU2.8 e4): marked FDroppedIn for DoAnchorBegin
    hidden method DoHoldAnchor(const AAnchor: int64; const ASig: int64; const ASecond: int64;
      const ASite: int64);
    begin
      if not self.DoAnchorHeld(AAnchor) then
        return;
      end;
      if not (self.DoMayDrop(ASig, ASite, AAnchor) or
        ((ASecond <> 0) and self.DoMayDrop(ASecond, ASite, AAnchor))) then
        self.FDroppedIn[AAnchor] := self.FFunction + 1;
        return;
      end;
      self.DoHoldSlot(AAnchor, self.DoUsedType(AAnchor));
    end;

    // A hold at the node ARoot for a value of the canonical type AType: a hidden slot,
    // empty, one of FManaged (a text's as DoTemporary's, a dynamic array's or a ref's by its
    // type), marked FHeld; one per node in a function (an indexed property's object is
    // both its member access's and its index access's: FHeldIn)
    hidden method DoHoldSlot(const ARoot: int64; const AType: int64);
    begin
      if self.FHeld[ARoot] and (self.FHeldIn[ARoot] = self.FFunction) and (self.FTempOf[ARoot] <> 0) then
        return;
      end;
      self.FHeldIn[ARoot] := self.FFunction;
      if self.DoIsText(AType) then
        self.DoTemporary(ARoot);
      else
        self.DoPointerTemporary(ARoot, AType);
      end;
      self.FHeld[ARoot] := true;
    end;

    // True when a parameter's caller passes it by reference: a var one, or one its routine's
    // linkage passes so (a const managed one under C++ linkage)
    hidden const method DoParamByRef(const AParam: int64): bool;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AParam].HasFlag(NodeFlag.VarParam) then
        return true;
      end;
      return PassedByReference(self.FTree, AParam, self.DoLinkageOf(self.FTree.ParentOf(AParam)));
    end;

    // The field a property's access reads (AWrite false) or writes through: its accessor
    // bound to a field (`read F` / `write F`), the property neither indexed nor
    // dispatched; 0 when an accessor's code runs instead (or there is none)
    hidden const method DoAccessorField(const AProperty: int64; const AWrite: bool): int64;
    var
      LAccessor: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree.CountOf(AProperty, NodeRole.Param) > 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.DoIsDispatched(AProperty) then
        return 0;
      end;
      if AWrite then
        LAccessor := PropertyWriteOf(self.FTree, AProperty);
      else
        LAccessor := self.FTree.FirstOf(AProperty, NodeRole.Read);
      end;
      if not self.DoIsBound(LAccessor) then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.FTree[LAccessor].ResolvedDecl;
    end;

    // ADecl added to the declarations of APath (DoPlacePath)
    hidden const method DoPathAdd(var APath: PlacePath; const ADecl: int64);
    begin
      if APath.Count >= len(APath.Decls) then
        setlength(APath.Decls, APath.Count * 2 + 8);
      end;
      APath.Decls[APath.Count] := ADecl;
      APath.Count := APath.Count + 1;
    end;

    // True when ADecl is one of APath's declarations
    hidden const method DoPathHas(const APath: PlacePath; const ADecl: int64): bool;
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to APath.Count - 1 do
        if APath.Decls[LI] = ADecl then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // The storage of the place APlace as SU2.8 e4 compares it, into APath (PlacePath): the
    // fields, embeds and module variables it lies in, from the place down through its
    // members and elements to the variable it starts at (its root). AWrite: the place is
    // written, so the walk stops at a member of an object reached through a ref (a write
    // there leaves the ref itself as it was); a read's walk goes on through the ref, since
    // a write of the ref may end the object. An element of a dynamic array or a text lies
    // in the array's block, which a write of the element may replace (copy on write), and
    // a static array's in the array itself: the walk goes on to the array's place.
    // Anything reached through a pointer, a weak ref or an accessor's code is Unknown. A
    // written place's whole value is written: every field and embed it holds by value is
    // added too (DoPathContained), so a write of the storage a field lies in (a receiver's,
    // a var parameter's place) names that field
    hidden const method DoPlacePath(const APlace: int64; const AWrite: bool; var APath: PlacePath);
    begin
      self.DoPlaceWalk(APlace, AWrite, APath);
      if AWrite and (APath.RootKind <> PathRoot.Unknown) then
        self.DoPathContained(self.DoUsedType(self.DoArgRoot(APlace)), APath, 0);
      end;
    end;

    // The fields and embeds a value of the canonical type AType holds by value, at any depth
    // (a static or dynamic array's elements, an aggregate's fields and embeds along its
    // parent chain; never through a ref, a pointer or a text), added to APath (each once);
    // past the depth limit the path is Unknown
    hidden const method DoPathContained(const AType: int64; var APath: PlacePath; const ADepth: int64);
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
      LAt: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LLevel: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if AType = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      if ADepth > ADAM_TYPES_MAX_DEPTH then
        APath.RootKind := PathRoot.Unknown;
        return;
      end;
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if (LClass = TypeClass.DynamicArray) or (LClass = TypeClass.StaticArray) then
        self.DoPathContained(TargetOf(self.FTree, AType), APath, ADepth + 1);
        return;
      end;
      if (LClass <> TypeClass.RecordType) and (LClass <> TypeClass.OverlayType) and
        (LClass <> TypeClass.ObjectType) then
        return;
      end;
      LAt := AType;
      LLevel := 0;
      while (LAt <> 0) and (LLevel <= ADAM_TYPES_MAX_DEPTH) do
        LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, LAt);
        for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
          LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
          LKind := self.FTree[LMember].Kind;
          if ((LKind = NodeKind.FieldDecl) or (LKind = NodeKind.EmbedDecl)) and not self.DoPathHas(APath, LMember) then
            self.DoPathAdd(APath, LMember);
            self.DoPathContained(self.DoPartType(LMember), APath, ADepth + 1);
          end;
        end;
        LAt := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, LAt);
        LLevel := LLevel + 1;
      end;
    end;

    // DoPlacePath's walk alone: the place's own path, its whole value's fields not added (a
    // receiver a callee writes through: the fields it writes are its summary's own)
    hidden const method DoPlaceWalk(const APlace: int64; const AWrite: bool; var APath: PlacePath);
    var
      LNode: int64;
      LOperand: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LClass: TypeClass;
      LDepth: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      APath.Count := 0;
      APath.RootKind := PathRoot.Unknown;
      APath.Root := 0;
      LNode := self.DoArgRoot(APlace);
      LDepth := 0;
      while LDepth <= ADAM_TYPES_MAX_DEPTH do
        LKind := self.FTree[LNode].Kind;
        if (LKind = NodeKind.MemberExpression) or (LKind = NodeKind.IndexExpression) then
          LOperand := self.DoArgRoot(self.FTree.FirstOf(LNode, NodeRole.Operand));
          LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(LOperand));
          if self.FTree[LNode].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Arrow) or (LClass = TypeClass.Pointer) or
            (LClass = TypeClass.UntypedPointer) or (LClass = TypeClass.WeakType) then
            return;
          end;
          if LKind = NodeKind.MemberExpression then
            LDecl := self.FTree[LNode].ResolvedDecl;
            if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.PropertyDecl) then
              LDecl := self.DoAccessorField(LDecl, AWrite);
            end;
            if LDecl = 0 then
              return;
            end;
            if (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind <> NodeKind.FieldDecl) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind <> NodeKind.EmbedDecl) then
              return;
            end;
            self.DoPathAdd(APath, LDecl);
            // A member reached through embeds lies in each of them (X.M of an embed E's M is
            // X.E.M), innermost first as the walk goes outward
            if self.FTree[LNode].ResolvedEmbed <> 0 then
              for LI := self.FTree.CountOf(LNode, NodeRole.EmbedStep) - 1 downto 0 do
                self.DoPathAdd(APath, self.FTree[self.FTree.NthOf(LNode, NodeRole.EmbedStep, LI)].ResolvedDecl);
              end;
              self.DoPathAdd(APath, self.FTree[LNode].ResolvedEmbed);
            end;
            if AWrite and ((LClass = TypeClass.RefType) or (LClass = TypeClass.TaskType) or
              (LClass = TypeClass.SequenceType) or (LClass = TypeClass.OwnType)) then
              APath.RootKind := PathRoot.None;
              return;
            end;
          else
            if self.DoIsPropertyAccess(LNode) then
              return;
            end;
          end;
          LNode := LOperand;
        else
          self.DoPathRoot(LNode, APath);
          return;
        end;
        LDepth := LDepth + 1;
      end;
    end;

    // The root of a place's path (DoPlacePath) at its innermost node ANode, into APath
    hidden const method DoPathRoot(const ANode: int64; var APath: PlacePath);
    var
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      LKind := self.FTree[ANode].Kind;
      if (LKind = NodeKind.SelfExpression) or (LKind = NodeKind.ParentExpression) then
        APath.RootKind := PathRoot.Receiver;
        return;
      end;
      if (LKind = NodeKind.CallExpression) or (LKind = NodeKind.RefNew) or (LKind = NodeKind.OwnNew) or
        (LKind = NodeKind.IntLiteral) or (LKind = NodeKind.FloatLiteral) or
        (LKind = NodeKind.StringLiteral) or (LKind = NodeKind.CharLiteral) or
        (LKind = NodeKind.BoolLiteral) or (LKind = NodeKind.NilLiteral) or
        (LKind = NodeKind.ArrayLiteral) or (LKind = NodeKind.RecordLiteral) or
        (LKind = NodeKind.SetLiteral) or (OperatorCallOf(self.FTree, ANode) <> 0) then
        APath.RootKind := PathRoot.None;
        return;
      end;
      if LKind <> NodeKind.NameExpression then
        return;
      end;
      LDecl := self.FTree[ANode].ResolvedDecl;
      if LDecl = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.Param then
        APath.Root := LDecl;
        if self.DoParamByRef(LDecl) then
          APath.RootKind := PathRoot.ByRef;
        else
          APath.RootKind := PathRoot.Own;
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.VarDecl then
        APath.Root := LDecl;
        if self.FTree.RoleOf(LDecl) = NodeRole.Local then
          APath.RootKind := PathRoot.Own;
        else
          self.DoPathAdd(APath, LDecl);
          APath.RootKind := PathRoot.Module;
        end;
        return;
      end;
      // a constant, a routine: no variable's storage
      APath.RootKind := PathRoot.None;
    end;

    // True when the write AWrite (DoPlacePath of a written place) may reach the storage of
    // the held place AHeld (DoMayDrop: its root known, or the caller's with a field on its
    // way): an unknown root, a place of the caller's (by reference, its object) naming no
    // field (whatever storage it aliases), a field or module variable both name, or the
    // same local. A written place of the caller's names every field its whole value holds
    // (DoPathContained), and a held one names its own: a field both name is how one meets
    // the other, whatever storage the caller's place aliases (the block it lies in is
    // kept by the caller's anchor hold, e3)
    hidden const method DoPathsMeet(const AWrite: PlacePath; const AHeld: PlacePath): bool;
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if AWrite.RootKind = PathRoot.Unknown then
        return true;
      end;
      if ((AWrite.RootKind = PathRoot.ByRef) or (AWrite.RootKind = PathRoot.Receiver)) and (AWrite.Count = 0) then
        return true;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to AWrite.Count - 1 do
        if self.DoPathHas(AHeld, AWrite.Decls[LI]) then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      return (AWrite.RootKind = PathRoot.Own) and (AHeld.RootKind = PathRoot.Own) and
        (AWrite.Root = AHeld.Root);
    end;

    // True when the way AObject (DoPlaceWalk, written) to the object a callee writes through
    // (SELF) may reach the held place AHeld: an unknown root, or a field or module variable
    // both name. Its root adds nothing more: the fields the callee writes through its
    // object are its summary's own (a whole receiver written names them all)
    hidden const method DoObjectMeets(const AObject: PlacePath; const AHeld: PlacePath): bool;
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if AObject.RootKind = PathRoot.Unknown then
        return true;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to AObject.Count - 1 do
        if self.DoPathHas(AHeld, AObject.Decls[LI]) then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // The index of the parameter AParam among ARoutine's own (-1: not one of them)
    hidden const method DoParamIndexOf(const ARoutine: int64; const AParam: int64): int64;
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param) - 1 do
        if self.FTree.NthOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param, LI) = AParam then
          return LI;
        end;
      end;
      return -1;
    end;

    // The argument the site ASite (a call, an object's ref new, a local's or a module
    // variable's constructor) passes for ASig's parameter AParam; 0 when there is none
    hidden const method DoSiteArg(const ASig: int64; const ASite: int64; const AParam: int64): int64;
    var
      LIndex: int64;
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LRole: NodeRole;
    begin
      LIndex := self.DoParamIndexOf(ASig, AParam);
      if LIndex < 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      // a declared operator's operands are its arguments, in its parameters' order
      if OperatorCallOf(self.FTree, ASite) <> 0 then
        return OperandAt(self.FTree, ASite, LIndex);
      end;
      LKind := self.FTree[ASite].Kind;
      LRole := NodeRole.Argument;
      if LKind = NodeKind.VarDecl then
        LRole := NodeRole.ConstructorArgument;
      else
        if (LKind <> NodeKind.CallExpression) and (LKind <> NodeKind.RefNew) and (LKind <> NodeKind.OwnNew) then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      if LIndex >= self.FTree.CountOf(ASite, LRole) then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.FTree.NthOf(ASite, LRole, LIndex);
    end;

    // The object the routine ASig runs on at the site ASite: the operand of a method call
    // or of a property access running an accessor; 0 for none (a routine's call, an object
    // being made: a ref new's, a constructor's); -2 the caller's own (a method named
    // without its object); -1 unknown (reached through a ptr, any other site)
    hidden const method DoSiteObject(const ASig: int64; const ASite: int64): int64;
    var
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LCallee: int64;
      LTarget: int64;
      LArrow: bool;
      LObject: int64;
    begin
      LKind := self.FTree[ASite].Kind;
      if LKind = NodeKind.CallExpression then
        if self.FTree[ASig].Kind <> NodeKind.MethodDecl then
          return 0;
        end;
        LCallee := self.FTree.FirstOf(ASite, NodeRole.Callee);
        if self.FTree[LCallee].Kind <> NodeKind.MemberExpression then
          return -2;
        end;
        if self.FTree[LCallee].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Arrow) then
          return -1;
        end;
        return self.FTree.FirstOf(LCallee, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      // an operator has no self
      if (LKind = NodeKind.RefNew) or (LKind = NodeKind.OwnNew) or (LKind = NodeKind.VarDecl) or
        (OperatorCallOf(self.FTree, ASite) <> 0) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LTarget := ASite;
      if LKind = NodeKind.AssignExpression then
        LTarget := self.FTree.FirstOf(ASite, NodeRole.Target);
      end;
      if not self.DoIsPropertyAccess(LTarget) then
        return -1;
      end;
      LObject := self.DoPropertyObject(LTarget, LArrow);
      if LArrow then
        return -1;
      end;
      if LObject = 0 then
        return -2;
      end;
      return LObject;
    end;

    // True when running ASig at the site ASite may drop the value of the place AHeld (SU2.8
    // e4): unknown without ASig's write summary (a routine value's, an external's, a
    // routine not summarized, SummarizeWrites); else when the
    // summary may reach AHeld's storage (DoPathsMeet): ALL, any write when AHeld's root is
    // the caller's or unknown, a field or module variable AHeld lies in, a var parameter's
    // argument at the site, a write through its object (SELF) when the object is no ref
    hidden const method DoMayDrop(const ASig: int64; const ASite: int64; const AHeld: int64): bool;
    var
      LEffects: int64;
      LFlags: uint64;
      LHeld: PlacePath;
      LWrite: PlacePath;
      LObject: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
      LArg: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if ASig = 0 then
        return true;
      end;
      // a dispatched method's summary is what any call of it may run (its own code and its
      // overrides', DoEffOverrides), ALL when a module out of sight may override it
      LEffects := self.FTree.FirstOf(ASig, NodeRole.Effects);
      if LEffects = 0 then
        return true;
      end;
      LFlags := self.FTree[LEffects].IntValue;
      if (LFlags & ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_ALL) <> uint64(0) then
        return true;
      end;
      if (self.FTree.ChildCount(LEffects) = 0) and ((LFlags & ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_SELF) = uint64(0)) then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoPlacePath(AHeld, false, LHeld);
      if LHeld.RootKind = PathRoot.Unknown then
        return true;
      end;
      // the caller's place itself (no field on its way): whatever storage it aliases
      if ((LHeld.RootKind = PathRoot.ByRef) or (LHeld.RootKind = PathRoot.Receiver)) and (LHeld.Count = 0) then
        return true;
      end;
      if (LFlags & ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_SELF) <> uint64(0) then
        LObject := self.DoSiteObject(ASig, ASite);
        if LObject < 0 then
          return true;
        end;
        // the fields it writes there are its summary's own; the object's own way to them
        // (an object reached through a ref: none) is the site's
        if (LObject <> 0) and not self.DoIsRefValue(self.DoUsedType(self.DoArgRoot(LObject))) then
          self.DoPlaceWalk(LObject, true, LWrite);
          if self.DoObjectMeets(LWrite, LHeld) then
            return true;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.ChildCount(LEffects) - 1 do
        LDecl := self.FTree[self.FTree.ChildAt(LEffects, LI)].ResolvedDecl;
        if LDecl = 0 then
          return true;
        end;
        if self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.Param then
          LArg := self.DoSiteArg(ASig, ASite, LDecl);
          if LArg = 0 then
            return true;
          end;
          self.DoPlacePath(LArg, true, LWrite);
          if self.DoPathsMeet(LWrite, LHeld) then
            return true;
          end;
        else
          if self.DoPathHas(LHeld, LDecl) then
            return true;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // SU2.8 e4 (the routine SummarizeWrites): every routine with a body in a module the
    // tree did not read from a compiled unit given its write summary, a WriteEffects child
    // (role Effects): IntValue its EFFECT bits, and unless ALL one EffectWrite child per
    // field, embed and module variable it may write (in source order: DoEffBefore) and per
    // var or by-reference parameter of its own it may write. Its own writes (an assignment's
    // target, `addr of`, ++ / --, a for's variable, setlength's array, DoEffWrite), then
    // what the routines it runs write (its calls, its accessors, the inits, dones and
    // copies its values' types run: DoEffEdge), to a fixed point (DoEffSolve). A routine
    // summarized already (a compiled unit's) is read as it is (DoEffDecode)
    method SummarizeWrites();
    var
      LI: int64;
      LModule: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      self.FEffSlotOf := ref Int64Map(-1);
      self.FReleaseSeen := ref Int64Map(-1);
      self.FEffRoutines := ref Int64List();
      self.FEffDeclIndex := ref Int64Map(-1);
      self.FEffDecls := ref Int64List();
      self.FEffLocalSlot := ref Int64List();
      self.FEffLocalDecl := ref Int64List();
      self.FEdgeFrom := ref Int64List();
      self.FEdgeCallee := ref Int64List();
      self.FEdgeSite := ref Int64List();
      self.FReleaseMemo := ref Int64Map(-1);
      self.FKidHead := ref Int64Map(-1);
      self.FKidType := ref Int64List();
      self.FKidNext := ref Int64List();
      self.FExposed := ref Int64Map(-1);
      self.FEffWords := 0;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.ChildCount(ADAM_AST_PROGRAM) - 1 do
        LModule := self.FTree.ChildAt(ADAM_AST_PROGRAM, LI);
        if (self.FTree.RoleOf(LModule) = NodeRole.Module) and not self.FTree[LModule].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Compiled) then
          self.DoEffSlots(LModule);
        end;
      end;
      // the slots made so far are this pass's; DoEffDecode adds the read ones after them
      LCount := self.FEffRoutines.Count;
      for LSlot := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        self.DoEffCollect(LSlot);
        self.DoEffOverrides(LSlot);
      end;
      self.DoEffSolve();
      for LSlot := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        self.DoEffWriteOut(LSlot);
      end;
    end;

    // True for the kinds that are routines with a summary of their own: a routine, a
    // method, an init, a done, a copy, an operator, a property's accessor
    hidden const method DoIsSummaryRoutine(const AKind: NodeKind): bool;
    begin
      return (AKind = NodeKind.RoutineDecl) or (AKind = NodeKind.MethodDecl) or
        (AKind = NodeKind.InitDecl) or (AKind = NodeKind.DoneDecl) or
        (AKind = NodeKind.CopyDecl) or (AKind = NodeKind.OperatorDecl) or
        (AKind = NodeKind.PropertyRead) or (AKind = NodeKind.PropertyWrite);
    end;

    // A new summary slot for the routine ARoutine, writing nothing yet
    hidden method DoEffNewSlot(const ARoutine: int64): int64;
    var
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      LSlot := self.FEffRoutines.Count;
      self.FEffRoutines.Add(ARoutine);
      if LSlot >= len(self.FEffFlags) then
        setlength(self.FEffFlags, LSlot * 2 + 64);
        setlength(self.FEffParams, LSlot * 2 + 64);
        setlength(self.FEffFixed, LSlot * 2 + 64);
      end;
      self.FEffFlags[LSlot] := uint64(0);
      self.FEffParams[LSlot] := uint64(0);
      self.FEffFixed[LSlot] := false;
      self.FEffSlotOf.Put(ARoutine, LSlot);
      return LSlot;
    end;

    // A slot for every routine with a body under ANode that has no summary yet, and for
    // every abstract method (its summary is its overrides', DoEffOverrides); a body is
    // entered only for its local types (DoEffBodyTypes: a nested routine is among its
    // routine's locals) and a generic declaration's
    // template is skipped (its instances are routines of their own). Every object type met
    // is noted under its parent (DoEffFamily), a generic one too
    hidden method DoEffSlots(const ANode: int64);
    var
      LChild: int64;
      LRole: NodeRole;
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LKind := self.FTree[ANode].Kind;
      if LKind = NodeKind.TypeDecl then
        self.DoEffFamily(ANode);
      end;
      if self.FTree.FirstOf(ANode, NodeRole.GenericParam) <> 0 then
        self.DoEffFamilies(ANode);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsSummaryRoutine(LKind) and (self.FTree.FirstOf(ANode, NodeRole.Effects) = 0) and
        ((self.FTree.FirstOf(ANode, NodeRole.Body) <> 0) or
        ((LKind = NodeKind.MethodDecl) and self.FTree[ANode].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Abstract))) then
        self.DoEffNewSlot(ANode);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.ChildCount(ANode) - 1 do
        LChild := self.FTree.ChildAt(ANode, LI);
        LRole := self.FTree.RoleOf(LChild);
        if LRole = NodeRole.Body then
          self.DoEffBodyTypes(LChild);
        else
          if LRole <> NodeRole.Effects then
            self.DoEffSlots(LChild);
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The local types among the statements under ANode (a body: BNF sec 5 type blocks) given
    // their slots and family as DoEffSlots gives a module's (their members' bodies entered
    // there in turn); the statements themselves are their routine's summary (DoEffWalk)
    hidden method DoEffBodyTypes(const ANode: int64);
    var
      LChild: int64;
      LRole: NodeRole;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.ChildCount(ANode) - 1 do
        LChild := self.FTree.ChildAt(ANode, LI);
        LRole := self.FTree.RoleOf(LChild);
        if LRole <> NodeRole.Effects then
          if (self.FTree[LChild].Kind = NodeKind.TypeDecl) and (LRole <> NodeRole.TypeOf) then
            self.DoEffSlots(LChild);
          else
            if not self.DoIsSummaryRoutine(self.FTree[LChild].Kind) then
              self.DoEffBodyTypes(LChild);
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // Every type declaration under ANode (a generic template's: no slots there) noted by
    // DoEffFamily
    hidden method DoEffFamilies(const ANode: int64);
    var
      LChild: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.ChildCount(ANode) - 1 do
        LChild := self.FTree.ChildAt(ANode, LI);
        if self.FTree.RoleOf(LChild) <> NodeRole.Effects then
          if self.FTree[LChild].Kind = NodeKind.TypeDecl then
            self.DoEffFamily(LChild);
          end;
          self.DoEffFamilies(LChild);
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The type declaration ADecl in the family: an object type with a parent noted as its
    // parent's direct descendant (FKidHead), a public alias of an object type marking that
    // type exposed (FExposed: a module that imports the alias may extend it)
    hidden method DoEffFamily(const ADecl: int64);
    var
      LBody: int64;
      LParent: int64;
      LNamed: int64;
    begin
      LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, ADecl);
      if LBody = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[LBody].Kind = NodeKind.ObjectType then
        LParent := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, ADecl);
        if LParent <> 0 then
          self.FKidNext.Add(self.FKidHead.Find(LParent));
          self.FKidHead.Put(LParent, self.FKidType.Count);
          self.FKidType.Add(ADecl);
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[ADecl].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Public) then
        LNamed := CanonicalOf(self.FTree, LBody);
        if (LNamed <> 0) and (LNamed <> ADecl) and (ClassOf(self.FTree, LNamed) = TypeClass.ObjectType) then
          self.FExposed.Put(LNamed, 1);
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // True when every type that extends the object type AType, at any depth, is one this
    // pass has noted (DoEffFamily), so a call or a release of it runs only code in sight: a
    // final type (none extends it); else a type of a module this pass summarizes that no
    // other module may name (an exe's or a dll's; a unit's not public, no public alias: BNF
    // sec 3, a declaration not public is private to its module), each descendant the same
    hidden const method DoEffClosed(const AType: int64): bool;
    var
      LModule: int64;
      LEntry: int64;
    begin
      if IsFinalType(self.FTree, AType) then
        return true;
      end;
      LModule := ModuleOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if (LModule = 0) or self.FTree[LModule].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Compiled) then
        return false;
      end;
      // only a unit is imported (BNF sec 1): an exe's or a dll's public names reach no module
      if (self.FTree[LModule].Module = ModuleKind.Unit) and
        (self.FTree[AType].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Public) or (self.FExposed.Find(AType) >= 0)) then
        return false;
      end;
      LEntry := self.FKidHead.Find(AType);
      while LEntry >= 0 do
        if not self.DoEffClosed(self.FKidType[LEntry]) then
          return false;
        end;
        LEntry := self.FKidNext[LEntry];
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // SU2.8 e5: the slot ASlot of a dispatched method holds what any call of it may run:
    // its own code (DoEffCollect) and every override below its type, each an edge with
    // site -1 (DoEffMapSite); a final one is overridden nowhere; ALL when a module out of
    // sight may override it (DoEffClosed)
    hidden method DoEffOverrides(const ASlot: int64);
    var
      LMethod: int64;
      LType: int64;
    begin
      LMethod := self.FEffRoutines[ASlot];
      if (self.FTree[LMethod].Kind <> NodeKind.MethodDecl) or not self.DoIsDispatched(LMethod) then
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[LMethod].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Final) then
        return;
      end;
      LType := self.FTree.ParentOf(self.FTree.ParentOf(LMethod));
      if (LType = 0) or (self.FTree[LType].Kind <> NodeKind.TypeDecl) or not self.DoEffClosed(LType) then
        self.DoEffAll(ASlot);
        return;
      end;
      self.DoEffOverridesIn(ASlot, LMethod, LType);
    end;

    // The edges of ASlot (DoEffOverrides) to the overrides of AMethod in the descendants of
    // AType: each method of the same name that overrides (an overload of that name too:
    // more than runs, never less)
    hidden method DoEffOverridesIn(const ASlot: int64; const AMethod: int64; const AType: int64);
    var
      LEntry: int64;
      LKid: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LEntry := self.FKidHead.Find(AType);
      while LEntry >= 0 do
        LKid := self.FKidType[LEntry];
        LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, LKid);
        for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
          LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
          if (self.FTree[LMember].Kind = NodeKind.MethodDecl) and self.FTree[LMember].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Override) and
            (self.FTree[LMember].Text = self.FTree[AMethod].Text) then
            self.DoEffEdge(ASlot, LMember, -1);
          end;
        end;
        self.DoEffOverridesIn(ASlot, AMethod, LKid);
        LEntry := self.FKidNext[LEntry];
      end;
    end;

    // The bit of the field, embed or module variable ADecl over FEffDecls (made the first
    // time it is asked for)
    hidden method DoEffDeclBit(const ADecl: int64): int64;
    var
      LIndex: int64;
    begin
      LIndex := self.FEffDeclIndex.Find(ADecl);
      if LIndex >= 0 then
        return LIndex;
      end;
      LIndex := self.FEffDecls.Count;
      self.FEffDecls.Add(ADecl);
      self.FEffDeclIndex.Put(ADecl, LIndex);
      return LIndex;
    end;

    // ASlot may write anything
    hidden method DoEffAll(const ASlot: int64);
    begin
      self.FEffFlags[ASlot] := self.FEffFlags[ASlot] | ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_ALL;
    end;

    // ASlot writes its routine's parameter AParam (a var or by-reference one): ALL when it
    // is not one of the routine's own (an outer routine's) or past the bits tracked
    hidden method DoEffParam(const ASlot: int64; const AParam: int64);
    var
      LIndex: int64;
    begin
      LIndex := self.DoParamIndexOf(self.FEffRoutines[ASlot], AParam);
      if (LIndex < 0) or (LIndex >= ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_PARAMS) then
        self.DoEffAll(ASlot);
        return;
      end;
      self.FEffParams[ASlot] := self.FEffParams[ASlot] | (uint64(1) shl uint64(LIndex));
    end;

    // The routine (or a property, for its accessors' index) whose own variable ADecl (a
    // local or a parameter) is; 0 for none
    hidden const method DoOwnerRoutine(const ADecl: int64): int64;
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LAt := self.FTree.ParentOf(ADecl);
      while LAt <> 0 do
        if self.DoIsSummaryRoutine(self.FTree[LAt].Kind) or (self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.PropertyDecl) then
          return LAt;
        end;
        LAt := self.FTree.ParentOf(LAt);
      end;
      return 0;
    end;

    // The bit AIndex (DoEffDeclBit) set in ASlot's words; true when it was clear
    hidden method DoEffSetBit(const ASlot: int64; const AIndex: int64): bool;
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LBit: uint64;
    begin
      LAt := ASlot * self.FEffWords + int64(uint64(AIndex) shr uint64(6));
      LBit := uint64(1) shl (uint64(AIndex) & uint64(63));
      if (self.FEffBits[LAt] & LBit) <> uint64(0) then
        return false;
      end;
      self.FEffBits[LAt] := self.FEffBits[LAt] | LBit;
      return true;
    end;

    // ASlot writes the place APath describes (DoPlacePath of a written place): its fields'
    // and module variables' bits (ASolved: set in FEffBits, the words known; else kept as
    // pairs, FEffLocalSlot / FEffLocalDecl), its routine's var or by-reference parameter,
    // its own object (SELF), anything (ALL: an unknown root, another routine's local). True
    // when ASlot's summary grew
    hidden method DoEffPath(const ASlot: int64; const APath: PlacePath; const ASolved: bool): bool;
    var
      LFlags: uint64;
      LParams: uint64;
      LOwner: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LGrew: bool;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LFlags := self.FEffFlags[ASlot];
      LParams := self.FEffParams[ASlot];
      LGrew := false;
      if APath.RootKind = PathRoot.Unknown then
        self.DoEffAll(ASlot);
      end;
      if APath.RootKind = PathRoot.Receiver then
        self.FEffFlags[ASlot] := self.FEffFlags[ASlot] | ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_SELF;
      end;
      if APath.RootKind = PathRoot.ByRef then
        self.DoEffParam(ASlot, APath.Root);
      end;
      if APath.RootKind = PathRoot.Own then
        LOwner := self.DoOwnerRoutine(APath.Root);
        if (LOwner <> self.FEffRoutines[ASlot]) and (LOwner <> self.FTree.ParentOf(self.FEffRoutines[ASlot])) then
          self.DoEffAll(ASlot);
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to APath.Count - 1 do
        if ASolved then
          LIndex := self.FEffDeclIndex.Find(APath.Decls[LI]);
          if LIndex < 0 then
            self.DoEffAll(ASlot);
          else
            if self.DoEffSetBit(ASlot, LIndex) then
              LGrew := true;
            end;
          end;
        else
          self.FEffLocalSlot.Add(ASlot);
          self.FEffLocalDecl.Add(self.DoEffDeclBit(APath.Decls[LI]));
        end;
      end;
      return LGrew or (self.FEffFlags[ASlot] <> LFlags) or (self.FEffParams[ASlot] <> LParams);
    end;

    // The fields and module variables of the written place APath known to the words before
    // they are counted (a var argument's, a method's object: DoEffEdge), so DoEffSolve can
    // set their bits
    hidden method DoEffRegister(const APath: PlacePath);
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to APath.Count - 1 do
        self.DoEffDeclBit(APath.Decls[LI]);
      end;
    end;

    // What the routine of ASlot does that its summary holds: its parameters by value it
    // owns, ended as it returns (DoEffRelease), then its body and its locals (DoEffWalk)
    hidden method DoEffCollect(const ASlot: int64);
    var
      LRoutine: int64;
      LChild: int64;
      LRole: NodeRole;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LRoutine := self.FEffRoutines[ASlot];
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.ChildCount(LRoutine) - 1 do
        LChild := self.FTree.ChildAt(LRoutine, LI);
        LRole := self.FTree.RoleOf(LChild);
        if LRole = NodeRole.Param then
          if (not self.FTree[LChild].HasFlag(NodeFlag.ConstParam)) and (not self.DoParamByRef(LChild)) then
            self.DoEffRelease(ASlot, self.DoDeclType(LChild));
          end;
        else
          if (LRole = NodeRole.Body) or (LRole = NodeRole.Local) then
            self.DoEffWalk(ASlot, LChild);
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The writes, calls and releases of the code at AId and under it for ASlot (a nested
    // routine is summarized alone)
    hidden method DoEffWalk(const ASlot: int64; const AId: int64);
    var
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LOp: OperatorKind;
      LIterator: int64;
      LInit: int64;
      LChild: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LKind := self.FTree[AId].Kind;
      // a member is summarized alone; a local type's declaration runs nothing
      if self.DoIsSummaryRoutine(LKind) or (LKind = NodeKind.TypeDecl) then
        return;
      end;
      LOp := self.FTree[AId].Op;
      if LKind = NodeKind.AssignExpression then
        self.DoEffWrite(ASlot, self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target));
      end;
      if ((LKind = NodeKind.UnaryExpression) or (LKind = NodeKind.PostfixExpression)) and
        ((LOp = OperatorKind.AddressOf) or (LOp = OperatorKind.Increment) or (LOp = OperatorKind.Decrement)) then
        self.DoEffWrite(ASlot, self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand));
      end;
      if (LKind = NodeKind.ForStatement) or (LKind = NodeKind.ForInStatement) then
        LIterator := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Iterator);
        if (LIterator <> 0) and (self.FTree[LIterator].Kind <> NodeKind.VarDecl) then
          self.DoEffWrite(ASlot, LIterator);
        end;
      end;
      if (LKind = NodeKind.VarDecl) or (LKind = NodeKind.RefNew) or (LKind = NodeKind.OwnNew) then
        if LKind = NodeKind.VarDecl then
          self.DoEffRelease(ASlot, self.DoDeclType(AId));
        else
          self.DoEffRelease(ASlot, self.DoUsedType(AId));
        end;
        LInit := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedCallee;
        if (LInit <> 0) and (self.FTree[LInit].Kind = NodeKind.InitDecl) then
          self.DoEffEdge(ASlot, LInit, AId);
        end;
      end;
      if self.DoIsCallSite(AId) then
        self.DoEffCall(ASlot, AId);
        self.DoEffRelease(ASlot, self.DoUsedType(AId));
      end;
      // an array comparison runs its elements' declared operator (no argument of the site
      // is one of its parameters: the elements are passed)
      if self.DoElementOperatorOf(AId) <> 0 then
        self.DoEffEdge(ASlot, self.DoElementOperatorOf(AId), 0);
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.AsyncExpression then
        // its task runs beside the code that goes on
        self.DoEffAll(ASlot);
      end;
      if ((LKind = NodeKind.MemberExpression) or (LKind = NodeKind.IndexExpression)) and
        self.DoIsPropertyAccess(AId) then
        self.DoEffAccess(ASlot, AId);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.ChildCount(AId) - 1 do
        LChild := self.FTree.ChildAt(AId, LI);
        if self.FTree.RoleOf(LChild) <> NodeRole.Effects then
          self.DoEffWalk(ASlot, LChild);
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // ASlot writes the place APlace: its storage (DoPlacePath, DoEffPath) and the end of
    // the value it held (DoEffRelease). A property's place written by its accessor's code
    // is that accessor's summary (DoEffAccess); a non-managed value written through a
    // pointer ends nothing (raw storage)
    hidden method DoEffWrite(const ASlot: int64; const APlace: int64);
    var
      LPlace: int64;
      LPath: PlacePath;
    begin
      LPlace := self.DoArgRoot(APlace);
      if self.DoIsPropertyAccess(LPlace) then
        if (self.FTree[LPlace].Kind = NodeKind.IndexExpression) or
          (self.DoAccessorField(self.FTree[LPlace].ResolvedDecl, true) = 0) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      self.DoPlacePath(LPlace, true, LPath);
      if (LPath.RootKind = PathRoot.Unknown) and not self.DoHoldsManaged(self.DoUsedType(LPlace)) then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoEffPath(ASlot, LPath, false);
      self.DoEffRelease(ASlot, self.DoUsedType(LPlace));
    end;

    // The call ACall of ASlot's routine: an edge to the routine it runs (DoCallSig); setlength
    // writes its array, create / destroy run an object's init / done (anything), every other
    // intrinsic, a cast and a typed pack's read write nothing; a routine value or any call
    // DoCallSig does not map may write anything
    hidden method DoEffCall(const ASlot: int64; const ACall: int64);
    var
      LSig: int64;
      LCallee: int64;
      LName: string;
    begin
      LSig := self.DoCallSig(ACall);
      if LSig = 0 then
        if self.DoIsCastCall(ACall) or self.DoIsPackAccess(ACall) then
          return;
        end;
        if self.DoIsIntrinsicCallee(ACall) then
          LCallee := self.FTree.FirstOf(ACall, NodeRole.Callee);
          LName := self.FTree[self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl].Text;
          if LName = "setlength" then
            self.DoEffWrite(ASlot, self.FTree.FirstOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument));
          end;
          if (LName = "create") or (LName = "destroy") then
            self.DoEffAll(ASlot);
          end;
          return;
        end;
        self.DoEffAll(ASlot);
        return;
      end;
      // a dispatched method's summary holds its overrides' (DoEffOverrides)
      self.DoEffEdge(ASlot, LSig, ACall);
    end;

    // The property access AId of ASlot's routine: an edge to each accessor whose code runs
    // for it (DoRunsAccessor); a dispatched property may run any override's (anything)
    hidden method DoEffAccess(const ASlot: int64; const AId: int64);
    var
      LProperty: int64;
      LRead: int64;
      LWrite: int64;
    begin
      LProperty := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedDecl;
      if self.DoIsDispatched(LProperty) then
        self.DoEffAll(ASlot);
        return;
      end;
      LRead := self.FTree.FirstOf(LProperty, NodeRole.Read);
      LWrite := PropertyWriteOf(self.FTree, LProperty);
      if self.DoRunsAccessor(LProperty, LRead) then
        self.DoEffEdge(ASlot, LRead, AId);
      end;
      if self.DoRunsAccessor(LProperty, LWrite) then
        self.DoEffEdge(ASlot, LWrite, AId);
      end;
    end;

    // An edge from ASlot to the routine ACallee its node ASite runs (0: a release's); the
    // places the site gives it to write known to the words (DoEffRegister: a var or
    // by-reference argument, the object of a method or an accessor), a summary read from a
    // compiled unit given its slot (DoEffDecode). ASite -1: an override's edge from the
    // method it overrides (DoEffOverrides), the same parameters and object, no site. A
    // routine that never returns adds nothing:
    // once it runs, no code below the frame that will catch or end is resumed, so no borrow
    // it could break is read again (the code that does run, a handler's or a cleanup's, is
    // in its own routine's summary)
    hidden method DoEffEdge(const ASlot: int64; const ACallee: int64; const ASite: int64);
    var
      LEffects: int64;
      LRole: NodeRole;
      LCount: int64;
      LObject: int64;
      LPath: PlacePath;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[ACallee].HasFlag(NodeFlag.NoReturn) then
        return;
      end;
      self.FEdgeFrom.Add(ASlot);
      self.FEdgeCallee.Add(ACallee);
      self.FEdgeSite.Add(ASite);
      if self.FEffSlotOf.Find(ACallee) < 0 then
        LEffects := self.FTree.FirstOf(ACallee, NodeRole.Effects);
        if LEffects <> 0 then
          self.DoEffDecode(ACallee, LEffects);
        end;
      end;
      if ASite <= 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LRole := NodeRole.Argument;
      if self.FTree[ASite].Kind = NodeKind.VarDecl then
        LRole := NodeRole.ConstructorArgument;
      end;
      LCount := self.FTree.CountOf(ASite, LRole);
      if LCount > self.FTree.CountOf(ACallee, NodeRole.Param) then
        LCount := self.FTree.CountOf(ACallee, NodeRole.Param);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        if self.DoParamByRef(self.FTree.NthOf(ACallee, NodeRole.Param, LI)) then
          self.DoPlacePath(self.FTree.NthOf(ASite, LRole, LI), true, LPath);
          self.DoEffRegister(LPath);
        end;
      end;
      LObject := self.DoSiteObject(ACallee, ASite);
      if LObject > 0 then
        self.DoPlaceWalk(LObject, true, LPath);
        self.DoEffRegister(LPath);
      end;
    end;

    // A slot for the routine ACallee read from its summary AEffects (a compiled unit's):
    // fixed, never written again
    hidden method DoEffDecode(const ACallee: int64; const AEffects: int64);
    var
      LSlot: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LSlot := self.DoEffNewSlot(ACallee);
      self.FEffFixed[LSlot] := true;
      self.FEffFlags[LSlot] := self.FTree[AEffects].IntValue;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.ChildCount(AEffects) - 1 do
        LDecl := self.FTree[self.FTree.ChildAt(AEffects, LI)].ResolvedDecl;
        if LDecl = 0 then
          self.DoEffAll(LSlot);
        else
          if self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.Param then
            self.DoEffParam(LSlot, LDecl);
          else
            self.FEffLocalSlot.Add(LSlot);
            self.FEffLocalDecl.Add(self.DoEffDeclBit(LDecl));
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // ASlot ends (or copies) a value of the canonical type AType: the routines that runs
    // (DoReleaseRuns) are its edges; anything when that may be any code
    hidden method DoEffRelease(const ASlot: int64; const AType: int64);
    var
      LCode: int64;
    begin
      LCode := self.DoReleaseRuns(AType, -1);
      if LCode = 2 then
        self.DoEffAll(ASlot);
      end;
      if LCode = 1 then
        self.DoReleaseRuns(AType, ASlot);
      end;
    end;

    // What ending, copying or building a value of the canonical type AType runs: 0 nothing,
    // 1 the inits, dones and copies of types that do not dispatch (each an edge of ASlot
    // when ASlot >= 0), 2 anything (a polymorphic object's, which a descendant in another
    // unit may override; an interface's or a task's). Known answers kept (FReleaseMemo)
    hidden method DoReleaseRuns(const AType: int64; const ASlot: int64): int64;
    var
      LCode: int64;
    begin
      if AType = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if ASlot < 0 then
        LCode := self.FReleaseMemo.Find(AType);
        if LCode >= 0 then
          return LCode;
        end;
      end;
      self.FReleaseSeen := ref Int64Map(-1);
      LCode := self.DoReleaseWalk(AType, ASlot);
      if ASlot < 0 then
        self.FReleaseMemo.Put(AType, LCode);
      end;
      return LCode;
    end;

    // DoReleaseRuns' walk over AType and the types its value holds: an array's element, a
    // ref's or an own's object, an aggregate's fields and embeds along its parent chain
    // (each type once a walk: FReleaseSeen); a polymorphic object's descendants' too when
    // all are in sight (DoEffClosed), else anything
    hidden method DoReleaseWalk(const AType: int64; const ASlot: int64): int64;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      if (AType = 0) or (self.FReleaseSeen.Find(AType) >= 0) then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.FReleaseSeen.Put(AType, 1);
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      // a sequence's last release may abort its generator: its finally / defer run any code
      if (LClass = TypeClass.InterfaceType) or (LClass = TypeClass.TaskType) or
        (LClass = TypeClass.SequenceType) then
        return 2;
      end;
      if (LClass = TypeClass.DynamicArray) or (LClass = TypeClass.StaticArray) or
        (LClass = TypeClass.RefType) or (LClass = TypeClass.OwnType) then
        return self.DoReleaseWalk(TargetOf(self.FTree, AType), ASlot);
      end;
      if (LClass <> TypeClass.RecordType) and (LClass <> TypeClass.OverlayType) and
        (LClass <> TypeClass.ObjectType) then
        return 0;
      end;
      if (LClass = TypeClass.ObjectType) and IsPolymorphic(self.FTree, AType) then
        // the value may be any descendant's (SU2.8 e5): known only when all are in sight
        if not self.DoEffClosed(AType) then
          return 2;
        end;
        return self.DoReleaseKids(AType, ASlot, self.DoReleaseLevels(AType, ASlot));
      end;
      return self.DoReleaseLevels(AType, ASlot);
    end;

    // DoReleaseWalk's code (and ASlot's edges) for AType's own level and its parents': the
    // inits, dones and copies each declares, the types its fields and embeds hold
    hidden method DoReleaseLevels(const AType: int64; const ASlot: int64): int64;
    var
      LCode: int64;
      LPart: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LDepth: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LCode := 0;
      LAt := AType;
      LDepth := 0;
      while (LAt <> 0) and (LDepth <= ADAM_TYPES_MAX_DEPTH) do
        LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, LAt);
        for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
          LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
          LKind := self.FTree[LMember].Kind;
          if (LKind = NodeKind.InitDecl) or (LKind = NodeKind.DoneDecl) or (LKind = NodeKind.CopyDecl) then
            LCode := 1;
            if ASlot >= 0 then
              self.DoEffEdge(ASlot, LMember, 0);
            end;
          end;
          if (LKind = NodeKind.FieldDecl) or (LKind = NodeKind.EmbedDecl) then
            LPart := self.DoReleaseWalk(self.DoPartType(LMember), ASlot);
            if LPart = 2 then
              return 2;
            end;
            if LPart > LCode then
              LCode := LPart;
            end;
          end;
        end;
        LAt := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, LAt);
        LDepth := LDepth + 1;
      end;
      return LCode;
    end;

    // ACode (DoReleaseWalk's so far) raised by the levels of every descendant of AType at
    // any depth (DoReleaseLevels: its own and its parents'), 2 as soon as one is anything
    hidden method DoReleaseKids(const AType: int64; const ASlot: int64; const ACode: int64): int64;
    var
      LCode: int64;
      LPart: int64;
      LEntry: int64;
    begin
      LCode := ACode;
      LEntry := self.FKidHead.Find(AType);
      while (LEntry >= 0) and (LCode < 2) do
        LPart := self.DoReleaseKids(self.FKidType[LEntry], ASlot,
          self.DoReleaseLevels(self.FKidType[LEntry], ASlot));
        if LPart > LCode then
          LCode := LPart;
        end;
        LEntry := self.FKidNext[LEntry];
      end;
      return LCode;
    end;

    // Every edge's callee's summary joined into its routine's until none grows: its fields
    // and module variables, ALL, and what it writes of the site's (DoEffMapSite)
    hidden method DoEffSolve();
    var
      LGrew: bool;
      LFrom: int64;
      LTo: int64;
      LFromAt: int64;
      LToAt: int64;
      LValue: uint64;
      LE: int64;
      LW: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      self.FEffWords := int64((uint64(self.FEffDecls.Count) + uint64(63)) shr uint64(6));
      setlength(self.FEffBits, self.FEffRoutines.Count * self.FEffWords);
      for LI := 0 to self.FEffLocalSlot.Count - 1 do
        self.DoEffSetBit(self.FEffLocalSlot[LI], self.FEffLocalDecl[LI]);
      end;
      LGrew := true;
      while LGrew do
        LGrew := false;
        for LE := 0 to self.FEdgeFrom.Count - 1 do
          LFrom := self.FEdgeFrom[LE];
          if (self.FEffFlags[LFrom] & ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_ALL) = uint64(0) then
            LTo := self.FEffSlotOf.Find(self.FEdgeCallee[LE]);
            if (LTo < 0) or ((self.FEffFlags[LTo] & ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_ALL) <> uint64(0)) then
              self.DoEffAll(LFrom);
              LGrew := true;
            else
              LFromAt := LFrom * self.FEffWords;
              LToAt := LTo * self.FEffWords;
              for LW := 0 to self.FEffWords - 1 do
                LValue := self.FEffBits[LFromAt + LW] | self.FEffBits[LToAt + LW];
                if LValue <> self.FEffBits[LFromAt + LW] then
                  self.FEffBits[LFromAt + LW] := LValue;
                  LGrew := true;
                end;
              end;
              if self.DoEffMapSite(LFrom, LTo, LE) then
                LGrew := true;
              end;
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // What the callee of ATo writes of the edge AEdge's site, written by AFrom: each var or
    // by-reference parameter's argument, its object when it writes through it (SELF: the
    // object's place unless a ref reaches it, AFrom's own object for a method named without
    // one); anything for a release's edge that writes a parameter. True when AFrom grew
    hidden method DoEffMapSite(const AFrom: int64; const ATo: int64; const AEdge: int64): bool;
    var
      LSite: int64;
      LCallee: int64;
      LParams: uint64;
      LOwnParams: uint64;
      LFlags: uint64;
      LObject: int64;
      LArg: int64;
      LPath: PlacePath;
      LGrew: bool;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LSite := self.FEdgeSite[AEdge];
      LCallee := self.FEdgeCallee[AEdge];
      LParams := self.FEffParams[ATo];
      LFlags := self.FEffFlags[AFrom];
      if LSite < 0 then
        // an override's: its parameters are the overridden method's, by position, and its
        // object the same one
        LOwnParams := self.FEffParams[AFrom];
        self.FEffParams[AFrom] := LOwnParams | LParams;
        self.FEffFlags[AFrom] := LFlags | (self.FEffFlags[ATo] & ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_SELF);
        return (self.FEffParams[AFrom] <> LOwnParams) or (self.FEffFlags[AFrom] <> LFlags);
      end;
      LGrew := false;
      if (LParams <> uint64(0)) and (LSite = 0) then
        self.DoEffAll(AFrom);
      end;
      if (LParams <> uint64(0)) and (LSite <> 0) then
        for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LCallee, NodeRole.Param) - 1 do
          if (LI < ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_PARAMS) and ((LParams & (uint64(1) shl uint64(LI))) <> uint64(0)) then
            LArg := self.DoSiteArg(LCallee, LSite, self.FTree.NthOf(LCallee, NodeRole.Param, LI));
            if LArg = 0 then
              self.DoEffAll(AFrom);
            else
              self.DoPlacePath(LArg, true, LPath);
              if self.DoEffPath(AFrom, LPath, true) then
                LGrew := true;
              end;
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      if ((self.FEffFlags[ATo] & ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_SELF) <> uint64(0)) and (LSite <> 0) then
        LObject := self.DoSiteObject(LCallee, LSite);
        if LObject = -2 then
          self.FEffFlags[AFrom] := self.FEffFlags[AFrom] | ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_SELF;
        end;
        if LObject = -1 then
          self.DoEffAll(AFrom);
        end;
        if (LObject > 0) and not self.DoIsRefValue(self.DoUsedType(self.DoArgRoot(LObject))) then
          self.DoPlaceWalk(LObject, true, LPath);
          if self.DoEffPath(AFrom, LPath, true) then
            LGrew := true;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return LGrew or (self.FEffFlags[AFrom] <> LFlags);
    end;

    // True when the declaration ALeft comes before ARight in source order (its file, then
    // its offset)
    hidden const method DoEffBefore(const ALeft: int64; const ARight: int64): bool;
    begin
      if self.FTree[ALeft].Place.FileName <> self.FTree[ARight].Place.FileName then
        return self.FTree[ALeft].Place.FileName < self.FTree[ARight].Place.FileName;
      end;
      return self.FTree[ALeft].StartOffset < self.FTree[ARight].StartOffset;
    end;

    // ASlot's summary written under its routine (see SummarizeWrites): its fields and module
    // variables in source order (an .acu's interface hash reads them: the same summary is
    // the same bytes whatever node ids a build gave them), then its parameters in order
    hidden method DoEffWriteOut(const ASlot: int64);
    var
      LRoutine: int64;
      LEffects: int64;
      LChild: int64;
      LFlags: uint64;
      LDecls: array of int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LMoved: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if self.FEffFixed[ASlot] then
        return;
      end;
      LRoutine := self.FEffRoutines[ASlot];
      LEffects := self.FTree.AddChild(LRoutine, NodeRole.Effects, NodeKind.WriteEffects,
        self.FTree[LRoutine].Place, 0, 0);
      LFlags := self.FEffFlags[ASlot];
      if (LFlags & ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_ALL) <> uint64(0) then
        self.FTree[LEffects].IntValue := ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_ALL;
        return;
      end;
      self.FTree[LEffects].IntValue := LFlags & ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_SELF;
      setlength(LDecls, 0);
      LCount := 0;
      for LIndex := 0 to self.FEffDecls.Count - 1 do
        LAt := ASlot * self.FEffWords + int64(uint64(LIndex) shr uint64(6));
        if (self.FEffBits[LAt] & (uint64(1) shl (uint64(LIndex) & uint64(63)))) <> uint64(0) then
          // insertion into source order
          setlength(LDecls, LCount + 1);
          LMoved := LCount;
          while (LMoved > 0) and self.DoEffBefore(self.FEffDecls[LIndex], LDecls[LMoved - 1]) do
            LDecls[LMoved] := LDecls[LMoved - 1];
            LMoved := LMoved - 1;
          end;
          LDecls[LMoved] := self.FEffDecls[LIndex];
          LCount := LCount + 1;
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LChild := self.FTree.AddChild(LEffects, NodeRole.Element, NodeKind.EffectWrite,
          self.FTree[LRoutine].Place, 0, 0);
        self.FTree[LChild].ResolvedDecl := LDecls[LI];
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LRoutine, NodeRole.Param) - 1 do
        if (LI < ADAM_LOWERING_EFFECT_PARAMS) and
          ((self.FEffParams[ASlot] & (uint64(1) shl uint64(LI))) <> uint64(0)) then
          LChild := self.FTree.AddChild(LEffects, NodeRole.Element, NodeKind.EffectWrite,
            self.FTree[LRoutine].Place, 0, 0);
          self.FTree[LChild].ResolvedDecl := self.FTree.NthOf(LRoutine, NodeRole.Param, LI);
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The declaration whose parameters the call ACall's arguments are passed to, as DoCall
    // lowers it (DoArguments): a method's, a runtime intrinsic's routine (ResolvedCallee),
    // a routine's (DoCalled), a routine value's routine type; 0 for a cast, a typed pack's
    // read, any other intrinsic and any call DoCall refuses
    hidden const method DoCallSig(const ACall: int64): int64;
    var
      LCallee: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      // a declared operator's own declaration (its operands its arguments)
      LDecl := OperatorCallOf(self.FTree, ACall);
      if LDecl <> 0 then
        return LDecl;
      end;
      if (self.FTree[ACall].Kind <> NodeKind.CallExpression) or self.DoIsCastCall(ACall) or
        self.DoIsPackAccess(ACall) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LCallee := self.FTree.FirstOf(ACall, NodeRole.Callee);
      if (self.FTree[LCallee].Kind = NodeKind.MemberExpression) and (self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl <> 0) and
        (self.FTree[self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl].Kind = NodeKind.MethodDecl) then
        return self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl;
      end;
      if NameKindOf(self.FTree, LCallee) = NodeKind.NameExpression then
        LDecl := self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl;
        if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) then
          if self.DoIsRuntimeIntrinsic(self.FTree[LDecl].Text) then
            return self.FTree[ACall].ResolvedCallee;
          end;
          return 0;
        end;
        LDecl := self.DoCalled(LCallee);
        if LDecl <> 0 then
          return LDecl;
        end;
      end;
      if self.DoIsRoutineValue(LCallee) then
        return self.FTree[self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedType].ResolvedDecl;
      end;
      return 0;
    end;

    // True when the call ACall names an intrinsic (BNF sec 7): its place arguments are
    // used within it, never kept
    hidden const method DoIsIntrinsicCallee(const ACall: int64): bool;
    var
      LCallee: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      LCallee := self.FTree.FirstOf(ACall, NodeRole.Callee);
      if NameKindOf(self.FTree, LCallee) <> NodeKind.NameExpression then
        return false;
      end;
      LDecl := self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl;
      return (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl);
    end;

    // Every local and parameter used under ARoot whose slot code outside its routine may
    // reach marked FUnpinned (DoReachedOut; SU2.8 e3): a callee could drop what such a
    // slot holds, so an argument read from it is held (DoStableArg)
    hidden method DoPins(const ARoot: int64);
    var
      LChild: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.ChildCount(ARoot) - 1 do
        LChild := self.FTree.ChildAt(ARoot, LI);
        // a for parallel's workers reach what it captures at once (T2): never pinned
        if self.FTree[LChild].Kind = NodeKind.Capture then
          LDecl := self.FTree[LChild].ResolvedDecl;
          if LDecl <> 0 then
            self.FUnpinned[LDecl] := true;
          end;
        end;
        if self.FTree[LChild].Kind = NodeKind.NameExpression then
          LDecl := self.FTree[LChild].ResolvedDecl;
          if (LDecl <> 0) and (not self.FUnpinned[LDecl]) and
            ((self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.Param) or (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.VarDecl)) and
            self.DoReachedOut(LChild) then
            self.FUnpinned[LDecl] := true;
          end;
        end;
        self.DoPins(LChild);
      end;
    end;

    // True when the use AUse of a variable (through parentheses) lets code outside its
    // routine reach the variable's slot: `addr of` it; an argument of a var parameter, of a
    // call DoCallSig does not map (an intrinsic's excepted: it uses the place within
    // itself), of an object's init (its arguments, a constructor's), or an index (an
    // indexed property's accessor takes it); a read, a target of its own routine's write
    // or a value argument reaches nothing
    hidden const method DoReachedOut(const AUse: int64): bool;
    var
      LUp: int64;
      LParent: int64;
      LRole: NodeRole;
      LSig: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LUp := AUse;
      while self.FTree[self.FTree.ParentOf(LUp)].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LUp := self.FTree.ParentOf(LUp);
      end;
      LParent := self.FTree.ParentOf(LUp);
      LRole := self.FTree.RoleOf(LUp);
      if (self.FTree[LParent].Kind = NodeKind.UnaryExpression) and (self.FTree[LParent].Op = OperatorKind.AddressOf) then
        return true;
      end;
      if (LRole = NodeRole.ConstructorArgument) or (LRole = NodeRole.Index) then
        return true;
      end;
      if LRole <> NodeRole.Argument then
        return false;
      end;
      if self.FTree[LParent].Kind <> NodeKind.CallExpression then
        return true;
      end;
      LSig := self.DoCallSig(LParent);
      if LSig = 0 then
        return not self.DoIsIntrinsicCallee(LParent);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LParent, NodeRole.Argument) - 1 do
        if self.FTree.NthOf(LParent, NodeRole.Argument, LI) = LUp then
          return (LI < self.FTree.CountOf(LSig, NodeRole.Param)) and
            self.FTree[self.FTree.NthOf(LSig, NodeRole.Param, LI)].HasFlag(NodeFlag.VarParam);
        end;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The temporaries of the full expression AExpr ended as it ends, as C++ ends them
    // (pcpp's truth: a ref made in place for an argument is done before the next
    // statement): every hidden slot DoTemporaries made at or under AExpr released and
    // emptied (DoEndTemporary), so the exits' cleanup and an unwind find nothing left
    // there. Nothing when the current block has ended. An async expression's own task ends
    // here like any temporary (a discarded task detaches: its thread holds its own
    // reference, System.Runtime's TaskStart), never what is below it (its call's
    // temporaries are its task entry's)
    hidden method DoEndTemporaries(const AExpr: int64);
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if (AExpr = 0) or self.DoEnded() then
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[AExpr].Kind = NodeKind.AsyncExpression then
        self.DoEndTemporary(AExpr);
        return;
      end;
      self.DoEndTemporary(AExpr);
      self.DoEndRangeScratch(AExpr);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.ChildCount(AExpr) - 1 do
        self.DoEndTemporaries(self.FTree.ChildAt(AExpr, LI));
      end;
    end;

    // The temporary AId's hidden slot (FTempOf; none: nothing) released at its type
    // (FTempTypeOf, DoReleaseAt) and emptied: a pointer one set to nil, an aggregate one
    // zeroed. A value object that ends by a done is ended only while its live flag holds
    // (DoReleaseLive: a call that never ran, a short-circuited one, or a result moved out
    // by an initializer or an assignment left nothing to end), the flag cleared
    hidden method DoEndTemporary(const AId: int64);
    var
      LSlot: int64;
      LType: int64;
    begin
      LSlot := self.FTempOf[AId];
      if LSlot = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LType := self.FTempTypeOf[AId];
      if (LType <> 0) and self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        if not self.DoReleaseLive(LSlot, LType, self.FLiveOf[AId], false, AId) then
          return;
        end;
        self.DoFill(LSlot, TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType), AId);
        return;
      end;
      if not self.DoReleaseAt(LSlot, LType, AId) then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoStore(LSlot, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, AId), AId);
    end;

    // The range scratch strings of the print / println / FormatStr call AId
    // (DoRangeTemporaries; none: nothing) released and emptied as its full expression ends,
    // as a text temporary is (DoEndTemporary): each string released (DoReleaseAt) and its
    // slot set to nil, so the exits' cleanup and an unwind find nothing left there
    hidden method DoEndRangeScratch(const AId: int64);
    var
      LSlot: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if self.FRangeScratchOf[AId] = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.DoRangeScratchCount(AId) - 1 do
        LSlot := self.FRangeSlots[self.FRangeScratchOf[AId] - 1 + LI];
        if not self.DoReleaseAt(LSlot, 0, AId) then
          return;
        end;
        self.DoStore(LSlot, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, AId), AId);
      end;
    end;

    // A new FManaged for the function about to be lowered (none of its slots yet, no exit
    // block, no protected region: DoStartRegions)
    hidden method DoStartManaged();
    begin
      self.FWorkerIndex := 0;
      self.FWorkerCount := 0;
      self.FManaged := ref Int64List();
      self.FManagedType := ref Int64List();
      self.FManagedLive := ref Int64List();
      self.FExitBlocks := ref Int64List();
      self.DoStartRegions();
    end;

    // No protected region and no waiting jump for the function about to be lowered
    hidden method DoStartRegions();
    begin
      self.FRegions := ref Int64List();
      self.FPadJumps := ref Int64List();
      self.FPadTargets := ref Int64List();
      self.FPadLoops := ref Int64List();
      self.FPadDepths := ref Int64List();
      self.FPadValueSlot := 0;
      self.FPadValueType := IrType.Void;
    end;

    // True when the current function cleans up its own managed slots as an unwind leaves it
    // (DoCleanupScopes): it holds any (FManaged) and is no funclet (a funclet's own are
    // released at its end, and an unwind never leaves one halfway)
    hidden const method DoCleansUp(): bool;
    begin
      return (self.FManaged.Count > 0) and (self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction).Parent = 0);
    end;

    // A new block the current one jumps to, where the function's code at an exit goes (its
    // managed slots released, its parts ended, its return): one of FExitBlocks, so its
    // cleanup scopes leave it out and a release that ends an object whose done raises never
    // runs twice
    hidden method DoExitBlock(const ANode: int64);
    var
      LBlock: int64;
    begin
      LBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoJumpTo(LBlock, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LBlock;
      self.FExitBlocks.Add(self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction).Blocks.Count - 1);
    end;

    // The slot ASlot, which holds what a value of the canonical type AType holds (0: a
    // text), one of FManaged: released at every exit of the current function. A dynamic
    // array's element map (DoElementMapData) and an aggregate's managed map
    // (DoManagedMapData) are made here, reported at ANode; false after LW0001 (the slot is
    // then no one's to release)
    hidden method DoAddManaged(const ASlot: int64; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    begin
      if self.DoIsArrayValue(AType) then
        if self.DoElementMapData(AType, ANode) = 0 then
          return false;
        end;
      else
        // a text, a ref and a weak need no map (a ref's block names its descriptor)
        if (AType <> 0) and (not self.DoIsText(AType)) and (not self.DoIsOwnerValue(AType)) and
          (self.DoManagedMapData(AType, ANode) = 0) then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      self.FManaged.Add(ASlot);
      self.FManagedType.Add(AType);
      self.FManagedLive.Add(self.DoLiveFlag(AType, ANode));
      return true;
    end;

    // The live flag of a slot ANode owns that holds a value of the canonical type AType
    // (FManagedLive, FLiveOf): for a value object whose type runs code where it is copied
    // or ended (DoHasLifetime: it moves) a bool slot, false (made with the slot, before
    // any of the function's code runs: nothing built yet), else 0
    hidden method DoLiveFlag(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LFlag: int64;
    begin
      if (AType = 0) or (not self.DoIsAggregate(AType)) or (not self.DoHasLifetime(AType)) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LFlag := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, 1, 1);
      self.DoStore(LFlag, self.DoConstant(IrType.Bool, 0, ANode), ANode);
      self.FLiveOf[ANode] := LFlag;
      return LFlag;
    end;

    // The live flag of the slot the local or temporary AId owns (FLiveOf; none: nothing)
    // set to AValue at ANode: true once its object is built or moved in, false once it is
    // ended or moved out
    hidden method DoSetLive(const AId: int64; const AValue: bool; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      if (AId = 0) or (self.FLiveOf[AId] = 0) then
        return;
      end;
      LValue := 0;
      if AValue then
        LValue := 1;
      end;
      self.DoStore(self.FLiveOf[AId], self.DoConstant(IrType.Bool, LValue, ANode), ANode);
    end;

    // The value of the canonical type AType at AAddress released (DoReleaseAt) only while
    // its live flag ALive holds (0: always), the flag then cleared: a branch over the
    // release into a join where the current block goes on. AExit: the release is part of
    // an exit (DoReleaseManaged), so its blocks are exit blocks too (FExitBlocks: outside
    // the cleanup scopes); false after LW0001
    hidden method DoReleaseLive(const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64; const ALive: int64;
      const AExit: bool; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LRelease: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
      LDone: bool;
    begin
      if ALive = 0 then
        return self.DoReleaseAt(AAddress, AType, ANode);
      end;
      LRelease := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      if AExit then
        self.FExitBlocks.Add(self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction).Blocks.Count - 1);
      end;
      LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      if AExit then
        self.FExitBlocks.Add(self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction).Blocks.Count - 1);
      end;
      self.DoBranchOn(self.DoLoad(ALive, IrType.Bool, ANode), LRelease, LJoin, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LRelease;
      // cleared first: a done that raises never finds its object live again
      self.DoStore(ALive, self.DoConstant(IrType.Bool, 0, ANode), ANode);
      LDone := self.DoReleaseAt(AAddress, AType, ANode);
      if not self.DoEnded() then
        self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, ANode);
      end;
      self.FBlock := LJoin;
      return LDone;
    end;

    // Every slot of FManaged released (DoReleaseLive under its live flag), the last made
    // first: at each of the current function's exits (a return, its end), in an exit block
    // of its own when the function cleans up (DoExitBlock: what follows, its parts ended
    // and its return, goes there too)
    hidden method DoReleaseManaged(const ANode: int64);
    var
      LExit: bool;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LExit := self.DoCleansUp();
      if LExit then
        self.DoExitBlock(ANode);
      end;
      for LI := self.FManaged.Count - 1 downto 0 do
        if not self.DoReleaseLive(self.FManaged[LI], self.FManagedType[LI], self.FManagedLive[LI],
          LExit, ANode) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The managed values held at AAddress by a value of the canonical type AType released:
    // a text (AType 0 or of the string family) by StrRelease, a dynamic array by ArrRelease
    // with its element map (DoElementMap), an aggregate holding them by ManagedRelease over
    // its managed map (DoManagedMap), an object that ends by a done ended first
    // (DoEndObject); false after LW0001
    hidden method DoReleaseAt(const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LValue: int64;
      LMap: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
    begin
      if (AType = 0) or self.DoIsText(AType) then
        LValue := self.DoLoad(AAddress, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrRelease, LValue, 0, ANode) <> 0;
      end;
      if self.DoIsArrayValue(AType) then
        LValue := self.DoLoad(AAddress, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        LMap := self.DoElementMap(AType, ANode);
        if LMap = 0 then
          return false;
        end;
        return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.ArrRelease, LValue, LMap, ANode) <> 0;
      end;
      // an own I / ref I releases its object's block (I3: through the itable's offset)
      if self.DoIsInterfaceOwner(AType) then
        LValue := self.DoLoad(AAddress, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.IntfRelease, LValue, 0, ANode) <> 0;
      end;
      // a ref's block names its descriptor: the last release ends the object there
      if self.DoIsRefValue(AType) then
        LValue := self.DoLoad(AAddress, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.RefRelease, LValue, 0, ANode) <> 0;
      end;
      // a weak gives back its watch (the block freed when it was the last)
      if self.DoIsWeakValue(AType) then
        LValue := self.DoLoad(AAddress, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.WeakRelease, LValue, 0, ANode) <> 0;
      end;
      // an object that ends by a done is ended first (its done reads its managed fields),
      // then its managed values released
      if self.DoNeedsEnd(AType) then
        if not self.DoEndObject(AAddress, AType, ANode) then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      // an aggregate that holds none (a copy decl's object, a done's) has nothing more
      if not self.DoHoldsManaged(AType) then
        return true;
      end;
      LMap := self.DoManagedMap(AType, ANode);
      if LMap = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(AAddress);
      LArgs.Add(LMap);
      return self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.ManagedRelease, LArgs, ANode) <> 0;
    end;

    // The value of the aggregate type AType (DoIsAggregate) at ASource copied to ADest at
    // ANode over the value ADest holds (an assignment's store): a type with no copy decl
    // in it as DoCopyValue copies it (ManagedAssign releases ADest's old managed values);
    // one with a copy decl somewhere (BNF sec 4 O5: `LB := LA`) is copied into a zeroed
    // slot of its own first (the source may be ADest itself or a part of it), then ADest's
    // old value ended (DoReleaseAt: its done, its managed values) and the copy's bytes
    // moved in
    hidden method DoAggregateCopy(const ADest: int64; const ASource: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ANode: int64);
    var
      LSize: int64;
      LTemp: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoHoldsMember(AType, NodeKind.CopyDecl) then
        self.DoCopyValue(ADest, ASource, AType, ANode);
        return;
      end;
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType);
      LTemp := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, LSize, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType));
      // zeroed each time it runs: a loop's next copy starts from nothing too
      self.DoFill(LTemp, LSize, ANode);
      if not self.DoCopyValue(LTemp, ASource, AType, ANode) then
        return;
      end;
      if not self.DoReleaseAt(ADest, AType, ANode) then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoCopyBytes(ADest, LTemp, LSize, ANode);
    end;

    // The value of the aggregate type AType at ASource copied at ANode into ADest, which
    // holds no value whose type runs code (zeroed, or holding managed values only, which
    // ManagedAssign releases as it stores): a type with no copy decl in it by its bytes
    // (DoCopyBytes) or, holding managed values, ManagedAssign over its managed map (each
    // source value gains a holder); one that ends by a done with no copy cannot be copied
    // (SEM's SM0427: LW0001 here). A static array holding a copy element by element
    // (DoEachElement); an object whose type declares a copy by its copy function (self
    // ADest, its const parameter ASource by reference: it builds the copy, BNF sec 4 O5);
    // any other object part by part (DoCopyParts). False after LW0001
    hidden method DoCopyValue(const ADest: int64; const ASource: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LCopy: int64;
      LFunction: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoHoldsMember(AType, NodeKind.CopyDecl) then
        if self.DoNeedsEnd(AType) then
          self.DoRefuse(ANode, "the lifetime of type '" + TypeText(self.FTree, AType) + "'");
          return false;
        end;
        return self.DoWholeCopy(ADest, ASource, AType, ANode);
      end;
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.StaticArray then
        return self.DoEachElement(ADest, ASource, AType, ElementWalk.Copied, ANode);
      end;
      LCopy := self.DoOwnMember(AType, NodeKind.CopyDecl);
      if LCopy = 0 then
        return self.DoCopyParts(ADest, ASource, AType, ANode);
      end;
      // a copy refused at its declaration was reported there
      LFunction := self.FFunctionOf[LCopy];
      if LFunction = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Call, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Link := LFunction;
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(ADest);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(ASource);
      return true;
    end;

    // The object at ASource, of the canonical object type AType that declares no copy and
    // holds one (in its parent part, a field, an embed, an array field's element), copied
    // at ANode into ADest (as DoCopyValue's) part by part (BNF sec 4 O5): the whole value
    // first, its bytes and its managed values (each gains a holder: the plain fields and
    // texts are copied as they are), then each part that holds a copy, the parent part
    // first and then the fields and embeds in declaration order, taken back to nothing
    // (DoClearPart) and copied by its own type's copy (DoCopyValue); last a polymorphic
    // object's vptr names its own type's vtable (the parent's copy left its level's
    // there). False after LW0001
    hidden method DoCopyParts(const ADest: int64; const ASource: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LParent: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LPart: int64;
      LTo: int64;
      LFrom: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoWholeCopy(ADest, ASource, AType, ANode) then
        return false;
      end;
      LParent := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if (LParent <> 0) and self.DoHoldsMember(LParent, NodeKind.CopyDecl) then
        LTo := self.DoUpcast(ADest, AType, LParent, ANode);
        LFrom := self.DoUpcast(ASource, AType, LParent, ANode);
        if not self.DoClearPart(LTo, LParent, ANode) then
          return false;
        end;
        if not self.DoCopyValue(LTo, LFrom, LParent, ANode) then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      LBody := BodyOf(self.FTree, AType);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
        LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(LBody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
        if (self.FTree[LMember].Kind = NodeKind.FieldDecl) or (self.FTree[LMember].Kind = NodeKind.EmbedDecl) then
          LPart := self.DoPartType(LMember);
          if self.DoHoldsMember(LPart, NodeKind.CopyDecl) then
            if self.FTree[LMember].ResolvedOffset < 0 then
              raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_FIELD_OFFSET + self.FTree[LMember].Text);
            end;
            LTo := self.DoByteOffset(ADest, self.FTree[LMember].ResolvedOffset, ANode);
            LFrom := self.DoByteOffset(ASource, self.FTree[LMember].ResolvedOffset, ANode);
            if not self.DoClearPart(LTo, LPart, ANode) then
              return false;
            end;
            if not self.DoCopyValue(LTo, LFrom, LPart, ANode) then
              return false;
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return self.DoSetVptr(ADest, AType, ANode);
    end;

    // The whole value of the canonical type AType at ASource copied at ANode into ADest as
    // plain data (DoCopyValue's copy of a type with no copy in it; DoCopyParts' first
    // step, which copies the parts holding one again by their copies): its bytes, or
    // ManagedAssign over its managed map (each managed value gains a holder, each old one
    // of ADest is released); false after LW0001
    hidden method DoWholeCopy(const ADest: int64; const ASource: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LSize: int64;
      LMap: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
    begin
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType);
      if not self.DoHoldsManaged(AType) then
        self.DoCopyBytes(ADest, ASource, LSize, ANode);
        return true;
      end;
      LMap := self.DoManagedMap(AType, ANode);
      if LMap = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(ADest);
      LArgs.Add(ASource);
      LArgs.Add(self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LSize, ANode));
      LArgs.Add(LMap);
      return self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.ManagedAssign, LArgs, ANode) <> 0;
    end;

    // The part at AAddress, of the canonical type AType, of a value DoWholeCopy has just
    // copied, taken back to nothing at ANode: the holders that copy gave its managed
    // values given back (ManagedRelease over its own managed map: no done runs, nothing
    // was built), its bytes zeroed, so its own copy builds it from empty; false after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoClearPart(const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LMap: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
    begin
      if self.DoHoldsManaged(AType) then
        LMap := self.DoManagedMap(AType, ANode);
        if LMap = 0 then
          return false;
        end;
        LArgs := ref Int64List();
        LArgs.Add(AAddress);
        LArgs.Add(LMap);
        if self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.ManagedRelease, LArgs, ANode) = 0 then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      self.DoFill(AAddress, TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType), ANode);
      return true;
    end;

    // A run of ACount managed values, the first AOffset bytes into the value, AStride bytes
    // apart, added to ARuns (four int64 each: offset, count, stride, element: 0 for texts,
    // else the canonical dynamic array type they are, which DoMapWords turns into the
    // offset of its element map); one value of the same element right after the last
    // run's, at its stride (or after a lone value at any distance), lengthens that run
    hidden method DoAddRun(const ARuns: ref Int64List; const AOffset: int64; const ACount: int64;
      const AStride: int64; const AElement: int64);
    var
      LLast: int64;
    begin
      LLast := ARuns.Count - ADAM_LOWERING_RUN_WORDS;
      if (LLast >= 0) and (ACount = 1) and (AOffset > ARuns[LLast]) and (ARuns[LLast + 3] = AElement) then
        if ARuns[LLast + 1] = 1 then
          ARuns.Put(LLast + 1, 2);
          ARuns.Put(LLast + 2, AOffset - ARuns[LLast]);
          return;
        end;
        if AOffset = ARuns[LLast] + ARuns[LLast + 1] * ARuns[LLast + 2] then
          ARuns.Put(LLast + 1, ARuns[LLast + 1] + 1);
          return;
        end;
      end;
      ARuns.Add(AOffset);
      ARuns.Add(ACount);
      ARuns.Add(AStride);
      ARuns.Add(AElement);
    end;

    // The runs of managed values (DoAddRun) a value of the canonical type AType holds when
    // it starts ABase bytes into the mapped value, added to ARuns: a text one, a dynamic
    // array one (its type as the run's element); a record's through its parent part, then
    // its fields (DoManagedRunsIn); a static array's element runs over all its elements
    // (one run when the element's values form one run that repeats evenly); nothing for a
    // type that holds none. False after LW0001 at ANode for a type whose values cannot be
    // mapped: an overlay's (a managed value shares its bytes)
    hidden method DoManagedRuns(const AType: int64; const ABase: int64; const ARuns: ref Int64List;
      const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
      LElement: ref Int64List;
      LCount: int64;
      LStride: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LJ: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoHoldsManaged(AType) then
        return true;
      end;
      if self.DoIsText(AType) then
        self.DoAddRun(ARuns, ABase, 1, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), 0);
        return true;
      end;
      if self.DoIsArrayValue(AType) then
        self.DoAddRun(ARuns, ABase, 1, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), AType);
        return true;
      end;
      if self.DoIsInterfaceOwner(AType) then
        self.DoAddRun(ARuns, ABase, 1, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), ADAM_LOWERING_INTF_ELEMENT);
        return true;
      end;
      if self.DoIsRefValue(AType) then
        self.DoAddRun(ARuns, ABase, 1, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), ADAM_LOWERING_REF_ELEMENT);
        return true;
      end;
      if self.DoIsWeakValue(AType) then
        self.DoAddRun(ARuns, ABase, 1, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), ADAM_LOWERING_WEAK_ELEMENT);
        return true;
      end;
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if (LClass = TypeClass.RecordType) or (LClass = TypeClass.ObjectType) then
        return self.DoManagedRunsIn(AType, BodyOf(self.FTree, AType), ABase, ARuns, ANode);
      end;
      if LClass <> TypeClass.StaticArray then
        self.DoRefuse(ANode, "the texts of type '" + TypeText(self.FTree, AType) + "'");
        return false;
      end;
      LElement := ref Int64List();
      if not self.DoManagedRuns(TargetOf(self.FTree, AType), 0, LElement, ANode) then
        return false;
      end;
      LCount := ArrayCount(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType);
      if LCount < 0 then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_ARRAY_COUNT + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
      end;
      LStride := self.DoElementSize(AType);
      if (LElement.Count = ADAM_LOWERING_RUN_WORDS) and (LElement[1] = 1) then
        self.DoAddRun(ARuns, ABase + LElement[0], LCount, LStride, LElement[3]);
        return true;
      end;
      if (LElement.Count = ADAM_LOWERING_RUN_WORDS) and (LElement[1] * LElement[2] = LStride) then
        self.DoAddRun(ARuns, ABase + LElement[0], LCount * LElement[1], LElement[2], LElement[3]);
        return true;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LJ := 0;
        while LJ < LElement.Count do
          self.DoAddRun(ARuns, ABase + LI * LStride + LElement[LJ], LElement[LJ + 1], LElement[LJ + 2],
            LElement[LJ + 3]);
          LJ := LJ + ADAM_LOWERING_RUN_WORDS;
        end;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The runs of managed values of the record ARecord's body ABody (ABase bytes into the
    // mapped value) added to ARuns: its parent part's at the part's offset, then each
    // field's at its own (an anonymous record's fields are its declaring type's, at their
    // own offsets); false after LW0001 at ANode for an anonymous overlay or an embed that
    // holds managed values
    hidden method DoManagedRunsIn(const ARecord: int64; const ABody: int64; const ABase: int64;
      const ARuns: ref Int64List; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LPart: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LPart := self.FTree.FirstOf(ABody, NodeRole.Parent);
      if LPart <> 0 then
        if self.FTree[LPart].ResolvedOffset < 0 then
          raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_FIELD_OFFSET + TypeText(self.FTree, ARecord));
        end;
        if not self.DoManagedRuns(CanonicalOf(self.FTree, LPart), ABase + self.FTree[LPart].ResolvedOffset,
          ARuns, ANode) then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ABody, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
        LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(ABody, NodeRole.Member, LI);
        LKind := self.FTree[LMember].Kind;
        if LKind = NodeKind.FieldDecl then
          if not self.DoFieldManagedRuns(LMember, ABase, ARuns, ANode) then
            return false;
          end;
        end;
        if LKind = NodeKind.AnonRecord then
          if not self.DoManagedRunsIn(ARecord, LMember, ABase, ARuns, ANode) then
            return false;
          end;
        end;
        if LKind = NodeKind.EmbedDecl then
          // an embed is a field (BNF sec 4): its type's runs, at its offset
          if not self.DoEmbedManagedRuns(LMember, ABase, ARuns, ANode) then
            return false;
          end;
        end;
        if (LKind = NodeKind.AnonOverlay) and self.DoMemberHoldsManaged(LMember) then
          self.DoRefuse(ANode, "the texts of " + self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(LMember));
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The runs of managed values of the field AField (ABase bytes into the mapped value, the
    // field at its ResolvedOffset from there) added to ARuns; false after LW0001 at ANode
    hidden method DoFieldManagedRuns(const AField: int64; const ABase: int64; const ARuns: ref Int64List;
      const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LType: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoDeclType(AField);
      if not self.DoHoldsManaged(LType) then
        return true;
      end;
      if self.FTree[AField].ResolvedOffset < 0 then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_FIELD_OFFSET + self.FTree[AField].Text);
      end;
      return self.DoManagedRuns(LType, ABase + self.FTree[AField].ResolvedOffset, ARuns, ANode);
    end;

    // The runs of managed values of the embed AEmbed (ABase bytes into the mapped value, the
    // embed at its ResolvedOffset from there: its type's runs, DoPartType) added to ARuns;
    // false after LW0001 at ANode
    hidden method DoEmbedManagedRuns(const AEmbed: int64; const ABase: int64; const ARuns: ref Int64List;
      const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LType: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoPartType(AEmbed);
      if not self.DoHoldsManaged(LType) then
        return true;
      end;
      if self.FTree[AEmbed].ResolvedOffset < 0 then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_FIELD_OFFSET + self.FTree[AEmbed].Text);
      end;
      return self.DoManagedRuns(LType, ABase + self.FTree[AEmbed].ResolvedOffset, ARuns, ANode);
    end;

    // True when the anonymous part or embed AMember holds a text or a dynamic array at any
    // depth
    hidden const method DoMemberHoldsManaged(const AMember: int64): bool;
    var
      LI: int64;
      LMember: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AMember].Kind = NodeKind.EmbedDecl then
        return self.DoHoldsManaged(CanonicalOf(self.FTree, self.FTree.FirstOf(AMember, NodeRole.TypeOf)));
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AMember, NodeRole.Member) - 1 do
        LMember := self.FTree.NthOf(AMember, NodeRole.Member, LI);
        if self.FTree[LMember].Kind = NodeKind.FieldDecl then
          if self.DoHoldsManaged(self.DoDeclType(LMember)) then
            return true;
          end;
        else
          if self.DoMemberHoldsManaged(LMember) then
            return true;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // The managed map of the canonical type AType added to AWords (System.Runtime's layout:
    // the count of runs, then each run's offset, count, stride and element word), then the
    // element map of each dynamic array type its runs hold (DoElementWords), each run's
    // element word the byte offset from this map's start to it. AEmitted pairs each array
    // type whose element map AWords holds already with its word index: a type met again
    // (a sibling run, or one that holds itself through an array) points back to it;
    // AAddresses gathers the words that are a routine's address (DoElementWords, DoAddWords).
    // False after LW0001 at ANode
    hidden method DoMapWords(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64; const AWords: ref Int64List;
      const AEmitted: ref Int64List; const AAddresses: ref Int64List): bool;
    var
      LRuns: ref Int64List;
    begin
      LRuns := ref Int64List();
      if not self.DoManagedRuns(AType, 0, LRuns, ANode) then
        return false;
      end;
      return self.DoRunWords(LRuns, ANode, AWords, AEmitted, AAddresses);
    end;

    // The managed map of the runs ARuns (DoManagedRuns', gathered at their offsets: a
    // type's, or a task object's parts, DoTaskDescriptorData) added to AWords, in
    // DoMapWords' layout with the element maps its runs need; false after LW0001 at ANode
    hidden method DoRunWords(const ARuns: ref Int64List; const ANode: int64; const AWords: ref Int64List;
      const AEmitted: ref Int64List; const AAddresses: ref Int64List): bool;
    var
      LStart: int64;
      LFirstRun: int64;
      LRun: int64;
      LArray: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LStart := AWords.Count;
      AWords.Add(ARuns.Count div ADAM_LOWERING_RUN_WORDS);
      LFirstRun := AWords.Count;
      for LI := 0 to ARuns.Count - 1 do
        AWords.Add(ARuns[LI]);
      end;
      for LRun := 0 to (ARuns.Count div ADAM_LOWERING_RUN_WORDS) - 1 do
        LArray := ARuns[LRun * ADAM_LOWERING_RUN_WORDS + 3];
        // a text run (0), a ref run (ADAM_LOWERING_REF_ELEMENT), a weak run
        // (ADAM_LOWERING_WEAK_ELEMENT) and an own I / ref I run (ADAM_LOWERING_INTF_ELEMENT)
        // keep their word
        if (LArray <> 0) and (LArray <> ADAM_LOWERING_REF_ELEMENT) and (LArray <> ADAM_LOWERING_WEAK_ELEMENT) and
          (LArray <> ADAM_LOWERING_INTF_ELEMENT) then
          LAt := -1;
          LI := 0;
          while (LAt < 0) and (LI < AEmitted.Count) do
            if AEmitted[LI] = LArray then
              LAt := AEmitted[LI + 1];
            end;
            LI := LI + 2;
          end;
          if LAt < 0 then
            LAt := AWords.Count;
            if not self.DoElementWords(LArray, ANode, AWords, AEmitted, AAddresses) then
              return false;
            end;
          end;
          AWords.Put(LFirstRun + LRun * ADAM_LOWERING_RUN_WORDS + 3, (LAt - LStart) * 8);
        end;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The element map of the canonical dynamic array type AArray added to AWords (its
    // element's size, its element routines' words (DoElementRoutines: each routine's word
    // and function recorded in AAddresses, the word itself 0), then the element type's
    // managed map: DoMapWords), AArray and its word index recorded in AEmitted first; false
    // after LW0001 at ANode
    hidden method DoElementWords(const AArray: int64; const ANode: int64; const AWords: ref Int64List;
      const AEmitted: ref Int64List; const AAddresses: ref Int64List): bool;
    var
      LRoutines: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LRoutines := self.DoElementRoutines(TargetOf(self.FTree, AArray), ANode);
      if LRoutines = -2 then
        return false;
      end;
      AEmitted.Add(AArray);
      AEmitted.Add(AWords.Count);
      AWords.Add(self.DoElementSize(AArray));
      // the build, the copy and the end, in FElementTriples' order
      for LI := 0 to ADAM_LOWERING_ELEMENT_HEAD - 2 do
        if (LRoutines >= 0) and (self.FElementTriples[LRoutines + LI] <> 0) then
          AAddresses.Add(AWords.Count);
          AAddresses.Add(self.FElementTriples[LRoutines + LI] - 1);
        end;
        AWords.Add(0);
      end;
      return self.DoMapWords(TargetOf(self.FTree, AArray), ANode, AWords, AEmitted, AAddresses);
    end;

    // The element routines of the canonical type AType as a dynamic array's element, made
    // the first time (FElementRoutinesOf): a build when building a value runs code
    // (DoNeedsBuild), a copy when copying one does (a copy decl in it: DoCopyValue), an end
    // when ending one does (DoNeedsEnd; its managed values are its map's to release after
    // it). A type that ends by a done and declares no copy cannot be copied (SEM's SM0427):
    // its copy word stays 0 beside an end word, which System.Runtime refuses to copy. The
    // index of its triple in FElementTriples, -1 for a type whose values run no code, -2
    // after LW0001 at ANode (reported once: a value that runs code where it is built,
    // copied or ended and is neither an object nor a static array of them, as DoBuildFields
    // refuses it as a part)
    hidden method DoElementRoutines(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      if self.FElementRoutinesOf[AType] > 0 then
        return self.FElementRoutinesOf[AType] - 1;
      end;
      if self.FElementRoutinesOf[AType] < 0 then
        return self.FElementRoutinesOf[AType];
      end;
      if not (self.DoHasLifetime(AType) or self.DoNeedsBuild(AType)) then
        self.FElementRoutinesOf[AType] := -1;
        return -1;
      end;
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if (LClass <> TypeClass.ObjectType) and (LClass <> TypeClass.StaticArray) then
        self.FElementRoutinesOf[AType] := -2;
        self.DoRefuse(ANode, "the lifetime of type '" + TypeText(self.FTree, AType) + "'");
        return -2;
      end;
      LAt := self.FElementTriples.Count;
      self.FElementTriples.Add(0);
      self.FElementTriples.Add(0);
      self.FElementTriples.Add(0);
      if self.DoNeedsBuild(AType) then
        self.FElementTriples.Put(LAt, self.DoElementFunction(AType, ElementWalk.Built, ANode) + 1);
      end;
      if self.DoHoldsMember(AType, NodeKind.CopyDecl) then
        self.FElementTriples.Put(LAt + 1, self.DoElementFunction(AType, ElementWalk.Copied, ANode) + 1);
      end;
      if self.DoNeedsEnd(AType) then
        self.FElementTriples.Put(LAt + 2, self.DoElementFunction(AType, ElementWalk.Ended, ANode) + 1);
      end;
      self.FElementRoutinesOf[AType] := LAt + 1;
      return LAt;
    end;

    // A new element routine of the canonical element type AType (DoElementRoutines) at
    // ANode, AWalk saying which: internal, taking the element's address (a copy the
    // zeroed element's, then its source's); its body (DoElementBody) is lowered last
    // (DoEndBodies), as the lowering of the routine whose element map asked for it is
    // still under way; its function id
    hidden method DoElementFunction(const AType: int64; const AWalk: ElementWalk; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LSymbol: string;
      LFunction: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
    begin
      LSymbol := ADAM_LOWERING_ELEMENT_BUILD_SYMBOL;
      if AWalk = ElementWalk.Copied then
        LSymbol := ADAM_LOWERING_ELEMENT_COPY_SYMBOL;
      end;
      if AWalk = ElementWalk.Ended then
        LSymbol := ADAM_LOWERING_ELEMENT_END_SYMBOL;
      end;
      LIndex := self.FElementFunctions.Count;
      LFunction := self.FModule.AddFunction(LSymbol + IntToStr(LIndex), IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Internal := true;
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.AddParam(IrType.Pointer);
      if AWalk = ElementWalk.Copied then
        self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.AddParam(IrType.Pointer);
      end;
      self.FElementFunctions.Add(LFunction);
      self.FElementTypes.Add(AType);
      self.FElementNodes.Add(ANode);
      // one more walk: setlength grows the array geometrically
      setlength(self.FElementWalks, LIndex + 1);
      self.FElementWalks[LIndex] := AWalk;
      return LFunction;
    end;

    // The body of the element routine AIndex (DoElementFunction): the element's address
    // (its one parameter; a copy's source the second), the element built (DoBuildObject),
    // copied into it (DoCopyValue: the runtime gives it zeroed) or ended (DoEndObject),
    // the return
    hidden method DoElementBody(const AIndex: int64);
    var
      LNode: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LWalk: ElementWalk;
    begin
      LNode := self.FElementNodes[AIndex];
      LType := self.FElementTypes[AIndex];
      LWalk := self.FElementWalks[AIndex];
      self.FFunction := self.FElementFunctions[AIndex];
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoStartManaged();
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Pointer, LNode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Imm := 0;
      if LWalk = ElementWalk.Built then
        if not self.DoBuildObject(LAddress, LType, 0, 0, NodeRole.Argument, LNode) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      if LWalk = ElementWalk.Ended then
        if not self.DoEndObject(LAddress, LType, LNode) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      if LWalk = ElementWalk.Copied then
        LSource := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Pointer, LNode);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LSource).Imm := 1;
        if not self.DoCopyValue(LAddress, LSource, LType, LNode) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      if not self.DoEnded() then
        self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, LNode);
      end;
    end;

    // The int64 words AWords from AFirst added to the data AData (little-endian), each word
    // AAddresses names (pairs: its index into AWords, a function id; in rising index order,
    // as DoElementWords adds them) the address of that function instead
    hidden method DoAddWords(const AData: int64; const AWords: ref Int64List; const AFirst: int64;
      const AAddresses: ref Int64List);
    var
      LNext: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LNext := 0;
      while (LNext < AAddresses.Count) and (AAddresses[LNext] < AFirst) do
        LNext := LNext + 2;
      end;
      for LI := AFirst to AWords.Count - 1 do
        if (LNext < AAddresses.Count) and (AAddresses[LNext] = LI) then
          self.FModule.DataAt(AData).AddAddress(self.FModule.FunctionAt(AAddresses[LNext + 1]).Symbol, 0);
          LNext := LNext + 2;
        else
          self.DoAddLe64(AData, AWords[LI]);
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // A read-only data blob of the int64 words AWords (little-endian, 8-aligned; a word
    // AAddresses names a routine's address, DoAddWords), its symbol ASymbol and its data id
    hidden method DoWordsData(const ASymbol: string; const AWords: ref Int64List; const AAddresses: ref Int64List;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LData: int64;
    begin
      LData := self.DoHelperData(ASymbol, 8, ANode);
      self.DoAddWords(LData, AWords, 0, AAddresses);
      return LData;
    end;

    // The read-only data of the managed map of the canonical type AType (a record or a
    // static array holding texts or dynamic arrays), made the first time (FManagedMapOf):
    // DoMapWords' words; 0 after LW0001 at ANode (reported once). A slot or a blob holding
    // such a value makes it where it is declared, so a type that cannot be mapped is
    // reported there
    hidden method DoManagedMapData(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LWords: ref Int64List;
      LAddresses: ref Int64List;
    begin
      if self.FManagedMapOf[AType] <> 0 then
        if self.FManagedMapOf[AType] < 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return self.FManagedMapOf[AType];
      end;
      self.FManagedMapOf[AType] := -1;
      LWords := ref Int64List();
      LAddresses := ref Int64List();
      if not self.DoMapWords(AType, ANode, LWords, ref Int64List(), LAddresses) then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.FManagedMapOf[AType] := self.DoWordsData(ADAM_LOWERING_MANAGED_MAP_SYMBOL, LWords, LAddresses, ANode);
      return self.FManagedMapOf[AType];
    end;

    // The read-only data of the element map of the canonical dynamic array type AType, made
    // the first time (FElementMapOf): DoElementWords' words; 0 after LW0001 at ANode
    // (reported once: an element type whose values cannot be mapped)
    hidden method DoElementMapData(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LWords: ref Int64List;
      LAddresses: ref Int64List;
    begin
      if self.FElementMapOf[AType] <> 0 then
        if self.FElementMapOf[AType] < 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return self.FElementMapOf[AType];
      end;
      self.FElementMapOf[AType] := -1;
      LWords := ref Int64List();
      LAddresses := ref Int64List();
      if not self.DoElementWords(AType, ANode, LWords, ref Int64List(), LAddresses) then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.FElementMapOf[AType] := self.DoWordsData(ADAM_LOWERING_ELEMENT_MAP_SYMBOL, LWords, LAddresses, ANode);
      return self.FElementMapOf[AType];
    end;

    // The address of the element map of the canonical dynamic array type AType
    // (DoElementMapData), at ANode; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoElementMap(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LData: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      LData := self.DoElementMapData(AType, ANode);
      if LData = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := LData;
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // The address of the managed map of the canonical type AType (DoManagedMapData), at
    // ANode; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoManagedMap(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LData: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      LData := self.DoManagedMapData(AType, ANode);
      if LData = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := LData;
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // The end function of the object type AType, which declares no done while its parts
    // end by one (RefRelease calls one routine through the descriptor): internal, taking
    // the object's address; its body (DoEndParts) is lowered last (DoEndBodies), as the
    // lowering of the routine whose ref new asked for it is still under way
    hidden method DoEndFunction(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LFunction: int64;
    begin
      LFunction := self.FModule.AddFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_REF_END_SYMBOL + IntToStr(self.FEndFunctions.Count),
        IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Internal := true;
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.AddParam(IrType.Pointer);
      self.FEndFunctions.Add(LFunction);
      self.FEndTypes.Add(AType);
      self.FEndNodes.Add(ANode);
      return LFunction;
    end;

    // Every end function's body (DoEndFunction: the object's address, its parts ended by
    // DoEndParts, which calls the parts' dones directly and makes no descriptor, the
    // return), every element routine's (DoElementBody), every task end's (DoTaskEndBody)
    // and every forward's (DoForwardBody, I4), each in a fresh function state, until none is
    // left: a body may ask for more (an element map or a descriptor it makes)
    hidden method DoEndBodies();
    var
      LObject: int64;
      LRef: int64;
      LElement: int64;
      LTask: int64;
    begin
      LRef := 0;
      LElement := 0;
      LTask := 0;
      while (LRef < self.FEndFunctions.Count) or (LElement < self.FElementFunctions.Count) or
        (LTask < self.FTaskEndFunctions.Count) or (self.FForwardsDone < self.FForwardFunctions.Count) do
        if self.FForwardsDone < self.FForwardFunctions.Count then
          self.DoForwardBodies();
          skip;
        end;
        if LRef < self.FEndFunctions.Count then
          self.FFunction := self.FEndFunctions[LRef];
          self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
          self.DoStartManaged();
          LObject := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Pointer, self.FEndNodes[LRef]);
          self.FModule.InstrAt(LObject).Imm := 0;
          self.DoEndParts(LObject, self.FEndTypes[LRef], self.FEndNodes[LRef]);
          if not self.DoEnded() then
            self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, self.FEndNodes[LRef]);
          end;
          LRef := LRef + 1;
        else
          if LElement < self.FElementFunctions.Count then
            self.DoElementBody(LElement);
            LElement := LElement + 1;
          else
            self.DoTaskEndBody(LTask);
            LTask := LTask + 1;
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The read-only data of the ref descriptor of the object type AType, made the first
    // time (FDescriptorOf): System.Runtime's layout, its size, the address of the function
    // that ends it (an address word: its done's, its end function's when it declares none
    // while its parts end by one, DoEndFunction; 0 when nothing ends), then its managed
    // map (DoMapWords, its element words counted from the map's own start). 0 after LW0001
    // at ANode (reported once: a part whose type cannot be mapped or ended)
    hidden method DoRefDescriptorData(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LDone: int64;
      LFunction: int64;
      LWords: ref Int64List;
      LAddresses: ref Int64List;
      LData: int64;
    begin
      if self.FDescriptorOf[AType] <> 0 then
        if self.FDescriptorOf[AType] < 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return self.FDescriptorOf[AType];
      end;
      self.FDescriptorOf[AType] := -1;
      LDone := self.DoOwnMember(AType, NodeKind.DoneDecl);
      LFunction := 0;
      if LDone <> 0 then
        LFunction := self.FFunctionOf[LDone];
        if LFunction = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      if (LDone = 0) and self.DoNeedsEnd(AType) then
        LFunction := self.DoEndFunction(AType, ANode);
      end;
      // the size and the done take the first two words: the map's element words count
      // from the map's own start (DoMapWords' start), word 2
      LWords := ref Int64List();
      LWords.Add(TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType));
      LWords.Add(0);
      LAddresses := ref Int64List();
      if not self.DoMapWords(AType, ANode, LWords, ref Int64List(), LAddresses) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LData := self.DoHelperData(ADAM_LOWERING_REF_DESCRIPTOR_SYMBOL,
        8, ANode);
      self.DoAddLe64(LData, LWords[0]);
      if LFunction = 0 then
        self.DoAddLe64(LData, 0);
      else
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddAddress(self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Symbol, 0);
      end;
      self.DoAddWords(LData, LWords, 2, LAddresses);
      self.FDescriptorOf[AType] := LData;
      return LData;
    end;

    // The ref new expression AId (`ref T(...)`, BNF sec 6): a new block for T (RefNew with
    // T's ref descriptor, its object zeroed), the object built by the init SEM picked
    // (DoBuildObject, the arguments AId's own), the block a reference kept in AId's hidden
    // slot (DoTemporaries; what an earlier pass left there released first); that block, 0
    // after LW0001
    hidden method DoRefNew(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LObject: int64;
      LData: int64;
      LDescriptor: int64;
      LBlock: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      LType := TargetOf(self.FTree, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType);
      if (LType = 0) or (ClassOf(self.FTree, LType) <> TypeClass.ObjectType) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LData := self.DoRefDescriptorData(LType, AId);
      if LData = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LDescriptor := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LDescriptor).Link := LData;
      LBlock := self.DoCallRuntimeSiteOne(RuntimeRoutine.RefNew, LDescriptor, AId,
        TypeText(self.FTree, LType));
      if LBlock = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LSlot := self.DoTempSlot(AId);
      if not self.DoReleaseAt(LSlot, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType, AId) then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoStore(LSlot, LBlock, AId);
      LObject := self.DoByteOffset(LBlock, ADAM_LOWERING_REF_HEADER, AId);
      if not self.DoBuildObject(LObject, LType, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedCallee, AId, NodeRole.Argument, AId) then
        return 0;
      end;
      return LBlock;
    end;

    // The offset into a task's object of the result of a call whose result type is AResult
    // (BNF sec 4 task type): past the runtime's words (ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_WORDS), at the
    // result's alignment. It depends on the result's type alone, so `await` finds it from
    // the task's type wherever the task was started
    hidden method DoTaskResultOffset(const AResult: int64): int64;
    begin
      return AlignUp(ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_WORDS, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AResult));
    end;

    // The call the async expression AAsync starts (its operand, into ACall), the routine or
    // the method it calls (ADecl; 0 for a routine value) and the signature that call runs
    // (ASig: the routine, the method, or the routine value's type's signature); false after
    // LW0001 at AAsync for a callee that is none of those
    hidden method DoAsyncTarget(const AAsync: int64; var ACall: int64; var ADecl: int64;
      var ASig: int64): bool;
    var
      LCallee: int64;
      LType: int64;
    begin
      ACall := self.FTree.FirstOf(AAsync, NodeRole.Operand);
      LCallee := self.FTree.FirstOf(ACall, NodeRole.Callee);
      ADecl := 0;
      ASig := 0;
      // a method's call (T1): its object is reached at the async (DoTaskMethod)
      if self.DoMethodMember(ACall) <> 0 then
        ADecl := self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl;
        ASig := ADecl;
        return true;
      end;
      if NameKindOf(self.FTree, LCallee) = NodeKind.NameExpression then
        ADecl := self.DoCalled(LCallee);
      end;
      if ADecl <> 0 then
        ASig := ADecl;
      else
        if not self.DoIsRoutineValue(LCallee) then
          self.DoRefuse(AAsync, "async of " + self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(ACall));
          return false;
        end;
        LType := self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedType;
        if self.DoSignatureOf(LType, AAsync) = 0 then
          return false;
        end;
        ASig := self.FTree[LType].ResolvedDecl;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The member access the call ACall runs a method through (its callee naming a method:
    // DoMethodCall's, an async's, T1); 0 for a routine's or a routine value's call
    hidden const method DoMethodMember(const ACall: int64): int64;
    var
      LCallee: int64;
    begin
      LCallee := self.FTree.FirstOf(ACall, NodeRole.Callee);
      if (self.FTree[LCallee].Kind = NodeKind.MemberExpression) and (self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl <> 0) and
        (self.FTree[self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl].Kind = NodeKind.MethodDecl) then
        return LCallee;
      end;
      return 0;
    end;

    // The ref a method task holds (T1): the receiver of the method call's member access
    // AMember, its parentheses off, when it is a ref (ref T, ref I: Semantics' SM0708 leaves
    // only that or a ptr); 0 through a ptr (`P->M()`, `P^.M()`: the caller keeps the object)
    hidden const method DoTaskHolder(const AMember: int64): int64;
    var
      LRoot: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AMember].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Arrow) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LRoot := self.DoArgRoot(self.FTree.FirstOf(AMember, NodeRole.Operand));
      if self.DoIsRefValue(self.DoUsedType(LRoot)) then
        return LRoot;
      end;
      return 0;
    end;

    // True when a task's object holds the code its call ACall of ADecl runs (T1): a routine
    // value's call (ADecl 0: the value) or a dispatched method's (an interface's or a
    // vtable's, DoIsVtableCall: the function its object's table names, read at the async)
    hidden const method DoTaskCoded(const ACall: int64; const ADecl: int64): bool;
    var
      LMember: int64;
    begin
      if ADecl = 0 then
        return true;
      end;
      LMember := self.DoMethodMember(ACall);
      return (LMember <> 0) and (self.DoIsInterfaceMember(ADecl) or self.DoIsVtableCall(LMember, ADecl));
    end;

    // The count of the words a task's object holds before its parameters' copies for the
    // call ACall of ADecl (T1), in this order: the code (DoTaskCoded), a method's self, the
    // ref that holds a method's object (DoTaskHolder)
    hidden const method DoTaskHeads(const ACall: int64; const ADecl: int64): int64;
    var
      LMember: int64;
      LCount: int64;
    begin
      LCount := 0;
      if self.DoTaskCoded(ACall, ADecl) then
        LCount := 1;
      end;
      LMember := self.DoMethodMember(ACall);
      if LMember <> 0 then
        LCount := LCount + 1;
        if self.DoTaskHolder(LMember) <> 0 then
          LCount := LCount + 1;
        end;
      end;
      return LCount;
    end;

    // The count of the call ACall's extra arguments past the fixed parameters of the
    // variadic signature ASig (T1: each copied into the task's object at DoTaskExtraType);
    // 0 for a signature that is not variadic
    hidden const method DoTaskExtras(const ACall: int64; const ASig: int64): int64;
    var
      LCount: int64;
    begin
      if not self.FTree[ASig].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Variadic) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LCount := self.FTree.CountOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument) - self.FTree.CountOf(ASig, NodeRole.Param);
      if LCount < 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return LCount;
    end;

    // The canonical type a task copies the extra argument AArg of a variadic call at: its
    // own (SEM converts none, BNF sec 4), nil as an untyped ptr (DoPackType)
    hidden const method DoTaskExtraType(const AArg: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoPackType(self.DoUsedType(AArg));
    end;

    // The part AMark of a task's or a generator's object marked built at ANode (G1c3 /
    // G1c4): AMark (one past the part's place in the build order) stored into the built
    // word at AWord (an address in the object). The object is built part by part after its
    // block exists, so a raise part way releases it with only some parts built
    hidden method DoMarkBuilt(const AWord: int64; const AMark: int64; const ANode: int64);
    begin
      self.DoStore(AWord, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, AMark, ANode), ANode);
    end;

    // The test that the part AMark (DoMarkBuilt) of an object was built at ANode: its built
    // word at AWord at least AMark
    hidden method DoBuiltTest(const AWord: int64; const AMark: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LBuilt: int64;
    begin
      LBuilt := self.DoLoad(AWord, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      return self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.SGreaterEqual, LBuilt, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, AMark, ANode),
        ANode);
    end;

    // True when the object of a task whose call ACall runs the signature ASig carries a
    // built word (G1c4, last in DoTaskLayout): a parameter's or an extra argument's copy
    // ends by a done. Its arguments are evaluated and copied after its block exists
    // (DoAsync), so a raise part way releases the block with only some copies made: the
    // end ends only those (DoTaskEndBuilt). Each such copy's mark is one past its place in
    // the build order (the parameters, then the extra arguments)
    hidden const method DoTaskBuilt(const ACall: int64; const ASig: int64): bool;
    var
      LParams: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LParams := self.FTree.CountOf(ASig, NodeRole.Param);
      for LI := 0 to LParams - 1 do
        if self.DoNeedsEnd(self.DoDeclType(self.FTree.NthOf(ASig, NodeRole.Param, LI))) then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.DoTaskExtras(ACall, ASig) - 1 do
        if self.DoNeedsEnd(self.DoTaskExtraType(self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, LParams + LI))) then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // The index in DoTaskLayout's offsets of the built word (DoTaskBuilt) of a task whose
    // call ACall of ADecl runs ASig: past the heads, the copies and the owns word
    hidden const method DoTaskBuiltIndex(const ACall: int64; const ADecl: int64; const ASig: int64): int64;
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LAt := self.DoTaskHeads(ACall, ADecl) + self.FTree.CountOf(ASig, NodeRole.Param) +
        self.DoTaskExtras(ACall, ASig);
      if self.DoTaskOwnsArgs(ASig) then
        LAt := LAt + 1;
      end;
      return LAt;
    end;

    // The value object of the canonical type AType at the offset AOffset of a task's object
    // AObject ended at ANode when it was built (its mark AMark at the built word at offset
    // ABuilt, DoBuiltTest; ABuilt below 0: the object has none, always built) and, when
    // AOwned is not 0, while AOwned holds (a copy the call takes: not taken yet). The owned
    // test comes first, the built word read only under it; false after LW0001
    hidden method DoTaskEndBuilt(const AObject: int64; const AOffset: int64; const AType: int64;
      const AOwned: int64; const ABuilt: int64; const AMark: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LTest: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
    begin
      LBody := 0;
      LJoin := 0;
      if AOwned <> 0 then
        LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
        LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
        self.DoBranchOn(AOwned, LBody, LJoin, ANode);
        self.FBlock := LBody;
      end;
      LTest := 0;
      if ABuilt >= 0 then
        LTest := self.DoBuiltTest(self.DoByteOffset(AObject, ABuilt, ANode), AMark, ANode);
      end;
      if not self.DoTaskEndPart(AObject, AOffset, AType, LTest, ANode) then
        return false;
      end;
      if AOwned <> 0 then
        self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, ANode);
        self.FBlock := LJoin;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The layout of the object of the task the async expression AAsync starts, its call
    // ACall of ADecl (0: a routine value) running the signature ASig: each part's offset
    // into the object added to AOffsets (the heads, DoTaskHeads: the code, a method's self,
    // the ref holding its object; then each parameter's copy, each extra argument's
    // (DoTaskExtras), then the word that says the call has not taken its copies yet when
    // the task may end some, DoTaskOwnsArgs, then the built word when it has one,
    // DoTaskBuilt), past the runtime's words and the result (DoTaskResultOffset); the
    // object's size, a multiple of 8
    hidden method DoTaskLayout(const AAsync: int64; const ACall: int64; const ADecl: int64;
      const ASig: int64; const AOffsets: ref Int64List): int64;
    var
      LResult: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LParams: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LAt := ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_WORDS;
      LResult := self.FTree[self.FTree[AAsync].ResolvedType].ResolvedType;
      if LResult <> 0 then
        LAt := self.DoTaskResultOffset(LResult) + TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LResult);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.DoTaskHeads(ACall, ADecl) - 1 do
        LAt := AlignUp(LAt, self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
        AOffsets.Add(LAt);
        LAt := LAt + self.FTarget.PointerSize();
      end;
      LParams := self.FTree.CountOf(ASig, NodeRole.Param);
      for LI := 0 to LParams - 1 do
        LType := self.DoDeclType(self.FTree.NthOf(ASig, NodeRole.Param, LI));
        LAt := AlignUp(LAt, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType));
        AOffsets.Add(LAt);
        LAt := LAt + TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.DoTaskExtras(ACall, ASig) - 1 do
        LType := self.DoTaskExtraType(self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, LParams + LI));
        LAt := AlignUp(LAt, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType));
        AOffsets.Add(LAt);
        LAt := LAt + TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType);
      end;
      if self.DoTaskOwnsArgs(ASig) then
        LAt := AlignUp(LAt, 8);
        AOffsets.Add(LAt);
        LAt := LAt + 8;
      end;
      if self.DoTaskBuilt(ACall, ASig) then
        LAt := AlignUp(LAt, 8);
        AOffsets.Add(LAt);
        LAt := LAt + 8;
      end;
      return AlignUp(LAt, 8);
    end;

    // True when the call of the signature ASig takes the value its parameter AParam is
    // given (DoOwnParam: a value parameter, by value or by copy, is the callee's to end; a
    // const or a var one is not)
    hidden const method DoParamTaken(const AParam: int64): bool;
    begin
      return (not self.FTree[AParam].HasFlag(NodeFlag.ConstParam)) and
        (not (self.FByRef[AParam] and not self.FByCopy[AParam]));
    end;

    // True when a task's call of the signature ASig takes a copy that ends by a done
    // (DoParamTaken, DoNeedsEnd): its object then says whether the call has taken them
    // (DoTaskLayout's owns word, 1 from DoAsync, before its first argument, until the entry
    // runs the call), so a call that never ran (TaskStart: no thread, or a raise while its
    // arguments were made, G1c4) leaves them for the task's end (DoTaskEndBody)
    hidden const method DoTaskOwnsArgs(const ASig: int64): bool;
    var
      LParam: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ASig, NodeRole.Param) - 1 do
        LParam := self.FTree.NthOf(ASig, NodeRole.Param, LI);
        if self.DoParamTaken(LParam) and self.DoNeedsEnd(self.DoDeclType(LParam)) then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // True when the object of a task the async expression AAsync starts (its call ACall of
    // the signature ASig) holds a value object that ends by a done: its result, or a copy of
    // an argument, an extra one's too (DoNeedsEnd); its descriptor's done is then its own
    // task end (DoTaskEndFunction), not the runtime's TaskDone
    hidden const method DoTaskEnds(const AAsync: int64; const ACall: int64; const ASig: int64): bool;
    var
      LResult: int64;
      LParams: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LResult := self.FTree[self.FTree[AAsync].ResolvedType].ResolvedType;
      if (LResult <> 0) and self.DoNeedsEnd(LResult) then
        return true;
      end;
      LParams := self.FTree.CountOf(ASig, NodeRole.Param);
      for LI := 0 to LParams - 1 do
        if self.DoNeedsEnd(self.DoDeclType(self.FTree.NthOf(ASig, NodeRole.Param, LI))) then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.DoTaskExtras(ACall, ASig) - 1 do
        if self.DoNeedsEnd(self.DoTaskExtraType(self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, LParams + LI))) then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // A new task end function for the async expression AAsync (internal, taking the task's
    // object: its descriptor's done); its body (DoTaskEndBody) is lowered last
    // (DoEndBodies); its function id
    hidden method DoTaskEndFunction(const AAsync: int64): int64;
    var
      LFunction: int64;
    begin
      LFunction := self.FModule.AddFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_END_SYMBOL + IntToStr(self.FTaskEndFunctions.Count),
        IrType.Void, AAsync);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Internal := true;
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.AddParam(IrType.Pointer);
      self.FTaskEndFunctions.Add(LFunction);
      self.FTaskEndNodes.Add(AAsync);
      return LFunction;
    end;

    // The value object of the canonical type AType at the offset AOffset of the task's
    // object AObject ended at ANode while ATest holds (0: always): a branch over the end
    // into a join where the current block goes on; false after LW0001
    hidden method DoTaskEndPart(const AObject: int64; const AOffset: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ATest: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LBody: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
    begin
      if ATest = 0 then
        return self.DoEndObject(self.DoByteOffset(AObject, AOffset, ANode), AType, ANode);
      end;
      LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(ATest, LBody, LJoin, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LBody;
      if not self.DoEndObject(self.DoByteOffset(AObject, AOffset, ANode), AType, ANode) then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LJoin;
      return true;
    end;

    // The body of the task end AIndex (DoTaskEndFunction): the task's object (its one
    // parameter) given to the runtime's TaskDone first (its call has ended by then), then,
    // the reverse of their build, its value objects that end by a done ended (DoTaskEnds):
    // the result once the call returned (the state ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_ENDED: a call that
    // raised stored none), the copies the call never takes (an extra argument's, DoParamTaken:
    // a const or a var parameter's), those it takes only while the call has not run
    // (DoTaskOwnsArgs' word); the return. RefRelease then releases the object's managed
    // values (its map: the ref holding a method's object too)
    hidden method DoTaskEndBody(const AIndex: int64);
    var
      LAsync: int64;
      LObject: int64;
      LCall: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
      LSig: int64;
      LOffsets: ref Int64List;
      LResult: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LParam: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LTest: int64;
      LOwned: int64;
      LExtras: int64;
      LArg: int64;
      LBuilt: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LAsync := self.FTaskEndNodes[AIndex];
      self.FFunction := self.FTaskEndFunctions[AIndex];
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoStartManaged();
      LObject := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Pointer, LAsync);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LObject).Imm := 0;
      // a generator's end: the runtime's GeneratorDone first, then its copies (DoGeneratorEnd)
      if self.FTree[LAsync].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Generator) then
        if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.GeneratorDone, LObject, 0, LAsync) = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        self.DoGeneratorEnd(LAsync, LObject);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.TaskDone, LObject, 0, LAsync) = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAsyncBlock(LAsync) then
        self.DoTaskBlockEnd(LAsync, LObject);
        return;
      end;
      if not self.DoAsyncTarget(LAsync, LCall, LDecl, LSig) then
        return;
      end;
      LOffsets := ref Int64List();
      self.DoTaskLayout(LAsync, LCall, LDecl, LSig, LOffsets);
      LFirst := self.DoTaskHeads(LCall, LDecl);
      LCount := self.FTree.CountOf(LSig, NodeRole.Param);
      LExtras := self.DoTaskExtras(LCall, LSig);
      LResult := self.FTree[self.FTree[LAsync].ResolvedType].ResolvedType;
      if (LResult <> 0) and self.DoNeedsEnd(LResult) then
        LTest := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.Equal,
          self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(LObject, ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_STATE_OFFSET, LAsync), IrType.Int64, LAsync),
          self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_ENDED, LAsync), LAsync);
        if not self.DoTaskEndPart(LObject, self.DoTaskResultOffset(LResult), LResult, LTest, LAsync) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      // the copies the call took end only when it never ran: the word says so; each copy
      // only once built (DoTaskBuilt: a raise while the arguments were made, G1c4)
      LBuilt := -1;
      if self.DoTaskBuilt(LCall, LSig) then
        LBuilt := LOffsets[self.DoTaskBuiltIndex(LCall, LDecl, LSig)];
      end;
      LOwned := 0;
      if self.DoTaskOwnsArgs(LSig) then
        LOwned := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.NotEqual,
          self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[LFirst + LCount + LExtras], LAsync), IrType.Int64, LAsync),
          self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, LAsync), LAsync);
      end;
      // an extra argument's copy is never the call's (it reads the copy in place)
      for LI := LExtras - 1 downto 0 do
        LArg := self.FTree.NthOf(LCall, NodeRole.Argument, LCount + LI);
        LType := self.DoTaskExtraType(LArg);
        if self.DoNeedsEnd(LType) then
          if not self.DoTaskEndBuilt(LObject, LOffsets[LFirst + LCount + LI], LType, 0, LBuilt,
            LCount + LI + 1, LAsync) then
            return;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      for LI := LCount - 1 downto 0 do
        LParam := self.FTree.NthOf(LSig, NodeRole.Param, LI);
        LType := self.DoDeclType(LParam);
        if self.DoNeedsEnd(LType) then
          LTest := 0;
          if self.DoParamTaken(LParam) then
            LTest := LOwned;
          end;
          if not self.DoTaskEndBuilt(LObject, LOffsets[LFirst + LI], LType, LTest, LBuilt, LI + 1, LAsync) then
            return;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      if not self.DoEnded() then
        self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, LAsync);
      end;
    end;

    // The read-only data of the task descriptor of the async expression AAsync (a ref
    // descriptor, System.Runtime's layout) whose call is ACall of ADecl (0: a routine
    // value) running ASig: the object's size ASize, the runtime's TaskDone as its done (or
    // its own end, DoTaskEnds), then the managed map over the object: the raise's text, the
    // result's values, the ref holding a method's object (DoTaskHolder: the last head),
    // each parameter's and extra argument's copy's at AOffsets (DoTaskLayout's; the code
    // and self, addresses, hold none); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoTaskDescriptorData(const AAsync: int64; const ACall: int64; const ADecl: int64;
      const ASig: int64; const AOffsets: ref Int64List; const ASize: int64): int64;
    var
      LDone: int64;
      LRuns: ref Int64List;
      LResult: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LParams: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LHolder: int64;
      LArg: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      // a task holding value objects that end by a done ends them by its own end, which
      // calls TaskDone first
      if self.DoTaskEnds(AAsync, ACall, ASig) then
        LDone := self.DoTaskEndFunction(AAsync);
      else
        LDone := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.TaskDone, AAsync);
        if LDone = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      LRuns := ref Int64List();
      self.DoAddRun(LRuns, ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_TEXT_OFFSET, 1, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), 0);
      LResult := self.FTree[self.FTree[AAsync].ResolvedType].ResolvedType;
      if (LResult <> 0) and (not self.DoManagedRuns(LResult, self.DoTaskResultOffset(LResult), LRuns, AAsync)) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LFirst := self.DoTaskHeads(ACall, ADecl);
      LMember := self.DoMethodMember(ACall);
      if LMember <> 0 then
        LHolder := self.DoTaskHolder(LMember);
        if (LHolder <> 0) and
          (not self.DoManagedRuns(self.DoUsedType(LHolder), AOffsets[LFirst - 1], LRuns, AAsync)) then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      LParams := self.FTree.CountOf(ASig, NodeRole.Param);
      for LI := 0 to LParams - 1 do
        if not self.DoManagedRuns(self.DoDeclType(self.FTree.NthOf(ASig, NodeRole.Param, LI)),
          AOffsets[LFirst + LI], LRuns, AAsync) then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.DoTaskExtras(ACall, ASig) - 1 do
        LArg := self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, LParams + LI);
        if not self.DoManagedRuns(self.DoTaskExtraType(LArg), AOffsets[LFirst + LParams + LI], LRuns, AAsync) then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      return self.DoTaskDescriptorWords(AAsync, LRuns, ASize, LDone);
    end;

    // The read-only data of the task descriptor of the async expression AAsync from its
    // object's size ASize, its done's function ADone and the managed runs ARuns over the
    // object (DoTaskDescriptorData's, DoTaskBlockData's); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoTaskDescriptorWords(const AAsync: int64; const ARuns: ref Int64List;
      const ASize: int64; const ADone: int64): int64;
    var
      LWords: ref Int64List;
      LAddresses: ref Int64List;
      LData: int64;
    begin
      // the size and the done take the first two words: the map's element words count
      // from the map's own start, word 2
      LWords := ref Int64List();
      LWords.Add(ASize);
      LWords.Add(0);
      LAddresses := ref Int64List();
      if not self.DoRunWords(ARuns, AAsync, LWords, ref Int64List(), LAddresses) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LData := self.DoHelperData(ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_DESCRIPTOR_SYMBOL,
        8, AAsync);
      self.DoAddLe64(LData, LWords[0]);
      self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddAddress(self.FModule.FunctionAt(ADone).Symbol, 0);
      self.DoAddWords(LData, LWords, 2, LAddresses);
      return LData;
    end;

    // A new entry function for the async expression AAsync (internal, taking the task's
    // object: TaskRun's argument); its body (DoTaskBody) is lowered last (DoDeferredBodies), as
    // the lowering of the routine holding AAsync is still under way
    hidden method DoTaskEntry(const AAsync: int64): int64;
    var
      LFunction: int64;
    begin
      LFunction := self.FModule.AddFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_ENTRY_SYMBOL + IntToStr(self.FTaskEntries.Count),
        IrType.Void, AAsync);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Internal := true;
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.AddParam(IrType.Pointer);
      self.FTaskEntries.Add(LFunction);
      self.FTaskNodes.Add(AAsync);
      return LFunction;
    end;

    // The argument AArg copied into its parameter's place AAddress in a new task's object
    // (zeroed by RefNew), as a value of the parameter's canonical type AType: a managed one
    // with a holder added (DoStoreManaged), an aggregate copied (DoCopyValue: a holder added
    // to each value it holds, a value object by its type's copy) or, a value object that is
    // a call's result, moved in (DoMoveObject: its temporary no longer live), any other
    // value stored; false after LW0001
    hidden method DoTaskArgument(const AArg: int64; const AType: int64; const AAddress: int64): bool;
    var
      LValue: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LFrom: int64;
    begin
      if self.DoIsManaged(AType) then
        LValue := self.DoValue(AArg);
        if LValue = 0 then
          return false;
        end;
        return self.DoStoreManaged(AAddress, LValue, AType, AArg) <> 0;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(AType) then
        LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(AArg);
        if LSource = 0 then
          return false;
        end;
        LFrom := self.DoMoveSource(AArg);
        if self.DoHasLifetime(AType) and (LFrom <> 0) and self.DoIsCallSite(LFrom) then
          self.DoMoveObject(AAddress, LSource, LFrom, AType, AArg);
          return true;
        end;
        return self.DoCopyValue(AAddress, LSource, AType, AArg);
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(AArg);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoStore(AAddress, LValue, AArg);
      return true;
    end;

    // The async expression AId (`async F(..)`, BNF sec 6): a new task block (RefNew with the
    // call site's task descriptor, DoTaskDescriptorData) kept in AId's hidden slot
    // (DoTemporaries; what an earlier pass left there released first), its entry
    // (DoTaskEntry) written into it, for a routine value that value, for a method its
    // object (DoTaskMethod: C++17 orders the object before the arguments), then each
    // argument copied into its parameter's place (DoTaskArgument: the caller evaluates and
    // copies them), an extra one at its own type (DoTaskExtraType), then its thread started
    // (TaskStart); that block, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAsync(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LCall: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
      LSig: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LParams: int64;
      LExtras: int64;
      LArg: int64;
      LOffsets: ref Int64List;
      LSize: int64;
      LData: int64;
      LBlock: int64;
      LObject: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LParam: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LBuilt: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if self.DoIsAsyncBlock(AId) then
        return self.DoAsyncBlock(AId);
      end;
      if not self.DoAsyncTarget(AId, LCall, LDecl, LSig) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LOffsets := ref Int64List();
      LSize := self.DoTaskLayout(AId, LCall, LDecl, LSig, LOffsets);
      LData := self.DoTaskDescriptorData(AId, LCall, LDecl, LSig, LOffsets, LSize);
      if LData = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LObject := self.DoTaskNew(AId, LData, LBlock);
      if LObject = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LFirst := self.DoTaskHeads(LCall, LDecl);
      LMember := self.DoMethodMember(LCall);
      if LMember <> 0 then
        if not self.DoTaskMethod(AId, LMember, LDecl, LObject, LOffsets) then
          return 0;
        end;
      else
        if LDecl = 0 then
          LValue := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(LCall, NodeRole.Callee));
          if LValue = 0 then
            return 0;
          end;
          LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[0], AId);
          self.DoStore(LAddress, LValue, AId);
        end;
      end;
      LParams := self.FTree.CountOf(LSig, NodeRole.Param);
      LExtras := self.DoTaskExtras(LCall, LSig);
      // the copies are the task's until its entry gives them to the call (DoTaskOwnsArgs),
      // from before the first one: a raise while they are made leaves those built for the
      // task's end (G1c4)
      if self.DoTaskOwnsArgs(LSig) then
        LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[LFirst + LParams + LExtras], AId);
        self.DoStore(LAddress, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 1, AId), AId);
      end;
      // each copy that ends by a done marked built once made (DoTaskBuilt)
      LBuilt := 0;
      if self.DoTaskBuilt(LCall, LSig) then
        LBuilt := self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[self.DoTaskBuiltIndex(LCall, LDecl, LSig)], AId);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LParams - 1 do
        LParam := self.FTree.NthOf(LSig, NodeRole.Param, LI);
        LType := self.DoDeclType(LParam);
        LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[LFirst + LI], AId);
        if not self.DoTaskArgument(self.FTree.NthOf(LCall, NodeRole.Argument, LI), LType, LAddress) then
          return 0;
        end;
        if (LBuilt <> 0) and self.DoNeedsEnd(LType) then
          self.DoMarkBuilt(LBuilt, LI + 1, AId);
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LExtras - 1 do
        LArg := self.FTree.NthOf(LCall, NodeRole.Argument, LParams + LI);
        LType := self.DoTaskExtraType(LArg);
        LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[LFirst + LParams + LI], AId);
        if not self.DoTaskArgument(LArg, LType, LAddress) then
          return 0;
        end;
        if (LBuilt <> 0) and self.DoNeedsEnd(LType) then
          self.DoMarkBuilt(LBuilt, LParams + LI + 1, AId);
        end;
      end;
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.TaskStart, LBlock, 0, AId) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return LBlock;
    end;

    // A new task block for the async expression AId (RefNew over its task descriptor's data
    // AData) kept in AId's hidden slot (DoTemporaries; what an earlier pass left there
    // released first), its entry (DoTaskEntry) written into it: the task's object (past the
    // ref header), ABlock the block; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoTaskNew(const AId: int64; const AData: int64; var ABlock: int64): int64;
    var
      LDescriptor: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LObject: int64;
      LEntry: int64;
    begin
      LDescriptor := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LDescriptor).Link := AData;
      ABlock := self.DoCallRuntimeSiteOne(RuntimeRoutine.RefNew, LDescriptor, AId, "task");
      if ABlock = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LSlot := self.DoTempSlot(AId);
      if not self.DoReleaseAt(LSlot, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType, AId) then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoStore(LSlot, ABlock, AId);
      LObject := self.DoByteOffset(ABlock, ADAM_LOWERING_REF_HEADER, AId);
      LEntry := self.DoEmit(IrOp.CodeAddress, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LEntry).Link := self.DoTaskEntry(AId);
      self.DoStore(self.DoByteOffset(LObject, ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_ENTRY_OFFSET, AId), LEntry, AId);
      return LObject;
    end;

    // True when the async expression AAsync is an async block (`async begin .. end`, T4): a
    // plain task over its block, no call
    hidden const method DoIsAsyncBlock(const AAsync: int64): bool;
    begin
      return self.FTree.FirstOf(AAsync, NodeRole.Body) <> 0;
    end;

    // True when the Capture ACapture of an async block (T4) has a copy in its task's object:
    // its variable has storage (a folded constant has none: read as it always is)
    hidden const method DoTaskCopies(const ACapture: int64): bool;
    begin
      return self.FSlotOf[self.FTree[ACapture].ResolvedDecl] <> 0;
    end;

    // The layout of the object of the task the async block AAsync starts (T4): past the
    // runtime's words (a plain task: no result), each Capture's copy (DoTaskCopies) at its
    // variable's canonical type, its offset added to AOffsets (0 for one with none), then the
    // built word when a copy ends by a done (DoTaskBlockEnds, G1c4: each such copy's mark one
    // past its Capture's index; a raise in a copy releases the block with only some made);
    // the object's size, a multiple of 8
    hidden method DoTaskBlockLayout(const AAsync: int64; const AOffsets: ref Int64List): int64;
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LCapture: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LAt := ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_WORDS;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AAsync, NodeRole.Capture) - 1 do
        LCapture := self.FTree.NthOf(AAsync, NodeRole.Capture, LI);
        if not self.DoTaskCopies(LCapture) then
          AOffsets.Add(0);
          skip;
        end;
        LType := self.DoDeclType(self.FTree[LCapture].ResolvedDecl);
        LAt := AlignUp(LAt, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType));
        AOffsets.Add(LAt);
        LAt := LAt + TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType);
      end;
      if self.DoTaskBlockEnds(AAsync) then
        LAt := AlignUp(LAt, 8);
        AOffsets.Add(LAt);
        LAt := LAt + 8;
      end;
      return AlignUp(LAt, 8);
    end;

    // True when the object of the task the async block AAsync starts (T4) holds a copy that
    // ends by a done (DoNeedsEnd): its descriptor's done is then its own task end
    // (DoTaskEndFunction, DoTaskBlockEnd)
    hidden const method DoTaskBlockEnds(const AAsync: int64): bool;
    var
      LCapture: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AAsync, NodeRole.Capture) - 1 do
        LCapture := self.FTree.NthOf(AAsync, NodeRole.Capture, LI);
        if self.DoTaskCopies(LCapture) and
          self.DoNeedsEnd(self.DoDeclType(self.FTree[LCapture].ResolvedDecl)) then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // The read-only data of the task descriptor of the async block AAsync (T4), its object
    // ASize bytes with its copies at AOffsets (DoTaskBlockLayout): the runtime's TaskDone as
    // its done (or its own end, DoTaskBlockEnds), the managed map over the raise's text and
    // each copy; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoTaskBlockData(const AAsync: int64; const AOffsets: ref Int64List;
      const ASize: int64): int64;
    var
      LDone: int64;
      LRuns: ref Int64List;
      LCapture: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if self.DoTaskBlockEnds(AAsync) then
        LDone := self.DoTaskEndFunction(AAsync);
      else
        LDone := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.TaskDone, AAsync);
        if LDone = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      LRuns := ref Int64List();
      self.DoAddRun(LRuns, ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_TEXT_OFFSET, 1, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), 0);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AAsync, NodeRole.Capture) - 1 do
        LCapture := self.FTree.NthOf(AAsync, NodeRole.Capture, LI);
        if self.DoTaskCopies(LCapture) and
          (not self.DoManagedRuns(self.DoDeclType(self.FTree[LCapture].ResolvedDecl), AOffsets[LI], LRuns, AAsync)) then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      return self.DoTaskDescriptorWords(AAsync, LRuns, ASize, LDone);
    end;

    // The value of the canonical type AType at the address ASource (a variable's storage)
    // copied into the zeroed place ADest of a new task's object at ANode, as an argument is
    // (DoTaskArgument): a managed one with a holder added (DoStoreManaged), an aggregate by
    // DoCopyValue (a holder added to each value it holds, a value object by its type's copy),
    // any other value loaded and stored; false after LW0001
    hidden method DoTaskCopy(const ASource: int64; const AType: int64; const ADest: int64;
      const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LIr: IrType;
    begin
      if self.DoIsManaged(AType) then
        return self.DoStoreManaged(ADest, self.DoLoad(ASource, IrType.Pointer, ANode), AType, ANode) <> 0;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(AType) then
        return self.DoCopyValue(ADest, ASource, AType, ANode);
      end;
      LIr := self.DoTypeAt(AType, ANode);
      if LIr = IrType.Void then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoStore(ADest, self.DoLoad(ASource, LIr, ANode), ANode);
      return true;
    end;

    // The async block AId (`async begin .. end`, BNF sec 6, T4): a new task (DoTaskNew over
    // its descriptor, DoTaskBlockData), each variable, constant and parameter of the routine
    // the block reads (its Capture children) copied into its object here, at the async
    // (DoTaskCopy: the task may outlive the routine), then its thread started (TaskStart);
    // that block, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAsyncBlock(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LOffsets: ref Int64List;
      LSize: int64;
      LData: int64;
      LBlock: int64;
      LObject: int64;
      LCapture: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LOffsets := ref Int64List();
      LSize := self.DoTaskBlockLayout(AId, LOffsets);
      LData := self.DoTaskBlockData(AId, LOffsets, LSize);
      if LData = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LObject := self.DoTaskNew(AId, LData, LBlock);
      if LObject = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AId, NodeRole.Capture) - 1 do
        LCapture := self.FTree.NthOf(AId, NodeRole.Capture, LI);
        if not self.DoTaskCopies(LCapture) then
          skip;
        end;
        LDecl := self.FTree[LCapture].ResolvedDecl;
        LType := self.DoDeclType(LDecl);
        LSource := self.DoDeclAddress(LDecl, LCapture);
        if not self.DoTaskCopy(LSource, LType, self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[LI], LCapture), LCapture) then
          return 0;
        end;
        // marked built once made (DoTaskBlockLayout's built word, last)
        if self.DoNeedsEnd(LType) then
          self.DoMarkBuilt(self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[LOffsets.Count - 1], LCapture), LI + 1, LCapture);
        end;
      end;
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.TaskStart, LBlock, 0, AId) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return LBlock;
    end;

    // The body of the entry of the async block AAsync (T4; DoTaskEntry, in its fresh function
    // state): the task's object (its one parameter); each Capture's variable reached through
    // its copy there (a slot holding the copy's address, the variable by reference while
    // this body is lowered: FSlotOf / FByRef, given back after; SEM lets no write reach it);
    // the block's temporaries and statement locals (DoCodeTemporaries over the async,
    // FBodyRoot); then its statements, the end releasing what the body holds and returning.
    // A raise leaves it for TaskRun's catching scope (the body's cleanup releases on the way)
    hidden method DoTaskBlockBody(const AAsync: int64);
    var
      LObject: int64;
      LOffsets: ref Int64List;
      LWord: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LCapture: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LSavedSlot: ref Int64List;
      LSavedByRef: BoolArray;
      LSavedByCopy: BoolArray;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      self.FRoutine := 0;
      self.FResultSlot := 0;
      self.FSelfSlot := 0;
      self.FVarargsSlot := 0;
      self.FPackSlot := 0;
      LObject := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Pointer, AAsync);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LObject).Imm := 0;
      LOffsets := ref Int64List();
      self.DoTaskBlockLayout(AAsync, LOffsets);
      LWord := self.FTarget.PointerSize();
      LCount := self.FTree.CountOf(AAsync, NodeRole.Capture);
      LSavedSlot := ref Int64List();
      setlength(LSavedByRef, LCount);
      setlength(LSavedByCopy, LCount);
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LCapture := self.FTree.NthOf(AAsync, NodeRole.Capture, LI);
        LDecl := self.FTree[LCapture].ResolvedDecl;
        LSavedSlot.Add(self.FSlotOf[LDecl]);
        LSavedByRef[LI] := self.FByRef[LDecl];
        LSavedByCopy[LI] := self.FByCopy[LDecl];
        if self.DoTaskCopies(LCapture) then
          LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(LCapture, LWord, self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
          self.DoStore(LSlot, self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[LI], LCapture), LCapture);
          self.FSlotOf[LDecl] := LSlot;
          self.FByRef[LDecl] := true;
          self.FByCopy[LDecl] := false;
        end;
      end;
      self.FBodyRoot := AAsync;
      self.DoCodeTemporaries(AAsync);
      self.FBodyRoot := 0;
      LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoJumpTo(LBody, AAsync);
      if self.DoArm(LBody, self.FTree.FirstOf(AAsync, NodeRole.Body), NodeRole.Statement) then
        self.DoReleaseManaged(AAsync);
        self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, AAsync);
      end;
      self.DoCleanupScopes(AAsync, self.DoLastBlock());
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LDecl := self.FTree[self.FTree.NthOf(AAsync, NodeRole.Capture, LI)].ResolvedDecl;
        self.FSlotOf[LDecl] := LSavedSlot[LI];
        self.FByRef[LDecl] := LSavedByRef[LI];
        self.FByCopy[LDecl] := LSavedByCopy[LI];
      end;
    end;

    // The rest of the task end of the async block AAsync (T4; DoTaskEndBody, after
    // TaskDone) over its object AObject: the reverse of their build, each copy that ends by a
    // done ended (DoTaskBlockEnds) once built (its mark, G1c4); the return. RefRelease then releases the object's
    // managed values (its map)
    hidden method DoTaskBlockEnd(const AAsync: int64; const AObject: int64);
    var
      LOffsets: ref Int64List;
      LCapture: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LOffsets := ref Int64List();
      self.DoTaskBlockLayout(AAsync, LOffsets);
      for LI := self.FTree.CountOf(AAsync, NodeRole.Capture) - 1 downto 0 do
        LCapture := self.FTree.NthOf(AAsync, NodeRole.Capture, LI);
        if not self.DoTaskCopies(LCapture) then
          skip;
        end;
        LType := self.DoDeclType(self.FTree[LCapture].ResolvedDecl);
        if self.DoNeedsEnd(LType) then
          if not self.DoTaskEndBuilt(AObject, LOffsets[LI], LType, 0, LOffsets[LOffsets.Count - 1], LI + 1,
            AAsync) then
            return;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      if not self.DoEnded() then
        self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, AAsync);
      end;
    end;

    // The element type T of the generator ARoutine (its result a sequence of T: BNF sec 4,
    // G1), canonical
    hidden const method DoGeneratorElement(const ARoutine: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.FTree[self.DoResultType(ARoutine)].ResolvedType;
    end;

    // The offset of the value of a generator's last yield in its object, for the element
    // type AElement: past the runtime's words at T's alignment, so it follows from T alone
    // (a for in over a sequence of T reads it whichever generator made the sequence)
    hidden const method DoGeneratorValueOffset(const AElement: int64): int64;
    begin
      return AlignUp(ADAM_LOWERING_GENERATOR_WORDS, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AElement));
    end;

    // The offset of the live word after the value of a generator's last yield (G1c2), for
    // an element type AElement with a lifetime (DoHasLifetime): nonzero once a yield has
    // built the value, so its next yield and the generator's end end it only then; by T
    // alone, as the value's
    hidden const method DoGeneratorLiveOffset(const AElement: int64): int64;
    begin
      return AlignUp(self.DoGeneratorValueOffset(AElement) + TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AElement), 8);
    end;

    // The index in DoGeneratorLayout's offsets of the self word of the generator method
    // ARoutine (past the value, and its live word for a T with a lifetime); the holder and
    // the self copy follow it
    hidden const method DoGeneratorSelfIndex(const ARoutine: int64): int64;
    begin
      if self.DoHasLifetime(self.DoGeneratorElement(ARoutine)) then
        return 2;
      end;
      return 1;
    end;

    // The layout of the object of the generator ARoutine (G1): the value
    // (DoGeneratorValueOffset), its live word for a T with a lifetime
    // (DoGeneratorLiveOffset), for a method (G1c2) the word holding self's address, the
    // holder (the ref block its call reached self through, DoGeneratorMethod) and the
    // copy of a self the ramp copies (at its owner type), then each parameter's copy at its
    // canonical type, then the built word when it has one (DoGeneratorBuilt, G1c3), their
    // offsets added to AOffsets in that order; the object's size, a multiple of 8
    hidden method DoGeneratorLayout(const ARoutine: int64; const AOffsets: ref Int64List): int64;
    var
      LElement: int64;
      LOwner: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LElement := self.DoGeneratorElement(ARoutine);
      LAt := self.DoGeneratorValueOffset(LElement);
      AOffsets.Add(LAt);
      LAt := LAt + TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LElement);
      if self.DoHasLifetime(LElement) then
        LAt := self.DoGeneratorLiveOffset(LElement);
        AOffsets.Add(LAt);
        LAt := LAt + 8;
      end;
      if self.DoGeneratorMethod(ARoutine) then
        LAt := AlignUp(LAt, self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
        AOffsets.Add(LAt);
        LAt := LAt + self.FTarget.PointerSize();
        AOffsets.Add(LAt);
        LAt := LAt + self.FTarget.PointerSize();
        LOwner := self.DoOwnerType(ARoutine);
        LAt := AlignUp(LAt, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LOwner));
        AOffsets.Add(LAt);
        LAt := LAt + TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LOwner);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param) - 1 do
        LType := self.DoDeclType(self.FTree.NthOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param, LI));
        LAt := AlignUp(LAt, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType));
        AOffsets.Add(LAt);
        LAt := LAt + TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType);
      end;
      if self.DoGeneratorBuilt(ARoutine) then
        LAt := AlignUp(LAt, 8);
        AOffsets.Add(LAt);
        LAt := LAt + 8;
      end;
      return AlignUp(LAt, 8);
    end;

    // The index in DoGeneratorLayout's offsets of the first parameter's copy of the
    // generator ARoutine (past the value and its live word, and a method's self word,
    // holder and self copy)
    hidden const method DoGeneratorFirstParam(const ARoutine: int64): int64;
    begin
      if self.DoGeneratorMethod(ARoutine) then
        return self.DoGeneratorSelfIndex(ARoutine) + 3;
      end;
      return self.DoGeneratorSelfIndex(ARoutine);
    end;

    // True when a copy the ramp of the generator ARoutine makes may raise (G1c3): a
    // parameter's copy or a method's self copy runs a copy (DoHoldsMember), or a self that
    // cannot be copied raises (GeneratorCopyFail); the ramp's copies are then a protected
    // region whose unwind releases the generator's block (DoGeneratorRamp)
    hidden const method DoGeneratorRampRaises(const ARoutine: int64): bool;
    var
      LOwner: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param) - 1 do
        LType := self.DoDeclType(self.FTree.NthOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param, LI));
        if self.DoHoldsMember(LType, NodeKind.CopyDecl) then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      if not self.DoGeneratorMethod(ARoutine) then
        return false;
      end;
      LOwner := self.DoOwnerType(ARoutine);
      return self.DoHoldsMember(LOwner, NodeKind.CopyDecl) or self.DoCannotCopy(LOwner);
    end;

    // True when the object of the generator ARoutine carries a built word (G1c3, last in
    // DoGeneratorLayout): its ramp may raise part way (DoGeneratorRampRaises) and a part it
    // builds ends by a done (a parameter's copy, a self copy that can be made). After each
    // such part the ramp stores there one past that part's place in the build order (the
    // parameters, then the self copy: DoGeneratorMark); the end ends only the parts built
    // (DoGeneratorBuiltTest), so a release after a raise part way ends no part never built
    hidden const method DoGeneratorBuilt(const ARoutine: int64): bool;
    var
      LOwner: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoGeneratorRampRaises(ARoutine) then
        return false;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param) - 1 do
        LType := self.DoDeclType(self.FTree.NthOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param, LI));
        if self.DoNeedsEnd(LType) then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      if not self.DoGeneratorMethod(ARoutine) then
        return false;
      end;
      LOwner := self.DoOwnerType(ARoutine);
      return self.DoNeedsEnd(LOwner) and not self.DoCannotCopy(LOwner);
    end;

    // The index in DoGeneratorLayout's offsets of the built word of the generator ARoutine
    // (DoGeneratorBuilt): past every parameter's copy
    hidden const method DoGeneratorBuiltIndex(const ARoutine: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoGeneratorFirstParam(ARoutine) + self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param);
    end;

    // The part AMark (one past its place in the build order, DoGeneratorBuilt) of the
    // object AObject (laid out at AOffsets) of the generator ARoutine marked built at ANode:
    // AMark stored into the built word; nothing when the object has none
    hidden method DoGeneratorMark(const ARoutine: int64; const AObject: int64;
      const AOffsets: ref Int64List; const AMark: int64; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LWord: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoGeneratorBuilt(ARoutine) then
        return;
      end;
      LWord := self.DoByteOffset(AObject, AOffsets[self.DoGeneratorBuiltIndex(ARoutine)], ANode);
      self.DoMarkBuilt(LWord, AMark, ANode);
    end;

    // The test that the part AMark (DoGeneratorMark) of the object AObject (laid out at
    // AOffsets) of the generator ARoutine was built: its built word at least AMark; 0 (the
    // part always built) when the object has no built word
    hidden method DoGeneratorBuiltTest(const ARoutine: int64; const AObject: int64;
      const AOffsets: ref Int64List; const AMark: int64): int64;
    var
      LWord: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoGeneratorBuilt(ARoutine) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LWord := self.DoByteOffset(AObject, AOffsets[self.DoGeneratorBuiltIndex(ARoutine)], ARoutine);
      return self.DoBuiltTest(LWord, AMark, ARoutine);
    end;

    // True when a value of the canonical type AType cannot be copied: it ends by a done
    // and holds no copy (DoCopyValue's LW0001, SEM's SM0427)
    hidden const method DoCannotCopy(const AType: int64): bool;
    begin
      return self.DoNeedsEnd(AType) and not self.DoHoldsMember(AType, NodeKind.CopyDecl);
    end;

    // True when a value in the object of the generator ARoutine ends by a done
    // (DoNeedsEnd): the last yield's value, a method's self copy or a parameter's copy; its
    // descriptor's done is then its own end (DoTaskEndFunction, DoGeneratorEnd), not the
    // runtime's GeneratorDone
    hidden const method DoGeneratorEnds(const ARoutine: int64): bool;
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if self.DoNeedsEnd(self.DoGeneratorElement(ARoutine)) then
        return true;
      end;
      if self.DoGeneratorMethod(ARoutine) and self.DoNeedsEnd(self.DoOwnerType(ARoutine)) then
        return true;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param) - 1 do
        if self.DoNeedsEnd(self.DoDeclType(self.FTree.NthOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param, LI))) then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // The read-only data of the descriptor of the generator ARoutine (G1), its object ASize
    // bytes laid out at AOffsets (DoGeneratorLayout): the runtime's GeneratorDone as its
    // done (or its own end, DoGeneratorEnds), the managed map over the raise's text, the
    // value, a method's holder (a ref) and self copy, and each parameter's copy; 0 after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoGeneratorData(const ARoutine: int64; const AOffsets: ref Int64List;
      const ASize: int64): int64;
    var
      LDone: int64;
      LRuns: ref Int64List;
      LSelf: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if self.DoGeneratorEnds(ARoutine) then
        LDone := self.DoTaskEndFunction(ARoutine);
      else
        LDone := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.GeneratorDone, ARoutine);
        if LDone = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      LRuns := ref Int64List();
      self.DoAddRun(LRuns, ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_TEXT_OFFSET, 1, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), 0);
      if not self.DoManagedRuns(self.DoGeneratorElement(ARoutine), AOffsets[0], LRuns, ARoutine) then
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.DoGeneratorMethod(ARoutine) then
        LSelf := self.DoGeneratorSelfIndex(ARoutine);
        self.DoAddRun(LRuns, AOffsets[LSelf + 1], 1, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), ADAM_LOWERING_REF_ELEMENT);
        if not self.DoManagedRuns(self.DoOwnerType(ARoutine), AOffsets[LSelf + 2], LRuns, ARoutine) then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      LFirst := self.DoGeneratorFirstParam(ARoutine);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param) - 1 do
        if not self.DoManagedRuns(self.DoDeclType(self.FTree.NthOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param, LI)),
          AOffsets[LFirst + LI], LRuns, ARoutine) then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      return self.DoTaskDescriptorWords(ARoutine, LRuns, ASize, LDone);
    end;

    // A new body function for the generator ARoutine (internal, taking its object:
    // GeneratorRun's call of its entry word); its body (DoGeneratorBody) is lowered last
    // (DoDeferredBodies, with the task entries); its function id
    hidden method DoGeneratorEntry(const ARoutine: int64): int64;
    var
      LFunction: int64;
    begin
      LFunction := self.FModule.AddFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_GENERATOR_SYMBOL + IntToStr(self.FTaskEntries.Count),
        IrType.Void, ARoutine);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Internal := true;
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.AddParam(IrType.Pointer);
      self.FTaskEntries.Add(LFunction);
      self.FTaskNodes.Add(ARoutine);
      return LFunction;
    end;

    // The ramp of the generator ARoutine (its own function, its parameters made: DoBody): a
    // call runs none of its statements. A new generator block (RefNew over its descriptor,
    // DoGeneratorData), its body function (DoGeneratorEntry) written as its entry, self's
    // each parameter copied into its object (DoTaskCopy: the body runs after the call has
    // returned, as an async block's copies, T4), then a method's self (DoGeneratorSelf: the
    // object its holder keeps, or a copy); then the routine's managed slots released and
    // the block returned (the caller holds it). When a copy may raise (DoGeneratorRampRaises,
    // G1c3) the copies are a protected region: the block kept in a slot (FSlotOf[ARoutine])
    // that its unwind funclet releases (DoRegionCleanup), the end then ending only the parts
    // built (DoGeneratorMark after each one that ends by a done)
    hidden method DoGeneratorRamp(const ARoutine: int64);
    var
      LFunction: ref IrFunction;
      LRaises: bool;
      LHandler: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LCopies: int64;
      LFirstBlock: int64;
      LLastBlock: int64;
      LAfter: int64;
      LFunclet: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LOffsets: ref Int64List;
      LSize: int64;
      LData: int64;
      LDescriptor: int64;
      LBlock: int64;
      LObject: int64;
      LEntry: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LParam: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LId: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LOffsets := ref Int64List();
      LSize := self.DoGeneratorLayout(ARoutine, LOffsets);
      LData := self.DoGeneratorData(ARoutine, LOffsets, LSize);
      if LData = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LDescriptor := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ARoutine);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LDescriptor).Link := LData;
      LBlock := self.DoCallRuntimeSiteOne(RuntimeRoutine.RefNew, LDescriptor, ARoutine, "generator");
      if LBlock = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LObject := self.DoByteOffset(LBlock, ADAM_LOWERING_REF_HEADER, ARoutine);
      LEntry := self.DoEmit(IrOp.CodeAddress, IrType.Pointer, ARoutine);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LEntry).Link := self.DoGeneratorEntry(ARoutine);
      self.DoStore(self.DoByteOffset(LObject, ADAM_LOWERING_TASK_ENTRY_OFFSET, ARoutine), LEntry, ARoutine);
      // The copies' blocks run from their own first block, entered once the block is kept
      LRaises := self.DoGeneratorRampRaises(ARoutine);
      LFunction := self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction);
      LHandler := 0;
      LFirstBlock := 0;
      if LRaises then
        LHandler := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.FrameHandler, ARoutine);
        if LHandler = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(ARoutine, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
        self.FSlotOf[ARoutine] := LSlot;
        self.DoStore(LSlot, LBlock, ARoutine);
        LCopies := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
        self.DoJumpTo(LCopies, ARoutine);
        self.FBlock := LCopies;
        LFirstBlock := LFunction.Blocks.Count - 1;
      end;
      LFirst := self.DoGeneratorFirstParam(ARoutine);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param) - 1 do
        LParam := self.FTree.NthOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param, LI);
        LType := self.DoDeclType(LParam);
        LSource := self.DoDeclAddress(LParam, LParam);
        if LSource = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        if not self.DoTaskCopy(LSource, LType, self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[LFirst + LI], LParam),
          LParam) then
          return;
        end;
        if self.DoNeedsEnd(LType) then
          self.DoGeneratorMark(ARoutine, LObject, LOffsets, LI + 1, LParam);
        end;
      end;
      // last: a self that cannot be copied raises (DoGeneratorSelf)
      if self.DoGeneratorMethod(ARoutine) then
        if not self.DoGeneratorSelf(ARoutine, LObject, LOffsets) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      // The region's scope over the copies' blocks; the code after them in a block of its own
      if LRaises then
        LLastBlock := LFunction.Blocks.Count - 1;
        LAfter := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
        self.DoJumpTo(LAfter, ARoutine);
        self.FBlock := LAfter;
        LFunclet := self.DoFinallyFunclet(ARoutine);
        LFunction.AddScope(LFirstBlock, LLastBlock, LFunclet, -1);
        self.FModule.FrameHandler := LHandler;
      end;
      LBody := self.FTree.FirstOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Body);
      self.DoReleaseManaged(LBody);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, LBody);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LBlock);
    end;

    // The self part of the object AObject (laid out at AOffsets) of the
    // generator method ARoutine, made last by its ramp (G1c2): the holder its call passed (FHolderSlot) stored
    // with a holder added (RefAssign; nil stays nil); with one, self's address as the call
    // gave it (the object that ref's block keeps alive, C# class iterators); with none, self
    // copied into the object at its owner type (DoTaskCopy, as an async block copies, T4:
    // a change after the call is not seen, C# struct iterators) and the copy's address
    // stored, marked built (DoGeneratorMark, its place past the parameters). A type that
    // cannot be copied (DoCannotCopy) reaches the copy only through a dispatched call on a
    // value of a copyable ancestor or an interface (SEM's SM0427 holds every other path):
    // the runtime's GeneratorCopyFail raises there, the ramp's region releasing the block
    // (G1c3: what the ramp built ends with it); false after LW0001
    hidden method DoGeneratorSelf(const ARoutine: int64; const AObject: int64;
      const AOffsets: ref Int64List): bool;
    var
      LOwner: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LHolder: int64;
      LSelf: int64;
      LWord: int64;
      LCopy: int64;
      LHeld: int64;
      LCopied: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
    begin
      LOwner := self.DoOwnerType(ARoutine);
      LAt := self.DoGeneratorSelfIndex(ARoutine);
      LHolder := self.DoLoad(self.FHolderSlot, IrType.Pointer, ARoutine);
      LSelf := self.DoLoad(self.FSelfSlot, IrType.Pointer, ARoutine);
      LWord := self.DoByteOffset(AObject, AOffsets[LAt], ARoutine);
      LCopy := self.DoByteOffset(AObject, AOffsets[LAt + 2], ARoutine);
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.RefAssign, self.DoByteOffset(AObject, AOffsets[LAt + 1], ARoutine),
        LHolder, ARoutine) = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LHeld := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LCopied := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.NotEqual, LHolder,
        self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ARoutine), ARoutine), LHeld, LCopied, ARoutine);
      self.FBlock := LHeld;
      self.DoStore(LWord, LSelf, ARoutine);
      self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, ARoutine);
      self.FBlock := LCopied;
      if self.DoCannotCopy(LOwner) then
        LArgs := ref Int64List();
        if self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.GeneratorCopyFail, LArgs, ARoutine) = 0 then
          return false;
        end;
      else
        if not self.DoTaskCopy(LSelf, LOwner, LCopy, ARoutine) then
          return false;
        end;
        if self.DoNeedsEnd(LOwner) then
          self.DoGeneratorMark(ARoutine, AObject, AOffsets, self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param) + 1,
            ARoutine);
        end;
      end;
      self.DoStore(LWord, LCopy, ARoutine);
      self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, ARoutine);
      self.FBlock := LJoin;
      return true;
    end;

    // The body function of the generator ARoutine (DoGeneratorEntry, in its fresh function
    // state; run on its coroutine by GeneratorRun): its object (the one parameter) kept in
    // FGeneratorSlot for the yields; self read from its word; each parameter reached
    // through its copy there (a slot holding the copy's address, the parameter by reference
    // while this body is lowered: FSlotOf / FByRef / FByCopy, given back after, since a
    // call of the generator lowered later reads its parameters' forms); the routine's
    // temporaries and locals;
    // then its statements, its end (or a return) releasing what the body holds and
    // returning: the generator has ended. A raise leaves it for GeneratorRun's guard, an
    // abort (raised at a yield) for its last catching scope; the body's cleanup runs on the way
    hidden method DoGeneratorBody(const ARoutine: int64);
    var
      LObject: int64;
      LOffsets: ref Int64List;
      LWord: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LParam: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LSavedSlot: ref Int64List;
      LSavedByRef: BoolArray;
      LSavedByCopy: BoolArray;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      self.FRoutine := ARoutine;
      self.FResultSlot := 0;
      self.FSelfSlot := 0;
      self.FVarargsSlot := 0;
      self.FPackSlot := 0;
      LObject := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Pointer, ARoutine);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LObject).Imm := 0;
      LWord := self.FTarget.PointerSize();
      self.FGeneratorSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(ARoutine, LWord, self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
      self.DoStore(self.FGeneratorSlot, LObject, ARoutine);
      LOffsets := ref Int64List();
      self.DoGeneratorLayout(ARoutine, LOffsets);
      if self.DoGeneratorMethod(ARoutine) then
        self.FSelfSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(ARoutine, LWord, self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
        self.DoStore(self.FSelfSlot, self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(LObject,
          LOffsets[self.DoGeneratorSelfIndex(ARoutine)], ARoutine), IrType.Pointer, ARoutine), ARoutine);
      end;
      LFirst := self.DoGeneratorFirstParam(ARoutine);
      LCount := self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param);
      LSavedSlot := ref Int64List();
      setlength(LSavedByRef, LCount);
      setlength(LSavedByCopy, LCount);
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LParam := self.FTree.NthOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param, LI);
        LSavedSlot.Add(self.FSlotOf[LParam]);
        LSavedByRef[LI] := self.FByRef[LParam];
        LSavedByCopy[LI] := self.FByCopy[LParam];
        LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(LParam, LWord, self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
        self.DoStore(LSlot, self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[LFirst + LI], LParam), LParam);
        self.FSlotOf[LParam] := LSlot;
        self.FByRef[LParam] := true;
        self.FByCopy[LParam] := false;
      end;
      self.DoCodeTemporaries(ARoutine);
      self.DoLocalSlots(ARoutine);
      self.DoLocalInits(ARoutine);
      LBody := self.FTree.FirstOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Body);
      self.DoStatements(LBody, NodeRole.Statement);
      if not self.DoEnded() then
        self.DoReleaseManaged(LBody);
        self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, LBody);
      end;
      self.DoCleanupScopes(ARoutine, self.DoLastBlock());
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LParam := self.FTree.NthOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param, LI);
        self.FSlotOf[LParam] := LSavedSlot[LI];
        self.FByRef[LParam] := LSavedByRef[LI];
        self.FByCopy[LParam] := LSavedByCopy[LI];
      end;
      self.FGeneratorSlot := 0;
      self.FSelfSlot := 0;
      self.FRoutine := 0;
    end;

    // The rest of the end of the generator ARoutine (DoTaskEndBody, after GeneratorDone)
    // over its object AObject, each value that ends by a done ended (DoGeneratorEnds): the
    // last yield's value while its live word says one was built (G1c2), then the reverse of
    // their build, each parameter's copy and a method's self copy (only when no holder was
    // passed: the ramp copied self), each only once built when the object has a built word
    // (DoGeneratorBuiltTest, G1c3: a ramp that raised part way); the return. RefRelease then
    // releases the object's managed values (its map: the holder too)
    hidden method DoGeneratorEnd(const ARoutine: int64; const AObject: int64);
    var
      LOffsets: ref Int64List;
      LElement: int64;
      LOwner: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LTest: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LOffsets := ref Int64List();
      self.DoGeneratorLayout(ARoutine, LOffsets);
      LElement := self.DoGeneratorElement(ARoutine);
      if self.DoNeedsEnd(LElement) then
        LTest := self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(AObject, LOffsets[1], ARoutine), IrType.Bool, ARoutine);
        if not self.DoTaskEndPart(AObject, LOffsets[0], LElement, LTest, ARoutine) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      LFirst := self.DoGeneratorFirstParam(ARoutine);
      for LI := self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param) - 1 downto 0 do
        LType := self.DoDeclType(self.FTree.NthOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param, LI));
        if self.DoNeedsEnd(LType) then
          LTest := self.DoGeneratorBuiltTest(ARoutine, AObject, LOffsets, LI + 1);
          if not self.DoTaskEndPart(AObject, LOffsets[LFirst + LI], LType, LTest, ARoutine) then
            return;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      if self.DoGeneratorMethod(ARoutine) then
        LOwner := self.DoOwnerType(ARoutine);
        LAt := self.DoGeneratorSelfIndex(ARoutine);
        if self.DoNeedsEnd(LOwner) and not self.DoCannotCopy(LOwner) then
          // built only by the copy, so the built word alone says so when there is one
          if self.DoGeneratorBuilt(ARoutine) then
            LTest := self.DoGeneratorBuiltTest(ARoutine, AObject, LOffsets,
              self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Param) + 1);
          else
            LTest := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.Equal,
              self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(AObject, LOffsets[LAt + 1], ARoutine), IrType.Pointer, ARoutine),
              self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ARoutine), ARoutine);
          end;
          if not self.DoTaskEndPart(AObject, LOffsets[LAt + 2], LOwner, LTest, ARoutine) then
            return;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      if not self.DoEnded() then
        self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, ARoutine);
      end;
    end;

    // `yield E` AId in a generator's body (BNF sec 5, G1; ResolvedJump the generator, E
    // converted to its T by SEM): E stored into the value in the generator's object
    // (FGeneratorSlot): a value object with a lifetime by DoYieldObject, any other as an
    // assignment stores it (DoYieldValue); E's temporaries ended, then GeneratorYield: the
    // resumer goes on (its for in reads the value) until the next resume, when this body
    // goes on here (an abort raised here instead)
    hidden method DoYield(const AId: int64);
    var
      LExpr: int64;
      LElement: int64;
      LObject: int64;
      LDest: int64;
    begin
      if self.FGeneratorSlot = 0 then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return;
      end;
      LExpr := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Value);
      LElement := self.DoGeneratorElement(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedJump);
      LObject := self.DoLoad(self.FGeneratorSlot, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      LDest := self.DoByteOffset(LObject, self.DoGeneratorValueOffset(LElement), AId);
      if self.DoHasLifetime(LElement) then
        if not self.DoYieldObject(AId, LExpr, LElement, LObject, LDest) then
          return;
        end;
      else
        if not self.DoYieldValue(AId, LExpr, LElement, LDest) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      self.DoEndTemporaries(LExpr);
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.GeneratorYield, LObject, 0, AId) = 0 then
        return;
      end;
    end;

    // The value of the yield AId's expression AExpr (of the element type AElement, no
    // lifetime) stored at ADest as an assignment stores it: a managed value by
    // DoStoreManaged (a holder added, the last yield's released), an aggregate by
    // DoAggregateCopy, a scalar by its bytes; false after LW0001
    hidden method DoYieldValue(const AId: int64; const AExpr: int64; const AElement: int64;
      const ADest: int64): bool;
    var
      LValue: int64;
      LSource: int64;
    begin
      if self.DoIsManaged(AElement) then
        LValue := self.DoValue(AExpr);
        if LValue = 0 then
          return false;
        end;
        return self.DoStoreManaged(ADest, LValue, AElement, AId) <> 0;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(AElement) then
        LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(AExpr);
        if LSource = 0 then
          return false;
        end;
        self.DoAggregateCopy(ADest, LSource, AElement, AId);
        return not self.DoEnded();
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(AExpr);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoStore(ADest, LValue, AId);
      return true;
    end;

    // The value object of the yield AId's expression AExpr (of the element type AElement,
    // which has a lifetime, G1c2) made the generator's value at ADest in its object AObject,
    // as an assignment to a local moves or copies it (DoMoveAssign): a copy built first into
    // a zeroed slot of its own (DoCopyValue: AExpr may name the old value itself), then the
    // old value ended only while the live word says one was built (DoReleaseLive, the word
    // cleared first), then the new one moved in (a call's result: DoMoveObject, its
    // temporary no longer live) or the copy's bytes, and the live word set; false after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoYieldObject(const AId: int64; const AExpr: int64; const AElement: int64;
      const AObject: int64; const ADest: int64): bool;
    var
      LFrom: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LTemp: int64;
      LLive: int64;
    begin
      LFrom := self.DoMoveSource(AExpr);
      if (LFrom <> 0) and not self.DoIsCallSite(LFrom) then
        LFrom := 0;
      end;
      LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(AExpr);
      if LSource = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AElement);
      LTemp := 0;
      if LFrom = 0 then
        LTemp := self.DoSizedSlot(AId, LSize, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AElement));
        // zeroed each time it runs: a loop's next copy starts from nothing too
        self.DoFill(LTemp, LSize, AId);
        if not self.DoCopyValue(LTemp, LSource, AElement, AId) then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      LLive := self.DoByteOffset(AObject, self.DoGeneratorLiveOffset(AElement), AId);
      if not self.DoReleaseLive(ADest, AElement, LLive, false, AId) then
        return false;
      end;
      if LFrom <> 0 then
        self.DoMoveObject(ADest, LSource, LFrom, AElement, AId);
      else
        self.DoCopyBytes(ADest, LTemp, LSize, AId);
      end;
      self.DoStore(LLive, self.DoConstant(IrType.Bool, 1, AId), AId);
      return true;
    end;

    // The method part of a new task's object AObject for the async expression AAsync (T1),
    // its call's member access AMember running AMethod, at AOffsets' heads (DoTaskHeads),
    // all made at the async as the call itself makes them: the ref that holds the object
    // stored with a holder added (DoTaskHolder: read once, the self below reads that value
    // through FPrimed), the object's address as the call's self (DoSelfArgumentIn: the
    // embed, the upcast; a nil ref raises here, in the caller), for a dispatched method the
    // function its object's itable or vtable names (DoItableTarget: self the object's
    // start; DoVtableTarget); false after LW0001
    hidden method DoTaskMethod(const AAsync: int64; const AMember: int64; const AMethod: int64;
      const AObject: int64; const AOffsets: ref Int64List): bool;
    var
      LInterface: bool;
      LCoded: bool;
      LAt: int64;
      LHolder: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LSelf: int64;
      LWord: int64;
      LCode: int64;
    begin
      LInterface := self.DoIsInterfaceMember(AMethod);
      LCoded := LInterface or self.DoIsVtableCall(AMember, AMethod);
      LAt := 0;
      if LCoded then
        LAt := 1;
      end;
      LHolder := self.DoTaskHolder(AMember);
      if LHolder <> 0 then
        LValue := self.DoManagedValue(LHolder);
        if LValue = 0 then
          return false;
        end;
        if self.DoStoreManaged(self.DoByteOffset(AObject, AOffsets[LAt + 1], AAsync), LValue,
          self.DoUsedType(LHolder), AAsync) = 0 then
          return false;
        end;
        self.FPrimed[LHolder] := LValue;
      end;
      LSelf := self.DoSelfArgumentIn(AMember, AMethod);
      if LHolder <> 0 then
        self.FPrimed[LHolder] := 0;
      end;
      if LSelf = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      if LInterface then
        LWord := LSelf;
        LCode := self.DoItableTarget(LWord, AMethod, AAsync, LSelf);
      else
        if LCoded then
          LCode := self.DoVtableTarget(LSelf, AMethod, AAsync);
        end;
      end;
      if LCoded then
        self.DoStore(self.DoByteOffset(AObject, AOffsets[0], AAsync), LCode, AAsync);
      end;
      self.DoStore(self.DoByteOffset(AObject, AOffsets[LAt], AAsync), LSelf, AAsync);
      return true;
    end;

    // The operand a task entry passes for the extra argument AArg of a clink variadic call
    // (T1) from its copy at AAddress in the task's object, at ANode, as DoVariadicArgument
    // passes the argument itself: an aggregate's bytes in a register widened to the 8-byte
    // slot, or the copy's address (the task's own copy, used by this one call); a managed
    // value its block (borrowed: the object holds it); any other value loaded at its type
    // and promoted (DoVariadicIr); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoTaskVariadicOperand(const AArg: int64; const AAddress: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
    begin
      LType := self.DoTaskExtraType(AArg);
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        LIr := self.DoAggregateIr(LType);
        if LIr = IrType.Void then
          return AAddress;
        end;
        return self.DoConvertIr(self.DoLoad(AAddress, LIr, ANode), IrType.UInt64, ANode);
      end;
      if self.DoIsManaged(LType) then
        return self.DoLoad(AAddress, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      end;
      LIr := self.DoTypeAt(LType, ANode);
      if LIr = IrType.Void then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoConvertIr(self.DoLoad(AAddress, LIr, ANode), self.DoVariadicIr(LIr), ANode);
    end;

    // The operand a task entry passes for the parameter AParam from its copy at AAddress in
    // the task's object (DoArgument's forms, the copy standing for the argument): for an
    // aggregate by copy or a parameter by reference the copy's address (the copy is the
    // task's own, used by this one call), for an aggregate in a register its bytes loaded as
    // that register's integer, else its value at its type (a managed one borrowed: the
    // object holds it); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoTaskOperand(const AParam: int64; const AAddress: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
    begin
      LType := self.DoDeclType(AParam);
      if self.FByCopy[AParam] or self.FByRef[AParam] then
        return AAddress;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        return self.DoLoad(AAddress, self.DoAggregateIr(LType), ANode);
      end;
      if self.DoIsManaged(LType) then
        return self.DoLoad(AAddress, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      end;
      LIr := self.DoTypeAt(LType, ANode);
      if LIr = IrType.Void then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoLoad(AAddress, LIr, ANode);
    end;

    // The result AId of the call ACall in the entry of the async expression AAsync stored
    // into the result place of the task's object AObject (DoTaskResultOffset) as a value of
    // the result type: a managed one from the call's temporary with a holder added
    // (DoStoreManaged; the temporary is released at the entry's exit), an aggregate from the
    // call's result slot (DoAggregateCopy), any other the call's value; nothing for a plain
    // task; false after LW0001
    hidden method DoTaskResult(const AAsync: int64; const ACall: int64; const AObject: int64;
      const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LResult: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      LResult := self.FTree[self.FTree[AAsync].ResolvedType].ResolvedType;
      if LResult = 0 then
        return true;
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(AObject, self.DoTaskResultOffset(LResult), AAsync);
      if self.DoIsManaged(LResult) then
        LValue := self.DoLoad(self.DoTempSlot(ACall), IrType.Pointer, AAsync);
        return self.DoStoreManaged(LAddress, LValue, LResult, AAsync) <> 0;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LResult) then
        if self.FSlotOf[ACall] = 0 then
          raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_CALL_RESULT + self.FTree.ConstructText(ACall));
        end;
        // a value object moves from the call's result (its temporary no longer live): the
        // task's object holds it, its end ends it (DoTaskEndBody)
        if self.DoHasLifetime(LResult) then
          self.DoMoveObject(LAddress, self.FSlotOf[ACall], ACall, LResult, AAsync);
          return true;
        end;
        return self.DoCopyValue(LAddress, self.FSlotOf[ACall], LResult, AAsync);
      end;
      self.DoStore(LAddress, AId, AAsync);
      return true;
    end;

    // The body of the entry of the async expression AAsync (DoTaskEntry): the task's object
    // (its one parameter), the code and a method's self read from it (DoTaskHeads), each
    // parameter's operand made from its copy there (DoTaskOperand), the extra arguments'
    // (DoTaskVariadicOperand, or a typed pack over their copies: DoPackFrom), the call (of
    // its routine, its external, its method, or through the code copied there), its result
    // stored (DoTaskResult), the entry's managed slots released, the return. A raise of the
    // call leaves it for TaskRun's catching scope
    hidden method DoTaskBody(const AAsync: int64);
    var
      LCall: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
      LSig: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LCoded: bool;
      LOffsets: ref Int64List;
      LObject: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LPlaces: ref Int64List;
      LTarget: int64;
      LSelf: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LParams: int64;
      LExtras: int64;
      LOperand: int64;
      LKind: IrOp;
      LLink: int64;
      LIrResult: IrType;
      LHeld: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LHolder: int64;
      LId: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoAsyncTarget(AAsync, LCall, LDecl, LSig) then
        return;
      end;
      LMember := self.DoMethodMember(LCall);
      LCoded := self.DoTaskCoded(LCall, LDecl);
      LOffsets := ref Int64List();
      self.DoTaskLayout(AAsync, LCall, LDecl, LSig, LOffsets);
      LObject := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Pointer, AAsync);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LObject).Imm := 0;
      // the call's managed result lands in a temporary of the entry (DoEmitCall)
      if self.DoIsManagedCall(LCall) then
        self.DoResultTemporary(LCall);
      end;
      LFirst := self.DoTaskHeads(LCall, LDecl);
      LTarget := 0;
      LSelf := 0;
      if LCoded then
        LTarget := self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[0], AAsync), IrType.Pointer, AAsync);
      end;
      if LMember <> 0 then
        LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[0], AAsync);
        if LCoded then
          LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[1], AAsync);
        end;
        LSelf := self.DoLoad(LAddress, IrType.Pointer, AAsync);
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LParams := self.FTree.CountOf(LSig, NodeRole.Param);
      for LI := 0 to LParams - 1 do
        LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[LFirst + LI], AAsync);
        LOperand := self.DoTaskOperand(self.FTree.NthOf(LSig, NodeRole.Param, LI), LAddress, AAsync);
        if LOperand = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LArgs.Add(LOperand);
      end;
      // the extra arguments read their copies in place: one by one for a clink variadic, as
      // a typed pack over them for a cpplink one (DoArguments' two forms)
      LExtras := self.DoTaskExtras(LCall, LSig);
      if self.DoIsPackVariadic(LSig) then
        LPlaces := ref Int64List();
        for LI := 0 to LExtras - 1 do
          LPlaces.Add(self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[LFirst + LParams + LI], AAsync));
        end;
        LOperand := self.DoPackFrom(LCall, LParams, LPlaces);
        if LOperand = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LArgs.Add(LOperand);
      else
        for LI := 0 to LExtras - 1 do
          LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[LFirst + LParams + LI], AAsync);
          LOperand := self.DoTaskVariadicOperand(self.FTree.NthOf(LCall, NodeRole.Argument, LParams + LI),
            LAddress, AAsync);
          if LOperand = 0 then
            return;
          end;
          LArgs.Add(LOperand);
        end;
      end;
      if LMember <> 0 then
        if LCoded then
          LKind := IrOp.CallIndirect;
          LLink := self.DoMethodSignature(LDecl, AAsync);
          if LLink = 0 then
            return;
          end;
          LIrResult := self.FModule.SignatureAt(LLink).ResultType;
        else
          LKind := IrOp.Call;
          LLink := self.FFunctionOf[LDecl];
          if LLink = 0 then
            return;
          end;
          LIrResult := self.FModule.FunctionAt(LLink).Signature.ResultType;
        end;
      else
        if LDecl = 0 then
          LKind := IrOp.CallIndirect;
          LLink := self.DoSignatureOf(self.FTree[self.FTree.FirstOf(LCall, NodeRole.Callee)].ResolvedType, AAsync);
          if LLink = 0 then
            return;
          end;
          LIrResult := self.FModule.SignatureAt(LLink).ResultType;
        else
          if self.FTree.FirstOf(LDecl, NodeRole.External) <> 0 then
            LKind := IrOp.CallExternal;
            LLink := self.DoExternal(LDecl);
            if LLink = 0 then
              return;
            end;
            LIrResult := self.FModule.ExternalAt(LLink).Signature.ResultType;
          else
            LKind := IrOp.Call;
            LLink := self.FFunctionOf[LDecl];
            if LLink = 0 then
              return;
            end;
            LIrResult := self.FModule.FunctionAt(LLink).Signature.ResultType;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      // the call takes its copies now: the task's end no longer ends them (DoTaskOwnsArgs)
      if self.DoTaskOwnsArgs(LSig) then
        LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[LFirst + LParams + LExtras], AAsync);
        self.DoStore(LAddress, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, AAsync), AAsync);
      end;
      // a generator method's holder: the ref the task holds (DoTaskHolder), nil through a ptr
      LHolder := 0;
      if (LMember <> 0) and self.DoGeneratorMethod(LDecl) then
        LHeld := self.DoTaskHolder(LMember);
        LValue := 0;
        if LHeld <> 0 then
          // the heads: the code (a coded call), self, then the holder
          if LCoded then
            LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[2], AAsync);
          else
            LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(LObject, LOffsets[1], AAsync);
          end;
          LValue := self.DoLoad(LAddress, IrType.Pointer, AAsync);
        end;
        LHolder := self.DoGeneratorHolderArg(LDecl, LHeld, LValue, LSelf, AAsync);
      end;
      LId := self.DoEmitCallWith(LCall, LSig, LKind, LLink, LIrResult, LTarget, LSelf, LHolder, LArgs);
      if LId = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      if not self.DoTaskResult(AAsync, LCall, LObject, LId) then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoReleaseManaged(AAsync);
      if not self.DoEnded() then
        self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, AAsync);
      end;
    end;

    // The body of the task entry AIndex (DoTaskEntry's function) in a fresh function state:
    // an async call's (DoTaskBody), an async block's (DoTaskBlockBody, T4)
    hidden method DoTaskEntryBody(const AIndex: int64);
    begin
      self.FFunction := self.FTaskEntries[AIndex];
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoStartManaged();
      // a generator's body function (DoGeneratorEntry): its routine's statements
      if self.FTree[self.FTaskNodes[AIndex]].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Generator) then
        self.DoGeneratorBody(self.FTaskNodes[AIndex]);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAsyncBlock(self.FTaskNodes[AIndex]) then
        self.DoTaskBlockBody(self.FTaskNodes[AIndex]);
        return;
      end;
      self.DoTaskBody(self.FTaskNodes[AIndex]);
    end;

    // The task the await expression AId waits for (its operand's value, borrowed: its holder
    // keeps it), once TaskAwait has returned (its call ended; a raise it ended with is
    // raised again there); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAwaitBlock(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LBlock: int64;
    begin
      LBlock := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand));
      if LBlock = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.TaskAwait, LBlock, 0, AId) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return LBlock;
    end;

    // The address of the result of the task the await expression AId waits for
    // (DoAwaitBlock): in its object, at DoTaskResultOffset of AId's type; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAwaitResult(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LBlock: int64;
    begin
      LBlock := self.DoAwaitBlock(AId);
      if LBlock = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoByteOffset(LBlock,
        ADAM_LOWERING_REF_HEADER + self.DoTaskResultOffset(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType), AId);
    end;

    // The value of the await expression AId (BNF sec 6) that is no managed value: a plain
    // task's (a statement: the wait alone, TaskAwait's call standing for it), else its
    // result read at its type (DoAwaitResult); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAwaitValue(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LAddress: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType = 0 then
        return self.DoAwaitBlock(AId);
      end;
      LIr := self.DoTypeAt(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType, AId);
      if LIr = IrType.Void then
        return 0;
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoAwaitResult(AId);
      if LAddress = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoLoad(LAddress, LIr, AId);
    end;

    // The managed result of the await expression AId (a text, a dynamic array, a ref or a
    // task: DoIsManaged), borrowed: read from the task's object (DoAwaitResult), which holds
    // it as long as the task does; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAwaitManaged(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      LAddress := self.DoAwaitResult(AId);
      if LAddress = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoLoad(LAddress, IrType.Pointer, AId);
    end;

    // create(P) / destroy(P) (BNF sec 7; SEM let only an assignable pointer to a record or
    // an overlay through): create stores CreateMem's zeroed block of the target's size into
    // P's place; destroy hands P's block and the target's managed map (nil when it holds no
    // managed value) to DestroyMem, then stores nil into P's place. P's place is reached in
    // the write form (DoAddressFor). The runtime call, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoHeapIntrinsic(const ACall: int64; const ACreate: bool): int64;
    var
      LArgument: int64;
      LTarget: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LBlock: int64;
      LMap: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LCall: int64;
      LNil: int64;
    begin
      LArgument := self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, 0);
      LTarget := TargetOf(self.FTree, self.FTree[LArgument].ResolvedType);
      if ACreate then
        LSize := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LTarget), ACall);
        LCall := self.DoCallRuntimeSiteOne(RuntimeRoutine.CreateMem, LSize, ACall,
          TypeText(self.FTree, LTarget));
        if LCall = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LAddress := self.DoAddressFor(LArgument, true);
        if LAddress = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        self.DoStore(LAddress, LCall, ACall);
        return LCall;
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoAddressFor(LArgument, true);
      if LAddress = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LBlock := self.DoLoad(LAddress, IrType.Pointer, ACall);
      if self.DoHoldsManaged(LTarget) then
        LMap := self.DoManagedMap(LTarget, ACall);
        if LMap = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
      else
        LMap := self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ACall);
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(LBlock);
      LArgs.Add(LMap);
      LCall := self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.DestroyMem, LArgs, ACall);
      if LCall = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LNil := self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ACall);
      self.DoStore(LAddress, LNil, ACall);
      return LCall;
    end;

    // ready(T) (BNF sec 7): TaskReady on the task's value (borrowed); its bool, 0 after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoReady(const ACall: int64): int64;
    var
      LBlock: int64;
    begin
      LBlock := self.DoValue(self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, 0));
      if LBlock = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.TaskReady, LBlock, 0, ACall);
    end;

    // cancel(T) (ACancel) / cancelled(T) / cancelled() (BNF sec 7, T3): TaskCancel /
    // TaskCancelled on the task's value (borrowed), TaskCancelledSelf with no argument (the
    // flag of the task whose call this thread runs); the call (cancelled's bool), 0 after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoCancel(const ACall: int64; const ACancel: bool): int64;
    var
      LBlock: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree.CountOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument) = 0 then
        return self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.TaskCancelledSelf, ref Int64List(), ACall);
      end;
      LBlock := self.DoValue(self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, 0));
      if LBlock = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if ACancel then
        return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.TaskCancel, LBlock, 0, ACall);
      end;
      return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.TaskCancelled, LBlock, 0, ACall);
    end;

    // alive(W) (BNF sec 7, M3.10g): WeakAlive on the weak's value (borrowed); its bool, 0
    // after LW0001
    hidden method DoWeakAlive(const ACall: int64): int64;
    var
      LBlock: int64;
    begin
      LBlock := self.DoValue(self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, 0));
      if LBlock = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.WeakAlive, LBlock, 0, ACall);
    end;

    // lock(W) (BNF sec 7, M3.10g): WeakLock on the weak's value (borrowed): a ref the call's
    // hidden slot holds (DoTemporaries' pointer temporary: what a previous pass left there
    // released first, as a call's ref result), nil once the object is gone; the block, 0
    // after LW0001
    hidden method DoWeakLock(const ACall: int64): int64;
    var
      LWeak: int64;
      LBlock: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      LWeak := self.DoValue(self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, 0));
      if LWeak = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LBlock := self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.WeakLock, LWeak, 0, ACall);
      if LBlock = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LSlot := self.DoTempSlot(ACall);
      if not self.DoReleaseAt(LSlot, self.FTree[ACall].ResolvedType, ACall) then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoStore(LSlot, LBlock, ACall);
      return LBlock;
    end;

    // The nil owner check (M3.11b; DESIGN sec 5: a nil own raises) of the block ABlock an
    // owner holds, before its object is reached at ANode: a nil block is a cold block of its
    // own calling the runtime's NilOwnerFail (code 3, `access through a nil own / ref`),
    // which never returns (the block still ends in a jump, as every block does). False after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoCheckNilOwner(const ABlock: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LHeld: int64;
      LBad: int64;
      LGood: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
    begin
      LHeld := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.NotEqual, ABlock, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ANode), ANode);
      LBad := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LGood := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(LHeld, LGood, LBad, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LBad;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      if self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.NilOwnerFail, LArgs, ANode) = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoJumpTo(LGood, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LGood;
      return true;
    end;

    // The address of the object the ref AOperand holds (its value, borrowed: the holder
    // keeps its reference; a call's or a ref new's kept in its hidden slot), past the
    // block's header, a nil ref raising first (DoCheckNilOwner); an own I / ref I's value
    // itself (I3: its itable word, the interface's place); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoRefObject(const AOperand: int64): int64;
    var
      LBlock: int64;
    begin
      LBlock := self.DoManagedValue(AOperand);
      if LBlock = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if not self.DoCheckNilOwner(LBlock, AOperand) then
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.DoIsInterfaceOwner(self.DoUsedType(AOperand)) then
        return LBlock;
      end;
      return self.DoByteOffset(LBlock, ADAM_LOWERING_REF_HEADER, AOperand);
    end;

    // The address the text or dynamic array argument AArg is passed at for a const
    // parameter by reference: a place's own (DoAddress), a temporary's hidden slot (its
    // value made first), else (a literal, a conditional's value) a slot holding its
    // borrowed value; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoManagedReference(const AArg: int64): int64;
    var
      LRoot: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LMoves: bool;
    begin
      LRoot := AArg;
      while self.FTree[LRoot].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LRoot := self.FTree.FirstOf(LRoot, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      // an own or a ref given for an own I / ref I moves to its itable word (I3): its own
      // slot holds the block, so a slot of its own holds the word
      LMoves := self.DoMovesOwner(AArg) or self.DoMovesOwner(LRoot);
      if self.DoIsPlace(LRoot) and (self.FTree[LRoot].ResolvedConst.Kind <> ConstKind.String) and not LMoves then
        return self.DoAddress(LRoot);
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(AArg);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if (self.FTempOf[LRoot] <> 0) and not LMoves then
        return self.FTempOf[LRoot];
      end;
      LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(AArg, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
      self.DoStore(LSlot, LValue, AArg);
      return LSlot;
    end;

    // A call at ANode of the runtime unit's routine AKind with the operands AArgs in order,
    // its allocation site stored around it when AKind makes a text (DoKindWhat,
    // DoCallRuntimeSite); the call, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoCallRuntimeArgs(const AKind: RuntimeRoutine; const AArgs: ref Int64List;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoCallRuntimeSite(AKind, AArgs, ANode, self.DoKindWhat(AKind));
    end;

    // The managed value AValue of the canonical type AType (DoIsManaged) stored into the
    // slot ASlot as an assignment stores it, at ANode: a text by StrAssign, a ref by
    // RefAssign, a weak by WeakAssign, a dynamic array by ArrAssign with its element map (a holder added, then the
    // old one released); the call, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoStoreManaged(const ASlot: int64; const AValue: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LMap: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
    begin
      if self.DoIsText(AType) then
        return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrAssign, ASlot, AValue, ANode);
      end;
      if self.DoIsInterfaceOwner(AType) then
        return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.IntfAssign, ASlot, AValue, ANode);
      end;
      if self.DoIsRefValue(AType) then
        return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.RefAssign, ASlot, AValue, ANode);
      end;
      if self.DoIsWeakValue(AType) then
        return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.WeakAssign, ASlot, AValue, ANode);
      end;
      LMap := self.DoElementMap(AType, ANode);
      if LMap = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(ASlot);
      LArgs.Add(AValue);
      LArgs.Add(LMap);
      return self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.ArrAssign, LArgs, ANode);
    end;

    // The managed local ALocal's slot (of the canonical type AType: a text or a dynamic
    // array), empty, one of FManaged (DoLocals' first pass); FSlotOf stays 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoManagedLocalSlot(const ALocal: int64; const AType: int64);
    var
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      LSlot := self.DoSlot(ALocal, AType, false);
      if LSlot = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoStore(LSlot, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ALocal), ALocal);
      if not self.DoAddManaged(LSlot, AType, ALocal) then
        self.FSlotOf[ALocal] := 0;
      end;
    end;

    // The managed local ALocal (of the canonical type AType, its slot made:
    // DoManagedLocalSlot): its initializer's value stored as an assignment stores it
    // (DoStoreManaged)
    hidden method DoManagedLocalInit(const ALocal: int64; const AType: int64);
    var
      LSlot: int64;
      LInit: int64;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      LSlot := self.FSlotOf[ALocal];
      LInit := self.FTree.FirstOf(ALocal, NodeRole.Initializer);
      if LInit = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(LInit);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      // a temporary initializer gives its reference over (the slot holds none yet)
      if self.DoTakenTemp(LInit) <> 0 then
        self.DoTakeTemp(LSlot, LValue, self.DoTakenTemp(LInit), AType, false, ALocal);
        return;
      end;
      self.DoStoreManaged(LSlot, LValue, AType, ALocal);
    end;

    // The slot of the managed variable AVariable (a text or a dynamic array) that the form
    // ANode changes (an assignment, a `+=`, a write into its units or elements, setlength):
    // the address of the place it names in its write form (DoAddressFor: a local, a value
    // parameter's own copy, a var parameter's target, a module variable, a field, an
    // element, a deref; through parentheses; a dynamic array on the way made its holder's
    // alone); 0 after LW0001 at ANode naming AWhat when AVariable is no place (SEM lets
    // only a variable be changed)
    hidden method DoManagedSlot(const AVariable: int64; const ANode: int64; const AWhat: string): int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AVariable].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression then
        return self.DoManagedSlot(self.FTree.FirstOf(AVariable, NodeRole.Operand), ANode, AWhat);
      end;
      if not self.DoIsPlace(AVariable) then
        self.DoRefuse(ANode, AWhat);
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoAddressFor(AVariable, true);
    end;

    // The first half of reading ASource, the source of an assignment or a `+=` to a text
    // (C++17 orders the source before the target; a class's operator= / += reads a source
    // object only when it runs): a text place's address (APlace true: DoTextSourceValue
    // loads it after the target's address is made, so a target index that changes the
    // source never leaves a freed text behind), else its value (a literal's block, a
    // temporary's text, a char's text: DoConcatSide); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoTextSource(const ASource: int64; var APlace: bool): int64;
    var
      LRoot: int64;
    begin
      LRoot := ASource;
      while self.FTree[LRoot].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LRoot := self.FTree.FirstOf(LRoot, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      APlace := self.DoIsPlace(LRoot) and (self.FTree[LRoot].ResolvedConst.Kind <> ConstKind.String) and
        self.DoIsManaged(self.FTree[LRoot].ResolvedType);
      if APlace then
        return self.DoAddress(LRoot);
      end;
      return self.DoConcatSide(ASource);
    end;

    // The source's text from DoTextSource's AFirst: a place's value loaded now, else AFirst
    hidden method DoTextSourceValue(const AFirst: int64; const APlace: bool; const ANode: int64): int64;
    begin
      if APlace then
        return self.DoLoad(AFirst, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      end;
      return AFirst;
    end;

    // The assignment AId to a text, a dynamic array or a ref: the source first
    // (DoTextSource), the target's slot (DoManagedSlot), then the source's value stored
    // there (DoStoreManaged: a holder added, then the old one released, so `LS := LS` keeps
    // it; a place's own or ref converted to an own I / ref I moved to its itable word as it
    // is loaded, DoReachOwner, I3); a source that is a temporary as a whole gives its
    // reference over (DoTakeTemp)
    hidden method DoManagedAssignment(const AId: int64);
    var
      LFirst: int64;
      LPlace: bool;
      LTarget: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LTaken: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      LSource := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source);
      LTarget := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target);
      if self.DoIsBoundProperty(LTarget) then
        // a property bound to its field: the object first, then the value (BNF sec 4)
        LSlot := self.DoManagedSlot(LTarget, AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        if LSlot = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LFirst := self.DoTextSource(LSource, LPlace);
        if LFirst = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      else
        LFirst := self.DoTextSource(LSource, LPlace);
        if LFirst = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LSlot := self.DoManagedSlot(LTarget, AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        if LSlot = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      LTaken := self.DoTakenTemp(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
      if LTaken <> 0 then
        self.DoTakeTemp(LSlot, LFirst, LTaken, self.FTree[LTarget].ResolvedType, true, AId);
        return;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoTextSourceValue(LFirst, LPlace, AId);
      if LPlace and (self.FTree[LSource].ResolvedConvert <> 0) then
        LValue := self.DoReachOwner(LValue, self.FTree[LSource].ResolvedType, self.FTree[LSource].ResolvedConvert, AId);
      end;
      self.DoStoreManaged(LSlot, LValue, self.FTree[LTarget].ResolvedType, AId);
    end;

    // The temporary the source ASource of an assignment or an initializer is as a whole
    // (through parentheses): a ref new's, a call's, a concatenation's or a utf8 call's
    // reference, kept in its hidden slot (DoTemporaries) and used at its own type or as a
    // ref of an ancestor (DoKeepsBlock); 0 for any other source
    hidden const method DoTakenTemp(const ASource: int64): int64;
    var
      LRoot: int64;
    begin
      LRoot := ASource;
      while self.FTree[LRoot].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LRoot := self.FTree.FirstOf(LRoot, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      if (self.FTempOf[LRoot] = 0) or (not self.DoKeepsBlock(LRoot)) or (not self.DoKeepsBlock(ASource)) or
        self.DoIsCharSide(LRoot) then
        return 0;
      end;
      return LRoot;
    end;

    // True when the expression AId's value is its own block where it is used: it converts
    // to nothing, or it is a ref converted to a ref (of an ancestor: the same block, its
    // object reached through it as before)
    hidden const method DoKeepsBlock(const AId: int64): bool;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConvert = 0 then
        return true;
      end;
      return self.DoIsRefValue(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType) and self.DoIsRefValue(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConvert);
    end;

    // The temporary ATemp's reference AValue (a value of the canonical type AType) taken
    // into the slot ASlot at ANode: the slot's old value released first (AHeld: the slot
    // may hold one), the value stored, the temporary's slot emptied, so the value has one
    // holder and ends when that one lets it go (not at the routine's exit)
    hidden method DoTakeTemp(const ASlot: int64; const AValue: int64; const ATemp: int64;
      const AType: int64; const AHeld: bool; const ANode: int64);
    begin
      if AHeld then
        if not self.DoReleaseAt(ASlot, AType, ANode) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      self.DoStore(ASlot, AValue, ANode);
      self.DoStore(self.DoTempSlot(ATemp), self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ANode), ANode);
    end;

    // The compound assignment AId on a text: `+=` joins the source (DoTextSource: a text, or
    // a char's text kept in its hidden slot) to the target's text by StrConcat, the new
    // reference stored by StrTake (the old one released, so `LS += LS` reads it first); the
    // source first, then the target (C++17's order), as DoCompound; LW0001 for another
    // operator, or a target DoManagedSlot refuses
    hidden method DoStringCompound(const AId: int64);
    var
      LFirst: int64;
      LPlace: bool;
      LSource: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LOld: int64;
      LJoined: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].Op <> OperatorKind.AddAssign then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsBoundProperty(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target)) then
        // a property bound to its field: the object first, then the value (BNF sec 4)
        LSlot := self.DoManagedSlot(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target), AId,
          self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        if LSlot = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LFirst := self.DoTextSource(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source), LPlace);
        if LFirst = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      else
        LFirst := self.DoTextSource(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source), LPlace);
        if LFirst = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LSlot := self.DoManagedSlot(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target), AId,
          self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        if LSlot = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      LSource := self.DoTextSourceValue(LFirst, LPlace, AId);
      LOld := self.DoLoad(LSlot, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      LJoined := self.DoCallRuntime(self.DoTextRoutine(RuntimeRoutine.StrConcat,
        self.FTree[self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target)].ResolvedType), LOld, LSource, AId);
      if LJoined = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrTake, LSlot, LJoined, AId);
    end;

    // True when the compound assignment AId is a string's `+=` with a char source (its
    // one-char string is a temporary, DoTemporaries)
    hidden const method DoIsCharCompound(const AId: int64): bool;
    begin
      return (self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.AssignExpression) and
        (self.FTree[AId].Op = OperatorKind.AddAssign) and
        self.DoIsText(self.FTree[self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target)].ResolvedType) and
        self.DoIsCharSide(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
    end;

    // The address of the unit of a text the index expression AId (through parentheses)
    // names (a string's byte, a wstring's UTF-16 unit): the text first, then the index (as
    // an array's element), the units after the block's header. To write it (AWrite: an
    // assignment, a compound, a step, an `addr of`), the text variable's block is made its
    // own first (StrUnique / WStrUnique: copy on write, a literal's block copied too:
    // DoManagedSlot's variables only); to read it, the text's value (a borrowed one). The
    // index is checked against the text's length in units (DoCheckLength, M3.11a); 0 after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoStringElement(const AId: int64; const AWrite: bool): int64;
    var
      LOperand: int64;
      LText: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LBase: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LScale: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression then
        return self.DoStringElement(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand), AWrite);
      end;
      LOperand := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand);
      LText := self.DoUsedType(LOperand);
      if AWrite then
        LSlot := self.DoManagedSlot(LOperand, AId, "a write through " + self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        if LSlot = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LBase := self.DoCallRuntime(self.DoTextRoutine(RuntimeRoutine.StrUnique, LText), LSlot, 0, AId);
        if not self.DoHoldWritten(LOperand, LBase, LText, AId) then
          return 0;
        end;
      else
        LBase := self.DoManagedValue(LOperand);
      end;
      if LBase = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LIndex := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Index));
      if LIndex = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      // every operand is emitted before the instruction that uses it; a wstring's unit is
      // 2 bytes, so its index counts twice that many
      LIndex := self.DoConvertIr(LIndex, IrType.Int64, AId);
      // the index check counts units: before a wstring's index becomes bytes
      if not self.DoCheckLength(LBase, LIndex, AId) then
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.DoIsWideText(LText) then
        LScale := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, ADAM_LOWERING_WIDE_UNIT, AId);
        LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Mul, IrType.Int64, AId);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LIndex);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LScale);
        LIndex := LId;
      end;
      LBase := self.DoByteOffset(LBase, ADAM_LOWERING_STRING_HEADER, AId);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Offset, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LBase);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LIndex);
      return LId;
    end;

    // Where the place AId is written (an assignment, a compound, a step): DoPlaceAddress's
    // write form (a string's unit, a dynamic array's element, and every dynamic array on
    // the way made its holder's alone first: DoAddressFor); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoWriteAddress(const AId: int64; var AMember: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoPlaceAddress(AId, true, AMember);
    end;

    // The comparison AId of two strings (= <> < <= > >=, SEM's: both sides of the string
    // family): both values, left first, ordered by StrCompare (-1, 0, 1), that order
    // compared with 0 by the operator's signed predicate; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoStringCompare(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LOrder: int64;
      LPredicate: IrPredicate;
    begin
      LPredicate := IrPredicate.Equal;
      if not self.DoPredicateOf(self.FTree[AId].Op, IrType.Int32, LPredicate) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LOrder := self.DoStringOrder(AId);
      if LOrder = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoCompareWith(LPredicate, LOrder, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int32, 0, AId), AId);
    end;

    // StrCompare (WStrCompare for wstrings: both sides are one family, SEM's) of the two
    // text operands of AId (left first): an int32 that is -1, 0 or 1; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoStringOrder(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LLeft: int64;
      LRight: int64;
    begin
      LLeft := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Left));
      if LLeft = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LRight := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Right));
      if LRight = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoCallRuntime(self.DoTextRoutine(RuntimeRoutine.StrCompare,
        self.DoUsedType(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Left))), LLeft, LRight, AId);
    end;

    // True when the call ACall of the intrinsic named AName works on a managed value: len
    // of a text or a dynamic array, setlength of a text or dynamic array variable
    hidden const method DoIsStringIntrinsic(const ACall: int64; const AName: string): bool;
    var
      LFirst: int64;
    begin
      if (AName <> "len") and (AName <> "setlength") then
        return false;
      end;
      LFirst := self.FTree.FirstOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument);
      return (LFirst <> 0) and self.DoIsManaged(self.FTree[LFirst].ResolvedType);
    end;

    // True when the call ACall of the intrinsic named AName is len of a static array (its
    // one argument's canonical type)
    hidden const method DoIsStaticLength(const ACall: int64; const AName: string): bool;
    var
      LFirst: int64;
    begin
      if AName <> "len" then
        return false;
      end;
      LFirst := self.FTree.FirstOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument);
      if LFirst = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      return ClassOf(self.FTree, self.FTree[LFirst].ResolvedType) = TypeClass.StaticArray;
    end;

    // The call ACall of len on a static array (DoIsStaticLength): the argument is lowered
    // for its effects (an index checked, a pointer read, a call run: DoAggregateSource),
    // then the length is the array type's element count (ArrayCount), an int64 constant;
    // LW0001 when the count is unknown; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoStaticLength(const ACall: int64): int64;
    var
      LFirst: int64;
      LCount: int64;
    begin
      LFirst := self.FTree.FirstOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument);
      LCount := ArrayCount(self.FTree, self.FTarget, self.FTree[LFirst].ResolvedType);
      if LCount < 0 then
        self.DoRefuse(ACall, "len of " + self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(LFirst));
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.DoAggregateSource(LFirst) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LCount, ACall);
    end;

    // The call ACall of len or setlength on a managed value (DoIsStringIntrinsic): len is
    // its StrLength (units or elements); setlength(S, N) runs StrSetLength (WStrSetLength,
    // or ArrSetLength with the array type's element map) on S's slot (DoManagedSlot) with N
    // (SEM converted it to int64), S first; the call, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoStringIntrinsic(const ACall: int64; const AName: string): int64;
    var
      LFirst: int64;
      LText: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LLength: int64;
      LMap: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
    begin
      LFirst := self.FTree.FirstOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument);
      if AName = "len" then
        LText := self.DoValue(LFirst);
        if LText = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrLength, LText, 0, ACall);
      end;
      LSlot := self.DoManagedSlot(LFirst, ACall, "setlength on " + self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(LFirst));
      if LSlot = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LLength := self.DoValue(self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, 1));
      if LLength = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.DoIsArrayValue(self.FTree[LFirst].ResolvedType) then
        LMap := self.DoElementMap(self.FTree[LFirst].ResolvedType, ACall);
        if LMap = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LArgs := ref Int64List();
        LArgs.Add(LSlot);
        LArgs.Add(LLength);
        LArgs.Add(LMap);
        return self.DoCallRuntimeSite(RuntimeRoutine.ArrSetLength, LArgs, ACall,
          self.DoArrayWhat(self.FTree[LFirst].ResolvedType));
      end;
      return self.DoCallRuntime(self.DoTextRoutine(RuntimeRoutine.StrSetLength,
        self.FTree[LFirst].ResolvedType), LSlot, LLength, ACall);
    end;

    // The call ACall of the atomic intrinsic AName (BNF sec 7, H4t2): the place's address
    // (its write form, but for atomicload's read), then each value (SEM converted it to the
    // place's type), in order, into one atomic op; atomiccas is a bool, atomicstore void,
    // the others the place's type. The instruction, 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAtomic(const ACall: int64; const AName: string): int64;
    var
      LFirst: int64;
      LOperands: ref Int64List;
      LValue: int64;
      LOp: IrOp;
      LResult: IrType;
      LId: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LOp := DoAtomicOpOf(AName);
      LFirst := self.FTree.FirstOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument);
      LOperands := ref Int64List();
      LValue := self.DoAddressFor(LFirst, LOp <> IrOp.AtomicLoad);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LOperands.Add(LValue);
      for LI := 1 to self.FTree.CountOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument) - 1 do
        LValue := self.DoValue(self.FTree.NthOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument, LI));
        if LValue = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LOperands.Add(LValue);
      end;
      LResult := self.DoIrType(self.FTree[LFirst].ResolvedType);
      if LOp = IrOp.AtomicCas then
        LResult := IrType.Bool;
      end;
      if LOp = IrOp.AtomicStore then
        LResult := IrType.Void;
      end;
      LId := self.DoEmit(LOp, LResult, ACall);
      for LI := 0 to LOperands.Count - 1 do
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LOperands[LI]);
      end;
      return LId;
    end;

    // True for an intrinsic that is a plain call of its runtime routine (SEM wrote it into
    // the call's ResolvedCallee): getmem / resizemem / freemem / paramcount (M3.7e), raise
    // (PLAN-SELFHOST S3: its string, borrowed, to the runtime's Raise, which never returns;
    // a temporary of the argument is released by the frame's cleanup as it unwinds),
    // paramstr (PLAN-SELFHOST S4: a new string, DoIsTextIntrinsicCall), ProjectPassword
    // (PLAN-ADAM T4d1: a new string, its operands the AST's, DoProjectPassword), raisecode
    // (raise's way, with its code), exccode / excmsg (the raise in flight's code and text, a
    // new string), the asserts (AUD6, BNF sec 8: the call's file and line added,
    // DoAssertCall)
    hidden const method DoIsRuntimeIntrinsic(const AName: string): bool;
    begin
      return (AName = "getmem") or (AName = "resizemem") or (AName = "freemem") or
        (AName = "paramcount") or (AName = "paramstr") or (AName = "raise") or
        (AName = "raisecode") or (AName = "ProjectPassword") or (AName = "exccode") or
        (AName = "excmsg") or StartsStr(ADAM_LOWERING_ASSERT_PREFIX, AName);
    end;

    // The call ACall of an assert (BNF sec 8): its runtime routine (AFunction, the
    // routine ARoutine's) called with its arguments (DoEmitCall), then the call's file and
    // line (where the runtime reports a failure), both made before the call; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAssertCall(const ACall: int64; const ARoutine: int64; const AFunction: int64): int64;
    var
      LFile: int64;
      LLine: int64;
      LGiven: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LGiven := self.FTree.CountOf(ACall, NodeRole.Argument);
      LFile := self.DoStringLiteral(ACall, self.FTree[ACall].Place.FileName);
      LLine := self.DoConstant(self.FModule.FunctionAt(AFunction).Signature.ParamTypes[LGiven + 1],
        int64(self.FTree[ACall].Place.Line), ACall);
      LId := self.DoEmitCall(ACall, ARoutine, IrOp.Call, AFunction,
        self.FModule.FunctionAt(AFunction).Signature.ResultType, 0, 0);
      if LId = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LFile);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LLine);
      return LId;
    end;

    // The call ACall of ProjectPassword(): the runtime's ProjectPassword (AFunction) called
    // with the program's scrambled pack password (the AST's ProjectSecret, which the Driver
    // put there) as a constant string block and its key (ProjectKey): the plain text is never
    // in the exe. Semantics refused the call outside a project build (SM0433)
    hidden method DoProjectPassword(const ACall: int64; const AFunction: int64): int64;
    var
      LData: int64;
      LKey: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LData := self.DoStringLiteral(ACall, self.FTree.ProjectSecret);
      LKey := self.DoConstant(self.FModule.FunctionAt(AFunction).Signature.ParamTypes[1],
        int64(self.FTree.ProjectKey), ACall);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Call, self.FModule.FunctionAt(AFunction).Signature.ResultType, ACall);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Link := AFunction;
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LData);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LKey);
      return LId;
    end;

    // True when AId is a call of a runtime intrinsic (DoIsRuntimeIntrinsic) typed a text:
    // its routine returns a new block (a ptr) the caller holds, kept in the call's hidden
    // slot (DoTemporaries, DoRuntimeIntrinsic) and released at the function's exits;
    // DoManagedValue reaches it through parentheses
    hidden const method DoIsTextIntrinsicCall(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LCallee: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind <> NodeKind.CallExpression then
        return false;
      end;
      LCallee := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Callee);
      if NameKindOf(self.FTree, LCallee) <> NodeKind.NameExpression then
        return false;
      end;
      LDecl := self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl;
      if (LDecl = 0) or (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind <> NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) then
        return false;
      end;
      return self.DoIsRuntimeIntrinsic(self.FTree[LDecl].Text) and self.DoIsText(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType);
    end;

    // What the call ACall of the runtime intrinsic AIntrinsic allocates (M3.12b): getmem's
    // and resizemem's blocks by their names, a new string (DoIsTextIntrinsicCall) "string";
    // "" for the others (freemem, paramcount, raise ...)
    hidden const method DoIntrinsicWhat(const ACall: int64; const AIntrinsic: int64): string;
    var
      LName: string;
    begin
      LName := self.FTree[AIntrinsic].Text;
      if (LName = "getmem") or (LName = "resizemem") then
        return LName;
      end;
      if self.DoIsTextIntrinsicCall(ACall) then
        return "string";
      end;
      return "";
    end;

    // The call ACall of the intrinsic AIntrinsic (DoIsRuntimeIntrinsic): its runtime routine
    // (ACall's ResolvedCallee) called with its arguments, which SEM converted to that
    // routine's parameter types (DoEmitCall); a text-typed one's new block taken into the
    // call's hidden slot (DoIsTextIntrinsicCall: StrTake releases what an earlier pass left
    // there); the call, 0 after LW0001 (no runtime unit, or one without the routine)
    hidden method DoRuntimeIntrinsic(const ACall: int64; const AIntrinsic: int64): int64;
    var
      LRoutine: int64;
      LFunction: int64;
      LSite: int64;
      LOuter: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LRoutine := self.FTree[ACall].ResolvedCallee;
      if (LRoutine = 0) or (self.FFunctionOf[LRoutine] = 0) then
        self.DoRefuse(ACall, "a call of " + self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AIntrinsic) + " with no runtime unit");
        return 0;
      end;
      LFunction := self.FFunctionOf[LRoutine];
      // the arguments lower inside the call (DoEmitCall): a runtime call among them gives
      // GAllocSite back to this call's site (FSiteOuter), not to the enclosing one
      LOuter := self.FSiteOuter;
      LSite := self.DoEnterSite(ACall, self.DoIntrinsicWhat(ACall, AIntrinsic));
      if LSite <> 0 then
        self.FSiteOuter := LSite;
      end;
      if self.FTree[AIntrinsic].Text = "ProjectPassword" then
        LId := self.DoProjectPassword(ACall, LFunction);
      else
        if StartsStr(ADAM_LOWERING_ASSERT_PREFIX, self.FTree[AIntrinsic].Text) then
          LId := self.DoAssertCall(ACall, LRoutine, LFunction);
        else
          LId := self.DoEmitCall(ACall, LRoutine, IrOp.Call, LFunction,
            self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.ResultType, 0, 0);
        end;
      end;
      self.FSiteOuter := LOuter;
      self.DoLeaveSite(LSite, ACall);
      if (LId = 0) or not self.DoIsTextIntrinsicCall(ACall) then
        return LId;
      end;
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrTake, self.DoTempSlot(ACall), LId, ACall) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return LId;
    end;

    // The entry function's exit: the runtime's exit routine (the exe module's
    // ResolvedCallee) called with the value ACode (0: the code 0), then its return (never
    // reached)
    hidden method DoExit(const ANode: int64; const ACode: int64);
    var
      LExit: int64;
      LCode: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LExit := self.FFunctionOf[self.FTree[self.FEntryModule].ResolvedCallee];
      LCode := ACode;
      if LCode = 0 then
        LCode := self.DoConstant(self.FModule.FunctionAt(LExit).Signature.ParamTypes[0], 0, ANode);
      end;
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Call, self.FModule.FunctionAt(LExit).Signature.ResultType, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Link := LExit;
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LCode);
      self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, ANode);
    end;

    // The instruction of the call ACall of the signature ASig (a routine, an external or a
    // routine type's signature node): AKind with ALink and the result type AResult, the
    // routine value ATarget its first operand when it is a calli (0: none), then the hidden
    // result slot (FHiddenResult), a method's object address ASelf (0: none, made by the
    // caller before the arguments) and the arguments (DoArguments); 0 after LW0001. An
    // aggregate result lands in a slot keyed by ACall (DoCallResult reads it): the hidden
    // slot (one that holds texts: the call's managed temporary, DoTemporaries, which the
    // callee assigns into), else the register's integer stored into it; a text result, a
    // reference the caller holds, is kept in the call's hidden slot (StrTake)
    hidden method DoEmitCall(const ACall: int64; const ASig: int64; const AKind: IrOp;
      const ALink: int64; const AResult: IrType; const ATarget: int64; const ASelf: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoEmitCallWith(ACall, ASig, AKind, ALink, AResult, ATarget, ASelf, 0, nil);
    end;

    // DoEmitCall's instruction with a generator method's holder AHolder after self (0:
    // none, DoGeneratorHolderArg) and the arguments AArgs already made (an accessor's: the
    // index and a write's value, DoAccessorCall; a task's copies); nil: the call ACall's
    // own (DoArguments)
    hidden method DoEmitCallWith(const ACall: int64; const ASig: int64; const AKind: IrOp;
      const ALink: int64; const AResult: IrType; const ATarget: int64; const ASelf: int64;
      const AHolder: int64; const AArgs: ref Int64List): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LHidden: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LId: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      // The hidden result slot is made before the arguments are lowered (each operand is
      // emitted before the instruction that uses it)
      LType := self.DoResultType(ASig);
      // a result is moved into the caller's slot, never copied: one whose type runs code
      // where it is copied or ended is a temporary under its live flag (DoEndTemporary;
      // an initializer, an assignment, a value argument or a return moves it out)
      LHidden := 0;
      if self.FHiddenResult[ASig] and (self.DoHoldsManaged(LType) or self.DoHasLifetime(LType)) then
        LHidden := self.DoTempSlot(ACall);
        self.FSlotOf[ACall] := LHidden;
      else
        if self.FHiddenResult[ASig] then
          LHidden := self.DoSlot(ACall, LType, false);
          if LHidden = 0 then
            return 0;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      LArgs := AArgs;
      if LArgs = nil then
        LArgs := self.DoArguments(ACall, ASig);
      end;
      if LArgs = nil then
        return 0;
      end;
      LId := self.DoEmit(AKind, AResult, ACall);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Link := ALink;
      if ATarget <> 0 then
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(ATarget);
      end;
      if LHidden <> 0 then
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LHidden);
      end;
      if ASelf <> 0 then
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(ASelf);
      end;
      if AHolder <> 0 then
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(AHolder);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LArgs.Count - 1 do
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LArgs[LI]);
      end;
      // the callee has built (or moved) its object into the call's temporary: live now
      if (LHidden <> 0) and self.DoHasLifetime(LType) then
        self.DoSetLive(ACall, true, ACall);
      end;
      if (LHidden = 0) and self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        LSlot := self.DoSlot(ACall, LType, false);
        if LSlot = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        self.DoStore(LSlot, LId, ACall);
      end;
      if self.DoIsText(LType) then
        if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrTake, self.DoTempSlot(ACall), LId, ACall) = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      // a dynamic array or a ref result, a reference the caller holds, kept in the call's
      // hidden slot: what a previous pass left there released first (ArrRelease, its
      // elements too; RefRelease, its object: StrTake would free the block alone)
      if self.DoIsArrayValue(LType) or self.DoIsOwnerValue(LType) then
        if not self.DoReleaseAt(self.DoTempSlot(ACall), LType, ACall) then
          return 0;
        end;
        self.DoStore(self.DoTempSlot(ACall), LId, ACall);
      end;
      return LId;
    end;

    // The IR signature calls through a value of the canonical routine type AType carry,
    // made the first time from its signature node (DoResultIr, DoFillSignature: its linkage
    // decides by-value / var / const and an aggregate result, as for a routine; a clink
    // variadic one is variadic); 0 after LW0001 at ANode (reported once): one DoPlainSignature
    // refuses, a parameter or result type the slice has none for
    hidden method DoSignatureOf(const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LSig: int64;
      LResult: IrType;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      if self.FSignatureOf[AType] > 0 then
        return self.FSignatureOf[AType];
      end;
      if self.FSignatureOf[AType] < 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.FSignatureOf[AType] := -1;
      LSig := self.FTree[AType].ResolvedDecl;
      if not self.DoPlainSignature(LSig, ANode) then
        return 0;
      end;
      if not self.DoResultIr(LSig, LResult) then
        return 0;
      end;
      if not self.DoParamsFit(LSig) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LId := self.FModule.AddSignature(LResult);
      self.DoFillSignature(LSig, self.FModule.SignatureAt(LId));
      self.FSignatureOf[AType] := LId;
      return LId;
    end;

    // The call ACall through the routine value ACallee (a variable, a parameter, a field, an
    // element, a call's result: anything of a routine type): the value first, then the call
    // (calli) of its type's signature; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoIndirectCall(const ACall: int64; const ACallee: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LSignature: int64;
      LTarget: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.FTree[ACallee].ResolvedType;
      LSignature := self.DoSignatureOf(LType, ACall);
      if LSignature = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LTarget := self.DoValue(ACallee);
      if LTarget = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoEmitCall(ACall, self.FTree[LType].ResolvedDecl, IrOp.CallIndirect, LSignature,
        self.FModule.SignatureAt(LSignature).ResultType, LTarget, 0);
    end;

    // True when the callee ACallee is a routine value (its type a routine type), not a
    // routine's name
    hidden const method DoIsRoutineValue(const ACallee: int64): bool;
    var
      LType: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.FTree[ACallee].ResolvedType;
      return (LType <> 0) and (ClassOf(self.FTree, LType) = TypeClass.RoutineType);
    end;

    // The call ACall: print / println (DoPrint), FormatStr (DoFormatStr), len / setlength on a string
    // (DoStringIntrinsic), len of a static array (DoStaticLength), a routine's or an
    // external's name (call /
    // callx), a routine value (DoIndirectCall); its instruction, 0 when refused (LW0001) or
    // when its routine was refused at its declaration
    hidden method DoCall(const ACall: int64): int64;
    var
      LCallee: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
      LLink: int64;
      LKind: IrOp;
      LResult: IrType;
    begin
      // a binary or unary expression running a type's declared operator (DoOperatorCall)
      LDecl := OperatorCallOf(self.FTree, ACall);
      if LDecl <> 0 then
        return self.DoOperatorCall(ACall, LDecl);
      end;
      LCallee := self.FTree.FirstOf(ACall, NodeRole.Callee);
      LDecl := 0;
      // A member access naming a method: the method runs on its object (DoMethodCall)
      if self.DoMethodMember(ACall) <> 0 then
        return self.DoMethodCall(ACall, LCallee, self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl);
      end;
      if NameKindOf(self.FTree, LCallee) = NodeKind.NameExpression then
        LDecl := self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl;
        if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) and
          ((self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "print") or (self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "println")) then
          return self.DoPrint(ACall, LDecl, self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "println");
        end;
        if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) and
          (self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "FormatStr") then
          return self.DoFormatStr(ACall);
        end;
        if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) and
          self.DoIsRuntimeIntrinsic(self.FTree[LDecl].Text) then
          return self.DoRuntimeIntrinsic(ACall, LDecl);
        end;
        if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) and
          self.DoIsStringIntrinsic(ACall, self.FTree[LDecl].Text) then
          return self.DoStringIntrinsic(ACall, self.FTree[LDecl].Text);
        end;
        if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) and
          self.DoIsStaticLength(ACall, self.FTree[LDecl].Text) then
          return self.DoStaticLength(ACall);
        end;
        if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) and
          DoIsAtomicIntrinsic(self.FTree[LDecl].Text) then
          return self.DoAtomic(ACall, self.FTree[LDecl].Text);
        end;
        if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) and
          (self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "ready") then
          return self.DoReady(ACall);
        end;
        if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) and
          ((self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "cancel") or (self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "cancelled")) then
          return self.DoCancel(ACall, self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "cancel");
        end;
        // workerindex() / workercount(): the for parallel body's parameters (T2; SEM
        // allows them only there)
        if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) and
          ((self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "workerindex") or (self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "workercount")) then
          if self.FWorkerIndex = 0 then
            self.DoRefuse(ACall, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(ACall));
            return 0;
          end;
          if self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "workerindex" then
            return self.FWorkerIndex;
          end;
          return self.FWorkerCount;
        end;
        if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) and
          (self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "alive") then
          return self.DoWeakAlive(ACall);
        end;
        if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) and
          (self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "lock") then
          return self.DoWeakLock(ACall);
        end;
        if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.IntrinsicDecl) and
          ((self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "create") or (self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "destroy")) then
          return self.DoHeapIntrinsic(ACall, self.FTree[LDecl].Text = "create");
        end;
        LDecl := self.DoCalled(LCallee);
      end;
      if LDecl = 0 then
        if self.DoIsRoutineValue(LCallee) then
          return self.DoIndirectCall(ACall, LCallee);
        end;
        if NameKindOf(self.FTree, LCallee) <> NodeKind.NameExpression then
          self.DoRefuse(LCallee, "a call through " + self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(LCallee));
        else
          if self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl = 0 then
            self.DoRefuse(LCallee, "a call of " + self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(LCallee));
          else
            self.DoRefuse(LCallee, "a call of " + self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(self.FTree[LCallee].ResolvedDecl));
          end;
        end;
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.FTree.FirstOf(LDecl, NodeRole.External) <> 0 then
        LKind := IrOp.CallExternal;
        LLink := self.DoExternal(LDecl);
        if LLink = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LResult := self.FModule.ExternalAt(LLink).Signature.ResultType;
      else
        LKind := IrOp.Call;
        LLink := self.FFunctionOf[LDecl];
        if LLink = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LResult := self.FModule.FunctionAt(LLink).Signature.ResultType;
      end;
      return self.DoEmitCall(ACall, LDecl, LKind, LLink, LResult, 0, 0);
    end;

    // The binary or unary expression ACall running the declared operator AOperator (BNF
    // sec 4 operator decl): a call of its function (no self: an operator has none) with the
    // operands as its arguments, in its parameters' order (DoArgument: by value or const
    // as a call's), its result as a call's (DoEmitCallWith: an aggregate in the slot keyed
    // by ACall, DoCallResult); 0 when its function was refused at its declaration or an
    // operand after LW0001
    hidden method DoOperatorCall(const ACall: int64; const AOperator: int64): int64;
    var
      LLink: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LValue: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LLink := self.FFunctionOf[AOperator];
      if LLink = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      for LI := 0 to OperandCount(self.FTree, ACall) - 1 do
        LValue := self.DoArgument(OperandAt(self.FTree, ACall, LI), self.FTree.NthOf(AOperator, NodeRole.Param, LI));
        if LValue = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LArgs.Add(LValue);
      end;
      return self.DoEmitCallWith(ACall, AOperator, IrOp.Call, LLink,
        self.FModule.FunctionAt(LLink).Signature.ResultType, 0, 0, 0, LArgs);
    end;

    // The address the method AMethod runs on for the call's member access AMember (its
    // self): the object's (DoObjectAddress: `P->M()` and `P^.M()` the ptr's value; a place
    // (a variable, a field, an element, self, parent) its address, in DoAddressFor's write
    // form unless the method is a const method (it changes nothing of its object); a call's
    // result its slot, DoAggregateSource), moved to the part of the type that declares
    // AMethod (DoUpcast: an inherited method runs on its own level's part); a method reached
    // through an embed (ResolvedEmbed) runs on the embed (DoEmbedObject, its write form
    // unless the method is a const method), upcast from the embed's type; 0 after LW0001
    // (through a weak, which Semantics refuses first: SM0360; through a ref or an own, the
    // object it holds). The
    // object's anchor (DoObjectAnchor: the block it lies in) is held for the call when the
    // method could drop it (DoAnchorBegin, SU2.8 e3), so self lives through the call
    hidden method DoSelfArgument(const AMember: int64; const AMethod: int64): int64;
    var
      LAnchor: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      LAnchor := self.DoObjectAnchor(self.FTree.FirstOf(AMember, NodeRole.Operand),
        self.FTree[AMember].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Arrow));
      if not self.DoAnchorBegin(LAnchor, not self.FTree[AMethod].HasFlag(NodeFlag.ConstMethod), AMember) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoSelfArgumentIn(AMember, AMethod);
      self.DoAnchorEnd(LAnchor, LAddress <> 0);
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // DoSelfArgument's address, its object's anchor held already
    hidden method DoSelfArgumentIn(const AMember: int64; const AMethod: int64): int64;
    var
      LAddress: int64;
      LType: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AMember].ResolvedEmbed <> 0 then
        LAddress := self.DoEmbedObject(AMember, AMember, not self.FTree[AMethod].HasFlag(NodeFlag.ConstMethod), LType);
        if LAddress = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return self.DoUpcast(LAddress, LType, self.DoOwnerType(AMethod), AMember);
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoObjectAddress(AMember, AMethod);
      if LAddress = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LType := self.DoUsedType(self.FTree.FirstOf(AMember, NodeRole.Operand));
      if self.FTree[AMember].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Arrow) or self.DoIsRefValue(LType) then
        LType := TargetOf(self.FTree, LType);
      end;
      return self.DoUpcast(LAddress, LType, self.DoOwnerType(AMethod), AMember);
    end;

    // The ref a call of the generator method AMethod through the member access AMember
    // reaches its object through (G1c2): the receiver, its parentheses off, when it is a
    // ref (ref T, ref I), the generator then holding its block; 0 for any other receiver
    // (a value, self, an own, a ptr's object: the ramp copies it) and for any other method
    hidden const method DoGeneratorHeld(const AMember: int64; const AMethod: int64): int64;
    var
      LRoot: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoGeneratorMethod(AMethod) then
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.FTree[AMember].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Arrow) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LRoot := self.DoArgRoot(self.FTree.FirstOf(AMember, NodeRole.Operand));
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(LRoot)) = TypeClass.RefType then
        return LRoot;
      end;
      return 0;
    end;

    // The ref AHeld (DoGeneratorHeld; 0: none) read once, before the call's self is made:
    // its value in AValue, handed to self's own reading (FPrimed) so both are one read;
    // false after LW0001
    hidden method DoGeneratorHoldBegin(const AHeld: int64; var AValue: int64): bool;
    begin
      AValue := 0;
      if AHeld = 0 then
        return true;
      end;
      AValue := self.DoManagedValue(AHeld);
      if AValue = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      self.FPrimed[AHeld] := AValue;
      return true;
    end;

    // The ref AHeld's value no longer handed out (DoGeneratorHoldBegin), self made
    hidden method DoGeneratorHoldEnd(const AHeld: int64);
    begin
      if AHeld <> 0 then
        self.FPrimed[AHeld] := 0;
      end;
    end;

    // The hidden holder operand of a call of AMethod at ANode (G1c2), 0 when AMethod is no
    // generator method (DoGeneratorMethod): nil for a receiver the ramp copies (AHeld 0);
    // the block of the ref AHeld whose value is AValue: a ref T's value itself, a ref I's
    // reached back from the object's start ASelf the itable call gives (I3: the object
    // lies past its block's header)
    hidden method DoGeneratorHolderArg(const AMethod: int64; const AHeld: int64; const AValue: int64;
      const ASelf: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoGeneratorMethod(AMethod) then
        return 0;
      end;
      if AHeld = 0 then
        return self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ANode);
      end;
      if self.DoIsInterfaceOwner(self.DoUsedType(AHeld)) then
        return self.DoByteOffset(ASelf, -ADAM_LOWERING_REF_HEADER, ANode);
      end;
      return AValue;
    end;

    // The address of the object AFrom's part of its ancestor ATo (the type that declares a
    // method called on it, a parameter's or a pointer's target), AAddress the AFrom
    // object's, moved by DoReachOffset; AAddress itself when they are one type
    hidden method DoUpcast(const AAddress: int64; const AFrom: int64; const ATo: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoByteOffset(AAddress, self.DoReachOffset(AFrom, ATo), ANode);
    end;

    // The bytes a reference to a value of AFrom moves by to stand for its ancestor ATo
    // (Types.ReachesAs): 0 for one type or between interfaces (an interface's itable starts
    // with its parent's slots, so one word serves both); to an interface, the offset of the
    // object's itable word for it (Layout.InterfaceWordOffset, I2); else the parent parts'
    // between them (DoPartOffset)
    hidden const method DoReachOffset(const AFrom: int64; const ATo: int64): int64;
    var
      LOffset: int64;
    begin
      if (AFrom = ATo) or (AFrom = 0) or (ATo = 0) then
        return 0;
      end;
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, ATo) = TypeClass.InterfaceType then
        if ClassOf(self.FTree, AFrom) = TypeClass.InterfaceType then
          return 0;
        end;
        LOffset := InterfaceWordOffset(self.FTree, AFrom, ATo);
        if LOffset < 0 then
          raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_ITABLE_WORD + TypeText(self.FTree, ATo) + " of " + TypeText(self.FTree, AFrom));
        end;
        return LOffset;
      end;
      return self.DoPartOffset(AFrom, ATo);
    end;

    // The offset of the object AFrom's part of its ancestor ATo from AFrom's start: each
    // parent part between them adds its Parent node's offset (Layout's; 0 for a plain
    // first parent, after the vptr when only the descendant is polymorphic); 0 when they
    // are one type
    hidden const method DoPartOffset(const AFrom: int64; const ATo: int64): int64;
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LPart: int64;
      LOffset: int64;
      LDepth: int64;
    begin
      LAt := AFrom;
      LOffset := 0;
      LDepth := 0;
      while (LAt <> 0) and (LAt <> ATo) and (LDepth <= ADAM_TYPES_MAX_DEPTH) do
        LPart := self.FTree.FirstOf(BodyOf(self.FTree, LAt), NodeRole.Parent);
        if (LPart = 0) or (self.FTree[LPart].ResolvedOffset < 0) then
          raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_FIELD_OFFSET + TypeText(self.FTree, LAt));
        end;
        LOffset := LOffset + self.FTree[LPart].ResolvedOffset;
        LAt := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, LAt);
        LDepth := LDepth + 1;
      end;
      return LOffset;
    end;

    // The address of the object the method call's member access AMember names, before any
    // upcast (DoSelfArgument's first half); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoObjectAddress(const AMember: int64; const AMethod: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoObjectIn(AMember, self.FTree.FirstOf(AMember, NodeRole.Operand),
        self.FTree[AMember].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Arrow), self.FTree[AMethod].HasFlag(NodeFlag.ConstMethod));
    end;

    // The address of the object the value AOperand is (the ptr's value when AArrow), for a
    // method or an accessor that runs on it at ANode: a ref's object, a place's address
    // (its write form unless AConst: the routine changes nothing of its object), a call's
    // result slot (DoAggregateSource); 0 after LW0001 (through a weak, which Semantics
    // refuses first: SM0360)
    hidden method DoObjectIn(const ANode: int64; const AOperand: int64; const AArrow: bool;
      const AConst: bool): int64;
    var
      LRoot: int64;
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      if AArrow then
        return self.DoValue(AOperand);
      end;
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(AOperand));
      if (LClass = TypeClass.RefType) or (LClass = TypeClass.OwnType) then
        return self.DoRefObject(AOperand);
      end;
      if LClass = TypeClass.WeakType then
        self.DoRefuse(ANode, "a method call through '" + TypeText(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(AOperand)) + "'");
        return 0;
      end;
      LRoot := AOperand;
      while self.FTree[LRoot].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LRoot := self.FTree.FirstOf(LRoot, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      if self.DoIsPlace(LRoot) then
        return self.DoAddressFor(LRoot, not AConst);
      end;
      return self.DoAggregateSource(AOperand);
    end;

    // The call ACall of the method AMethod (its callee the member access AMember): a
    // dispatched one through its object's vtable (DoDispatchCall) unless named through
    // parent (`parent.M()` runs the parent's own method, as C++'s qualified call does);
    // else the object's address first (DoSelfArgument: C++17 orders the object before the
    // arguments), then the call with it as self (DoEmitCall); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoMethodCall(const ACall: int64; const AMember: int64; const AMethod: int64): int64;
    var
      LFunction: int64;
      LHeld: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LSelf: int64;
    begin
      // an interface's method runs through the itable of the object behind it (I2)
      if self.DoIsInterfaceMember(AMethod) then
        return self.DoInterfaceCall(ACall, AMember, AMethod);
      end;
      if self.DoIsVtableCall(AMember, AMethod) then
        return self.DoDispatchCall(ACall, AMember, AMethod);
      end;
      LFunction := self.FFunctionOf[AMethod];
      if LFunction = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LHeld := self.DoGeneratorHeld(AMember, AMethod);
      if not self.DoGeneratorHoldBegin(LHeld, LValue) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LSelf := self.DoSelfArgument(AMember, AMethod);
      self.DoGeneratorHoldEnd(LHeld);
      if LSelf = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoEmitCallWith(ACall, AMethod, IrOp.Call, LFunction,
        self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.ResultType, 0, LSelf,
        self.DoGeneratorHolderArg(AMethod, LHeld, LValue, LSelf, ACall), nil);
    end;

    // True when the call of the method AMethod through the member access AMember runs
    // through its object's vtable: a dispatched method not named through parent
    // (`parent.M()` runs the parent's own method, as C++'s qualified call does; `parent.M()`
    // of an embed's M is the embed's M (parent.E.M()), which dispatches as any E.M() does)
    hidden const method DoIsVtableCall(const AMember: int64; const AMethod: int64): bool;
    var
      LOperand: int64;
    begin
      LOperand := self.DoArgRoot(self.FTree.FirstOf(AMember, NodeRole.Operand));
      return self.DoIsDispatched(AMethod) and ((self.FTree[LOperand].Kind <> NodeKind.ParentExpression) or
        (self.FTree[AMember].ResolvedEmbed <> 0));
    end;

    // The call ACall of the dispatched method AMethod through its object's vtable: the
    // object's address (DoSelfArgument, at the declaring level's part: a polymorphic
    // chain shares offset 0 and the vptr there), the function in AMethod's slot of the
    // vtable it points to (DoVtableTarget), then the call (calli) of AMethod's signature
    // with it as self; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoDispatchCall(const ACall: int64; const AMember: int64; const AMethod: int64): int64;
    var
      LSignature: int64;
      LHeld: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LSelf: int64;
      LTarget: int64;
    begin
      LSignature := self.DoMethodSignature(AMethod, ACall);
      if LSignature = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LHeld := self.DoGeneratorHeld(AMember, AMethod);
      if not self.DoGeneratorHoldBegin(LHeld, LValue) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LSelf := self.DoSelfArgument(AMember, AMethod);
      self.DoGeneratorHoldEnd(LHeld);
      if LSelf = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LTarget := self.DoVtableTarget(LSelf, AMethod, ACall);
      return self.DoEmitCallWith(ACall, AMethod, IrOp.CallIndirect, LSignature,
        self.FModule.SignatureAt(LSignature).ResultType, LTarget, LSelf,
        self.DoGeneratorHolderArg(AMethod, LHeld, LValue, LSelf, ACall), nil);
    end;

    // The function in the dispatched method AMethod's slot of the vtable the object at
    // ASelf points to (its vptr at the declaring level's part), read at ANode
    hidden method DoVtableTarget(const ASelf: int64; const AMethod: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LVtable: int64;
      LEntry: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AMethod].ResolvedSlot < 0 then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_SLOT + self.FTree[AMethod].Text);
      end;
      LVtable := self.DoLoad(ASelf, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      LEntry := self.DoByteOffset(LVtable, int64(self.FTree[AMethod].ResolvedSlot) * self.FTarget.PointerSize(),
        ANode);
      return self.DoLoad(LEntry, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
    end;

    // True when the method or accessor AMember is an interface's (its declaring type an
    // interface: I2, it runs through an itable)
    hidden const method DoIsInterfaceMember(const AMember: int64): bool;
    var
      LOwner: int64;
    begin
      LOwner := MethodOwnerOf(self.FTree, AMember);
      return (LOwner <> 0) and (self.FTree[LOwner].Kind = NodeKind.InterfaceType);
    end;

    // The call ACall of the interface method AMethod through its itable (I2): the interface
    // value, the address of the object's itable word (DoSelfArgument: a parent interface
    // shares its word), then the function its slot names and the object's start
    // (DoItableTarget), then the call (calli) of AMethod's signature with the object as
    // self; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoInterfaceCall(const ACall: int64; const AMember: int64; const AMethod: int64): int64;
    var
      LSignature: int64;
      LHeld: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LWord: int64;
      LSelf: int64;
      LTarget: int64;
    begin
      LSignature := self.DoMethodSignature(AMethod, ACall);
      if LSignature = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LHeld := self.DoGeneratorHeld(AMember, AMethod);
      if not self.DoGeneratorHoldBegin(LHeld, LValue) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LWord := self.DoSelfArgument(AMember, AMethod);
      self.DoGeneratorHoldEnd(LHeld);
      if LWord = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LTarget := self.DoItableTarget(LWord, AMethod, ACall, LSelf);
      return self.DoEmitCallWith(ACall, AMethod, IrOp.CallIndirect, LSignature,
        self.FModule.SignatureAt(LSignature).ResultType, LTarget, LSelf,
        self.DoGeneratorHolderArg(AMethod, LHeld, LValue, LSelf, ACall), nil);
    end;

    // The function the interface method AMethod's slot names (past the itable's header
    // words) in the itable the object's itable word at AWord points at, read at ANode, and
    // in ASelf the object's start (the word moved back by the itable's offset, I2)
    hidden method DoItableTarget(const AWord: int64; const AMethod: int64; const ANode: int64;
      var ASelf: int64): int64;
    var
      LTable: int64;
      LBack: int64;
      LEntry: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AMethod].ResolvedSlot < 0 then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_SLOT + self.FTree[AMethod].Text);
      end;
      LTable := self.DoLoad(AWord, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      LBack := self.DoLoad(LTable, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      ASelf := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Offset, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(ASelf).Operands.Add(AWord);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(ASelf).Operands.Add(LBack);
      LEntry := self.DoByteOffset(LTable, (ADAM_LOWERING_ITABLE_HEADER + int64(self.FTree[AMethod].ResolvedSlot)) *
        self.FTarget.PointerSize(), ANode);
      return self.DoLoad(LEntry, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
    end;

    // The IR signature calls of the dispatched method AMethod through a vtable carry
    // (FSignatureOf), made the first time from its declaration as its function's is
    // (DoResultIr, DoParamsFit, DoFillSignature: self after the hidden result); an
    // abstract method has no function, so its calls need this one. 0 after LW0001 at ANode
    // (reported once)
    hidden method DoMethodSignature(const AMethod: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LResult: IrType;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      if self.FSignatureOf[AMethod] > 0 then
        return self.FSignatureOf[AMethod];
      end;
      if self.FSignatureOf[AMethod] < 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.FSignatureOf[AMethod] := -1;
      if not self.DoPlainSignature(AMethod, ANode) then
        return 0;
      end;
      if not self.DoResultIr(AMethod, LResult) then
        return 0;
      end;
      if not self.DoParamsFit(AMethod) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LId := self.FModule.AddSignature(LResult);
      self.DoFillSignature(AMethod, self.FModule.SignatureAt(LId));
      self.FSignatureOf[AMethod] := LId;
      return LId;
    end;

    // The object the property access AId (DoIsPropertyAccess) reads or writes through, and
    // in AArrow whether it is reached through a ptr (`P->X`): X of X.P, X of X.P[i] (the
    // index's operand is the member access naming the same property), X of a default X[i]
    hidden const method DoPropertyObject(const AId: int64; var AArrow: bool): int64;
    var
      LOperand: int64;
    begin
      LOperand := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand);
      AArrow := false;
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.MemberExpression then
        AArrow := self.FTree[AId].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Arrow);
        return LOperand;
      end;
      if (self.FTree[LOperand].Kind = NodeKind.MemberExpression) and
        (self.FTree[LOperand].ResolvedDecl = self.FTree[AId].ResolvedDecl) then
        AArrow := self.FTree[LOperand].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Arrow);
        return self.FTree.FirstOf(LOperand, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      return LOperand;
    end;

    // The call at AId (a property access) of the accessor AAccessor (a read, or a write
    // given its value as the expression ASource or the operand AValue made already, the
    // other 0): self first (the object's address, DoObjectIn: a read changes nothing of its
    // object; moved to the declaring level's part, DoUpcast), then for a dispatched
    // property not named through parent the function in its vtable slot (the read's slot,
    // the write's one after it: Layout), then the index (the property's index parameter,
    // DoArgument) and the value (DoArgument, or DoValueArgument), then the call
    // (DoEmitCallWith, its result kept as a call's is, keyed by AId); an interface's
    // property runs through the itable of the object behind its value (I3: the word moved
    // back by the itable's offset is self, the accessor's slot past the itable's header,
    // the write's one after the read's); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAccessorCall(const AId: int64; const AAccessor: int64; const ASource: int64;
      const AValue: int64): int64;
    var
      LProperty: int64;
      LObject: int64;
      LRoot: int64;
      LAnchor: int64;
      LArrow: bool;
      LDispatch: bool;
      LKind: IrOp;
      LLink: int64;
      LResult: IrType;
      LSelf: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LEmbedAt: int64;
      LTarget: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LParam: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LInterface: bool;
      LTable: int64;
      LBack: int64;
      LWord: int64;
    begin
      LProperty := self.FTree.ParentOf(AAccessor);
      LInterface := self.DoIsInterfaceMember(AAccessor);
      LObject := self.DoPropertyObject(AId, LArrow);
      LRoot := LObject;
      while self.FTree[LRoot].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LRoot := self.FTree.FirstOf(LRoot, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      // `parent.P` runs the parent's own accessor; `parent.P` of an embed's P is the embed's
      // P (parent.E.P), which dispatches as any E.P does
      LDispatch := LInterface or (self.DoIsDispatched(LProperty) and
        ((self.FTree[LRoot].Kind <> NodeKind.ParentExpression) or (self.DoEmbedOf(AId) <> 0)));
      if LDispatch then
        if self.FTree[LProperty].ResolvedSlot < 0 then
          raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_SLOT + self.FTree[LProperty].Text);
        end;
        LKind := IrOp.CallIndirect;
        LLink := self.DoMethodSignature(AAccessor, AId);
        if LLink = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LResult := self.FModule.SignatureAt(LLink).ResultType;
      else
        LKind := IrOp.Call;
        LLink := self.FFunctionOf[AAccessor];
        if LLink = 0 then
          // refused at its declaration (reported there)
          return 0;
        end;
        LResult := self.FModule.FunctionAt(LLink).Signature.ResultType;
      end;
      // the object's anchor held for the call when the accessor could drop it (SU2.8 e3)
      LAnchor := self.DoObjectAnchor(LObject, LArrow);
      if not self.DoAnchorBegin(LAnchor, self.FTree[AAccessor].Kind <> NodeKind.PropertyRead, AId) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LEmbedAt := self.DoEmbedOf(AId);
      if LEmbedAt <> 0 then
        // a property reached through an embed: its accessor runs on the embed
        LSelf := self.DoEmbedObject(LEmbedAt, AId, self.FTree[AAccessor].Kind <> NodeKind.PropertyRead, LType);
        self.DoAnchorEnd(LAnchor, LSelf <> 0);
        if LSelf = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
      else
        LSelf := self.DoObjectIn(AId, LObject, LArrow, self.FTree[AAccessor].Kind = NodeKind.PropertyRead);
        self.DoAnchorEnd(LAnchor, LSelf <> 0);
        if LSelf = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LType := self.DoUsedType(LObject);
        if LArrow or self.DoIsRefValue(LType) then
          LType := TargetOf(self.FTree, LType);
        end;
      end;
      LSelf := self.DoUpcast(LSelf, LType, self.DoOwnerType(AAccessor), AId);
      LTarget := 0;
      if LDispatch then
        LSlot := int64(self.FTree[LProperty].ResolvedSlot);
        if self.FTree[AAccessor].Kind = NodeKind.PropertyWrite then
          LSlot := LSlot + 1;
        end;
        if LInterface then
          // the itable's word: self moves back to the object, the slot is past the header
          LWord := LSelf;
          LTable := self.DoLoad(LWord, IrType.Pointer, AId);
          LBack := self.DoLoad(LTable, IrType.Int64, AId);
          LSelf := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Offset, IrType.Pointer, AId);
          self.FModule.InstrAt(LSelf).Operands.Add(LWord);
          self.FModule.InstrAt(LSelf).Operands.Add(LBack);
          LTarget := self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(LTable, (ADAM_LOWERING_ITABLE_HEADER + LSlot) *
            self.FTarget.PointerSize(), AId), IrType.Pointer, AId);
        else
          LTarget := self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(self.DoLoad(LSelf, IrType.Pointer, AId),
            LSlot * self.FTarget.PointerSize(), AId), IrType.Pointer, AId);
        end;
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LParam := self.FTree.FirstOf(LProperty, NodeRole.Param);
      if LParam <> 0 then
        if self.FTree[AId].Kind <> NodeKind.IndexExpression then
          raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_PROPERTY_INDEX + self.FTree[LProperty].Text);
        end;
        LValue := self.DoArgument(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Index), LParam);
        if LValue = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LArgs.Add(LValue);
      end;
      if self.FTree[AAccessor].Kind = NodeKind.PropertyWrite then
        LParam := self.DoParamAt(AAccessor, self.DoParamCount(AAccessor) - 1);
        if ASource <> 0 then
          LValue := self.DoArgument(ASource, LParam);
        else
          LValue := self.DoValueArgument(AValue, LParam, AId);
        end;
        if LValue = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LArgs.Add(LValue);
      end;
      return self.DoEmitCallWith(AId, AAccessor, LKind, LLink, LResult, LTarget, LSelf, 0, LArgs);
    end;

    // The operand a value AValue made already (a compound assignment's or a step's new
    // value) passes for the write accessor's value parameter AParam, as DoArgument passes
    // an argument: an aggregate's AValue is the address of its own slot
    // (DoPropertySetCompound's), passed as it is by reference or by copy (nothing reads that
    // slot after the call), else its bytes as the register's integer (DoAggregateIr); a
    // managed value (a text held by its temporary: DoPropertyTextCompound) borrowed, by
    // reference the address of a slot holding it (DoManagedReference's way); a scalar by
    // reference the address of a slot holding it, else itself
    hidden method DoValueArgument(const AValue: int64; const AParam: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoDeclType(AParam);
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        if self.FByRef[AParam] or self.FByCopy[AParam] then
          return AValue;
        end;
        return self.DoLoad(AValue, self.DoAggregateIr(LType), ANode);
      end;
      if self.FByRef[AParam] or self.FByCopy[AParam] then
        LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType),
          TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType));
        self.DoStore(LSlot, AValue, ANode);
        return LSlot;
      end;
      return AValue;
    end;

    // The bound field AField of the property access AId (an accessor bound to it, reached
    // through its object: DoPropertyObject, DoFieldAddressIn; AWrite its write form; a
    // property reached through an embed, the field in the embed: DoEmbedObject); a
    // bitfield's is its lane's (DoFieldBitRead / DoFieldBitWrite reach the field in it);
    // 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoBoundAddress(const AId: int64; const AField: int64; const AWrite: bool): int64;
    var
      LArrow: bool;
      LObject: int64;
      LEmbedAt: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LBase: int64;
    begin
      LEmbedAt := self.DoEmbedOf(AId);
      if LEmbedAt <> 0 then
        LBase := self.DoEmbedObject(LEmbedAt, AId, AWrite, LType);
        if LBase = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return self.DoByteOffset(LBase, self.DoMemberOffset(LType, AField), AId);
      end;
      LObject := self.DoPropertyObject(AId, LArrow);
      return self.DoFieldAddressIn(AId, LObject, LArrow, AField, AWrite);
    end;

    // The value the property access AId (DoIsPropertyAccess) reads: a read bound to a
    // field of a property that does not dispatch is that field's (DoBoundAddress: a text's
    // or a dynamic array's block borrowed, as a place's; an aggregate its address); any
    // other read is its accessor's call (DoAccessorCall: an aggregate result's slot, as
    // DoCallResult gives it); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPropertyGet(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LProperty: int64;
      LRead: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
      LCall: int64;
    begin
      LProperty := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedDecl;
      LRead := self.FTree.FirstOf(LProperty, NodeRole.Read);
      LType := self.DoDeclType(LProperty);
      if self.DoIsBound(LRead) and (not self.DoIsDispatched(LProperty)) then
        LAddress := self.DoBoundAddress(AId, self.FTree[LRead].ResolvedDecl, false);
        if (LAddress = 0) or self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
          return LAddress;
        end;
        if self.FTree[self.FTree[LRead].ResolvedDecl].ResolvedBitWidth >= 0 then
          return self.DoFieldBitRead(self.FTree[LRead].ResolvedDecl, LAddress, AId);
        end;
        if self.DoIsManaged(LType) then
          return self.DoLoad(LAddress, IrType.Pointer, AId);
        end;
        LIr := self.DoTypeAt(LType, AId);
        if LIr = IrType.Void then
          return 0;
        end;
        return self.DoLoad(LAddress, LIr, AId);
      end;
      LCall := self.DoAccessorCall(AId, LRead, 0, 0);
      if (LCall = 0) or (not self.DoIsAggregate(LType)) then
        return LCall;
      end;
      if self.FSlotOf[AId] = 0 then
        raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_CALL_RESULT + self.FTree.ConstructText(AId));
      end;
      return self.FSlotOf[AId];
    end;

    // True when the property access AId reads through its read accessor's function (a body,
    // or a dispatched property) a value that is or holds managed values: its result is a
    // temporary in a hidden slot, as a call's (DoTemporaries, DoResultTemporary). A member
    // access naming an indexed property is never read alone (the index reads it)
    hidden const method DoIsManagedPropertyCall(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LProperty: int64;
      LType: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoIsPropertyAccess(AId) then
        return false;
      end;
      LProperty := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedDecl;
      if (self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.MemberExpression) and (self.FTree.FirstOf(LProperty, NodeRole.Param) <> 0) then
        return false;
      end;
      if self.DoIsBound(self.FTree.FirstOf(LProperty, NodeRole.Read)) and (not self.DoIsDispatched(LProperty)) then
        return false;
      end;
      LType := self.DoDeclType(LProperty);
      return self.DoIsManaged(LType) or (self.DoIsAggregate(LType) and self.DoHoldsManaged(LType));
    end;

    // The property access ATarget written: its value the expression ASource or the operand
    // AValue made already (the other 0). A write bound to a field of a property that does
    // not dispatch stores into that field as an assignment does (the value first, then the
    // field's address, DoBoundAddress: a managed value by DoStoreManaged, an aggregate
    // copied); any other write is its accessor's call (DoAccessorCall). SEM has made sure
    // there is a write (SM0375)
    hidden method DoPropertySet(const ATarget: int64; const ASource: int64; const AValue: int64);
    var
      LProperty: int64;
      LWrite: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LFrom: int64;
    begin
      LProperty := self.FTree[ATarget].ResolvedDecl;
      LWrite := PropertyWriteOf(self.FTree, LProperty);
      if (not self.DoIsBound(LWrite)) or self.DoIsDispatched(LProperty) then
        self.DoAccessorCall(ATarget, LWrite, ASource, AValue);
        return;
      end;
      LType := self.DoDeclType(LProperty);
      LValue := AValue;
      if ASource <> 0 then
        if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
          LValue := self.DoAggregateSource(ASource);
        else
          LValue := self.DoValue(ASource);
        end;
      end;
      if LValue = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoBoundAddress(ATarget, self.FTree[LWrite].ResolvedDecl, true);
      if LAddress = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[self.FTree[LWrite].ResolvedDecl].ResolvedBitWidth >= 0 then
        self.DoFieldBitWrite(self.FTree[LWrite].ResolvedDecl, LAddress, LValue, ATarget);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        // a call's result of a type that runs code where it is copied or ended moves in
        // over the field's old value (ended first), any other value is assigned
        if self.DoHasLifetime(LType) and (ASource <> 0) then
          LFrom := self.DoMoveSource(ASource);
          if (LFrom <> 0) and self.DoIsCallSite(LFrom) then
            if self.DoReleaseAt(LAddress, LType, ATarget) then
              self.DoMoveObject(LAddress, LValue, LFrom, LType, ATarget);
            end;
            return;
          end;
        end;
        self.DoAggregateCopy(LAddress, LValue, LType, ATarget);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsManaged(LType) then
        self.DoStoreManaged(LAddress, LValue, LType, ATarget);
        return;
      end;
      self.DoStore(LAddress, LValue, ATarget);
    end;

    // The assignment AId to the property access ATarget: ':=' writes the source
    // (DoPropertySet); a compound assignment reads the property (DoPropertyGet) after its
    // value (C++17's order, as DoCompound), combines them and writes the result back: a
    // typed ptr's (DoPropertyPointerCompound), a set's (DoPropertySetCompound), a text's
    // (DoPropertyTextCompound), an integer's or a float's at the property's type; LW0001
    // for an operator the type does not take
    hidden method DoPropertyAssign(const AId: int64; const ATarget: int64);
    var
      LOp: IrOp;
      LType: IrType;
      LValue: int64;
      LOld: int64;
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].Op = OperatorKind.Assign then
        self.DoPropertySet(ATarget, self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source), 0);
        return;
      end;
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, self.FTree[ATarget].ResolvedType);
      if LClass = TypeClass.Pointer then
        self.DoPropertyPointerCompound(AId, ATarget);
        return;
      end;
      if LClass = TypeClass.SetType then
        self.DoPropertySetCompound(AId, ATarget);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsText(self.FTree[ATarget].ResolvedType) then
        self.DoPropertyTextCompound(AId, ATarget);
        return;
      end;
      LOp := IrOp.Add;
      LType := self.DoIrType(self.FTree[ATarget].ResolvedType);
      if (not self.DoCompoundIrOp(self.FTree[AId].Op, LOp)) or (not self.DoOpFits(LOp, LType)) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
      if LValue = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LOld := self.DoPropertyGet(ATarget);
      if LOld = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoPropertySet(ATarget, 0, self.DoComputeIn(LOp, LOld, LValue, LType, AId));
    end;

    // The compound assignment AId on the typed ptr property ATarget: `+=` / `-=` move its
    // value by the source's count of elements (DoMovePointer; the source first, then the
    // read, as DoPointerCompound) and write it back; LW0001 for any other operator
    hidden method DoPropertyPointerCompound(const AId: int64; const ATarget: int64);
    var
      LOp: OperatorKind;
      LValue: int64;
      LOld: int64;
    begin
      LOp := self.FTree[AId].Op;
      if (LOp <> OperatorKind.AddAssign) and (LOp <> OperatorKind.SubtractAssign) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
      if LValue = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LOld := self.DoPropertyGet(ATarget);
      if LOld = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoPropertySet(ATarget, 0, self.DoMovePointer(LOld, LValue, self.FTree[ATarget].ResolvedType,
        LOp = OperatorKind.SubtractAssign, AId));
    end;

    // The compound assignment AId on the set property ATarget (+= -= *= &= |=): the
    // source's address first, then the property read (an aggregate: its address), both
    // combined lane by lane into a slot of its own keyed by AId (DoSetLanesInto, as
    // DoSetOperation builds a set), and that slot written (DoPropertySet with its address)
    hidden method DoPropertySetCompound(const AId: int64; const ATarget: int64);
    var
      LType: int64;
      LSetOp: OperatorKind;
      LSource: int64;
      LOld: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.FTree[ATarget].ResolvedType;
      LSetOp := OperatorKind.None;
      if not self.DoSetOpOf(self.FTree[AId].Op, LSetOp) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return;
      end;
      LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
      if LSource = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LOld := self.DoPropertyGet(ATarget);
      if LOld = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LSlot := self.DoSlot(AId, LType, false);
      if LSlot = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoSetLanesInto(LSlot, LOld, LSource, LType, LSetOp, AId);
      self.DoPropertySet(ATarget, 0, LSlot);
    end;

    // The compound assignment AId on the text property ATarget: `+=` reads the source
    // first (DoTextSource, as DoStringCompound), then the property (DoPropertyGet: its
    // field's text borrowed, or its read's result, a temporary), joins them by StrConcat
    // into AId's own temporary (DoTemporaries: DoIsPropertyTextCompound; ended with its
    // full expression, so a write that raises leaves nothing behind) and writes that text
    // (DoPropertySet: a bound field takes a holder, an accessor's value parameter adds its
    // own); LW0001 for another operator
    hidden method DoPropertyTextCompound(const AId: int64; const ATarget: int64);
    var
      LFirst: int64;
      LPlace: bool;
      LOld: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LJoined: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].Op <> OperatorKind.AddAssign then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return;
      end;
      LFirst := self.DoTextSource(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source), LPlace);
      if LFirst = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LOld := self.DoPropertyGet(ATarget);
      if LOld = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LSource := self.DoTextSourceValue(LFirst, LPlace, AId);
      LJoined := self.DoCallRuntime(self.DoTextRoutine(RuntimeRoutine.StrConcat,
        self.FTree[ATarget].ResolvedType), LOld, LSource, AId);
      if LJoined = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrTake, self.DoTempSlot(AId), LJoined, AId) = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoPropertySet(ATarget, 0, LJoined);
    end;

    // True when AId is a `+=` on a text property (through parentheses) written by its
    // accessors: its joined text is a temporary of its own (DoPropertyTextCompound)
    hidden const method DoIsPropertyTextCompound(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LTarget: int64;
    begin
      if (self.FTree[AId].Kind <> NodeKind.AssignExpression) or
        (self.FTree[AId].Op <> OperatorKind.AddAssign) then
        return false;
      end;
      LTarget := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target);
      while self.FTree[LTarget].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LTarget := self.FTree.FirstOf(LTarget, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      return self.DoIsPropertyAccess(LTarget) and self.DoIsText(self.FTree[LTarget].ResolvedType);
    end;

    // The step AId (`++` / `--`) of the property access AOperand, an integer or a typed
    // ptr (BNF sec 4, his rule 2026-11-10: as X += 1): read (DoPropertyGet), one added or
    // taken away (a ptr moved by one element: DoMovePointer), written back
    // (DoPropertySet); the new value for a prefix step (APrefix), the old one for a postfix;
    // 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPropertyStep(const AId: int64; const AOperand: int64; const APrefix: bool): int64;
    var
      LType: IrType;
      LOp: IrOp;
      LOld: int64;
      LNew: int64;
      LPointer: bool;
    begin
      LType := self.DoIrType(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType);
      LPointer := ClassOf(self.FTree, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType) = TypeClass.Pointer;
      if (not LPointer) and (not IsIntegerType(LType)) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LOp := IrOp.Add;
      if self.FTree[AId].Op = OperatorKind.Decrement then
        LOp := IrOp.Sub;
      end;
      LOld := self.DoPropertyGet(AOperand);
      if LOld = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if LPointer then
        LNew := self.DoMovePointer(LOld, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 1, AId), self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType,
          LOp = IrOp.Sub, AId);
      else
        LNew := self.DoComputeIn(LOp, LOld, self.DoConstant(LType, 1, AId), LType, AId);
      end;
      self.DoPropertySet(AOperand, 0, LNew);
      if APrefix then
        return LNew;
      end;
      return LOld;
    end;

    // The routine value of AId, a name of a routine (DoCalled): codeaddr of its function,
    // importaddr of an external; 0 when it was refused at its declaration (reported there)
    hidden method DoRoutineValue(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LDecl: int64;
      LLink: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LDecl := self.DoCalled(AId);
      if self.FTree.FirstOf(LDecl, NodeRole.External) <> 0 then
        LLink := self.DoExternal(LDecl);
        if LLink = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.ImportAddress, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      else
        LLink := self.FFunctionOf[LDecl];
        if LLink = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.CodeAddress, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      end;
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Link := LLink;
      return LId;
    end;

    // The bool ALeft APredicate ARight, at ANode (both of one type: Ssa's compare)
    hidden method DoCompareWith(const APredicate: IrPredicate; const ALeft: int64;
      const ARight: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Compare, IrType.Bool, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Predicate := APredicate;
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(ALeft);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(ARight);
      return LId;
    end;

    // The value AValue (of the canonical type AFrom) as the canonical type ATo, at ANode:
    // AValue itself when both travel as one IR type; to bool, C++'s `AValue <> 0` (an
    // integer, a ptr: nil is false; a float by une, so -0.0 is false and a NaN true, as
    // C++'s `x != 0`); else a convert (extension by AFrom's signedness, truncation, or a
    // move between ptr and a 64-bit integer); 0 after LW0001 when ATo has no IR type, or
    // AValue none bool takes
    hidden method DoConvertTo(const AValue: int64; const AFrom: int64; const ATo: int64;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: IrType;
      LFrom: IrType;
    begin
      LType := self.DoIrType(ATo);
      LFrom := self.FModule.InstrAt(AValue).ValueType;
      if (ClassOf(self.FTree, AFrom) = TypeClass.Pointer) and (ClassOf(self.FTree, ATo) = TypeClass.Pointer) then
        return self.DoReachPointer(AValue, AFrom, ATo, ANode);
      end;
      if LType = LFrom then
        return AValue;
      end;
      if (LType = IrType.Bool) and (IsIntegerType(LFrom) or (LFrom = IrType.Pointer)) then
        return self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.NotEqual, AValue, self.DoConstant(LFrom, 0, ANode),
          ANode);
      end;
      if (LType = IrType.Bool) and IsFloatType(LFrom) then
        return self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.FNotEqual, AValue, self.DoConstant(LFrom, 0, ANode),
          ANode);
      end;
      if (LType = IrType.Void) or (LType = IrType.Bool) then
        self.DoRefuse(ANode, "a conversion from '" + TypeText(self.FTree, AFrom) + "' to '" +
          TypeText(self.FTree, ATo) + "'");
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoConvertIr(AValue, LType, ANode);
    end;

    // The ptr AValue of the canonical type AFrom as the ptr type ATo (BNF sec 6: a ptr to T
    // converts to a ptr to an ancestor of T, Types.ReachesAs; a pointer cast also back down
    // and across), at ANode, nil staying nil (each move a block of its own past a nil test,
    // joined by a phi): to an ancestor, moved to its part (DoReachOffset: a parent part's
    // offset, an interface's itable word, I2); from an interface, or to an interface from a
    // polymorphic object, through the object behind it (DoCrossPointer); to a descendant
    // object or record, moved back by the ancestor part's offset in it (DoPartOffset);
    // AValue itself for any other pair (an untyped ptr, an unrelated target)
    hidden method DoReachPointer(const AValue: int64; const AFrom: int64; const ATo: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LFromTarget: int64;
      LToTarget: int64;
    begin
      LFromTarget := TargetOf(self.FTree, AFrom);
      LToTarget := TargetOf(self.FTree, ATo);
      if (LFromTarget = LToTarget) or not self.DoIsReachable(LFromTarget) or not self.DoIsReachable(LToTarget) then
        return AValue;
      end;
      if IsAncestorOf(self.FTree, LToTarget, LFromTarget) then
        return self.DoMoveUnlessNil(AValue, self.DoReachOffset(LFromTarget, LToTarget), ANode);
      end;
      if self.DoIsInterface(LFromTarget) then
        return self.DoCrossPointer(AValue, LFromTarget, LToTarget, ANode);
      end;
      if self.DoIsInterface(LToTarget) then
        if (ClassOf(self.FTree, LFromTarget) = TypeClass.ObjectType) and IsPolymorphic(self.FTree, LFromTarget) then
          return self.DoCrossPointer(AValue, LFromTarget, LToTarget, ANode);
        end;
        return AValue;
      end;
      if IsAncestorOf(self.FTree, LFromTarget, LToTarget) then
        return self.DoMoveUnlessNil(AValue, -self.DoPartOffset(LToTarget, LFromTarget), ANode);
      end;
      return AValue;
    end;

    // The ptr AValue to an AFromTarget (an interface, or a polymorphic object) cast to a ptr
    // to the unrelated AToTarget (BNF sec 6 pointer cast, I3: an interface is a virtual
    // base, so the address moves), at ANode; nil stays nil (a block of its own past a nil
    // test, joined by a phi). The object's start first: an interface's itable word moved
    // back by its itable's offset (as DoTestedObject), a polymorphic object's own address.
    // To an object type, that start (a polymorphic type's part is at 0 of any descendant; a
    // plain one sits past the vptr, aligned as it is); to an interface, its itable word in
    // that object, found by the runtime's InterfaceOffset over its dynamic TypeInfo, nil when
    // the object has none (an unchecked cast never raises: `as` is the checked form). 0
    // after LW0001
    hidden method DoCrossPointer(const AValue: int64; const AFromTarget: int64; const AToTarget: int64;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LNil: int64;
      LIsNil: int64;
      LStart: int64;
      LMove: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
      LBack: int64;
      LObject: int64;
      LResult: int64;
      LMoveEnd: int64;
      LTarget: int64;
      LOffset: int64;
      LFound: int64;
      LGood: int64;
      LInner: int64;
      LWord: int64;
      LLookEnd: int64;
    begin
      // nil made before the branch: the join's operand from the nil edge
      LNil := self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ANode);
      LIsNil := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.Equal, AValue, LNil, ANode);
      LStart := self.FBlock;
      LMove := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(LIsNil, LJoin, LMove, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LMove;
      LObject := AValue;
      if self.DoIsInterface(AFromTarget) then
        // the itable's first word: the offset back from the itable word to the object's start
        LBack := self.DoLoad(self.DoLoad(AValue, IrType.Pointer, ANode), IrType.Int64, ANode);
        LObject := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Offset, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LObject).Operands.Add(AValue);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LObject).Operands.Add(LBack);
      end;
      if not self.DoIsInterface(AToTarget) then
        LResult := LObject;
        if not IsPolymorphic(self.FTree, AToTarget) then
          // a plain ancestor of the polymorphic object: placed past its vptr (Layout's
          // DoObjectBase)
          LResult := self.DoByteOffset(LObject, AlignUp(self.FTarget.PointerSize(),
            TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AToTarget)), ANode);
        end;
      else
        LTarget := self.DoTypeInfoAddress(AToTarget, ANode);
        if LTarget = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LOffset := self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.InterfaceOffset, self.DoDynamicTypeInfo(LObject, ANode), LTarget,
          ANode);
        if LOffset = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        LFound := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.SGreaterEqual, LOffset, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, ANode), ANode);
        LLookEnd := self.FBlock;
        LGood := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
        LInner := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
        self.DoBranchOn(LFound, LGood, LInner, ANode);
        self.FBlock := LGood;
        LWord := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Offset, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LWord).Operands.Add(LObject);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LWord).Operands.Add(LOffset);
        self.DoJumpTo(LInner, ANode);
        self.FBlock := LInner;
        LResult := self.DoJoinOf(IrType.Pointer, LWord, LGood, LNil, LLookEnd, ANode);
      end;
      LMoveEnd := self.FBlock;
      self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LJoin;
      return self.DoJoinOf(IrType.Pointer, LResult, LMoveEnd, LNil, LStart, ANode);
    end;

    // The pointer AValue moved by AOffset bytes unless it is nil (nil stays nil: the move is
    // a block of its own past a nil test, joined by a phi), at ANode; AValue itself when
    // AOffset is 0
    hidden method DoMoveUnlessNil(const AValue: int64; const AOffset: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LIsNil: int64;
      LStart: int64;
      LMove: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
      LMoved: int64;
    begin
      if AOffset = 0 then
        return AValue;
      end;
      LIsNil := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.Equal, AValue, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ANode), ANode);
      LStart := self.FBlock;
      LMove := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(LIsNil, LJoin, LMove, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LMove;
      LMoved := self.DoByteOffset(AValue, AOffset, ANode);
      self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LJoin;
      return self.DoJoinOf(IrType.Pointer, AValue, LStart, LMoved, LMove, ANode);
    end;

    // True when the call AId names a type: a cast written as a call (BNF sec 6, TColor(N))
    hidden const method DoIsCastCall(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      LDecl := self.FTree[self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Callee)].ResolvedDecl;
      if LDecl = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      return (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.TypeDecl) or
        (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.ForwardType);
    end;

    // The code unit ACode (one UTF-16 unit) added to the blob AData, little-endian
    hidden method DoAddUnit16(const AData: int64; const ACode: uint32);
    begin
      self.FModule.DataAt(AData).AddByte(uint8(ACode & 0xFF));
      self.FModule.DataAt(AData).AddByte(uint8((ACode >> 8) & 0xFF));
    end;

    // The string literal ALiteral as the C string a ptr to const char / wchar APtrType
    // points at (BNF sec 6 pointer cast, a literal's type-driven form): a read-only blob of
    // its bytes and a NUL (char), or its text as UTF-16 code units and a NUL unit (wchar:
    // the target's 16 bits, a code point past 0xFFFF as its surrogate pair); its address
    hidden method DoCStringLiteral(const ALiteral: int64; const APtrType: int64): int64;
    var
      LText: string;
      LWide: bool;
      LData: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LCode: uint32;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LText := self.FTree[ALiteral].ResolvedConst.Text;
      LWide := ClassOf(self.FTree, TargetOf(self.FTree, APtrType)) = TypeClass.WideChar;
      if LWide then
        LData := self.DoHelperData(ADAM_LOWERING_TEXT_SYMBOL,
          2, ALiteral);
        LI := 0;
        while LI < len(LText) do
          LCode := DecodeUtf8Char(LText, LI);
          if LCode > 0xFFFF then
            // A surrogate pair: the high ten bits, then the low ten, of LCode - 0x10000
            LCode := LCode - 0x10000;
            self.DoAddUnit16(LData, 0xD800 + (LCode >> 10));
            self.DoAddUnit16(LData, 0xDC00 + (LCode & 0x3FF));
          else
            self.DoAddUnit16(LData, LCode);
          end;
        end;
        self.DoAddUnit16(LData, 0);
      else
        LData := self.DoHelperData(ADAM_LOWERING_TEXT_SYMBOL,
          1, ALiteral);
        for LI := 0 to len(LText) - 1 do
          self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(uint8(LText[LI]));
        end;
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(uint8(0));
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ALiteral);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := LData;
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // AId with its parentheses off
    hidden const method DoUnparen(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LAt := AId;
      while self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LAt := self.FTree.FirstOf(LAt, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      return LAt;
    end;

    // The cast AId (a type cast, a pointer cast, a call naming a type) of AOperand: the
    // operand's value as AId's type (a string literal into a ptr to const char / wchar its C
    // string, DoCStringLiteral); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoCast(const AId: int64; const AOperand: int64): int64;
    var
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      if (self.FTree[self.DoUnparen(AOperand)].Kind = NodeKind.StringLiteral) and
        IsPointerClass(ClassOf(self.FTree, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType)) then
        return self.DoCStringLiteral(self.DoUnparen(AOperand), self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType);
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(AOperand);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoConvertTo(LValue, self.DoUsedType(AOperand), self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType, AId);
    end;

    // The IR op of the binary operator AOp, in AIrOp; true when the slice lowers it (+ - * /
    // & | xor shl shr div mod: BNF sec 6, one OperatorKind per meaning; shr's is the logical
    // shift, DoBinary makes a signed one sar; div / mod's the signed division, DoBinary makes
    // an unsigned one udiv / urem; `/` is real division, fdiv, its operands floats by SEM).
    // DoOpFits says which types each takes
    hidden const method DoBinaryIrOp(const AOp: OperatorKind; var AIrOp: IrOp): bool;
    begin
      if AOp = OperatorKind.Divide then
        AIrOp := IrOp.FDiv;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.Add then
        AIrOp := IrOp.Add;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.Subtract then
        AIrOp := IrOp.Sub;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.Multiply then
        AIrOp := IrOp.Mul;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.BitAnd then
        AIrOp := IrOp.BitAnd;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.BitOr then
        AIrOp := IrOp.BitOr;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.Xor then
        AIrOp := IrOp.BitXor;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.ShiftLeft then
        AIrOp := IrOp.Shl;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.ShiftRight then
        AIrOp := IrOp.Shr;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.IntDivide then
        AIrOp := IrOp.SDiv;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.Modulo then
        AIrOp := IrOp.SRem;
        return true;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // True when the IR op AOp of an operator or a compound runs on AType: on a float add, sub,
    // mul and fdiv (C++'s float operators; the bit operators, shifts, div and mod take no
    // float: SEM refuses them first); on an integer every op but fdiv
    hidden const method DoOpFits(const AOp: IrOp; const AType: IrType): bool;
    begin
      if IsFloatType(AType) then
        return (AOp = IrOp.Add) or (AOp = IrOp.Sub) or (AOp = IrOp.Mul) or (AOp = IrOp.FDiv);
      end;
      return IsIntegerType(AType) and (AOp <> IrOp.FDiv);
    end;

    // The IR op AOp as the machine runs it on AType: a right shift of a signed type is sar,
    // a div / mod of an unsigned one udiv / urem (DESIGN sec 6: truncation toward zero
    // either way, the remainder's sign the dividend's)
    hidden const method DoMachineOp(const AOp: IrOp; const AType: IrType): IrOp;
    begin
      if (AOp = IrOp.Shr) and IsSignedType(AType) then
        return IrOp.Sar;
      end;
      if (AOp = IrOp.SDiv) and (not IsSignedType(AType)) then
        return IrOp.UDiv;
      end;
      if (AOp = IrOp.SRem) and (not IsSignedType(AType)) then
        return IrOp.URem;
      end;
      return AOp;
    end;

    // The value AValue as the IR type AType, at ANode: AValue itself when it already is,
    // else a convert (extension by AValue's signedness, truncation, or a move between ptr
    // and a 64-bit integer)
    hidden method DoConvertIr(const AValue: int64; const AType: IrType; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LId: int64;
    begin
      if self.FModule.InstrAt(AValue).ValueType = AType then
        return AValue;
      end;
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Convert, AType, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(AValue);
      return LId;
    end;

    // ALeft AOp ARight for a step or a compound assignment on a target of the integer or
    // float type AType, at ANode, as AType again: C++ computes it at the promoted type (an
    // 8 / 16-bit type at int32, BNF sec 6; a float at its own) and converts the result back.
    // ALeft is of AType, ARight too except a shift's count, which keeps its own type (never
    // converted). Computing a narrow target at int32 is also what keeps `int8 -128 %= -1`
    // from an 8-bit idiv's fault
    hidden method DoComputeIn(const AOp: IrOp; const ALeft: int64; const ARight: int64;
      const AType: IrType; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LWide: IrType;
      LLeft: int64;
      LRight: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LWide := AType;
      if (AType = IrType.Int8) or (AType = IrType.Int16) or (AType = IrType.UInt8) or
        (AType = IrType.UInt16) then
        LWide := IrType.Int32;
      end;
      LLeft := self.DoConvertIr(ALeft, LWide, ANode);
      LRight := ARight;
      if (AOp <> IrOp.Shl) and (AOp <> IrOp.Shr) then
        LRight := self.DoConvertIr(ARight, LWide, ANode);
      end;
      LId := self.DoEmit(self.DoMachineOp(AOp, LWide), LWide, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LLeft);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LRight);
      return self.DoConvertIr(LId, AType, ANode);
    end;

    // The distance in elements from the ptr ARight to the ptr ALeft, both of the typed ptr
    // type APtrType, at ANode: their byte distance as int64, divided by the element's size
    // (signed: a ptr below the other gives a negative count, BNF sec 4 `ptr - ptr`). A
    // zero-size element's two ptrs are counted in bytes (no divide by zero)
    hidden method DoPointerDistance(const ALeft: int64; const ARight: int64;
      const APtrType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LLeft: int64;
      LRight: int64;
      LBytes: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LScale: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      // every operand is emitted before the instruction that uses it
      LLeft := self.DoConvertIr(ALeft, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LRight := self.DoConvertIr(ARight, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LBytes := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Sub, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LBytes).Operands.Add(LLeft);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LBytes).Operands.Add(LRight);
      LSize := self.DoElementSize(APtrType);
      if (LSize = 0) or (LSize = 1) then
        return LBytes;
      end;
      LScale := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LSize, ANode);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.SDiv, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LBytes);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LScale);
      return LId;
    end;

    // The binary AId when it is a pointer's arithmetic (SEM's DoAdditive: `ptr + n`,
    // `n + ptr`, `ptr - n` a ptr moved by n elements; `ptr - ptr` the elements between, an
    // int64), its value in AValue (0 after LW0001), the operands left to right; false when
    // AId is no `+` / `-` on a typed ptr
    hidden method DoPointerArithmetic(const AId: int64; var AValue: int64): bool;
    var
      LOp: OperatorKind;
      LLeft: int64;
      LRight: int64;
      LLeftType: int64;
      LRightType: int64;
      LLeftIsPtr: bool;
      LRightIsPtr: bool;
      LLeftValue: int64;
      LRightValue: int64;
    begin
      LOp := self.FTree[AId].Op;
      if (LOp <> OperatorKind.Add) and (LOp <> OperatorKind.Subtract) then
        return false;
      end;
      LLeft := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Left);
      LRight := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Right);
      LLeftType := self.DoUsedType(LLeft);
      LRightType := self.DoUsedType(LRight);
      LLeftIsPtr := ClassOf(self.FTree, LLeftType) = TypeClass.Pointer;
      LRightIsPtr := ClassOf(self.FTree, LRightType) = TypeClass.Pointer;
      if (not LLeftIsPtr) and (not LRightIsPtr) then
        return false;
      end;
      AValue := 0;
      LLeftValue := self.DoValue(LLeft);
      if LLeftValue = 0 then
        return true;
      end;
      LRightValue := self.DoValue(LRight);
      if LRightValue = 0 then
        return true;
      end;
      if LLeftIsPtr and LRightIsPtr then
        AValue := self.DoPointerDistance(LLeftValue, LRightValue, LLeftType, AId);
        return true;
      end;
      if LLeftIsPtr then
        AValue := self.DoMovePointer(LLeftValue, LRightValue, LLeftType,
          LOp = OperatorKind.Subtract, AId);
        return true;
      end;
      AValue := self.DoMovePointer(LRightValue, LLeftValue, LRightType, false, AId);
      return true;
    end;

    // The binary operator AId on integers or floats: both operands' values, each already
    // converted by SEM to AId's type (its ResolvedType: C++'s usual arithmetic conversions;
    // a shift's count keeps its own type), combined by its IR op (a right shift of a signed
    // type is sar, a div / mod of an unsigned one udiv / urem, DESIGN sec 6; an integer
    // divide by zero faults as the hardware does, no check here; a float's follows IEEE 754:
    // inf or NaN); a pointer's arithmetic is DoPointerArithmetic's; 0 after LW0001 (another
    // operator, or a type the op does not take: DoOpFits; comparisons, `and` / `or` and a
    // bool's `xor` come here through DoBinaryExpression)
    hidden method DoBinary(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LOp: IrOp;
      LType: IrType;
      LLeft: int64;
      LRight: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LId := 0;
      if self.DoPointerArithmetic(AId, LId) then
        return LId;
      end;
      LOp := IrOp.Add;
      LType := self.DoIrType(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType);
      if (not self.DoBinaryIrOp(self.FTree[AId].Op, LOp)) or (not self.DoOpFits(LOp, LType)) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LOp := self.DoMachineOp(LOp, LType);
      LLeft := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Left));
      if LLeft = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LRight := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Right));
      if LRight = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LId := self.DoEmit(LOp, LType, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LLeft);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LRight);
      return LId;
    end;

    // The compare predicate of the float operator AOp, in APredicate: C's rules (= and the
    // orders false on a NaN, <> true); false for any other operator
    hidden const method DoFloatPredicateOf(const AOp: OperatorKind;
      var APredicate: IrPredicate): bool;
    begin
      if AOp = OperatorKind.Equal then
        APredicate := IrPredicate.FEqual;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.NotEqual then
        APredicate := IrPredicate.FNotEqual;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.Less then
        APredicate := IrPredicate.FLess;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.LessEqual then
        APredicate := IrPredicate.FLessEqual;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.Greater then
        APredicate := IrPredicate.FGreater;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.GreaterEqual then
        APredicate := IrPredicate.FGreaterEqual;
        return true;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // True when a comparison's operands of AType compare in the IR: an integer, a bool, a
    // ptr or a float
    hidden const method DoIsComparable(const AType: IrType): bool;
    begin
      return IsArithmeticType(AType) or (AType = IrType.Bool) or (AType = IrType.Pointer);
    end;

    // The compare predicate of the operator AOp on two values of AType, in APredicate: = and
    // <>, and a bool's xor (true when the two differ); < <= > >= signed or unsigned as AType
    // is (a bool, a ptr unsigned); a float's by DoFloatPredicateOf; false for any other
    // operator
    hidden const method DoPredicateOf(const AOp: OperatorKind; const AType: IrType;
      var APredicate: IrPredicate): bool;
    var
      LSigned: bool;
    begin
      if IsFloatType(AType) then
        return self.DoFloatPredicateOf(AOp, APredicate);
      end;
      LSigned := IsSignedType(AType);
      if AOp = OperatorKind.Equal then
        APredicate := IrPredicate.Equal;
        return true;
      end;
      if (AOp = OperatorKind.NotEqual) or (AOp = OperatorKind.Xor) then
        APredicate := IrPredicate.NotEqual;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.Less then
        APredicate := IrPredicate.ULess;
        if LSigned then
          APredicate := IrPredicate.SLess;
        end;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.LessEqual then
        APredicate := IrPredicate.ULessEqual;
        if LSigned then
          APredicate := IrPredicate.SLessEqual;
        end;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.Greater then
        APredicate := IrPredicate.UGreater;
        if LSigned then
          APredicate := IrPredicate.SGreater;
        end;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.GreaterEqual then
        APredicate := IrPredicate.UGreaterEqual;
        if LSigned then
          APredicate := IrPredicate.SGreaterEqual;
        end;
        return true;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // True when the comparison AId's operands are arrays, static or dynamic (BNF sec 6:
    // element by element, DoArrayCompare)
    hidden const method DoIsArrayCompare(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Left)));
      return (LClass = TypeClass.StaticArray) or (LClass = TypeClass.DynamicArray);
    end;

    // The address an array operand AId of the comparison ACompare is read at: a static
    // array's place or slot (DoAggregateSource); a dynamic array's value (its block, nil
    // when empty) in a slot of its own, so both kinds walk the same way (DoEqualAt,
    // DoOrderAt). When the elements' declared operator runs (DoElementOperatorOf) the
    // operand lives through its calls as a call's const argument does (SU2.8 e3): a static
    // array's anchor held (DoAnchoredAddress), a dynamic array's block in its hold
    // (DoArrayCompareHolds, DoHeldValue). 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoArrayOperand(const AId: int64; const ACompare: int64): int64;
    var
      LOperator: int64;
      LBlock: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      LOperator := self.DoElementOperatorOf(ACompare);
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(AId)) = TypeClass.StaticArray then
        if LOperator <> 0 then
          return self.DoAnchoredAddress(AId, false, true);
        end;
        return self.DoAggregateSource(AId);
      end;
      LBlock := self.DoValue(AId);
      if LBlock = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if (LOperator <> 0) and self.DoNeedsArrayHold(AId, LOperator, ACompare) then
        LBlock := self.DoHeldValue(AId, LBlock, self.DoUsedType(AId));
        if LBlock = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
      end;
      LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(AId, 8, 8);
      self.DoStore(LSlot, LBlock, AId);
      return LSlot;
    end;

    // The operator an array comparison AId runs on its elements of a record or an object
    // type (Semantics' pick, its ResolvedCallee: = for = and <>, < for the orders); 0 for
    // any other node
    hidden const method DoElementOperatorOf(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind <> NodeKind.BinaryExpression then
        return 0;
      end;
      LDecl := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedCallee;
      if (LDecl = 0) or (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind <> NodeKind.OperatorDecl) then
        return 0;
      end;
      return LDecl;
    end;

    // True when the dynamic array operand AArg of the comparison ACompare must be held
    // while its elements' operator AOperator runs (DoNeedsHold's rule for a borrowed
    // value): it is no value the comparison keeps alive (DoStableArg) and the operator may
    // drop it (DoMayDrop)
    hidden const method DoNeedsArrayHold(const AArg: int64; const AOperator: int64;
      const ACompare: int64): bool;
    begin
      if self.DoStableArg(AArg) then
        return false;
      end;
      return self.DoMayDrop(AOperator, ACompare, AArg);
    end;

    // The holds of the array comparison AId whose elements' declared operator runs
    // (DoElementOperatorOf), as a call's const arguments get them (DoArgHolds): a dynamic
    // array operand's block (DoNeedsArrayHold: a hold slot, DoHoldSlot), a static array
    // operand's anchor (DoHoldAnchor)
    hidden method DoArrayCompareHolds(const AId: int64; const AOperator: int64);
    var
      LI: int64;
      LArg: int64;
      LType: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to 1 do
        LArg := OperandAt(self.FTree, AId, LI);
        LType := self.DoUsedType(LArg);
        if ClassOf(self.FTree, LType) = TypeClass.DynamicArray then
          if self.DoNeedsArrayHold(LArg, AOperator, AId) then
            self.DoHoldSlot(self.DoArgRoot(LArg), LType);
          end;
        else
          self.DoHoldAnchor(self.DoAnchorOf(LArg), AOperator, 0, AId);
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The bool the elements' declared operator AOperator gives for the values of the
    // canonical type AType at ALeftAt and ARightAt (BNF sec 4 operator decl, an array
    // comparison's pair), at ANode: a call of its function with each value passed for its
    // parameter (DoElementArgument); 0 when its function was refused at its declaration
    // or after LW0001
    hidden method DoElementOperatorCall(const AOperator: int64; const ALeftAt: int64;
      const ARightAt: int64; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LLink: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      LLink := self.FFunctionOf[AOperator];
      if LLink = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LValue := self.DoElementArgument(ALeftAt, AType, self.FTree.NthOf(AOperator, NodeRole.Param, 0), ANode);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LArgs.Add(LValue);
      LValue := self.DoElementArgument(ARightAt, AType, self.FTree.NthOf(AOperator, NodeRole.Param, 1), ANode);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LArgs.Add(LValue);
      return self.DoEmitCallWith(ANode, AOperator, IrOp.Call, LLink,
        self.FModule.FunctionAt(LLink).Signature.ResultType, 0, 0, 0, LArgs);
    end;

    // The operand the element of the canonical type AType at AAddress passes for the
    // operator parameter AParam, at ANode (DoArgument's rules for a place's value): moved
    // to the parameter's ancestor part (DoUpcast); a value object whose type runs code
    // where it is copied or ended, by value, the callee's own copy in a zeroed slot
    // (DoCopyValue: the callee ends it); by copy (FByCopy) a slot its bytes are copied into
    // (one that holds texts: the element's own address, the callee makes its copy); by
    // reference its address; in a register its bytes as that register's integer
    // (DoAggregateIr); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoElementArgument(const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64; const AParam: int64;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoDeclType(AParam);
      LAt := AAddress;
      if LType <> AType then
        LAt := self.DoUpcast(AAddress, AType, LType, ANode);
      end;
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType);
      if self.DoHasLifetime(LType) and (not self.FTree[AParam].HasFlag(NodeFlag.ConstParam)) and
        ((not self.FByRef[AParam]) or self.FByCopy[AParam]) then
        LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, LSize, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType));
        // zeroed each time it runs: the loop's next pair starts from nothing too
        self.DoFill(LSlot, LSize, ANode);
        if not self.DoCopyValue(LSlot, LAt, LType, ANode) then
          return 0;
        end;
        if self.FByCopy[AParam] then
          return LSlot;
        end;
        return self.DoLoad(LSlot, self.DoAggregateIr(LType), ANode);
      end;
      if self.FByCopy[AParam] then
        if self.DoHoldsManaged(LType) then
          return LAt;
        end;
        LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, LSize, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType));
        self.DoCopyBytes(LSlot, LAt, LSize, ANode);
        return LSlot;
      end;
      if self.FByRef[AParam] then
        return LAt;
      end;
      return self.DoLoad(LAt, self.DoAggregateIr(LType), ANode);
    end;

    // The comparison AId of two arrays of one type (BNF sec 6, user 2026-10-13: element by
    // element, as C++'s std::array / std::vector compare): = and <> by DoEqualAt (equal
    // lengths and every element pair equal, a float's by its own =: a NaN is equal to
    // nothing); < <= > >= <=> by DoOrderAt's lexicographic -1 / 0 / 1 (the first element
    // pair that orders decides, else the shorter is below), compared with 0 (<=> is that
    // order itself, at AId's type); left operand first; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoArrayCompare(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LLeftId: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LOp: OperatorKind;
      LLeftAt: int64;
      LRightAt: int64;
      LEqual: int64;
      LOrder: int64;
      LPredicate: IrPredicate;
    begin
      LLeftId := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Left);
      LType := self.DoUsedType(LLeftId);
      LOp := self.FTree[AId].Op;
      LLeftAt := self.DoArrayOperand(LLeftId, AId);
      if LLeftAt = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LRightAt := self.DoArrayOperand(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Right), AId);
      if LRightAt = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if (LOp = OperatorKind.Equal) or (LOp = OperatorKind.NotEqual) then
        LEqual := self.DoEqualAt(LLeftAt, LRightAt, LType, AId);
        if (LEqual = 0) or (LOp = OperatorKind.Equal) then
          return LEqual;
        end;
        return self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.Equal, LEqual, self.DoConstant(IrType.Bool, 0, AId), AId);
      end;
      LOrder := self.DoOrderAt(LLeftAt, LRightAt, LType, AId);
      if LOrder = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if LOp = OperatorKind.Compare then
        return self.DoConvertIr(LOrder, self.DoIrType(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType), AId);
      end;
      LPredicate := IrPredicate.Equal;
      if not self.DoPredicateOf(LOp, IrType.Int32, LPredicate) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoCompareWith(LPredicate, LOrder, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int32, 0, AId), AId);
    end;

    // The IR type two values of the canonical type AType compare as, one by one (an own /
    // ref / weak as its block's ptr); Void when they are none DoIsComparable takes
    hidden const method DoCompareIr(const AType: int64): IrType;
    var
      LType: IrType;
    begin
      LType := self.DoIrType(AType);
      if self.DoIsOwnerValue(AType) then
        LType := IrType.Pointer;
      end;
      if not self.DoIsComparable(LType) then
        return IrType.Void;
      end;
      return LType;
    end;

    // The number of elements of the dynamic array block ABlock (nil when empty: 0), an int64,
    // at ANode
    hidden method DoBlockCount(const ABlock: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LCount: int64;
      LHeld: int64;
      LRead: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
    begin
      LCount := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, 8, 8);
      self.DoStore(LCount, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, ANode), ANode);
      LHeld := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.NotEqual, ABlock, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, ANode), ANode);
      LRead := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(LHeld, LRead, LJoin, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LRead;
      self.DoStore(LCount, self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(ABlock, ADAM_LOWERING_BLOCK_LENGTH, ANode),
        IrType.Int64, ANode), ANode);
      self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LJoin;
      return self.DoLoad(LCount, IrType.Int64, ANode);
    end;

    // The bool: the two values of the canonical type AType at ALeftAt and ARightAt are
    // equal, at ANode. A static array's elements pair by pair (DoElementsEqual); a dynamic
    // array's when the lengths match; a set's bits (DoSetCompareAt); a text's by StrCompare
    // (WStrCompare); any other comparable value by its own = (a float's ordered: a NaN is
    // equal to nothing); a record's or an object's by its declared = (Semantics' pick for
    // the comparison ANode: DoElementOperatorCall). 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoEqualAt(const ALeftAt: int64; const ARightAt: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
      LType: IrType;
      LCount: int64;
      LOrder: int64;
      LPredicate: IrPredicate;
    begin
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if LClass = TypeClass.StaticArray then
        LCount := ArrayCount(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType);
        if LCount < 0 then
          raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_ARRAY_COUNT + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
        end;
        return self.DoElementsEqual(ALeftAt, ARightAt, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LCount, ANode),
          AType, ANode);
      end;
      if LClass = TypeClass.DynamicArray then
        return self.DoBlocksEqual(self.DoLoad(ALeftAt, IrType.Pointer, ANode),
          self.DoLoad(ARightAt, IrType.Pointer, ANode), AType, ANode);
      end;
      if LClass = TypeClass.SetType then
        return self.DoSetCompareAt(ALeftAt, ARightAt, AType, OperatorKind.Equal, ANode);
      end;
      if self.DoIsText(AType) then
        LOrder := self.DoTextOrderAt(ALeftAt, ARightAt, AType, ANode);
        if LOrder = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.Equal, LOrder, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int32, 0, ANode), ANode);
      end;
      if (self.DoElementOperatorOf(ANode) <> 0) and self.DoIsReachable(AType) then
        return self.DoElementOperatorCall(self.DoElementOperatorOf(ANode), ALeftAt, ARightAt, AType, ANode);
      end;
      LType := self.DoCompareIr(AType);
      LPredicate := IrPredicate.Equal;
      if (LType = IrType.Void) or (not self.DoPredicateOf(OperatorKind.Equal, LType, LPredicate)) then
        self.DoRefuse(ANode, "a comparison of arrays of '" + TypeText(self.FTree, AType) + "'");
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoCompareWith(LPredicate, self.DoLoad(ALeftAt, LType, ANode),
        self.DoLoad(ARightAt, LType, ANode), ANode);
    end;

    // The bool: the dynamic array blocks ALeft and ARight (of the dynamic array type AType)
    // hold as many elements and every pair is equal (DoElementsEqual, run only when the
    // lengths match), at ANode; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoBlocksEqual(const ALeft: int64; const ARight: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LResult: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LSame: int64;
      LWalk: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
      LEqual: int64;
    begin
      LResult := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, 1, 1);
      self.DoStore(LResult, self.DoConstant(IrType.Bool, 0, ANode), ANode);
      LCount := self.DoBlockCount(ALeft, ANode);
      LSame := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.Equal, LCount, self.DoBlockCount(ARight, ANode), ANode);
      LWalk := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(LSame, LWalk, LJoin, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LWalk;
      // an empty block is nil: its elements are never read (the count is 0)
      LEqual := self.DoElementsEqual(self.DoByteOffset(ALeft, ADAM_LOWERING_ARRAY_HEADER, ANode),
        self.DoByteOffset(ARight, ADAM_LOWERING_ARRAY_HEADER, ANode), LCount, AType, ANode);
      if LEqual = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoStore(LResult, LEqual, ANode);
      self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LJoin;
      return self.DoLoad(LResult, IrType.Bool, ANode);
    end;

    // The bool: the first ACount (an int64 value) elements of the array type AType from
    // ALeftAt and from ARightAt are equal pair by pair (DoEqualAt), at ANode: a loop that
    // leaves at the first unequal pair; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoElementsEqual(const ALeftAt: int64; const ARightAt: int64; const ACount: int64;
      const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LResult: int64;
      LCounter: int64;
      LHead: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LNext: int64;
      LUnequal: int64;
      LExit: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LEqual: int64;
    begin
      LResult := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, 1, 1);
      self.DoStore(LResult, self.DoConstant(IrType.Bool, 1, ANode), ANode);
      LCounter := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, 8, 8);
      self.DoStore(LCounter, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, ANode), ANode);
      LHead := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LNext := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LUnequal := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LExit := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoJumpTo(LHead, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LHead;
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      self.DoBranchOn(self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.SLess, LIndex, ACount, ANode), LBody, LExit, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LBody;
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LEqual := self.DoEqualAt(self.DoMovePointer(ALeftAt, LIndex, AType, false, ANode),
        self.DoMovePointer(ARightAt, LIndex, AType, false, ANode), TargetOf(self.FTree, AType), ANode);
      if LEqual = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoBranchOn(LEqual, LNext, LUnequal, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LNext;
      self.DoStepCounter(LCounter, ANode);
      self.DoJumpTo(LHead, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LUnequal;
      self.DoStore(LResult, self.DoConstant(IrType.Bool, 0, ANode), ANode);
      self.DoJumpTo(LExit, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LExit;
      return self.DoLoad(LResult, IrType.Bool, ANode);
    end;

    // The int64 counter in the slot ACounter one step on, at ANode
    hidden method DoStepCounter(const ACounter: int64; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LIndex: int64;
      LOne: int64;
      LNext: int64;
    begin
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(ACounter, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      // every operand is emitted before the instruction that uses it
      LOne := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 1, ANode);
      LNext := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Add, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LNext).Operands.Add(LIndex);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LNext).Operands.Add(LOne);
      self.DoStore(ACounter, LNext, ANode);
    end;

    // StrCompare (WStrCompare) of the two texts of the canonical type AType at ALeftAt and
    // ARightAt: an int32 that is -1, 0 or 1, at ANode; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoTextOrderAt(const ALeftAt: int64; const ARightAt: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.DoCallRuntime(self.DoTextRoutine(RuntimeRoutine.StrCompare, AType),
        self.DoLoad(ALeftAt, IrType.Pointer, ANode), self.DoLoad(ARightAt, IrType.Pointer, ANode), ANode);
    end;

    // The int32 -1, 0 or 1 as the value of the canonical type AType at ALeftAt is below,
    // equal to or above the one at ARightAt, at ANode (an array comparison's order, BNF
    // sec 6): a static array's elements lexicographically (DoElementsOrder); a dynamic
    // array's over the shorter length, then the shorter below (DoBlocksOrder); a text's by
    // StrCompare; any other ordered value by (left > right) - (left < right), a float's by
    // its ordered compares (a NaN on either side is neither: 0, the pair skipped as C++'s
    // lexicographical compare skips an equivalent pair); a record's or an object's by its
    // declared < (DoElementLessOrder). 0 after LW0001 (a set has no order)
    hidden method DoOrderAt(const ALeftAt: int64; const ARightAt: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LClass: TypeClass;
      LType: IrType;
      LCount: int64;
      LAbove: IrPredicate;
      LBelow: IrPredicate;
      LLeft: int64;
      LRight: int64;
      LIsAbove: int64;
      LIsBelow: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if LClass = TypeClass.StaticArray then
        LCount := ArrayCount(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType);
        if LCount < 0 then
          raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_ARRAY_COUNT + TypeText(self.FTree, AType));
        end;
        return self.DoElementsOrder(ALeftAt, ARightAt, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LCount, ANode),
          AType, ANode);
      end;
      if LClass = TypeClass.DynamicArray then
        return self.DoBlocksOrder(self.DoLoad(ALeftAt, IrType.Pointer, ANode),
          self.DoLoad(ARightAt, IrType.Pointer, ANode), AType, ANode);
      end;
      if self.DoIsText(AType) then
        return self.DoTextOrderAt(ALeftAt, ARightAt, AType, ANode);
      end;
      if (self.DoElementOperatorOf(ANode) <> 0) and self.DoIsReachable(AType) then
        return self.DoElementLessOrder(self.DoElementOperatorOf(ANode), ALeftAt, ARightAt, AType, ANode);
      end;
      LType := IrType.Void;
      if LClass <> TypeClass.SetType then
        LType := self.DoCompareIr(AType);
      end;
      LAbove := IrPredicate.Equal;
      LBelow := IrPredicate.Equal;
      if (LType = IrType.Void) or (not self.DoPredicateOf(OperatorKind.Greater, LType, LAbove)) or
        (not self.DoPredicateOf(OperatorKind.Less, LType, LBelow)) then
        self.DoRefuse(ANode, "an ordering of arrays of '" + TypeText(self.FTree, AType) + "'");
        return 0;
      end;
      LLeft := self.DoLoad(ALeftAt, LType, ANode);
      LRight := self.DoLoad(ARightAt, LType, ANode);
      LIsAbove := self.DoConvertIr(self.DoCompareWith(LAbove, LLeft, LRight, ANode), IrType.Int32, ANode);
      LIsBelow := self.DoConvertIr(self.DoCompareWith(LBelow, LLeft, LRight, ANode), IrType.Int32, ANode);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Sub, IrType.Int32, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LIsAbove);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LIsBelow);
      return LId;
    end;

    // The order of the values of the record or object type AType at ALeftAt and ARightAt
    // by their declared < AOperator (C++'s lexicographical rule): (right < left) - (left <
    // right), an int32 at ANode, each call's bool converted (neither: 0, the pair skipped);
    // 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoElementLessOrder(const AOperator: int64; const ALeftAt: int64; const ARightAt: int64;
      const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LAbove: int64;
      LBelow: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LAbove := self.DoElementOperatorCall(AOperator, ARightAt, ALeftAt, AType, ANode);
      if LAbove = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LAbove := self.DoConvertIr(LAbove, IrType.Int32, ANode);
      LBelow := self.DoElementOperatorCall(AOperator, ALeftAt, ARightAt, AType, ANode);
      if LBelow = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LBelow := self.DoConvertIr(LBelow, IrType.Int32, ANode);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Sub, IrType.Int32, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LAbove);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LBelow);
      return LId;
    end;

    // The order of the dynamic array blocks ALeft and ARight (of the dynamic array type
    // AType), at ANode: their elements over the shorter length (DoElementsOrder), and when
    // that is 0 the lengths' own order (the shorter below); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoBlocksOrder(const ALeft: int64; const ARight: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LResult: int64;
      LShorter: int64;
      LLeftCount: int64;
      LRightCount: int64;
      LRightShorter: int64;
      LTakeRight: int64;
      LWalk: int64;
      LOrder: int64;
      LTie: int64;
      LExit: int64;
      LIsAbove: int64;
      LIsBelow: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LResult := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, 4, 4);
      LShorter := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, 8, 8);
      LLeftCount := self.DoBlockCount(ALeft, ANode);
      LRightCount := self.DoBlockCount(ARight, ANode);
      self.DoStore(LShorter, LLeftCount, ANode);
      LRightShorter := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.SLess, LRightCount, LLeftCount, ANode);
      LTakeRight := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LWalk := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(LRightShorter, LTakeRight, LWalk, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LTakeRight;
      self.DoStore(LShorter, LRightCount, ANode);
      self.DoJumpTo(LWalk, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LWalk;
      LOrder := self.DoElementsOrder(self.DoByteOffset(ALeft, ADAM_LOWERING_ARRAY_HEADER, ANode),
        self.DoByteOffset(ARight, ADAM_LOWERING_ARRAY_HEADER, ANode),
        self.DoLoad(LShorter, IrType.Int64, ANode), AType, ANode);
      if LOrder = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoStore(LResult, LOrder, ANode);
      LTie := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LExit := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.Equal, LOrder, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int32, 0, ANode),
        ANode), LTie, LExit, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LTie;
      LIsAbove := self.DoConvertIr(self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.SGreater, LLeftCount, LRightCount, ANode),
        IrType.Int32, ANode);
      LIsBelow := self.DoConvertIr(self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.SLess, LLeftCount, LRightCount, ANode),
        IrType.Int32, ANode);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Sub, IrType.Int32, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LIsAbove);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LIsBelow);
      self.DoStore(LResult, LId, ANode);
      self.DoJumpTo(LExit, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LExit;
      return self.DoLoad(LResult, IrType.Int32, ANode);
    end;

    // The order of the first ACount (an int64 value) elements of the array type AType from
    // ALeftAt and from ARightAt, at ANode: a loop that leaves with the first pair's order
    // that is not 0 (DoOrderAt), else 0; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoElementsOrder(const ALeftAt: int64; const ARightAt: int64; const ACount: int64;
      const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LResult: int64;
      LCounter: int64;
      LHead: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LNext: int64;
      LDecided: int64;
      LExit: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LOrder: int64;
    begin
      LResult := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, 4, 4);
      self.DoStore(LResult, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int32, 0, ANode), ANode);
      LCounter := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, 8, 8);
      self.DoStore(LCounter, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, ANode), ANode);
      LHead := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LNext := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LDecided := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LExit := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoJumpTo(LHead, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LHead;
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      self.DoBranchOn(self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.SLess, LIndex, ACount, ANode), LBody, LExit, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LBody;
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, ANode);
      LOrder := self.DoOrderAt(self.DoMovePointer(ALeftAt, LIndex, AType, false, ANode),
        self.DoMovePointer(ARightAt, LIndex, AType, false, ANode), TargetOf(self.FTree, AType), ANode);
      if LOrder = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoStore(LResult, LOrder, ANode);
      self.DoBranchOn(self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.Equal, LOrder, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int32, 0, ANode),
        ANode), LNext, LDecided, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LNext;
      self.DoStepCounter(LCounter, ANode);
      self.DoJumpTo(LHead, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LDecided;
      self.DoJumpTo(LExit, ANode);
      self.FBlock := LExit;
      return self.DoLoad(LResult, IrType.Int32, ANode);
    end;

    // The comparison AId (= <> < <= > >=, or `xor` of two bools): both operands' values,
    // brought by SEM to one type (numbers to their common type, the rest to each other's),
    // compared by the predicate of that type's signedness (a float's by C's NaN rules); two
    // sets by their bits (DoSetCompare); two arrays element by element (DoArrayCompare);
    // two strings by their bytes (DoStringCompare); 0 after LW0001 (operands of a type
    // that is no integer, bool, char, choices, pointer, float, set, array or string)
    hidden method DoComparison(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LLeftId: int64;
      LType: IrType;
      LPredicate: IrPredicate;
      LLeft: int64;
      LRight: int64;
    begin
      LLeftId := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Left);
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(LLeftId)) = TypeClass.SetType then
        return self.DoSetCompare(AId);
      end;
      if self.DoIsArrayCompare(AId) then
        return self.DoArrayCompare(AId);
      end;
      if self.DoIsText(self.DoUsedType(LLeftId)) then
        return self.DoStringCompare(AId);
      end;
      LType := self.DoIrType(self.DoUsedType(LLeftId));
      // two refs or weaks (or one and nil) compare their blocks
      if self.DoIsOwnerValue(self.DoUsedType(LLeftId)) then
        LType := IrType.Pointer;
      end;
      LPredicate := IrPredicate.Equal;
      if (not self.DoIsComparable(LType)) or
        (not self.DoPredicateOf(self.FTree[AId].Op, LType, LPredicate)) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LLeft := self.DoValue(LLeftId);
      if LLeft = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LRight := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Right));
      if LRight = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoCompareWith(LPredicate, LLeft, LRight, AId);
    end;

    // `<=>` AId: an int32 (SEM's type for it) that is -1, 0 or 1 as the left operand is
    // below, equal to or above the right (both brought by SEM to one type, ordered by its
    // signedness): (left > right) - (left < right), each bool converted to int32 (two
    // floats by their ordered compares: a NaN on either side is neither, so 0); two strings'
    // is StrCompare's own -1 / 0 / 1 (DoStringOrder), two arrays' their lexicographic order
    // (DoArrayCompare); 0 after LW0001 (operands of a type that is no integer, bool, char,
    // choices, pointer, float, array or string)
    hidden method DoThreeWay(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LLeftId: int64;
      LType: IrType;
      LResult: IrType;
      LAbove: IrPredicate;
      LBelow: IrPredicate;
      LLeft: int64;
      LRight: int64;
      LIsAbove: int64;
      LIsBelow: int64;
      LOrder: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LLeftId := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Left);
      if self.DoIsArrayCompare(AId) then
        return self.DoArrayCompare(AId);
      end;
      if self.DoIsText(self.DoUsedType(LLeftId)) then
        LOrder := self.DoStringOrder(AId);
        if LOrder = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return self.DoConvertIr(LOrder, self.DoIrType(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType), AId);
      end;
      LType := self.DoIrType(self.DoUsedType(LLeftId));
      LResult := self.DoIrType(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType);
      LAbove := IrPredicate.Equal;
      LBelow := IrPredicate.Equal;
      if (not self.DoIsComparable(LType)) or (not IsIntegerType(LResult)) or
        (not self.DoPredicateOf(OperatorKind.Greater, LType, LAbove)) or
        (not self.DoPredicateOf(OperatorKind.Less, LType, LBelow)) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LLeft := self.DoValue(LLeftId);
      if LLeft = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LRight := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Right));
      if LRight = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LIsAbove := self.DoConvertIr(self.DoCompareWith(LAbove, LLeft, LRight, AId), LResult, AId);
      LIsBelow := self.DoConvertIr(self.DoCompareWith(LBelow, LLeft, LRight, AId), LResult, AId);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Sub, LResult, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LIsAbove);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LIsBelow);
      return LId;
    end;

    // A jump from the current block to ATarget, at ANode; none from a block a noreturn call
    // ends (a check's raise, Halt): control never leaves it, so it ends in an Unreachable
    // and ATarget gets no edge from it
    hidden method DoJumpTo(const ATarget: int64; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LJump: int64;
    begin
      if self.DoCloseNoReturn() then
        return;
      end;
      LJump := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Jump, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LJump).Targets.Add(ATarget);
    end;

    // A branch on the bool ACondition from the current block: to AOnTrue when it holds, else
    // to AOnFalse, at ANode
    hidden method DoBranchOn(const ACondition: int64; const AOnTrue: int64; const AOnFalse: int64;
      const ANode: int64);
    var
      LBranch: int64;
    begin
      LBranch := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Branch, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LBranch).Operands.Add(ACondition);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LBranch).Targets.Add(AOnTrue);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LBranch).Targets.Add(AOnFalse);
    end;

    // The phi of AType in the current block (a join): AFirst from the edge of the block
    // AFirstEnd, ASecond from that of ASecondEnd, at ANode
    hidden method DoJoinOf(const AType: IrType; const AFirst: int64; const AFirstEnd: int64;
      const ASecond: int64; const ASecondEnd: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LPhi: int64;
    begin
      LPhi := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Phi, AType, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LPhi).Operands.Add(AFirst);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LPhi).Targets.Add(AFirstEnd);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LPhi).Operands.Add(ASecond);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LPhi).Targets.Add(ASecondEnd);
      return LPhi;
    end;

    // `and` / `or` (`&&` / `||`) AId, short-circuit (BNF sec 6): the left bool decides in its
    // block; only when it does not (true for and, false for or) does the right one run, in a
    // block of its own; both meet in a join block whose phi takes the left value from the
    // left's edge (there it is the answer: false for and, true for or) and the right value
    // from the right's
    hidden method DoShortCircuit(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LLeft: int64;
      LLeftEnd: int64;
      LRightBlock: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
      LRight: int64;
      LRightEnd: int64;
    begin
      LLeft := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Left));
      if LLeft = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      // the left's own and / or may have ended in another block than it began in
      LLeftEnd := self.FBlock;
      LRightBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      if self.FTree[AId].Op = OperatorKind.LogicalAnd then
        self.DoBranchOn(LLeft, LRightBlock, LJoin, AId);
      else
        self.DoBranchOn(LLeft, LJoin, LRightBlock, AId);
      end;
      self.FBlock := LRightBlock;
      LRight := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Right));
      if LRight = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LRightEnd := self.FBlock;
      self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, AId);
      self.FBlock := LJoin;
      return self.DoJoinOf(IrType.Bool, LLeft, LLeftEnd, LRight, LRightEnd, AId);
    end;

    // `? :` AId (BNF sec 6): the condition's bool picks a block; each branch's value (SEM
    // brought both to AId's type) is made in its own block, so only the chosen one runs; a
    // join's phi takes the value from the edge that ran (a text's or a dynamic array's a
    // borrowed value, as each side's is: a temporary a side makes lives in its hidden
    // slot); 0 after LW0001 (a type that is no integer, bool, char, choices, pointer, text
    // or dynamic array: floats and aggregates come with their milestones)
    hidden method DoConditional(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: IrType;
      LCondition: int64;
      LThenBlock: int64;
      LElseBlock: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
      LThen: int64;
      LThenEnd: int64;
      LElse: int64;
      LElseEnd: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoIrType(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType);
      if self.DoIsManaged(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType) then
        LType := IrType.Pointer;
      end;
      if (not IsIntegerType(LType)) and (LType <> IrType.Bool) and (LType <> IrType.Pointer) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LCondition := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Condition));
      if LCondition = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LThenBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LElseBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(LCondition, LThenBlock, LElseBlock, AId);
      self.FBlock := LThenBlock;
      LThen := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Then));
      if LThen = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      // a branch's own and / or / ?: may have ended in another block than it began in
      LThenEnd := self.FBlock;
      self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, AId);
      self.FBlock := LElseBlock;
      LElse := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Else));
      if LElse = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LElseEnd := self.FBlock;
      self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, AId);
      self.FBlock := LJoin;
      return self.DoJoinOf(LType, LThen, LThenEnd, LElse, LElseEnd, AId);
    end;

    // The binary expression AId: and / or short-circuit, a comparison, `<=>`, `in`
    // (DoSetIn), a bool's xor (a compare: the two differ), else the integer operators
    // (DoBinary); a set operation's value is an aggregate (DoAggregateSource)
    hidden method DoBinaryExpression(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LOp: OperatorKind;
    begin
      // a type's declared operator runs as a call of its function
      if OperatorCallOf(self.FTree, AId) <> 0 then
        return self.DoCall(AId);
      end;
      LOp := self.FTree[AId].Op;
      if (LOp = OperatorKind.LogicalAnd) or (LOp = OperatorKind.LogicalOr) then
        return self.DoShortCircuit(AId);
      end;
      if LOp = OperatorKind.Compare then
        return self.DoThreeWay(AId);
      end;
      if LOp = OperatorKind.In then
        return self.DoSetIn(AId);
      end;
      if (LOp = OperatorKind.Equal) or (LOp = OperatorKind.NotEqual) or
        (LOp = OperatorKind.Less) or (LOp = OperatorKind.LessEqual) or
        (LOp = OperatorKind.Greater) or (LOp = OperatorKind.GreaterEqual) then
        return self.DoComparison(AId);
      end;
      if (LOp = OperatorKind.Xor) and
        (self.DoIrType(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType) = IrType.Bool) then
        return self.DoComparison(AId);
      end;
      return self.DoBinary(AId);
    end;

    // `++` / `--` AId on its operand (an integer, char or wchar SEM found assignable; AId's
    // type is the operand's own): the operand's address once, its value loaded, one added
    // or taken at the promoted type and stored back as the operand's type; the value is the
    // new one for a prefix step (APrefix), the old one for a postfix; a typed ptr steps by
    // one element (DoMovePointer); a bitfield operand is read and written through its lane,
    // a string's byte after copy on write (DoWriteAddress); 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoStep(const AId: int64; const APrefix: bool): int64;
    var
      LType: IrType;
      LIsPtr: bool;
      LOp: IrOp;
      LMember: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LOld: int64;
      LNew: int64;
      LOperand: int64;
    begin
      // a property stepped through its accessors (one that is its field is a place)
      LOperand := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand);
      while self.FTree[LOperand].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LOperand := self.FTree.FirstOf(LOperand, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      if self.DoIsPropertyAccess(LOperand) then
        return self.DoPropertyStep(AId, LOperand, APrefix);
      end;
      LType := self.DoIrType(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType);
      LIsPtr := ClassOf(self.FTree, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType) = TypeClass.Pointer;
      if (not IsIntegerType(LType)) and (not LIsPtr) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LOp := IrOp.Add;
      if self.FTree[AId].Op = OperatorKind.Decrement then
        LOp := IrOp.Sub;
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoWriteAddress(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand), LMember);
      if LAddress = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LOld := self.DoReadAt(LMember, LAddress, LType, AId);
      if LIsPtr then
        LNew := self.DoMovePointer(LOld, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 1, AId),
          self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType, LOp = IrOp.Sub, AId);
      else
        LNew := self.DoComputeIn(LOp, LOld, self.DoConstant(LType, 1, AId), LType, AId);
      end;
      self.DoWriteAt(LMember, LAddress, LNew, AId);
      if APrefix then
        // A prefix step's value is the operand after the store: for a bitfield what its
        // width kept (int32 : 3 at 3 steps to -4), read back from the lane
        if LMember <> 0 then
          return self.DoReadAt(LMember, LAddress, LType, AId);
        end;
        return LNew;
      end;
      return LOld;
    end;

    // True when the value-giving unary operator AOp runs on AType: `+` / `-` on an integer
    // or a float, `~` on an integer only
    hidden const method DoUnaryFits(const AOp: OperatorKind; const AType: IrType): bool;
    begin
      if (AOp = OperatorKind.Plus) or (AOp = OperatorKind.Negate) then
        return IsIntegerType(AType) or IsFloatType(AType);
      end;
      return (AOp = OperatorKind.BitNot) and IsIntegerType(AType);
    end;

    // The unary operator AId: `not` / `!` on a bool is a compare with false; prefix `++` /
    // `--` a step (DoStep); `addr of` a place its address (DoAddress: a local's or a
    // parameter's slot, a module variable's data, a deref's ptr, an element's, a field's);
    // on an integer, unary plus is its operand's value (promoted by SEM), minus a
    // neg, `~` a not; on a float, plus its value and minus a neg (the sign bit flipped:
    // -0.0 from +0.0); 0 after LW0001 (another operator, or a type it does not take)
    hidden method DoUnary(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LOp: OperatorKind;
      LType: IrType;
      LOperand: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      // the unary minus a type's declared `operator -` runs: a call of its function
      if OperatorCallOf(self.FTree, AId) <> 0 then
        return self.DoCall(AId);
      end;
      LOp := self.FTree[AId].Op;
      if (LOp = OperatorKind.Increment) or (LOp = OperatorKind.Decrement) then
        return self.DoStep(AId, true);
      end;
      if LOp = OperatorKind.AddressOf then
        // An assignable place may be written through its address: a string's or a dynamic
        // array's block on the way made its holder's alone first (DoAddressFor's write
        // form). A place that cannot be assigned has a ptr to const (Semantics), which no
        // write goes through: its storage shared as it is, nothing copied (BNF sec 4)
        return self.DoAddressFor(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand),
          not IsConstTarget(self.FTree, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType));
      end;
      LType := self.DoIrType(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType);
      if (LOp = OperatorKind.LogicalNot) and (LType = IrType.Bool) then
        LOperand := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand));
        if LOperand = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.Equal, LOperand,
          self.DoConstant(IrType.Bool, 0, AId), AId);
      end;
      if not self.DoUnaryFits(LOp, LType) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return 0;
      end;
      LOperand := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand));
      if (LOperand = 0) or (LOp = OperatorKind.Plus) then
        return LOperand;
      end;
      if LOp = OperatorKind.Negate then
        LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Neg, LType, AId);
      else
        LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.BitNot, LType, AId);
      end;
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LOperand);
      return LId;
    end;

    // Where the place AId is read and written: for a bitfield its lane's address, AMember
    // the member access naming it; else its own address, AMember 0. The one address a
    // load-and-store form (a compound assignment, a step) uses for both; AWrite:
    // DoAddressFor's write form; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPlaceAddress(const AId: int64; const AWrite: bool; var AMember: int64): int64;
    begin
      AMember := self.DoBitfieldPlace(AId);
      if AMember <> 0 then
        return self.DoFieldAddress(AMember, AWrite);
      end;
      return self.DoAddressFor(AId, AWrite);
    end;

    // The value at AAddress, a place DoPlaceAddress gave (AMember its bitfield or 0), of the
    // IR type AType: a bitfield read from its lane, else a load
    hidden method DoReadAt(const AMember: int64; const AAddress: int64; const AType: IrType;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    begin
      if AMember <> 0 then
        return self.DoBitRead(AMember, AAddress);
      end;
      return self.DoLoad(AAddress, AType, ANode);
    end;

    // AValue written to AAddress, a place DoPlaceAddress gave (AMember its bitfield or 0): a
    // bitfield written into its lane, else a store
    hidden method DoWriteAt(const AMember: int64; const AAddress: int64; const AValue: int64;
      const ANode: int64);
    begin
      if AMember <> 0 then
        self.DoBitWrite(AMember, AAddress, AValue);
        return;
      end;
      self.DoStore(AAddress, AValue, ANode);
    end;

    // The value held by the place AId (DoIsPlace), read at its type; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoPlaceValue(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LMember: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LType: IrType;
    begin
      LAddress := self.DoPlaceAddress(AId, false, LMember);
      if LAddress = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LType := self.DoTypeAt(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType, AId);
      if LType = IrType.Void then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoReadAt(LMember, LAddress, LType, AId);
    end;

    // The value of expression AId before any conversion; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoOwnValue(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LKind: NodeKind;
    begin
      LKind := NameKindOf(self.FTree, AId);
      if LKind = NodeKind.ParenExpression then
        return self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand));
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.AssignExpression then
        return self.DoAssignedValue(AId, AssignedForm.Scalar);
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.AwaitExpression then
        return self.DoAwaitValue(AId);
      end;
      // A typed pack's read (before the place and call forms its member and call look like)
      if self.DoIsPackAccess(AId) then
        return self.DoPackValue(AId);
      end;
      if (LKind = NodeKind.TypeCast) or (LKind = NodeKind.PointerCast) then
        return self.DoCast(AId, self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Operand));
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.BinaryExpression then
        return self.DoBinaryExpression(AId);
      end;
      // A routine named as a value (BNF sec 4, PLAN-RECORDS R5): its code address
      if (LKind = NodeKind.NameExpression) and (self.DoCalled(AId) <> 0) then
        return self.DoRoutineValue(AId);
      end;
      // A property read through its accessors (one that is its field is a place)
      if self.DoIsPropertyAccess(AId) then
        return self.DoPropertyGet(AId);
      end;
      if self.DoIsPlace(AId) then
        return self.DoPlaceValue(AId);
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.UnaryExpression then
        return self.DoUnary(AId);
      end;
      if (LKind = NodeKind.PostfixExpression) and
        ((self.FTree[AId].Op = OperatorKind.Increment) or
        (self.FTree[AId].Op = OperatorKind.Decrement)) then
        return self.DoStep(AId, false);
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.ConditionalExpression then
        return self.DoConditional(AId);
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.IsExpression then
        return self.DoIsValue(AId);
      end;
      // `ptr to S as T` (an object's `as` is a place, above; a ref's a managed value)
      if LKind = NodeKind.AsExpression then
        return self.DoAsHolder(AId);
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.VarargsExpression then
        return self.DoVarargsValue(AId);
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.CallExpression then
        if self.DoIsCastCall(AId) then
          return self.DoCast(AId, self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Argument));
        end;
        return self.DoCall(AId);
      end;
      // A string literal used as a ptr to const char / wchar (SEM's implicit form): its C
      // string; as a string or wstring value it is M3.8's
      if (LKind = NodeKind.StringLiteral) and IsPointerClass(ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(AId))) then
        return self.DoCStringLiteral(AId, self.DoUsedType(AId));
      end;
      self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
      return 0;
    end;

    // The 64 bits of the constant AId folded to, read as a value of the canonical type
    // AType: under a char or wchar type the code at the width and sign the target gives it
    // (a char's stored bits are its low bits: char(200) is -56 where char is signed, as
    // SEM's DoFoldedBits reads it), any other constant's bits as they are
    hidden const method DoConstBits(const AId: int64; const AType: int64): int64;
    var
      LBits: int64;
      LClass: TypeClass;
    begin
      LBits := int64(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConst.Bits);
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if (LClass = TypeClass.Char) or (LClass = TypeClass.WideChar) then
        return ReadLowBits(LBits, CharTypeBits(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType),
          IsCharTypeSigned(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType));
      end;
      return LBits;
    end;

    // True when expression AId folded to a constant whose bits Lowering writes as they are
    // (an integer, a char, a bool or nil: DoConstBits reads them)
    hidden const method DoIsFolded(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LConst: ConstKind;
    begin
      LConst := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConst.Kind;
      return (LConst = ConstKind.Signed) or (LConst = ConstKind.Unsigned) or (LConst = ConstKind.Char) or
        (LConst = ConstKind.Boolean) or (LConst = ConstKind.Nil);
    end;

    // True when expression AId is a constant Lowering writes as a float: a folded float, or
    // a folded integer / char / bool used as a float (DoFloatConstant converts it)
    hidden const method DoIsFloatConstant(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LUsed: IrType;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConst.Kind = ConstKind.Float then
        return true;
      end;
      if not self.DoIsFolded(AId) then
        return false;
      end;
      LUsed := self.DoIrType(self.DoUsedType(AId));
      return (LUsed = IrType.Float32) or (LUsed = IrType.Float64);
    end;

    // The float constant AId (DoIsFloatConstant) as the float type it is used as: its value
    // converted once, as C converts it (to nearest: an integer straight to the float type,
    // a float64 constant to float32), written as that type's IEEE bits; 0 after LW0001 when
    // it is used as a type that is no float (never from a valid tree: SEM refuses a float
    // converted implicitly to an integer, SM0200, and Folding folds a written cast)
    hidden method DoFloatConstant(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LUsed: int64;
      LType: IrType;
      LKind: ConstKind;
      LInt: int64;
      LBits: int64;
    begin
      LUsed := self.DoUsedType(AId);
      LType := self.DoIrType(LUsed);
      if (LType <> IrType.Float32) and (LType <> IrType.Float64) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, "a conversion from '" + TypeText(self.FTree, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType) +
          "' to '" + TypeText(self.FTree, LUsed) + "'");
        return 0;
      end;
      LKind := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConst.Kind;
      if LKind = ConstKind.Float then
        if LType = IrType.Float32 then
          LBits := int64(Float32ToBits(float32(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConst.Float)));
        else
          LBits := int64(Float64ToBits(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConst.Float));
        end;
        return self.DoConstant(LType, LBits, AId);
      end;
      if LKind = ConstKind.Unsigned then
        if LType = IrType.Float32 then
          LBits := int64(Float32ToBits(float32(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConst.Bits)));
        else
          LBits := int64(Float64ToBits(float64(self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConst.Bits)));
        end;
        return self.DoConstant(LType, LBits, AId);
      end;
      // A signed integer, a char (its code at its own type's sign) or a bool (0 / 1)
      LInt := self.DoConstBits(AId, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType);
      if LType = IrType.Float32 then
        LBits := int64(Float32ToBits(float32(LInt)));
      else
        LBits := int64(Float64ToBits(float64(LInt)));
      end;
      return self.DoConstant(LType, LBits, AId);
    end;

    // The value of expression AId where it is used (its constant when it folded: a float one
    // by DoFloatConstant, any other (DoIsFolded) read at its own type), converted to the type
    // it is used as; 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoValue(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      // under the target of an assignment used as a value, each value is made once
      if (self.FPinned <> nil) and self.DoIsPinned(AId, true) then
        LValue := self.FPinned.Find(AId);
        if LValue >= 0 then
          return LValue;
        end;
        LValue := self.DoMadeValue(AId);
        if LValue <> 0 then
          self.FPinned.Put(AId, LValue);
        end;
        return LValue;
      end;
      return self.DoMadeValue(AId);
    end;

    // DoValue's value of the expression AId, made
    hidden method DoMadeValue(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: IrType;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      // A string's or a dynamic array's value has its own forms (a literal's block, a
      // concatenation, a call's temporary, a place's)
      if self.DoIsManaged(self.DoUsedType(AId)) then
        return self.DoManagedValue(AId);
      end;
      if self.DoIsFloatConstant(AId) then
        return self.DoFloatConstant(AId);
      end;
      if self.DoIsFolded(AId) then
        LType := self.DoTypeAt(self.DoUsedType(AId), AId);
        if LType = IrType.Void then
          return 0;
        end;
        // a char read at its own type; one converted to a wchar (a literal: SEM wrote its
        // wide unit) at the wchar's width and sign
        if ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoUsedType(AId)) = TypeClass.WideChar then
          return self.DoConstant(LType, self.DoConstBits(AId, self.DoUsedType(AId)), AId);
        end;
        return self.DoConstant(LType, self.DoConstBits(AId, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType), AId);
      end;
      LValue := self.DoOwnValue(AId);
      if (LValue = 0) or (self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConvert = 0) then
        return LValue;
      end;
      return self.DoConvertTo(LValue, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType, self.FTree[AId].ResolvedConvert,
        AId);
    end;

    // The IR op of the compound assignment operator AOp, in AIrOp; true for += -= *= /= %=
    // &= |= <<= >>= (BNF sec 6; /= is fdiv, a float target's only: on an integer it is SEM's
    // SM0250). DoOpFits says which target types each takes
    hidden const method DoCompoundIrOp(const AOp: OperatorKind; var AIrOp: IrOp): bool;
    begin
      if AOp = OperatorKind.DivideAssign then
        AIrOp := IrOp.FDiv;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.AddAssign then
        AIrOp := IrOp.Add;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.SubtractAssign then
        AIrOp := IrOp.Sub;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.MultiplyAssign then
        AIrOp := IrOp.Mul;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.ModuloAssign then
        AIrOp := IrOp.SRem;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.BitAndAssign then
        AIrOp := IrOp.BitAnd;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.BitOrAssign then
        AIrOp := IrOp.BitOr;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.ShiftLeftAssign then
        AIrOp := IrOp.Shl;
        return true;
      end;
      if AOp = OperatorKind.ShiftRightAssign then
        AIrOp := IrOp.Shr;
        return true;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // The compound assignment AId on the typed ptr ATarget: `+=` / `-=` move it by the
    // value's count of elements (the value first, then the target's address once, as
    // DoCompound); LW0001 for any other operator
    hidden method DoPointerCompound(const AId: int64; const ATarget: int64);
    var
      LOp: OperatorKind;
      LValue: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LOld: int64;
    begin
      LOp := self.FTree[AId].Op;
      if (LOp <> OperatorKind.AddAssign) and (LOp <> OperatorKind.SubtractAssign) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsBoundProperty(ATarget) then
        // a property bound to its field: the object first, then the value (BNF sec 4)
        LAddress := self.DoAddressFor(ATarget, true);
        if LAddress = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LValue := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
        if LValue = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      else
        LValue := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
        if LValue = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LAddress := self.DoAddressFor(ATarget, true);
        if LAddress = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      LOld := self.DoLoad(LAddress, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      self.DoStore(LAddress, self.DoMovePointer(LOld, LValue, self.FTree[ATarget].ResolvedType,
        LOp = OperatorKind.SubtractAssign, AId), AId);
    end;

    // The compound assignment AId on an integer or float target (any place, a bitfield
    // through its lane: DoPlaceAddress): the value first (C++17 orders it before the
    // target; SEM converted it to the target's type, a shift's count excepted; a property
    // bound to its field takes its object first, BNF sec 4: DoIsBoundProperty), then the
    // target's address once, its value read, combined at the promoted type (a float at its
    // own) and written back as the target's type; `+=` / `-=` on a typed ptr moves it
    // (DoPointerCompound), a set's is DoSetCompound's, a string's DoStringCompound's (a
    // string's byte is written through DoWriteAddress); LW0001 for another target type or an
    // op the type does not take (DoOpFits)
    hidden method DoCompound(const AId: int64);
    var
      LOp: IrOp;
      LTarget: int64;
      LType: IrType;
      LValue: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LOld: int64;
    begin
      LOp := IrOp.Add;
      LTarget := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target);
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, self.FTree[LTarget].ResolvedType) = TypeClass.Pointer then
        self.DoPointerCompound(AId, LTarget);
        return;
      end;
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, self.FTree[LTarget].ResolvedType) = TypeClass.SetType then
        self.DoSetCompound(AId);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsText(self.FTree[LTarget].ResolvedType) then
        self.DoStringCompound(AId);
        return;
      end;
      LType := self.DoIrType(self.FTree[LTarget].ResolvedType);
      if (not self.DoCompoundIrOp(self.FTree[AId].Op, LOp)) or (not self.DoOpFits(LOp, LType)) then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsBoundProperty(LTarget) then
        // a property bound to its field: the object first, then the value (BNF sec 4)
        LAddress := self.DoWriteAddress(LTarget, LMember);
        if LAddress = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LValue := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
        if LValue = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      else
        LValue := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
        if LValue = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LAddress := self.DoWriteAddress(LTarget, LMember);
        if LAddress = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      LOld := self.DoReadAt(LMember, LAddress, LType, AId);
      self.DoWriteAt(LMember, LAddress, self.DoComputeIn(LOp, LOld, LValue, LType, AId), AId);
    end;

    // The assignment AId: plain ':=' to a place (a bitfield written into its lane, a
    // string's byte after copy on write: DoWriteAddress; the value first, a property bound
    // to its field's object first: DoIsBoundProperty), else a compound assignment
    // (DoCompound); a string's ':=' is DoManagedAssignment's; an aggregate's ':=' (a
    // record, an overlay, a static array) copies its bytes (DoAggregateAssign)
    hidden method DoAssign(const AId: int64);
    var
      LValue: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LTarget: int64;
    begin
      // a property written through its accessors (one that is its field is a place)
      LTarget := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target);
      while self.FTree[LTarget].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LTarget := self.FTree.FirstOf(LTarget, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      if self.DoIsPropertyAccess(LTarget) then
        self.DoPropertyAssign(AId, LTarget);
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[AId].Op <> OperatorKind.Assign then
        self.DoCompound(AId);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(self.FTree[self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target)].ResolvedType) then
        self.DoAggregateAssign(AId);
        return;
      end;
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, self.FTree[self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target)].ResolvedType) =
        TypeClass.Varargs then
        self.DoPackAssign(AId);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsManaged(self.FTree[self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target)].ResolvedType) then
        self.DoManagedAssignment(AId);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsBoundProperty(LTarget) then
        // a property bound to its field: the object first, then the value (BNF sec 4)
        LAddress := self.DoWriteAddress(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target), LMember);
        if LAddress = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LValue := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
        if LValue = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      else
        LValue := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
        if LValue = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LAddress := self.DoWriteAddress(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target), LMember);
        if LAddress = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      self.DoWriteAt(LMember, LAddress, LValue, AId);
    end;

    // The assignment AId used as a value (BNF sec 6: assignment is an expression; its value
    // is its target's after the write, as C++'s is, so `LA := LB := 4` sets both): the
    // assignment lowered (DoAssign) with every place under its target and every value
    // strictly below it made once (FPinned), then the target read back from them in AForm:
    // a scalar's value, a managed value's block (borrowed) or an aggregate's address; an
    // assignment in its source pins its own target meanwhile. 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAssignedValue(const AId: int64; const AForm: AssignedForm): int64;
    var
      LSavedPins: ref Int64Map;
      LSavedRoot: int64;
      LTarget: int64;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      LTarget := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target);
      LSavedPins := self.FPinned;
      LSavedRoot := self.FPinRoot;
      self.FPinned := ref Int64Map(-1);
      self.FPinRoot := LTarget;
      self.DoAssign(AId);
      LValue := 0;
      if not self.DoEnded() then
        if AForm = AssignedForm.Scalar then
          LValue := self.DoValue(LTarget);
        else
          if AForm = AssignedForm.Managed then
            LValue := self.DoManagedValue(LTarget);
          else
            LValue := self.DoAggregateSource(LTarget);
          end;
        end;
      end;
      self.FPinned := LSavedPins;
      self.FPinRoot := LSavedRoot;
      return LValue;
    end;

    // True when the assignment target AId (past its parens) is a property bound to its
    // field, so a place (DoIsPlace, DoBoundField): BNF sec 4 has `X := v` evaluate its
    // object then the value and `X OP= v` the object, the value, the current value, where
    // a plain place takes its value first (C++17's order)
    hidden const method DoIsBoundProperty(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LAt := self.DoUnparen(AId);
      return (self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.MemberExpression) and self.DoNamesProperty(LAt);
    end;

    // The aggregate assignment AId (a record, an overlay or a static array): the source's
    // address first, then the target's (the scalar path's order), then the value copied
    // (DoAggregateCopy: its bytes, its texts by its text map); a value object whose type
    // runs code where it is copied or ended goes by DoMoveAssign
    hidden method DoAggregateAssign(const AId: int64);
    var
      LTarget: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LDest: int64;
    begin
      LTarget := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target);
      if self.DoHasLifetime(self.FTree[LTarget].ResolvedType) then
        self.DoMoveAssign(AId);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsBoundProperty(LTarget) then
        // a property bound to its field: the object first, then the value (BNF sec 4)
        LDest := self.DoAddressFor(LTarget, true);
        if LDest = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
        if LSource = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      else
        LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
        if LSource = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LDest := self.DoAddressFor(LTarget, true);
        if LDest = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      self.DoAggregateCopy(LDest, LSource, self.FTree[LTarget].ResolvedType, AId);
    end;

    // The assignment AId of a value object whose type runs code where it is copied or
    // ended (DoHasLifetime; pcpp's truth, C++'s move and copy assignment): the source made
    // first, a call's result moved, any other value copied by its type's copy into a
    // zeroed slot of its own (DoCopyValue, BNF sec 4 O5: the source may be the target
    // itself or a part of it); then the target's old object ended (a local under its live
    // flag) and the new one moved in (DoMoveObject: the call's temporary no longer live;
    // the copy's bytes), the target live
    hidden method DoMoveAssign(const AId: int64);
    var
      LTarget: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LFrom: int64;
      LTo: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LDest: int64;
      LLive: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LTemp: int64;
    begin
      LTarget := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Target);
      LType := self.FTree[LTarget].ResolvedType;
      LFrom := self.DoMoveSource(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
      if (LFrom <> 0) and not self.DoIsCallSite(LFrom) then
        LFrom := 0;
      end;
      LDest := 0;
      if self.DoIsBoundProperty(LTarget) then
        // a property bound to its field: the object first, then the value (BNF sec 4)
        LDest := self.DoAddressFor(LTarget, true);
        if LDest = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Source));
      if LSource = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType);
      LTemp := 0;
      if LFrom = 0 then
        LTemp := self.DoSizedSlot(AId, LSize, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType));
        // zeroed each time it runs: a loop's next copy starts from nothing too
        self.DoFill(LTemp, LSize, AId);
        if not self.DoCopyValue(LTemp, LSource, LType, AId) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      if LDest = 0 then
        LDest := self.DoAddressFor(LTarget, true);
        if LDest = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      // a local is ended only while live; any other place (a field, a var parameter's
      // object) always holds a built one
      LTo := self.DoMoveSource(LTarget);
      LLive := 0;
      if LTo <> 0 then
        LLive := self.FLiveOf[LTo];
      end;
      if not self.DoReleaseLive(LDest, LType, LLive, false, AId) then
        return;
      end;
      if LFrom <> 0 then
        self.DoMoveObject(LDest, LSource, LFrom, LType, AId);
      else
        self.DoCopyBytes(LDest, LTemp, LSize, AId);
      end;
      self.DoSetLive(LTo, true, AId);
    end;

    // The return statement AId, with or without a value; in the program block it ends the
    // program as the block's end does (a jump to the entry's end block: the finalize
    // chain, then the runtime's exit with 0); in a section it leaves the section. Inside a
    // protected region the cleanups run first (DoJumpOut, DoKeepReturn: the value is read
    // before them and kept)
    hidden method DoReturn(const AId: int64);
    var
      LExpr: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      if (self.FEntry <> 0) and (self.FFunction = self.FEntry) then
        if not self.DoJumpOut(self.FEntryEnd, 0, AId) then
          self.DoJumpTo(self.FEntryEnd, AId);
        end;
        return;
      end;
      LExpr := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Value);
      if LExpr = 0 then
        if self.DoJumpOut(ADAM_LOWERING_RETURN_PAD, 0, AId) then
          return;
        end;
        self.DoReleaseManaged(AId);
        self.DoExitParts(AId);
        self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, AId);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(self.DoUsedType(LExpr)) then
        self.DoAggregateReturn(AId, LExpr);
        return;
      end;
      // The value is read before the managed slots are released (it may be one of them); a
      // text or a dynamic array goes back as a reference the caller holds (one more holder:
      // the slot it came from releases its own)
      LValue := self.DoValue(LExpr);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsManaged(self.DoUsedType(LExpr)) then
        if self.DoAddHolder(LValue, self.DoUsedType(LExpr), AId) = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      if self.DoKeepReturn(LValue, AId) then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoReleaseManaged(AId);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LValue);
    end;

    // The return AId of the aggregate value AExpr: through the hidden result pointer
    // (FResultSlot holds it) it is copied to the caller's slot (DoAggregateCopy: one that
    // holds texts is assigned over what the caller's managed temporary held) and that
    // address goes back; else its bytes go back as the register's integer (DoAggregateIr)
    hidden method DoAggregateReturn(const AId: int64; const AExpr: int64);
    var
      LType: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LFrom: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoUsedType(AExpr);
      // a value object whose type runs code where it is copied or ended goes back through
      // the hidden pointer (DoResultIr): moved out when it is a local, an owned value
      // parameter or a call's result (pcpp's truth: never ended here), else copied by its
      // type's copy into the caller's empty slot (DoCopyValue, BNF sec 4 O5)
      LFrom := 0;
      if self.DoHasLifetime(LType) then
        if self.FResultSlot = 0 then
          raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_HIDDEN_RESULT + self.FTree.ConstructText(AExpr));
        end;
        LFrom := self.DoMoveSource(AExpr);
      end;
      LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(AExpr);
      if LSource = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      if self.FResultSlot <> 0 then
        LValue := self.DoLoad(self.FResultSlot, IrType.Pointer, AId);
        if LFrom <> 0 then
          self.DoMoveObject(LValue, LSource, LFrom, LType, AId);
        else
          if self.DoHasLifetime(LType) then
            if not self.DoCopyValue(LValue, LSource, LType, AId) then
              return;
            end;
          else
            self.DoAggregateCopy(LValue, LSource, LType, AId);
          end;
        end;
      else
        LValue := self.DoLoad(LSource, self.DoAggregateIr(LType), AId);
      end;
      if self.DoKeepReturn(LValue, AId) then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoReleaseManaged(AId);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LValue);
    end;

    // The statement AId; code after a return goes to a new block nothing jumps to
    hidden method DoStatement(const AId: int64);
    var
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LExpr: int64;
    begin
      if self.DoEnded() then
        self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      end;
      LKind := self.FTree[AId].Kind;
      // a lead init call built its part already, before the body (DoEnterParts)
      if self.DoIsLeadStatement(AId) then
        return;
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.ExpressionStatement then
        LExpr := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Value);
        if self.FTree[LExpr].Kind = NodeKind.AssignExpression then
          self.DoAssign(LExpr);
        else
          self.DoValue(LExpr);
        end;
        self.DoEndTemporaries(LExpr);
        return;
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.ReturnStatement then
        self.DoReturn(AId);
        return;
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.YieldStatement then
        self.DoYield(AId);
        return;
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.Block then
        self.DoStatements(AId, NodeRole.Statement);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsStatementLocal(AId) then
        self.DoStatementLocal(AId);
        return;
      end;
      // a type block among statements runs nothing: its TypeInfo and member functions are
      // made with the module's (DoLocalTypes)
      if LKind = NodeKind.TypeDecl then
        return;
      end;
      // an @message among statements runs nothing: Semantics reported it (BNF sec 2 / 5);
      // an @breakpoint marks its line with code of its own (IrOp.Mark: the debugger's
      // address there, DESIGN sec 9)
      if LKind = NodeKind.Directive then
        if self.FTree[AId].Text = ADAM_LOWERING_DIRECTIVE_MESSAGE then
          return;
        end;
        if self.FTree[AId].Text = ADAM_LOWERING_DIRECTIVE_BREAKPOINT then
          self.DoEmit(IrOp.Mark, IrType.Void, AId);
          return;
        end;
      end;
      if self.DoFlow(AId) then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
    end;

    // The flow statement AId of BNF sec 5 (if, while, repeat, for, match, leave, skip)
    // lowered; false when AId is none of them
    hidden method DoFlow(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LKind: NodeKind;
    begin
      LKind := self.FTree[AId].Kind;
      if LKind = NodeKind.IfStatement then
        self.DoIf(AId);
        return true;
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.WhileStatement then
        self.DoWhile(AId);
        return true;
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.RepeatStatement then
        self.DoRepeat(AId);
        return true;
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.ForStatement then
        self.DoFor(AId);
        return true;
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.ForInStatement then
        self.DoForIn(AId);
        return true;
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.MatchStatement then
        self.DoMatch(AId);
        // the subject is read by every label test: its temporaries end with the match
        self.DoEndTemporaries(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Subject));
        return true;
      end;
      if (LKind = NodeKind.LeaveStatement) or (LKind = NodeKind.SkipStatement) then
        self.DoLeaveSkip(AId);
        return true;
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.GuardStatement then
        self.DoGuard(AId);
        return true;
      end;
      if (LKind = NodeKind.LockStatement) or (LKind = NodeKind.TryLockStatement) then
        self.DoLock(AId);
        return true;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // The statements of AParent in the role ARole (a block's Statement, an if's Then /
    // Else), in order
    hidden method DoStatements(const AParent: int64; const ARole: NodeRole);
    begin
      self.DoStatementsFrom(AParent, ARole, 0);
    end;

    // AParent's statements in the role ARole from the AFrom-th on, in order; a defer
    // statement among them takes the rest of the list as its region (DoDefer)
    hidden method DoStatementsFrom(const AParent: int64; const ARole: NodeRole;
      const AFrom: int64);
    var
      LI: int64;
      LStatement: int64;
    begin
      for LI := AFrom to self.FTree.CountOf(AParent, ARole) - 1 do
        LStatement := self.FTree.NthOf(AParent, ARole, LI);
        if self.FTree[LStatement].Kind = NodeKind.DeferStatement then
          self.DoDefer(LStatement, AParent, ARole, LI + 1);
          return;
        end;
        self.DoStatement(LStatement);
      end;
    end;

    // The defer statement AId (BNF sec 5, D1), the AFrom-th on of AParent's statements in
    // ARole the ones after it: its statement runs when the list ends, by any way out, the
    // last defer first (a later defer is a region inside this one). With nothing after it,
    // it runs here. Else the rest is a protected region (DoEnterRegion) whose cleanup is the
    // defer's statement (DoRegionCleanup), as a lock's: where the rest falls through, in a
    // block after it; on a return, leave or skip, in their pads (DoClosePads); on an unwind,
    // in a funclet (DoFinallyFunclet) the scope over the rest's blocks names. Inside a
    // loop's statements each pass enters and leaves it. LW0001 inside a guard's finally or
    // another region's funclet (a funclet's funclet would reach two frames), and with no
    // frame handler
    hidden method DoDefer(const AId: int64; const AParent: int64; const ARole: NodeRole;
      const AFrom: int64);
    var
      LFunction: ref IrFunction;
      LHandler: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LLast: int64;
      LBodyFalls: bool;
      LBodyEnd: int64;
      LRun: int64;
      LFunclet: int64;
    begin
      if AFrom >= self.FTree.CountOf(AParent, ARole) then
        // The list ends right here: the statement runs now
        self.DoRegionCleanup(AId);
        return;
      end;
      LFunction := self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction);
      if LFunction.Parent <> 0 then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId) + " inside a guard's finally");
        return;
      end;
      LHandler := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.FrameHandler, AId);
      if LHandler = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoEnded() then
        self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      end;
      // A jump out of the rest runs the deferred statement on its way (DoJumpOut)
      self.DoEnterRegion(AId);
      LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoJumpTo(LBody, AId);
      // The rest's blocks run from their own first block to the last one they made
      self.FBlock := LBody;
      LFirst := LFunction.Blocks.Count - 1;
      self.DoStatementsFrom(AParent, ARole, AFrom);
      LLast := LFunction.Blocks.Count - 1;
      LBodyFalls := not self.DoEnded();
      LBodyEnd := self.FBlock;
      // Where the rest falls through: the deferred statement, then the code after the list
      LRun := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      if LBodyFalls then
        self.FBlock := LBodyEnd;
        self.DoJumpTo(LRun, AId);
      end;
      self.FBlock := LRun;
      self.DoClosePads(AId);
      self.DoRegionCleanup(AId);
      // Added after every scope inside the rest: the innermost comes first
      LFunclet := self.DoFinallyFunclet(AId);
      LFunction.AddScope(LFirst, LLast, LFunclet, -1);
      self.FModule.FrameHandler := LHandler;
    end;

    // AParent's statements in the role ARole lowered from the block ABlock; true when they
    // fall through (the block they end in has no terminator)
    hidden method DoArm(const ABlock: int64; const AParent: int64; const ARole: NodeRole): bool;
    begin
      self.FBlock := ABlock;
      self.DoStatements(AParent, ARole);
      return not self.DoEnded();
    end;

    // A jump to ATarget from the end of the block AFrom (an arm that fell through), at ANode
    hidden method DoJumpFrom(const AFrom: int64; const ATarget: int64; const ANode: int64);
    begin
      self.FBlock := AFrom;
      self.DoJumpTo(ATarget, ANode);
    end;

    // The if statement AId: a branch on its condition to the then statements and to the else
    // statements, or straight to the join when there are none. With an else, the join is
    // made only when a side falls through to it: when both end (a return in each), what
    // follows starts a block nothing jumps to, as after a return
    hidden method DoIf(const AId: int64);
    var
      LCondition: int64;
      LThen: int64;
      LElse: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
      LThenFalls: bool;
      LThenEnd: int64;
      LElseFalls: bool;
      LElseEnd: int64;
    begin
      LCondition := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Condition));
      if LCondition = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoEndTemporaries(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Condition));
      LThen := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      if self.FTree.CountOf(AId, NodeRole.Else) = 0 then
        LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
        self.DoBranchOn(LCondition, LThen, LJoin, AId);
        if self.DoArm(LThen, AId, NodeRole.Then) then
          self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, AId);
        end;
        self.FBlock := LJoin;
        return;
      end;
      LElse := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoBranchOn(LCondition, LThen, LElse, AId);
      LThenFalls := self.DoArm(LThen, AId, NodeRole.Then);
      LThenEnd := self.FBlock;
      LElseFalls := self.DoArm(LElse, AId, NodeRole.Else);
      LElseEnd := self.FBlock;
      if (not LThenFalls) and (not LElseFalls) then
        return;
      end;
      LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      if LThenFalls then
        self.DoJumpFrom(LThenEnd, LJoin, AId);
      end;
      if LElseFalls then
        self.DoJumpFrom(LElseEnd, LJoin, AId);
      end;
      self.FBlock := LJoin;
    end;

    // The while statement AId: a head block testing the condition on every pass, to the
    // body (which jumps back to the head when it falls through) or to the exit block; leave
    // goes to the exit, skip to the head
    hidden method DoWhile(const AId: int64);
    var
      LHead: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LExit: int64;
      LCondition: int64;
    begin
      LHead := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LExit := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoJumpTo(LHead, AId);
      self.FBlock := LHead;
      LCondition := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Condition));
      if LCondition = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoEndTemporaries(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Condition));
      self.DoBranchOn(LCondition, LBody, LExit, AId);
      self.FExitOf[AId] := LExit;
      self.FNextOf[AId] := LHead;
      if self.DoArm(LBody, AId, NodeRole.Statement) then
        self.DoJumpTo(LHead, AId);
      end;
      self.FBlock := LExit;
    end;

    // The repeat statement AId: the body first (it falls through to the test block), the
    // test evaluating the until condition, to the exit when it holds, else back to the
    // body; leave goes to the exit, skip to the test
    hidden method DoRepeat(const AId: int64);
    var
      LBody: int64;
      LTest: int64;
      LExit: int64;
      LCondition: int64;
    begin
      LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LTest := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LExit := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoJumpTo(LBody, AId);
      self.FExitOf[AId] := LExit;
      self.FNextOf[AId] := LTest;
      if self.DoArm(LBody, AId, NodeRole.Statement) then
        self.DoJumpTo(LTest, AId);
      end;
      self.FBlock := LTest;
      LCondition := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Condition));
      if LCondition = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoEndTemporaries(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Condition));
      self.DoBranchOn(LCondition, LExit, LBody, AId);
      self.FBlock := LExit;
    end;

    // The for AId's bounds, in PaskalCPP's order: the start stored in the iterator
    // AIterator, then the end evaluated once into the for's own slot (AEnd, of the
    // iterator's type: SEM converted both bounds to it); the iterator's address, 0 after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoForBounds(const AId: int64; const AIterator: int64; var AEnd: int64): int64;
    var
      LAddress: int64;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      LAddress := self.DoAddressFor(AIterator, true);
      if LAddress = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Start));
      if LValue = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoStore(LAddress, LValue, AId);
      LValue := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Limit));
      if LValue = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      AEnd := self.DoSlot(AId, self.FTree[AIterator].ResolvedType, false);
      if AEnd = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      self.DoStore(AEnd, LValue, AId);
      return LAddress;
    end;

    // A branch from the current block on `I AOp end` (the iterator at AAddress, the end in
    // the slot AEnd, both of AIr, signed or unsigned as AIr is): to AOnTrue when it holds,
    // else to AOnFalse, at ANode
    hidden method DoForTest(const AOp: OperatorKind; const AAddress: int64; const AEnd: int64;
      const AIr: IrType; const AOnTrue: int64; const AOnFalse: int64; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LPredicate: IrPredicate;
      LIterator: int64;
      LEnd: int64;
    begin
      // <=, >= and <> on an integer type always have a predicate
      if not self.DoPredicateOf(AOp, AIr, LPredicate) then
        return;
      end;
      LIterator := self.DoLoad(AAddress, AIr, ANode);
      LEnd := self.DoLoad(AEnd, AIr, ANode);
      self.DoBranchOn(self.DoCompareWith(LPredicate, LIterator, LEnd, ANode), AOnTrue, AOnFalse,
        ANode);
    end;

    // The for AId's step: its iterator (at AAddress, of AIr) one up (to) or one down
    // (downto), computed at the promoted type and stored back (a char's, a choice's ordinal
    // the same way)
    hidden method DoForStep(const AId: int64; const AAddress: int64; const AIr: IrType);
    var
      LOp: IrOp;
      LOld: int64;
      LNew: int64;
    begin
      LOp := IrOp.Add;
      if self.FTree[AId].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Downto) then
        LOp := IrOp.Sub;
      end;
      LOld := self.DoLoad(AAddress, AIr, AId);
      LNew := self.DoComputeIn(LOp, LOld, self.DoConstant(AIr, 1, AId), AIr, AId);
      self.DoStore(AAddress, LNew, AId);
    end;

    // The for statement AId by PaskalCPP's contract (BNF sec 5; its emitter's DoEmitFor):
    // the bounds (DoForBounds), the loop entered when I <= end (>= for downto); after each
    // pass the next block leaves when I = end, else a step block steps I by one and goes
    // round again, so I never steps past the end nor its type's last value, and keeps the
    // start on an empty range; leave goes to the exit, skip to the next block (the step
    // still runs). The next block and the step take the iterator's address again: a
    // threadstatic's is the running thread's copy, and a yield in the statements may resume
    // a generator's body on another thread (G1d0)
    hidden method DoFor(const AId: int64);
    var
      LIterator: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
      LAddress: int64;
      LEnd: int64;
      LOp: OperatorKind;
      LBody: int64;
      LNext: int64;
      LStep: int64;
      LExit: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Parallel) then
        self.DoParallelFor(AId);
        return;
      end;
      LIterator := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Iterator);
      LIr := self.DoTypeAt(self.FTree[LIterator].ResolvedType, LIterator);
      if LIr = IrType.Void then
        return;
      end;
      LEnd := 0;
      LAddress := self.DoForBounds(AId, LIterator, LEnd);
      if LAddress = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      // both bounds are stored: their temporaries end here
      self.DoEndTemporaries(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Start));
      self.DoEndTemporaries(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Limit));
      LOp := OperatorKind.LessEqual;
      if self.FTree[AId].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Downto) then
        LOp := OperatorKind.GreaterEqual;
      end;
      LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LNext := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LStep := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LExit := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoForTest(LOp, LAddress, LEnd, LIr, LBody, LExit, AId);
      self.FExitOf[AId] := LExit;
      self.FNextOf[AId] := LNext;
      if self.DoArm(LBody, AId, NodeRole.Statement) then
        self.DoJumpTo(LNext, AId);
      end;
      self.FBlock := LNext;
      LAddress := self.DoAddressFor(LIterator, true);
      if LAddress = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoForTest(OperatorKind.NotEqual, LAddress, LEnd, LIr, LStep, LExit, AId);
      self.FBlock := LStep;
      LAddress := self.DoAddressFor(LIterator, true);
      if LAddress = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoForStep(AId, LAddress, LIr);
      self.DoJumpTo(LBody, AId);
      self.FBlock := LExit;
    end;

    // The hold of the for in AId (BNF sec 5, G1) on the value it walks, made with the
    // function's temporaries (DoTemporaries): a text's or a dynamic array's block (a holder
    // of its own: the loop walks the value as it was at its start, copy on write), a static
    // array holding managed values or values with a lifetime (a copy of its own, ended under
    // its live flag); none for any other (a plain static array or a set is copied by its
    // bytes into a slot of DoForIn's)
    hidden method DoForInTemporary(const AId: int64);
    var
      LType: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoUsedType(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Value));
      if self.DoIsText(LType) then
        self.DoTemporary(AId);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsArrayValue(LType) or (ClassOf(self.FTree, LType) = TypeClass.SequenceType) then
        self.DoPointerTemporary(AId, LType);
        return;
      end;
      if (ClassOf(self.FTree, LType) <> TypeClass.StaticArray) or
        not (self.DoHoldsManaged(LType) or self.DoHasLifetime(LType)) then
        return;
      end;
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType);
      LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(AId, LSize, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType));
      self.DoFill(LSlot, LSize, AId);
      self.FTempOf[AId] := LSlot;
      self.FTempTypeOf[AId] := LType;
      self.DoAddManaged(LSlot, LType, AId);
    end;

    // The element of a for in stored into its iterator AIterator, of the canonical type
    // AElement, as an assignment stores it: from the address ASource, or (ASource 0) the
    // scalar AValue. An aggregate by DoAggregateCopy, one with a lifetime as DoMoveAssign
    // moves a copy in (the iterator's old object ended under its live flag); a managed
    // value by DoStoreManaged (a holder added, the old one released); a scalar by its bytes.
    // False after LW0001
    hidden method DoForInStore(const AIterator: int64; const ASource: int64; const AValue: int64;
      const AElement: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LDest: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
      LSize: int64;
      LTemp: int64;
      LTo: int64;
      LLive: int64;
    begin
      LDest := self.DoAddressFor(AIterator, true);
      if LDest = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      if ASource = 0 then
        self.DoStore(LDest, AValue, ANode);
        return true;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(AElement) then
        if not self.DoHasLifetime(AElement) then
          self.DoAggregateCopy(LDest, ASource, AElement, ANode);
          return not self.DoEnded();
        end;
        LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AElement);
        LTemp := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, LSize, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AElement));
        // zeroed each pass: the next copy starts from nothing too
        self.DoFill(LTemp, LSize, ANode);
        if not self.DoCopyValue(LTemp, ASource, AElement, ANode) then
          return false;
        end;
        LTo := self.DoMoveSource(AIterator);
        LLive := 0;
        if LTo <> 0 then
          LLive := self.FLiveOf[LTo];
        end;
        if not self.DoReleaseLive(LDest, AElement, LLive, false, ANode) then
          return false;
        end;
        self.DoCopyBytes(LDest, LTemp, LSize, ANode);
        self.DoSetLive(LTo, true, ANode);
        return true;
      end;
      if self.DoIsManaged(AElement) then
        return self.DoStoreManaged(LDest, self.DoLoad(ASource, IrType.Pointer, ANode), AElement,
          ANode) <> 0;
      end;
      LIr := self.DoTypeAt(AElement, ANode);
      if LIr = IrType.Void then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoStore(LDest, self.DoLoad(ASource, LIr, ANode), ANode);
      return true;
    end;

    // `for X in S do .. end;` AId over an array, a string, a wstring or a set (BNF sec 5,
    // G1; a sequence's is DoForInSequence's). S is read once, here, and walked as it was: a text's or a
    // dynamic array's block held (DoForInTemporary's slot, a holder added), a static array
    // copied (into that slot when it holds managed values or lifetimes, else into a plain
    // slot by its bytes), a set's bytes copied; then S's temporaries end. A counter slot
    // from 0 while below the count (a static array's, a set's member range, else the
    // block's length): the head tests it; the body stores the element (DoForInStore: an
    // array's at the counter, a text's unit, a set's member low + counter when its bit is
    // set, else straight to the next pass) and runs the statements; `skip` goes to the next
    // block (the counter one more, back to the head), `leave` to the exit, where the hold
    // ends (DoEndTemporary; a return or an unwind releases it with the function's managed
    // slots)
    hidden method DoForIn(const AId: int64);
    var
      LSubject: int64;
      LIterator: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LElement: int64;
      LClass: TypeClass;
      LValue: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LCopy: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LCountSlot: int64;
      LCounter: int64;
      LLow: int64;
      LHigh: int64;
      LHead: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LStatements: int64;
      LNext: int64;
      LExit: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LBase: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LByte: int64;
      LBit: int64;
      LMember: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
      LScale: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LSubject := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Value);
      LIterator := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Iterator);
      LType := self.DoUsedType(LSubject);
      LElement := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedType;
      LClass := ClassOf(self.FTree, LType);
      if LClass = TypeClass.SequenceType then
        self.DoForInSequence(AId);
        return;
      end;
      // a scalar element's IR type (a managed or aggregate one is stored by its address)
      LIr := IrType.Void;
      if not (self.DoIsManaged(LElement) or self.DoIsAggregate(LElement)) then
        LIr := self.DoTypeAt(LElement, LIterator);
        if LIr = IrType.Void then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      LLow := 0;
      LHigh := 0;
      LCopy := 0;
      LCountSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(AId, 8, 8);
      if (LClass = TypeClass.Text) or (LClass = TypeClass.WideText) or (LClass = TypeClass.DynamicArray) then
        if LClass = TypeClass.DynamicArray then
          LValue := self.DoValue(LSubject);
        else
          LValue := self.DoManagedValue(LSubject);
        end;
        if LValue = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        if self.DoAddHolder(LValue, LType, AId) = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        self.DoStore(self.DoTempSlot(AId), LValue, AId);
        LCount := self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.StrLength, LValue, 0, AId);
        if LCount = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        self.DoStore(LCountSlot, self.DoConvertIr(LCount, IrType.Int64, AId), AId);
      else
        // a static array or a set: its bytes (or its copy) in a slot of the loop's own
        LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(LSubject);
        if LSource = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType);
        if self.FTempOf[AId] <> 0 then
          LCopy := self.FTempOf[AId];
          if not self.DoCopyValue(LCopy, LSource, LType, AId) then
            return;
          end;
          self.DoSetLive(AId, true, AId);
        else
          LCopy := self.DoSizedSlot(AId, LSize, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType));
          self.DoCopyBytes(LCopy, LSource, LSize, AId);
        end;
        if LClass = TypeClass.SetType then
          if not SetRange(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType, LLow, LHigh) then
            raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_LOW_BOUND + TypeText(self.FTree, LType));
          end;
          LCount := LHigh - LLow + 1;
        else
          LCount := ArrayCount(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType);
          if LCount < 0 then
            raise(ADAM_LOWERING_FAULT_ARRAY_COUNT + TypeText(self.FTree, LType));
          end;
        end;
        self.DoStore(LCountSlot, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LCount, AId), AId);
      end;
      // S is read once: its temporaries end here
      self.DoEndTemporaries(LSubject);
      LCounter := self.DoSizedSlot(AId, 8, 8);
      self.DoStore(LCounter, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, AId), AId);
      LHead := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LStatements := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LNext := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LExit := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoJumpTo(LHead, AId);
      self.FBlock := LHead;
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, AId);
      self.DoBranchOn(self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.SLess, LIndex,
        self.DoLoad(LCountSlot, IrType.Int64, AId), AId), LBody, LExit, AId);
      self.FBlock := LBody;
      // the counter read again in the body: its value is the body's own
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, AId);
      if LClass = TypeClass.SetType then
        // the member's byte (its bit div 8), then its bit in that byte (its bit mod 8); every
        // operand emitted before the instruction that uses it
        LByte := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.Shr, LIndex, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 3, AId),
          IrType.Int64, AId);
        LAt := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Offset, IrType.Pointer, AId);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LAt).Operands.Add(LCopy);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LAt).Operands.Add(LByte);
        LByte := self.DoConvertIr(self.DoLoad(LAt, IrType.UInt8, AId), IrType.Int64, AId);
        LBit := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.BitAnd, self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.Shr, LByte,
          self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.BitAnd, LIndex, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 7, AId), IrType.Int64, AId),
          IrType.Int64, AId), self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 1, AId), IrType.Int64, AId);
        LMember := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
        self.DoBranchOn(self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.NotEqual, LBit, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, AId),
          AId), LMember, LNext, AId);
        self.FBlock := LMember;
        LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, AId);
        LValue := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.Add, LIndex, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LLow, AId), IrType.Int64, AId);
        // a bool member is the compare (no integer converts to bool), any other the value as
        // its IR type
        if LIr = IrType.Bool then
          LValue := self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.NotEqual, LValue, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, AId), AId);
        else
          LValue := self.DoConvertIr(LValue, LIr, AId);
        end;
        if not self.DoForInStore(LIterator, 0, LValue, LElement, AId) then
          return;
        end;
      else
        if (LClass = TypeClass.Text) or (LClass = TypeClass.WideText) then
          LBase := self.DoByteOffset(self.DoLoad(self.DoTempSlot(AId), IrType.Pointer, AId),
            ADAM_LOWERING_STRING_HEADER, AId);
          // a wstring's unit is 2 bytes
          if LClass = TypeClass.WideText then
            LScale := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, ADAM_LOWERING_WIDE_UNIT, AId);
            LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Mul, IrType.Int64, AId);
            self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LIndex);
            self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LScale);
            LIndex := LId;
          end;
          LAt := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Offset, IrType.Pointer, AId);
          self.FModule.InstrAt(LAt).Operands.Add(LBase);
          self.FModule.InstrAt(LAt).Operands.Add(LIndex);
        else
          if LClass = TypeClass.DynamicArray then
            LBase := self.DoByteOffset(self.DoLoad(self.DoTempSlot(AId), IrType.Pointer, AId),
              ADAM_LOWERING_ARRAY_HEADER, AId);
          else
            LBase := LCopy;
          end;
          LAt := self.DoMovePointer(LBase, LIndex, LType, false, AId);
        end;
        if not self.DoForInStore(LIterator, LAt, 0, LElement, AId) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      self.DoJumpTo(LStatements, AId);
      self.FExitOf[AId] := LExit;
      self.FNextOf[AId] := LNext;
      if self.DoArm(LStatements, AId, NodeRole.Statement) then
        self.DoJumpTo(LNext, AId);
      end;
      self.FBlock := LNext;
      // the operands emitted before the add that uses them
      LIndex := self.DoLoad(LCounter, IrType.Int64, AId);
      LId := self.DoComputeIn(IrOp.Add, LIndex, self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 1, AId), IrType.Int64, AId);
      self.DoStore(LCounter, LId, AId);
      self.DoJumpTo(LHead, AId);
      self.FBlock := LExit;
      self.DoEndTemporary(AId);
    end;

    // `for X in S do .. end;` AId over a sequence (BNF sec 5, G1): S read once and held
    // (DoForInTemporary's slot, a holder added; its block kept in FSlotOf[AId] for the
    // cleanup), S's temporaries ended. The passes are a protected region (DoEnterRegion):
    // the head resumes the generator (GeneratorResume: false once it has ended; a raise out
    // of its body is raised again there), the body stores its value (in its object at
    // DoGeneratorValueOffset: DoForInStore) and runs the statements; `skip` goes back to the
    // head, `leave` to the exit, both inside the region. Its cleanup aborts a generator the
    // loop leaves unfinished (DoRegionCleanup: GeneratorAbort, nothing for one that ended):
    // after the exit, in the pads of a return or a jump out of the loop (DoClosePads), in a
    // funclet on an unwind (DoFinallyFunclet). Then the hold ends (DoEndTemporary; a return
    // or an unwind releases it with the function's managed slots). LW0001 inside a guard's
    // finally (a funclet's funclet would reach two frames), and with no frame handler
    hidden method DoForInSequence(const AId: int64);
    var
      LFunction: ref IrFunction;
      LHandler: int64;
      LSubject: int64;
      LIterator: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LElement: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LHead: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LStatements: int64;
      LExit: int64;
      LRun: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LLast: int64;
      LMore: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LFunclet: int64;
    begin
      LFunction := self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction);
      if LFunction.Parent <> 0 then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId) + " inside a guard's finally");
        return;
      end;
      LHandler := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.FrameHandler, AId);
      if LHandler = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LSubject := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Value);
      LIterator := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Iterator);
      LType := self.DoUsedType(LSubject);
      LElement := self.FTree[LType].ResolvedType;
      LValue := self.DoValue(LSubject);
      if LValue = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoAddHolder(LValue, LType, AId) = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoStore(self.DoTempSlot(AId), LValue, AId);
      LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(AId, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
      self.FSlotOf[AId] := LSlot;
      self.DoStore(LSlot, LValue, AId);
      // S is read once: its temporaries end here
      self.DoEndTemporaries(LSubject);
      // A jump out of the passes aborts the generator on its way (DoJumpOut)
      self.DoEnterRegion(AId);
      LHead := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoJumpTo(LHead, AId);
      // The passes' blocks run from the head to the last one the statements made
      LFirst := LFunction.Blocks.Count - 1;
      LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LStatements := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LExit := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.FBlock := LHead;
      LMore := self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.GeneratorResume, self.DoLoad(LSlot, IrType.Pointer, AId), 0, AId);
      if LMore = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoBranchOn(LMore, LBody, LExit, AId);
      self.FBlock := LBody;
      LAt := self.DoByteOffset(self.DoLoad(LSlot, IrType.Pointer, AId),
        ADAM_LOWERING_REF_HEADER + self.DoGeneratorValueOffset(LElement), AId);
      if not self.DoForInStore(LIterator, LAt, 0, LElement, AId) then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoJumpTo(LStatements, AId);
      self.FExitOf[AId] := LExit;
      self.FNextOf[AId] := LHead;
      if self.DoArm(LStatements, AId, NodeRole.Statement) then
        self.DoJumpTo(LHead, AId);
      end;
      LLast := LFunction.Blocks.Count - 1;
      // The loop's end and its leave: the abort (none for an ended generator) after the
      // region's blocks, then the code after the loop
      LRun := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.FBlock := LExit;
      self.DoJumpTo(LRun, AId);
      self.FBlock := LRun;
      self.DoClosePads(AId);
      self.DoRegionCleanup(AId);
      // Added after every scope inside the passes: the innermost comes first
      LFunclet := self.DoFinallyFunclet(AId);
      LFunction.AddScope(LFirst, LLast, LFunclet, -1);
      self.FModule.FrameHandler := LHandler;
      self.DoEndTemporary(AId);
    end;

    // The address of the storage of the variable or parameter ADecl of the current function
    // (a by-reference one's address its slot holds); 0 when it has no slot (a folded
    // constant, or a refusal reported at its declaration)
    hidden method DoDeclAddress(const ADecl: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    begin
      if self.FSlotOf[ADecl] = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      if self.FByRef[ADecl] then
        return self.DoLoad(self.FSlotOf[ADecl], IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      end;
      return self.FSlotOf[ADecl];
    end;

    // `for parallel [(W)] I := A to|downto B do .. end;` AId (BNF sec 5, T2): its bounds
    // (converted to I's type by SEM) and W evaluated once, here; its frame, a slot of one
    // address per word: self's object first when the routine is a method's, then each
    // Capture's variable's storage (DoDeclAddress; nil for one with none), so the body
    // reaches them by reference; then System.Runtime's ParallelRun called with the body's
    // function (DoParallelEntry, lowered last: DoParallelBody), the frame, the bounds as 64
    // bits (extended by their signedness), the flags (downto, unsigned, W given) and W. It
    // returns once every iteration has ended, raising again the first raise of the body
    hidden method DoParallelFor(const AId: int64);
    var
      LIterator: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
      LStart: int64;
      LLimit: int64;
      LWorkersNode: int64;
      LWorkers: int64;
      LFlags: int64;
      LWord: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LFrame: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LEntry: int64;
      LSelf: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LIterator := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Iterator);
      LIr := self.DoTypeAt(self.FTree[LIterator].ResolvedType, LIterator);
      if LIr = IrType.Void then
        return;
      end;
      LStart := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Start));
      if LStart = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LLimit := self.DoValue(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Limit));
      if LLimit = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LFlags := 0;
      if self.FTree[AId].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Downto) then
        LFlags := LFlags | ADAM_LOWERING_PARALLEL_DOWNTO;
      end;
      if not IsSignedType(LIr) then
        LFlags := LFlags | ADAM_LOWERING_PARALLEL_UNSIGNED;
      end;
      LWorkersNode := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Value);
      if LWorkersNode <> 0 then
        LWorkers := self.DoValue(LWorkersNode);
        if LWorkers = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LWorkers := self.DoConvertIr(LWorkers, IrType.Int64, AId);
        LFlags := LFlags | ADAM_LOWERING_PARALLEL_GIVEN;
      else
        LWorkers := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, AId);
      end;
      // the bounds and W are read once: their temporaries end here
      self.DoEndTemporaries(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Start));
      self.DoEndTemporaries(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Limit));
      if LWorkersNode <> 0 then
        self.DoEndTemporaries(LWorkersNode);
      end;
      LWord := self.FTarget.PointerSize();
      LSelf := 0;
      if self.FSelfSlot <> 0 then
        LSelf := 1;
      end;
      LCount := self.FTree.CountOf(AId, NodeRole.Capture) + LSelf;
      if LCount = 0 then
        LFrame := self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, AId);
      else
        LFrame := self.DoSizedSlot(AId, LCount * LWord, self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
        LAt := 0;
        if LSelf <> 0 then
          self.DoStore(LFrame, self.DoLoad(self.FSelfSlot, IrType.Pointer, AId), AId);
          LAt := 1;
        end;
        for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AId, NodeRole.Capture) - 1 do
          LAddress := self.DoDeclAddress(self.FTree[self.FTree.NthOf(AId, NodeRole.Capture, LI)].ResolvedDecl, AId);
          if LAddress = 0 then
            LAddress := self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, AId);
          end;
          self.DoStore(self.DoByteOffset(LFrame, (LAt + LI) * LWord, AId), LAddress, AId);
        end;
      end;
      LEntry := self.DoEmit(IrOp.CodeAddress, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LEntry).Link := self.DoParallelEntry(AId, LSelf);
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(LEntry);
      LArgs.Add(LFrame);
      LArgs.Add(self.DoConvertIr(LStart, IrType.Int64, AId));
      LArgs.Add(self.DoConvertIr(LLimit, IrType.Int64, AId));
      LArgs.Add(self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LFlags, AId));
      LArgs.Add(LWorkers);
      self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.ParallelRun, LArgs, AId);
    end;

    // A new body function for the for parallel AFor (internal, System.Runtime's
    // ParallelEntry: the frame, the value, the worker, the workers' count; a bool back),
    // ASelf 1 when its frame starts with self; its body (DoParallelBody) is lowered last
    // (DoDeferredBodies), as the lowering of the routine holding AFor is still under way
    hidden method DoParallelEntry(const AFor: int64; const ASelf: int64): int64;
    var
      LFunction: int64;
    begin
      LFunction := self.FModule.AddFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_PARALLEL_SYMBOL + IntToStr(self.FParallelEntries.Count),
        IrType.Bool, AFor);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Internal := true;
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.AddParam(IrType.Pointer);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.AddParam(IrType.Int64);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.AddParam(IrType.Int64);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Signature.AddParam(IrType.Int64);
      self.FParallelEntries.Add(LFunction);
      self.FParallelNodes.Add(AFor);
      self.FParallelSelves.Add(ASelf);
      return LFunction;
    end;

    // Every for parallel body (DoParallelEntry's functions, DoParallelBody) and task entry's
    // body (DoTaskEntry's, DoTaskEntryBody; a generator's body function too, DoGeneratorEntry),
    // each in a fresh function state, until none is left: a body may hold another for
    // parallel or async, an async block's either (T4)
    hidden method DoDeferredBodies();
    var
      LParallel: int64;
      LTask: int64;
    begin
      LParallel := 0;
      LTask := 0;
      while (LParallel < self.FParallelEntries.Count) or (LTask < self.FTaskEntries.Count) do
        if LParallel < self.FParallelEntries.Count then
          self.DoParallelBody(LParallel);
          LParallel := LParallel + 1;
          skip;
        end;
        self.DoTaskEntryBody(LTask);
        LTask := LTask + 1;
      end;
    end;

    // The body function AIndex (DoParallelEntry) of a for parallel: its parameters (the
    // worker and the count are workerindex() / workercount()); self and each Capture's
    // variable reached through the frame (a slot holding the address the frame word gives,
    // the variable by reference while this body is lowered: FSlotOf / FByRef, given back
    // after); the iterator a slot of its own holding the value at its type; the body's
    // temporaries and statement locals (DoCodeTemporaries over the loop, FBodyRoot);
    // then the statements, a leave ending the body with true (no new iteration starts), its
    // end and a skip with false, each exit releasing what the body holds
    hidden method DoParallelBody(const AIndex: int64);
    var
      LFor: int64;
      LFrame: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LWord: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LCapture: int64;
      LDecl: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LIterator: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
      LBody: int64;
      LNext: int64;
      LExit: int64;
      LId: int64;
      LResult: int64;
      LSavedSlot: ref Int64List;
      LSavedByRef: BoolArray;
      LSavedByCopy: BoolArray;
      LCount: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LFor := self.FParallelNodes[AIndex];
      self.FFunction := self.FParallelEntries[AIndex];
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoStartManaged();
      self.FRoutine := 0;
      self.FResultSlot := 0;
      self.FSelfSlot := 0;
      self.FVarargsSlot := 0;
      self.FPackSlot := 0;
      LFrame := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Pointer, LFor);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LFrame).Imm := 0;
      LValue := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Int64, LFor);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LValue).Imm := 1;
      self.FWorkerIndex := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Int64, LFor);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FWorkerIndex).Imm := 2;
      self.FWorkerCount := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Int64, LFor);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FWorkerCount).Imm := 3;
      LWord := self.FTarget.PointerSize();
      LAt := 0;
      if self.FParallelSelves[AIndex] <> 0 then
        self.FSelfSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(LFor, LWord, self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
        self.DoStore(self.FSelfSlot, self.DoLoad(LFrame, IrType.Pointer, LFor), LFor);
        LAt := 1;
      end;
      LCount := self.FTree.CountOf(LFor, NodeRole.Capture);
      LSavedSlot := ref Int64List();
      setlength(LSavedByRef, LCount);
      setlength(LSavedByCopy, LCount);
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LCapture := self.FTree.NthOf(LFor, NodeRole.Capture, LI);
        LDecl := self.FTree[LCapture].ResolvedDecl;
        LSavedSlot.Add(self.FSlotOf[LDecl]);
        LSavedByRef[LI] := self.FByRef[LDecl];
        LSavedByCopy[LI] := self.FByCopy[LDecl];
        // one with no storage (a folded constant) is read as it always is
        if self.FSlotOf[LDecl] <> 0 then
          LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(LCapture, LWord, self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
          self.DoStore(LSlot, self.DoLoad(self.DoByteOffset(LFrame, (LAt + LI) * LWord, LCapture),
            IrType.Pointer, LCapture), LCapture);
          self.FSlotOf[LDecl] := LSlot;
          self.FByRef[LDecl] := true;
          self.FByCopy[LDecl] := false;
        end;
      end;
      LIterator := self.FTree.FirstOf(LFor, NodeRole.Iterator);
      LIr := self.DoTypeAt(self.FTree[LIterator].ResolvedType, LIterator);
      LSlot := self.DoSlot(LIterator, self.FTree[LIterator].ResolvedType, false);
      if (LIr <> IrType.Void) and (LSlot <> 0) then
        self.DoStore(LSlot, self.DoConvertIr(LValue, LIr, LFor), LFor);
        self.FBodyRoot := LFor;
        self.DoCodeTemporaries(LFor);
        self.FBodyRoot := 0;
        LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
        LNext := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
        LExit := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
        self.FExitOf[LFor] := LExit;
        self.FNextOf[LFor] := LNext;
        self.DoJumpTo(LBody, LFor);
        if self.DoArm(LBody, LFor, NodeRole.Statement) then
          self.DoJumpTo(LNext, LFor);
        end;
        // each result made before its return (a terminator ends its block)
        self.FBlock := LNext;
        self.DoReleaseManaged(LFor);
        LResult := self.DoConstant(IrType.Bool, 0, LFor);
        LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, LFor);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LResult);
        self.FBlock := LExit;
        self.DoReleaseManaged(LFor);
        LResult := self.DoConstant(IrType.Bool, 1, LFor);
        LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, LFor);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LResult);
        self.DoCleanupScopes(LFor, self.DoLastBlock());
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LDecl := self.FTree[self.FTree.NthOf(LFor, NodeRole.Capture, LI)].ResolvedDecl;
        self.FSlotOf[LDecl] := LSavedSlot[LI];
        self.FByRef[LDecl] := LSavedByRef[LI];
        self.FByCopy[LDecl] := LSavedByCopy[LI];
      end;
      self.FSelfSlot := 0;
      self.FWorkerIndex := 0;
      self.FWorkerCount := 0;
    end;

    // True when ARoot's child AChild is passed by the temporaries' walk (DoTemporaries): a
    // for parallel's body belongs to its own function (DoParallelBody), its bounds and W to
    // the routine's, and its iterator's slot is made by its body (T2); an async block's
    // body belongs to its task's entry (DoTaskBlockBody, T4). FBodyRoot is the loop or the
    // block whose body is being lowered
    hidden const method DoPassesTemporaries(const ARoot: int64; const AChild: int64): bool;
    var
      LRole: NodeRole;
    begin
      if self.FTree[ARoot].Kind = NodeKind.AsyncExpression then
        return (self.FTree.RoleOf(AChild) = NodeRole.Body) and (ARoot <> self.FBodyRoot);
      end;
      if (self.FTree[ARoot].Kind <> NodeKind.ForStatement) or
        (not self.FTree[ARoot].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Parallel)) then
        return false;
      end;
      LRole := self.FTree.RoleOf(AChild);
      if LRole = NodeRole.Statement then
        return ARoot <> self.FBodyRoot;
      end;
      if LRole = NodeRole.Iterator then
        return true;
      end;
      return ARoot = self.FBodyRoot;
    end;

    // True when AId is a var or const declaration among statements (BNF sec 5: a var block
    // in a statement list), not a routine's own (Local), a module's (Declaration) or a for
    // parallel's iterator
    hidden const method DoIsStatementLocal(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LRole: NodeRole;
    begin
      if (self.FTree[AId].Kind <> NodeKind.VarDecl) and (self.FTree[AId].Kind <> NodeKind.ConstDecl) then
        return false;
      end;
      LRole := self.FTree.RoleOf(AId);
      return (LRole <> NodeRole.Local) and (LRole <> NodeRole.Declaration) and
        (LRole <> NodeRole.Iterator);
    end;

    // The slot of the statement local AId (DoIsStatementLocal), made with the function's
    // temporaries (before any of its code runs: a managed one empty, an aggregate zeroed,
    // released at every exit) as a routine's own local's is (DoLocalSlot); a scalar
    // constant needs none (its uses are folded)
    hidden method DoStatementSlot(const AId: int64);
    var
      LType: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.VarDecl then
        self.DoLocalSlot(AId);
        return;
      end;
      LType := self.DoDeclType(AId);
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        self.DoAggregateLocalSlot(AId, LType);
      end;
    end;

    // The statement local AId (DoIsStatementLocal) where its declaration stands: what an
    // earlier pass left in its slot ended first (a loop's body runs it again: a managed
    // value released and its slot emptied, an aggregate's values released under its live
    // flag and its bytes zeroed), then its initializer stored or zero (DoLocalInit, an
    // aggregate constant's DoAggregateLocalInit); its initializer's temporaries end
    hidden method DoStatementLocal(const AId: int64);
    var
      LType: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      LSlot := self.FSlotOf[AId];
      if LSlot = 0 then
        // a refused one was reported at its declaration; a scalar constant is folded
        return;
      end;
      LType := self.DoDeclType(AId);
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        if self.DoHoldsManaged(LType) or self.DoHasLifetime(LType) then
          if not self.DoReleaseLive(LSlot, LType, self.FLiveOf[AId], false, AId) then
            return;
          end;
        end;
        self.DoFill(LSlot, TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType), AId);
      else
        if self.DoIsManaged(LType) then
          if not self.DoReleaseAt(LSlot, LType, AId) then
            return;
          end;
          self.DoStore(LSlot, self.DoConstant(IrType.Pointer, 0, AId), AId);
        end;
      end;
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.VarDecl then
        self.DoLocalInit(AId);
      else
        self.DoAggregateLocalInit(AId, LType);
      end;
      self.DoEndTemporaries(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Initializer));
    end;

    // A branch from the current block on `subject AOp bound` (the subject loaded from its
    // slot AAddress, of AIr; the bound ABound's folded value (SEM checked it: an integer, a
    // char's code, a choice's number) read at the subject type AType, as SEM orders the
    // labels), signed or unsigned as AIr is: to AOnTrue when it holds, else to AOnFalse
    hidden method DoMatchTest(const AOp: OperatorKind; const AAddress: int64; const ABound: int64;
      const AType: int64; const AIr: IrType; const AOnTrue: int64; const AOnFalse: int64);
    var
      LPredicate: IrPredicate;
      LSubject: int64;
      LBound: int64;
    begin
      if self.DoIsText(AType) then
        self.DoStringMatchTest(AAddress, ABound, AType, AOnTrue, AOnFalse);
        return;
      end;
      // =, <= and >= on an integer type always have a predicate
      if not self.DoPredicateOf(AOp, AIr, LPredicate) then
        return;
      end;
      LSubject := self.DoLoad(AAddress, AIr, ABound);
      LBound := self.DoConstant(AIr, self.DoConstBits(ABound, AType), ABound);
      self.DoBranchOn(self.DoCompareWith(LPredicate, LSubject, LBound, ABound), AOnTrue, AOnFalse,
        ABound);
    end;

    // A branch from the current block on a text match's label ABound (a string constant of
    // the subject type AType's width, BNF sec 5: compared exactly, no range): the subject's
    // text, held in the slot AAddress, against the label's block (DoManagedValue's: a
    // wstring label's units) by StrCompare / WStrCompare, to AOnTrue when they are equal,
    // else to AOnFalse
    hidden method DoStringMatchTest(const AAddress: int64; const ABound: int64; const AType: int64;
      const AOnTrue: int64; const AOnFalse: int64);
    var
      LSubject: int64;
      LLabel: int64;
      LOrder: int64;
    begin
      LSubject := self.DoLoad(AAddress, IrType.Pointer, ABound);
      LLabel := self.DoManagedValue(ABound);
      if LLabel = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LOrder := self.DoCallRuntime(self.DoTextRoutine(RuntimeRoutine.StrCompare, AType), LSubject,
        LLabel, ABound);
      if LOrder = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoBranchOn(self.DoCompareWith(IrPredicate.Equal, LOrder,
        self.DoConstant(IrType.Int32, 0, ABound), ABound), AOnTrue, AOnFalse, ABound);
    end;

    // A branch from the current block on the label ALabel of a match whose subject is in
    // the slot AAddress (of the canonical type AType, travelling as AIr): to AArm when the
    // subject is its value, or inside its range (low <= subject, then subject <= high in a
    // block of its own), else to ANext
    hidden method DoMatchLabel(const ALabel: int64; const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64;
      const AIr: IrType; const AArm: int64; const ANext: int64);
    var
      LInside: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree.CountOf(ALabel, NodeRole.HighBound) = 0 then
        self.DoMatchTest(OperatorKind.Equal, AAddress, self.FTree.FirstOf(ALabel, NodeRole.LowBound),
          AType, AIr, AArm, ANext);
        return;
      end;
      LInside := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoMatchTest(OperatorKind.GreaterEqual, AAddress,
        self.FTree.FirstOf(ALabel, NodeRole.LowBound), AType, AIr, LInside, ANext);
      self.FBlock := LInside;
      self.DoMatchTest(OperatorKind.LessEqual, AAddress,
        self.FTree.FirstOf(ALabel, NodeRole.HighBound), AType, AIr, AArm, ANext);
    end;

    // The match statement AId by PaskalCPP's contract (BNF sec 5; its emitter's
    // DoEmitMatch): the subject evaluated once into the match's own slot; then each arm's
    // labels tested in source order (DoMatchLabel; a string subject's by StrCompare,
    // DoStringMatchTest), the first that holds entering that
    // arm's statements, a label that does not going on to the next test; when none holds,
    // the else statements (none written: straight on). An arm or the else that falls
    // through goes to the exit, and so does a leave (FExitOf); a skip names its loop
    hidden method DoMatch(const AId: int64);
    var
      LSubject: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
      LValue: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LExit: int64;
      LArm: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LNext: int64;
      LTests: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LJ: int64;
    begin
      LSubject := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Subject);
      LType := self.DoUsedType(LSubject);
      if self.DoIsText(LType) then
        // a string subject's value (borrowed, or a temporary's) in a ptr slot: the labels
        // are all tested before any arm runs, so no arm can free it under a test
        LIr := IrType.Pointer;
        LValue := self.DoValue(LSubject);
        if LValue = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LAddress := self.DoSizedSlot(AId, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
      else
        LIr := self.DoTypeAt(LType, LSubject);
        if LIr = IrType.Void then
          return;
        end;
        LValue := self.DoValue(LSubject);
        if LValue = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        LAddress := self.DoSlot(AId, LType, false);
        if LAddress = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      self.DoStore(LAddress, LValue, AId);
      LExit := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.FExitOf[AId] := LExit;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AId, NodeRole.Arm) - 1 do
        LArm := self.FTree.NthOf(AId, NodeRole.Arm, LI);
        LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
        for LJ := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LArm, NodeRole.Label) - 1 do
          LNext := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
          self.DoMatchLabel(self.FTree.NthOf(LArm, NodeRole.Label, LJ), LAddress, LType, LIr,
            LBody, LNext);
          self.FBlock := LNext;
        end;
        // the arm's statements go in their own block; the tests go on where the last
        // label's test left off
        LTests := self.FBlock;
        if self.DoArm(LBody, LArm, NodeRole.Statement) then
          self.DoJumpTo(LExit, LArm);
        end;
        self.FBlock := LTests;
      end;
      if self.DoArm(self.FBlock, AId, NodeRole.Else) then
        self.DoJumpTo(LExit, AId);
      end;
      self.FBlock := LExit;
    end;

    // The leave or skip AId: a jump to the exit (leave) or the next block (skip) of the loop
    // or match its ResolvedJump names, through the cleanups of every protected region it
    // leaves (DoJumpOut); LW0001 when that statement got no blocks (one not lowered yet)
    hidden method DoLeaveSkip(const AId: int64);
    var
      LTarget: int64;
      LBlock: int64;
    begin
      LTarget := self.FTree[AId].ResolvedJump;
      if self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.LeaveStatement then
        LBlock := self.FExitOf[LTarget];
      else
        LBlock := self.FNextOf[LTarget];
      end;
      if LBlock = 0 then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId));
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoJumpOut(LBlock, LTarget, AId) then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoJumpTo(LBlock, AId);
    end;

    // The protected region ANode entered (a guard with a finally, before its body): jumps
    // out of it from here on wait for its pads (DoClosePads). Entering the outermost one
    // makes the slot a return's value waits in (FPadValueSlot, when the function gives a
    // value): made here, it is set before every return inside and read in every pad after
    hidden method DoEnterRegion(const ANode: int64);
    var
      LType: IrType;
    begin
      if self.FRegions.Count = 0 then
        self.FPadValueSlot := 0;
        LType := self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction).Signature.ResultType;
        if LType <> IrType.Void then
          self.FPadValueType := LType;
          self.FPadValueSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(ANode, ADAM_LOWERING_PAD_VALUE_BYTES,
            ADAM_LOWERING_PAD_VALUE_BYTES);
        end;
      end;
      self.FRegions.Add(ANode);
    end;

    // True when the protected region at ADepth of FRegions is left by a jump out of the loop
    // or match ALoop (0: a return, which leaves every region of its function): the region
    // lies inside ALoop
    hidden const method DoRegionLeft(const ADepth: int64; const ALoop: int64): bool;
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      if ALoop = 0 then
        return true;
      end;
      LAt := self.FTree.ParentOf(self.FRegions[ADepth]);
      while LAt <> 0 do
        if LAt = ALoop then
          return true;
        end;
        LAt := self.FTree.ParentOf(LAt);
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // True when a jump toward ATarget (a block, or ADAM_LOWERING_RETURN_PAD) out of the loop
    // or match ALoop (0: a return) leaves a protected region: then it is made as a jump
    // waiting on the innermost one (DoPadJump), at ANode. The regions are nested, so it
    // leaves one only when it leaves the innermost
    hidden method DoJumpOut(const ATarget: int64; const ALoop: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    begin
      if self.FRegions.Count = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      if not self.DoRegionLeft(self.FRegions.Count - 1, ALoop) then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoPadJump(ATarget, ALoop, ANode);
      return true;
    end;

    // A jump from the current block, at ANode, toward ATarget out of ALoop (DoJumpOut's),
    // its target left for the innermost region's pad (DoClosePads adds it)
    hidden method DoPadJump(const ATarget: int64; const ALoop: int64; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LJump: int64;
    begin
      LJump := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Jump, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FPadJumps.Add(LJump);
      self.FPadTargets.Add(ATarget);
      self.FPadLoops.Add(ALoop);
      self.FPadDepths.Add(self.FRegions.Count - 1);
    end;

    // True when the return at ANode keeps its value AValue for after the cleanups: it is
    // inside a protected region, so the value is stored in FPadValueSlot and the return is a
    // jump waiting on the region (DoPadJump); its tail is DoPadReturn's
    hidden method DoKeepReturn(const AValue: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    begin
      if self.FRegions.Count = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoStore(self.FPadValueSlot, AValue, ANode);
      self.DoPadJump(ADAM_LOWERING_RETURN_PAD, 0, ANode);
      return true;
    end;

    // The protected region ANode left (the innermost of FRegions, every block it covers
    // made): one pad block per target its waiting jumps go to, made now so that no scope of
    // ANode covers it (a raise in its cleanup never runs ANode's cleanup again); each pad
    // runs ANode's cleanup (DoRegionCleanup), then goes on to the next region's pad when the
    // jump leaves that one too (DoJumpOut), else to its target (a return's: DoPadReturn).
    // The current block comes back as it was
    hidden method DoClosePads(const ANode: int64);
    var
      LDepth: int64;
      LBlock: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LPad: int64;
      LTarget: int64;
      LLoop: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LJ: int64;
    begin
      LDepth := self.FRegions.Count - 1;
      self.FRegions.RemoveLast();
      LBlock := self.FBlock;
      // The jumps made by the pads (waiting on outer regions) come after LCount
      LCount := self.FPadJumps.Count;
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        if self.FPadDepths[LI] = LDepth then
          LTarget := self.FPadTargets[LI];
          LLoop := self.FPadLoops[LI];
          LPad := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
          // Every jump of this region toward the same target goes to the one pad
          for LJ := LI to LCount - 1 do
            if (self.FPadDepths[LJ] = LDepth) and (self.FPadTargets[LJ] = LTarget) then
              self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FPadJumps[LJ]).Targets.Add(LPad);
              self.FPadDepths.Put(LJ, -1);
            end;
          end;
          self.FBlock := LPad;
          self.DoRegionCleanup(ANode);
          if not self.DoEnded() then
            if not self.DoJumpOut(LTarget, LLoop, ANode) then
              if LTarget = ADAM_LOWERING_RETURN_PAD then
                self.DoPadReturn(ANode);
              else
                self.DoJumpTo(LTarget, ANode);
              end;
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      self.FBlock := LBlock;
    end;

    // The cleanup of the protected region ANode, lowered where the current block is: a
    // guard's finally statements; a lock's or a taken trylock's MutexLeave of the mutex
    // whose address DoLock kept (FSlotOf[ANode]: in a funclet, the parent's slot); a defer
    // statement's statement (DoDefer); a for in over a sequence's GeneratorAbort of the
    // block DoForInSequence kept (FSlotOf[ANode]: an unfinished generator aborted, nothing
    // for one that ended); a generator ramp's RefRelease of the block DoGeneratorRamp kept
    // (FSlotOf[ANode], G1c3: its end ends only the parts built)
    hidden method DoRegionCleanup(const ANode: int64);
    var
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[ANode].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Generator) then
        LAddress := self.DoLoad(self.FSlotOf[ANode], IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.RefRelease, LAddress, 0, ANode) = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[ANode].Kind = NodeKind.ForInStatement then
        LAddress := self.DoLoad(self.FSlotOf[ANode], IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.GeneratorAbort, LAddress, 0, ANode) = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[ANode].Kind = NodeKind.DeferStatement then
        self.DoStatements(ANode, NodeRole.Statement);
        return;
      end;
      if (self.FTree[ANode].Kind = NodeKind.LockStatement) or
        (self.FTree[ANode].Kind = NodeKind.TryLockStatement) then
        LAddress := self.DoLoad(self.FSlotOf[ANode], IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.MutexLeave, LAddress, 0, ANode) = 0 then
          return;
        end;
        return;
      end;
      self.DoStatements(ANode, NodeRole.Finally);
    end;

    // The lock / trylock statement AId (BNF sec 5): its mutex's address read once into a
    // slot (FSlotOf[AId]: the subject may name an element whose index the statements
    // change); lock: MutexEnter, trylock: MutexTryEnter with its wait (none: 0, one try),
    // then a branch to the statements when taken, else to the else statements (made before
    // the statements, so no scope of the region covers them). The statements are a
    // protected region (DoEnterRegion) whose cleanup is the MutexLeave (DoRegionCleanup):
    // where they fall through, in a block after them; on a return, leave or skip, in their
    // pads (DoClosePads); on an unwind, in a funclet (DoFinallyFunclet) the scope over their
    // blocks names. LW0001 inside a guard's finally (a funclet's funclet would reach two
    // frames), and with no frame handler
    hidden method DoLock(const AId: int64);
    var
      LFunction: ref IrFunction;
      LHandler: int64;
      LTry: bool;
      LAddress: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LLimit: int64;
      LWait: int64;
      LTaken: int64;
      LElse: int64;
      LBody: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LLast: int64;
      LBodyFalls: bool;
      LBodyEnd: int64;
      LRelease: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
      LFunclet: int64;
    begin
      LFunction := self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction);
      if LFunction.Parent <> 0 then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AId) + " inside a guard's finally");
        return;
      end;
      LHandler := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.FrameHandler, AId);
      if LHandler = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LTry := self.FTree[AId].Kind = NodeKind.TryLockStatement;
      LAddress := self.DoAddressFor(self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Subject), true);
      if LAddress = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(AId, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
      self.FSlotOf[AId] := LSlot;
      self.DoStore(LSlot, LAddress, AId);
      LElse := 0;
      if LTry then
        LLimit := self.FTree.FirstOf(AId, NodeRole.Limit);
        if LLimit <> 0 then
          LWait := self.DoValue(LLimit);
          if LWait = 0 then
            return;
          end;
        else
          LWait := self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, 0, AId);
        end;
        LTaken := self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.MutexTryEnter, LAddress, LWait, AId);
        if LTaken = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      else
        if self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.MutexEnter, LAddress, 0, AId) = 0 then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      // A jump out of the statements lets go of the mutex on its way (DoJumpOut)
      self.DoEnterRegion(AId);
      // The else block first: the statements' range starts at their own first block
      if LTry then
        LElse := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      end;
      LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      if LTry then
        self.DoBranchOn(LTaken, LBody, LElse, AId);
      else
        self.DoJumpTo(LBody, AId);
      end;
      // The statements' blocks run from their own first block to the last one they made
      self.FBlock := LBody;
      LFirst := LFunction.Blocks.Count - 1;
      self.DoStatements(AId, NodeRole.Statement);
      LLast := LFunction.Blocks.Count - 1;
      LBodyFalls := not self.DoEnded();
      LBodyEnd := self.FBlock;
      // Where the statements fall through: the let go, then the code after the statement
      LRelease := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      if LBodyFalls then
        self.FBlock := LBodyEnd;
        self.DoJumpTo(LRelease, AId);
      end;
      self.FBlock := LRelease;
      self.DoClosePads(AId);
      self.DoRegionCleanup(AId);
      LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, AId);
      if LTry then
        self.FBlock := LElse;
        self.DoStatements(AId, NodeRole.Else);
        if not self.DoEnded() then
          self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, AId);
        end;
      end;
      // Added after every scope inside the statements: the innermost comes first
      LFunclet := self.DoFinallyFunclet(AId);
      LFunction.AddScope(LFirst, LLast, LFunclet, -1);
      self.FModule.FrameHandler := LHandler;
      self.FBlock := LJoin;
    end;

    // A return's tail after its last pad, at ANode: the managed slots released, then the
    // value DoKeepReturn kept returned; with none (the function gives no value) its parts
    // ended and the return, as a return without a value does
    hidden method DoPadReturn(const ANode: int64);
    var
      LValue: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      if self.FPadValueSlot = 0 then
        self.DoReleaseManaged(ANode);
        self.DoExitParts(ANode);
        self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, ANode);
        return;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoLoad(self.FPadValueSlot, self.FPadValueType, ANode);
      self.DoReleaseManaged(ANode);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LValue);
    end;

    // The guard AId (BNF sec 5) with an except part, a finally part or both: its body in
    // blocks of its own, entered by a jump. An except part: its statements in blocks after
    // the body's, the target of a catching scope over the body's blocks (the platform unit's
    // filter, RuntimeRoutine.Catch: the runtime's raise or a hardware fault), so a raise in
    // the body unwinds the frames inside and the dispatcher resumes there, the part's first
    // call the runtime's FaultTaken (a fault the filter took becomes the raise in flight);
    // where the body falls through, a jump
    // past them. A finally part: its statements where the body (and the except part) fall
    // through, the same statements again as a funclet (DoFinallyFunclet) and a scope over
    // the body's and the except part's blocks naming it, added after the catching scope, so
    // an unwind leaving the guard runs them too and a raise the except part catches runs them
    // after it (the module's FrameHandler, the platform unit's, is the frame's handler); a
    // return, leave or skip out of the body or the except part runs them on its way (a
    // protected region: DoEnterRegion, its pads DoClosePads). A
    // guard with neither part, or with an empty finally and no except part, leaves the body
    // alone. LW0001 for a guard inside a finally (a funclet's funclet would reach two
    // frames), and with no frame handler or filter
    hidden method DoGuard(const AId: int64);
    var
      LFunction: ref IrFunction;
      LHandler: int64;
      LFilter: int64;
      LExcept: bool;
      LFinally: bool;
      LBody: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LLast: int64;
      LBodyFalls: bool;
      LBodyEnd: int64;
      LCatch: int64;
      LTarget: int64;
      LCovered: int64;
      LExceptFalls: bool;
      LExceptEnd: int64;
      LJoin: int64;
      LFunclet: int64;
      LTaken: int64;
    begin
      LExcept := self.FTree[AId].HasFlag(NodeFlag.ExceptPart);
      LFinally := self.FTree.CountOf(AId, NodeRole.Finally) > 0;
      if (not LExcept) and (not LFinally) then
        self.DoStatements(AId, NodeRole.Statement);
        return;
      end;
      LFunction := self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction);
      if LFunction.Parent <> 0 then
        self.DoRefuse(AId, "a guard inside a guard's finally");
        return;
      end;
      LHandler := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.FrameHandler, AId);
      if LHandler = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LFilter := 0;
      LTaken := 0;
      if LExcept then
        LFilter := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.Catch, AId);
        LTaken := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.FaultTaken, AId);
        if (LFilter = 0) or (LTaken = 0) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      // A jump out of the body or the except part runs the finally on its way (DoJumpOut)
      if LFinally then
        self.DoEnterRegion(AId);
      end;
      // The body's blocks run from its own first block to the last one it made
      LBody := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoJumpTo(LBody, AId);
      self.FBlock := LBody;
      LFirst := LFunction.Blocks.Count - 1;
      self.DoStatements(AId, NodeRole.Statement);
      LLast := LFunction.Blocks.Count - 1;
      LBodyFalls := not self.DoEnded();
      LBodyEnd := self.FBlock;
      LCovered := LLast;
      LExceptFalls := false;
      LExceptEnd := 0;
      LTarget := 0;
      if LExcept then
        // The except part's blocks follow the body's: no jump reaches its first one, the
        // dispatcher resumes there (the catching scope's target, a block index)
        LCatch := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
        LTarget := LFunction.Blocks.Count - 1;
        self.FBlock := LCatch;
        // a hardware fault the filter took becomes the raise in flight before the part's
        // first statement (the runtime's FaultTaken)
        self.DoCallPlain(LTaken, AId);
        self.DoStatements(AId, NodeRole.Except);
        LExceptFalls := not self.DoEnded();
        LExceptEnd := self.FBlock;
        LCovered := LFunction.Blocks.Count - 1;
      end;
      // Where the body and the except part fall through: the finally's statements inline, or
      // the code after the guard
      LJoin := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      if LBodyFalls then
        self.FBlock := LBodyEnd;
        self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, AId);
      end;
      if LExceptFalls then
        self.FBlock := LExceptEnd;
        self.DoJumpTo(LJoin, AId);
      end;
      self.FBlock := LJoin;
      // The pads of the jumps out of the body and the except part, after every block the
      // finally's scope covers
      if LFinally then
        self.DoClosePads(AId);
      end;
      // Added after every guard inside the body and the except part: the innermost scope
      // comes first, the catching scope before this guard's finally
      if LExcept then
        LFunction.AddScope(LFirst, LLast, LFilter, LTarget);
      end;
      if LFinally then
        self.DoStatements(AId, NodeRole.Finally);
        LFunclet := self.DoFinallyFunclet(AId);
        LFunction.AddScope(LFirst, LCovered, LFunclet, -1);
      end;
      self.FModule.FrameHandler := LHandler;
    end;

    // The cleanup of the protected region AId (DoRegionCleanup: a guard's finally
    // statements, a lock's MutexLeave) as a funclet of the current function (IR
    // Parent: it runs in this function's frame, reached through its frame parameter): an
    // internal function (uint8, ptr): void, its symbol the parent's and
    // ADAM_LOWERING_FINALLY_SYMBOL with its id, the statements lowered into it as they are
    // inline (a local, a parameter or self is the parent's slot), its own managed slots
    // released at its end. The parent's lowering state comes back as it was; returns the
    // funclet
    hidden method DoFinallyFunclet(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LParent: int64;
      LBlock: int64;
      LManaged: ref Int64List;
      LManagedType: ref Int64List;
      LManagedLive: ref Int64List;
      LExitBlocks: ref Int64List;
      LRegions: ref Int64List;
      LPadJumps: ref Int64List;
      LPadTargets: ref Int64List;
      LPadLoops: ref Int64List;
      LPadDepths: ref Int64List;
      LPadValueSlot: int64;
      LPadValueType: IrType;
      LFunclet: int64;
      LFunction: ref IrFunction;
      LFrame: int64;
    begin
      LParent := self.FFunction;
      LBlock := self.FBlock;
      LManaged := self.FManaged;
      LManagedType := self.FManagedType;
      LManagedLive := self.FManagedLive;
      LExitBlocks := self.FExitBlocks;
      LRegions := self.FRegions;
      LPadJumps := self.FPadJumps;
      LPadTargets := self.FPadTargets;
      LPadLoops := self.FPadLoops;
      LPadDepths := self.FPadDepths;
      LPadValueSlot := self.FPadValueSlot;
      LPadValueType := self.FPadValueType;
      // The id AddFunction hands out next, so the symbol is the function's own
      LFunclet := self.FModule.AddFunction(self.FModule.FunctionAt(LParent).Symbol +
        ADAM_LOWERING_FINALLY_SYMBOL + IntToStr(self.FModule.FunctionCount), IrType.Void, AId);
      LFunction := self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunclet);
      LFunction.Internal := true;
      self.FModule.SetParent(LFunclet, LParent);
      LFunction.Signature.AddParam(IrType.UInt8);
      LFunction.Signature.AddParam(IrType.Pointer);
      self.FFunction := LFunclet;
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(LFunclet);
      LFrame := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Pointer, AId);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LFrame).Imm := 1;
      LFunction.FrameValue := LFrame;
      self.DoStartManaged();
      self.DoRegionCleanup(AId);
      if not self.DoEnded() then
        self.DoReleaseManaged(AId);
        self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, AId);
      end;
      self.FFunction := LParent;
      self.FBlock := LBlock;
      self.FManaged := LManaged;
      self.FManagedType := LManagedType;
      self.FManagedLive := LManagedLive;
      self.FExitBlocks := LExitBlocks;
      self.FRegions := LRegions;
      self.FPadJumps := LPadJumps;
      self.FPadTargets := LPadTargets;
      self.FPadLoops := LPadLoops;
      self.FPadDepths := LPadDepths;
      self.FPadValueSlot := LPadValueSlot;
      self.FPadValueType := LPadValueType;
      return LFunclet;
    end;

    // A funclet of the current function (its frame parameter, as DoFinallyFunclet's) that
    // releases every slot of the function's FManaged, the last made first (DoReleaseAt on
    // the parent's slots), its symbol the parent's and ADAM_LOWERING_CLEANUP_SYMBOL; made at
    // ANode. The parent's lowering state comes back as it was; returns the funclet, 0 after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoCleanupFunclet(const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LParent: int64;
      LBlock: int64;
      LFunclet: int64;
      LFunction: ref IrFunction;
      LFrame: int64;
      LDone: bool;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LParent := self.FFunction;
      LBlock := self.FBlock;
      LFunclet := self.FModule.AddFunction(self.FModule.FunctionAt(LParent).Symbol +
        ADAM_LOWERING_CLEANUP_SYMBOL, IrType.Void, ANode);
      LFunction := self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunclet);
      LFunction.Internal := true;
      self.FModule.SetParent(LFunclet, LParent);
      LFunction.Signature.AddParam(IrType.UInt8);
      LFunction.Signature.AddParam(IrType.Pointer);
      self.FFunction := LFunclet;
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(LFunclet);
      LFrame := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LFrame).Imm := 1;
      LFunction.FrameValue := LFrame;
      LDone := true;
      for LI := self.FManaged.Count - 1 downto 0 do
        if LDone and (not self.DoReleaseLive(self.FManaged[LI], self.FManagedType[LI],
          self.FManagedLive[LI], false, ANode)) then
          LDone := false;
        end;
      end;
      if LDone then
        self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, ANode);
      end;
      self.FFunction := LParent;
      self.FBlock := LBlock;
      if not LDone then
        return 0;
      end;
      return LFunclet;
    end;

    // The position of the current function's last block (in its Blocks)
    hidden const method DoLastBlock(): int64;
    begin
      return self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction).Blocks.Count - 1;
    end;

    // The current function's cleanup (DoCleansUp; after its whole body is lowered, ANode
    // its node, before any catching scope): its funclet (DoCleanupFunclet) the handler of
    // one scope per run of its blocks that are no exit block (FExitBlocks: a block's own
    // release is never run again by an unwind), positions 0 up to ALast; added after its
    // guards' scopes (the outermost); the module's FrameHandler the platform unit's
    hidden method DoCleanupScopes(const ANode: int64; const ALast: int64);
    var
      LFunction: ref IrFunction;
      LHandler: int64;
      LFunclet: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoCleansUp() then
        return;
      end;
      LHandler := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.FrameHandler, ANode);
      if LHandler = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LFunclet := self.DoCleanupFunclet(ANode);
      if LFunclet = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LFunction := self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction);
      LFirst := -1;
      for LAt := 0 to ALast do
        if self.FExitBlocks.IndexOf(LAt) >= 0 then
          if LFirst >= 0 then
            LFunction.AddScope(LFirst, LAt - 1, LFunclet, -1);
            LFirst := -1;
          end;
        else
          if LFirst < 0 then
            LFirst := LAt;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      if LFirst >= 0 then
        LFunction.AddScope(LFirst, ALast, LFunclet, -1);
      end;
      self.FModule.FrameHandler := LHandler;
    end;

    // ARoutine's parameters, each stored in its slot at entry (a reference one's address,
    // an aggregate in a register its bytes); a hidden result pointer first, kept in
    // FResultSlot (0 when ARoutine has none), then a method's self, kept in FSelfSlot (0
    // for a routine), a generator method's holder in FHolderSlot (DoGeneratorMethod), the
    // real parameters after them; a cpplink variadic's pack header
    // last, kept in FPackSlot (DoPackParam)
    hidden method DoParams(const ARoutine: int64);
    var
      LSignature: ref IrSignature;
      LParam: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LLast: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LSignature := self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction).Signature;
      self.FResultSlot := 0;
      LLast := LSignature.ParamCount - 1;
      if self.DoIsPackVariadic(ARoutine) then
        LLast := LLast - 1;
      end;
      LFirst := 0;
      if self.FHiddenResult[ARoutine] then
        LValue := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Pointer, ARoutine);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LValue).Imm := 0;
        self.FResultSlot := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Slot, IrType.Pointer, ARoutine);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FResultSlot).Imm := self.FTarget.PointerSize();
        self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FResultSlot).Align := self.FTarget.PointerAlign();
        self.DoStore(self.FResultSlot, LValue, ARoutine);
        LFirst := 1;
      end;
      self.FSelfSlot := 0;
      if self.DoHasSelf(ARoutine) then
        LValue := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Pointer, ARoutine);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LValue).Imm := LFirst;
        self.FSelfSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(ARoutine, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
        self.DoStore(self.FSelfSlot, LValue, ARoutine);
        LFirst := LFirst + 1;
      end;
      self.FHolderSlot := 0;
      if self.DoGeneratorMethod(ARoutine) then
        LValue := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Pointer, ARoutine);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LValue).Imm := LFirst;
        self.FHolderSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(ARoutine, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
        self.DoStore(self.FHolderSlot, LValue, ARoutine);
        LFirst := LFirst + 1;
      end;
      for LI := LFirst to LLast do
        LParam := self.DoParamAt(ARoutine, LI - LFirst);
        LValue := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, LSignature.ParamTypes[LI], LParam);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LValue).Imm := LI;
        LSlot := self.DoSlot(LParam, self.DoDeclType(LParam), self.FByRef[LParam]);
        if LSlot <> 0 then
          self.DoStore(LSlot, LValue, LParam);
          self.DoOwnParam(LParam, LSlot, LValue);
        end;
      end;
      self.DoPackParam(ARoutine);
      self.DoVarargsCursor(ARoutine);
    end;

    // The parameter AParam (its slot ASlot, its incoming value AValue) made the routine's
    // own when it is a value that holds texts (C++ copies a value parameter): a text or a
    // dynamic array by value gets a holder (StrAddRef), its slot one of FManaged (released
    // by its type); an aggregate holding them passed by copy (its caller's address,
    // DoArgument) is copied into a zeroed slot of its own (DoAggregateCopy), one of
    // FManaged, and the parameter's slot then holds that copy's address. A const one by
    // value is borrowed (SU2.8 e3): the routine never writes it, and its caller keeps a
    // holder for the whole call (DoArgument: an argument a callee could drop is held by the
    // call's own hold), so it gets no holder and no release here. A value object whose
    // type runs code where it is copied or ended (DoHasLifetime) arrives as the caller's
    // copy made for the call, or a call's result moved (DoOwnArgument): by value it is the
    // routine's to end, live from the entry, one of FManaged (by copy its bytes moved into
    // a slot of its own, which the parameter's slot then points at: an exit's cleanup
    // reaches the frame's slots, never the incoming address; in a register its slot); a
    // const one binds the caller's value (BNF sec 4 O5: no copy), never ended here
    hidden method DoOwnParam(const AParam: int64; const ASlot: int64; const AValue: int64);
    var
      LType: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LOwn: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoDeclType(AParam);
      if self.DoIsManaged(LType) and (not self.FByRef[AParam]) then
        if self.FTree[AParam].HasFlag(NodeFlag.ConstParam) then
          return;
        end;
        self.DoAddHolder(AValue, LType, AParam);
        self.DoAddManaged(ASlot, LType, AParam);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) and self.DoHasLifetime(LType) then
        if self.FTree[AParam].HasFlag(NodeFlag.ConstParam) or
          (self.FByRef[AParam] and not self.FByCopy[AParam]) then
          return;
        end;
        LOwn := ASlot;
        if self.FByCopy[AParam] then
          LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType);
          LOwn := self.DoSizedSlot(AParam, LSize, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType));
          self.DoCopyBytes(LOwn, AValue, LSize, AParam);
          self.DoStore(ASlot, LOwn, AParam);
        end;
        if self.DoAddManaged(LOwn, LType, AParam) then
          self.DoSetLive(AParam, true, AParam);
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if (not self.FByCopy[AParam]) or (not self.DoHoldsManaged(LType)) then
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoManagedMapData(LType, AParam) = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType);
      LOwn := self.DoSizedSlot(AParam, LSize, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType));
      self.DoFill(LOwn, LSize, AParam);
      self.DoAggregateCopy(LOwn, AValue, LType, AParam);
      self.DoAddManaged(LOwn, LType, AParam);
      self.DoStore(ASlot, LOwn, AParam);
    end;

    // A cpplink variadic ARoutine's pack (FPackSlot, 0 for any other routine): a ptr slot
    // holding its last parameter, the address of the header its caller built
    hidden method DoPackParam(const ARoutine: int64);
    var
      LSignature: ref IrSignature;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      self.FPackSlot := 0;
      if not self.DoIsPackVariadic(ARoutine) then
        return;
      end;
      LSignature := self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction).Signature;
      LValue := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Parameter, IrType.Pointer, ARoutine);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LValue).Imm := LSignature.ParamCount - 1;
      self.FPackSlot := self.DoSizedSlot(ARoutine, self.FTarget.PointerSize(), self.FTarget.PointerAlign());
      self.DoStore(self.FPackSlot, LValue, ARoutine);
    end;

    // A variadic ARoutine's varargs cursor (FVarargsSlot, 0 for any other routine): a ptr
    // slot holding the address of its first variadic argument (varargsstart)
    hidden method DoVarargsCursor(const ARoutine: int64);
    var
      LStart: int64;
    begin
      self.FVarargsSlot := 0;
      if not self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction).Signature.Variadic then
        return;
      end;
      LStart := self.DoEmit(IrOp.VarargsStart, IrType.Pointer, ARoutine);
      self.FVarargsSlot := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Slot, IrType.Pointer, ARoutine);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FVarargsSlot).Imm := self.FTarget.PointerSize();
      self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FVarargsSlot).Align := self.FTarget.PointerAlign();
      self.DoStore(self.FVarargsSlot, LStart, ARoutine);
    end;

    // The aggregate local ALocal's slot of the type AType (DoIsAggregate; DoLocals' first
    // pass): of the type's size and alignment, zeroed (BNF sec 4 for a record or an overlay;
    // every variable without an initializer starts zeroed here; one holding texts is one of
    // FManaged); FSlotOf stays 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoAggregateLocalSlot(const ALocal: int64; const AType: int64);
    var
      LSlot: int64;
      LSize: int64;
    begin
      LSlot := self.DoSlot(ALocal, AType, false);
      if LSlot = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType);
      self.DoFill(LSlot, LSize, ALocal);
      // one that holds managed values, ends by a done or copies by a copy decl is ended /
      // released at every exit of the routine, the last declared first (DoReleaseAt),
      // under its live flag (DoLiveFlag: it moves)
      if (self.DoHoldsManaged(AType) or self.DoHasLifetime(AType)) and
        (not self.DoAddManaged(LSlot, AType, ALocal)) then
        self.FSlotOf[ALocal] := 0;
      end;
    end;

    // The aggregate local ALocal of the type AType (its slot made: DoAggregateLocalSlot):
    // its initializer's value copied in when it has one (DoAggregateSource,
    // DoAggregateCopy; a value object whose type runs code where it is copied or ended
    // moved in from a call's result, DoMoveObject, any other value copied by its type's
    // copy, DoCopyValue), else an object built; live from then on (DoSetLive)
    hidden method DoAggregateLocalInit(const ALocal: int64; const AType: int64);
    var
      LSlot: int64;
      LInit: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LFrom: int64;
    begin
      LSlot := self.FSlotOf[ALocal];
      LInit := self.FTree.FirstOf(ALocal, NodeRole.Initializer);
      if LInit = 0 then
        // an object built by its init (SEM's pick, the local's ResolvedCallee, with its
        // arguments) or by its parts' (DoBuildObject)
        if self.DoNeedsBuild(AType) or (self.FTree[ALocal].ResolvedCallee <> 0) then
          self.DoBuildObject(LSlot, AType, self.FTree[ALocal].ResolvedCallee, ALocal,
            NodeRole.ConstructorArgument, ALocal);
        end;
        // built: from here its exits end it (its live flag)
        self.DoSetLive(ALocal, true, ALocal);
        return;
      end;
      // a value object that runs code where it is copied or ended takes a call's result
      // (pcpp's truth: moved, ended once, by the local), any other value by its copy
      LFrom := 0;
      if self.DoHasLifetime(AType) then
        LFrom := self.DoMoveSource(LInit);
        if (LFrom <> 0) and not self.DoIsCallSite(LFrom) then
          LFrom := 0;
        end;
      end;
      LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(LInit);
      if LSource = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      if LFrom <> 0 then
        self.DoMoveObject(LSlot, LSource, LFrom, AType, ALocal);
        self.DoSetLive(ALocal, true, ALocal);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoHasLifetime(AType) then
        if self.DoCopyValue(LSlot, LSource, AType, ALocal) then
          self.DoSetLive(ALocal, true, ALocal);
        end;
        return;
      end;
      self.DoAggregateCopy(LSlot, LSource, AType, ALocal);
    end;

    // True when the local variable ALocal has init arguments while its type is no object
    // (SEM gives them to nothing else: DoLocalSlot reports it, LW0001)
    hidden const method DoIsBadConstruct(const ALocal: int64; const AType: int64): bool;
    begin
      return (self.FTree.CountOf(ALocal, NodeRole.ConstructorArgument) > 0) and
        (ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) <> TypeClass.ObjectType);
    end;

    // The local variable ALocal's slot (DoLocalSlotOf); none made for one that needs one
    // (any but a varargs pack) is a refusal reported there: FSlotRefused keeps its uses
    // from reporting it again
    hidden method DoLocalSlot(const ALocal: int64);
    begin
      self.DoLocalSlotOf(ALocal);
      if (self.FSlotOf[ALocal] = 0) and (ClassOf(self.FTree, self.DoDeclType(ALocal)) <> TypeClass.Varargs) then
        self.FSlotRefused[ALocal] := true;
      end;
    end;

    // The local variable ALocal's slot (DoLocals' first pass, before any local's
    // initializer runs: a raise in one finds every managed slot empty, which the function's
    // cleanup releases as it unwinds): an aggregate's zeroed (DoAggregateLocalSlot), a
    // managed one's empty (DoManagedLocalSlot), a scalar's; a varargs pack's is its own
    // (DoPackLocal, in the second pass); none after LW0001
    hidden method DoLocalSlotOf(const ALocal: int64);
    var
      LType: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoDeclType(ALocal);
      if self.DoIsBadConstruct(ALocal, LType) then
        self.DoRefuse(ALocal, "a constructed " + self.FTree.ConstructText(ALocal));
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        self.DoAggregateLocalSlot(ALocal, LType);
        return;
      end;
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, LType) = TypeClass.Varargs then
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsManaged(LType) then
        self.DoManagedLocalSlot(ALocal, LType);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoTypeAt(LType, ALocal) = IrType.Void then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoSlot(ALocal, LType, false);
    end;

    // The local variable ALocal in its slot (DoLocalSlot made it; none after LW0001),
    // holding its initializer's value, else zero (an aggregate local: DoAggregateLocalInit,
    // a managed one: DoManagedLocalInit); a varargs pack made (DoPackLocal)
    hidden method DoLocalInit(const ALocal: int64);
    var
      LType: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
      LSlot: int64;
      LInit: int64;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoDeclType(ALocal);
      if self.DoIsBadConstruct(ALocal, LType) then
        return;
      end;
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, LType) = TypeClass.Varargs then
        self.DoPackLocal(ALocal);
        return;
      end;
      LSlot := self.FSlotOf[ALocal];
      if LSlot = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        self.DoAggregateLocalInit(ALocal, LType);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsManaged(LType) then
        self.DoManagedLocalInit(ALocal, LType);
        return;
      end;
      LIr := self.DoTypeAt(LType, ALocal);
      LInit := self.FTree.FirstOf(ALocal, NodeRole.Initializer);
      if LInit = 0 then
        LValue := self.DoConstant(LIr, 0, ALocal);
      else
        LValue := self.DoValue(LInit);
      end;
      if LValue <> 0 then
        self.DoStore(LSlot, LValue, ALocal);
      end;
    end;

    // ARoutine's locals: variables get their slots; an aggregate constant gets one too,
    // filled as a variable's (DoAggregateLocalSlot / Init; SEM keeps it unwritten); a scalar
    // constant needs none (its uses are folded); a local type needs none either (its
    // TypeInfo and member functions are made with the module's: DoLocalTypes); anything
    // else (a nested routine) is LW0001. Two passes in declaration order: every slot first (DoLocalSlot:
    // each managed one empty before anything can raise, an init's parts included), then
    // the initializers (DoLocalInits)
    hidden method DoLocalSlots(const ARoutine: int64);
    var
      LLocal: int64;
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LType: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Local) - 1 do
        LLocal := self.FTree.NthOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Local, LI);
        LKind := self.FTree[LLocal].Kind;
        if LKind = NodeKind.VarDecl then
          self.DoLocalSlot(LLocal);
        else
          if LKind = NodeKind.ConstDecl then
            LType := self.DoDeclType(LLocal);
            if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
              self.DoAggregateLocalSlot(LLocal, LType);
            end;
          else
            if LKind <> NodeKind.TypeDecl then
              self.DoRefuse(LLocal, "a local " + self.FTree.ConstructText(LLocal));
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // ARoutine's locals' initializers (their slots made: DoLocalSlots), in declaration order
    hidden method DoLocalInits(const ARoutine: int64);
    var
      LLocal: int64;
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LType: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Local) - 1 do
        LLocal := self.FTree.NthOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Local, LI);
        LKind := self.FTree[LLocal].Kind;
        if LKind = NodeKind.VarDecl then
          self.DoLocalInit(LLocal);
          // each initializer is a full expression: its temporaries end once it is stored
          self.DoEndTemporaries(self.FTree.FirstOf(LLocal, NodeRole.Initializer));
        else
          if LKind = NodeKind.ConstDecl then
            LType := self.DoDeclType(LLocal);
            if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) and (self.FSlotOf[LLocal] <> 0) then
              self.DoAggregateLocalInit(LLocal, LType);
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // An init's object parts built before its body runs (DoBuildParts on self: the parent
    // part, then the object fields; BNF sec 4, D3), a copy's made (DoEnterCopy), then its
    // object's vptr set to its own level's vtable; a done's vptr set to its own level's at
    // its entry (DoSetVptr: the body's virtual calls reach this level's methods, never a
    // descendant's that is not built yet or already ended, as in C++); nothing for any
    // other routine
    hidden method DoEnterParts(const ANode: int64);
    var
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LOwner: int64;
      LSelf: int64;
    begin
      LKind := self.FTree[self.FRoutine].Kind;
      if (LKind <> NodeKind.InitDecl) and (LKind <> NodeKind.DoneDecl) and (LKind <> NodeKind.CopyDecl) then
        return;
      end;
      LOwner := self.DoOwnerType(self.FRoutine);
      LSelf := self.DoLoad(self.FSelfSlot, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      if LKind = NodeKind.InitDecl then
        if not self.DoBuildParts(LSelf, LOwner, self.FRoutine, ANode) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.CopyDecl then
        if not self.DoEnterCopy(LSelf, LOwner, ANode) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      self.DoSetVptr(LSelf, LOwner, ANode);
    end;

    // A copy's object parts made before its body runs, at ANode, in the empty object at
    // ASelf of the canonical type AType (BNF sec 4 O5: it builds the copy as an init
    // builds an object): the parent part copied from its source's parent part by the
    // parent's own copy (DoCopyValue: as plain data for a parent that holds none), then
    // the fields built as an init builds them (DoBuildFields: they start empty, the body
    // fills them); false after LW0001
    hidden method DoEnterCopy(const ASelf: int64; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LParam: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LParent: int64;
    begin
      LParam := self.FTree.NthOf(self.FRoutine, NodeRole.Param, 0);
      LSource := self.FSlotOf[LParam];
      if LSource = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      if self.FByRef[LParam] then
        LSource := self.DoLoad(LSource, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      end;
      LParent := ParentTypeOf(self.FTree, AType);
      if LParent <> 0 then
        if not self.DoCopyValue(self.DoUpcast(ASelf, AType, LParent, ANode),
          self.DoUpcast(LSource, AType, LParent, ANode), LParent, ANode) then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      return self.DoBuildFields(ASelf, AType, self.FRoutine, ANode);
    end;

    // A done's object parts ended at one of its exits, after its locals are released
    // (DoEndParts on self: the fields from the last, then the parent part); nothing for
    // any other routine
    hidden method DoExitParts(const ANode: int64);
    begin
      if (self.FRoutine = 0) or (self.FTree[self.FRoutine].Kind <> NodeKind.DoneDecl) then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoEndParts(self.DoLoad(self.FSelfSlot, IrType.Pointer, ANode), self.DoOwnerType(self.FRoutine),
        ANode);
    end;

    // The body of ARoutine (given its function): parameters, an init's parts
    // (DoEnterParts), locals, statements, and the return at its end when the last block
    // has none (a result routine's end is unreachable, SM0612: it returns zero; a done's
    // parts ended before it, DoExitParts)
    hidden method DoBody(const ARoutine: int64);
    var
      LResult: IrType;
      LBody: int64;
      LZero: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      self.FFunction := self.FFunctionOf[ARoutine];
      self.FRoutine := ARoutine;
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LResult := self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction).Signature.ResultType;
      self.DoStartManaged();
      self.DoParams(ARoutine);
      // a bound accessor (of a dispatched property) has no body: its code is the field's
      if self.DoIsAccessor(ARoutine) and self.DoIsBound(ARoutine) then
        self.DoBoundAccessor(ARoutine);
        self.FRoutine := 0;
        return;
      end;
      // a generator's function is its ramp; its body runs on a coroutine of its own (G1)
      if self.FTree[ARoutine].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Generator) then
        self.DoGeneratorRamp(ARoutine);
        self.FRoutine := 0;
        return;
      end;
      // The string temporaries' slots are made before any code that may use them (a
      // local's initializer included) and before the first branch
      self.DoCodeTemporaries(ARoutine);
      self.DoLocalSlots(ARoutine);
      self.DoEnterParts(ARoutine);
      self.DoLocalInits(ARoutine);
      LBody := self.FTree.FirstOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Body);
      self.DoStatements(LBody, NodeRole.Statement);
      if self.DoEnded() then
        self.FRoutine := 0;
        return;
      end;
      self.DoReleaseManaged(LBody);
      self.DoExitParts(LBody);
      self.FRoutine := 0;
      if LResult = IrType.Void then
        self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, LBody);
        return;
      end;
      // A hidden result routine hands back the caller's slot (its bytes stay as they are)
      if self.FResultSlot <> 0 then
        LZero := self.DoLoad(self.FResultSlot, IrType.Pointer, LBody);
      else
        LZero := self.DoConstant(LResult, 0, LBody);
      end;
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, LBody);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LZero);
    end;

    // True when the method AMethod dispatches (virtual, override or abstract: BNF sec 4,
    // D7; final only closes one of them, SM0336): its calls go through its object's
    // vtable (DoDispatchCall), its slot Layout's ResolvedSlot
    hidden const method DoIsDispatched(const AMethod: int64): bool;
    begin
      return self.FTree[AMethod].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Virtual) or self.FTree[AMethod].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Override) or
        self.FTree[AMethod].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Abstract);
    end;

    // The code of the bound accessor AAccessor of a dispatched property (DoBody made its
    // parameters: self in FSelfSlot, a write's value in its property's slot, DoParamAt):
    // its field reached from self (the declaring level's part, which a call through the
    // vtable upcasts to), then read or written as the field itself is (DoBoundRead,
    // DoBoundWrite; a bitfield through its lane: DoFieldBitRead / DoFieldBitWrite), the
    // routine's managed slots released, and its return
    hidden method DoBoundAccessor(const AAccessor: int64);
    var
      LProperty: int64;
      LField: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LSelf: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LProperty := self.FTree.ParentOf(AAccessor);
      LField := self.FTree[AAccessor].ResolvedDecl;
      LType := self.DoDeclType(LProperty);
      LSelf := self.DoLoad(self.FSelfSlot, IrType.Pointer, AAccessor);
      LAddress := self.DoByteOffset(LSelf, self.DoMemberOffset(self.DoOwnerType(AAccessor), LField), AAccessor);
      if self.FTree[AAccessor].Kind = NodeKind.PropertyWrite then
        if self.FTree[LField].ResolvedBitWidth >= 0 then
          // the value parameter is the property's slot (DoParamAt), a scalar
          if self.FSlotOf[LProperty] = 0 then
            return;
          end;
          LIr := self.DoTypeAt(LType, AAccessor);
          if LIr = IrType.Void then
            return;
          end;
          self.DoFieldBitWrite(LField, LAddress, self.DoLoad(self.FSlotOf[LProperty], LIr, AAccessor), AAccessor);
        else
          if not self.DoBoundWrite(LProperty, LAddress, LType, AAccessor) then
            return;
          end;
        end;
        self.DoReleaseManaged(AAccessor);
        self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, AAccessor);
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[LField].ResolvedBitWidth >= 0 then
        LValue := self.DoFieldBitRead(LField, LAddress, AAccessor);
      else
        LValue := self.DoBoundRead(LAddress, LType, AAccessor);
      end;
      if LValue = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoReleaseManaged(AAccessor);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, AAccessor);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(LValue);
    end;

    // The value a bound read accessor gives back from its field at AAddress (of the
    // canonical type AType), as DoReturn gives a value back: a text, a dynamic array or a
    // ref with one more holder (StrAddRef: the caller holds it); an aggregate copied to
    // the caller's hidden result (FResultSlot) and that address, or its bytes as the
    // register's integer (DoAggregateIr); any other value loaded at its type; 0 after
    // LW0001
    hidden method DoBoundRead(const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LValue: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
    begin
      if self.DoIsAggregate(AType) then
        if self.FResultSlot <> 0 then
          LValue := self.DoLoad(self.FResultSlot, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
          // the caller's slot is empty (a temporary): the field's value is copied in
          if not self.DoCopyValue(LValue, AAddress, AType, ANode) then
            return 0;
          end;
          return LValue;
        end;
        return self.DoLoad(AAddress, self.DoAggregateIr(AType), ANode);
      end;
      if self.DoIsManaged(AType) then
        LValue := self.DoLoad(AAddress, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        if self.DoAddHolder(LValue, AType, ANode) = 0 then
          return 0;
        end;
        return LValue;
      end;
      LIr := self.DoTypeAt(AType, ANode);
      if LIr = IrType.Void then
        return 0;
      end;
      return self.DoLoad(AAddress, LIr, ANode);
    end;

    // The value of a bound write accessor (its property AProperty stands for that
    // parameter, DoParamAt) stored into its field at AAddress (of the canonical type
    // AType): a managed one as an assignment stores it (DoStoreManaged: a holder added,
    // the old one released); an aggregate copied (DoAggregateCopy) from the caller's copy
    // (by copy: its slot holds the address) or from its own slot (its bytes came in a
    // register); any other value stored at its type; false after LW0001
    hidden method DoBoundWrite(const AProperty: int64; const AAddress: int64; const AType: int64;
      const ANode: int64): bool;
    var
      LSlot: int64;
      LSource: int64;
      LIr: IrType;
    begin
      LSlot := self.FSlotOf[AProperty];
      if LSlot = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(AType) then
        LSource := LSlot;
        if self.FByRef[AProperty] then
          LSource := self.DoLoad(LSlot, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
        end;
        self.DoAggregateCopy(AAddress, LSource, AType, ANode);
        return true;
      end;
      if self.DoIsManaged(AType) then
        return self.DoStoreManaged(AAddress, self.DoLoad(LSlot, IrType.Pointer, ANode), AType, ANode) <> 0;
      end;
      LIr := self.DoTypeAt(AType, ANode);
      if LIr = IrType.Void then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoStore(AAddress, self.DoLoad(LSlot, LIr, ANode), ANode);
      return true;
    end;

    // Every node under AId (a type declaration) that has a body: a method (plain or
    // dispatched: a vtable slot holds its function), an init, a done and a property
    // accessor and a copy get their functions (DoRegister: self first, DoHasSelf), their
    // bodies lowered with the routines'; so does a bound accessor of a dispatched property
    // (its vtable slot needs a function: DoBoundAccessor makes its code from the field);
    // so does an operator (no self: its operands are its parameters)
    hidden method DoTypeBodies(const AId: int64);
    var
      LChild: int64;
      LKind: NodeKind;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.ChildCount(AId) - 1 do
        LChild := self.FTree.ChildAt(AId, LI);
        LKind := self.FTree[LChild].Kind;
        if self.FTree.FirstOf(LChild, NodeRole.Body) <> 0 then
          if (LKind = NodeKind.MethodDecl) or (LKind = NodeKind.InitDecl) or (LKind = NodeKind.DoneDecl) or
            (LKind = NodeKind.CopyDecl) or (LKind = NodeKind.OperatorDecl) or self.DoIsAccessor(LChild) then
            self.DoRegister(LChild);
          else
            self.DoRefuse(LChild, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(LChild));
          end;
        else
          if self.DoIsAccessor(LChild) and self.DoIsBound(LChild) and
            self.DoIsDispatched(self.FTree.ParentOf(LChild)) then
            self.DoRegister(LChild);
          else
            self.DoTypeBodies(LChild);
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The folded value AValue of the bitfield AField or-ed into its lane at ALane in ABytes
    // (the lane the field type's size; the value moved to the field's bit and masked to its
    // width: the bits a run-time DoBitWrite leaves); false when AValue did not fold
    hidden method DoConstLane(const AValue: int64; const AField: int64; var ABytes: ByteArray;
      const ALane: int64): bool;
    var
      LSize: int64;
      LBit: int64;
      LMask: uint64;
      LPart: uint64;
      LLane: uint64;
    begin
      if not self.DoIsFolded(AValue) then
        return false;
      end;
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, self.DoDeclType(AField));
      LBit := int64(self.FTree[AField].ResolvedBitOffset);
      LMask := uint64(BitMask(int64(self.FTree[AField].ResolvedBitWidth), LBit));
      LPart := uint64(self.DoConstBits(AValue, self.FTree[AValue].ResolvedType));
      LPart := (LPart shl uint64(LBit)) & LMask;
      LLane := GetLe(ABytes, ALane, LSize);
      LLane := (LLane & (~LMask)) | LPart;
      PutLe(ABytes, ALane, LLane, LSize);
      return true;
    end;

    // The constant value AExpr of the type AType written into ABytes at AOffset: a folded
    // scalar's bits little-endian at the type's size (DoConstBits), a record literal's field
    // inits each at its field's offset (a bitfield into its lane: DoConstLane; a nested
    // literal the same way), a field it does not name left as the bytes were (zero), a
    // static array's array literal each element at its index times the element's size (a
    // dynamic array's is a block made at run time), through parentheses; with ATexts a
    // managed value too (DoConstText: a literal's block address as a word in AWords, nil as
    // zero); false when any part did not fold (the value is then built at run time)
    hidden method DoConstBytes(const AExpr: int64; const AType: int64; var ABytes: ByteArray;
      const AOffset: int64; const ATexts: bool; var AWords: Int64Array): bool;
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LRecord: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LInit: int64;
      LField: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LOffset: int64;
      LElement: int64;
      LStride: int64;
      LItem: int64;
    begin
      LAt := AExpr;
      while self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.ParenExpression do
        LAt := self.FTree.FirstOf(LAt, NodeRole.Operand);
      end;
      if self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.SetLiteral then
        return self.DoSetBytes(LAt, AType, ABytes, AOffset, false);
      end;
      if self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.ArrayLiteral then
        if ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) <> TypeClass.StaticArray then
          return false;
        end;
        LElement := TargetOf(self.FTree, AType);
        LStride := self.DoElementSize(AType);
        for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LAt, NodeRole.Element) - 1 do
          LItem := self.FTree.NthOf(LAt, NodeRole.Element, LI);
          if not self.DoConstBytes(self.FTree.FirstOf(LItem, NodeRole.LowBound), LElement, ABytes,
            AOffset + LI * LStride, ATexts, AWords) then
            return false;
          end;
        end;
        return true;
      end;
      if self.FTree[LAt].Kind = NodeKind.RecordLiteral then
        LRecord := self.FTree[LAt].ResolvedType;
        for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LAt, NodeRole.Argument) - 1 do
          LInit := self.FTree.NthOf(LAt, NodeRole.Argument, LI);
          LField := self.FTree[LInit].ResolvedDecl;
          LValue := self.FTree.FirstOf(LInit, NodeRole.Value);
          LOffset := AOffset + self.DoMemberOffset(LRecord, LField);
          if self.FTree[LField].ResolvedBitWidth >= 0 then
            if not self.DoConstLane(LValue, LField, ABytes, LOffset) then
              return false;
            end;
          else
            if not self.DoConstBytes(LValue, self.DoDeclType(LField), ABytes, LOffset, ATexts,
              AWords) then
              return false;
            end;
          end;
        end;
        return true;
      end;
      // a text or a dynamic array is a block's address: bytes known before the program runs
      // only as a literal's constant block (a word the blob's placing fills) or nil
      if ATexts and self.DoIsManaged(AType) then
        return self.DoConstText(LAt, AType, AOffset, AWords);
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(AType) or self.DoIsManaged(AType) or (not self.DoIsFolded(LAt)) then
        return false;
      end;
      // a float place takes a float's bits, never a folded integer's (an integer SEM
      // converted to the float: its value is built at run time, as a float constant's is)
      if ClassOf(self.FTree, AType) = TypeClass.Float then
        return false;
      end;
      PutLe(ABytes, AOffset, uint64(self.DoConstBits(LAt, self.FTree[LAt].ResolvedType)),
        TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType));
      return true;
    end;

    // The folded managed value AExpr of the managed type AType at AOffset (DoConstBytes with
    // texts): a string constant's literal block (DoStringBlock, DoWideBlock for a wstring)
    // as the word AOffset, its blob added to AWords (two entries each), "" and nil the zero
    // bytes already there; false for any other value (it did not fold)
    hidden method DoConstText(const AExpr: int64; const AType: int64; const AOffset: int64;
      var AWords: Int64Array): bool;
    var
      LBlock: int64;
      LCount: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree[AExpr].ResolvedConst.Kind = ConstKind.String then
        if self.DoIsWideText(AType) then
          LBlock := self.DoWideBlock(AExpr, self.DoWideUnits(AExpr));
        else
          LBlock := self.DoStringBlock(AExpr, self.FTree[AExpr].ResolvedConst.Text);
        end;
        if LBlock <> 0 then
          LCount := len(AWords);
          setlength(AWords, LCount + 2);
          AWords[LCount] := AOffset;
          AWords[LCount + 1] := LBlock;
        end;
        return true;
      end;
      if not self.DoIsFolded(AExpr) then
        return false;
      end;
      return self.DoConstBits(AExpr, self.FTree[AExpr].ResolvedType) = 0;
    end;

    // The blob of the address word at the byte offset AOffset in AWords (DoConstText's
    // pairs), 0 when none starts there
    hidden const method DoWordAt(const AWords: Int64Array; const AOffset: int64): int64;
    var
      LK: int64;
    begin
      LK := 0;
      while LK < len(AWords) do
        if AWords[LK] = AOffset then
          return AWords[LK + 1];
        end;
        LK := LK + 2;
      end;
      return 0;
    end;

    // The data blob of the module variable or constant ADecl of the aggregate type AType
    // (or, with ATexts, of a managed one), named ASymbol (internal when AInternal): its
    // initializer's bytes when they all fold (DoConstBytes; with ATexts a literal's text as
    // an address word to its constant block, DoConstText; a blob of AKind, a variable's
    // all-zero bytes with no word Zeroed), noted in FDataWritten; else a Zeroed blob its
    // initializer is copied into at the entry (DoGlobalInit)
    hidden method DoAggregateData(const ADecl: int64; const AType: int64; const ASymbol: string;
      const AKind: IrDataKind; const AInternal: bool; const ATexts: bool);
    var
      LInit: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LBytes: ByteArray;
      LWords: Int64Array;
      LKind: IrDataKind;
      LData: int64;
      LWord: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LZero: bool;
    begin
      LInit := self.FTree.FirstOf(ADecl, NodeRole.Initializer);
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType);
      setlength(LBytes, LSize);
      for LK := 0 to LSize - 1 do
        LBytes[LK] := 0;
      end;
      setlength(LWords, 0);
      LKind := IrDataKind.Zeroed;
      if (LInit <> 0) and self.DoConstBytes(LInit, AType, LBytes, 0, ATexts, LWords) then
        self.FDataWritten[ADecl] := true;
        LKind := AKind;
        if (AKind = IrDataKind.Variable) and (len(LWords) = 0) then
          LZero := true;
          for LK := 0 to LSize - 1 do
            if LBytes[LK] <> 0 then
              LZero := false;
            end;
          end;
          if LZero then
            LKind := IrDataKind.Zeroed;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      LData := self.FModule.AddDataOfKind(ASymbol, LKind, TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, AType),
        ADecl);
      if LKind = IrDataKind.Zeroed then
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).Reserve(LSize);
      else
        // Its bytes in order, an address word (8 bytes the placing fills) where one starts
        LK := 0;
        while LK < LSize do
          LWord := self.DoWordAt(LWords, LK);
          if LWord <> 0 then
            self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddAddress(self.FModule.DataAt(LWord).Symbol, 0);
            LK := LK + self.FTarget.PointerSize();
          else
            self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(LBytes[LK]);
            LK := LK + 1;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      self.FModule.DataAt(LData).Internal := AInternal;
      self.FDataOf[ADecl] := LData;
    end;

    // The module constant ADecl when it is an aggregate (a scalar constant folds into every
    // use and needs no data): a ReadOnly blob of its bytes, global (another unit's code
    // links to it), named by ADAM_LOWERING_CONST_SYMBOL, its module's name and its own
    // (DoAggregateData)
    hidden method DoGlobalConst(const ADecl: int64);
    var
      LType: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoDeclType(ADecl);
      if not self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        return;
      end;
      if self.FDeclaring then
        self.DoDeclareData(ADecl, self.DoConstSymbol(ADecl), false);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoHoldsManaged(LType) and (self.DoManagedMapData(LType, ADecl) = 0) then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoAggregateData(ADecl, LType, self.DoConstSymbol(ADecl), IrDataKind.ReadOnly, false,
        false);
    end;

    // The symbol of the aggregate module constant ADecl's blob (ADAM_LOWERING_CONST_SYMBOL,
    // its module's name, '_', its own)
    hidden const method DoConstSymbol(const ADecl: int64): string;
    begin
      return ADAM_LOWERING_CONST_SYMBOL + self.FTree[self.FTree.ParentOf(ADecl)].Text + "_" +
        self.FTree[ADecl].Text;
    end;

    // Another unit's module variable or aggregate constant ADecl given a declared blob of
    // ASymbol (its bytes are that unit's object's, SU2.4): its uses are its address by
    // symbol, a threadstatic's through ThreadAddress; nothing of it runs here. AInternal
    // is what the defining unit makes it (a private variable is internal there): a body
    // copy that reaches an internal one cannot link and is dropped (DoReachesInternal)
    hidden method DoDeclareData(const ADecl: int64; const ASymbol: string; const AInternal: bool);
    var
      LData: int64;
    begin
      LData := self.FModule.AddDataOfKind(ASymbol, IrDataKind.Zeroed, 1, ADecl);
      self.FModule.DataAt(LData).Declared := true;
      self.FModule.DataAt(LData).Internal := AInternal;
      self.FModule.DataAt(LData).ThreadLocal := self.FTree[ADecl].HasFlag(NodeFlag.ThreadStatic);
      self.FDataOf[ADecl] := LData;
      self.FDataWritten[ADecl] := true;
    end;

    // The module variable ADecl in its data blob, named by its ResolvedSymbol (internal
    // when it is its module's private one, Symbols.HasInternalSymbol): its initializer's
    // folded bits, little-endian at its size, when they are not all zero (a Variable blob),
    // else a Zeroed one of its size; an initializer that did not fold leaves it Zeroed and
    // runs in its unit's variable inits (DoUnitVarInit); an aggregate's blob holds its initializer's
    // bytes when they fold, else it is Zeroed and its initializer copied in there
    // (DoAggregateData); a text's blob is a Zeroed pointer (the empty text), its
    // initializer stored at the entry (DoGlobalInit) and its text released by its module's
    // teardown at process exit (DoTeardown). LW0001: an external one (M3.13), a constructed
    // one, one of a type with no machine value (a dynamic array: M3.9, an object: M3.10). A
    // threadstatic one (BNF sec 3) goes through DoThreadStatic
    hidden method DoGlobal(const ADecl: int64);
    begin
      if self.FDeclaring then
        if self.FTree.FirstOf(ADecl, NodeRole.External) = 0 then
          self.DoDeclareData(ADecl, self.FTree[ADecl].ResolvedSymbol, self.DoInternal(ADecl));
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree[ADecl].HasFlag(NodeFlag.ThreadStatic) then
        self.DoThreadStatic(ADecl);
        return;
      end;
      self.DoGlobalData(ADecl, false);
    end;

    // The threadstatic module variable ADecl: its blob as DoGlobalData makes it for a
    // thread (a managed value's literal start as an address word to its constant block),
    // flagged ThreadLocal (every thread's starting copy: the loader copies it per thread, so
    // nothing of it runs at the entry; its address is a ThreadAddress, DoDataAddress). A
    // managed one (string, dynamic array, ref) or one holding one is released as its thread
    // ends: the main thread's by its module's teardown (DoTeardown), every other thread's
    // by its unit's thread release (DoUnitRelease). SEM leaves it a constant
    // initializer or none; LW0001: one whose initializer did not fold into its bytes. The
    // blob is made first, so its uses lower and a refusal is the variable's one report
    hidden method DoThreadStatic(const ADecl: int64);
    var
      LType: int64;
      LInit: int64;
      LFolded: bool;
    begin
      LType := self.DoDeclType(ADecl);
      self.DoGlobalData(ADecl, true);
      if self.FDataOf[ADecl] = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      self.FModule.DataAt(self.FDataOf[ADecl]).ThreadLocal := true;
      LInit := self.FTree.FirstOf(ADecl, NodeRole.Initializer);
      LFolded := true;
      if LInit <> 0 then
        LFolded := self.FDataWritten[ADecl] or ((not self.DoIsAggregate(LType)) and
          (not self.DoIsManaged(LType)) and self.DoIsFolded(LInit));
      end;
      if not LFolded then
        self.DoRefuse(ADecl, "a threadstatic " + self.FTree.ConstructText(ADecl) +
          " whose initializer does not fold");
        return;
      end;
      // its bytes are its start: the entry stores nothing into it (DoGlobalInit)
      self.FDataWritten[ADecl] := true;
    end;

    // The module variable ADecl's data blob (DoGlobal's header); for a thread's copy
    // (AThread: DoThreadStatic) a managed value, or an aggregate holding one, folds a
    // literal's text into its bytes as an address word (DoAggregateData with texts)
    hidden method DoGlobalData(const ADecl: int64; const AThread: bool);
    var
      LType: int64;
      LInit: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LAlign: int64;
      LBits: int64;
      LBytes: ByteArray;
      LData: int64;
      LK: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree.FirstOf(ADecl, NodeRole.External) <> 0 then
        self.DoRefuse(ADecl, "an external " + self.FTree.ConstructText(ADecl));
        return;
      end;
      LType := self.DoDeclType(ADecl);
      // init arguments build an object (at the entry, DoGlobalInit); SEM gives them to
      // nothing else
      if (self.FTree.CountOf(ADecl, NodeRole.ConstructorArgument) > 0) and
        (ClassOf(self.FTree, LType) <> TypeClass.ObjectType) then
        self.DoRefuse(ADecl, "a constructed " + self.FTree.ConstructText(ADecl));
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        if self.DoHoldsManaged(LType) and (self.DoManagedMapData(LType, ADecl) = 0) then
          return;
        end;
        self.DoAggregateData(ADecl, LType, self.FTree[ADecl].ResolvedSymbol, IrDataKind.Variable,
          self.DoInternal(ADecl), AThread);
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsManaged(LType) then
        if self.DoIsArrayValue(LType) and (self.DoElementMapData(LType, ADecl) = 0) then
          return;
        end;
        // a thread's copy starts at its literal's block (or nil) in its own bytes
        if AThread then
          self.DoAggregateData(ADecl, LType, self.FTree[ADecl].ResolvedSymbol, IrDataKind.Variable,
            self.DoInternal(ADecl), true);
          return;
        end;
        LData := self.FModule.AddDataOfKind(self.FTree[ADecl].ResolvedSymbol, IrDataKind.Zeroed,
          self.FTarget.PointerAlign(), ADecl);
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).Reserve(self.FTarget.PointerSize());
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).Internal := self.DoInternal(ADecl);
        self.FDataOf[ADecl] := LData;
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoTypeAt(LType, ADecl) = IrType.Void then
        return;
      end;
      LInit := self.FTree.FirstOf(ADecl, NodeRole.Initializer);
      LBits := 0;
      if (LInit <> 0) and self.DoIsFolded(LInit) then
        LBits := self.DoConstBits(LInit, self.FTree[LInit].ResolvedType);
      end;
      LSize := TypeSize(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType);
      LAlign := TypeAlign(self.FTree, self.FTarget, LType);
      if LBits = 0 then
        LData := self.FModule.AddDataOfKind(self.FTree[ADecl].ResolvedSymbol, IrDataKind.Zeroed,
          LAlign, ADecl);
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).Reserve(LSize);
      else
        LData := self.FModule.AddDataOfKind(self.FTree[ADecl].ResolvedSymbol, IrDataKind.Variable,
          LAlign, ADecl);
        // A scalar's size is 1..8 bytes: PutLe's range
        setlength(LBytes, LSize);
        PutLe(LBytes, 0, uint64(LBits), LSize);
        for LK := 0 to LSize - 1 do
          self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(LBytes[LK]);
        end;
      end;
      self.FModule.DataAt(LData).Internal := self.DoInternal(ADecl);
      self.FDataOf[ADecl] := LData;
    end;

    // The module declaration ADecl: a routine with a body gets its function (an external
    // gets its entry when called), a module variable its data (DoGlobal), an aggregate
    // constant its data (DoGlobalConst); a type's bodies and anything else that would need
    // code are LW0001; scalar constants, forwards and errors need none
    hidden method DoDeclaration(const ADecl: int64);
    var
      LKind: NodeKind;
    begin
      LKind := self.FTree[ADecl].Kind;
      if LKind = NodeKind.RoutineDecl then
        if self.FTree.FirstOf(ADecl, NodeRole.External) = 0 then
          self.DoRegister(ADecl);
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.VarDecl then
        self.DoGlobal(ADecl);
        return;
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.TypeDecl then
        // its TypeInfo is its own unit's to define (DoTypeInfo), used here or not
        if not self.FDeclaring then
          self.DoTypeInfo(ADecl, ADecl);
        end;
        self.DoTypeBodies(ADecl);
        return;
      end;
      if LKind = NodeKind.ConstDecl then
        self.DoGlobalConst(ADecl);
        return;
      end;
      if (LKind = NodeKind.ForwardRoutine) or
        (LKind = NodeKind.ForwardType) or (LKind = NodeKind.Error) then
        return;
      end;
      self.DoRefuse(ADecl, "a module's " + self.FTree.ConstructText(ADecl));
    end;

    // Every local type under ANode (a type block of a routine or among statements, in any
    // routine's, member's, section's or the program block's code: BNF sec 3 / 5) given what
    // a module's type gets (DoDeclaration: its TypeInfo, its member functions), in source
    // order; a module-level type is its module's declaration, an inline type its type's
    // (DoTypeBodies), a generic template's are its instances' (M10)
    hidden method DoLocalTypes(const ANode: int64);
    var
      LChild: int64;
      LRole: NodeRole;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.ChildCount(ANode) - 1 do
        LChild := self.FTree.ChildAt(ANode, LI);
        LRole := self.FTree.RoleOf(LChild);
        if (LRole <> NodeRole.Effects) and (self.FTree.FirstOf(LChild, NodeRole.GenericParam) = 0) then
          if (self.FTree[LChild].Kind = NodeKind.TypeDecl) and (LRole <> NodeRole.Declaration) and
            (LRole <> NodeRole.TypeOf) then
            self.DoDeclaration(LChild);
          end;
          self.DoLocalTypes(LChild);
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The module AModule's declarations (another unit's declared: FDeclaring), then its own
    // local types (DoLocalTypes); an exe's
    // block is the program block (DoFindEntry), any other module's block is LW0001; the
    // initialize and finalize sections get their functions once the entry is known
    // (DoRegisterSections)
    hidden method DoModule(const AModule: int64);
    var
      LBlock: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AModule, NodeRole.Declaration) - 1 do
        self.DoDeclaration(self.FTree.NthOf(AModule, NodeRole.Declaration, LI));
      end;
      // another unit's local types are its own: nothing here names them
      if not self.FDeclaring then
        self.DoLocalTypes(AModule);
      end;
      LBlock := self.FTree.FirstOf(AModule, NodeRole.Body);
      if LBlock <> 0 then
        if self.FTree[AModule].Module = ModuleKind.Exe then
          self.FEntryModule := AModule;
        else
          self.DoRefuse(LBlock, "the block of " + self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(AModule));
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // Whether the program has an entry (FHasEntry: an exe's block and the runtime's exit to
    // end it with) and its function: the parts' __adam_entry (the IR's Entry), or the exe
    // unit's block function (public, ADAM_LOWERING_BLOCK_SYMBOL and its name), which the
    // entry calls; LW0001 at the block, in the exe's own unit, when the program has no
    // runtime exit (no runtime unit)
    hidden method DoFindEntry();
    var
      LExit: int64;
    begin
      if self.FEntryModule = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LExit := self.FTree[self.FEntryModule].ResolvedCallee;
      if (LExit = 0) or (self.FFunctionOf[LExit] = 0) then
        if self.FUnit = self.FEntryModule then
          self.DoRefuse(self.FTree.FirstOf(self.FEntryModule, NodeRole.Body),
            "the block of " + self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(self.FEntryModule) + " with no runtime unit");
        end;
        self.FEntryModule := 0;
        return;
      end;
      self.FHasEntry := true;
      if self.FUnit = ADAM_LOWERING_PARTS then
        self.FEntry := self.FModule.AddFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_ENTRY_SYMBOL, IrType.Void,
          self.FEntryModule);
        self.FModule.Entry := self.FEntry;
      end;
      if self.FUnit = self.FEntryModule then
        self.FEntry := self.FModule.AddFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_BLOCK_SYMBOL +
          self.FTree[self.FEntryModule].Text, IrType.Void, self.FEntryModule);
      end;
    end;

    // The function of ASymbol (no parameters, no result) another object defines (the parts'
    // view of a unit's entry points, SU2.4), declared at ANode
    hidden method DoDeclaredFunction(const ASymbol: string; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LFunction: int64;
    begin
      LFunction := self.FModule.AddFunction(ASymbol, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Declared := true;
      return LFunction;
    end;

    // A call at ANode of the function AFunction (no arguments, no result)
    hidden method DoCallPlain(const AFunction: int64; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Call, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Link := AFunction;
    end;

    // The module variable ADecl with no initializer built in the entry when it is an
    // object built by its init (SEM's pick, ADecl's ResolvedCallee, with its arguments) or
    // by its parts' (DoBuildObject), in its unit's variable inits (DoUnitVarInit); LW0001 at it
    // with no entry to run it
    hidden method DoGlobalBuild(const ADecl: int64);
    var
      LType: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.DoDeclType(ADecl);
      if (not self.DoNeedsBuild(LType)) and (self.FTree[ADecl].ResolvedCallee = 0) then
        return;
      end;
      if not self.FHasEntry then
        self.DoRefuse(ADecl, "the init of a module's " + self.FTree.ConstructText(ADecl) +
          " with no entry to run it");
        return;
      end;
      self.DoBuildObject(self.DoDataAddress(ADecl, ADecl), LType, self.FTree[ADecl].ResolvedCallee, ADecl,
        NodeRole.ConstructorArgument, ADecl);
    end;

    // The module variable's or aggregate constant's ADecl initializer when it did not fold
    // (DoGlobal / DoAggregateData left its data Zeroed): its value stored into its data in
    // the entry (an aggregate's bytes copied, DoAggregateSource); LW0001 at it with no
    // entry to run it
    hidden method DoGlobalInit(const ADecl: int64);
    var
      LInit: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LSource: int64;
    begin
      if (self.FTree[ADecl].Kind <> NodeKind.VarDecl) and (self.FTree[ADecl].Kind <> NodeKind.ConstDecl) then
        return;
      end;
      LInit := self.FTree.FirstOf(ADecl, NodeRole.Initializer);
      if (LInit = 0) and (self.FDataOf[ADecl] <> 0) and (self.FTree[ADecl].Kind = NodeKind.VarDecl) then
        self.DoGlobalBuild(ADecl);
        return;
      end;
      if (LInit = 0) or (self.FDataOf[ADecl] = 0) or self.FDataWritten[ADecl] then
        return;
      end;
      LType := self.DoDeclType(ADecl);
      // a text's or a dynamic array's value is a block's address: even a folded one is
      // stored at run time
      if self.DoIsFolded(LInit) and (not self.DoIsManaged(LType)) then
        return;
      end;
      if not self.FHasEntry then
        self.DoRefuse(LInit, "the initializer of a module's " + self.FTree.ConstructText(ADecl) +
          " with no entry to run it");
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAggregate(LType) then
        LSource := self.DoAggregateSource(LInit);
        if LSource <> 0 then
          // the variable is still empty at the entry: its value is copied in (DoCopyValue)
          self.DoCopyValue(self.DoDataAddress(ADecl, LInit), LSource, LType, LInit);
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if self.DoIsManaged(LType) then
        LValue := self.DoValue(LInit);
        if LValue <> 0 then
          self.DoStoreManaged(self.DoDataAddress(ADecl, LInit), LValue, LType, LInit);
        end;
        return;
      end;
      LValue := self.DoValue(LInit);
      if LValue <> 0 then
        self.DoStore(self.DoDataAddress(ADecl, LInit), LValue, LInit);
      end;
    end;

    // The module AModule placed in FOrder after every module it imports, each module once
    // (FOrdered): its variables and its initialize section are ready before its
    // importer's run
    hidden method DoOrderModule(const AModule: int64);
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if (AModule = 0) or self.FOrdered[AModule] then
        return;
      end;
      self.FOrdered[AModule] := true;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AModule, NodeRole.Import) - 1 do
        self.DoOrderModule(self.FTree[self.FTree.NthOf(AModule, NodeRole.Import, LI)].ResolvedUnit);
      end;
      self.FOrder.Add(AModule);
    end;

    // FOrder made: the runtime unit first (every module may call it), then each module of
    // the tree after its imports (the tree lists the main module first, so walking it in
    // its own order would run an importer before its imports)
    hidden method DoOrderModules();
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      self.DoOrderModule(self.FTree.Runtime);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ADAM_AST_PROGRAM, NodeRole.Module) - 1 do
        self.DoOrderModule(self.FTree.NthOf(ADAM_AST_PROGRAM, NodeRole.Module, LI));
      end;
    end;

    // The unit's variable init function (ADAM_LOWERING_VARINIT_SYMBOL and its name, public;
    // the entry calls every unit's in FOrder before anything else runs): a hidden slot for
    // every temporary in its module variables' and constants' initializers (DoTemporaries),
    // then its initializers that did not fold and its objects' builds (DoGlobalInit), in
    // declaration order, its temporaries released, its return; empty when it has none
    hidden method DoUnitVarInit();
    var
      LDecl: int64;
      LJ: int64;
    begin
      self.FFunction := self.FModule.AddFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_VARINIT_SYMBOL +
        self.FTree[self.FUnit].Text, IrType.Void, self.FUnit);
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoStartManaged();
      for LJ := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(self.FUnit, NodeRole.Declaration) - 1 do
        LDecl := self.FTree.NthOf(self.FUnit, NodeRole.Declaration, LJ);
        if ((self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.VarDecl) or (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.ConstDecl)) and
          (self.FTree.FirstOf(LDecl, NodeRole.Initializer) <> 0) then
          self.DoCodeTemporaries(LDecl);
        end;
      end;
      for LJ := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(self.FUnit, NodeRole.Declaration) - 1 do
        self.DoGlobalInit(self.FTree.NthOf(self.FUnit, NodeRole.Declaration, LJ));
      end;
      self.DoReleaseManaged(self.FUnit);
      self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, self.FUnit);
      self.DoCleanupScopes(self.FUnit, self.DoLastBlock());
    end;

    // The section ASection of the module AModule (ARole Initialize or Finalize) given its
    // function, internal, named by APrefix and the module's name; LW0001 at it when there
    // is no entry to run it
    hidden method DoRegisterSection(const AModule: int64; const ARole: NodeRole;
      const APrefix: string);
    var
      LSection: int64;
      LFunction: int64;
    begin
      LSection := self.FTree.FirstOf(AModule, ARole);
      if (LSection = 0) or (self.FTree[LSection].Kind = NodeKind.Error) then
        return;
      end;
      if not self.FHasEntry then
        self.DoRefuse(LSection, self.FTree.ConstructPhrase(LSection) + " with no entry to run it");
        return;
      end;
      LFunction := self.FModule.AddFunction(APrefix + self.FTree[AModule].Text, IrType.Void,
        LSection);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Internal := true;
      self.FFunctionOf[LSection] := LFunction;
    end;

    // The unit's initialize and finalize sections given their functions (its start calls
    // the initialize, its teardown the finalize)
    hidden method DoRegisterSections();
    begin
      self.DoRegisterSection(self.FUnit, NodeRole.Initialize, ADAM_LOWERING_INITIALIZE_SYMBOL);
      self.DoRegisterSection(self.FUnit, NodeRole.Finalize, ADAM_LOWERING_FINALIZE_SYMBOL);
    end;

    // The body of the section ASection (one with a function, DoRegisterSection), a routine
    // body (BNF sec 1): its own locals' slots and initializers as a routine's (DoLocalSlots,
    // DoLocalInits), its statements, then its return unless the last block ended already
    // (a `return;` in it leaves the section: DoReturn)
    hidden method DoSectionBody(const ASection: int64);
    var
      LBody: int64;
    begin
      self.FFunction := self.FFunctionOf[ASection];
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoStartManaged();
      LBody := self.FTree.FirstOf(ASection, NodeRole.Body);
      // the temporaries of its locals' initializers too, before the first branch
      self.DoCodeTemporaries(ASection);
      self.DoLocalSlots(ASection);
      self.DoLocalInits(ASection);
      self.DoStatements(LBody, NodeRole.Statement);
      if not self.DoEnded() then
        self.DoReleaseManaged(LBody);
        self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, LBody);
      end;
    end;

    // The unit's sections with a function lowered, the initialize first
    hidden method DoSectionBodies();
    var
      LSection: int64;
    begin
      LSection := self.FTree.FirstOf(self.FUnit, NodeRole.Initialize);
      if (LSection <> 0) and (self.FFunctionOf[LSection] <> 0) then
        self.DoSectionBody(LSection);
        self.DoCleanupScopes(LSection, self.DoLastBlock());
      end;
      LSection := self.FTree.FirstOf(self.FUnit, NodeRole.Finalize);
      if (LSection <> 0) and (self.FFunctionOf[LSection] <> 0) then
        self.DoSectionBody(LSection);
        self.DoCleanupScopes(LSection, self.DoLastBlock());
      end;
    end;

    // A call from the entry of the module AModule's section in ARole, when it has one with
    // a function
    hidden method DoCallSection(const AModule: int64; const ARole: NodeRole);
    var
      LSection: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LSection := self.FTree.FirstOf(AModule, ARole);
      if (LSection = 0) or (self.FFunctionOf[LSection] = 0) then
        return;
      end;
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Call, IrType.Void, LSection);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Link := self.FFunctionOf[LSection];
    end;

    // The exe's thread callback (IrModule.ThreadCallback): the platform unit's
    // (RuntimeRoutine.ThreadCallback, SEM's find) when it has one, the routine the OS calls
    // as each thread starts and ends (the runtime's thread end runs from it)
    hidden method DoThreadCallback();
    var
      LDecl: int64;
    begin
      LDecl := self.FTree.RuntimeRoutineOf(RuntimeRoutine.ThreadCallback);
      if (LDecl <> 0) and (self.FFunctionOf[LDecl] <> 0) then
        self.FModule.ThreadCallback := self.FFunctionOf[LDecl];
      end;
    end;

    // The unit's thread release (ADAM_LOWERING_UNIT_RELEASE_SYMBOL and its name, public;
    // the program's thread release calls every unit's, DoProgramRelease): the calling
    // thread's copy of each of its managed threadstatics or ones holding one
    // (DoThreadStatic) released as DoTeardown releases a module variable, its last declared
    // first; empty when it has none (the main thread's copies are released by its teardown)
    hidden method DoUnitRelease();
    var
      LDecl: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LDone: bool;
      LJ: int64;
    begin
      self.FFunction := self.FModule.AddFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_UNIT_RELEASE_SYMBOL +
        self.FTree[self.FUnit].Text, IrType.Void, self.FUnit);
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LDone := false;
      LJ := self.FTree.CountOf(self.FUnit, NodeRole.Declaration) - 1;
      while (LJ >= 0) and not LDone do
        LDecl := self.FTree.NthOf(self.FUnit, NodeRole.Declaration, LJ);
        if (self.FDataOf[LDecl] <> 0) and (self.FTree[LDecl].Kind = NodeKind.VarDecl) and
          self.FTree[LDecl].HasFlag(NodeFlag.ThreadStatic) then
          LType := self.DoDeclType(LDecl);
          if self.DoHoldsManaged(LType) or self.DoNeedsEnd(LType) then
            // a refused release (reported) ends the function here
            LDone := not self.DoReleaseAt(self.DoDataAddress(LDecl, self.FUnit), LType, self.FUnit);
          end;
        end;
        LJ := LJ - 1;
      end;
      self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, self.FUnit);
    end;

    // The program's thread release (the parts' own, internal,
    // ADAM_LOWERING_THREAD_RELEASE_SYMBOL): every unit's thread release called, module by
    // module in reverse FOrder; handed to the runtime by the entry at ANode
    // (RuntimeRoutine.SetThreadRelease given its address), which runs it as each thread but
    // the main one ends
    hidden method DoProgramRelease(const ANode: int64);
    var
      LFunction: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LEntryFunction: int64;
      LEntryBlock: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LFunction := self.FModule.AddFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_THREAD_RELEASE_SYMBOL, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Internal := true;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.CodeAddress, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := LFunction;
      self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.SetThreadRelease, LAddress, 0, ANode);
      // Its body, lowered aside: the entry goes on where it was after it
      LEntryFunction := self.FFunction;
      LEntryBlock := self.FBlock;
      self.FFunction := LFunction;
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(LFunction);
      for LI := self.FOrder.Count - 1 downto 0 do
        self.DoCallPlain(self.DoDeclaredFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_UNIT_RELEASE_SYMBOL +
          self.FTree[self.FOrder[LI]].Text, ANode), ANode);
      end;
      self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FFunction := LEntryFunction;
      self.FBlock := LEntryBlock;
    end;

    // The parts' entry function's body (SU2.4: every unit's code is its own object's, the
    // entry calls each one's entry points by symbol): every unit's variable inits in FOrder
    // (DoUnitVarInit), the thread callback noted (DoThreadCallback), the program's thread
    // release handed over (DoProgramRelease), the site list handed over (DoHandSites), the
    // heap report registered as the first exit handler (so it runs last), then every
    // unit's start in FOrder (DoUnitStart: its initialize, then its teardown registered;
    // BNF sec 1: exit handlers run last registered first, so the teardowns run in reverse
    // FOrder, each after every handler registered later), the task wait registered, the
    // program block's function called (DoBlockBody), then the runtime's exit with 0, which
    // runs the exit handlers; a catching scope around it all (DoEntryCatch)
    hidden method DoEntryBody();
    var
      LBody: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      self.FFunction := self.FEntry;
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FEntry);
      self.DoStartManaged();
      LBody := self.FTree.FirstOf(self.FEntryModule, NodeRole.Body);
      for LI := 0 to self.FOrder.Count - 1 do
        self.DoCallPlain(self.DoDeclaredFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_VARINIT_SYMBOL +
          self.FTree[self.FOrder[LI]].Text, LBody), LBody);
      end;
      self.DoThreadCallback();
      self.DoProgramRelease(LBody);
      self.DoHandSites(LBody);
      self.DoResDataTable(LBody);
      self.DoAtExit(self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.ReportHeap, LBody), LBody);
      for LI := 0 to self.FOrder.Count - 1 do
        self.DoCallPlain(self.DoDeclaredFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_START_SYMBOL +
          self.FTree[self.FOrder[LI]].Text, LBody), LBody);
      end;
      // Registered last, so it runs first: every running task (a discarded one detached
      // included) ends before any module's teardown (M3.8g0b3)
      self.DoAtExit(self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.TaskWait, LBody), LBody);
      if self.FTree[self.FEntryModule].HasFlag(NodeFlag.UnitTests) then
        self.DoExit(LBody, self.DoTestRunner(LBody));
      else
        self.DoCallPlain(self.DoDeclaredFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_BLOCK_SYMBOL +
          self.FTree[self.FEntryModule].Text, LBody), LBody);
        self.DoExit(LBody, 0);
      end;
      self.DoEntryCatch(LBody);
    end;

    // The symbol of the function of the test block numbered AIndex (among its module's
    // tests, from 0) of the module AModule
    hidden const method DoTestSymbol(const AModule: int64; const AIndex: int64): string;
    begin
      return ADAM_LOWERING_TEST_SYMBOL + self.FTree[AModule].Text + "_" + IntToStr(AIndex);
    end;

    // The test runner the entry of a build with @unitTestMode on runs at ANode in place of
    // the program block (BNF sec 8; NodeFlag.UnitTests on the exe module): the runtime's
    // TestStart given the count of the program's tests, its TestRun per test (its name,
    // its function by symbol, its file and line), the modules in FOrder (every unit's
    // tests before the exe's own), each module's in source order, then its TestEnd; its
    // result (the count of failed tests, the exit code), 0 after LW0001
    hidden method DoTestRunner(const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LRun: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LModule: int64;
      LTest: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LArgs: ref Int64List;
      LI: int64;
      LJ: int64;
    begin
      LRun := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.TestRun, ANode);
      if LRun = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LCount := 0;
      for LI := 0 to self.FOrder.Count - 1 do
        LCount := LCount + self.FTree.CountOf(self.FOrder[LI], NodeRole.Test);
      end;
      LArgs := ref Int64List();
      LArgs.Add(self.DoConstant(IrType.Int64, LCount, ANode));
      if self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.TestStart, LArgs, ANode) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FOrder.Count - 1 do
        LModule := self.FOrder[LI];
        for LJ := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LModule, NodeRole.Test) - 1 do
          LTest := self.FTree.NthOf(LModule, NodeRole.Test, LJ);
          LArgs := ref Int64List();
          LArgs.Add(self.DoStringLiteral(LTest, self.FTree[LTest].Text));
          LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.CodeAddress, IrType.Pointer, LTest);
          self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := self.DoDeclaredFunction(
            self.DoTestSymbol(LModule, LJ), LTest);
          LArgs.Add(LAddress);
          LArgs.Add(self.DoStringLiteral(LTest, self.FTree[LTest].Place.FileName));
          LArgs.Add(self.DoConstant(self.FModule.FunctionAt(LRun).Signature.ParamTypes[3],
            int64(self.FTree[LTest].Place.Line), LTest));
          if self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.TestRun, LArgs, LTest) = 0 then
            return 0;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return self.DoCallRuntimeArgs(RuntimeRoutine.TestEnd, ref Int64List(), ANode);
    end;

    // The unit's test blocks (BNF sec 8) given their functions (public, DoTestSymbol) and
    // lowered, each body as a section's (DoSectionBody); only the entry's test runner calls
    // them (DoTestRunner). A unit's are always lowered (a program not in test mode calls
    // none, so link-time removal drops them); an exe's only with @unitTestMode on (off:
    // checked, not compiled in); a dll's or a lib's never run (SM0113), so never lowered
    hidden method DoTestBodies();
    var
      LTest: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      match self.FTree[self.FUnit].Module of
        ModuleKind.Exe:
          if not self.FTree[self.FUnit].HasFlag(NodeFlag.UnitTests) then
            return;
          end;
        ModuleKind.Dll, ModuleKind.Lib:
          return;
      else
        // a unit's tests are lowered
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(self.FUnit, NodeRole.Test) - 1 do
        LTest := self.FTree.NthOf(self.FUnit, NodeRole.Test, LI);
        self.FFunctionOf[LTest] := self.FModule.AddFunction(self.DoTestSymbol(self.FUnit, LI),
          IrType.Void, LTest);
        self.DoSectionBody(LTest);
        self.DoCleanupScopes(LTest, self.DoLastBlock());
      end;
    end;

    // The exe unit's block function's body (FEntry, DoFindEntry; the parts' entry calls it):
    // the program block's statements, then its end block (FEntryEnd, where the block's end
    // and its returns go): its temporaries released, its return; its cleanup scopes
    hidden method DoBlockBody();
    var
      LBody: int64;
    begin
      self.FFunction := self.FEntry;
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FEntry);
      self.FEntryEnd := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FEntry);
      self.DoStartManaged();
      LBody := self.FTree.FirstOf(self.FEntryModule, NodeRole.Body);
      self.DoCodeTemporaries(LBody);
      self.DoStatements(LBody, NodeRole.Statement);
      if not self.DoEnded() then
        self.DoJumpTo(self.FEntryEnd, LBody);
      end;
      // The program block's string temporaries released, before the return
      self.FBlock := self.FEntryEnd;
      self.DoReleaseManaged(LBody);
      self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, LBody);
      self.DoCleanupScopes(LBody, self.DoLastBlock());
    end;

    // The unit's start (ADAM_LOWERING_START_SYMBOL and its name, public; the entry calls
    // every unit's in FOrder): its initialize section called, then its teardown
    // (DoTeardown, when it has one) registered as an exit handler; its return
    hidden method DoUnitStart();
    begin
      self.FFunction := self.FModule.AddFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_START_SYMBOL +
        self.FTree[self.FUnit].Text, IrType.Void, self.FUnit);
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      self.DoCallSection(self.FUnit, NodeRole.Initialize);
      self.DoAtExit(self.DoTeardown(self.FUnit, self.FUnit), self.FUnit);
      self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, self.FUnit);
    end;

    // AFunction (0: nothing) registered by the entry at ANode as an exit handler: its code
    // address handed to the runtime's AtExit
    hidden method DoAtExit(const AFunction: int64; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LAddress: int64;
    begin
      if AFunction = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.CodeAddress, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := AFunction;
      self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.AtExit, LAddress, 0, ANode);
    end;

    // The module AModule's teardown, the exit handler the entry at ANode registers right
    // after its initialize: a function of its own, internal (ADAM_LOWERING_TEARDOWN_SYMBOL and
    // the module's name), that calls its finalize section, then releases its module variables
    // and aggregate constants (DoReleaseModuleGlobals); 0 when it has neither. Its body is
    // lowered aside: the entry goes on where it was after it
    hidden method DoTeardown(const AModule: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LSection: int64;
      LFunction: int64;
      LEntryFunction: int64;
      LEntryBlock: int64;
    begin
      LSection := self.FTree.FirstOf(AModule, NodeRole.Finalize);
      if ((LSection = 0) or (self.FFunctionOf[LSection] = 0)) and
        (not self.DoHasModuleGlobals(AModule)) then
        return 0;
      end;
      LFunction := self.FModule.AddFunction(ADAM_LOWERING_TEARDOWN_SYMBOL +
        self.FTree[AModule].Text, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(LFunction).Internal := true;
      LEntryFunction := self.FFunction;
      LEntryBlock := self.FBlock;
      self.FFunction := LFunction;
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(LFunction);
      self.DoCallSection(AModule, NodeRole.Finalize);
      self.DoReleaseModuleGlobals(AModule, ANode);
      self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.DoCatchAll(ANode, RuntimeRoutine.CatchRaise, RuntimeRoutine.Unhandled);
      self.FFunction := LEntryFunction;
      self.FBlock := LEntryBlock;
      return LFunction;
    end;

    // The entry's catch, after its whole body (ANode its block): its own cleanup scopes
    // (DoCleanupScopes), then one catching scope around all of its blocks, the outermost,
    // its filter the platform unit's (RuntimeRoutine.Catch: the runtime's raise) and its
    // target a catch block made last, which no jump reaches: the frames inside unwound (each
    // finally and cleanup run, the entry's own included), the dispatcher resumes there, and
    // it calls the runtime's Unhandled (the report, then the process ends: its return is
    // never reached). A raise a guard's except part catches never gets here (DoGuard)
    hidden method DoEntryCatch(const ANode: int64);
    begin
      self.DoCleanupScopes(ANode, self.DoLastBlock());
      self.DoCatchAll(ANode, RuntimeRoutine.CatchRaise, RuntimeRoutine.Unhandled);
    end;

    // One catching scope around every block of the function being lowered (FFunction), the
    // outermost: its filter the platform unit's AFilter and its target a block made last that
    // calls the runtime's ACatch, which never returns. CatchRaise and Unhandled: a raise
    // only (a hardware fault goes on to the platform's last filter, reported with no
    // teardown), reported (the entry's, DoEntryCatch, each module's teardown's, DoTeardown:
    // a raise in a finalize is reported as one in the program block is, and the runtime's
    // ThreadRun's, a started thread's). CatchAbort and GeneratorEnd: a generator's abort only
    // (no guard takes it), which ends the generator (the runtime's GeneratorRun's, G1)
    hidden method DoCatchAll(const ANode: int64; const AFilter: RuntimeRoutine;
      const ACatch: RuntimeRoutine);
    var
      LLast: int64;
      LFilter: int64;
      LHandler: int64;
      LCatch: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LLast := self.DoLastBlock();
      LFilter := self.DoRuntimeFunction(AFilter, ANode);
      LHandler := self.DoRuntimeFunction(RuntimeRoutine.FrameHandler, ANode);
      LCatch := self.DoRuntimeFunction(ACatch, ANode);
      if (LFilter = 0) or (LHandler = 0) or (LCatch = 0) then
        return;
      end;
      self.FBlock := self.FModule.AddBlock(self.FFunction);
      LId := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Call, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Link := LCatch;
      self.DoEmit(IrOp.Ret, IrType.Void, ANode);
      self.FModule.FunctionAt(self.FFunction).AddScope(0, LLast, LFilter, LLast + 1);
      self.FModule.FrameHandler := LHandler;
    end;

    // Whether the module declaration ADecl is a module variable or aggregate constant with a
    // blob whose value its module's teardown releases (it holds a managed value or one that
    // ends)
    hidden method DoReleasesAtTeardown(const ADecl: int64): bool;
    var
      LType: int64;
    begin
      if (self.FDataOf[ADecl] = 0) or ((self.FTree[ADecl].Kind <> NodeKind.VarDecl) and
        (self.FTree[ADecl].Kind <> NodeKind.ConstDecl)) then
        return false;
      end;
      LType := self.DoDeclType(ADecl);
      return self.DoHoldsManaged(LType) or self.DoNeedsEnd(LType);
    end;

    // Whether the module AModule has a declaration its teardown releases
    // (DoReleasesAtTeardown)
    hidden method DoHasModuleGlobals(const AModule: int64): bool;
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AModule, NodeRole.Declaration) - 1 do
        if self.DoReleasesAtTeardown(self.FTree.NthOf(AModule, NodeRole.Declaration, LI)) then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // The module AModule's module variables and aggregate constants released by its teardown
    // at ANode (after its finalize, which may still use them), its last declared first
    // (DoReleaseAt; the calling thread's copy of a threadstatic)
    hidden method DoReleaseModuleGlobals(const AModule: int64; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LDecl: int64;
      LJ: int64;
    begin
      for LJ := self.FTree.CountOf(AModule, NodeRole.Declaration) - 1 downto 0 do
        LDecl := self.FTree.NthOf(AModule, NodeRole.Declaration, LJ);
        if self.DoReleasesAtTeardown(LDecl) then
          if not self.DoReleaseAt(self.DoDataAddress(LDecl, ANode), self.DoDeclType(LDecl),
            ANode) then
            return;
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The @linklibrary names of the module AModule, in their order, added to the IR module
    // (the Parser checked each name's shape; the link finds it)
    hidden method DoLinkLibraries(const AModule: int64);
    var
      LDirective: int64;
      LArg: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(AModule, NodeRole.Directive) - 1 do
        LDirective := self.FTree.NthOf(AModule, NodeRole.Directive, LI);
        if (self.FTree[LDirective].Text = ADAM_LOWERING_DIRECTIVE_LINK) and
          (self.FTree.CountOf(LDirective, NodeRole.Argument) > 0) then
          LArg := self.FTree.NthOf(LDirective, NodeRole.Argument, 0);
          self.FModule.AddLinkLibrary(self.FTree[LArg].Decoded, LArg);
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The 4 bytes of AValue, little-endian, added to the data blob AData
    hidden method DoAddLe32(const AData: int64; const AValue: int64);
    var
      LBits: uint64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LBits := uint64(AValue);
      for LI := 0 to 3 do
        self.FModule.DataAt(AData).AddByte(uint8(LBits & 255));
        LBits := LBits shr 8;
      end;
    end;

    // The index among the program's modules (ADAM_AST_PROGRAM's, in their order) of the
    // module holding the node ANode; the module count when none holds it
    hidden const method DoModuleRank(const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LAt := ANode;
      while (LAt <> 0) and (self.FTree.ParentOf(LAt) <> ADAM_AST_PROGRAM) do
        LAt := self.FTree.ParentOf(LAt);
      end;
      LCount := self.FTree.CountOf(ADAM_AST_PROGRAM, NodeRole.Module);
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        if self.FTree.NthOf(ADAM_AST_PROGRAM, NodeRole.Module, LI) = LAt then
          return LI;
        end;
      end;
      return LCount;
    end;

    // The sort key of the site at index AIndex (site number - 1) in source order (M3.12b):
    // its module's rank (the whole-program AST's file order), then its line, its column,
    // then the order Lowering met it, packed high to low into one int64 (rank 10 bits, line
    // 20, column 12, index 21; a line or column past its field is held at the field's top)
    hidden const method DoSiteKey(const AIndex: int64): int64;
    var
      LNode: int64;
      LRank: int64;
      LLine: int64;
      LColumn: int64;
    begin
      LNode := self.FSiteNodes[AIndex];
      LRank := self.DoModuleRank(LNode);
      if (LRank >= 1024) or (AIndex >= 2097152) then
        raise("Lowering: allocation sites past the site table's key (M3.12b)");
      end;
      LLine := int64(self.FTree[LNode].Place.Line);
      if LLine > 1048575 then
        LLine := 1048575;
      end;
      LColumn := int64(self.FTree[LNode].Place.Column);
      if LColumn > 4095 then
        LColumn := 4095;
      end;
      return (LRank shl 53) | (LLine shl 33) | (LColumn shl 21) | AIndex;
    end;

    // The offset of the text AText in the site table's text pool (ATexts / AOffsets: the
    // texts in it so far and where each starts; AEnd its length so far), added at its end
    // (NUL-ended) when not there yet
    hidden method DoPoolText(var ATexts: StringArray; var AOffsets: Int64Array;
      var AEnd: int64; const AText: string): int64;
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to len(ATexts) - 1 do
        if ATexts[LI] = AText then
          return AOffsets[LI];
        end;
      end;
      LI := len(ATexts);
      setlength(ATexts, LI + 1);
      setlength(AOffsets, LI + 1);
      ATexts[LI] := AText;
      AOffsets[LI] := AEnd;
      AEnd := AEnd + len(AText) + 1;
      return AOffsets[LI];
    end;

    // The allocation sites given their ids in source order (M3.12b): sorted by DoSiteKey,
    // site id I the I-th, every stored site constant (FSiteStores) patched to its id, then
    // the exe's site table written (DoSiteTable)
    hidden method DoNumberSites();
    var
      LKeys: Int64Array;
      LOrder: Int64Array;
      LIdOf: Int64Array;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      setlength(LKeys, len(self.FSiteNodes));
      for LI := 0 to len(self.FSiteNodes) - 1 do
        LKeys[LI] := self.DoSiteKey(LI);
      end;
      SortInt64s(LKeys);
      setlength(LOrder, len(LKeys));
      setlength(LIdOf, len(LKeys));
      for LI := 0 to len(LKeys) - 1 do
        // the key's low 21 bits are the site's index (DoSiteKey)
        LOrder[LI] := LKeys[LI] & 2097151;
        LIdOf[LOrder[LI]] := LI + 1;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to len(self.FSiteStores) - 1 do
        self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FSiteStores[LI]).Imm := LIdOf[self.FSiteStoreOf[LI] - 1];
      end;
      self.DoSiteTable(LOrder);
    end;

    // The symbol of the module AModule's site table (ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_SYMBOL, '_', its
    // name; public: the parts' site list holds its address)
    hidden const method DoSitesSymbol(const AModule: int64): string;
    begin
      return ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_SYMBOL + "_" + self.FTree[AModule].Text;
    end;

    // The unit's site table's data blob (DoSitesSymbol, 8-aligned, writable: the runtime
    // writes its base word), made on the first ask: a site store reads its base word
    // (DoStoreSite) before DoSiteTable writes its bytes
    hidden method DoSiteData(): int64;
    begin
      if self.FSiteData = 0 then
        self.FSiteData := self.FModule.AddDataOfKind(self.DoSitesSymbol(self.FUnit),
          IrDataKind.Variable, 8, self.FUnit);
      end;
      return self.FSiteData;
    end;

    // A debug build's entry at ANode hands the site list (the parts' own,
    // ADAM_LOWERING_SITELIST_SYMBOL: a uint64 count, then the address of every unit's site
    // table in the program's module order, the order DoSiteKey ranked them in when the
    // program was one module) to the runtime's leak tracker (M4.L1: HeapSiteList(list
    // address); each table's header holds its unit's line table's address, M4.L2) before
    // its exit handlers are registered (a block records only its site id and its return
    // addresses, the tables are read at the report); nothing when sites are off (a release
    // build) or the runtime has no HeapSiteList (it is the runtime's only under `@ifdef DEBUG`)
    hidden method DoHandSites(const ANode: int64);
    var
      LList: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if not self.DoSitesOn() then
        return;
      end;
      if self.FTree.RuntimeRoutineOf(RuntimeRoutine.HeapSiteList) = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LCount := self.FTree.CountOf(ADAM_AST_PROGRAM, NodeRole.Module);
      LList := self.FModule.AddData(ADAM_LOWERING_SITELIST_SYMBOL, 8, ANode);
      self.FModule.DataAt(LList).Internal := true;
      self.DoAddLe32(LList, LCount);
      self.DoAddLe32(LList, 0);
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        self.FModule.DataAt(LList).AddAddress(self.DoSitesSymbol(
          self.FTree.NthOf(ADAM_AST_PROGRAM, NodeRole.Module, LI)), 0);
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := LList;
      self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.HeapSiteList, LAddress, 0, ANode);
    end;

    // The entry at ANode hands the program's @addresdata table (BNF sec 2; the layout at
    // ADAM_LOWERING_RESDATA_SYMBOL) to the runtime's ResDataTable before any module starts:
    // every key of every module (a compiled unit's too: its directives are in the tree),
    // in byte-wise key order, each with its file's bytes read now (Semantics checked the
    // file is there; one gone since is read as empty) and one zero byte after them, so a
    // text reads as a C string. Nothing when the program adds no key (the runtime then
    // holds none) or the runtime has no ResDataTable
    hidden method DoResDataTable(const ANode: int64);
    var
      LIndex: ref StringIdMap;
      LKeys: StringArray;
      LPaths: StringArray;
      LSorted: StringArray;
      LModule: int64;
      LDirective: int64;
      LArg: int64;
      LTable: int64;
      LPool: int64;
      LBlob: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LBytes: ptr to uint8;
      LPath: ptr to char;
      LAddress: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LJ: int64;
      LK: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTree.RuntimeRoutineOf(RuntimeRoutine.ResDataTable) = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      // Every key once (a second is SM0121, a build that never lowers), with its file
      LIndex := ref StringIdMap();
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ADAM_AST_PROGRAM, NodeRole.Module) - 1 do
        LModule := self.FTree.NthOf(ADAM_AST_PROGRAM, NodeRole.Module, LI);
        for LJ := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(LModule, NodeRole.Directive) - 1 do
          LDirective := self.FTree.NthOf(LModule, NodeRole.Directive, LJ);
          if (self.FTree[LDirective].Text = ADAM_LOWERING_DIRECTIVE_RESDATA) and
            not self.FTree[LDirective].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Recovered) and
            (self.FTree.CountOf(LDirective, NodeRole.Argument) = 2) then
            LArg := self.FTree.NthOf(LDirective, NodeRole.Argument, 0);
            if LIndex.Find(self.FTree[LArg].Decoded) = 0 then
              LK := len(LKeys);
              setlength(LKeys, LK + 1);
              setlength(LPaths, LK + 1);
              LKeys[LK] := self.FTree[LArg].Decoded;
              LPaths[LK] := self.FTree[self.FTree.NthOf(LDirective, NodeRole.Argument, 1)].ResolvedPath;
              LIndex.Put(LKeys[LK], LK + 1);
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      if len(LKeys) = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LSorted := LKeys;
      SortStrings(LSorted);
      LTable := self.FModule.AddData(ADAM_LOWERING_RESDATA_SYMBOL, 8, ANode);
      self.FModule.DataAt(LTable).Internal := true;
      LPool := self.FModule.AddData(ADAM_LOWERING_RESDATA_KEYS_SYMBOL, 1, ANode);
      self.FModule.DataAt(LPool).Internal := true;
      self.DoAddLe64(LTable, len(LSorted));
      LAt := 0;
      for LI := 0 to len(LSorted) - 1 do
        LK := LIndex.Find(LSorted[LI]) - 1;
        // The key's text, NUL-ended, in the pool
        self.FModule.DataAt(LTable).AddAddress(ADAM_LOWERING_RESDATA_KEYS_SYMBOL, LAt);
        for LJ := 0 to len(LSorted[LI]) - 1 do
          self.FModule.DataAt(LPool).AddByte(uint8(LSorted[LI][LJ]));
        end;
        self.FModule.DataAt(LPool).AddByte(0);
        LAt := LAt + len(LSorted[LI]) + 1;
        // The file's bytes, then the zero byte after them (not counted)
        LBlob := self.FModule.AddData(ADAM_LOWERING_RESDATA_SYMBOL + "_" + IntToStr(LI),
          ADAM_LOWERING_RESDATA_ALIGN, ANode);
        self.FModule.DataAt(LBlob).Internal := true;
        LCount := 0;
        LBytes := nil;
        LPath := StringToC(LPaths[LK]);
        if LPath <> nil then
          LBytes := ptr to uint8(ReadFileBytes(ptr to const char(LPath), LCount));
          freemem(LPath);
        end;
        for LJ := 0 to LCount - 1 do
          self.FModule.DataAt(LBlob).AddByte(LBytes[LJ]);
        end;
        self.FModule.DataAt(LBlob).AddByte(0);
        if LBytes <> nil then
          freemem(LBytes);
        end;
        self.FModule.DataAt(LTable).AddAddress(ADAM_LOWERING_RESDATA_SYMBOL + "_" + IntToStr(LI), 0);
        self.DoAddLe64(LTable, LCount);
      end;
      LAddress := self.DoEmit(IrOp.Address, IrType.Pointer, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LAddress).Link := LTable;
      self.DoCallRuntime(RuntimeRoutine.ResDataTable, LAddress, 0, ANode);
    end;

    // The unit's allocation site table (M3.12b; one per unit, SU2.4), writable data named
    // by DoSitesSymbol, little-endian: the 8 bytes ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_MAGIC, the layout's
    // version (uint32, ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_VERSION) and the site count N (uint32); the
    // address of the unit's code-address line table (an address word, M4.L2: the blob
    // ADAM_LOWERING_LINES_SYMBOL, '_' and its name, made here, empty, the module's
    // LineTable, which the backend fills once the code is laid out); the base word (uint32,
    // 0 here: the runtime writes the ids of the units before it, HeapSiteList) and 4 zero
    // bytes, ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_HEADER in all; then N records of four uint32, record I
    // being the unit's site I + 1 (AOrder: the sites' indexes in id order): its line, its
    // column, its file's name (alone, no folder: the same exe wherever it was built) and
    // what it allocates, each of the two a byte offset into the pool of NUL-ended texts
    // right after the records (each text once). Every unit has one when sites are on, none
    // of them its sites
    hidden method DoSiteTable(const AOrder: Int64Array);
    var
      LData: int64;
      LTexts: StringArray;
      LOffsets: Int64Array;
      LEnd: int64;
      LFiles: Int64Array;
      LWhats: Int64Array;
      LNode: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LJ: int64;
    begin
      LEnd := 0;
      setlength(LFiles, len(AOrder));
      setlength(LWhats, len(AOrder));
      for LI := 0 to len(AOrder) - 1 do
        LNode := self.FSiteNodes[AOrder[LI]];
        LFiles[LI] := self.DoPoolText(LTexts, LOffsets, LEnd,
          ExtractFileName(self.FTree[LNode].Place.FileName));
        LWhats[LI] := self.DoPoolText(LTexts, LOffsets, LEnd, self.FSiteWhats[AOrder[LI]]);
      end;
      LData := self.DoSiteData();
      for LI := 0 to len(ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_MAGIC) - 1 do
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(uint8(ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_MAGIC[LI]));
      end;
      self.DoAddLe32(LData, ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_VERSION);
      self.DoAddLe32(LData, len(AOrder));
      if self.FModule.LineTable = 0 then
        self.FModule.LineTable := self.FModule.AddData(ADAM_LOWERING_LINES_SYMBOL + "_" +
          self.FTree[self.FUnit].Text, 8, self.FUnit);
        self.FModule.DataAt(self.FModule.LineTable).Internal := true;
      end;
      self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddAddress(self.FModule.DataAt(self.FModule.LineTable).Symbol, 0);
      // the base word and its pad (ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_BASE .. ADAM_LOWERING_SITES_HEADER)
      self.DoAddLe32(LData, 0);
      self.DoAddLe32(LData, 0);
      for LI := 0 to len(AOrder) - 1 do
        LNode := self.FSiteNodes[AOrder[LI]];
        self.DoAddLe32(LData, int64(self.FTree[LNode].Place.Line));
        self.DoAddLe32(LData, int64(self.FTree[LNode].Place.Column));
        self.DoAddLe32(LData, LFiles[LI]);
        self.DoAddLe32(LData, LWhats[LI]);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to len(LTexts) - 1 do
        for LJ := 0 to len(LTexts[LI]) - 1 do
          self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(uint8(LTexts[LI][LJ]));
        end;
        self.FModule.DataAt(LData).AddByte(0);
      end;
    end;

    // True when the subtree of ANode holds no more nodes than ACap still allows (each node
    // takes one; the count stops once it is past)
    hidden const method DoSubtreeWithin(const ANode: int64; var ACap: int64): bool;
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      ACap := ACap - 1;
      if ACap < 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.ChildCount(ANode) - 1 do
        if not self.DoSubtreeWithin(self.FTree.ChildAt(ANode, LI), ACap) then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // True when ARoutine (another unit's routine, a declared function) may get a body copy
    // (DoInlineCopy): it has a body of its own (not a bound accessor), no generic part, and
    // a subtree of at most ADAM_LOWERING_COPY_NODES nodes (a larger one is never small
    // enough for the inliner's budgets, so its lowering would be wasted)
    hidden method DoCopyable(const ARoutine: int64): bool;
    var
      LCap: int64;
    begin
      if ARoutine = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      if self.FTree.FirstOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.Body) = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      if self.FTree.CountOf(ARoutine, NodeRole.GenericParam) > 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      if self.DoIsAccessor(ARoutine) and self.DoIsBound(ARoutine) then
        return false;
      end;
      // a generator's ramp names its body function, which only its own unit lowers
      if self.FTree[ARoutine].HasFlag(NodeFlag.Generator) then
        return false;
      end;
      LCap := ADAM_LOWERING_COPY_NODES;
      return self.DoSubtreeWithin(ARoutine, LCap);
    end;

    // True when a function from AFirst on (a body copy and the funclets lowered with it)
    // reaches another unit's internal function or blob: a symbol only that unit's object
    // has, which no other object can link to
    hidden const method DoReachesInternal(const AFirst: int64): bool;
    var
      LFunction: ref IrFunction;
      LBlock: ref IrBlock;
      LInstr: ref IrInstr;
      LLink: int64;
      LF: int64;
      LB: int64;
      LK: int64;
    begin
      for LF := AFirst to self.FModule.FunctionCount - 1 do
        LFunction := self.FModule.FunctionAt(LF);
        for LB := 0 to LFunction.Blocks.Count - 1 do
          LBlock := self.FModule.BlockAt(LFunction.Blocks[LB]);
          for LK := 0 to LBlock.Instrs.Count - 1 do
            LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(LBlock.Instrs[LK]);
            LLink := LInstr.Link;
            if (LInstr.Kind = IrOp.Call) or (LInstr.Kind = IrOp.CodeAddress) then
              if self.FModule.FunctionAt(LLink).Declared and
                self.FModule.FunctionAt(LLink).Internal then
                return true;
              end;
            end;
            if (LInstr.Kind = IrOp.Address) or (LInstr.Kind = IrOp.ThreadAddress) then
              if self.FModule.DataAt(LLink).Declared and self.FModule.DataAt(LLink).Internal then
                return true;
              end;
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // The body of AFunction's routine (another unit's, DoCopyable) lowered here as a copy:
    // a new internal function (ADAM_LOWERING_INLINE_SYMBOL), AFunction's InlineBody, which
    // only the inliner reads (Adam.Opt.Inline: AA.3, the callee lowered from the AST at the
    // call's unit); a call of the routine inside it stays a call of AFunction. A copy that
    // reaches another unit's internal symbol (DoReachesInternal) is dropped with its
    // funclets: declared, no blocks, no scopes (nothing refers to them, nothing is made)
    hidden method DoInlineCopy(const AFunction: int64);
    var
      LRoutine: int64;
      LCopy: int64;
      LDeclared: ref IrFunction;
      LFunction: ref IrFunction;
      LF: int64;
    begin
      LRoutine := self.FDeclaredRoutines.Find(AFunction);
      if not self.DoCopyable(LRoutine) then
        return;
      end;
      LDeclared := self.FModule.FunctionAt(AFunction);
      LCopy := self.FModule.AddFunction(LDeclared.Symbol + ADAM_LOWERING_INLINE_SYMBOL,
        LDeclared.Signature.ResultType, LRoutine);
      LFunction := self.FModule.FunctionAt(LCopy);
      LFunction.Internal := true;
      LFunction.NoReturn := LDeclared.NoReturn;
      self.DoFillSignature(LRoutine, LFunction.Signature);
      // the body lowered into the copy, then the routine's function the declared one again
      self.FFunctionOf[LRoutine] := LCopy;
      self.DoBody(LRoutine);
      self.DoCleanupScopes(LRoutine, self.DoLastBlock());
      self.FFunctionOf[LRoutine] := AFunction;
      if self.DoReachesInternal(LCopy) then
        for LF := LCopy to self.FModule.FunctionCount - 1 do
          LFunction := self.FModule.FunctionAt(LF);
          LFunction.Declared := true;
          LFunction.Blocks := ref Int64List();
          LFunction.ClearScopes();
        end;
        return;
      end;
      LDeclared.InlineBody := LCopy;
    end;

    // A release build's body copies (DoInlineCopy) of every other unit's routine a function
    // of this unit calls directly, once each, in the order of the first call; the copies'
    // own calls are not followed (a copy is inlined once: what it calls stays a call)
    hidden method DoInlineCopies();
    var
      LQueue: ref Int64List;
      LQueued: ref Int64Map;
      LFunction: ref IrFunction;
      LBlock: ref IrBlock;
      LInstr: ref IrInstr;
      LOwn: int64;
      LF: int64;
      LB: int64;
      LK: int64;
    begin
      LQueue := ref Int64List();
      LQueued := ref Int64Map(0);
      LOwn := self.FModule.FunctionCount;
      for LF := 1 to LOwn - 1 do
        LFunction := self.FModule.FunctionAt(LF);
        if LFunction.Declared then
          skip;
        end;
        for LB := 0 to LFunction.Blocks.Count - 1 do
          LBlock := self.FModule.BlockAt(LFunction.Blocks[LB]);
          for LK := 0 to LBlock.Instrs.Count - 1 do
            LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(LBlock.Instrs[LK]);
            if (LInstr.Kind = IrOp.Call) and (LQueued.Find(LInstr.Link) = 0) and
              (self.FDeclaredRoutines.Find(LInstr.Link) <> 0) then
              LQueued.Put(LInstr.Link, 1);
              LQueue.Add(LInstr.Link);
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      for LF := 0 to LQueue.Count - 1 do
        self.DoInlineCopy(LQueue[LF]);
      end;
    end;

    // Every module's routines and variables given their functions and blobs, the unit's
    // own, every other one's declared (DoModule under FDeclaring); the entry found; then
    // for the parts: the @linklibrary names of every module and the entry's body; for a
    // unit: its sections, every body lowered, its variable inits, its program block (the
    // exe unit), its start and its thread release, the task and end functions, its site
    // table (with no entry, the initializers and sections that need one are LW0001)
    method Run();
    var
      LReached: BoolArray;
      LI: int64;
      LModule: int64;
    begin
      // Only the modules the unit can name are declared: its imports, theirs, and the
      // runtime's (the parts name the runtime's alone)
      setlength(LReached, self.FTree.Count);
      if self.FUnit <> ADAM_LOWERING_PARTS then
        DoReach(self.FTree, self.FUnit, LReached);
      end;
      DoReach(self.FTree, self.FTree.Runtime, LReached);
      for LI := 0 to self.FTree.CountOf(ADAM_AST_PROGRAM, NodeRole.Module) - 1 do
        LModule := self.FTree.NthOf(ADAM_AST_PROGRAM, NodeRole.Module, LI);
        if LReached[LModule] then
          self.FDeclaring := LModule <> self.FUnit;
          self.DoModule(LModule);
        else
          // the program block's module is known to every unit (the entry it needs)
          if (self.FTree[LModule].Module = ModuleKind.Exe) and
            (self.FTree.FirstOf(LModule, NodeRole.Body) <> 0) then
            self.FEntryModule := LModule;
          end;
        end;
        if self.FUnit = ADAM_LOWERING_PARTS then
          self.DoLinkLibraries(LModule);
        end;
      end;
      self.FDeclaring := false;
      self.DoFindEntry();
      self.DoOrderModules();
      if self.FUnit = ADAM_LOWERING_PARTS then
        if self.FEntry <> 0 then
          self.DoEntryBody();
        end;
        return;
      end;
      self.DoRegisterSections();
      for LI := 0 to self.FRoutines.Count - 1 do
        self.DoBody(self.FRoutines[LI]);
        self.DoCleanupScopes(self.FRoutines[LI], self.DoLastBlock());
        // the runtime's start of a started thread: the entry's last catching scope
        if self.FRoutines[LI] = self.FTree.RuntimeRoutineOf(RuntimeRoutine.ThreadRun) then
          self.DoCatchAll(self.FRoutines[LI], RuntimeRoutine.CatchRaise,
            RuntimeRoutine.Unhandled);
        end;
        // a generator's coroutine run: its abort's last catching scope (G1)
        if self.FRoutines[LI] = self.FTree.RuntimeRoutineOf(RuntimeRoutine.GeneratorRun) then
          self.DoCatchAll(self.FRoutines[LI], RuntimeRoutine.CatchAbort,
            RuntimeRoutine.GeneratorEnd);
        end;
      end;
      self.DoSectionBodies();
      self.DoTestBodies();
      self.DoUnitVarInit();
      if self.FEntry <> 0 then
        self.DoBlockBody();
      end;
      self.DoUnitStart();
      self.DoUnitRelease();
      // the for parallel bodies first (one may hold an async), then the task entries: an
      // end function one of them asks for is lowered after
      self.DoDeferredBodies();
      self.DoEndBodies();
      // a release build: the body copies of the other units' routines it calls, for the
      // inliner (Adam.Opt.Inline)
      if not self.FTree.IsDebugBuild() then
        self.DoInlineCopies();
        // a copy's itable may have asked for a forward (I4)
        self.DoForwardBodies();
      end;
      // every function lowered: the sites take their ids in source order (M3.12b)
      if self.DoSitesOn() then
        self.DoNumberSites();
      end;
    end;
  end;

// The unit AUnit (a module of the program in ATree, analyzed, laid out and named, with no
// errors) lowered alone for ATarget into one IrModule (SU2.4, see the header): its own
// routines, variables and sections, its entry points for the program's entry (variable
// inits, start, thread release; the exe unit's block function), its site table; every
// other module's routine and variable a declared function or blob, which its own object
// defines. Reports go to ADiagnostics. With no target (nil) nothing is lowered: the
// Driver has reported the missing target (DR0004)
public routine LowerUnit(const ATree: ref SyntaxTree; const ATarget: ref Target;
  const ADiagnostics: ref Diagnostics; const AUnit: int64): ref IrModule;
var
  LLowerer: ref Lowerer;
begin
  LLowerer := ref Lowerer(ATree, ATarget, ADiagnostics, AUnit);
  if ATarget <> nil then
    LLowerer.Run();
  end;
  return LLowerer.Lowered;
end;

// The program's parts in ATree lowered for ATarget into one IrModule (SU2.4): the entry
// (the IR's Entry; every unit's entry points called by symbol, see DoEntryBody), the
// program's thread release, the site list, every module's @linklibrary names; every
// module declared. Made every build: it alone knows which units the program has
public routine LowerProgramParts(const ATree: ref SyntaxTree; const ATarget: ref Target;
  const ADiagnostics: ref Diagnostics): ref IrModule;
begin
  return LowerUnit(ATree, ATarget, ADiagnostics, ADAM_LOWERING_PARTS);
end;

// Every routine of the modules ATree did not read from a compiled unit given its write
// summary (SU2.8 e4: its WriteEffects node, Lowerer.SummarizeWrites), which DoMayDrop reads
// to leave out the holds no callee can need. Run once the tree is checked and before any
// unit's interface hash is taken (an importer depends on a summary: the hash holds it) or
// any unit is lowered; nothing for no target (nil)
public routine SummarizeWrites(const ATree: ref SyntaxTree; const ATarget: ref Target;
  const ADiagnostics: ref Diagnostics);
var
  LLowerer: ref Lowerer;
begin
  if ATarget = nil then
    return;
  end;
  LLowerer := ref Lowerer(ATree, ATarget, ADiagnostics, ADAM_LOWERING_PARTS);
  LLowerer.SummarizeWrites();
end;

end.
